window.LALITHA_NAMES = [{"number":1,"name":"श्रीमाता","samasa":["श्रिया युता श्रीयुता। श्रीयुता माता।","श्रिया माता।","श्रियं (लक्ष्मीं) माति (परिच्छिनत्ति। तेन अनवधिकश्रीरूपः मोक्षः)।","श्रियं (विषं) माति (कण्ठे स्थापयति)।"],"wordByWord":["श्री / श्रिया - Lakshmi, wealth, auspiciousness, splendour, learning.","युता - endowed with, possessed of.","माता - mother.","श्रियं माति - She measures, limits, classifies, distributes, or contains Śrī.","विषं माति - She holds poison in the throat; the feminine counterpart of Śrīkaṇṭha."],"summary":["श्रीमाता means the supreme mother. When we are in deep trouble, the first word uttered by us involuntarily is Mā. Human beings are afflicted by three kinds of tāpas (difficulties), which cannot be solved by the mother in her human form. Worshipping Her, who has given birth to the whole world, will prevent birth again in this world from the mother's womb. The best of love is mother's affection. Thus to contemplate and worship Her as the mother will give us proximity to Her. Śrī means Lakṣmī (goddess of wealth). Thus Śrīmātā means Lakṣmī's mother. Śrī also means Sarasvatī (goddess of learning). She is mother of both Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī. Mā means \"to measure\". Śrīmātā therefore means that She is capable of measuring wealth. One that measures is superior to the one that is measured. She is the one who classified the Vedas. From this angle, Śrīdevī can also be indicated as Brahmā and/or Vyāsa. Śrī means venom. One who held the venom in her throat (māti). Lord Parameśvara is called Śrīkaṇṭha because he retained the Hālāhala venom in his throat."],"searchText":"1 श्रीमाता श्रिया युता श्रीयुता। श्रीयुता माता। श्रिया माता। श्रियं (लक्ष्मीं) माति (परिच्छिनत्ति। तेन अनवधिकश्रीरूपः मोक्षः)। श्रियं (विषं) माति (कण्ठे स्थापयति)। श्री / श्रिया - lakshmi, wealth, auspiciousness, splendour, learning. युता - endowed with, possessed of. माता - mother. श्रियं माति - she measures, limits, classifies, distributes, or contains śrī. विषं माति - she holds poison in the throat; the feminine counterpart of śrīkaṇṭha. श्रीमाता means the supreme mother. when we are in deep trouble, the first word uttered by us involuntarily is mā. human beings are afflicted by three kinds of tāpas (difficulties), which cannot be solved by the mother in her human form. worshipping her, who has given birth to the whole world, will prevent birth again in this world from the mother's womb. the best of love is mother's affection. thus to contemplate and worship her as the mother will give us proximity to her. śrī means lakṣmī (goddess of wealth). thus śrīmātā means lakṣmī's mother. śrī also means sarasvatī (goddess of learning). she is mother of both lakṣmī and sarasvatī. mā means \"to measure\". śrīmātā therefore means that she is capable of measuring wealth. one that measures is superior to the one that is measured. she is the one who classified the vedas. from this angle, śrīdevī can also be indicated as brahmā and/or vyāsa. śrī means venom. one who held the venom in her throat (māti). lord parameśvara is called śrīkaṇṭha because he retained the hālāhala venom in his throat. अर्थ (meaning): she who is \"endowed with श्री\". therefore, she is the माता who is eternally accompanied by divine splendor and auspiciousness. अर्थ (meaning): the mother who is accompanied by or identified with श्री. अर्थ (meaning): श्रियं माति इति श्रीमाता. she who measures, limits, or controls material लक्ष्मी (wealth). by putting a limit on material existence, she bestows the limitless, boundless state of मोक्ष (liberation). अर्थ (meaning): she who contains the श्री (poison) in her throat. this derivation identifies the divine mother directly with the cosmic action of containing the poison during the churning of the ocean, establishing non-difference from नीलकण्ठ (shiva).","esoteric":["अर्थ (Meaning): She who is \"endowed with श्री\". Therefore, she is the माता who is eternally accompanied by divine splendor and auspiciousness.","अर्थ (Meaning): The Mother who is accompanied by or identified with श्री.","अर्थ (Meaning): श्रियं माति इति श्रीमाता. She who measures, limits, or controls material लक्ष्मी (wealth). By putting a limit on material existence, she bestows the limitless, boundless state of मोक्ष (liberation).","अर्थ (Meaning): She who contains the श्री (poison) in her throat. This derivation identifies the Divine Mother directly with the cosmic action of containing the poison during the churning of the ocean, establishing non-difference from नीलकण्ठ (Shiva)."]},{"number":2,"name":"श्रीमहाराज्ञी","samasa":["महती च असौ राज्ञी च महाराज्ञी। श्रीयुता महाराज्ञी श्रीमहाराज्ञी।"],"wordByWord":["श्री - auspiciousness, splendour, divine wealth.","महती - great.","राज्ञी - queen, ruler.","महाराज्ञी - great empress.","श्रीयुता महाराज्ञी - the great empress endowed with Śrī."],"summary":["श्रीमहाराज्ञी means the great empress and protector of the whole world. She represents the protecting function of the Supreme Being, expressed in the Vedic idea \"yena jātāni jīvanti\": that by which born beings live. The name also contains three secret syllables of Śrīvidyā, to be learned properly from a teacher. She is not called empress merely because She is the consort of an emperor; She governs by Her own authority and carries out the work of cosmic rule Herself."],"searchText":"2 श्रीमहाराज्ञी महती च असौ राज्ञी च महाराज्ञी। श्रीयुता महाराज्ञी श्रीमहाराज्ञी। श्री - auspiciousness, splendour, divine wealth. महती - great. राज्ञी - queen, ruler. महाराज्ञी - great empress. श्रीयुता महाराज्ञी - the great empress endowed with śrī. श्रीमहाराज्ञी means the great empress and protector of the whole world. she represents the protecting function of the supreme being, expressed in the vedic idea \"yena jātāni jīvanti\": that by which born beings live. the name also contains three secret syllables of śrīvidyā, to be learned properly from a teacher. she is not called empress merely because she is the consort of an emperor; she governs by her own authority and carries out the work of cosmic rule herself. the conventional meaning of a royal monarch ruling an empire is elevated to cosmic and mantric planes: i. the sovereign of manifestation and dissolution the title राज्ञी comes from the verbal root राज् (rāj), meaning \"to shine\" or \"to illuminate.\" she is the महाराज्ञी because she shines supreme as the independent, self-luminous consciousness (स्वप्रकाश चिद्रूप) that illuminates the entire universe. unlike planetary rulers or cosmic deities (like indra or brahmā) whose domains are temporary and bounded by time, her sovereignty spans across all three cosmic states: creation (sṛṣṭi), preservation (sthiti), and dissolution (saṃhāra). ii. the ruler of the nine enclosures (śrī cakra) in the esoteric geography of the śrī cakra, the three outermost lines are called the bhūpura. within the entire citadel (śrī nagara), she sits at the absolute center at the बिन्दु (bindu). esoteric mapping: as the महाराज्ञी, she is the absolute commanding consciousness of the entire cosmic diagram. all the peripheral or enclosure deities (āvaraṇa devatās) act merely as her structural expansions or rays of light. iii. resolution into non-duality (advaita) true sovereignty lies in the absence of a second entity. if there is a rival or a separate object, dominion is limited. because she is the non-dual supreme reality (ekam-eva-advitīyam), there is nothing outside of her. her rule is absolute because the universe is her own self-projection (vimarśa). therefore, श्रीमहाराज्ञी signifies the supreme, unconditioned state of absolute autonomy (स्वातन्त्र्य शक्ति).","esoteric":["The conventional meaning of a royal monarch ruling an empire is elevated to cosmic and mantric planes:","I. The Sovereign of Manifestation and Dissolution","The title राज्ञी comes from the verbal root राज् (rāj), meaning \"to shine\" or \"to illuminate.\"","She is the महाराज्ञी because She shines supreme as the independent, self-luminous consciousness (स्वप्रकाश चिद्रूप) that illuminates the entire universe.","Unlike planetary rulers or cosmic deities (like Indra or Brahmā) whose domains are temporary and bounded by time, Her sovereignty spans across all three cosmic states: creation (Sṛṣṭi), preservation (Sthiti), and dissolution (Saṃhāra).","II. The Ruler of the Nine Enclosures (Śrī Cakra)","In the esoteric geography of the Śrī Cakra, the three outermost lines are called the Bhūpura. Within the entire citadel (Śrī Nagara), She sits at the absolute center at the बिन्दु (Bindu).","Esoteric Mapping: As the महाराज्ञी, She is the absolute commanding consciousness of the entire cosmic diagram. All the peripheral or enclosure deities (Āvaraṇa Devatās) act merely as Her structural expansions or rays of light.","III. Resolution into Non-Duality (Advaita)","true sovereignty lies in the absence of a second entity. If there is a rival or a separate object, dominion is limited.","Because She is the non-dual supreme reality (Ekam-eva-advitīyam), there is nothing outside of Her. Her rule is absolute because the universe is Her own self-projection (Vimarśa). Therefore, श्रीमहाराज्ञी signifies the supreme, unconditioned state of absolute autonomy (स्वातन्त्र्य शक्ति)."]},{"number":3,"name":"श्रीमत्सिंहासनेश्वरी","samasa":["सिंहचिह्नितासनं सिंहासनम्। सिंहासनस्य ईश्वरी।","आसनेषु सिंहः (श्रेष्ठम्)। श्रीमच्च तत्सिंहासनं च श्रीमत्सिंहासनम्। तस्य ईश्वरी।","सिंहः आसनं यस्याः सा सिंहासना। सिंहासना च असौ ईश्वरी च।","सिंहेन (हिंसया) असनं (क्षेपणं) सिंहासनम्। तत्र ईश्वरी (समर्था)।","श्रीमती च असौ सिंहासनेश्वरी च।"],"wordByWord":["श्रीमत् - splendid, auspicious, endowed with wealth.","सिंह - lion; also connected with power and majesty.","आसन - seat, throne.","सिंहासन - lion-throne, the royal throne.","ईश्वरी - sovereign lady, ruler, controller.","श्रीमत्सिंहासनस्य ईश्वरी - the sovereign of the auspicious lion-throne."],"summary":["श्रीमत्सिंहासनेश्वरी means She herself rides on a lion and uses it as a seat. She controls and rules the world seated on a great grand throne. The seat of a king is a throne — siṃhāsana. The seat of kings is designed as if the ruler is seated on a lion, because the lion is the king of animals. By virtue of Her position as a controller and ruler of World Empire, She is the lord of siṃhāsana, symbolises the wealth (Lakṣmī) of the empire of the Universe and seated in this throne. It also means that She is siṃhavāhinī — one who rides on a lion. the demon Mahiṣa was killed by Śrīdevī riding on a lion. She thus acquired the names of Mahiṣaghnī (killer of Mahiṣa) and siṃhāsaneśvarī. The word siṃha is derived from the verb hiṃsā. siṃha is the corrupted form of hiṃsā. Thus hiṃsāsaneśvarī means, one who has the power to destroy the whole world — the third function of the Supreme Being, namely to destroy, is indicated here."],"searchText":"3 श्रीमत्सिंहासनेश्वरी सिंहचिह्नितासनं सिंहासनम्। सिंहासनस्य ईश्वरी। आसनेषु सिंहः (श्रेष्ठम्)। श्रीमच्च तत्सिंहासनं च श्रीमत्सिंहासनम्। तस्य ईश्वरी। सिंहः आसनं यस्याः सा सिंहासना। सिंहासना च असौ ईश्वरी च। सिंहेन (हिंसया) असनं (क्षेपणं) सिंहासनम्। तत्र ईश्वरी (समर्था)। श्रीमती च असौ सिंहासनेश्वरी च। श्रीमत् - splendid, auspicious, endowed with wealth. सिंह - lion; also connected with power and majesty. आसन - seat, throne. सिंहासन - lion-throne, the royal throne. ईश्वरी - sovereign lady, ruler, controller. श्रीमत्सिंहासनस्य ईश्वरी - the sovereign of the auspicious lion-throne. श्रीमत्सिंहासनेश्वरी means she herself rides on a lion and uses it as a seat. she controls and rules the world seated on a great grand throne. the seat of a king is a throne — siṃhāsana. the seat of kings is designed as if the ruler is seated on a lion, because the lion is the king of animals. by virtue of her position as a controller and ruler of world empire, she is the lord of siṃhāsana, symbolises the wealth (lakṣmī) of the empire of the universe and seated in this throne. it also means that she is siṃhavāhinī — one who rides on a lion. the demon mahiṣa was killed by śrīdevī riding on a lion. she thus acquired the names of mahiṣaghnī (killer of mahiṣa) and siṃhāsaneśvarī. the word siṃha is derived from the verb hiṃsā. siṃha is the corrupted form of hiṃsā. thus hiṃsāsaneśvarī means, one who has the power to destroy the whole world — the third function of the supreme being, namely to destroy, is indicated here. she is the supreme ruler and residing deity of the royal throne of consciousness. the lion denotes absolute dominion over the created universe. it stands supreme above all other divine seats or states of yogic absorption. this directly maps her identity to the cosmic power that rides upon the lion (the vehicle of durgā / jagadambā), representing the absolute control and direction of the untamed, kinetic energy of the cosmos (rajo-guṇa). this addresses the saṃhāra-krama (the dissolution phase of consciousness). she is the sovereign power that completely eliminates samsāra, throwing away the limitations of names and forms to reveal the undifferentiated self. it confirms that her absolute rule over the throne of the universe is not dry or purely destructive, but is eternally infused with श्रीमद्—the nectarine, auspicious, and blissful light of pure awareness (cit-vilāsa).","esoteric":["She is the supreme ruler and residing deity of the royal throne of consciousness. The lion denotes absolute dominion over the created universe.","It stands supreme above all other divine seats or states of yogic absorption.","This directly maps Her identity to the cosmic power that rides upon the lion (the vehicle of Durgā / Jagadambā), representing the absolute control and direction of the untamed, kinetic energy of the cosmos (Rajo-guṇa).","This addresses the Saṃhāra-krama (the dissolution phase of consciousness). She is the sovereign power that completely eliminates Samsāra, throwing away the limitations of names and forms to reveal the undifferentiated Self.","It confirms that Her absolute rule over the throne of the universe is not dry or purely destructive, but is eternally infused with श्रीमद्—the nectarine, auspicious, and blissful light of pure awareness (Cit-vilāsa)."]},{"number":4,"name":"चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता","samasa":["अग्नेः कुण्डम् अग्निकुण्डम्। चिद् एव अग्निकुण्डं वा चिदरूपं अग्निकुण्डं वा चिदग्निकुण्डम्।","तस्मात् सम्भूता चिदाग्निकुण्डसम्भूता। अथवा तत्र सम्यक् (अभेदेन) भूता (स्थिता)।"],"wordByWord":["चित् - consciousness, knowledge, Brahman.","अग्नि - fire.","कुण्ड - fire-pit, sacrificial pit.","चिदग्निकुण्ड - the sacrificial fire-pit of consciousness or knowledge.","सम्भूता - born, arisen, emerged, fully manifested.","चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता - She who emerged from the fire-pit of consciousness."],"summary":["चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता means one who emerged from the sacrificial fire of knowledge. The word cit means flawless Brahman, and cidagni is the fire of knowledge that destroys the darkness of ignorance. Śrīdevī emerged from this fire of cit; in other words, Her real form appears from the sacrificial fire of knowledge to annihilate ignorance. This fire of knowledge is praised in spiritual literature, as in the Bhagavad Gītā phrase jñānāgniḥ sarvakarmāṇi bhasmasāt kurute tathā. The legend of Bhaṇḍāsura occurs in the Brahmāṇḍa Purāṇa, where this sahasranāma is recited. Indra and the devas performed a sacrifice to propitiate Śrīdevī and destroy Bhaṇḍāsura. That sacrificial fire was called cidagnikuṇḍa, and Śrīdevī emerged from that kuṇḍa. The false “I” connected with the physical and causal bodies is offered into this fire, and Śrīdevī, the real “I,” emerges. The name is also connected with raho-yāga, where vāsanās, actions, duties, merits, and sins are offered into the fire of knowledge."],"searchText":"4 चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता अग्नेः कुण्डम् अग्निकुण्डम्। चिद् एव अग्निकुण्डं वा चिदरूपं अग्निकुण्डं वा चिदग्निकुण्डम्। तस्मात् सम्भूता चिदाग्निकुण्डसम्भूता। अथवा तत्र सम्यक् (अभेदेन) भूता (स्थिता)। चित् - consciousness, knowledge, brahman. अग्नि - fire. कुण्ड - fire-pit, sacrificial pit. चिदग्निकुण्ड - the sacrificial fire-pit of consciousness or knowledge. सम्भूता - born, arisen, emerged, fully manifested. चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता - she who emerged from the fire-pit of consciousness. चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता means one who emerged from the sacrificial fire of knowledge. the word cit means flawless brahman, and cidagni is the fire of knowledge that destroys the darkness of ignorance. śrīdevī emerged from this fire of cit; in other words, her real form appears from the sacrificial fire of knowledge to annihilate ignorance. this fire of knowledge is praised in spiritual literature, as in the bhagavad gītā phrase jñānāgniḥ sarvakarmāṇi bhasmasāt kurute tathā. the legend of bhaṇḍāsura occurs in the brahmāṇḍa purāṇa, where this sahasranāma is recited. indra and the devas performed a sacrifice to propitiate śrīdevī and destroy bhaṇḍāsura. that sacrificial fire was called cidagnikuṇḍa, and śrīdevī emerged from that kuṇḍa. the false “i” connected with the physical and causal bodies is offered into this fire, and śrīdevī, the real “i,” emerges. the name is also connected with raho-yāga, where vāsanās, actions, duties, merits, and sins are offered into the fire of knowledge. i. the alchemical dissolution of duality in external rituals, objects are offered into a physical fire-pit to be consumed. esoterically, the चिदग्निकुण्ड is the internal fire of pure awareness (jñānāgni). the sādhaka pours the entire manifest universe, along with their individual ego (jīva-bhāva), into this fire as an oblation (āhuti). when all sense of separation is completely burned away, what remains and emerges out of that absolute void of consciousness is the supreme deity herself—चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता. ii. the awakening of the absolute ego (ahaṃtā) as the phrase \"तत्र सम्यक् अभेदेन स्थिता\" implies, she does not leave the fire; she is the very stability of that non-dual consciousness. she represents the pure, unconditioned cosmic i-consciousness (विमर्श / पूर्णांहता) that dawns when the dry intellect is consumed by spiritual fire.","esoteric":["I. The Alchemical Dissolution of Duality","In external rituals, objects are offered into a physical fire-pit to be consumed. Esoterically, the चिदग्निकुण्ड is the internal fire of pure awareness (Jñānāgni). The Sādhaka pours the entire manifest universe, along with their individual ego (Jīva-bhāva), into this fire as an oblation (Āhuti). When all sense of separation is completely burned away, what remains and emerges out of that absolute void of consciousness is the supreme deity Herself—चिदग्निकुण्डसम्भूता.","II. The Awakening of the Absolute Ego (Ahaṃtā)","As the phrase \"तत्र सम्यक् अभेदेन स्थिता\" implies, She does not leave the fire; She is the very stability of that non-dual consciousness. She represents the pure, unconditioned cosmic I-consciousness (विमर्श / पूर्णांहता) that dawns when the dry intellect is consumed by spiritual fire."]},{"number":5,"name":"देवकार्यसमुद्यता","samasa":["देवानां कार्याणि देवकार्याणि।","देवकार्याणां समुद्यता (शेषषष्ठ्या तदर्थं समुद्यता)।"],"wordByWord":["देव - devas, divine beings.","कार्य - work, task, purpose.","देवकार्य - the task or purpose of the Devas.","समुद्यता - risen, come forward, prepared, engaged.","देवकार्यसमुद्यता - She who has come forward for the purpose of the Devas."],"summary":["देवकार्यसमुद्यता means one who came forward to serve the devas. Though Śrīdevī is eternal, She assumes a particular form to help the devas accomplish their purpose. This is expressed in the verse: devānāṃ kāryasiddhyartham āvirbhavati sā yadā, utpanneti tadā loke sā nityāpy abhidhīyate. The devas seek the destruction of demons such as Bhaṇḍāsura and Mahiṣāsura, and She incarnates to remove their distress. Demons like Bhaṇḍāsura represent beings bound by ignorance; actions arising from ignorance and selfish aims take the form of hostile forces. Śrīdevī appears in different forms to free the devas from this bondage, so that they may perform their divine functions. This name, together with the previous one, describes Śrīdevī’s cit-prakāśa form, and the following names proceed to Her vimarśa form."],"searchText":"5 देवकार्यसमुद्यता देवानां कार्याणि देवकार्याणि। देवकार्याणां समुद्यता (शेषषष्ठ्या तदर्थं समुद्यता)। देव - devas, divine beings. कार्य - work, task, purpose. देवकार्य - the task or purpose of the devas. समुद्यता - risen, come forward, prepared, engaged. देवकार्यसमुद्यता - she who has come forward for the purpose of the devas. देवकार्यसमुद्यता means one who came forward to serve the devas. though śrīdevī is eternal, she assumes a particular form to help the devas accomplish their purpose. this is expressed in the verse: devānāṃ kāryasiddhyartham āvirbhavati sā yadā, utpanneti tadā loke sā nityāpy abhidhīyate. the devas seek the destruction of demons such as bhaṇḍāsura and mahiṣāsura, and she incarnates to remove their distress. demons like bhaṇḍāsura represent beings bound by ignorance; actions arising from ignorance and selfish aims take the form of hostile forces. śrīdevī appears in different forms to free the devas from this bondage, so that they may perform their divine functions. this name, together with the previous one, describes śrīdevī’s cit-prakāśa form, and the following names proceed to her vimarśa form. i. the true identity of the \"devas\" in the esoteric vocabulary of the agamas and upaniṣads, the word देव (deva) is derived from the root दिव् (div - to shine). the devakārya (task of the gods) is the liberation of these faculties from the tyrannical grip of भण्डासुर (bhaṇḍāsura, who represents cosmic limitation, ignorance, and the ego). she is samudyatā because her entire manifest nature is geared toward freeing the senses from bondage. ii. the dynamic architecture of grace (anugraha) the term समुद्यता signifies absolute readiness and immediate, active expression. she represents the kinetic projection of divine grace (anugraha-śakti) that actively intervenes in the cosmos to restore equilibrium whenever the individual soul cries out for liberation. iii. the resolution of śeṣa-ṣaṣṭhī by utilizing śeṣa-ṣaṣṭhī (\"the remaining genitive relations\"), the grammar implies that her relationship to the divine work is not an external chore or an accidental duty. the work is not separate from her essence; rather, the protection, evolution, and ultimate dissolution of the universe back into the absolute is her natural, spontaneous play (līlā).","esoteric":["I. The True Identity of the \"Devas\"","In the esoteric vocabulary of the Agamas and Upaniṣads, the word देव (Deva) is derived from the root दिव् (div - to shine). The Devakārya (task of the gods) is the liberation of these faculties from the tyrannical grip of भण्डासुर (Bhaṇḍāsura, who represents cosmic limitation, ignorance, and the ego). She is Samudyatā because Her entire manifest nature is geared toward freeing the senses from bondage.","II. The Dynamic Architecture of Grace (Anugraha)","The term समुद्यता signifies absolute readiness and immediate, active expression. She represents the kinetic projection of divine grace (Anugraha-śakti) that actively intervenes in the cosmos to restore equilibrium whenever the individual soul cries out for liberation.","III. The Resolution of Śeṣa-ṣaṣṭhī","By utilizing Śeṣa-ṣaṣṭhī (\"the remaining genitive relations\"), the grammar implies that Her relationship to the divine work is not an external chore or an accidental duty. The work is not separate from Her essence; rather, the protection, evolution, and ultimate dissolution of the universe back into the absolute is Her natural, spontaneous play (Līlā)."]},{"number":6,"name":"उद्यद्भानुसहस्राभा","samasa":["उद्यतां भानूनां सहस्रम् उद्यद्भानुसहस्रम्। तस्य आभया तुल्या आभा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["उद्यत् - rising.","भानु - sun.","सहस्र - thousand; also infinite or countless.","आभा - lustre, colour, splendour.","उद्यद्भानुसहस्राभा - She whose lustre is like that of thousands of rising suns."],"summary":["उद्यद्भानुसहस्राभा means Her lustre is equal to thousands of rising suns. The word sahasram also means infinite. Her lustre is equal to infinite rays of rising suns. The word sahasram can be attributed to “sun” or its “rays”. In that case, Her splendour can be equated to countless rising suns or countless rays of a rising sun. The word ābhā can be interpreted as “lustre” or “colour”. Śrīdevī is famous both for Her lustre and Her crimson colour. In the morning, the rising sun graciously reduces the intensity of the heat emanating from his light, just for us to see his cherry-coloured rays. Similarly, Śrīdevī is also of crimson colour. This colour itself is called aruṇa, one of the names of the Sun himself. Every mood or character has a colour. The colour of kindness or graciousness is crimson. The forthcoming names seek to detail three more forms, namely the sthūla, sūkṣma, and param forms."],"searchText":"6 उद्यद्भानुसहस्राभा उद्यतां भानूनां सहस्रम् उद्यद्भानुसहस्रम्। तस्य आभया तुल्या आभा यस्याः सा। उद्यत् - rising. भानु - sun. सहस्र - thousand; also infinite or countless. आभा - lustre, colour, splendour. उद्यद्भानुसहस्राभा - she whose lustre is like that of thousands of rising suns. उद्यद्भानुसहस्राभा means her lustre is equal to thousands of rising suns. the word sahasram also means infinite. her lustre is equal to infinite rays of rising suns. the word sahasram can be attributed to “sun” or its “rays”. in that case, her splendour can be equated to countless rising suns or countless rays of a rising sun. the word ābhā can be interpreted as “lustre” or “colour”. śrīdevī is famous both for her lustre and her crimson colour. in the morning, the rising sun graciously reduces the intensity of the heat emanating from his light, just for us to see his cherry-coloured rays. similarly, śrīdevī is also of crimson colour. this colour itself is called aruṇa, one of the names of the sun himself. every mood or character has a colour. the colour of kindness or graciousness is crimson. the forthcoming names seek to detail three more forms, namely the sthūla, sūkṣma, and param forms. i. the dynamic spanda of consciousness unlike a static sun sitting at its zenith, उद्यताम् signifies the precise moment of dawning—the transition from darkness to absolute illumination. in mantra-śāstra, this represents स्पन्द (spanda), the initial throb or kinetic leap of consciousness as it moves from the unmanifest (prakāśa) to manifest awareness (vimarśa). she is not merely light; she is the dynamic, active dawning of absolute reality within the practitioner's consciousness. ii. the dissolution of mental obscurity a single sun removes the darkness of the external world, but it leaves shadows. the imagery of a thousand rising suns shining simultaneously means there is no possibility of a shadow anywhere in the cosmos. this represents the total, instantaneous destruction of मूलाविद्या (mūlāvidyā, root cosmic ignorance). when her light dawns in the dahara-ākāśa (the inner space of the heart), the illusion of division is instantly incinerated by the uniform red glow of non-dual awareness. iii. the radiance of the kāmakalā the intense red luster of the rising suns specifically encrypts the red seed-potency of the śrī vidyā triad. the infinite rays are the letters of the alphabet (mātṛkās) spreading outward to construct the universe, all anchored in her singular, self-luminous essence.","esoteric":["I. The Dynamic Spanda of Consciousness","Unlike a static sun sitting at its zenith, उद्यताम् signifies the precise moment of dawning—the transition from darkness to absolute illumination. In Mantra-Śāstra, this represents स्पन्द (Spanda), the initial throb or kinetic leap of consciousness as it moves from the unmanifest (Prakāśa) to manifest awareness (Vimarśa). She is not merely light; She is the dynamic, active dawning of absolute reality within the practitioner's consciousness.","II. The Dissolution of Mental Obscurity","A single sun removes the darkness of the external world, but it leaves shadows. The imagery of a thousand rising suns shining simultaneously means there is no possibility of a shadow anywhere in the cosmos. this represents the total, instantaneous destruction of मूलाविद्या (mūlāvidyā, root cosmic ignorance). When Her light dawns in the Dahara-ākāśa (the inner space of the heart), the illusion of division is instantly incinerated by the uniform red glow of non-dual awareness.","III. The Radiance of the Kāmakalā","The intense red luster of the rising suns specifically encrypts the red seed-potency of the Śrī Vidyā triad. The infinite rays are the letters of the alphabet (Mātṛkās) spreading outward to construct the universe, all anchored in Her singular, self-luminous essence."]},{"number":7,"name":"चतुर्बाहुसमन्विता","samasa":["चतुर्भिः बाहुभिः समन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["चतुर्भिः - with four.","बाहुभिः - arms, hands.","समन्विता - endowed with, possessed of.","चतुर्बाहुसमन्विता - She who is endowed with four arms."],"summary":["चतुर्बाहुसमन्विता means one with four hands. Śrīdevī has four hands — two from each shoulder in front and back. The four hands only have been indicated in the forms usually contemplated during meditation. Hands come first and foremost whenever we try to concentrate on the form mentioned in the dhyāna śloka (meditation verse). The four Devīs who are the commandants of Śrīdevī's army, namely Aśvārūḍhā, Sampatkarī, Mantriṇī and Vārāhī, may be deemed to be the four hands of Śrīdevī. The mantras pertaining to the above four Devīs are indicated by this name. The dhyāna verse of this sahasranāma mentions only two hands for Śrīdevī.Mention was made about the four hands and followed by the weapons carried in these four hands."],"searchText":"7 चतुर्बाहुसमन्विता चतुर्भिः बाहुभिः समन्विता। चतुर्भिः - with four. बाहुभिः - arms, hands. समन्विता - endowed with, possessed of. चतुर्बाहुसमन्विता - she who is endowed with four arms. चतुर्बाहुसमन्विता means one with four hands. śrīdevī has four hands — two from each shoulder in front and back. the four hands only have been indicated in the forms usually contemplated during meditation. hands come first and foremost whenever we try to concentrate on the form mentioned in the dhyāna śloka (meditation verse). the four devīs who are the commandants of śrīdevī's army, namely aśvārūḍhā, sampatkarī, mantriṇī and vārāhī, may be deemed to be the four hands of śrīdevī. the mantras pertaining to the above four devīs are indicated by this name. the dhyāna verse of this sahasranāma mentions only two hands for śrīdevī.mention was made about the four hands and followed by the weapons carried in these four hands. i. the mastery over the antaḥkaraṇa (internal organs) the four faculties: मनस् (manas - the deliberating mind), बुद्धि (buddhi - the decisive intellect), चित्त (citta - the memory/retentive consciousness), and अहङ्कार (ahaṅkāra - the ego-sense). by being perfectly integrated with these four arms, she signifies that the individual human psyche is merely a limited reflection of her four cosmic vectors of awareness. she holds absolute command over the psychological mechanism of every living being. ii. the structural anchors of the śrī cakra in the ritual mapping of the śrī cakra, the four arms correspond directly to the weapons she wields, which occupy specific spatial directions in the central chamber (bindu-cakra). the arms represent the deployment of her primordial cosmic energies: इच्छा (icchā - will), ज्ञान (jñāna - knowledge), and क्रिया (kriyā - action). the four arms represent the four standard paths of vedic revelation (the four vedas) and the four absolute states of consciousness (jāgrat, svapna, suṣupti, and turīya), showing that she encompasses both the transactional states of experience and the transcendent reality. iii. the resolution of samanvitā the prefix सम् (sam) implies perfection and absolute equilibrium, while अन्विता (anvitā) implies an inseparable, intrinsic connection (anvaya). these four arms are not accidental appendages attached to her form; they are the natural, spontaneous structural expansions of her non-dual essence as she projects outward from the unmanifest point into cosmic play (līlā).","esoteric":["I. The Mastery Over the Antaḥkaraṇa (Internal Organs)","The Four Faculties: मनस् (Manas - the deliberating mind), बुद्धि (Buddhi - the decisive intellect), चित्त (Citta - the memory/retentive consciousness), and अहङ्कार (Ahaṅkāra - the ego-sense).","By being perfectly integrated with these four arms, She signifies that the individual human psyche is merely a limited reflection of Her four cosmic vectors of awareness. She holds absolute command over the psychological mechanism of every living being.","II. The Structural Anchors of the Śrī Cakra","In the ritual mapping of the Śrī Cakra, the four arms correspond directly to the weapons She wields, which occupy specific spatial directions in the central chamber (Bindu-cakra).","The arms represent the deployment of Her primordial cosmic energies: इच्छा (Icchā - Will), ज्ञान (Jñāna - Knowledge), and क्रिया (Kriyā - Action).","The four arms represent the four standard paths of Vedic revelation (the four Vedas) and the four absolute states of consciousness (Jāgrat, Svapna, Suṣupti, and Turīya), showing that She encompasses both the transactional states of experience and the transcendent reality.","III. The Resolution of Samanvitā","The prefix सम् (sam) implies perfection and absolute equilibrium, while अन्विता (anvitā) implies an inseparable, intrinsic connection (anvaya). these four arms are not accidental appendages attached to Her form; they are the natural, spontaneous structural expansions of Her non-dual essence as She projects outward from the unmanifest point into cosmic play (Līlā)."]},{"number":8,"name":"रागस्वरूपपाशाढ्या","samasa":["राग एव स्वं रूपः यस्य पाशस्य सः रागस्वरूपपाशः। तेन आढ्या।"],"wordByWord":["राग - attachment, desire, love.","स्वरूप - own form, essential nature.","पाश - noose, rope, bond.","आढ्या - endowed with, rich in, furnished with.","रागस्वरूपपाशाढ्या - She who is furnished with the noose whose very form is desire."],"summary":["रागस्वरूपपाशाढ्या means one who carries the weapon of desire in the form of a noose. A noose is a rope thrown to tie and drag something. Śrīdevī is holding both the ends of the noose in one hand. It is in the sthūla form in Her rear left arm. The presiding deity is Aśvārūḍhā. Rāga and anurāga are the two features of mind — wish and desire. This is the vāsanā form of the weapon noose. This form has the twin opposite characters namely love and hatred. Vāsanā is the effect of the deeds of previous births of jīva. In the hands of Śrīdevī these take the form of icchā śakti and jñāna śakti. The noose helps us to round up and drag a distant object to oneself. We will be able to do this only if both the ends of the noose are under our control. Śrīdevī holds both the ends of the noose in Her hand. This indicates that \"our wishes will get fulfilled automatically by Her grace.\""],"searchText":"8 रागस्वरूपपाशाढ्या राग एव स्वं रूपः यस्य पाशस्य सः रागस्वरूपपाशः। तेन आढ्या। राग - attachment, desire, love. स्वरूप - own form, essential nature. पाश - noose, rope, bond. आढ्या - endowed with, rich in, furnished with. रागस्वरूपपाशाढ्या - she who is furnished with the noose whose very form is desire. रागस्वरूपपाशाढ्या means one who carries the weapon of desire in the form of a noose. a noose is a rope thrown to tie and drag something. śrīdevī is holding both the ends of the noose in one hand. it is in the sthūla form in her rear left arm. the presiding deity is aśvārūḍhā. rāga and anurāga are the two features of mind — wish and desire. this is the vāsanā form of the weapon noose. this form has the twin opposite characters namely love and hatred. vāsanā is the effect of the deeds of previous births of jīva. in the hands of śrīdevī these take the form of icchā śakti and jñāna śakti. the noose helps us to round up and drag a distant object to oneself. we will be able to do this only if both the ends of the noose are under our control. śrīdevī holds both the ends of the noose in her hand. this indicates that \"our wishes will get fulfilled automatically by her grace.\" i. the transmutation of rāga (desire) for ordinary bound souls (jīvas), rāga is an afflictive mental modification (kleśa) that binds them tightly to the objective wheel of births and deaths. when this same power belongs to the divine mother, it is इच्छाशक्ति (icchā-śakti—the primordial will of the absolute). it is the pure, cosmic desire to manifest, play, and ultimately reclaim all projected beings. by holding this noose, she demonstrates that she controls the very fabric of cosmic attraction. ii. the noose as the gravity of grace linguistically, a noose catches, pulls, and restrains an object that is moving away. her noose represents the inward-pulling gravity of her divine grace (anugraha). when the practitioner's mind wanders outward into the multi-colored illusions of the world, her pāśa catches the outward-bound consciousness and pulls it firmly back toward the silent center—the bindu. iii. the structural placement in worshipping the śrī cakra this weapon is held in her lower-left hand and is structurally related to the element of space and sound. in the ritual meditation (dhyāna), the sādhaka visualizes this noose not as a rope of bondage, but as a radiant, loop of absolute crimson light that represents the ultimate beauty and captivating power of the self (ātma-rati).","esoteric":["I. The Transmutation of Rāga (Desire)","For ordinary bound souls (jīvas), rāga is an afflictive mental modification (kleśa) that binds them tightly to the objective wheel of births and deaths. When this same power belongs to the Divine Mother, it is इच्छाशक्ति (Icchā-śakti—the primordial Will of the Absolute). It is the pure, cosmic desire to manifest, play, and ultimately reclaim all projected beings. By holding this noose, She demonstrates that She controls the very fabric of cosmic attraction.","II. The Noose as the Gravity of Grace","Linguistically, a noose catches, pulls, and restrains an object that is moving away. Her noose represents the inward-pulling gravity of Her divine grace (anugraha). When the practitioner's mind wanders outward into the multi-colored illusions of the world, Her pāśa catches the outward-bound consciousness and pulls it firmly back toward the silent center—the Bindu.","III. The Structural Placement in Worshipping the Śrī Cakra","this weapon is held in Her lower-left hand and is structurally related to the element of space and sound. In the ritual meditation (dhyāna), the Sādhaka visualizes this noose not as a rope of bondage, but as a radiant, loop of absolute crimson light that represents the ultimate beauty and captivating power of the Self (Ātma-rati)."]},{"number":9,"name":"क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशोज्ज्वला","samasa":["क्रोधस्य आकार इव आकारः यस्य अङ्कुशस्य सः क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशः। तेन उज्ज्वला।"],"wordByWord":["क्रोध - anger.","आकार - form, shape; also knowledge as the form taken by the mind.","अङ्कुश - goad, elephant-hook.","उज्ज्वला - shining, resplendent.","क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशोज्ज्वला - She who shines with the goad whose form is anger."],"summary":["क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशोज्ज्वला means Her lustre is enhanced by holding the goad symbolising anger. Goad is a pointed weapon used by a mahout to control an elephant. It has a sharp edge. Elephant is one of the biggest and strongest among all animals. It is extremely difficult to control a rogue elephant. Goad is the only weapon which can control it. In the hands of Śrīdevī it is in a sthūla form. Its vāsanā form is anger. If the mind is not able to get what it wants or does not derive the satisfaction expected out of it, the mental reaction is anger. It is symbolised by the lustrous goad worn by Śrīdevī. Krodhākārāṅkuśam can be interpreted in two ways — (1) goad in the form of anger or (2) anger and ākāra, knowledge. How is ākāra interpreted as knowledge? When we see an object through our eyes, our mind recognises and takes the \"form\" of that object — that is ākāra. If we see a book, our mind recognises the form of the book and becomes that form itself."],"searchText":"9 क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशोज्ज्वला क्रोधस्य आकार इव आकारः यस्य अङ्कुशस्य सः क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशः। तेन उज्ज्वला। क्रोध - anger. आकार - form, shape; also knowledge as the form taken by the mind. अङ्कुश - goad, elephant-hook. उज्ज्वला - shining, resplendent. क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशोज्ज्वला - she who shines with the goad whose form is anger. क्रोधाकाराङ्कुशोज्ज्वला means her lustre is enhanced by holding the goad symbolising anger. goad is a pointed weapon used by a mahout to control an elephant. it has a sharp edge. elephant is one of the biggest and strongest among all animals. it is extremely difficult to control a rogue elephant. goad is the only weapon which can control it. in the hands of śrīdevī it is in a sthūla form. its vāsanā form is anger. if the mind is not able to get what it wants or does not derive the satisfaction expected out of it, the mental reaction is anger. it is symbolised by the lustrous goad worn by śrīdevī. krodhākārāṅkuśam can be interpreted in two ways — (1) goad in the form of anger or (2) anger and ākāra, knowledge. how is ākāra interpreted as knowledge? when we see an object through our eyes, our mind recognises and takes the \"form\" of that object — that is ākāra. if we see a book, our mind recognises the form of the book and becomes that form itself. * **the power of restraint:** while anger in ordinary mortals is a binding mental modification, in her hands, the goad represents the power of **ज्ञानशक्ति** (*jñāna-śakti* — the power of pure discernment). * **cosmic correction:** just as a goad keeps an elephant on the right track, her goad reins in the outward-bound senses, stopping the mental fluctuations and redirecting the mind toward inner absorption (*samādhi*).","esoteric":["* **The Power of Restraint:** While anger in ordinary mortals is a binding mental modification, in Her hands, the goad represents the power of **ज्ञानशक्ति** (*Jñāna-śakti* — the power of pure discernment).","* **Cosmic Correction:** Just as a goad keeps an elephant on the right track, Her goad reins in the outward-bound senses, stopping the mental fluctuations and redirecting the mind toward inner absorption (*Samādhi*)."]},{"number":10,"name":"मनोरूपेक्षुकोदण्डा","samasa":["मन एव रूपं यस्य इक्षोः सः मनोरूपेक्षुः। इक्षुमयं कोदण्डं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मनस् - mind.","रूप - form.","इक्षु - sugarcane.","कोदण्ड - bow.","मनोरूपेक्षु - sugarcane whose form is mind.","मनोरूपेक्षुकोदण्डा - She who bears the sugarcane bow whose form is mind."],"summary":["मनोरूपेक्षुकोदण्डा means She dons a bow made of sugarcane — the physical form of \"mind\". Śrīdevī has in her left forearm a bow made of sugarcane. Its symbolic form is the mind. Its presiding deity is Mantriṇī. The action of the mind executed through the five organs is to take the form of the object seen and realise that \"I see the object\", \"This can give me pleasure\", \"I desire to get this object\", \"This gives me sorrow and hence I should avoid it\" and the like. This is called saṅkalpa. At the same time the thought \"Is this object suitable for me or not\", \"Should I try to get it or not\", and the like are called vikalpa. The action of the mind is of these two types. This mind takes the form of sugarcane bow in the hands of Śrīdevī. In general a bow is made up of completely dry bamboo slats and is capable of being bent and unbent. Sugarcane is full of moisture; Sugarcane bow is a weapon, though it is sweet; again it is sweet though it is a weapon."],"searchText":"10 मनोरूपेक्षुकोदण्डा मन एव रूपं यस्य इक्षोः सः मनोरूपेक्षुः। इक्षुमयं कोदण्डं यस्याः सा। मनस् - mind. रूप - form. इक्षु - sugarcane. कोदण्ड - bow. मनोरूपेक्षु - sugarcane whose form is mind. मनोरूपेक्षुकोदण्डा - she who bears the sugarcane bow whose form is mind. मनोरूपेक्षुकोदण्डा means she dons a bow made of sugarcane — the physical form of \"mind\". śrīdevī has in her left forearm a bow made of sugarcane. its symbolic form is the mind. its presiding deity is mantriṇī. the action of the mind executed through the five organs is to take the form of the object seen and realise that \"i see the object\", \"this can give me pleasure\", \"i desire to get this object\", \"this gives me sorrow and hence i should avoid it\" and the like. this is called saṅkalpa. at the same time the thought \"is this object suitable for me or not\", \"should i try to get it or not\", and the like are called vikalpa. the action of the mind is of these two types. this mind takes the form of sugarcane bow in the hands of śrīdevī. in general a bow is made up of completely dry bamboo slats and is capable of being bent and unbent. sugarcane is full of moisture; sugarcane bow is a weapon, though it is sweet; again it is sweet though it is a weapon. the sugarcane bow represents **मनस्** (*manas*), the choosing and doubting mind. * **the sweetness of the mind:** sugarcane must be crushed and processed to yield its sweet juice; similarly, the mind must be systematically refined through spiritual discipline to experience its inherent, nectarine bliss (*svātmānanda*). * **the seat of kriyā-śakti:** because she holds the mind as an instrument (*kodaṇḍa*), she proves that the cosmic mind is entirely under her command as **क्रियाशक्ति** (*kriyā-śakti* — the power of action).","esoteric":["the sugarcane bow represents **मनस्** (*Manas*), the choosing and doubting mind.","* **The Sweetness of the Mind:** Sugarcane must be crushed and processed to yield its sweet juice; similarly, the mind must be systematically refined through spiritual discipline to experience its inherent, nectarine bliss (*Svātmānanda*).","* **The Seat of Kriyā-śakti:** Because She holds the mind as an instrument (*kodaṇḍa*), She proves that the cosmic mind is entirely under Her command as **क्रियाशक्ति** (*Kriyā-śakti* — the power of action)."]},{"number":11,"name":"पञ्चतन्मात्रसायका","samasa":["पञ्च तन्मात्राणि एव सायकाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्च - five.","तन्मात्राणि - subtle sense-elements; sound, touch, form/colour, taste, smell.","सायकाः - arrows.","पञ्चतन्मात्रसायका - She whose arrows are the five tanmatras."],"summary":["पञ्चतन्मात्रसायका means one who has five characteristics as arrows. In Her physical form, Śrīdevī has five flowers as arrows in Her right forearm namely Lotus, Red Lotus, Red Lily, Red Jasmine and Mango flower. The characteristics of these arrows are the effect they make on the objects attacked by them namely to induce happiness, to give taste, to enthrall, to dry out and to kill. The presiding deity of these arrows is Vārāhī also known as Daṇḍanātha. The secret form of these arrows is the five self-characteristics (tanmātras). These characteristics are the unique features of the five elements, which constitute the physical earth. Elements (bhūtas) and Self-Characteristics (tanmātras): Space (ākāśa) — Sound (śabda); Wind / Air (vāyu) — Sense of touch (sparśa); Fire (agni) — Form / Colour (rūpa); Water (jala) — Taste (rasa); Earth (pṛthvī) — Odour (gandha). These characteristics stand alone only in the very intricate and atomic state of the elements. The Universe, we perceive is the composite form of these elements and hence each element cannot be perceived separately."],"searchText":"11 पञ्चतन्मात्रसायका पञ्च तन्मात्राणि एव सायकाः यस्याः सा। पञ्च - five. तन्मात्राणि - subtle sense-elements; sound, touch, form/colour, taste, smell. सायकाः - arrows. पञ्चतन्मात्रसायका - she whose arrows are the five tanmatras. पञ्चतन्मात्रसायका means one who has five characteristics as arrows. in her physical form, śrīdevī has five flowers as arrows in her right forearm namely lotus, red lotus, red lily, red jasmine and mango flower. the characteristics of these arrows are the effect they make on the objects attacked by them namely to induce happiness, to give taste, to enthrall, to dry out and to kill. the presiding deity of these arrows is vārāhī also known as daṇḍanātha. the secret form of these arrows is the five self-characteristics (tanmātras). these characteristics are the unique features of the five elements, which constitute the physical earth. elements (bhūtas) and self-characteristics (tanmātras): space (ākāśa) — sound (śabda); wind / air (vāyu) — sense of touch (sparśa); fire (agni) — form / colour (rūpa); water (jala) — taste (rasa); earth (pṛthvī) — odour (gandha). these characteristics stand alone only in the very intricate and atomic state of the elements. the universe, we perceive is the composite form of these elements and hence each element cannot be perceived separately. the five floral arrows are the five *tanmātras*: sound (*śabda*), touch (*sparśa*), form (*rūpa*), taste (*rasa*), and smell (*gandha*). * **dissolution of sensory leakage:** usually, these five elements pull human attention outward into physical attachment. when she shoots these floral arrows into the practitioner's heart, they pierce the outer sensory layer and dissolve objective experience, returning the senses to their pure, uncompounded state within consciousness.","esoteric":["The five floral arrows are the five *Tanmātras*: sound (*śabda*), touch (*sparśa*), form (*rūpa*), taste (*rasa*), and smell (*gandha*).","* **Dissolution of Sensory Leakage:** Usually, these five elements pull human attention outward into physical attachment. When She shoots these floral arrows into the practitioner's heart, they pierce the outer sensory layer and dissolve objective experience, returning the senses to their pure, uncompounded state within consciousness."]},{"number":12,"name":"निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जद्ब्रह्माण्डमण्डला","samasa":["निजः (स्वकीयः) यः अरुणप्रभायाः पूरः निजारुणप्रभापूरः।","तस्मिन् मज्जन्तीति निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जानि।","तेषामेव ब्रह्माण्डानां मण्डलानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निज - own, natural.","अरुण - red, crimson.","प्रभा - lustre, light.","पूर - flood, fullness, flow.","मज्जत् - sinking, immersed.","ब्रह्माण्ड - universe, cosmic egg, galaxy.","मण्डल - sphere, zone, circle.","निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जद्ब्रह्माण्डमण्डला - She in whose own crimson lustre the spheres of universes are immersed."],"summary":["निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जद्ब्रह्माण्डमण्डला means one who immerses the zones of galaxy by the flow of Her lustre. Our Earth, space and the stellar zone constitute one galaxy (brahmāṇḍam). Universe (brahmāṇḍamaṇḍalam) consists of millions of such galaxies. Śrīdevī sinks this entire universe in Her red lustre. Again the red lustre alone shines immersing them all. The physical form of Śrīdevī's red lustre is described in the ensuing names. This description starts from Her hair and ends in Her feet."],"searchText":"12 निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जद्ब्रह्माण्डमण्डला निजः (स्वकीयः) यः अरुणप्रभायाः पूरः निजारुणप्रभापूरः। तस्मिन् मज्जन्तीति निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जानि। तेषामेव ब्रह्माण्डानां मण्डलानि यस्याः सा। निज - own, natural. अरुण - red, crimson. प्रभा - lustre, light. पूर - flood, fullness, flow. मज्जत् - sinking, immersed. ब्रह्माण्ड - universe, cosmic egg, galaxy. मण्डल - sphere, zone, circle. निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जद्ब्रह्माण्डमण्डला - she in whose own crimson lustre the spheres of universes are immersed. निजारुणप्रभापूरमज्जद्ब्रह्माण्डमण्डला means one who immerses the zones of galaxy by the flow of her lustre. our earth, space and the stellar zone constitute one galaxy (brahmāṇḍam). universe (brahmāṇḍamaṇḍalam) consists of millions of such galaxies. śrīdevī sinks this entire universe in her red lustre. again the red lustre alone shines immersing them all. the physical form of śrīdevī's red lustre is described in the ensuing names. this description starts from her hair and ends in her feet. this name proves *advaita-vāda* (non-duality) and the primacy of *shakti*: * **the red flood of vimarśa:** the red glow represents **विमर्श** (*vimarśa* — self-reflective consciousness). the universe is not a dry, external entity sitting apart from her. it is entirely suspended, sustained, and dissolved (*majjat*) inside her infinite, self-luminous red light of awareness.","esoteric":["This name proves *Advaita-vāda* (non-duality) and the primacy of *Shakti*:","* **The Red Flood of Vimarśa:** The red glow represents **विमर्श** (*Vimarśa* — self-reflective consciousness). The universe is not a dry, external entity sitting apart from Her. It is entirely suspended, sustained, and dissolved (*majjat*) inside Her infinite, self-luminous red light of awareness."]},{"number":13,"name":"चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागसौगन्धिकलसत्कचा","samasa":["चम्पकानि च अशोकाश्च पुन्नागाश्च चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागाः।","तैः लसन्तः कचाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["चम्पक - champaka / magnolia flower.","अशोक - ashoka flower.","पुन्नाग - punnaga flower.","सौगन्धिक - fragrant, red lotus / fragrant flower.","लसत् - shining, bedecked, adorned.","कचा - hair.","चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागसौगन्धिकलसत्कचा - She whose hair shines adorned with fragrant flowers such as Champaka, Ashoka, Punnaga and Red Lotus."],"summary":["चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागसौगन्धिकलसत्कचा means one who has beautiful hair studded with Magnolia, Aśoka, Rhizophora mucronata (punnāga) and Red Lotus flowers. It is Śrīdevī's hair bedecked with flowers, which emerges first out of the sacrificial fire; hence the description of the Śrīdevī's physical form commences with the hair. The first part of Her mantra is equated with Her face. Thus the description starts with the hair."],"searchText":"13 चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागसौगन्धिकलसत्कचा चम्पकानि च अशोकाश्च पुन्नागाश्च चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागाः। तैः लसन्तः कचाः यस्याः सा। चम्पक - champaka / magnolia flower. अशोक - ashoka flower. पुन्नाग - punnaga flower. सौगन्धिक - fragrant, red lotus / fragrant flower. लसत् - shining, bedecked, adorned. कचा - hair. चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागसौगन्धिकलसत्कचा - she whose hair shines adorned with fragrant flowers such as champaka, ashoka, punnaga and red lotus. चम्पकाशोकपुन्नागसौगन्धिकलसत्कचा means one who has beautiful hair studded with magnolia, aśoka, rhizophora mucronata (punnāga) and red lotus flowers. it is śrīdevī's hair bedecked with flowers, which emerges first out of the sacrificial fire; hence the description of the śrīdevī's physical form commences with the hair. the first part of her mantra is equated with her face. thus the description starts with the hair. this name initiates the *keśādi-pāda-varṇana* (head-to-toe description) of the devi. * **esoteric hair as chidākāśa:** the dark, dense tresses (*kaca*) represent the unmanifest primordial cosmic space (*chidākāśa*). the shining, fragrant flowers represent the active, manifest seeds of spiritual wisdom and virtue blossoming within the crown chakra (**सहस्रार** — *sahasrāra*).","esoteric":["This name initiates the *Keśādi-pāda-varṇana* (head-to-toe description) of the Devi.","* **Esoteric Hair as Chidākāśa:** The dark, dense tresses (*kaca*) represent the unmanifest primordial cosmic space (*Chidākāśa*). The shining, fragrant flowers represent the active, manifest seeds of spiritual wisdom and virtue blossoming within the crown chakra (**सहस्रार** — *Sahasrāra*)."]},{"number":14,"name":"कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरमण्डिता","samasa":["कुरुविन्दमणीनां श्रेणी कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणी।","तया कनत् (दीप्यमानः) कोटीरः (मुकुटः) कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरः।","तेन मण्डिता।"],"wordByWord":["कुरुविन्दमणि - ruby gemstone.","श्रेणी - row, string, series.","कनत् - shining, glittering.","कोटीर - crown.","मण्डिता - adorned.","कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरमण्डिता - She who is adorned with a crown glittering with rows of ruby stones."],"summary":["कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरमण्डिता means one whose crown is adorned with rows of kuruvinda rubies. Śrīdevī's crown is studded with a string of Rubies. Adorning of rubies will result in fulfillment of desires. Attachment will be created to good things; desire, affection, welfare and devotion to Śrī Viṣṇu also. Śrīdevī's crown is of koṭīra model. This is a particular design, which does not hide beauty of the hair as well as the flowers adorned. The crowns worn by men will hide the hair and is called makuṭa, mukuṭa or kirīṭa. The red rubies match the red lustre of Śrīdevī's body. Meditation of Śrīdevī's face with the crown will increase the devotion."],"searchText":"14 कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरमण्डिता कुरुविन्दमणीनां श्रेणी कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणी। तया कनत् (दीप्यमानः) कोटीरः (मुकुटः) कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरः। तेन मण्डिता। कुरुविन्दमणि - ruby gemstone. श्रेणी - row, string, series. कनत् - shining, glittering. कोटीर - crown. मण्डिता - adorned. कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरमण्डिता - she who is adorned with a crown glittering with rows of ruby stones. कुरुविन्दमणिश्रेणीकनत्कोटीरमण्डिता means one whose crown is adorned with rows of kuruvinda rubies. śrīdevī's crown is studded with a string of rubies. adorning of rubies will result in fulfillment of desires. attachment will be created to good things; desire, affection, welfare and devotion to śrī viṣṇu also. śrīdevī's crown is of koṭīra model. this is a particular design, which does not hide beauty of the hair as well as the flowers adorned. the crowns worn by men will hide the hair and is called makuṭa, mukuṭa or kirīṭa. the red rubies match the red lustre of śrīdevī's body. meditation of śrīdevī's face with the crown will increase the devotion. * **sovereignty of the unmanī:** *kuruvinda* denotes a rare class of crimson ruby. the crown (*koṭīra*) sits above the head, symbolizing the transcendent state above the sahasrāra—known as **उन्मनी** (*unmanī*) or the state of pure, non-dual sovereignty over all creation.","esoteric":["* **Sovereignty of the Unmanī:** *Kuruvinda* denotes a rare class of crimson ruby. The crown (*koṭīra*) sits above the head, symbolizing the transcendent state above the Sahasrāra—known as **उन्मनी** (*unmanī*) or the state of pure, non-dual sovereignty over all creation."]},{"number":15,"name":"अष्टमीचन्द्रविभ्राजदलिकस्थलशोभिता","samasa":["अष्टम्यां चन्द्रः अष्टमीचन्द्रः।","अलिकस्य (ललाटस्य) स्थलम् अलिकस्थलम्।","अष्टमीचन्द्रेण इव विभ्राजता अलिकस्थलेन शोभिता।"],"wordByWord":["अष्टमी - eighth lunar day.","चन्द्र - moon.","विभ्राजत् - shining brilliantly.","अलिकस्थल - forehead.","शोभिता - beautified, made splendid.","अष्टमीचन्द्रविभ्राजदलिकस्थलशोभिता - She whose forehead shines like the moon of the eighth lunar day."],"summary":["अष्टमीचन्द्रविभ्राजदलिकस्थलशोभिता means one whose forehead shines like the Moon on the eighth day of lunar half month. Of the fifteen phases of the moon, on the eighth day of bright lunar half month the eighth phase will be seen. Or reduced up to eight phases on the eighth day of the lunar dark half month and moon will be visible as a semicircle. In the emerging form of Śrīdevī from the sacrificial fire, the crown, hair and flowers come out one after the other and the forehead emerges as an inverted semicircle resembling the eighth day moon, with flawless cool light. This can be compared to 46th verse of Saundaryalaharī starting with lalāṭaṃ lāvaṇyadvitīṃ vimalābhāti."],"searchText":"15 अष्टमीचन्द्रविभ्राजदलिकस्थलशोभिता अष्टम्यां चन्द्रः अष्टमीचन्द्रः। अलिकस्य (ललाटस्य) स्थलम् अलिकस्थलम्। अष्टमीचन्द्रेण इव विभ्राजता अलिकस्थलेन शोभिता। अष्टमी - eighth lunar day. चन्द्र - moon. विभ्राजत् - shining brilliantly. अलिकस्थल - forehead. शोभिता - beautified, made splendid. अष्टमीचन्द्रविभ्राजदलिकस्थलशोभिता - she whose forehead shines like the moon of the eighth lunar day. अष्टमीचन्द्रविभ्राजदलिकस्थलशोभिता means one whose forehead shines like the moon on the eighth day of lunar half month. of the fifteen phases of the moon, on the eighth day of bright lunar half month the eighth phase will be seen. or reduced up to eight phases on the eighth day of the lunar dark half month and moon will be visible as a semicircle. in the emerging form of śrīdevī from the sacrificial fire, the crown, hair and flowers come out one after the other and the forehead emerges as an inverted semicircle resembling the eighth day moon, with flawless cool light. this can be compared to 46th verse of saundaryalaharī starting with lalāṭaṃ lāvaṇyadvitīṃ vimalābhāti. * **the light of the ājñā:** the eighth-day moon is a perfect, balanced semi-circle. the forehead represents the seat of the **आज्ञा चक्र** (*ājñā cakra*), the gateway of intuitive knowledge. it represents the *kāmakaḷā* structure, wherein the crescent moon represents the upper dynamic arc holding the equilibrium of shiva and shakti.","esoteric":["* **The Light of the Ājñā:** The eighth-day moon is a perfect, balanced semi-circle. The forehead represents the seat of the **आज्ञा चक्र** (*Ājñā Cakra*), the gateway of intuitive knowledge. It represents the *Kāmakaḷā* structure, wherein the crescent moon represents the upper dynamic arc holding the equilibrium of Shiva and Shakti."]},{"number":16,"name":"मुखचन्द्रकलङ्काभमृगनाभिविशेषका","samasa":["मुखम् एव चन्द्र इति रूपकं तत्कलङ्कत्वेन तुल्यः मृगनाभेः (कस्तूर्याः) विशेषकः (तिलकः) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मुख - face.","चन्द्र - moon.","कलङ्क - dark mark, spot.","आभ - resembling.","मृगनाभि - musk.","विशेषक - tilaka, decorative mark.","मुखचन्द्रकलङ्काभमृगनाभिविशेषका - She whose musk tilaka resembles the dark mark on the moon-like face."],"summary":["मुखचन्द्रकलङ्काभमृगनाभिविशेषका means the bindi (musk dot) on the forehead of Śrīdevī resembles the black spot on the surface of the Moon and it further beautifies the face. It is a literary tradition to consider the black spot on the moon as a stain on the life of the Moon god. The Moon is sometimes described as mṛgāṅka, as the stain looks like a deer and as śaśāṅka as the stain also looks like a rabbit. When Śrīdevī's forehead is described as a semicircular Moon (crescent), there is no stain, but the musk spot beautifies the face."],"searchText":"16 मुखचन्द्रकलङ्काभमृगनाभिविशेषका मुखम् एव चन्द्र इति रूपकं तत्कलङ्कत्वेन तुल्यः मृगनाभेः (कस्तूर्याः) विशेषकः (तिलकः) यस्याः सा। मुख - face. चन्द्र - moon. कलङ्क - dark mark, spot. आभ - resembling. मृगनाभि - musk. विशेषक - tilaka, decorative mark. मुखचन्द्रकलङ्काभमृगनाभिविशेषका - she whose musk tilaka resembles the dark mark on the moon-like face. मुखचन्द्रकलङ्काभमृगनाभिविशेषका means the bindi (musk dot) on the forehead of śrīdevī resembles the black spot on the surface of the moon and it further beautifies the face. it is a literary tradition to consider the black spot on the moon as a stain on the life of the moon god. the moon is sometimes described as mṛgāṅka, as the stain looks like a deer and as śaśāṅka as the stain also looks like a rabbit. when śrīdevī's forehead is described as a semicircular moon (crescent), there is no stain, but the musk spot beautifies the face. * **māyā as an ornament:** the dark spot on the moon is traditionally a flaw, but on the face of consciousness (the devi), the black musk mark (*tilaka*) increases her beauty. this represents **माया** (*māyā*). to the bound soul, *māyā* is a blemish of ignorance; but to the devi, it is a mere decorative ornament of her creative play (*līlā*), entirely under her sovereignty.","esoteric":["* **Māyā as an Ornament:** The dark spot on the moon is traditionally a flaw, but on the face of consciousness (the Devi), the black musk mark (*tilaka*) increases Her beauty. This represents **माया** (*Māyā*). To the bound soul, *Māyā* is a blemish of ignorance; but to the Devi, it is a mere decorative ornament of Her creative play (*Līlā*), entirely under Her sovereignty."]},{"number":17,"name":"वदनस्मरमाङ्गल्यगृहतोरणचिल्लिका","samasa":["वदनम् एव स्मरस्य माङ्गल्यगृहं तस्य तोरण एव चिल्लिका (भ्रूलता) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वदन - face.","स्मर - Cupid, Manmatha.","माङ्गल्यगृह - auspicious house.","तोरण - festoon, arch at entrance.","चिल्लिका - eyebrow-creeper.","वदनस्मरमाङ्गल्यगृहतोरणचिल्लिका - She whose eyebrows are the festoons at the auspicious house of Cupid, which is Her face."],"summary":["वदनस्मरमाङ्गल्यगृहतोरणचिल्लिका means one whose eyebrows look like festoons in front of Cupid's house which is Śrīdevī's face. The roof at the entrance of the houses will be constructed in a raised manner so that the house is not affected by rain or Sunshine. This is called festoon. Śrīdevī's face is so beautiful as to infatuate Śrī Kāmeśvara. Thus Cupid uses this face as an office for his auspicious activities. The eyebrows look like beautiful festoons in front of this house (office)."],"searchText":"17 वदनस्मरमाङ्गल्यगृहतोरणचिल्लिका वदनम् एव स्मरस्य माङ्गल्यगृहं तस्य तोरण एव चिल्लिका (भ्रूलता) यस्याः सा। वदन - face. स्मर - cupid, manmatha. माङ्गल्यगृह - auspicious house. तोरण - festoon, arch at entrance. चिल्लिका - eyebrow-creeper. वदनस्मरमाङ्गल्यगृहतोरणचिल्लिका - she whose eyebrows are the festoons at the auspicious house of cupid, which is her face. वदनस्मरमाङ्गल्यगृहतोरणचिल्लिका means one whose eyebrows look like festoons in front of cupid's house which is śrīdevī's face. the roof at the entrance of the houses will be constructed in a raised manner so that the house is not affected by rain or sunshine. this is called festoon. śrīdevī's face is so beautiful as to infatuate śrī kāmeśvara. thus cupid uses this face as an office for his auspicious activities. the eyebrows look like beautiful festoons in front of this house (office). * **the primal throb (spanda):** *smara* (cupid) is the cosmic desire for manifestation. her face is the palace where this auspicious creation begins. the curve of her eyebrows (*cillikā*) represents the creative tension or vibration (**स्पन्द** — *spanda*) that triggers the projection of space and time.","esoteric":["* **The Primal Throb (Spanda):** *Smara* (Cupid) is the cosmic desire for manifestation. Her face is the palace where this auspicious creation begins. The curve of Her eyebrows (*cillikā*) represents the creative tension or vibration (**स्पन्द** — *Spanda*) that triggers the projection of space and time."]},{"number":18,"name":"वक्त्रलक्ष्मीपरीवाहचलन्मीनाभलोचना","samasa":["वक्त्रलक्ष्म्याः मुखकान्तेः परीवाहे चलद्भ्यां मीनाभ्यां तुल्ये लोचने यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वक्त्र - face.","लक्ष्मी - beauty, splendour.","परीवाह - stream, flow.","चलत् - moving.","मीन - fish.","आभ - resembling.","लोचना - eyes.","वक्त्रलक्ष्मीपरीवाहचलन्मीनाभलोचना - She whose eyes resemble fish moving in the stream of the beauty of Her face."],"summary":["वक्त्रलक्ष्मीपरीवाहचलन्मीनाभलोचना means one whose eyes look like fish swimming in the stream of beauty of Śrīdevī's face. The beauty of Śrīdevī's face undergoes momentary changes and this continuous change looks like a steady and slow stream. The motion of Śrīdevī's two eyes is compared to the fast movement of fish in this stream, which increases its beauty. Fish are not mammals but lay eggs. It is believed that fish nurse their offspring just by affectionate looks. Similarly, Śrīdevī's eyes, which are compared to fish swimming in the stream of beauty, uplift Her devotees just by a gracious look. She is therefore called Mīnākṣī, here referred to as Mīnābhalocanā."],"searchText":"18 वक्त्रलक्ष्मीपरीवाहचलन्मीनाभलोचना वक्त्रलक्ष्म्याः मुखकान्तेः परीवाहे चलद्भ्यां मीनाभ्यां तुल्ये लोचने यस्याः सा। वक्त्र - face. लक्ष्मी - beauty, splendour. परीवाह - stream, flow. चलत् - moving. मीन - fish. आभ - resembling. लोचना - eyes. वक्त्रलक्ष्मीपरीवाहचलन्मीनाभलोचना - she whose eyes resemble fish moving in the stream of the beauty of her face. वक्त्रलक्ष्मीपरीवाहचलन्मीनाभलोचना means one whose eyes look like fish swimming in the stream of beauty of śrīdevī's face. the beauty of śrīdevī's face undergoes momentary changes and this continuous change looks like a steady and slow stream. the motion of śrīdevī's two eyes is compared to the fast movement of fish in this stream, which increases its beauty. fish are not mammals but lay eggs. it is believed that fish nurse their offspring just by affectionate looks. similarly, śrīdevī's eyes, which are compared to fish swimming in the stream of beauty, uplift her devotees just by a gracious look. she is therefore called mīnākṣī, here referred to as mīnābhalocanā. * **solar and lunar currents:** fish animate the water in which they swim. esoterically, the two eyes represent the cosmic tracks of the sun and the moon, or the twin subtle channels **इडा** (*iḍā*) and **पिङ्गला** (*piṅgalā*). their movement (*calat*) governs the rhythmic cycles of cosmic time.","esoteric":["* **Solar and Lunar Currents:** Fish animate the water in which they swim. Esoterically, the two eyes represent the cosmic tracks of the Sun and the Moon, or the twin subtle channels **इडा** (*Iḍā*) and **पिङ्गला** (*Piṅgalā*). Their movement (*calat*) governs the rhythmic cycles of cosmic time."]},{"number":19,"name":"नवचम्पकपुष्पाभनासादण्डविराजिता","samasa":["नवचम्पकस्य पुष्पं नवचम्पकपुष्पम्। तेन तुल्यः नासादण्डेन विराजिता।"],"wordByWord":["नव - new, fresh, partly blossomed.","चम्पकपुष्प - champaka flower.","आभ - like, resembling.","नासादण्ड - bridge or shaft of the nose.","विराजिता - shining, adorned.","नवचम्पकपुष्पाभनासादण्डविराजिता - She whose nose shines like a fresh Champaka flower."],"summary":["नवचम्पकपुष्पाभनासादण्डविराजिता means one whose nose is like a fresh campaka flower. Nava can be interpreted as \"new\" or \"partly blossomed\". A partly blossomed campaka bud generates a pleasant aroma."],"searchText":"19 नवचम्पकपुष्पाभनासादण्डविराजिता नवचम्पकस्य पुष्पं नवचम्पकपुष्पम्। तेन तुल्यः नासादण्डेन विराजिता। नव - new, fresh, partly blossomed. चम्पकपुष्प - champaka flower. आभ - like, resembling. नासादण्ड - bridge or shaft of the nose. विराजिता - shining, adorned. नवचम्पकपुष्पाभनासादण्डविराजिता - she whose nose shines like a fresh champaka flower. नवचम्पकपुष्पाभनासादण्डविराजिता means one whose nose is like a fresh campaka flower. nava can be interpreted as \"new\" or \"partly blossomed\". a partly blossomed campaka bud generates a pleasant aroma. * **the path of suṣumṇā:** the campaka bud is perfectly linear and flawless. in *kuṇdoṣṭi-yoga*, the straightness of the nose bridge is the physical external indicator of the straight alignment of the **सुषुम्णा नाडी** (*suṣumṇā nādī*). its linear beauty represents the straight path of the ascending lifeforce (*prāṇa*).","esoteric":["* **The Path of Suṣumṇā:** The Campaka bud is perfectly linear and flawless. In *Kuṇdoṣṭi-yoga*, the straightness of the nose bridge is the physical external indicator of the straight alignment of the **सुषुम्णा नाडी** (*Suṣumṇā Nādī*). Its linear beauty represents the straight path of the ascending lifeforce (*Prāṇa*)."]},{"number":20,"name":"ताराकान्तितिरस्कारिनासाभरणभासुरा","samasa":["तारायाः कान्तिं तिरस्करोतीति ताराकान्तितिरस्कारि। तदेव नासाभरणम्। तेन भासुरा (शोभमाना)।"],"wordByWord":["तारा - star; also name of a deity.","कान्ति - lustre, brilliance.","तिरस्कारि - surpassing, putting to shame.","नासाभरण - nose ornament, nose ring.","भासुरा - shining, brilliant.","ताराकान्तितिरस्कारिनासाभरणभासुरा - She who shines with a nose ornament that surpasses the brilliance of the stars."],"summary":["ताराकान्तितिरस्कारिनासाभरणभासुरा means one whose nose ring challenges the lustre of the stars. Tārā can also be interpreted to mean the two Devīs — Maṅgalā and Śuklā or the Devatā — Tārakā. Śrīdevī's nose rings are made of Ruby and Pearl."],"searchText":"20 ताराकान्तितिरस्कारिनासाभरणभासुरा तारायाः कान्तिं तिरस्करोतीति ताराकान्तितिरस्कारि। तदेव नासाभरणम्। तेन भासुरा (शोभमाना)। तारा - star; also name of a deity. कान्ति - lustre, brilliance. तिरस्कारि - surpassing, putting to shame. नासाभरण - nose ornament, nose ring. भासुरा - shining, brilliant. ताराकान्तितिरस्कारिनासाभरणभासुरा - she who shines with a nose ornament that surpasses the brilliance of the stars. ताराकान्तितिरस्कारिनासाभरणभासुरा means one whose nose ring challenges the lustre of the stars. tārā can also be interpreted to mean the two devīs — maṅgalā and śuklā or the devatā — tārakā. śrīdevī's nose rings are made of ruby and pearl. * **the luminous point of self:** stars represent distant, objective, finite points of light in the external sky. her nose-pearl, which rests closest to the breath of life (*prāṇa*), represents the singular, immediate point of pure subjective light (*bindu*). it outshines the stars because inner self-awareness far eclipses any external cosmic object.","esoteric":["* **The Luminous Point of Self:** Stars represent distant, objective, finite points of light in the external sky. Her nose-pearl, which rests closest to the breath of life (*Prāṇa*), represents the singular, immediate point of pure subjective light (*Bindu*). It outshines the stars because inner self-awareness far eclipses any external cosmic object."]},{"number":21,"name":"कदम्बमञ्जरीकॢप्तकर्णपूरमनोहरा","samasa":["कदम्बमञ्जर्या क्लृप्तः (कल्पितः) कर्णपूरः कदम्बमञ्जरीक्लृप्तः। तेन मनोहरा (रमणीया)।"],"wordByWord":["कदम्बमञ्जरी - bunch of Kadamba flowers.","कॢप्त / क्लृप्त - arranged, made, fashioned.","कर्णपूर - ear ornament or floral filling for the ear.","मनोहरा - captivating, charming, stealing the mind.","कदम्बमञ्जरीकॢप्तकर्णपूरमनोहरा - She who enchants by wearing Kadamba flower-bunches as ear ornaments."],"summary":["कदम्बमञ्जरीकॢप्तकर्णपूरमनोहरा means one who wears a bunch of kadamba flowers in Her ears and steals the heart with Her beauty. Wearing a bunch of flowers in the earlobes increases the beauty. Kadamba flower is suitable for such adornment. A garden of kadamba trees is situated outside the Cintāmaṇi Gṛha, the abode of Śrīdevī, in Śrīpura. Śrīdevī wears the flowers plucked from those trees to adorn Her ear."],"searchText":"21 कदम्बमञ्जरीकॢप्तकर्णपूरमनोहरा कदम्बमञ्जर्या क्लृप्तः (कल्पितः) कर्णपूरः कदम्बमञ्जरीक्लृप्तः। तेन मनोहरा (रमणीया)। कदम्बमञ्जरी - bunch of kadamba flowers. कॢप्त / क्लृप्त - arranged, made, fashioned. कर्णपूर - ear ornament or floral filling for the ear. मनोहरा - captivating, charming, stealing the mind. कदम्बमञ्जरीकॢप्तकर्णपूरमनोहरा - she who enchants by wearing kadamba flower-bunches as ear ornaments. कदम्बमञ्जरीकॢप्तकर्णपूरमनोहरा means one who wears a bunch of kadamba flowers in her ears and steals the heart with her beauty. wearing a bunch of flowers in the earlobes increases the beauty. kadamba flower is suitable for such adornment. a garden of kadamba trees is situated outside the cintāmaṇi gṛha, the abode of śrīdevī, in śrīpura. śrīdevī wears the flowers plucked from those trees to adorn her ear. the kadamba tree represents the dense forest of manifest existence. the ears are the receptors of sound (*śabda*), the primary quality of space (*ākāśa*) and the source of speech. * **the ornaments of śruti:** by wearing kadamba blossoms as ear ornaments, she shows that all sound, all vedic revelation (*śruti*), and all manifest languages are merely beautiful ornaments hanging upon her listening consciousness.","esoteric":["The Kadamba tree represents the dense forest of manifest existence. The ears are the receptors of sound (*śabda*), the primary quality of space (*ākāśa*) and the source of speech.","* **The Ornaments of Śruti:** By wearing Kadamba blossoms as ear ornaments, She shows that all sound, all Vedic revelation (*Śruti*), and all manifest languages are merely beautiful ornaments hanging upon Her listening consciousness."]},{"number":22,"name":"ताटङ्कयुगलीभूततपनोडुपमण्डला","samasa":["उडनि पातीति उडपः।","अभूतं ताटङ्कयुगलं भूतम् इति ताटङ्कयुगलीभूतम्।","तथा तपनस्य (सूर्यस्य) उडपस्य (चन्द्रस्य) च मण्डले यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["ताटङ्क - large ear ornament, palm-leaf type ornament.","युगलीभूत - becoming a pair.","तपन - sun.","उडुप - moon.","मण्डल - disc, orb.","ताटङ्कयुगलीभूततपनोडुपमण्डला - She whose ear-ornaments are the paired discs of the Sun and Moon."],"summary":["ताटङ्कयुगलीभूततपनोडुपमण्डला means one who wears the Sun and Moon as two large earrings. One type of ornament worn by ladies in their ears is called tāṭaṅka (palm-leaf). The Sun and the Moon take the form of these tāṭaṅkas to beautify Śrīdevī's face. The Sun and the Moon have the fortune to become Śrīdevī's eyes, earrings and Her breasts. Tāṭaṅka is considered to be an auspicious ornament for sumaṅgalīs (ladies living with their husbands). Śrī Ādi Śaṅkara, in his Saundaryalaharī, describes with awe that Śrī Parameśvara could survive, even after consuming the Hālāhala (poison), only by the power of Śrīdevī's tāṭaṅkas (28th verse of Saundaryalaharī)."],"searchText":"22 ताटङ्कयुगलीभूततपनोडुपमण्डला उडनि पातीति उडपः। अभूतं ताटङ्कयुगलं भूतम् इति ताटङ्कयुगलीभूतम्। तथा तपनस्य (सूर्यस्य) उडपस्य (चन्द्रस्य) च मण्डले यस्याः सा। ताटङ्क - large ear ornament, palm-leaf type ornament. युगलीभूत - becoming a pair. तपन - sun. उडुप - moon. मण्डल - disc, orb. ताटङ्कयुगलीभूततपनोडुपमण्डला - she whose ear-ornaments are the paired discs of the sun and moon. ताटङ्कयुगलीभूततपनोडुपमण्डला means one who wears the sun and moon as two large earrings. one type of ornament worn by ladies in their ears is called tāṭaṅka (palm-leaf). the sun and the moon take the form of these tāṭaṅkas to beautify śrīdevī's face. the sun and the moon have the fortune to become śrīdevī's eyes, earrings and her breasts. tāṭaṅka is considered to be an auspicious ornament for sumaṅgalīs (ladies living with their husbands). śrī ādi śaṅkara, in his saundaryalaharī, describes with awe that śrī parameśvara could survive, even after consuming the hālāhala (poison), only by the power of śrīdevī's tāṭaṅkas (28th verse of saundaryalaharī). the *tāṭaṅka* (ear-ring) is the symbol of eternal auspiciousness (*saumaṅgalya*), as she never undergoes widowhood. * **wielding time:** the sun and moon are the twin cosmic measurers of time. by wearing them as mere ear-rings, she wears time itself as an accessory. this also represents that the solar and lunar breaths (**इडा** and **पिङ्गला**) are anchored in her cosmic hearing.","esoteric":["The *Tāṭaṅka* (ear-ring) is the symbol of eternal auspiciousness (*Saumaṅgalya*), as She never undergoes widowhood.","* **Wielding Time:** The Sun and Moon are the twin cosmic measurers of time. By wearing them as mere ear-rings, She wears Time itself as an accessory. This also represents that the solar and lunar breaths (**इडा** and **पिङ्गला**) are anchored in Her cosmic hearing."]},{"number":23,"name":"पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभाविकपोलभूः","samasa":["पद्मरागशिलाम् एव आदर्शं परिभवतीति पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभूः।","ईदृशी कपोलभूः (गण्डभित्तिः) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पद्मरागशिला - ruby/sapphire-like red precious stone.","आदर्श - mirror, glass.","परिभावि / परिभू - surpassing, excelling.","कपोलभूः - cheek surface.","पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभाविकपोलभूः - She whose cheeks surpass a mirror made of Padmaraga stone."],"summary":["पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभाविकपोलभूः means one whose cheeks are more wonderful than a glass made of padmarāga (Sapphire). Śrīdevī's cheeks are smooth and reflect like a mirror. Since it also seems to be red on account of Her complexion, the cheeks seem to be superior to a glass made of Sapphire."],"searchText":"23 पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभाविकपोलभूः पद्मरागशिलाम् एव आदर्शं परिभवतीति पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभूः। ईदृशी कपोलभूः (गण्डभित्तिः) यस्याः सा। पद्मरागशिला - ruby/sapphire-like red precious stone. आदर्श - mirror, glass. परिभावि / परिभू - surpassing, excelling. कपोलभूः - cheek surface. पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभाविकपोलभूः - she whose cheeks surpass a mirror made of padmaraga stone. पद्मरागशिलादर्शपरिभाविकपोलभूः means one whose cheeks are more wonderful than a glass made of padmarāga (sapphire). śrīdevī's cheeks are smooth and reflect like a mirror. since it also seems to be red on account of her complexion, the cheeks seem to be superior to a glass made of sapphire. * **cheeks of reflection:** a mirror reflects whatever stands before it but has no color of its own. her cheeks, however, are like ruby mirrors—they are red with her own internal bliss (*vimarśa*) and reflect the entire universe back to itself.","esoteric":["* **Cheeks of Reflection:** A mirror reflects whatever stands before it but has no color of its own. Her cheeks, however, are like ruby mirrors—they are red with Her own internal bliss (*Vimarśa*) and reflect the entire universe back to itself."]},{"number":24,"name":"नवविद्रुमबिम्बश्रीन्यक्कारिरदनच्छदा","samasa":["रदनानां छदः रदनच्छदः।","नवानां विद्रुमबिम्बानां श्रियं न्यक्कुरुतः (अधःकुरुतः) रदनच्छदौ यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["नव - fresh, new.","विद्रुम - coral.","बिम्ब - bimba fruit.","श्री - beauty, lustre.","न्यक्कारि - putting down, surpassing, outshining.","रदनच्छद - lips, covering of the teeth.","नवविद्रुमबिम्बश्रीन्यक्कारिरदनच्छदा - She whose lips surpass the beauty of fresh coral and bimba fruit."],"summary":["नवविद्रुमबिम्बश्रीन्यक्कारिरदनच्छदा means one whose gorgeous lips challenge the lustre of fresh corals and the bimba fruit (a fruit of a creeper, which when ripe is red). Śrīdevī's lips are red in colour, by nature. Coral and the bimba fruit are the two usually referred to for comparing lustrous red objects. Śrīdevī's rosy lips surpass these two objects. Radanacchada is another version and the meaning is the same."],"searchText":"24 नवविद्रुमबिम्बश्रीन्यक्कारिरदनच्छदा रदनानां छदः रदनच्छदः। नवानां विद्रुमबिम्बानां श्रियं न्यक्कुरुतः (अधःकुरुतः) रदनच्छदौ यस्याः सा। नव - fresh, new. विद्रुम - coral. बिम्ब - bimba fruit. श्री - beauty, lustre. न्यक्कारि - putting down, surpassing, outshining. रदनच्छद - lips, covering of the teeth. नवविद्रुमबिम्बश्रीन्यक्कारिरदनच्छदा - she whose lips surpass the beauty of fresh coral and bimba fruit. नवविद्रुमबिम्बश्रीन्यक्कारिरदनच्छदा means one whose gorgeous lips challenge the lustre of fresh corals and the bimba fruit (a fruit of a creeper, which when ripe is red). śrīdevī's lips are red in colour, by nature. coral and the bimba fruit are the two usually referred to for comparing lustrous red objects. śrīdevī's rosy lips surpass these two objects. radanacchada is another version and the meaning is the same. * **the portal of grace:** lips enclose speech. their deep red color signifies her overflowing compassion (*karuṇā*). before her speech transforms into spoken words, it sits behind the red barrier of her lips as pure, unmanifest grace. the lips mock coral because coral is dead mineral material, whereas her lips glow with the pulsing, vibrant life of supreme consciousness.","esoteric":["* **The Portal of Grace:** Lips enclose speech. Their deep red color signifies Her overflowing compassion (*karuṇā*). Before Her speech transforms into spoken words, it sits behind the red barrier of Her lips as pure, unmanifest grace. The lips mock coral because coral is dead mineral material, whereas Her lips glow with the pulsing, vibrant life of supreme consciousness."]},{"number":25,"name":"शुद्धविद्याङ्कुराकारद्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयोज्ज्वला","samasa":["शुद्धविद्यायाः अङ्कुराणाम् इव आकारः यस्य द्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयस्य, तेन द्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयेन उज्ज्वला।"],"wordByWord":["शुद्धविद्या - Shuddha Vidya, superior Shodashakshari Mantra / Sree Vidya.","अङ्कुर - sprout, shoot.","आकार - form, shape.","द्विज - twice-born; also tooth.","पङ्क्तिद्वय - two rows.","उज्ज्वला - shining, resplendent.","शुद्धविद्याङ्कुराकारद्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयोज्ज्वला - She who shines with two rows of teeth resembling sprouts of Shuddha Vidya."],"summary":["शुद्धविद्याङ्कुराकारद्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयोज्ज्वला means one whose rows of teeth shine like sprouts of śuddha vidyā. The word dvija means twice born. This term is used to describe three different things: a. Brahmin — First birth from the mother and the second when the upanayanam is performed (when the sacred thread is first worn). b. Birds — First birth as egg and the second when the chick comes out of the egg. c. Tooth — First as milk teeth and second when the tooth sprouts in place of fallen teeth. Śuddha vidyā refers to the superior ṣoḍaśākṣarī mantra. It consists of 16 letters or bījas. Bījas also mean seeds. The teeth look like the two sprouts from the seeds — the upper and lower rows. Dattātreya Saṃhitā and other texts state that śuddha vidyā is the same as Śrīvidyā. Thus the 16 letters of Ṣoḍaśī vidyā are hidden in this name. Brahmins learn and propagate Vedas. Thus they are called vidyāṅkuras that is sprout of vidyā. Śrīdevī's two rows of teeth are compared to two rows of Brahmins, the sprout of vidyā."],"searchText":"25 शुद्धविद्याङ्कुराकारद्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयोज्ज्वला शुद्धविद्यायाः अङ्कुराणाम् इव आकारः यस्य द्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयस्य, तेन द्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयेन उज्ज्वला। शुद्धविद्या - shuddha vidya, superior shodashakshari mantra / sree vidya. अङ्कुर - sprout, shoot. आकार - form, shape. द्विज - twice-born; also tooth. पङ्क्तिद्वय - two rows. उज्ज्वला - shining, resplendent. शुद्धविद्याङ्कुराकारद्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयोज्ज्वला - she who shines with two rows of teeth resembling sprouts of shuddha vidya. शुद्धविद्याङ्कुराकारद्विजपङ्क्तिद्वयोज्ज्वला means one whose rows of teeth shine like sprouts of śuddha vidyā. the word dvija means twice born. this term is used to describe three different things: a. brahmin — first birth from the mother and the second when the upanayanam is performed (when the sacred thread is first worn). b. birds — first birth as egg and the second when the chick comes out of the egg. c. tooth — first as milk teeth and second when the tooth sprouts in place of fallen teeth. śuddha vidyā refers to the superior ṣoḍaśākṣarī mantra. it consists of 16 letters or bījas. bījas also mean seeds. the teeth look like the two sprouts from the seeds — the upper and lower rows. dattātreya saṃhitā and other texts state that śuddha vidyā is the same as śrīvidyā. thus the 16 letters of ṣoḍaśī vidyā are hidden in this name. brahmins learn and propagate vedas. thus they are called vidyāṅkuras that is sprout of vidyā. śrīdevī's two rows of teeth are compared to two rows of brahmins, the sprout of vidyā. * **the smile of realization:** *śuddha-vidyā* is the state of cosmic realization where the thought \"i am the universe\" sparkles clearly. her teeth are the white, sprouting shoots of this realization. when she smiles, she unleashes the light of pure knowledge that destroys the dark illusion of cosmic separation in the mind of the disciple.","esoteric":["* **The Smile of Realization:** *Śuddha-vidyā* is the state of cosmic realization where the thought \"I am the universe\" sparkles clearly. Her teeth are the white, sprouting shoots of this realization. When She smiles, She unleashes the light of pure knowledge that destroys the dark illusion of cosmic separation in the mind of the disciple."]},{"number":26,"name":"कर्पूरवीटिकामोदसमाकर्षिदिगन्तरा","samasa":["• कर्पूरेण (करुपूरादिभिः) युक्ता वीटिका (ताम्बूलः)। तस्याः आमोदं याः समाकर्षन्ति। ताः एव दिशः अन्तं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कर्पूर — camphor","वीटिका — betel packet; tamboola","आमोद — pleasant aroma","समाकर्षि — attracting; drawing towards","दिगन्तरा — the quarters and the intervening spaces","कर्पूरवीटिकामोदसमाकर्षिदिगन्तरा — She who attracts the quarters by the aroma of the camphor-scented betel from Her mouth"],"summary":["कर्पूरवीटिकामोदसमाकर्षिदिगन्तरा means one who attracts the four directions towards Her by the pleasant aroma of the betel (tāmbūla) emanating from Her lotus-like mouth, or one who spreads that aroma in all directions. Vīṭikā is a small pack (folded inside a betel leaf) with proper mixture of aromatic spices such as camphor, cardamom, cloves, musk, saffron, nutmeg, betelnut, lime, etc. The aroma emanating from Śrīdevī's mouth when She chews the vīṭikā spreads in all directions. It is symbolically described as if the directions compete with each other in surrounding Śrīdevī to have a scent of this aroma. Dik refers to the four directions and digambara is the intervening space between the four directions such as Southeast, Southwest, etc. The name samākarṣa-digantarā is also mentioned as samākarṣi-digantarā in some editions. There is no difference in meaning between these two versions."],"searchText":"26 कर्पूरवीटिकामोदसमाकर्षिदिगन्तरा • कर्पूरेण (करुपूरादिभिः) युक्ता वीटिका (ताम्बूलः)। तस्याः आमोदं याः समाकर्षन्ति। ताः एव दिशः अन्तं यस्याः सा। कर्पूर — camphor वीटिका — betel packet; tamboola आमोद — pleasant aroma समाकर्षि — attracting; drawing towards दिगन्तरा — the quarters and the intervening spaces कर्पूरवीटिकामोदसमाकर्षिदिगन्तरा — she who attracts the quarters by the aroma of the camphor-scented betel from her mouth कर्पूरवीटिकामोदसमाकर्षिदिगन्तरा means one who attracts the four directions towards her by the pleasant aroma of the betel (tāmbūla) emanating from her lotus-like mouth, or one who spreads that aroma in all directions. vīṭikā is a small pack (folded inside a betel leaf) with proper mixture of aromatic spices such as camphor, cardamom, cloves, musk, saffron, nutmeg, betelnut, lime, etc. the aroma emanating from śrīdevī's mouth when she chews the vīṭikā spreads in all directions. it is symbolically described as if the directions compete with each other in surrounding śrīdevī to have a scent of this aroma. dik refers to the four directions and digambara is the intervening space between the four directions such as southeast, southwest, etc. the name samākarṣa-digantarā is also mentioned as samākarṣi-digantarā in some editions. there is no difference in meaning between these two versions. * **the diffusion of wisdom:** camphor (*karpūra*) burns completely without leaving any residue, symbolizing the total dissolution of the ego. the betel roll (*vīṭikā*) contains spices that stimulate and sweeten. the fragrance of her chewing this *vīṭikā* is the diffusion of spiritual wisdom (*vidyā*) that spreads in all directions to attract and awaken dormant souls everywhere.","esoteric":["* **The Diffusion of Wisdom:** Camphor (*karpūra*) burns completely without leaving any residue, symbolizing the total dissolution of the ego. The betel roll (*vīṭikā*) contains spices that stimulate and sweeten. The fragrance of Her chewing this *vīṭikā* is the diffusion of spiritual wisdom (*Vidyā*) that spreads in all directions to attract and awaken dormant souls everywhere."]},{"number":27,"name":"निजसल्लापमाधुर्यविनिर्भर्त्सितकच्छपी","samasa":["• नीजस्य (स्वीयस्य) सल्लापस्य माधुर्येण विनिर्भर्त्सिता कच्छपी यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["निज — own","सल्लाप — speech; conversation","माधुर्य — sweetness","विनिर्भर्त्सित — humbled; put to shame","कच्छपी — the Veena of Saraswathi","निजसल्लापमाधुर्यविनिर्भर्त्सितकच्छपी — She whose own sweet speech humbles the Kacchapi Veena"],"summary":["निजसल्लापमाधुर्यविनिर्भर्त्सितकच्छपी means one whose sweet voice humbles the vīṇā (a string instrument) called Kacchapī in the hands of Śrī Sarasvatī (goddess of learning). Kacchapī is the name of Śrī Sarasvatī's vīṇā. Normally, in any string instrument like vīṇā, only the musical notes will be heard and not the lyrics of a song. But since Śrī Sarasvatī is the embodiment of sound and music, the musical notes as well as the words in the lyrics are heard from Her vīṇā. However, the words would not be explicit, but resemble the utterances of parrot and infants. Śrīdevī's voice is so sweet, that it wins over the sweetness of Śrī Sarasvatī's vīṇā. There is one verse in Saundaryalaharī (66th verse beginning with vipañcyā gāyantī). It is stated that when Śrī Sarasvatī played Her vīṇā in the presence of Śrīdevī, She admired its sweetness and uttered the word \"awesome\". On hearing this Śrī Sarasvatī was ashamed by the sweetness of Śrīdevī's voice which surpassed the sound of Her vīṇā and kept it inside its cover."],"searchText":"27 निजसल्लापमाधुर्यविनिर्भर्त्सितकच्छपी • नीजस्य (स्वीयस्य) सल्लापस्य माधुर्येण विनिर्भर्त्सिता कच्छपी यया सा। निज — own सल्लाप — speech; conversation माधुर्य — sweetness विनिर्भर्त्सित — humbled; put to shame कच्छपी — the veena of saraswathi निजसल्लापमाधुर्यविनिर्भर्त्सितकच्छपी — she whose own sweet speech humbles the kacchapi veena निजसल्लापमाधुर्यविनिर्भर्त्सितकच्छपी means one whose sweet voice humbles the vīṇā (a string instrument) called kacchapī in the hands of śrī sarasvatī (goddess of learning). kacchapī is the name of śrī sarasvatī's vīṇā. normally, in any string instrument like vīṇā, only the musical notes will be heard and not the lyrics of a song. but since śrī sarasvatī is the embodiment of sound and music, the musical notes as well as the words in the lyrics are heard from her vīṇā. however, the words would not be explicit, but resemble the utterances of parrot and infants. śrīdevī's voice is so sweet, that it wins over the sweetness of śrī sarasvatī's vīṇā. there is one verse in saundaryalaharī (66th verse beginning with vipañcyā gāyantī). it is stated that when śrī sarasvatī played her vīṇā in the presence of śrīdevī, she admired its sweetness and uttered the word \"awesome\". on hearing this śrī sarasvatī was ashamed by the sweetness of śrīdevī's voice which surpassed the sound of her vīṇā and kept it inside its cover. * **the primal sound (nāda):** the lute *kacchapī* produces the highest form of instrumental music. however, her sweet conversation represents the primordial, unmanifest sound (**नाद** — *nāda* or *parā-vāk*) from which all music and languages emerge. the copy (instrumental music) is naturally shamed and humbled before the sweet, original source (her voice).","esoteric":["* **The Primal Sound (Nāda):** The lute *Kacchapī* produces the highest form of instrumental music. However, Her sweet conversation represents the primordial, unmanifest sound (**नाद** — *Nāda* or *Parā-vāk*) from which all music and languages emerge. The copy (instrumental music) is naturally shamed and humbled before the sweet, original source (Her voice)."]},{"number":28,"name":"मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्कामेशमानसा","samasa":["• मन्दस्य स्मितस्य (ईशद्धासस्य) प्रभापूरे मज्जतीति मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्। तदेव कामस्य ईशस्य मानसं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मन्द — soft; gentle","स्मित — smile","प्रभापूर — flood of light","मज्जत् — sinking; immersed","कामेश — Sree Kameshwara","मानस — mind","मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्कामेशमानसा — She whose soft smile floods and immerses the mind of Kameshwara"],"summary":["मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्कामेशमानसा means one who overwhelms Śrī Kāmeśvara's mind in the inundation of Her smile. Smita means smile — without the teeth being visible. Especially mandasmita means a very soft smile. Majjat means sinking. Śrī Kāmeśvara does not want to come out of the flood of light that is Śrīdevī's smile. At the same time He does not want to miss the opportunity of enjoying the beauty of the other parts; hence the use of the expression \"sinking\". In Kāmakalā, Kāma means bindu. Kalā means Sun, Moon and fire. Bindu denotes ahaṅkāra. Kāma and kalā denote Kāmakalā. Kāmeśvara means both Rājarājeśvara and the embodiment of Kāmakalā. When Śrīdevī emerged out of the fire of knowledge (cidagnikuṇḍa), before crowning Her as empress, the question arose as who can be made as Her consort. The only eligible candidate was Śrī Kāmeśvara. But the devas were perplexed as His physical appearance — with knotted locks, covered with an elephant skin or wearing nothing at all, with snakes as jewels and with ash smeared all over the body — was in no way a match to Her bewitching beauty."],"searchText":"28 मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्कामेशमानसा • मन्दस्य स्मितस्य (ईशद्धासस्य) प्रभापूरे मज्जतीति मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्। तदेव कामस्य ईशस्य मानसं यस्याः सा। मन्द — soft; gentle स्मित — smile प्रभापूर — flood of light मज्जत् — sinking; immersed कामेश — sree kameshwara मानस — mind मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्कामेशमानसा — she whose soft smile floods and immerses the mind of kameshwara मन्दस्मितप्रभापूरमज्जत्कामेशमानसा means one who overwhelms śrī kāmeśvara's mind in the inundation of her smile. smita means smile — without the teeth being visible. especially mandasmita means a very soft smile. majjat means sinking. śrī kāmeśvara does not want to come out of the flood of light that is śrīdevī's smile. at the same time he does not want to miss the opportunity of enjoying the beauty of the other parts; hence the use of the expression \"sinking\". in kāmakalā, kāma means bindu. kalā means sun, moon and fire. bindu denotes ahaṅkāra. kāma and kalā denote kāmakalā. kāmeśvara means both rājarājeśvara and the embodiment of kāmakalā. when śrīdevī emerged out of the fire of knowledge (cidagnikuṇḍa), before crowning her as empress, the question arose as who can be made as her consort. the only eligible candidate was śrī kāmeśvara. but the devas were perplexed as his physical appearance — with knotted locks, covered with an elephant skin or wearing nothing at all, with snakes as jewels and with ash smeared all over the body — was in no way a match to her bewitching beauty. * **the dissolution of transcendent mind:** kāmeśvara represents the supreme, unmoving, detached observer (*prakāśa*). even her gentle, subtle smile (*mandasmita*) possesses such immense kinetic power (*vimarśa*) that it completely dissolves and sweeps away shiva's detached stillness, bringing him into a state of ecstatic, non-dual union. it represents the perfect fusion of shiva and shakti. to cover all 1,000 names from your document in a single go would exceed the output limits of a single message. let us proceed systematically with the next logical section: names 29 to 50. here is the raw markdown block for the next batch of your samāsa-vigrahas, ready to be copied and pasted directly into your.md file.","esoteric":["* **The Dissolution of Transcendent Mind:** Kāmeśvara represents the supreme, unmoving, detached observer (*Prakāśa*). Even Her gentle, subtle smile (*mandasmita*) possesses such immense kinetic power (*Vimarśa*) that it completely dissolves and sweeps away Shiva's detached stillness, bringing Him into a state of ecstatic, non-dual union. It represents the perfect fusion of Shiva and Shakti.","To cover all 1,000 names from your document in a single go would exceed the output limits of a single message. Let us proceed systematically with the next logical section: Names 29 to 50.","Here is the raw Markdown block for the next batch of your samāsa-vigrahas, ready to be copied and pasted directly into your.md file."]},{"number":29,"name":"अनाकलितसादृश्यचिबुकश्रीविराजिता","samasa":["• अनाकलितं (न कल्पितं) यत् सादृश्यं यस्याः चिबुकश्रियाः तादृश्या चिबुकश्रिया विराजिता।"],"wordByWord":["अनाकलित — not imagined; not conceived","सादृश्य — similarity; comparison","चिबुक — chin","श्री — beauty; splendour","विराजिता — shining","अनाकलितसादृश्यचिबुकश्रीविराजिता — She who shines by the incomparable beauty of Her chin"],"summary":["अनाकलितसादृश्यचिबुकश्रीविराजिता means one who shines by virtue of the incomparable beauty of Her chin. Even the Vāgdevatās (the goddess of words) could not find similes to describe the beauty of Her chin. Śrī Ādi Śaṅkara also opines the same, in his Saundaryalaharī, as kathaṅkāraṃ brūmastava cibukam aupamyarahitam (67th verse). Cubuka or cibuka mean the same."],"searchText":"29 अनाकलितसादृश्यचिबुकश्रीविराजिता • अनाकलितं (न कल्पितं) यत् सादृश्यं यस्याः चिबुकश्रियाः तादृश्या चिबुकश्रिया विराजिता। अनाकलित — not imagined; not conceived सादृश्य — similarity; comparison चिबुक — chin श्री — beauty; splendour विराजिता — shining अनाकलितसादृश्यचिबुकश्रीविराजिता — she who shines by the incomparable beauty of her chin अनाकलितसादृश्यचिबुकश्रीविराजिता means one who shines by virtue of the incomparable beauty of her chin. even the vāgdevatās (the goddess of words) could not find similes to describe the beauty of her chin. śrī ādi śaṅkara also opines the same, in his saundaryalaharī, as kathaṅkāraṃ brūmastava cibukam aupamyarahitam (67th verse). cubuka or cibuka mean the same. * **the incomparable point of non-duality:** in aesthetic descriptions, every facial feature has a standard poetic parallel (e.g., eyes like lotus petals, forehead like the crescent moon). however, the chin has no poetic parallel in nature. because she is the non-dual absolute, any comparison (*sādṛśya*) with worldly objects is fundamentally impossible (*anākalita*).","esoteric":["* **The Incomparable Point of Non-Duality:** In aesthetic descriptions, every facial feature has a standard poetic parallel (e.g., eyes like lotus petals, forehead like the crescent moon). However, the chin has no poetic parallel in nature. Because She is the non-dual absolute, any comparison (*sādṛśya*) with worldly objects is fundamentally impossible (*anākalita*)."]},{"number":30,"name":"कामेशबद्धमाङ्गल्यसूत्रशोभितकन्धरा","samasa":["• कामेशेन (परमशिवेन) बद्धं यत् माङ्गल्यसूत्रं तेन शोभिता कन्धरा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कामेश — Sree Kameshwara","बद्ध — tied","माङ्गल्यसूत्र — auspicious marriage string","शोभित — beautified","कन्धरा — neck","कामेशबद्धमाङ्गल्यसूत्रशोभितकन्धरा — She whose neck is beautified by the auspicious string tied by Kamesha"],"summary":["कामेशबद्धमाङ्गल्यसूत्रशोभितकन्धरा means one whose neck is so beautiful by the auspicious string tied by Śrī Kāmeśvara at the time of wedding. Śrīdevī is a nityā sumaṅgalī, who is always a sumaṅgalī, wearing the maṅgala sūtra. Although She emerged out of cidagni kuṇḍa, already wearing the maṅgala sūtra, the devas wanted to see the wedding ceremony of the Holy couple and made Him tie the string again on Śrīdevī. Śrī Parameśvara acquired the name Kāmāri after he reduced Cupid to ashes. Yet on seeing Śrīdevī, it appears that He gave life to Cupid and subjected Himself as the aim for the arrows by Cupid so that love would arise in Him upon Śrīdevī, that too through the grace of Śrīdevī. Thus He becomes the lord of Cupid — Kāmeśan. Induced by His desire to marry Śrīdevī, Īśvara made friendship with Cupid and was worshipped by him as \"Thou art my Lord\". This maṅgala sūtra tied by Kāmeśa showered blessings to the entire world. The first such beneficiary of this shower was Rati-Manmatha (Cupid) couple and that too for the upliftment of the whole world."],"searchText":"30 कामेशबद्धमाङ्गल्यसूत्रशोभितकन्धरा • कामेशेन (परमशिवेन) बद्धं यत् माङ्गल्यसूत्रं तेन शोभिता कन्धरा यस्याः सा। कामेश — sree kameshwara बद्ध — tied माङ्गल्यसूत्र — auspicious marriage string शोभित — beautified कन्धरा — neck कामेशबद्धमाङ्गल्यसूत्रशोभितकन्धरा — she whose neck is beautified by the auspicious string tied by kamesha कामेशबद्धमाङ्गल्यसूत्रशोभितकन्धरा means one whose neck is so beautiful by the auspicious string tied by śrī kāmeśvara at the time of wedding. śrīdevī is a nityā sumaṅgalī, who is always a sumaṅgalī, wearing the maṅgala sūtra. although she emerged out of cidagni kuṇḍa, already wearing the maṅgala sūtra, the devas wanted to see the wedding ceremony of the holy couple and made him tie the string again on śrīdevī. śrī parameśvara acquired the name kāmāri after he reduced cupid to ashes. yet on seeing śrīdevī, it appears that he gave life to cupid and subjected himself as the aim for the arrows by cupid so that love would arise in him upon śrīdevī, that too through the grace of śrīdevī. thus he becomes the lord of cupid — kāmeśan. induced by his desire to marry śrīdevī, īśvara made friendship with cupid and was worshipped by him as \"thou art my lord\". this maṅgala sūtra tied by kāmeśa showered blessings to the entire world. the first such beneficiary of this shower was rati-manmatha (cupid) couple and that too for the upliftment of the whole world. * **the unbroken thread of cosmic order:** the *māṅgalyasūtra* represents the eternal, indissoluble bond between *prakāśa* (shiva) and *vimarśa* (shakti). because shiva is immortal, her state of auspiciousness is eternal (*nitya-sumaṅgalī*). esoterically, the thread around her neck represents the *sūtrātman*—the singular, thread-like cosmic consciousness that runs through and holds together all individual souls (*jīvas*) in the universe.","esoteric":["* **The Unbroken Thread of Cosmic Order:** The *māṅgalyasūtra* represents the eternal, indissoluble bond between *Prakāśa* (Shiva) and *Vimarśa* (Shakti). Because Shiva is immortal, Her state of auspiciousness is eternal (*Nitya-Sumaṅgalī*). Esoterically, the thread around Her neck represents the *Sūtrātman*—the singular, thread-like cosmic consciousness that runs through and holds together all individual souls (*jīvas*) in the universe."]},{"number":31,"name":"कनकाङ्गदकेयूरकमनीयभुजान्विता","samasa":["• अङ्गं ददातीति अङ्गदम्। कनकम् एव अङ्गदं येषां केयूराणां तैः कमनीया ये भुजाः तैः अन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["कनक — gold","अङ्गद — armlet; shoulder bangle","केयूर — upper-arm ornament","कमनीय — beautiful","भुजा — arms","अन्विता — endowed with","कनकाङ्गदकेयूरकमनीयभुजान्विता — She whose beautiful arms are adorned with golden armlets and Keyuras"],"summary":["कनकाङ्गदकेयूरकमनीयभुजान्विता means one whose shoulders are adorned by golden shoulder bangles. Aṅgada and keyūra are the two ornaments worn on the hands. Keyūra is for beautification whereas aṅgada acts as a shield for shoulders and arms of warriors. As Śrīdevī is a queen, She wears both the ornaments."],"searchText":"31 कनकाङ्गदकेयूरकमनीयभुजान्विता • अङ्गं ददातीति अङ्गदम्। कनकम् एव अङ्गदं येषां केयूराणां तैः कमनीया ये भुजाः तैः अन्विता। कनक — gold अङ्गद — armlet; shoulder bangle केयूर — upper-arm ornament कमनीय — beautiful भुजा — arms अन्विता — endowed with कनकाङ्गदकेयूरकमनीयभुजान्विता — she whose beautiful arms are adorned with golden armlets and keyuras कनकाङ्गदकेयूरकमनीयभुजान्विता means one whose shoulders are adorned by golden shoulder bangles. aṅgada and keyūra are the two ornaments worn on the hands. keyūra is for beautification whereas aṅgada acts as a shield for shoulders and arms of warriors. as śrīdevī is a queen, she wears both the ornaments. * **the pillars of action:** her arms represent the active, protective powers of the cosmos. the armlets (*aṅgada* and *keyūra*) symbolize the cosmic laws (*dharma*) that decorate and guide her infinite power of action (**क्रियाशक्ति** — *kriyā-śakti*). gold (*kanaka*) represents the immutable, eternal truth of consciousness that remains unchanged regardless of the forms it takes.","esoteric":["* **The Pillars of Action:** Her arms represent the active, protective powers of the cosmos. The armlets (*aṅgada* and *keyūra*) symbolize the cosmic laws (*Dharma*) that decorate and guide Her infinite power of action (**क्रियाशक्ति** — *Kriyā-śakti*). Gold (*kanaka*) represents the immutable, eternal truth of consciousness that remains unchanged regardless of the forms it takes."]},{"number":32,"name":"रत्नग्रैवेयचिन्ताकलोलमुक्ताफलान्विता","samasa":["• रत्नखचितेन ग्रैवेयेण चिन्ताकेन च लोलैः मुक्ताफलैः च अन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["रत्न — gemstone","ग्रैवेय — neck pendant or necklace ornament","चिन्ताक — neck ornament/pendant","लोल — swinging","मुक्ताफल — pearls","अन्विता — endowed with; adorned","रत्नग्रैवेयचिन्ताकलोलमुक्ताफलान्विता — She who is adorned with a gem-studded neck ornament and swinging pearls"],"summary":["रत्नग्रैवेयचिन्ताकलोलमुक्ताफलान्विता means one who wears a necklace with a pendant studded with gemstones and garland of Pearls. Grīvā means neck. Graiveya means the pendant in the necklace which adorns the neck and the string of Pearls aligning the necklace. The necklace, the pendant and the string of pearls represent the three types of devotees. Some will be chanting the names of Śrīdevī (doing japa), but their minds will be wandering somewhere else. Their thoughts of Śrīdevī stop with the neck. They are graiveya cintakas, limiting their thought of Śrīdevī above the neck. They hang and swing from the necklace of Śrīdevī, hence they are called lolas. For some others, the thoughts and actions will be oscillating between Śrīdevī and other extraneous thoughts, like a pendant hanging from the necklace. The third type is the muktas — the detached. They have got rid of their extraneous thoughts and action and think of Śrīdevī only. Thus, this name classifies the devotees into three types. The fruits of actions of these three types of devotees are also different."],"searchText":"32 रत्नग्रैवेयचिन्ताकलोलमुक्ताफलान्विता • रत्नखचितेन ग्रैवेयेण चिन्ताकेन च लोलैः मुक्ताफलैः च अन्विता। रत्न — gemstone ग्रैवेय — neck pendant or necklace ornament चिन्ताक — neck ornament/pendant लोल — swinging मुक्ताफल — pearls अन्विता — endowed with; adorned रत्नग्रैवेयचिन्ताकलोलमुक्ताफलान्विता — she who is adorned with a gem-studded neck ornament and swinging pearls रत्नग्रैवेयचिन्ताकलोलमुक्ताफलान्विता means one who wears a necklace with a pendant studded with gemstones and garland of pearls. grīvā means neck. graiveya means the pendant in the necklace which adorns the neck and the string of pearls aligning the necklace. the necklace, the pendant and the string of pearls represent the three types of devotees. some will be chanting the names of śrīdevī (doing japa), but their minds will be wandering somewhere else. their thoughts of śrīdevī stop with the neck. they are graiveya cintakas, limiting their thought of śrīdevī above the neck. they hang and swing from the necklace of śrīdevī, hence they are called lolas. for some others, the thoughts and actions will be oscillating between śrīdevī and other extraneous thoughts, like a pendant hanging from the necklace. the third type is the muktas — the detached. they have got rid of their extraneous thoughts and action and think of śrīdevī only. thus, this name classifies the devotees into three types. the fruits of actions of these three types of devotees are also different. * **the medallion of pure thought:** the neck-ornament (*graiveya*) rests over the throat, the center of speech (*viśuddhi*). the pendant is called **चिन्ताक** (*cintāka*), derived from the root *cint* (to meditate or think). this represents that the focus of her meditative thought is the welfare of her devotees. the dangling pearls (*muktāphala*) represent the individual souls who have achieved liberation (*mukti*), clustered close to her throat, bathing in the sound of her grace.","esoteric":["* **The Medallion of Pure Thought:** The neck-ornament (*graiveya*) rests over the throat, the center of speech (*Viśuddhi*). The pendant is called **चिन्ताक** (*cintāka*), derived from the root *cint* (to meditate or think). This represents that the focus of Her meditative thought is the welfare of Her devotees. The dangling pearls (*muktāphala*) represent the individual souls who have achieved liberation (*mukti*), clustered close to Her throat, bathing in the sound of Her grace."]},{"number":33,"name":"कामेश्वरप्रेमरत्नमणिप्रतिपणस्तनी","samasa":["• कामेश्वरस्य प्रेम एव रत्नमणिः। रत्नमणौ प्रतिपणभूतौ स्तनौ यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कामेश्वर — Sree Kameshwara","प्रेम — love","रत्नमणि — gem; jewel","प्रतिपण — price; exchange","स्तनी — having breasts","कामेश्वरप्रेमरत्नमणिप्रतिपणस्तनी — She who offers Her breasts as the price for the gem of Kameshwara’s love"],"summary":["कामेश्वरप्रेमरत्नमणिप्रतिपणस्तनी means one who offers Her breasts as price (or in exchange) for the gem of love of Śrī Kāmeśvara. Śrīdevī has purchased Śrī Kāmeśvara's invaluable love for Her, with Her breasts. Śrīdevī has offered twice the price or price like (two jewels of breasts) for a single jewel of Śrī Kāmeśvara's love. (Refer 4th verse of Saundaryalaharī — phalam api ca vāñchāsamadhikaṃ)."],"searchText":"33 कामेश्वरप्रेमरत्नमणिप्रतिपणस्तनी • कामेश्वरस्य प्रेम एव रत्नमणिः। रत्नमणौ प्रतिपणभूतौ स्तनौ यस्याः सा। कामेश्वर — sree kameshwara प्रेम — love रत्नमणि — gem; jewel प्रतिपण — price; exchange स्तनी — having breasts कामेश्वरप्रेमरत्नमणिप्रतिपणस्तनी — she who offers her breasts as the price for the gem of kameshwara’s love कामेश्वरप्रेमरत्नमणिप्रतिपणस्तनी means one who offers her breasts as price (or in exchange) for the gem of love of śrī kāmeśvara. śrīdevī has purchased śrī kāmeśvara's invaluable love for her, with her breasts. śrīdevī has offered twice the price or price like (two jewels of breasts) for a single jewel of śrī kāmeśvara's love. (refer 4th verse of saundaryalaharī — phalam api ca vāñchāsamadhikaṃ). * **the great cosmic transaction:** the \"wager\" (*pratipaṇa*) refers to a cosmic game of dice played between shiva and shakti. her breasts represent the dual polarities of creation—**प्रकाश** (*prakāśa*) and **विमर्श** (*vimarśa*). to obtain her supreme, dual-natured manifestation, shiva wagers his entire undivided, silent love. this represents the absolute, reciprocal self-surrender between the divine couple.","esoteric":["* **The Great Cosmic Transaction:** The \"wager\" (*pratipaṇa*) refers to a cosmic game of dice played between Shiva and Shakti. Her breasts represent the dual polarities of creation—**प्रकाश** (*Prakāśa*) and **विमर्श** (*Vimarśa*). To obtain Her supreme, dual-natured manifestation, Shiva wagers His entire undivided, silent love. This represents the absolute, reciprocal self-surrender between the divine couple."]},{"number":34,"name":"नाभ्यालवालरोमालिलताफलकुचद्वयी","samasa":["• नाभिः एव आलवालः यस्याः रोमालवल्याः लतायाः तस्याः फलभूता कुचद्वयी यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["नाभि — navel","आलवाल — trench; basin at the root","रोमाली — line of hair","लता — creeper","फल — fruit","कुचद्वयी — two breasts","नाभ्यालवालरोमालिलताफलकुचद्वयी — She whose two breasts are fruits of the creeper-like hair-line rising from the navel-trench"],"summary":["नाभ्यालवालरोमालिलताफलकुचद्वयी means Śrīdevī's two breasts are like fruits in a creeper (line of hair) climbing from the trench (the navel). The deep navel is like a trench. The narrow line of hair grown upwards from the navel is like a creeper. The two breasts appear as if they are hanging from the creeper (an excellent metaphor)."],"searchText":"34 नाभ्यालवालरोमालिलताफलकुचद्वयी • नाभिः एव आलवालः यस्याः रोमालवल्याः लतायाः तस्याः फलभूता कुचद्वयी यस्याः सा। नाभि — navel आलवाल — trench; basin at the root रोमाली — line of hair लता — creeper फल — fruit कुचद्वयी — two breasts नाभ्यालवालरोमालिलताफलकुचद्वयी — she whose two breasts are fruits of the creeper-like hair-line rising from the navel-trench नाभ्यालवालरोमालिलताफलकुचद्वयी means śrīdevī's two breasts are like fruits in a creeper (line of hair) climbing from the trench (the navel). the deep navel is like a trench. the narrow line of hair grown upwards from the navel is like a creeper. the two breasts appear as if they are hanging from the creeper (an excellent metaphor). * **the root of vital force:** the navel (*nābhi*) represents the **मणिपूर चक्र** (*maṇipūra cakra*), the seat of fire and metabolic origin. the upward-climbing hairline (*romāli*) represents the movement of the ascending lifeforce (*prāṇa*) traveling up the central channel. the twin breasts produced as \"fruits\" represent the nourishing wisdom and bliss (*sarasvatī* and *lakṣmī* potencies) that blossom when the energy rises to the heart center (*anāhata*).","esoteric":["* **The Root of Vital Force:** The navel (*nābhi*) represents the **मणिपूर चक्र** (*Maṇipūra Cakra*), the seat of fire and metabolic origin. The upward-climbing hairline (*romāli*) represents the movement of the ascending lifeforce (*Prāṇa*) traveling up the central channel. The twin breasts produced as \"fruits\" represent the nourishing wisdom and bliss (*Sarasvatī* and *Lakṣmī* potencies) that blossom when the energy rises to the heart center (*Anāhata*)."]},{"number":35,"name":"लक्ष्यरोमलताधारतासमुन्नेयमध्यमा","samasa":["• लक्ष्यितुं योग्या या रोमलताधारता तया सम्यगुन्नेयं मध्यमं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["लक्ष्य — to be inferred; to be noticed","रोमलता — creeper-like line of hair","आधारता — state of being the support/base","समुन्नेय — to be presumed; inferred","मध्यमा — waist; middle","लक्ष्यरोमलताधारतासमुन्नेयमध्यमा — She whose waist is inferred as the base of the creeper-like hair-line"],"summary":["लक्ष्यरोमलताधारतासमुन्नेयमध्यमा means one for whom, the existence of a waist base for the climbing creeper of line of hair is to be presumed. The creeper of hair line mentioned in the previous name is visible. But the base where the root of the creeper is located is not to be seen. The existence of a limb as waist is to be presumed. As per Sāmudrika Śāstra, the waist of upper classes of women will be so small as to be presumed as non-existent."],"searchText":"35 लक्ष्यरोमलताधारतासमुन्नेयमध्यमा • लक्ष्यितुं योग्या या रोमलताधारता तया सम्यगुन्नेयं मध्यमं यस्याः सा। लक्ष्य — to be inferred; to be noticed रोमलता — creeper-like line of hair आधारता — state of being the support/base समुन्नेय — to be presumed; inferred मध्यमा — waist; middle लक्ष्यरोमलताधारतासमुन्नेयमध्यमा — she whose waist is inferred as the base of the creeper-like hair-line लक्ष्यरोमलताधारतासमुन्नेयमध्यमा means one for whom, the existence of a waist base for the climbing creeper of line of hair is to be presumed. the creeper of hair line mentioned in the previous name is visible. but the base where the root of the creeper is located is not to be seen. the existence of a limb as waist is to be presumed. as per sāmudrika śāstra, the waist of upper classes of women will be so small as to be presumed as non-existent. * **the inferred reality of brahman:** in sanskrit poetics, an incredibly slender waist represents beauty. the waist (representing the supreme, unmanifest *brahman*) cannot be seen directly by the physical senses. however, its existence is masterfully inferred by looking at the manifest world of name and form (the hairline).","esoteric":["* **The Inferred Reality of Brahman:** In Sanskrit poetics, an incredibly slender waist represents beauty. The waist (representing the supreme, unmanifest *Brahman*) cannot be seen directly by the physical senses. However, its existence is masterfully inferred by looking at the manifest world of name and form (the hairline)."]},{"number":36,"name":"स्तनभारदलन्मध्यपट्टबन्धवलित्रया","samasa":["• स्तनयोः भारेण दलत इव मध्यस्य पट्टबन्धः एव वलित्रयं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्तनभार — weight of the breasts","दलत् — breaking; cracking as if","मध्य — middle; waist","पट्टबन्ध — bandage; belt-like binding","वलित्रय — three folds","स्तनभारदलन्मध्यपट्टबन्धवलित्रया — She whose three abdominal folds appear as bandages around a waist breaking under the weight of Her breasts"],"summary":["स्तनभारदलन्मध्यपट्टबन्धवलित्रया means one whose three folds in the abdominal area appear to be three bandages worn on the waist to prevent it from breaking due to the weight of the breasts. Sāmudrika Śāstra specifies that higher class men and women will have three lines (folds) on their forehead, neck and abdomen. They are signs of extremely good fortune."],"searchText":"36 स्तनभारदलन्मध्यपट्टबन्धवलित्रया • स्तनयोः भारेण दलत इव मध्यस्य पट्टबन्धः एव वलित्रयं यस्याः सा। स्तनभार — weight of the breasts दलत् — breaking; cracking as if मध्य — middle; waist पट्टबन्ध — bandage; belt-like binding वलित्रय — three folds स्तनभारदलन्मध्यपट्टबन्धवलित्रया — she whose three abdominal folds appear as bandages around a waist breaking under the weight of her breasts स्तनभारदलन्मध्यपट्टबन्धवलित्रया means one whose three folds in the abdominal area appear to be three bandages worn on the waist to prevent it from breaking due to the weight of the breasts. sāmudrika śāstra specifies that higher class men and women will have three lines (folds) on their forehead, neck and abdomen. they are signs of extremely good fortune. * **the three folds of space-time:** the three folds (*vali-traya*) represent the three cosmic boundaries: the three *guṇas* (sattva, rajas, tamas), the three worlds, and the three divisions of time (past, present, future). these boundaries act as the \"protective binding strap\" (*paṭṭabandha*) that stabilizes and holds the weight of manifest creation, preventing the absolute unmanifest consciousness from collapsing.","esoteric":["* **The Three Folds of Space-Time:** The three folds (*vali-traya*) represent the three cosmic boundaries: the three *Guṇas* (Sattva, Rajas, Tamas), the three worlds, and the three divisions of time (past, present, future). These boundaries act as the \"protective binding strap\" (*paṭṭabandha*) that stabilizes and holds the weight of manifest creation, preventing the absolute unmanifest consciousness from collapsing."]},{"number":37,"name":"अरुणारुणकौसुम्भवस्त्रभास्वत्कटीतटी","samasa":["• अरुणारुणेन (अतिशयेन अरुणेन अरुणवद् अरुणं वा) कौसुम्भं यद् वस्त्रं तेन भास्वती कट्याः तटी यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अरुणारुण — deep red; crimson","कौसुम्भ — red silk dyed with Kusumbha","वस्त्र — cloth","भास्वत् — shining","कटीतटी — slope/region of the waist","अरुणारुणकौसुम्भवस्त्रभास्वत्कटीतटी — She whose waist shines with crimson-red silk cloth"],"summary":["अरुणारुणकौसुम्भवस्त्रभास्वत्कटीतटी means one whose waist shines with the crimson silk worn on it. The dual expression aruṇa-aruṇa means dark red or Crimson. The Red here is like that of Aruṇa, the charioteer of the Sun God, who rises before Sun rises. Kausumbha vastra means Red silk cloth. The juice of kausumbha herb is used to dye cloths in Red; hence kausumbha vastra. Śrīdevī has worn kausumbha vastra on Her waist. It appears as though Aruṇa Vāgdevatā’s name is indirectly stated here."],"searchText":"37 अरुणारुणकौसुम्भवस्त्रभास्वत्कटीतटी • अरुणारुणेन (अतिशयेन अरुणेन अरुणवद् अरुणं वा) कौसुम्भं यद् वस्त्रं तेन भास्वती कट्याः तटी यस्याः सा। अरुणारुण — deep red; crimson कौसुम्भ — red silk dyed with kusumbha वस्त्र — cloth भास्वत् — shining कटीतटी — slope/region of the waist अरुणारुणकौसुम्भवस्त्रभास्वत्कटीतटी — she whose waist shines with crimson-red silk cloth अरुणारुणकौसुम्भवस्त्रभास्वत्कटीतटी means one whose waist shines with the crimson silk worn on it. the dual expression aruṇa-aruṇa means dark red or crimson. the red here is like that of aruṇa, the charioteer of the sun god, who rises before sun rises. kausumbha vastra means red silk cloth. the juice of kausumbha herb is used to dye cloths in red; hence kausumbha vastra. śrīdevī has worn kausumbha vastra on her waist. it appears as though aruṇa vāgdevatā’s name is indirectly stated here. * **the garment of pure desire:** safflower (*kusumbha*) yields a vibrant, glowing red dye. the hip region corresponds to the **स्वाधिष्ठान** (*svādhiṣṭhāna*) and **मूलाधार** (*mūlādhāra*) cakras, which govern primal energy and stability. her intensely red garment represents the covering of **इच्छाशक्ति** (*icchā-śakti* — pure will and creative desire) that wraps around the root of cosmic manifestation.","esoteric":["* **The Garment of Pure Desire:** Safflower (*kusumbha*) yields a vibrant, glowing red dye. The hip region corresponds to the **स्वाधिष्ठान** (*Svādhiṣṭhāna*) and **मूलाधार** (*Mūlādhāra*) cakras, which govern primal energy and stability. Her intensely red garment represents the covering of **इच्छाशक्ति** (*Icchā-śakti* — pure will and creative desire) that wraps around the root of cosmic manifestation."]},{"number":38,"name":"रत्नकिङ्किणिकारम्यरशनादामभूषिता","samasa":["• रत्नैः (रत्नमयीभिः) किङ्किणिकाभिः रम्येण रशनया एव दाम्या भूषिता।"],"wordByWord":["रत्न — gem","किङ्किणिका — small tinkling bell","रम्य — beautiful","रशना — girdle; waist-string","दाम — garland/string","भूषिता — adorned","रत्नकिङ्किणिकारम्यरशनादामभूषिता — She adorned with a beautiful girdle-string lined with gem-bells"],"summary":["रत्नकिङ्किणिकारम्यरशनादामभूषिता means one who wears a girdle string (mekhalā-sūtra) lined with tinkling gems. The golden girdle string is lined with small tinkle bells. The small gems inside the bells make a soft pleasant sound. The part of Śrīdevī's body below the neck and above the thigh represents the central portion of Pañcadaśākṣarī mantra consisting of six letters."],"searchText":"38 रत्नकिङ्किणिकारम्यरशनादामभूषिता • रत्नैः (रत्नमयीभिः) किङ्किणिकाभिः रम्येण रशनया एव दाम्या भूषिता। रत्न — gem किङ्किणिका — small tinkling bell रम्य — beautiful रशना — girdle; waist-string दाम — garland/string भूषिता — adorned रत्नकिङ्किणिकारम्यरशनादामभूषिता — she adorned with a beautiful girdle-string lined with gem-bells रत्नकिङ्किणिकारम्यरशनादामभूषिता means one who wears a girdle string (mekhalā-sūtra) lined with tinkling gems. the golden girdle string is lined with small tinkle bells. the small gems inside the bells make a soft pleasant sound. the part of śrīdevī's body below the neck and above the thigh represents the central portion of pañcadaśākṣarī mantra consisting of six letters. * **the rhythms of the cosmos:** the belt is tied around the waist, stabilizing the center of gravity. the jingling of the tiny bells (*kiṅkiṇikā*) represents the subtle, rhythmic vibrations of the unmanifest sound (*aṇu-nāda* or *nāda-bindu*) that continuously hums at the base of creation, driving the cycles of nature.","esoteric":["* **The Rhythms of the Cosmos:** The belt is tied around the waist, stabilizing the center of gravity. The jingling of the tiny bells (*kiṅkiṇikā*) represents the subtle, rhythmic vibrations of the unmanifest sound (*Aṇu-nāda* or *Nāda-bindu*) that continuously hums at the base of creation, driving the cycles of nature."]},{"number":39,"name":"कामेशज्ञातसौभाग्यमार्दवोरुद्वयान्विता","samasa":["• कामेशेन एव ज्ञाते सौभाग्यमार्दवे ययोः ऊर्वोः तयोः द्वयेन अन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["कामेश — Sree Kameshwara","ज्ञात — known","सौभाग्य — exquisiteness; beauty","मार्दव — softness","ऊरुद्वय — two thighs","अन्विता — endowed with","कामेशज्ञातसौभाग्यमार्दवोरुद्वयान्विता — She endowed with two thighs whose beauty and softness are known only to Kameshwara"],"summary":["कामेशज्ञातसौभाग्यमार्दवोरुद्वयान्विता means one who has two beautiful and soft thighs known only to Śrī Kāmeśvara. The softness and the smoothness of Her thighs are known only to Śrī Kāmeśvara. Saubhāgya here means exquisiteness or beauty."],"searchText":"39 कामेशज्ञातसौभाग्यमार्दवोरुद्वयान्विता • कामेशेन एव ज्ञाते सौभाग्यमार्दवे ययोः ऊर्वोः तयोः द्वयेन अन्विता। कामेश — sree kameshwara ज्ञात — known सौभाग्य — exquisiteness; beauty मार्दव — softness ऊरुद्वय — two thighs अन्विता — endowed with कामेशज्ञातसौभाग्यमार्दवोरुद्वयान्विता — she endowed with two thighs whose beauty and softness are known only to kameshwara कामेशज्ञातसौभाग्यमार्दवोरुद्वयान्विता means one who has two beautiful and soft thighs known only to śrī kāmeśvara. the softness and the smoothness of her thighs are known only to śrī kāmeśvara. saubhāgya here means exquisiteness or beauty. * **the unknowable essence of bliss:** the thighs are kept covered, symbolizing that which is secret and deeply private. her deepest bliss (*saubhāgya*) and tenderness (*mārdava*) are completely inaccessible to the external, dualistic mind. only when the individual consciousness completely dissolves into kāmeśvara (pure, non-dual subjective awareness) can this supreme, intimate state of divine bliss be realized.","esoteric":["* **The Unknowable Essence of Bliss:** The thighs are kept covered, symbolizing that which is secret and deeply private. Her deepest bliss (*saubhāgya*) and tenderness (*mārdava*) are completely inaccessible to the external, dualistic mind. Only when the individual consciousness completely dissolves into Kāmeśvara (pure, non-dual subjective awareness) can this supreme, intimate state of divine bliss be realized."]},{"number":40,"name":"माणिक्यमकुटाकारजानुद्वयविराजिता","samasa":["• माणिक्येन निर्मितस्य मकुटस्य इव आकारः ययोः जानुद्वययोः तयोः विराजिता।"],"wordByWord":["माणिक्य — ruby","मकुट — crown; hard cap","आकार — form; shape","जानुद्वय — two knees","विराजिता — shining","माणिक्यमकुटाकारजानुद्वयविराजिता — She whose two knees resemble ruby crowns"],"summary":["माणिक्यमकुटाकारजानुद्वयविराजिता means one whose knees resemble hard, Red caps made of rubies. The knees are so Red and seem to be like a hard cap. The softness of the thighs mentioned in the previous name is contrasted with the hardness of the knees. The reason for hardness of Śrīdevī's knees is stated in the 82nd verse of Saundaryalaharī. Mukuṭa and makuṭa — both have the same meaning."],"searchText":"40 माणिक्यमकुटाकारजानुद्वयविराजिता • माणिक्येन निर्मितस्य मकुटस्य इव आकारः ययोः जानुद्वययोः तयोः विराजिता। माणिक्य — ruby मकुट — crown; hard cap आकार — form; shape जानुद्वय — two knees विराजिता — shining माणिक्यमकुटाकारजानुद्वयविराजिता — she whose two knees resemble ruby crowns माणिक्यमकुटाकारजानुद्वयविराजिता means one whose knees resemble hard, red caps made of rubies. the knees are so red and seem to be like a hard cap. the softness of the thighs mentioned in the previous name is contrasted with the hardness of the knees. the reason for hardness of śrīdevī's knees is stated in the 82nd verse of saundaryalaharī. mukuṭa and makuṭa — both have the same meaning. * **the kneeling of cosmic powers:** the knees provide the structural pivot for bowing and kneeling.","esoteric":["* **The Kneeling of Cosmic Powers:** The knees provide the structural pivot for bowing and kneeling."]},{"number":41,"name":"इंद्रगोपपरिक्षिप्तस्मरतूणाभजंघिका","samasa":["• इंद्रगोपैः परितः क्षिप्तौ यौ स्मरस्य तूणौ तयोः तुल्ये जङ्घिके यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["इन्द्रगोप — firefly/red insect","परिक्षिप्त — surrounded","स्मर — Cupid","तूण — quiver","जंघिका — shanks","इंद्रगोपपरिक्षिप्तस्मरतूणाभजंघिका — She whose shanks resemble Cupid’s quiver surrounded by fireflies"],"summary":["इंद्रगोपपरिक्षिप्तस्मरतूणाभजंघिका means one whose shanks resemble Cupid's quiver surrounded by fireflies. A quiver is a case for carrying arrows, carried by the warriors, with a broad mouth and tapered at the bottom. The two shanks of Śrīdevī are firm and reddish. This resembles Cupid's quiver surrounded by insects sparkling at night. The brightness of the ankles is enhanced by the sparkling insects. The reddish legs are glowing naturally, but as a metaphor this is compared to the fireflies shining in the night. Śrī Ādi Śaṅkara says in 83rd verse of Saundaryalaharī, that Cupid, who was burnt down by Lord Śiva was waiting for an opportunity to seek revenge on Him, and when He was attracted by Śrīdevī's beauty, Cupid made Śrīdevī's shanks his quiver and Her toes his arrows; parājetuṃ rudraṃ dviguṇaśaragarbhau girisute niṣaṅgau jaṅghe te viṣamaviśikho bāḍhamakṛta."],"searchText":"41 इंद्रगोपपरिक्षिप्तस्मरतूणाभजंघिका • इंद्रगोपैः परितः क्षिप्तौ यौ स्मरस्य तूणौ तयोः तुल्ये जङ्घिके यस्याः सा। इन्द्रगोप — firefly/red insect परिक्षिप्त — surrounded स्मर — cupid तूण — quiver जंघिका — shanks इंद्रगोपपरिक्षिप्तस्मरतूणाभजंघिका — she whose shanks resemble cupid’s quiver surrounded by fireflies इंद्रगोपपरिक्षिप्तस्मरतूणाभजंघिका means one whose shanks resemble cupid's quiver surrounded by fireflies. a quiver is a case for carrying arrows, carried by the warriors, with a broad mouth and tapered at the bottom. the two shanks of śrīdevī are firm and reddish. this resembles cupid's quiver surrounded by insects sparkling at night. the brightness of the ankles is enhanced by the sparkling insects. the reddish legs are glowing naturally, but as a metaphor this is compared to the fireflies shining in the night. śrī ādi śaṅkara says in 83rd verse of saundaryalaharī, that cupid, who was burnt down by lord śiva was waiting for an opportunity to seek revenge on him, and when he was attracted by śrīdevī's beauty, cupid made śrīdevī's shanks his quiver and her toes his arrows; parājetuṃ rudraṃ dviguṇaśaragarbhau girisute niṣaṅgau jaṅghe te viṣamaviśikho bāḍhamakṛta. * **the quivers of creative force:** the quivers of cupid hold the arrows of desire. the *indragopa* insect is famous in sanskrit literature for its deep, velvety crimson color. this indicates that her lower limbs hold the concentrated, velvet-red potential of all creative forces, ready to be deployed to guide and capture the minds of seekers, turning them away from worldly pursuits.","esoteric":["* **The Quivers of Creative Force:** The quivers of Cupid hold the arrows of desire. The *Indragopa* insect is famous in Sanskrit literature for its deep, velvety crimson color. This indicates that Her lower limbs hold the concentrated, velvet-red potential of all creative forces, ready to be deployed to guide and capture the minds of seekers, turning them away from worldly pursuits."]},{"number":42,"name":"गूढगुल्फा","samasa":["• गूढौ गुल्फौ यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["गूढ — hidden; covered","गुल्फ — ankle","गूढगुल्फा — She whose ankles are covered/hidden by firm muscles"],"summary":["गूढगुल्फा means one whose shanks are covered by firm muscles. Gulpha refers to the calf muscles above the ankles; it means firm and beautiful ankles."],"searchText":"42 गूढगुल्फा • गूढौ गुल्फौ यस्याः सा। गूढ — hidden; covered गुल्फ — ankle गूढगुल्फा — she whose ankles are covered/hidden by firm muscles गूढगुल्फा means one whose shanks are covered by firm muscles. gulpha refers to the calf muscles above the ankles; it means firm and beautiful ankles. * **the veiled path of yoga:** *gūḍha* means hidden or secret. in *aṣṭāṅga-yoga*, the ankles represent the physical structural transition to the feet (contact with the earth). her hidden ankles represent that the path of transitioning from material existence (*samsāra*) to spiritual elevation is deeply hidden and must be approached through secret, internal contemplation rather than ostentatious external display.","esoteric":["* **The Veiled Path of Yoga:** *Gūḍha* means hidden or secret. In *Aṣṭāṅga-yoga*, the ankles represent the physical structural transition to the feet (contact with the earth). Her hidden ankles represent that the path of transitioning from material existence (*Samsāra*) to spiritual elevation is deeply hidden and must be approached through secret, internal contemplation rather than ostentatious external display."]},{"number":43,"name":"कूर्मपृष्ठजयिष्णुप्रपदान्विता","samasa":["• कूर्मयोः पृष्ठे जयिष्णुनी (जयतः इति) ये प्रपदे (पादाग्रे) ताभ्याम् अन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["कूर्म — turtle","पृष्ठ — back","जयिष्णु — excelling; surpassing","प्रपद — forepart of foot; foot front","अन्विता — endowed with","कूर्मपृष्ठजयिष्णुप्रपदान्विता — She whose feet surpass the back of a turtle"],"summary":["कूर्मपृष्ठजयिष्णुप्रपदान्विता means one whose foot resembles a turtle's back. The back of the feet of higher class women would be pyramid like. In the absence of any other suitable comparison, turtle's back (though of an inferior class) is used as a simile. this simile is not the most appropriate one; padaṃ te kīrtīnāṃ prapadam apadaṃ devi vipadāṃ kathaṃ nītaṃ sadbhiḥ kaṭhinakamaṭhīkarparatulām."],"searchText":"43 कूर्मपृष्ठजयिष्णुप्रपदान्विता • कूर्मयोः पृष्ठे जयिष्णुनी (जयतः इति) ये प्रपदे (पादाग्रे) ताभ्याम् अन्विता। कूर्म — turtle पृष्ठ — back जयिष्णु — excelling; surpassing प्रपद — forepart of foot; foot front अन्विता — endowed with कूर्मपृष्ठजयिष्णुप्रपदान्विता — she whose feet surpass the back of a turtle कूर्मपृष्ठजयिष्णुप्रपदान्विता means one whose foot resembles a turtle's back. the back of the feet of higher class women would be pyramid like. in the absence of any other suitable comparison, turtle's back (though of an inferior class) is used as a simile. this simile is not the most appropriate one; padaṃ te kīrtīnāṃ prapadam apadaṃ devi vipadāṃ kathaṃ nītaṃ sadbhiḥ kaṭhinakamaṭhīkarparatulām. * **the base of cosmic stability:** the tortoise (*kūrma*) is the classic symbol of ultimate stability and withdrawal of the senses. by having feet that conquer the tortoise shell, she is identified as the supreme foundation of the entire universe, holding the pristine, unshakeable stability (**कूर्म-नाडी** — the channel of complete physical and mental stillness).","esoteric":["* **The Base of Cosmic Stability:** The tortoise (*Kūrma*) is the classic symbol of ultimate stability and withdrawal of the senses. By having feet that conquer the tortoise shell, She is identified as the supreme foundation of the entire universe, holding the pristine, unshakeable stability (**कूर्म-नाडी** — the channel of complete physical and mental stillness)."]},{"number":44,"name":"नखदीधितिसंछन्ननमज्जनतमोगुणा","samasa":["• नखानां दीधितिभिः (किरणैः) सम्यक् छन्नो नमतां जनानां तमोगुणः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["नख — nail","दीधिति — ray; lustre","संछन्न — covered; enveloped","नमज्जन — people who bow/prostrate","तमोगुण — darkness; ignorance","नखदीधितिसंछन्ननमज्जनतमोगुणा — She whose toenail rays cover and remove the darkness of those who bow to Her"],"summary":["नखदीधितिसंछन्ननमज्जनतमोगुणा means one who removes the darkness of ignorance of those who prostrate (tamo guṇa) before Her by the lustre of Her toe nails. When Brahmā, Viṣṇu and other devas prostrate before Śrīdevī's feet, the lustre of their crown face the lustre of Śrīdevī's toe nails, and unable to stand, their brightness go back inside them and remove the darkness of ignorance. Or, just by contact, the lustre of the toe nails removes the darkness of ignorance. Not only for the devas, but also for all those who worship Śrīdevī, the same benefit i.e. the removal of ignorance — is obtained."],"searchText":"44 नखदीधितिसंछन्ननमज्जनतमोगुणा • नखानां दीधितिभिः (किरणैः) सम्यक् छन्नो नमतां जनानां तमोगुणः यस्याः सा। नख — nail दीधिति — ray; lustre संछन्न — covered; enveloped नमज्जन — people who bow/prostrate तमोगुण — darkness; ignorance नखदीधितिसंछन्ननमज्जनतमोगुणा — she whose toenail rays cover and remove the darkness of those who bow to her नखदीधितिसंछन्ननमज्जनतमोगुणा means one who removes the darkness of ignorance of those who prostrate (tamo guṇa) before her by the lustre of her toe nails. when brahmā, viṣṇu and other devas prostrate before śrīdevī's feet, the lustre of their crown face the lustre of śrīdevī's toe nails, and unable to stand, their brightness go back inside them and remove the darkness of ignorance. or, just by contact, the lustre of the toe nails removes the darkness of ignorance. not only for the devas, but also for all those who worship śrīdevī, the same benefit i.e. the removal of ignorance — is obtained. * **the dawn of inner light:** *tamas* is the dark quality of inertia, sleep, and spiritual blindness. when a devotee bows their head to her feet, their crown (*sahasrāra*) comes into contact with the light rays emanating from her toe-nails. these ten toe-nails act like ten miniature suns, instantly dissolving the deep-seated darkness of spiritual ignorance (*avidyā*) and replacing it with the light of self-realization.","esoteric":["* **The Dawn of Inner Light:** *Tamas* is the dark quality of inertia, sleep, and spiritual blindness. When a devotee bows their head to Her feet, their crown (*Sahasrāra*) comes into contact with the light rays emanating from Her toe-nails. These ten toe-nails act like ten miniature suns, instantly dissolving the deep-seated darkness of spiritual ignorance (*Avidyā*) and replacing it with the light of self-realization."]},{"number":45,"name":"पदद्वयप्रभाजालपराकृतसरोरुहा","samasa":["• पदद्वयस्य प्रभाजालेन पराकृते सरोरुहे यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पदद्वय — two feet","प्रभाजाल — net/mass of lustre","पराकृत — surpassed; defeated","सरोरुह — lotus","पदद्वयप्रभाजालपराकृतसरोरुहा — She whose two feet surpass the lotus by their lustre"],"summary":["पदद्वयप्रभाजालपराकृतसरोरुहा means one who won over the lotus flower by the lustre of Her two feet. Generally, it is a literary tradition to take the lotus flower for comparison with the face, feet and eyes of beautiful men and women. Lustre, softness, beautiful structure and a lovely appearance are the special features of a lotus. In the case of Śrīdevī's feet, there is one more special characteristic. Lotus will blossom and shrivel on the same day, whereas Śrīdevī's feet remain permanently lustrous, and thus they win over lotus."],"searchText":"45 पदद्वयप्रभाजालपराकृतसरोरुहा • पदद्वयस्य प्रभाजालेन पराकृते सरोरुहे यस्याः सा। पदद्वय — two feet प्रभाजाल — net/mass of lustre पराकृत — surpassed; defeated सरोरुह — lotus पदद्वयप्रभाजालपराकृतसरोरुहा — she whose two feet surpass the lotus by their lustre पदद्वयप्रभाजालपराकृतसरोरुहा means one who won over the lotus flower by the lustre of her two feet. generally, it is a literary tradition to take the lotus flower for comparison with the face, feet and eyes of beautiful men and women. lustre, softness, beautiful structure and a lovely appearance are the special features of a lotus. in the case of śrīdevī's feet, there is one more special characteristic. lotus will blossom and shrivel on the same day, whereas śrīdevī's feet remain permanently lustrous, and thus they win over lotus. * **the transcendent lotus:** the red lotus (*saroruha*) is the standard symbol of beauty and purity in the material world. however, the lotus grows out of mud and water. her feet, being pure consciousness, excel the lotus because they are entirely self-luminous (*svaprakāśa*) and free from any worldly origin. they represent the ultimate sanctuary of absolute purity.","esoteric":["* **The Transcendent Lotus:** The red lotus (*saroruha*) is the standard symbol of beauty and purity in the material world. However, the lotus grows out of mud and water. Her feet, being pure consciousness, excel the lotus because they are entirely self-luminous (*Svaprakāśa*) and free from any worldly origin. They represent the ultimate sanctuary of absolute purity."]},{"number":46,"name":"शिञ्जानमणिमञ्जीरमण्डितश्रीपदाम्बुजा","samasa":["• सिञ्जानाः मणयः ययोः मञ्जीरयोः ताभ्यां मण्डिता श्रीः ययोः पदाम्बुजयोः तादृशे पदाम्बुजे यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शिञ्जान — tinkling","मणि — gem","मञ्जीर — anklet","मण्डित — decorated","श्री — auspicious beauty","पदाम्बुज — lotus feet","शिञ्जानमणिमञ्जीरमण्डितश्रीपदाम्बुजा — She whose lotus feet are decorated with tinkling gem anklets"],"summary":["शिञ्जानमणिमञ्जीरमण्डितश्रीपदाम्बुजा means one whose Lotus feet are decorated with anklets with tinkling bells. The anklets worn on Śrīdevī's feet have bells fixed with gems. They make a sweet and soft jingle while oscillating. They add śrī to Her lotus feet. (Śrī is one word which cannot be translated into any other language, to bring forth its entire meaning). Broadly it means \"all that is good\". Śiñjana is another expression in some texts. The meaning is the same."],"searchText":"46 शिञ्जानमणिमञ्जीरमण्डितश्रीपदाम्बुजा • सिञ्जानाः मणयः ययोः मञ्जीरयोः ताभ्यां मण्डिता श्रीः ययोः पदाम्बुजयोः तादृशे पदाम्बुजे यस्याः सा। शिञ्जान — tinkling मणि — gem मञ्जीर — anklet मण्डित — decorated श्री — auspicious beauty पदाम्बुज — lotus feet शिञ्जानमणिमञ्जीरमण्डितश्रीपदाम्बुजा — she whose lotus feet are decorated with tinkling gem anklets शिञ्जानमणिमञ्जीरमण्डितश्रीपदाम्बुजा means one whose lotus feet are decorated with anklets with tinkling bells. the anklets worn on śrīdevī's feet have bells fixed with gems. they make a sweet and soft jingle while oscillating. they add śrī to her lotus feet. (śrī is one word which cannot be translated into any other language, to bring forth its entire meaning). broadly it means \"all that is good\". śiñjana is another expression in some texts. the meaning is the same. * **the melodies of creation:** the sweet tinkling (*siñjāna*) of her anklets represents the primordial cosmic sound (**नाद** — *nāda*). as she walks (manifests and directs cosmic processes), the movement of her feet unleashes the primary vibrations that organize chaos into ordered space and time. it is the music of the spheres playing at her feet.","esoteric":["* **The Melodies of Creation:** The sweet tinkling (*siñjāna*) of Her anklets represents the primordial cosmic sound (**नाद** — *Nāda*). As She walks (manifests and directs cosmic processes), the movement of Her feet unleashes the primary vibrations that organize chaos into ordered space and time. It is the music of the spheres playing at Her feet."]},{"number":47,"name":"मरालीमन्दगमना","samasa":["• मराली इव मन्दगमनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मराली — female swan","मन्द — slow; gentle","गमन — gait; movement","मरालीमन्दगमना — She whose gentle gait is like that of a female swan"],"summary":["मरालीमन्दगमना means one whose gait is slow and beautiful like a female swan. The gait of a swan is always soft and beautiful. The gait of a female swan is all the more graceful. Thus the female swan is compared. Everyone stands spellbound by the beauty of Śrīdevī coming out of the sacrificial fire. The same idea is expressed in Saundaryalaharī and Mūka Pañcaśatī. The swans in Śrīdevī's palace try to learn and copy the gait of Śrīdevī. The soft sound of Śrīdevī's anklets seem to teach lessons to the swans. Marālīnāṃ yam abhyāsanakalana-mūlagurave (Mūka Pañcaśatī — Pādāravinda Śatakam — 3). That part of Śrīdevī's body below the waist represents the Śaktikūṭa of Śrīdevī's mantra consisting of four syllables."],"searchText":"47 मरालीमन्दगमना • मराली इव मन्दगमनं यस्याः सा। मराली — female swan मन्द — slow; gentle गमन — gait; movement मरालीमन्दगमना — she whose gentle gait is like that of a female swan मरालीमन्दगमना means one whose gait is slow and beautiful like a female swan. the gait of a swan is always soft and beautiful. the gait of a female swan is all the more graceful. thus the female swan is compared. everyone stands spellbound by the beauty of śrīdevī coming out of the sacrificial fire. the same idea is expressed in saundaryalaharī and mūka pañcaśatī. the swans in śrīdevī's palace try to learn and copy the gait of śrīdevī. the soft sound of śrīdevī's anklets seem to teach lessons to the swans. marālīnāṃ yam abhyāsanakalana-mūlagurave (mūka pañcaśatī — pādāravinda śatakam — 3). that part of śrīdevī's body below the waist represents the śaktikūṭa of śrīdevī's mantra consisting of four syllables. * **the gait of ultimate discrimination:** the swan (*marālī* or *haṃsa*) is the ultimate symbol of spiritual discrimination (*viveka*), possessing the legendary ability to separate milk from water. her slow, majestic gait (*manda-gamana*) represents the steady, deliberate process of divine discrimination that separates the eternal reality (*nitya*) from the transient illusion (*anitya*) in the cosmos.","esoteric":["* **The Gait of Ultimate Discrimination:** The swan (*marālī* or *haṃsa*) is the ultimate symbol of spiritual discrimination (*Viveka*), possessing the legendary ability to separate milk from water. Her slow, majestic gait (*manda-gamana*) represents the steady, deliberate process of divine discrimination that separates the eternal reality (*Nitya*) from the transient illusion (*Anitya*) in the cosmos."]},{"number":48,"name":"महालावण्यशेवधिः","samasa":["• महतः लावण्यस्य शेवधिः।"],"wordByWord":["महा — great","लावण्य — beauty; charm","शेवधि — treasure; repository","महालावण्यशेवधिः — She who is the great repository of all beauty"],"summary":["महालावण्यशेवधिः means She is a repository or container of all beauty. Śrīdevī's divine beauty is unparalleled. Her face is described as a container gathering all the beauty. The below 12th verse of Saundaryalaharī may also be referred. tvadīyaṃ saundaryaṃ tuhinagirikanye tulayituṃ kavīndrāḥ kalpante kathamapi viriñciprabhṛtayaḥ."],"searchText":"48 महालावण्यशेवधिः • महतः लावण्यस्य शेवधिः। महा — great लावण्य — beauty; charm शेवधि — treasure; repository महालावण्यशेवधिः — she who is the great repository of all beauty महालावण्यशेवधिः means she is a repository or container of all beauty. śrīdevī's divine beauty is unparalleled. her face is described as a container gathering all the beauty. the below 12th verse of saundaryalaharī may also be referred. tvadīyaṃ saundaryaṃ tuhinagirikanye tulayituṃ kavīndrāḥ kalpante kathamapi viriñciprabhṛtayaḥ. * **the inexhaustible source of aesthetic grace:** *lāvaṇya* is not mere physical symmetry; it is defined in aesthetics as the glowing, fluid luster that shines through a form, like saltiness in food or light through a pearl. as the *śevadhi* (treasure-house), she is the singular source from which all beauty, art, harmony, and aesthetic joy in the universe are drawn.","esoteric":["* **The Inexhaustible Source of Aesthetic Grace:** *Lāvaṇya* is not mere physical symmetry; it is defined in aesthetics as the glowing, fluid luster that shines through a form, like saltiness in food or light through a pearl. As the *śevadhi* (treasure-house), She is the singular source from which all beauty, art, harmony, and aesthetic joy in the universe are drawn."]},{"number":49,"name":"सर्वारुणा","samasa":["• सर्वम् एव अरुणं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सर्व — all; entire","अरुण — red; crimson","सर्वारुणा — She who is entirely red/crimson"],"summary":["सर्वारुणा means Her body, garments, jewels, flower and lustre are all Red. It was not just because She emerged from the sacrificial fire, but it was natural to Her. Lauhityam etasya sarvasya vimarśaḥ — asau yas tāmro aruṇaḥ."],"searchText":"49 सर्वारुणा • सर्वम् एव अरुणं यस्याः सा। सर्व — all; entire अरुण — red; crimson सर्वारुणा — she who is entirely red/crimson सर्वारुणा means her body, garments, jewels, flower and lustre are all red. it was not just because she emerged from the sacrificial fire, but it was natural to her. lauhityam etasya sarvasya vimarśaḥ — asau yas tāmro aruṇaḥ. * **the uniform glow of self-reflection:** red (*aruṇa*) is the color of *vimarśa* (self-awareness and compassion). by being *sarvāruṇā*, there is no patch of darkness or other color within her. this signifies the absolute homogeneity (*ekarasatva*) of her non-dual nature. she is pure, unadulterated, uniform consciousness, radiating unconditional love and grace throughout the cosmos.","esoteric":["* **The Uniform Glow of Self-Reflection:** Red (*Aruṇa*) is the color of *Vimarśa* (Self-awareness and compassion). By being *Sarvāruṇā*, there is no patch of darkness or other color within Her. This signifies the absolute homogeneity (*Ekarasatva*) of Her non-dual nature. She is pure, unadulterated, uniform consciousness, radiating unconditional love and grace throughout the cosmos."]},{"number":50,"name":"अनवद्याङ्गी","samasa":["• अनवद्याङ्गी। न अवद्यानि अनवद्यानि। तानि अङ्गानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अनवद्य — faultless; without blemish","अङ्ग — limb","अनवद्याङ्गी — She whose limbs are flawless"],"summary":["अनवद्याङ्गी means one who has a flawless body structure. Her flawless body looked at from foot to head or from head to foot bestows bliss on those who are blessed to have a vision."],"searchText":"50 अनवद्याङ्गी • अनवद्याङ्गी। न अवद्यानि अनवद्यानि। तानि अङ्गानि यस्याः सा। अनवद्य — faultless; without blemish अङ्ग — limb अनवद्याङ्गी — she whose limbs are flawless अनवद्याङ्गी means one who has a flawless body structure. her flawless body looked at from foot to head or from head to foot bestows bliss on those who are blessed to have a vision. * **the flawless state of absolute reality:** *avadya* means that which can be criticized, limited, or found faulty. every created object in the relative world has some inherent defect or limitation. because she is the uncreated, primordial source of all being, her form (*aṅgī*) is completely flawless (*anavadya*), representing the pristine, unconditioned state of absolute perfection.","esoteric":["* **The Flawless State of Absolute Reality:** *Avadya* means that which can be criticized, limited, or found faulty. Every created object in the relative world has some inherent defect or limitation. Because She is the uncreated, primordial source of all being, Her form (*aṅgī*) is completely flawless (*anavadya*), representing the pristine, unconditioned state of absolute perfection."]},{"number":51,"name":"सर्वाभरणभूषिता","samasa":["• सर्वाभरणभूषिता। सर्वैः आभरणैः भूषिता।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वैः — all","भूषिता। — adorned"],"summary":["सर्वाभरणभूषिता means one who is adorned with all ornaments. The jewels worn by Śrīdevī, from the cūḍāmaṇi worn on the head to the toe ring, are described in Kalpa Sūtra, Kālikā Purāṇa, etc. For one who has a flawless body structure, all the jewels try to add to Her beauty, but fail in their attempts. On the other hand, the elegance of the jewels is enhanced by their presence on Śrīdevī's body. The list of jewels is given under the 235th name, Catuḥṣaṣṭyupacārāḍhyā. It can also be interpreted to mean that Śrīdevī is the one who endows the status of ornaments on the jewels worn by Her. The same name occurs as the 140th one in Lalitā Triśatī as Sarvābharaṇabhūṣitā or Sarvabhūṣaṇabhūṣitā."],"searchText":"51 सर्वाभरणभूषिता • सर्वाभरणभूषिता। सर्वैः आभरणैः भूषिता। सर्वैः — all भूषिता। — adorned सर्वाभरणभूषिता means one who is adorned with all ornaments. the jewels worn by śrīdevī, from the cūḍāmaṇi worn on the head to the toe ring, are described in kalpa sūtra, kālikā purāṇa, etc. for one who has a flawless body structure, all the jewels try to add to her beauty, but fail in their attempts. on the other hand, the elegance of the jewels is enhanced by their presence on śrīdevī's body. the list of jewels is given under the 235th name, catuḥṣaṣṭyupacārāḍhyā. it can also be interpreted to mean that śrīdevī is the one who endows the status of ornaments on the jewels worn by her. the same name occurs as the 140th one in lalitā triśatī as sarvābharaṇabhūṣitā or sarvabhūṣaṇabhūṣitā. the cosmos as her ornament: she does not require external gems to gain splendor; rather, the ornaments themselves gain beauty by touching her form. esoterically, the \"all ornaments\" (sarvābharaṇa) represent the entire manifest universe. the stars, planets, elements, and all levels of cosmic principles (tattvas) are the decorative jewels resting upon her infinite body of consciousness.","esoteric":["The Cosmos as Her Ornament: She does not require external gems to gain splendor; rather, the ornaments themselves gain beauty by touching Her form. Esoterically, the \"all ornaments\" (sarvābharaṇa) represent the entire manifest universe. The stars, planets, elements, and all levels of cosmic principles (tattvas) are the decorative jewels resting upon Her infinite body of consciousness."]},{"number":52,"name":"शिवकामेश्वराङ्कस्था","samasa":["• शिवश्च असौ कामश्च असौ ईश्वरश्चेति शिवकामेश्वरः। तस्य अङ्के तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["शिवकामेश्वराङ्कस्था means one who sits on the left lap of Her consort Śrī Śivakāmeśvara. Kāma means a beautiful person. Śiva means the auspicious one. Īśvara is the one who controls or rules over the actions of others according to his wish. Thus, He is Śivakāmeśvara. Kāmeśvara is one who is capable of taking any form of his choice. The statement ātmā vā idam agra āsīt, eka eva so'kāmayata conveys this idea. What is referred to here is the icchā śakti of the Supreme Being. All the explanations given above are equally applicable to Her."],"searchText":"52 शिवकामेश्वराङ्कस्था • शिवश्च असौ कामश्च असौ ईश्वरश्चेति शिवकामेश्वरः। तस्य अङ्के तिष्ठतीति। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. शिवकामेश्वराङ्कस्था means one who sits on the left lap of her consort śrī śivakāmeśvara. kāma means a beautiful person. śiva means the auspicious one. īśvara is the one who controls or rules over the actions of others according to his wish. thus, he is śivakāmeśvara. kāmeśvara is one who is capable of taking any form of his choice. the statement ātmā vā idam agra āsīt, eka eva so'kāmayata conveys this idea. what is referred to here is the icchā śakti of the supreme being. all the explanations given above are equally applicable to her. the union of stillness and kinship: aṅka means the lap, but it also represents the central point or locus. shiva-kāmeśvara represents prakāśa (unmoving, transcendent consciousness). she (as vimarśa or active self-awareness) resides permanently at the very core of his being. this sits at the center of the śrī cakra(bindu), symbolizing that creation only occurs when the transcendent father and dynamic mother exist in absolute, inseparable embrace.","esoteric":["The Union of Stillness and Kinship: Aṅka means the lap, but it also represents the central point or locus. Shiva-Kāmeśvara represents Prakāśa (unmoving, transcendent consciousness). She (as Vimarśa or active self-awareness) resides permanently at the very core of His being. This sits at the center of the Śrī Cakra(Bindu), symbolizing that creation only occurs when the transcendent father and dynamic mother exist in absolute, inseparable embrace."]},{"number":53,"name":"शिवा","samasa":["• शिवं करोतीति।","• शिवाभेदात् शिवा।","• शेते अस्मिन् सर्वमिति।"],"wordByWord":["शिवा — auspicious; Śiva","शिवं — auspicious; Śiva","शिवा। — auspicious; Śiva"],"summary":["शिवा means Śiva's consort, and hence She is inseparable from Śiva. She is the embodiment of auspiciousness, the bestower of auspiciousness, the icchā śakti of the Supreme Being, and liberation personified. Everything ultimately rests with Śrīdevī. Parameśvara has eight forms, namely Earth, Water, Fire, Wind, Space, Sun, Moon and jīva. His consort is Śivā."],"searchText":"53 शिवा • शिवं करोतीति। • शिवाभेदात् शिवा। • शेते अस्मिन् सर्वमिति। शिवा — auspicious; śiva शिवं — auspicious; śiva शिवा। — auspicious; śiva शिवा means śiva's consort, and hence she is inseparable from śiva. she is the embodiment of auspiciousness, the bestower of auspiciousness, the icchā śakti of the supreme being, and liberation personified. everything ultimately rests with śrīdevī. parameśvara has eight forms, namely earth, water, fire, wind, space, sun, moon and jīva. his consort is śivā. just as fire and its burning power are inseparable, shiva and his power of consciousness (śaktī) are one. she is śivā because she is the active delivery of his peaceful, auspicious nature to the universe. furthermore, as the ultimate resting place (śete asmin sarvam), she is the great cosmic womb into which all creation sleeps during the great dissolution (mahāpralaya).","esoteric":["Just as fire and its burning power are inseparable, Shiva and His power of consciousness (Śaktī) are one. She is Śivā because She is the active delivery of His peaceful, auspicious nature to the universe. Furthermore, as the ultimate resting place (śete asmin sarvam), She is the great cosmic womb into which all creation sleeps during the great dissolution (Mahāpralaya)."]},{"number":54,"name":"स्वाधीनवल्लभा","samasa":["• स्वस्याः अधीनः वल्लभः यस्याः/यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["वल्लभः — beloved consort"],"summary":["स्वाधीनवल्लभा means one who has a loving and amenable consort. Śiva's śakti (energy) is Devī. Energy is a characteristic feature, which cannot exist on its own, but always exists with matter. Thus it means that Śakti lives with Śiva and is obedient to Her. But in fact Śiva is controlled by Śakti and always seeks Her help in all his actions. In practice, if anybody is idle he is referred to as śava. One by whose grace women got their husbands. Sukanyā wed Cyavana, Śacī Devī wed Indra and Rukmiṇī wed Kṛṣṇa by worshipping Śrīdevī and by Her blessings. Although She is independent and not under the control of Parameśvara, She is his beloved. Svādhīna — independent; vallabha — beloved. When Vāgdevīs started to explain the dwelling of Śrīdevī, they first talk about the lap of Śiva and then continue to describe other dwellings."],"searchText":"54 स्वाधीनवल्लभा • स्वस्याः अधीनः वल्लभः यस्याः/यया सा। वल्लभः — beloved consort स्वाधीनवल्लभा means one who has a loving and amenable consort. śiva's śakti (energy) is devī. energy is a characteristic feature, which cannot exist on its own, but always exists with matter. thus it means that śakti lives with śiva and is obedient to her. but in fact śiva is controlled by śakti and always seeks her help in all his actions. in practice, if anybody is idle he is referred to as śava. one by whose grace women got their husbands. sukanyā wed cyavana, śacī devī wed indra and rukmiṇī wed kṛṣṇa by worshipping śrīdevī and by her blessings. although she is independent and not under the control of parameśvara, she is his beloved. svādhīna — independent; vallabha — beloved. when vāgdevīs started to explain the dwelling of śrīdevī, they first talk about the lap of śiva and then continue to describe other dwellings. the sovereignty of will: in external aesthetics, this describes a woman whose husband is completely devoted to her. esoterically, the vallabha (beloved) is shiva, who represents pure, unmoving existence. he remains passive and inactive until she activates him. because he yields his absolute power to her dynamic direction, she holds complete sway over him. it represents that the active expression of the divine is entirely the domain of her supreme will (स्वातन्त्र्यशक्ति — svātantrya-śakti).","esoteric":["The Sovereignty of Will: In external aesthetics, this describes a woman whose husband is completely devoted to Her. Esoterically, the Vallabha (beloved) is Shiva, who represents pure, unmoving existence. He remains passive and inactive until She activates Him. Because He yields His absolute power to Her dynamic direction, She holds complete sway over Him. It represents that the active expression of the divine is entirely the domain of Her supreme Will (स्वातन्त्र्यशक्ति — Svātantrya-śakti)."]},{"number":55,"name":"सुमेरुमध्यशृङ्गस्था","samasa":["• सुमेरुमध्यशृङ्गस्था।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["सुमेरुमध्यशृङ्गस्था means one who dwells in the central peak of mount Meru. Sumeru is a golden mountain which supports the Earth as its base. There are three peaks located triangularly in the centre of the mountain, and there is another fourth and higher peak at the centre of the triangle. The Śrīnagara where Śrīdevī dwells is in this fourth peak. These details are beautifully described in Lalitā-stavarāja written by sage Durvāsā."],"searchText":"55 सुमेरुमध्यशृङ्गस्था • सुमेरुमध्यशृङ्गस्था। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. सुमेरुमध्यशृङ्गस्था means one who dwells in the central peak of mount meru. sumeru is a golden mountain which supports the earth as its base. there are three peaks located triangularly in the centre of the mountain, and there is another fourth and higher peak at the centre of the triangle. the śrīnagara where śrīdevī dwells is in this fourth peak. these details are beautifully described in lalitā-stavarāja written by sage durvāsā. the axis of the subtle body: mount sumeru is the cosmic golden mountain at the center of the universe. in the esoteric geography of the subtle body (piṇḍāṇḍa), sumeru represents the spinal column (merudaṇḍa). the \"middle peak\" (madhya-śṛṅga) is the topmost point of this axis—the sahasrāra at the crown of the head. therefore, she is sumerumadhyaśṛṅgasthā because her ultimate, supreme station of rest is the crown center of non-dual union.","esoteric":["The Axis of the Subtle Body: Mount Sumeru is the cosmic golden mountain at the center of the universe. In the esoteric geography of the subtle body (Piṇḍāṇḍa), Sumeru represents the spinal column (Merudaṇḍa). The \"middle peak\" (madhya-śṛṅga) is the topmost point of this axis—the Sahasrāra at the crown of the head. Therefore, She is Sumerumadhyaśṛṅgasthā because Her ultimate, supreme station of rest is the crown center of non-dual union."]},{"number":56,"name":"श्रीमन्नगरनायिका","samasa":["• श्रीमत् नगरं श्रीमन्नगरम्। तस्य नायिका।"],"wordByWord":["नगरं — city","नायिका। — mistress; leader"],"summary":["श्रीमन्नगरनायिका means the head of Śrīnagara. Śrīnagara is always known as Śrīmad Lakṣmī Vidyā Nagaram, and Śrīdevī is its head of state. This city (nagara) is said to be in two locations; one is as stated in Lalitā-stavarāja. The other is the centre of Sudhāsamudra as told in Rudrayāmala. Śrīmannagaram may also be understood to mean Śrīcakra and hence Śrīcakra nāyikā. This has also been stated in Gauḍapāda Sūtras."],"searchText":"56 श्रीमन्नगरनायिका • श्रीमत् नगरं श्रीमन्नगरम्। तस्य नायिका। नगरं — city नायिका। — mistress; leader श्रीमन्नगरनायिका means the head of śrīnagara. śrīnagara is always known as śrīmad lakṣmī vidyā nagaram, and śrīdevī is its head of state. this city (nagara) is said to be in two locations; one is as stated in lalitā-stavarāja. the other is the centre of sudhāsamudra as told in rudrayāmala. śrīmannagaram may also be understood to mean śrīcakra and hence śrīcakra nāyikā. this has also been stated in gauḍapāda sūtras. the citadel of consciousness: śrī-nagara is the mystical, multi-walled city described in śākta cosmology. esoterically, this city is the śrī cakra itself, which maps the entire journey of consciousness from the outer gates of the physical world to the central point of the self. she is the nāyikā (the commanding directress) because she rules over every gateway, enclosure, and sub-deity (āvaraṇa devatā) within this cosmic diagram.","esoteric":["The Citadel of Consciousness: Śrī-Nagara is the mystical, multi-walled city described in Śākta cosmology. Esoterically, this city is the Śrī Cakra itself, which maps the entire journey of consciousness from the outer gates of the physical world to the central point of the Self. She is the Nāyikā (the commanding directress) because She rules over every gateway, enclosure, and sub-deity (Āvaraṇa Devatā) within this cosmic diagram."]},{"number":57,"name":"चिन्तामणिगृहान्तस्था","samasa":["• चिन्तामणिभिः रचितं गृहं चिन्तामणिगृहम्। तस्य अन्तः तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["गृहं — house","अन्तः — inside"],"summary":["चिन्तामणिगृहान्तस्था means one who dwells in a house constructed of cintāmaṇi. Cintāmaṇi is a gemstone which bestows all the desires of the mind. Cintāmaṇi-gṛha is a palace built with cintāmaṇi gems. She dwells in it. The syllables in Śrīdevī's mantra are also capable of bestowing what the mind desires and hence referred to as cintāmaṇi. Śrīdevī dwells in those syllables (bījākṣaras)."],"searchText":"57 चिन्तामणिगृहान्तस्था • चिन्तामणिभिः रचितं गृहं चिन्तामणिगृहम्। तस्य अन्तः तिष्ठतीति। गृहं — house अन्तः — inside चिन्तामणिगृहान्तस्था means one who dwells in a house constructed of cintāmaṇi. cintāmaṇi is a gemstone which bestows all the desires of the mind. cintāmaṇi-gṛha is a palace built with cintāmaṇi gems. she dwells in it. the syllables in śrīdevī's mantra are also capable of bestowing what the mind desires and hence referred to as cintāmaṇi. śrīdevī dwells in those syllables (bījākṣaras). the temple of pure intellect: the cintāmaṇi is a gem that instantly yields whatever is thought of (cintita). esoterically, the cintāmaṇi-gṛha is the heart-space (dahara-ākāśa) of a purified seeker whose thoughts are completely aligned with the divine. she dwells deep within this refined state of mind, demonstrating that she is easily reached and experienced when the intellect is cleared of worldly desires.","esoteric":["The Temple of Pure Intellect: The Cintāmaṇi is a gem that instantly yields whatever is thought of (cintita). Esoterically, the Cintāmaṇi-gṛha is the heart-space (Dahara-ākāśa) of a purified seeker whose thoughts are completely aligned with the divine. She dwells deep within this refined state of mind, demonstrating that She is easily reached and experienced when the intellect is cleared of worldly desires."]},{"number":58,"name":"पञ्चब्रह्मासनस्थिता","samasa":["• पञ्चभिः ब्रह्मभिः निर्मितं आसनं पञ्चब्रह्मासनम्। तस्मिन् स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्चभिः — with five","ब्रह्मभिः — Brahmā/Brahman","आसनं — seat","स्थिता। — situated"],"summary":["पञ्चब्रह्मासनस्थिता means one who sits on a seat made of five Brahmans. These Brahmans respectively are the legs on Southeast, Southwest, Northwest and Northeast directions and the sitting plank. Since all these five emerge from and ultimately converge in the same Parabrahman, they are also referred to as Brahmans. Sometimes Śrīdevī absorbs in Herself the energies of these five Brahmans like creation, etc. In those situations these five Brahmans are called pañcapretas."],"searchText":"58 पञ्चब्रह्मासनस्थिता • पञ्चभिः ब्रह्मभिः निर्मितं आसनं पञ्चब्रह्मासनम्। तस्मिन् स्थिता। पञ्चभिः — with five ब्रह्मभिः — brahmā/brahman आसनं — seat स्थिता। — situated पञ्चब्रह्मासनस्थिता means one who sits on a seat made of five brahmans. these brahmans respectively are the legs on southeast, southwest, northwest and northeast directions and the sitting plank. since all these five emerge from and ultimately converge in the same parabrahman, they are also referred to as brahmans. sometimes śrīdevī absorbs in herself the energies of these five brahmans like creation, etc. in those situations these five brahmans are called pañcapretas. the sovereign of five cosmic functions: the \"five brahmās\" are the five deities responsible for the cosmic cycles: brahmā (creation), viṣṇu(preservation), rudra (dissolution), īśvara (concealment), and sadāśiva (grace). these five act merely as the physical legs and plank of her royal seat. this shows that the highest cosmic powers are entirely subordinate to her, serving as instruments for her supreme, play-filled commands.","esoteric":["The Sovereign of Five Cosmic Functions: The \"five Brahmās\" are the five deities responsible for the cosmic cycles: Brahmā (Creation), Viṣṇu(Preservation), Rudra (Dissolution), Īśvara (Concealment), and Sadāśiva (Grace). These five act merely as the physical legs and plank of Her royal seat. This shows that the highest cosmic powers are entirely subordinate to Her, serving as instruments for Her supreme, play-filled commands."]},{"number":59,"name":"महापद्माटवीसंस्था","samasa":["• महान्ति पद्मानि यस्याम् अटव्यां सम्यक् तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["पद्मानि — lotus"],"summary":["महापद्माटवीसंस्था means one who lives in a great lotus forest. This jungle is in the centre of Cintāmaṇi-gṛha. She also lives in the brahmarandhra, below the skull, in a lotus with thousand or countless petals. Mahāpadma is a superior species of elephants. The forest inhabited by such elephants is Gajāraṇya, also known as Tiruvānaikā, a temple near Tiruchirapalli in Tamil Nadu. The presiding deity of this temple is Śrī Akhilāṇḍeśvarī."],"searchText":"59 महापद्माटवीसंस्था • महान्ति पद्मानि यस्याम् अटव्यां सम्यक् तिष्ठतीति। पद्मानि — lotus महापद्माटवीसंस्था means one who lives in a great lotus forest. this jungle is in the centre of cintāmaṇi-gṛha. she also lives in the brahmarandhra, below the skull, in a lotus with thousand or countless petals. mahāpadma is a superior species of elephants. the forest inhabited by such elephants is gajāraṇya, also known as tiruvānaikā, a temple near tiruchirapalli in tamil nadu. the presiding deity of this temple is śrī akhilāṇḍeśvarī. the forest of spiritual centers: in the subtle anatomy of yoga, each energy center (cakra) is represented as a lotus. the \"great lotus forest\" (mahā-padmāṭavī) represents the entire system of these interconnected spiritual centers within the subtle body. she is saṃsthā (fully established) throughout this forest, indicating that she is the singular, underlying lifeforce running through every single node of the energy network.","esoteric":["The Forest of Spiritual Centers: In the subtle anatomy of yoga, each energy center (cakra) is represented as a lotus. The \"Great Lotus Forest\" (Mahā-padmāṭavī) represents the entire system of these interconnected spiritual centers within the subtle body. She is Saṃsthā (fully established) throughout this forest, indicating that She is the singular, underlying lifeforce running through every single node of the energy network."]},{"number":60,"name":"कदम्बवनवासिनी","samasa":["• कदम्बानां वने वसतीति।"],"wordByWord":["वने — forest"],"summary":["कदम्बवनवासिनी means one who lives in kadamba woods. Cintāmaṇi-gṛha is a palace of gems surrounded by a jungle of kadamba trees. Śrīdevī dwells in this jungle. Śrīpura is surrounded by 25 walls made of metals and gems representing 25 concepts (tattvas). The kadamba jungle is located between the gold and silver walls. Madurai, a holy city in Tamil Nadu, is also known as Kadambavana. Śrīdevī is the presiding deity there with the name Mīnākṣī."],"searchText":"60 कदम्बवनवासिनी • कदम्बानां वने वसतीति। वने — forest कदम्बवनवासिनी means one who lives in kadamba woods. cintāmaṇi-gṛha is a palace of gems surrounded by a jungle of kadamba trees. śrīdevī dwells in this jungle. śrīpura is surrounded by 25 walls made of metals and gems representing 25 concepts (tattvas). the kadamba jungle is located between the gold and silver walls. madurai, a holy city in tamil nadu, is also known as kadambavana. śrīdevī is the presiding deity there with the name mīnākṣī. the realm of sweet manifestation: the kadamba forest represents the thick, lush variety of the manifest world. the kadamba blossom is noted for its spherical, golden shape and sweet fragrance. by dwelling in this forest, she shows that her presence is not confined to ascetic withdrawal; she is actively present and can be experienced within the rich, sweet, and fragrant variety of life itself.","esoteric":["The Realm of Sweet Manifestation: The Kadamba forest represents the thick, lush variety of the manifest world. The Kadamba blossom is noted for its spherical, golden shape and sweet fragrance. By dwelling in this forest, She shows that Her presence is not confined to ascetic withdrawal; She is actively present and can be experienced within the rich, sweet, and fragrant variety of life itself."]},{"number":61,"name":"सुधासागरमध्यस्था","samasa":["• सुधायाः सागरस्य मध्ये तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["सुधायाः — nectar","सागरस्य — ocean","मध्ये — middle"],"summary":["सुधासागरमध्यस्था means one who lives in the centre of the ocean of nectar. The location of this ocean of nectar is given differently in various sources. the Cintāmaṇi-gṛha is located in this ocean. this ocean is located in the city of Aparājitā, which can be reached by worshipping a god with attributes (saguṇopāsanā). Aparājitā for Śrīdevī worshippers is like Kailāsa for Śiva worshippers and Śrī Vaikuṇṭha for Viṣṇu's worshippers. There are two tanks in this city called Āram and Nyam, which are referred to as Sudhā Sāgara."],"searchText":"61 सुधासागरमध्यस्था • सुधायाः सागरस्य मध्ये तिष्ठतीति। सुधायाः — nectar सागरस्य — ocean मध्ये — middle सुधासागरमध्यस्था means one who lives in the centre of the ocean of nectar. the location of this ocean of nectar is given differently in various sources. the cintāmaṇi-gṛha is located in this ocean. this ocean is located in the city of aparājitā, which can be reached by worshipping a god with attributes (saguṇopāsanā). aparājitā for śrīdevī worshippers is like kailāsa for śiva worshippers and śrī vaikuṇṭha for viṣṇu's worshippers. there are two tanks in this city called āram and nyam, which are referred to as sudhā sāgara. the reservoir of infinite bliss: the \"ocean of nectar\" represents the infinite, concentrated reservoir of spiritual bliss (ānanda-rasa) that lies within the sahasrāra. when the kuṇḍalinī energy reaches this crown center, it releases a flood of cool, ecstatic nectar. she sits at the very center (madhyasthā) of this reservoir, showing that she is the ultimate source and keeper of that supreme, non-dual joy.","esoteric":["The Reservoir of Infinite Bliss: The \"ocean of nectar\" represents the infinite, concentrated reservoir of spiritual bliss (Ānanda-rasa) that lies within the Sahasrāra. When the Kuṇḍalinī energy reaches this crown center, it releases a flood of cool, ecstatic nectar. She sits at the very center (madhyasthā) of this reservoir, showing that She is the ultimate source and keeper of that supreme, non-dual joy."]},{"number":62,"name":"कामाक्षी","samasa":["• कामे अक्षिणी यस्याः सा।","• कामः ईश्वरः एव नेत्रः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कामे — desire; Kāma","कामः — desire; Kāma","ईश्वरः — lord"],"summary":["कामाक्षी means one with beautiful eyes. One who has beloved Kāmeśvara as Her eyes. One who bestows all desires of Her devotees by Her eyes. One who has Sarasvatī (Kā) and Lakṣmī (Mā) as Her eyes. Brahmā performed a sacrifice in this place seeking the powers of creation. Śrīdevī was called Kāmākṣī as She fulfilled Brahmā's desires. Kāma (Cupid) was destroyed by Paramaśiva's third eye and restored to life by Śrīdevī's vision. Thus Kāmākṣī."],"searchText":"62 कामाक्षी • कामे अक्षिणी यस्याः सा। • कामः ईश्वरः एव नेत्रः यस्याः सा। कामे — desire; kāma कामः — desire; kāma ईश्वरः — lord कामाक्षी means one with beautiful eyes. one who has beloved kāmeśvara as her eyes. one who bestows all desires of her devotees by her eyes. one who has sarasvatī (kā) and lakṣmī (mā) as her eyes. brahmā performed a sacrifice in this place seeking the powers of creation. śrīdevī was called kāmākṣī as she fulfilled brahmā's desires. kāma (cupid) was destroyed by paramaśiva's third eye and restored to life by śrīdevī's vision. thus kāmākṣī. the glance of creation and grace: kāma here represents the divine, unselfish desire to bless and liberate. her eyes are kāmākṣī because a single glance from her possesses the power to instantly fulfill the spiritual aspirations of her devotees. alternatively, because shiva is her \"eyes,\" she perceives the entire universe through the lens of pure, non-dual consciousness.","esoteric":["The Glance of Creation and Grace: Kāma here represents the divine, unselfish desire to bless and liberate. Her eyes are Kāmākṣī because a single glance from Her possesses the power to instantly fulfill the spiritual aspirations of Her devotees. Alternatively, because Shiva is Her \"eyes,\" She perceives the entire universe through the lens of pure, non-dual consciousness."]},{"number":63,"name":"कामदायिनी","samasa":["• कामं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["कामं — desire; Kāma"],"summary":["कामदायिनी means one who fulfills Her devotees’ desires. Dāyinī means one who gives to Her devotees, and Kāma indicates Kāmeśvara; thus She leads Her devotees to Kāmeśvara and makes them one with Him. Kāmadāyinī means one who is auspiciously united with the destroyer of Kāma. Śrīdevī has Kāma as dāyam, hereditary property. Her association with Kāma is timeless."],"searchText":"63 कामदायिनी • कामं ददातीति। कामं — desire; kāma कामदायिनी means one who fulfills her devotees’ desires. dāyinī means one who gives to her devotees, and kāma indicates kāmeśvara; thus she leads her devotees to kāmeśvara and makes them one with him. kāmadāyinī means one who is auspiciously united with the destroyer of kāma. śrīdevī has kāma as dāyam, hereditary property. her association with kāma is timeless. the giver of the ultimate goal: while she fulfills the mundane, preliminary desires (puruṣārthas of dharma, artha, and kāma) of her devotees to build their trust, her ultimate gift is the supreme desire: मोक्ष (mokṣa — liberation). she is kāmadāyinī because she destroys the desire for limited, worldly objects and replaces it with the singular, consuming desire for self-realization.","esoteric":["The Giver of the Ultimate Goal: While She fulfills the mundane, preliminary desires (Puruṣārthas of Dharma, Artha, and Kāma) of Her devotees to build their trust, Her ultimate gift is the supreme desire: मोक्ष (Mokṣa — liberation). She is Kāmadāyinī because She destroys the desire for limited, worldly objects and replaces it with the singular, consuming desire for self-realization."]},{"number":64,"name":"देवर्षिगणसङ्घातस्तूयमानात्मवैभवा","samasa":["• देवानां गणश्च ऋषीनां गणश्च यः तयोः सङ्घातेन स्तूयमानः आत्मा (स्वरूपं) यस्य तद्वत् वैभवं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["देवानां — of the Devas","सङ्घातेन — multitude","स्तूयमानः — being praised","आत्मा — self","स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature","वैभवं — glory"],"summary":["देवर्षिगणसङ्घातस्तूयमानात्मवैभवा means one whom groups of devas and ṛṣis (gods and sages) pray to, and celebrate. Vibhu means omnipresent. Vaibhava is omnipresence. Śrīdevī is omnipresent so that She can bestow Her devotees' desires everywhere and immediately. Saṅghātastūyamāna means one whom groups of devas and sages pray to. Devas and sages pray to Her in various forms. Devas and sages pray to Śrīdevī to get released from this hell. If interpreted as samyak-ghāta, it means totally annihilated. Ātman is the dynamic form of Śrīdevī — omnipresent, omnipotent, love in all forms (sat, cit and ānanda — that is existence, knowledge and bliss). It is in this form that groups of devas and sages pray to Her. This ātman is the undivided form of Śrīdevī. Refer: sadānandaḥ pūrṇaḥ svātmāiva paradevatā Lalitā (Bhāvanopaniṣad — 28). In this name Śrīdevī's omnipresence, omnipotence and boundless energy are indicated."],"searchText":"64 देवर्षिगणसङ्घातस्तूयमानात्मवैभवा • देवानां गणश्च ऋषीनां गणश्च यः तयोः सङ्घातेन स्तूयमानः आत्मा (स्वरूपं) यस्य तद्वत् वैभवं यस्याः सा। देवानां — of the devas सङ्घातेन — multitude स्तूयमानः — being praised आत्मा — self स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature वैभवं — glory देवर्षिगणसङ्घातस्तूयमानात्मवैभवा means one whom groups of devas and ṛṣis (gods and sages) pray to, and celebrate. vibhu means omnipresent. vaibhava is omnipresence. śrīdevī is omnipresent so that she can bestow her devotees' desires everywhere and immediately. saṅghātastūyamāna means one whom groups of devas and sages pray to. devas and sages pray to her in various forms. devas and sages pray to śrīdevī to get released from this hell. if interpreted as samyak-ghāta, it means totally annihilated. ātman is the dynamic form of śrīdevī — omnipresent, omnipotent, love in all forms (sat, cit and ānanda — that is existence, knowledge and bliss). it is in this form that groups of devas and sages pray to her. this ātman is the undivided form of śrīdevī. refer: sadānandaḥ pūrṇaḥ svātmāiva paradevatā lalitā (bhāvanopaniṣad — 28). in this name śrīdevī's omnipresence, omnipotence and boundless energy are indicated. the focus of all cosmic intellects: the devas represent the shining cosmic administrative forces, and the ṛṣis represent the seers of ultimate truth. by having her glory continuously praised by them, it shows that the highest spiritual intellects and cosmic forces in the universe are constantly focused on and directed toward her. she is the ultimate destination of all cosmic and contemplative inquiry.","esoteric":["The Focus of All Cosmic Intellects: The Devas represent the shining cosmic administrative forces, and the Ṛṣis represent the seers of ultimate truth. By having Her glory continuously praised by them, it shows that the highest spiritual intellects and cosmic forces in the universe are constantly focused on and directed toward Her. She is the ultimate destination of all cosmic and contemplative inquiry."]},{"number":65,"name":"भण्डासुरवधोद्युक्तशक्तिसेनासमन्विता","samasa":["• भण्डनामकोऽसुरः भण्डासुरः। तस्य वधे उद्युक्तानां शक्तीनां सेनाभिः सम्यक् अन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["वधे — slaying","सेनाभिः — army"],"summary":["भण्डासुरवधोद्युक्तशक्तिसेनासमन्विता means one who is leading an army of Śaktis intent on destroying the demon called Bhaṇḍa. She stands prepared to achieve that objective with an army of Śaktis in different forms created by Her. One with whom the several forms of Śakti are an integral part. When Manmatha (Cupid) was reduced to ashes by the fire of Śiva's third eye, Lord Gaṇapati collected the ashes and made a male figure out of them. It came alive, did penance and obtained many boons from Śiva. Brahmā acclaimed this achievement saying, “Bhaṇḍ, Bhaṇḍ” (good, good), and hence he got the name Bhaṇḍāsura. His cruel demonic character was the result of his emergence from the ashes arising out of the fire of anger of Śiva. Śrīdevī came with the army of Śaktis to destroy him. Bhaṇḍa was bound by his own ignorance, and lived with the thought that sensual pleasures are supreme (asuṣu manyate asuraḥ). He was ignorant of his ātmasvarūpa (soul). It was necessary to destroy his cruel demonic character."],"searchText":"65 भण्डासुरवधोद्युक्तशक्तिसेनासमन्विता • भण्डनामकोऽसुरः भण्डासुरः। तस्य वधे उद्युक्तानां शक्तीनां सेनाभिः सम्यक् अन्विता। वधे — slaying सेनाभिः — army भण्डासुरवधोद्युक्तशक्तिसेनासमन्विता means one who is leading an army of śaktis intent on destroying the demon called bhaṇḍa. she stands prepared to achieve that objective with an army of śaktis in different forms created by her. one with whom the several forms of śakti are an integral part. when manmatha (cupid) was reduced to ashes by the fire of śiva's third eye, lord gaṇapati collected the ashes and made a male figure out of them. it came alive, did penance and obtained many boons from śiva. brahmā acclaimed this achievement saying, “bhaṇḍ, bhaṇḍ” (good, good), and hence he got the name bhaṇḍāsura. his cruel demonic character was the result of his emergence from the ashes arising out of the fire of anger of śiva. śrīdevī came with the army of śaktis to destroy him. bhaṇḍa was bound by his own ignorance, and lived with the thought that sensual pleasures are supreme (asuṣu manyate asuraḥ). he was ignorant of his ātmasvarūpa (soul). it was necessary to destroy his cruel demonic character. bhaṇḍa means \"one who mimics or mocks.\" the demon bhaṇḍāsura represents अविद्या (avidyā — spiritual ignorance) which mocks the true, non-dual nature of the self by projecting the illusion of division. the armies of shaktisrepresent the various rays of spiritual knowledge (vidyā-vṛttis). she is samanvitā(fully integrated) with these forces, showing that her entire manifest power is geared toward destroying the ego and restoring spiritual truth.","esoteric":["Bhaṇḍa means \"one who mimics or mocks.\" The demon Bhaṇḍāsura represents अविद्या (Avidyā — spiritual ignorance) which mocks the true, non-dual nature of the Self by projecting the illusion of division. The armies of Shaktisrepresent the various rays of spiritual knowledge (vidyā-vṛttis). She is Samanvitā(fully integrated) with these forces, showing that Her entire manifest power is geared toward destroying the ego and restoring spiritual truth."]},{"number":66,"name":"सम्पत्करीसमारूढसिन्धुरव्रजसेविता","samasa":["• सम्पत्कर्या (दवतया) समारूढानां सिन्धुराणां यः व्रजः तेन सेविता।","• सम्पत्कर्यां (सुखसम्पन्मयी या चित्तवृत्तिः तस्यां) रमारूढैः सिन्धुरव्रजैः सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["सम्पत्करीसमारूढसिन्धुरव्रजसेविता means one who is worshipped by the elephant brigade commanded by Sampatkarī. Sindhura means an elephant. This commander is mounted on an elephant called Raṇakolāhala. She emerged out of the elephant goad in the hands of Śrīdevī and commanded the elephant brigade of thousands of elephants. Sampatkarī Vidyā is a powerful mantra. It finds a place in the Svatantra Tantra and consists of three syllables (bījākṣaras). The mental state which is full of the wealth pleasure is called Sampatkarī. This mental state is founded on the objects of senses like sound. These objects are equated with elephants. Thus Śrīdevī is said to be worshipped by Sampatkarī elephant. The knowledge which enables one to identify the knower, the knowledge and the object of knowledge separately and their correlation is known as Sampatkarī."],"searchText":"66 सम्पत्करीसमारूढसिन्धुरव्रजसेविता • सम्पत्कर्या (दवतया) समारूढानां सिन्धुराणां यः व्रजः तेन सेविता। • सम्पत्कर्यां (सुखसम्पन्मयी या चित्तवृत्तिः तस्यां) रमारूढैः सिन्धुरव्रजैः सेविता। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. सम्पत्करीसमारूढसिन्धुरव्रजसेविता means one who is worshipped by the elephant brigade commanded by sampatkarī. sindhura means an elephant. this commander is mounted on an elephant called raṇakolāhala. she emerged out of the elephant goad in the hands of śrīdevī and commanded the elephant brigade of thousands of elephants. sampatkarī vidyā is a powerful mantra. it finds a place in the svatantra tantra and consists of three syllables (bījākṣaras). the mental state which is full of the wealth pleasure is called sampatkarī. this mental state is founded on the objects of senses like sound. these objects are equated with elephants. thus śrīdevī is said to be worshipped by sampatkarī elephant. the knowledge which enables one to identify the knower, the knowledge and the object of knowledge separately and their correlation is known as sampatkarī. the control of mind-elephants: exoterically, sampatkarī is the elephant-commander of lalitā's army. an elephant represents wild, raw strength. esoterically, sampat means spiritual wealth, and sindhura (elephant) represents the powerful, hard-to-tame mind. she is served by these forces because when a practitioner gains spiritual wealth, the wild, chaotic faculties of the mind are completely brought under control, acting as disciplined vehicles that serve the inner self.","esoteric":["The Control of Mind-Elephants: Exoterically, Sampatkarī is the elephant-commander of Lalitā's army. An elephant represents wild, raw strength. Esoterically, Sampat means spiritual wealth, and Sindhura (elephant) represents the powerful, hard-to-tame mind. She is served by these forces because when a practitioner gains spiritual wealth, the wild, chaotic faculties of the mind are completely brought under control, acting as disciplined vehicles that serve the inner Self."]},{"number":67,"name":"अश्वारूढाधिष्ठिताश्वकोटिकोटिभिरावृता","samasa":["• अश्वारूढया (देवतया) अधिष्ठितानां अश्वानां कोटिगुणिताभिः कोटिभिः आवृता।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["अश्वारूढाधिष्ठिताश्वकोटिकोटिभिरावृता means one who is surrounded by crores of horses commanded by Aśvārūḍhā. The commander of Śrīdevī's horse brigade is Aśvārūḍhā, who emerged out of Śrīdevī's noose and is always mounted on a horse called Aparājitā. The five sources of knowledge are equated to horses on which is mounted the mind. Thus the mind is Aśvārūḍhā. It is only through the senses, the instruments of knowledge and action, that the mind carries out its activities of resolution and implementation. Śrīdevī is surrounded by horses symbolising senses controlled by the mind. She is the master and controller of the senses."],"searchText":"67 अश्वारूढाधिष्ठिताश्वकोटिकोटिभिरावृता • अश्वारूढया (देवतया) अधिष्ठितानां अश्वानां कोटिगुणिताभिः कोटिभिः आवृता। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. अश्वारूढाधिष्ठिताश्वकोटिकोटिभिरावृता means one who is surrounded by crores of horses commanded by aśvārūḍhā. the commander of śrīdevī's horse brigade is aśvārūḍhā, who emerged out of śrīdevī's noose and is always mounted on a horse called aparājitā. the five sources of knowledge are equated to horses on which is mounted the mind. thus the mind is aśvārūḍhā. it is only through the senses, the instruments of knowledge and action, that the mind carries out its activities of resolution and implementation. śrīdevī is surrounded by horses symbolising senses controlled by the mind. she is the master and controller of the senses. the mastery of sensory winds: in the mystical chariot of the body, horses represent the senses (indriyas), which gallop wildly toward external objects. the goddess aśvārūḍhā (literally, \"she who rides the horse\") represents the power of प्राणायाम (prāṇāyāma) and sensory control (pratyāhāra). by being surrounded by these disciplined cavalry forces, she demonstrates that when the breath and senses are completely mastered, they form a protective, impenetrable fortress of peace around the inner consciousness.","esoteric":["The Mastery of Sensory Winds: In the mystical chariot of the body, horses represent the senses (indriyas), which gallop wildly toward external objects. The goddess Aśvārūḍhā (literally, \"She who rides the horse\") represents the power of प्राणायाम (Prāṇāyāma) and sensory control (Pratyāhāra). By being surrounded by these disciplined cavalry forces, She demonstrates that when the breath and senses are completely mastered, they form a protective, impenetrable fortress of peace around the inner consciousness."]},{"number":68,"name":"चक्रराजरथारूढसर्वायुधपरिष्कृता","samasa":["• चक्रराजाख्यं रथम् आरूढैः सर्वैः आयुधैः परिष्कृता।","• श्रीचक्रमेव (श्रीविद्या) रथम्। तम् आरूढानि यानि सर्वायुधानि (आत्मज्ञानसाधनानि) तैः परिष्कृता।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वैः — all","आयुधैः — weapon"],"summary":["चक्रराजरथारूढसर्वायुधपरिष्कृता means one who is mounted on the Śrīcakra chariot surrounded by all kinds of weapons. Śrīcakra is considered as the king of all cakras (yantras of gods) and hence is called Śrī Cakrarāja. Śrīdevī is always present in this, and this is also the chariot of Śrīdevī. The nine dvārāṇis of Śrīcakra are the nine tiers of the chariot. The area of Śrīcakra is 4 yojanas and the height 10 yojanas. The Sarvānandamaya cakra in the centre of the Śrīcakra shines as the flag on the top of the chariot. It is called ānandadhvaja (flag of bliss). The four weapons of Śrīdevī, namely, pāśa (noose), aṅkuśa (goad), sugarcane bow and flower arrows mount the chariot before Śrīdevī enters and take their positions around Her seat, assuming the form of Śaktis. Similarly all the other weapons also mounted the chariot assuming their respective forms of Śaktis. Normally a soldier mounts the chariot carrying all the weapons, but here the weapons assume the forms of Śaktis and mount the chariot on their own."],"searchText":"68 चक्रराजरथारूढसर्वायुधपरिष्कृता • चक्रराजाख्यं रथम् आरूढैः सर्वैः आयुधैः परिष्कृता। • श्रीचक्रमेव (श्रीविद्या) रथम्। तम् आरूढानि यानि सर्वायुधानि (आत्मज्ञानसाधनानि) तैः परिष्कृता। सर्वैः — all आयुधैः — weapon चक्रराजरथारूढसर्वायुधपरिष्कृता means one who is mounted on the śrīcakra chariot surrounded by all kinds of weapons. śrīcakra is considered as the king of all cakras (yantras of gods) and hence is called śrī cakrarāja. śrīdevī is always present in this, and this is also the chariot of śrīdevī. the nine dvārāṇis of śrīcakra are the nine tiers of the chariot. the area of śrīcakra is 4 yojanas and the height 10 yojanas. the sarvānandamaya cakra in the centre of the śrīcakra shines as the flag on the top of the chariot. it is called ānandadhvaja (flag of bliss). the four weapons of śrīdevī, namely, pāśa (noose), aṅkuśa (goad), sugarcane bow and flower arrows mount the chariot before śrīdevī enters and take their positions around her seat, assuming the form of śaktis. similarly all the other weapons also mounted the chariot assuming their respective forms of śaktis. normally a soldier mounts the chariot carrying all the weapons, but here the weapons assume the forms of śaktis and mount the chariot on their own. the vehicle of divine methods: the cakrarāja is her nine-tiered war chariot, which represents the śrī cakra. her weapons are not physical instruments of violence, but rather the highly refined, sharp methods of self-investigation and spiritual discrimination (atma-jñāna-sādhanā). she is pariṣkṛtā (fully decorated and prepared) with these methods, showing that the entire śrī cakra structure is designed to equip the seeker with the intellectual weapons needed to destroy illusion.","esoteric":["The Vehicle of Divine Methods: The Cakrarāja is Her nine-tiered war chariot, which represents the Śrī Cakra. Her weapons are not physical instruments of violence, but rather the highly refined, sharp methods of self-investigation and spiritual discrimination (Atma-jñāna-sādhanā). She is Pariṣkṛtā (fully decorated and prepared) with these methods, showing that the entire Śrī Cakra structure is designed to equip the seeker with the intellectual weapons needed to destroy illusion."]},{"number":69,"name":"गेयचक्ररथारूढमन्त्रिणीपरिसेविता","samasa":["• गेयं चक्रं यस्य तादृशः रथः यस्य (सर्यमण्डलस्य) तस्मिन् आरूढभिः मन्त्रिणीभिः परिसेविता।"],"wordByWord":["चक्रं — wheel; chakra"],"summary":["गेयचक्ररथारूढमन्त्रिणीपरिसेविता means one who is worshipped by Mantriṇī Devī who rides the Geya cakra. Śyāmalā is a Śakti created by Śrīdevī out of Her sugarcane bow as an embodiment of mind energy. Her complexion is that of raincloud, and Her knowledge of music is profound. She has a vīṇā in one hand and a parrot in another. She is capable of bestowing on Her devotees, sweet voice, knowledge of music and power to attract the mind. She has taken charge of administrative functions of Śrīdevī's kingdom. In statecraft, the king or queen may have to have consultations on many matters without others' knowledge. Just as mantras are said to be secret, matters in statecraft are also referred to by the same name. One who renders such advice is called mantrī or Mantriṇī. Geya means famous. It has seven tiers. When it moves, the sound it makes is like musical notes, and that is another reason why it is called Geya (musical) chariot. Yoginīs occupy the seven tiers of this chariot. Gey means important; cakraratha means Devī mounted on a circular chariot; ārūḍha means one who contemplates on; Mantriṇī means one who is worshiped by those initiated into the mantra."],"searchText":"69 गेयचक्ररथारूढमन्त्रिणीपरिसेविता • गेयं चक्रं यस्य तादृशः रथः यस्य (सर्यमण्डलस्य) तस्मिन् आरूढभिः मन्त्रिणीभिः परिसेविता। चक्रं — wheel; chakra गेयचक्ररथारूढमन्त्रिणीपरिसेविता means one who is worshipped by mantriṇī devī who rides the geya cakra. śyāmalā is a śakti created by śrīdevī out of her sugarcane bow as an embodiment of mind energy. her complexion is that of raincloud, and her knowledge of music is profound. she has a vīṇā in one hand and a parrot in another. she is capable of bestowing on her devotees, sweet voice, knowledge of music and power to attract the mind. she has taken charge of administrative functions of śrīdevī's kingdom. in statecraft, the king or queen may have to have consultations on many matters without others' knowledge. just as mantras are said to be secret, matters in statecraft are also referred to by the same name. one who renders such advice is called mantrī or mantriṇī. geya means famous. it has seven tiers. when it moves, the sound it makes is like musical notes, and that is another reason why it is called geya (musical) chariot. yoginīs occupy the seven tiers of this chariot. gey means important; cakraratha means devī mounted on a circular chariot; ārūḍha means one who contemplates on; mantriṇī means one who is worshiped by those initiated into the mantra. the guidance of sacred sound: geyacakra literally means \"the wheel of song.\" the prime minister, mantriṇī (also known as rāja-śyāmalā), represents the power of मन्त्र (mantra) and sacred music. she sits close to the queen, showing that the systematic practice of sacred chanting and sound absorption is the prime counselor that guides and prepares the seeker's mind to receive the final grace of the queen.","esoteric":["The Guidance of Sacred Sound: Geyacakra literally means \"the wheel of song.\" The prime minister, Mantriṇī (also known as Rāja-śyāmalā), represents the power of मन्त्र (Mantra) and sacred music. She sits close to the Queen, showing that the systematic practice of sacred chanting and sound absorption is the prime counselor that guides and prepares the seeker's mind to receive the final grace of the Queen."]},{"number":70,"name":"किरिचक्ररथारूढदण्डनाथापुरस्कृता","samasa":["• किरयाकृतीनि चक्राणि यस्य तं रथम् आरूढया दण्डनाथया पुरस्कृता।","• किरीणां (सृष्टीनां तेन लयानामपि) चक्रम् एव रथः। तस्यऽपि दण्डनाथेन पुरस्कृता (न स्वाधीनीकृता)।"],"wordByWord":["चक्राणि — wheel; chakra","चक्रम् — wheel; chakra"],"summary":["किरिचक्ररथारूढदण्डनाथापुरस्कृता means one who is piloted by Daṇḍanāthā riding the chariot called Kiricakra. Kiri, or kiṭi, means varāha (boar), and Daṇḍanāthā's chariot is in the shape of a boar. Daṇḍanāthā is also known as Vārāhī. She was created by Śrīdevī from Her five arrows and is the commander-in-chief of Śrīdevī's army. She carries the weapon called daṇḍāyudha in Her hand. She has a very strong physique like a wild boar and hence is called Vārāhī. She is shrewd enough to act according to Śrīdevī's will and hence is known as Saṅketā. She is also Ājñācakreśvarī, one who is responsible for carrying out Śrīdevī's orders. She resides in the ājñācakra in the human body. The Kiricakra has five tiers, occupied by Yoginīs. Kiri also means the cycle of creation, sustenance and destruction; Daṇḍanāthā is mounted on the chariot symbolising this cycle."],"searchText":"70 किरिचक्ररथारूढदण्डनाथापुरस्कृता • किरयाकृतीनि चक्राणि यस्य तं रथम् आरूढया दण्डनाथया पुरस्कृता। • किरीणां (सृष्टीनां तेन लयानामपि) चक्रम् एव रथः। तस्यऽपि दण्डनाथेन पुरस्कृता (न स्वाधीनीकृता)। चक्राणि — wheel; chakra चक्रम् — wheel; chakra किरिचक्ररथारूढदण्डनाथापुरस्कृता means one who is piloted by daṇḍanāthā riding the chariot called kiricakra. kiri, or kiṭi, means varāha (boar), and daṇḍanāthā's chariot is in the shape of a boar. daṇḍanāthā is also known as vārāhī. she was created by śrīdevī from her five arrows and is the commander-in-chief of śrīdevī's army. she carries the weapon called daṇḍāyudha in her hand. she has a very strong physique like a wild boar and hence is called vārāhī. she is shrewd enough to act according to śrīdevī's will and hence is known as saṅketā. she is also ājñācakreśvarī, one who is responsible for carrying out śrīdevī's orders. she resides in the ājñācakra in the human body. the kiricakra has five tiers, occupied by yoginīs. kiri also means the cycle of creation, sustenance and destruction; daṇḍanāthā is mounted on the chariot symbolising this cycle. the enforcement of cosmic justice: kiricakra represents the fierce, heavy boar-shaped chariot, and daṇḍanāthā (vārāhī) represents the absolute power of क्रियाशक्ति (kriyā-śakti — execution and justice). she rides ahead of the queen, clearing the path of spiritual obstacles. she represents the unbending, structured laws of karma and cosmic order (dharma) that systematically dismantle the chaotic, ego-driven distortions of the seeker's mind.","esoteric":["The Enforcement of Cosmic Justice: Kiricakra represents the fierce, heavy boar-shaped chariot, and Daṇḍanāthā (Vārāhī) represents the absolute power of क्रियाशक्ति (Kriyā-śakti — execution and justice). She rides ahead of the Queen, clearing the path of spiritual obstacles. She represents the unbending, structured laws of karma and cosmic order (Dharma) that systematically dismantle the chaotic, ego-driven distortions of the seeker's mind."]},{"number":71,"name":"ज्वालामालिनिकाक्षिप्तवह्निप्राकारमध्यगा","samasa":["• ज्वालामालिनिकया तदाक्षिप्तस्य वह्निमयस्य प्राकारस्य मध्यगा।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["ज्वालामालिनिकाक्षिप्तवह्निप्राकारमध्यगा means one who dwells in the centre of the fire-fort built by Jvālāmālinī. In the Śrīcakra, fifteen Nityā Devīs are seated, five on each side of the triangle around the bindu. They are immortal and represent time. Śrīdevī Herself occupies the bindusthāna as the sixteenth Mahānityā. Jvālāmālinī is one of these Nityās. During the battle with Bhaṇḍāsura, Śrīdevī instructed Jvālāmālinī to build a fort of fire to protect Her army, and She stayed in its centre with Her forces. Jvālāmālinī represents the five Śakti triangles, and the vahniprākāra represents the four Śiva triangles in the form of fire. All nine triangles are integrated, with Śrīdevī at the bindusthāna in the centre. Though She is the cause of creation, sustenance and destruction, She remains unaffected by these acts, like one surrounded by sparks of fire yet untouched."],"searchText":"71 ज्वालामालिनिकाक्षिप्तवह्निप्राकारमध्यगा • ज्वालामालिनिकया तदाक्षिप्तस्य वह्निमयस्य प्राकारस्य मध्यगा। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. ज्वालामालिनिकाक्षिप्तवह्निप्राकारमध्यगा means one who dwells in the centre of the fire-fort built by jvālāmālinī. in the śrīcakra, fifteen nityā devīs are seated, five on each side of the triangle around the bindu. they are immortal and represent time. śrīdevī herself occupies the bindusthāna as the sixteenth mahānityā. jvālāmālinī is one of these nityās. during the battle with bhaṇḍāsura, śrīdevī instructed jvālāmālinī to build a fort of fire to protect her army, and she stayed in its centre with her forces. jvālāmālinī represents the five śakti triangles, and the vahniprākāra represents the four śiva triangles in the form of fire. all nine triangles are integrated, with śrīdevī at the bindusthāna in the centre. though she is the cause of creation, sustenance and destruction, she remains unaffected by these acts, like one surrounded by sparks of fire yet untouched. the ring of fire (kuṇḍalinī protection): jvālāmālinī is one of the nityā deities of the śrī cakra who rules over the aspect of consuming fire. the \"fortress of fire\" (vahniprākāra) represents the impenetrable, purifying heat of spiritual energy (kuṇḍalinī-tapas) that surrounds the central consciousness (bindu). she resides in the middle of this fire-ring, signifying that she is fully protected from external mental distractions and is accessible only to those who can withstand the intense heat of purification.","esoteric":["The Ring of Fire (Kuṇḍalinī Protection): Jvālāmālinī is one of the Nityā deities of the Śrī Cakra who rules over the aspect of consuming fire. The \"fortress of fire\" (vahniprākāra) represents the impenetrable, purifying heat of spiritual energy (Kuṇḍalinī-tapas) that surrounds the central consciousness (Bindu). She resides in the middle of this fire-ring, signifying that She is fully protected from external mental distractions and is accessible only to those who can withstand the intense heat of purification."]},{"number":72,"name":"भण्डसैन्यवधोद्युक्तशक्तिविक्रमहर्षिता","samasa":["• भण्डासुरस्य सैन्यस्य वधे उद्युक्तानां शक्तीनाः विक्रमेण हर्षिता।","• भण्डस्य (जीवभावस्य) सैन्यस्य (द्वैतविषयिणः वृत्तीनां) वधे उद्युक्तानां शक्तीनां विशेषेण क्रमेण हर्षिता।"],"wordByWord":["वधे — slaying"],"summary":["भण्डसैन्यवधोद्युक्तशक्तिविक्रमहर्षिता means one who is pleased with the valour of the Śaktis engaged in destroying Bhaṇḍa's army. Śrīdevī created an army of Śaktis out of Her own self to destroy Bhaṇḍa's army, and She was pleased when Her army achieved that purpose. Bhaṇḍāsura represents ignorance that fails to recognise the Self. His army arises from mental aberrations and differentiation. To counter this, Śrīdevī Herself took many forms as Śaktis and destroyed that ignorance. She was pleased by the gradual destruction of ignorance and the emergence of knowledge."],"searchText":"72 भण्डसैन्यवधोद्युक्तशक्तिविक्रमहर्षिता • भण्डासुरस्य सैन्यस्य वधे उद्युक्तानां शक्तीनाः विक्रमेण हर्षिता। • भण्डस्य (जीवभावस्य) सैन्यस्य (द्वैतविषयिणः वृत्तीनां) वधे उद्युक्तानां शक्तीनां विशेषेण क्रमेण हर्षिता। वधे — slaying भण्डसैन्यवधोद्युक्तशक्तिविक्रमहर्षिता means one who is pleased with the valour of the śaktis engaged in destroying bhaṇḍa's army. śrīdevī created an army of śaktis out of her own self to destroy bhaṇḍa's army, and she was pleased when her army achieved that purpose. bhaṇḍāsura represents ignorance that fails to recognise the self. his army arises from mental aberrations and differentiation. to counter this, śrīdevī herself took many forms as śaktis and destroyed that ignorance. she was pleased by the gradual destruction of ignorance and the emergence of knowledge. bhaṇḍasainya represents the infinite, deceptive armies of dualistic thoughts, desires, and conditioning that reinforce the false ego (jīva-bhāva). the śaktis are the individual pure awarenesses (jñāna-vṛttis) that systematically conquer these dualistic impulses. the mother's \"delight\" (harṣitā) is the rising tide of non-dual bliss (ānanda) that overflows when the practitioner's inner duality is progressively dissolved.","esoteric":["Bhaṇḍasainya represents the infinite, deceptive armies of dualistic thoughts, desires, and conditioning that reinforce the false ego (jīva-bhāva). The Śaktis are the individual pure awarenesses (jñāna-vṛttis) that systematically conquer these dualistic impulses. The Mother's \"delight\" (harṣitā) is the rising tide of non-dual bliss (Ānanda) that overflows when the practitioner's inner duality is progressively dissolved."]},{"number":73,"name":"नित्यापराक्रमाटोपनिरीक्षणसमुत्सुका","samasa":["• नित्यानां पराक्रमस्य यः आटोपः तस्य निरीक्षणे सम्यक् उत्सुका।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["नित्यापराक्रमाटोपनिरीक्षणसमुत्सुका means one who was eager and delighted to witness the valour of the Nityā Devīs. Bhaṇḍāsura sent fifteen generals to battle, and the fifteen Nityās of Śrīdevī's army faced and defeated them. During the battle, two generals, Damanaka and Citragupta, surrounded the Śrī Cakrarāja chariot and began fighting by unfair means. The fifteen Tithi Nityās displayed their prowess by destroying them in front of Śrīdevī, to Her delight. Because of their permanence, the powers of the Self are called Nityās. Their increasing valour represents inward self-realisation. A person attains inner bliss when the immortal soul-power wins over the demonic forces that arise again and again in the mind."],"searchText":"73 नित्यापराक्रमाटोपनिरीक्षणसमुत्सुका • नित्यानां पराक्रमस्य यः आटोपः तस्य निरीक्षणे सम्यक् उत्सुका। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. नित्यापराक्रमाटोपनिरीक्षणसमुत्सुका means one who was eager and delighted to witness the valour of the nityā devīs. bhaṇḍāsura sent fifteen generals to battle, and the fifteen nityās of śrīdevī's army faced and defeated them. during the battle, two generals, damanaka and citragupta, surrounded the śrī cakrarāja chariot and began fighting by unfair means. the fifteen tithi nityās displayed their prowess by destroying them in front of śrīdevī, to her delight. because of their permanence, the powers of the self are called nityās. their increasing valour represents inward self-realisation. a person attains inner bliss when the immortal soul-power wins over the demonic forces that arise again and again in the mind. the observership of the absolute: the fifteen nityās represent the fifteen lunar days (tithis) of the calendar, which translate internally to the changing states of human consciousness and breath. their \"valor\" (parākrāma) is the continuous, dynamic process of life and spiritual transformation. she is samutsukā (eagerly observing) because she is the ultimate, detached witness (sākṣī-caitanya) who takes delight in the spontaneous play of her own dynamic time-phases without ever being bound by them.","esoteric":["The Observership of the Absolute: The fifteen Nityās represent the fifteen lunar days (tithis) of the calendar, which translate internally to the changing states of human consciousness and breath. Their \"valor\" (parākrāma) is the continuous, dynamic process of life and spiritual transformation. She is Samutsukā (eagerly observing) because She is the ultimate, detached Witness (Sākṣī-caitanya) who takes delight in the spontaneous play of Her own dynamic time-phases without ever being bound by them."]},{"number":74,"name":"भण्डपुत्रवधोद्युक्तबालाविक्रमनन्दिता","samasa":["• भण्डस्य पुत्राणां वधे उद्युक्तायाः बालायाः (बालाख्यदेव्याः) विक्रमे नन्दिता।"],"wordByWord":["वधे — slaying","उद्युक्तायाः — ready; engaged"],"summary":["भण्डपुत्रवधोद्युक्तबालाविक्रमनन्दिता means one who was pleased with the valour of Bālā, who set out to destroy Bhaṇḍa's sons. When Bhaṇḍa saw the destruction of his soldiers, he sent his thirty sons, beginning with Caturbāhu and ending with Upamāya, to continue the battle. They were killed by Bālā Tripurasundarī, Śrīdevī's daughter. Bālā is a child who is always nine years old. She wore armour that emerged from Śrīdevī's armour and fought Bhaṇḍa's sons while riding a small chariot called Karṇiratha. Śrīdevī was delighted with Bālā's fighting skill. Śrīdevī's mantra is Pañcadaśākṣarī, made of the three groups Vāgbhava, Kāmarāja and Śakti. The Bālā mantra has three syllables, Aiṃ, Klīṃ and Sauḥ, corresponding to these three groups. The Bālā mantra is called Laghu Śrīvidyā. Before Śrīvidyā dīkṣā is given, the Bālā mantra is first taught."],"searchText":"74 भण्डपुत्रवधोद्युक्तबालाविक्रमनन्दिता • भण्डस्य पुत्राणां वधे उद्युक्तायाः बालायाः (बालाख्यदेव्याः) विक्रमे नन्दिता। वधे — slaying उद्युक्तायाः — ready; engaged भण्डपुत्रवधोद्युक्तबालाविक्रमनन्दिता means one who was pleased with the valour of bālā, who set out to destroy bhaṇḍa's sons. when bhaṇḍa saw the destruction of his soldiers, he sent his thirty sons, beginning with caturbāhu and ending with upamāya, to continue the battle. they were killed by bālā tripurasundarī, śrīdevī's daughter. bālā is a child who is always nine years old. she wore armour that emerged from śrīdevī's armour and fought bhaṇḍa's sons while riding a small chariot called karṇiratha. śrīdevī was delighted with bālā's fighting skill. śrīdevī's mantra is pañcadaśākṣarī, made of the three groups vāgbhava, kāmarāja and śakti. the bālā mantra has three syllables, aiṃ, klīṃ and sauḥ, corresponding to these three groups. the bālā mantra is called laghu śrīvidyā. before śrīvidyā dīkṣā is given, the bālā mantra is first taught. slaying the offspring of ignorance: in the battle narrative, bhaṇḍāsura's thirty sons represent the offspring of ignorance—the secondary mental distortions like doubt (saṃśaya), fear (bhaya), jealousy, and hatred. goddess bālā-tripurasundarīrepresents the initial, youthful dawn of pure intuitive knowledge within the seeker's heart. the mother's rejoicing (nanditā) signifies that even a small, child-like spark of true spiritual awareness (bālā) is completely sufficient to wipe out the complex offspring of ego and ignorance.","esoteric":["Slaying the Offspring of Ignorance: In the battle narrative, Bhaṇḍāsura's thirty sons represent the offspring of ignorance—the secondary mental distortions like doubt (saṃśaya), fear (bhaya), jealousy, and hatred. Goddess Bālā-Tripurasundarīrepresents the initial, youthful dawn of pure intuitive knowledge within the seeker's heart. The Mother's rejoicing (nanditā) signifies that even a small, child-like spark of true spiritual awareness (Bālā) is completely sufficient to wipe out the complex offspring of ego and ignorance."]},{"number":75,"name":"मन्त्रिण्यम्बाविरचितविषङ्गवधतोषिता","samasa":["• मन्त्रिण्यम्बया विरचितेन विषङ्गाख्यस्य वधेन तोषिता।"],"wordByWord":["वधेन — slaying"],"summary":["मन्त्रिण्यम्बाविरचितविषङ्गवधतोषिता means one who was pleased by the killing of the demon Viṣaṅga by Mantriṇī Ambā, also called Śyāmalā. Bhaṇḍa performed penance to Lord Rudra and gained the power to create demons as he wished. He created Viśukra from his right shoulder and Viṣaṅga from his left shoulder, treated them as his brothers, and made Viṣaṅga his minister and Viśukra his commander-in-chief. Śyāmalā, the Mantriṇī Devī, killed Viṣaṅga, and Śrīdevī was pleased. Saṅga means attachment or interest, and vi means wrong or hostile; therefore Viṣaṅga means wrongful attachment. It indicates indulgence in wrong acts through the organs. Mantriṇī, as the mantra-śakti of Śrīdevī, destroys this wrongful attraction."],"searchText":"75 मन्त्रिण्यम्बाविरचितविषङ्गवधतोषिता • मन्त्रिण्यम्बया विरचितेन विषङ्गाख्यस्य वधेन तोषिता। वधेन — slaying मन्त्रिण्यम्बाविरचितविषङ्गवधतोषिता means one who was pleased by the killing of the demon viṣaṅga by mantriṇī ambā, also called śyāmalā. bhaṇḍa performed penance to lord rudra and gained the power to create demons as he wished. he created viśukra from his right shoulder and viṣaṅga from his left shoulder, treated them as his brothers, and made viṣaṅga his minister and viśukra his commander-in-chief. śyāmalā, the mantriṇī devī, killed viṣaṅga, and śrīdevī was pleased. saṅga means attachment or interest, and vi means wrong or hostile; therefore viṣaṅga means wrongful attachment. it indicates indulgence in wrong acts through the organs. mantriṇī, as the mantra-śakti of śrīdevī, destroys this wrongful attraction. overcoming spiritual apathy: viṣaṅga literally means \"hostile attachment\" or \"crooked path.\" in the inner battle, he represents the stubborn mental tendencies of doubt, crooked logic, and spiritual apathy that distract the seeker. mantriṇī(rāja-śyāmalā) represents the power of sacred sound, devotion, and mantra. her slaying of viṣaṅga demonstrates that the crooked distortions of the logical mind are effortlessly straightened and dissolved through the practice of mantra absorption and loving devotion.","esoteric":["Overcoming Spiritual Apathy: Viṣaṅga literally means \"hostile attachment\" or \"crooked path.\" In the inner battle, he represents the stubborn mental tendencies of doubt, crooked logic, and spiritual apathy that distract the seeker. Mantriṇī(Rāja-śyāmalā) represents the power of sacred sound, devotion, and mantra. Her slaying of Viṣaṅga demonstrates that the crooked distortions of the logical mind are effortlessly straightened and dissolved through the practice of mantra absorption and loving devotion."]},{"number":76,"name":"विशुक्रप्राणहरणवाराहीवीर्यनन्दिता","samasa":["• विशुक्रस्य प्राणस्य हरतीति हरणं तादृशेन वाराह्याः वीर्येण नन्दिता।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["विशुक्रप्राणहरणवाराहीवीर्यनन्दिता means one who was pleased with the prowess of Vārāhī when she took the life of Viśukra. Viśukra was the commander-in-chief of Bhaṇḍa. Vārāhī, the commander-in-chief of Śrīdevī, killed him, and Śrīdevī was happy to see this. Vi can mean hostile, and śukra means light or strength; thus Viśukra means one who spends his energy against the ātma-śakti. It can also be understood as vi, excess; śuk, sorrow; and ra, one who brings: one who brings excessive sorrow. He was killed by Vārāhī, the kriyā-śakti of Śrīdevī. In this sequence, Bālā Devī destroys the three sins and makes the ātma-tattva shine, Mantriṇī helps focus the wavering mind and soul, and Daṇḍanāthā gives strength for determined action."],"searchText":"76 विशुक्रप्राणहरणवाराहीवीर्यनन्दिता • विशुक्रस्य प्राणस्य हरतीति हरणं तादृशेन वाराह्याः वीर्येण नन्दिता। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. विशुक्रप्राणहरणवाराहीवीर्यनन्दिता means one who was pleased with the prowess of vārāhī when she took the life of viśukra. viśukra was the commander-in-chief of bhaṇḍa. vārāhī, the commander-in-chief of śrīdevī, killed him, and śrīdevī was happy to see this. vi can mean hostile, and śukra means light or strength; thus viśukra means one who spends his energy against the ātma-śakti. it can also be understood as vi, excess; śuk, sorrow; and ra, one who brings: one who brings excessive sorrow. he was killed by vārāhī, the kriyā-śakti of śrīdevī. in this sequence, bālā devī destroys the three sins and makes the ātma-tattva shine, mantriṇī helps focus the wavering mind and soul, and daṇḍanāthā gives strength for determined action. severing the impurity of mind: viśukra literally means \"devoid of semen\" or \"having dried-up essence,\" representing the dry, highly critical intellectualism that doubts spiritual truths and depletes one's energy. vārāhī (daṇḍanāthā) is the goddess of willpower and unyielding action. her slaying of viśukra represents the complete eradication of dry intellectual arrogance, allowing the seeker to recover their vital essence and channel it toward genuine spiritual experience.","esoteric":["Severing the Impurity of Mind: Viśukra literally means \"devoid of semen\" or \"having dried-up essence,\" representing the dry, highly critical intellectualism that doubts spiritual truths and depletes one's energy. Vārāhī (Daṇḍanāthā) is the goddess of willpower and unyielding action. Her slaying of Viśukra represents the complete eradication of dry intellectual arrogance, allowing the seeker to recover their vital essence and channel it toward genuine spiritual experience."]},{"number":77,"name":"कामेश्वरमुखालोककल्पितश्रीगणेश्वरा","samasa":["• कामेश्वरस्य मुखस्य आलोकेन कल्पितः श्रीगणेश्वरः येया सा।"],"wordByWord":["मुखस्य — face"],"summary":["कामेश्वरमुखालोककल्पितश्रीगणेश्वरा means one who created Śrī Gaṇeśvara merely by looking at the face of Śrī Kāmeśvara. Seeing the destruction of his army, Bhaṇḍa ordered Viśukra to set up the Vighnayantra. This yantra, made by the illusion of demons, was placed in the midst of Śrīdevī's army. Because of it, the army was affected by eight feelings: laziness, disinterest in fighting, the thought that they could not succeed, fatigue, sleepiness, unconsciousness, lack of courage, and loss of self-respect. Mantriṇī complained to Śrīdevī. Śrīdevī glanced at Śrī Kāmeśvara seated by Her side. Their glances merged with smile and affection, and Śrī Gaṇapati emerged with an elephant face, embracing Siddhalakṣmī called Vallabhā. He held pomegranate, mace, sugarcane bow, spear, cakra, conch, noose, lily flower, paddy crops, and one of his own tusks; in his trunk he carried a gem-made sacred pot."],"searchText":"77 कामेश्वरमुखालोककल्पितश्रीगणेश्वरा • कामेश्वरस्य मुखस्य आलोकेन कल्पितः श्रीगणेश्वरः येया सा। मुखस्य — face कामेश्वरमुखालोककल्पितश्रीगणेश्वरा means one who created śrī gaṇeśvara merely by looking at the face of śrī kāmeśvara. seeing the destruction of his army, bhaṇḍa ordered viśukra to set up the vighnayantra. this yantra, made by the illusion of demons, was placed in the midst of śrīdevī's army. because of it, the army was affected by eight feelings: laziness, disinterest in fighting, the thought that they could not succeed, fatigue, sleepiness, unconsciousness, lack of courage, and loss of self-respect. mantriṇī complained to śrīdevī. śrīdevī glanced at śrī kāmeśvara seated by her side. their glances merged with smile and affection, and śrī gaṇapati emerged with an elephant face, embracing siddhalakṣmī called vallabhā. he held pomegranate, mace, sugarcane bow, spear, cakra, conch, noose, lily flower, paddy crops, and one of his own tusks; in his trunk he carried a gem-made sacred pot. the birth of wisdom from pure seeing: this names the birth of gaṇeśa. esoterically, kāmeśvara is the supreme father (prakāśa), and lalitā is the mother (vimarśa). her gazing upon his face is the reflective look of self-awareness (विमर्श रूप). out of this mutual, ecstatic gazing—without any physical contact—arises gaṇeśvara (the lord of the inner categories of mind). gaṇeśa represents the birth of pure spiritual wisdom and obstacle-removing discrimination, born directly from the non-dual union of stillness and reflection.","esoteric":["The Birth of Wisdom from Pure Seeing: This names the birth of Gaṇeśa. Esoterically, Kāmeśvara is the supreme father (Prakāśa), and Lalitā is the mother (Vimarśa). Her gazing upon His face is the reflective look of Self-awareness (विमर्श रूप). Out of this mutual, ecstatic gazing—without any physical contact—arises Gaṇeśvara (the lord of the inner categories of mind). Gaṇeśa represents the birth of pure spiritual wisdom and obstacle-removing discrimination, born directly from the non-dual union of stillness and reflection."]},{"number":78,"name":"महागणेशनिर्भिन्नविघ्नयन्त्रप्रहर्षिता","samasa":["• महागणेशेन निःशेषेण भिन्नैः विघ्नयन्त्रैः प्रकर्षेण हर्षिता।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["महागणेशनिर्भिन्नविघ्नयन्त्रप्रहर्षिता means one who rejoiced when Mahāgaṇeśa broke the Vighnayantra. The Vighnayantra was a magical obstacle-device set up among Śrīdevī's army. It produced obstruction, weakness, discouragement and loss of self-respect. Śrī Gaṇeśvara, born from Śrīdevī's glance toward Śrī Kāmeśvara, destroyed this device. Śrīdevī rejoiced when the obstacles affecting Her army were removed. The meaning is closely connected with the previous name, where Śrī Gaṇeśvara is brought forth to clear the obstruction created by Bhaṇḍa's forces."],"searchText":"78 महागणेशनिर्भिन्नविघ्नयन्त्रप्रहर्षिता • महागणेशेन निःशेषेण भिन्नैः विघ्नयन्त्रैः प्रकर्षेण हर्षिता। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. महागणेशनिर्भिन्नविघ्नयन्त्रप्रहर्षिता means one who rejoiced when mahāgaṇeśa broke the vighnayantra. the vighnayantra was a magical obstacle-device set up among śrīdevī's army. it produced obstruction, weakness, discouragement and loss of self-respect. śrī gaṇeśvara, born from śrīdevī's glance toward śrī kāmeśvara, destroyed this device. śrīdevī rejoiced when the obstacles affecting her army were removed. the meaning is closely connected with the previous name, where śrī gaṇeśvara is brought forth to clear the obstruction created by bhaṇḍa's forces. shattering the machinery of obstacles: during the war with bhaṇḍa, the demons threw a magical stone diagram (vighna-yantra) that paralyzed the śaktis' progress. gaṇeśa shattered it into pieces. esoterically, the vighna-yantras are the deep-seated mental blocks, doubts, and subconscious patterns that paralyze spiritual practice. mahāgaṇeśa represents the roar of intuitive wisdom. when this wisdom dawns, it completely breaks the complex machinery of subconscious limitations, bringing deep joy (praharṣitā) to the inner self.","esoteric":["Shattering the Machinery of Obstacles: During the war with Bhaṇḍa, the demons threw a magical stone diagram (vighna-yantra) that paralyzed the Śaktis' progress. Gaṇeśa shattered it into pieces. Esoterically, the vighna-yantras are the deep-seated mental blocks, doubts, and subconscious patterns that paralyze spiritual practice. Mahāgaṇeśa represents the roar of intuitive wisdom. When this wisdom dawns, it completely breaks the complex machinery of subconscious limitations, bringing deep joy (praharṣitā) to the inner self."]},{"number":79,"name":"भण्डासुरेन्द्रनिर्मुक्तशस्त्रप्रत्यस्त्रवर्षिणी","samasa":["• भण्डेनासुरेन्द्रेण निर्मुक्तानां शस्त्राणां प्रत्यस्त्राणां च वर्षतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["भण्डासुरेन्द्रनिर्मुक्तशस्त्रप्रत्यस्त्रवर्षिणी means one who showered counter-missiles against the weapons released by Bhaṇḍāsura. Weapons used in war are of two kinds: śastras, hand-held weapons such as sword, mace and spear, used against nearby enemies; and astras, missiles aimed at enemies at a distance. Bhaṇḍāsura attacked Śrīdevī with his weapons, and She at once countered them with matching missiles. If someone thinks Śrīdevī is near and already possessed, She appears far away; if someone longs for Her from afar, She appears very near. In this way She plays with Bhaṇḍa. The thought of God destroys from a distance the demonic character of ignorance that attacks the nature of the Self."],"searchText":"79 भण्डासुरेन्द्रनिर्मुक्तशस्त्रप्रत्यस्त्रवर्षिणी • भण्डेनासुरेन्द्रेण निर्मुक्तानां शस्त्राणां प्रत्यस्त्राणां च वर्षतीति। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. भण्डासुरेन्द्रनिर्मुक्तशस्त्रप्रत्यस्त्रवर्षिणी means one who showered counter-missiles against the weapons released by bhaṇḍāsura. weapons used in war are of two kinds: śastras, hand-held weapons such as sword, mace and spear, used against nearby enemies; and astras, missiles aimed at enemies at a distance. bhaṇḍāsura attacked śrīdevī with his weapons, and she at once countered them with matching missiles. if someone thinks śrīdevī is near and already possessed, she appears far away; if someone longs for her from afar, she appears very near. in this way she plays with bhaṇḍa. the thought of god destroys from a distance the demonic character of ignorance that attacks the nature of the self. the perfect balance of remedial grace: in the warfare of consciousness, when the ego (bhaṇḍa) throws weapons of delusion (like anger, greed, or attachment), she immediately launches the perfect counter-weapons (pratyastra) to neutralize them. for every mental illness and binding pattern that the relative world presents, her grace contains the exact antidote, establishing equilibrium and peace within the seeker.","esoteric":["The Perfect Balance of Remedial Grace: In the warfare of consciousness, when the ego (Bhaṇḍa) throws weapons of delusion (like anger, greed, or attachment), She immediately launches the perfect counter-weapons (pratyastra) to neutralize them. For every mental illness and binding pattern that the relative world presents, Her grace contains the exact antidote, establishing equilibrium and peace within the seeker."]},{"number":80,"name":"कराङ्गुलिनखोत्पन्ननारायणदशाकृतिः","samasa":["• कराङ्गुलिषु ये नखानाः सन्धयः तेषु उत्पन्नस्य नारायणस्य दशाकृतयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["कराङ्गुलिनखोत्पन्ननारायणदशाकृतिः means one who is accompanied by the ten forms of Śrī Nārāyaṇa that emerged from Her ten fingernails. Bhaṇḍāsura used the missile called Sarvāsurāstra to create demons such as Somaka, Rāvaṇa and Hiraṇyākṣa, who began fighting Śrīdevī. In a moment, She made the ten forms of Śrī Nārāyaṇa arise from Her ten fingernails. Each form fought the corresponding demon and killed him. Nārāyaṇa can indicate both jīva and Īśvara. Daśākṛti can be understood in relation to the states of the jīva and the works of Īśvara. The five states of the jīva are waking, dream, deep sleep, turīya and turīyātīta. The five works of Nārāyaṇa are creation, sustenance, destruction, concealment and grace. She performs all these effortlessly through Her ten fingernails."],"searchText":"80 कराङ्गुलिनखोत्पन्ननारायणदशाकृतिः • कराङ्गुलिषु ये नखानाः सन्धयः तेषु उत्पन्नस्य नारायणस्य दशाकृतयः यस्याः सा। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. कराङ्गुलिनखोत्पन्ननारायणदशाकृतिः means one who is accompanied by the ten forms of śrī nārāyaṇa that emerged from her ten fingernails. bhaṇḍāsura used the missile called sarvāsurāstra to create demons such as somaka, rāvaṇa and hiraṇyākṣa, who began fighting śrīdevī. in a moment, she made the ten forms of śrī nārāyaṇa arise from her ten fingernails. each form fought the corresponding demon and killed him. nārāyaṇa can indicate both jīva and īśvara. daśākṛti can be understood in relation to the states of the jīva and the works of īśvara. the five states of the jīva are waking, dream, deep sleep, turīya and turīyātīta. the five works of nārāyaṇa are creation, sustenance, destruction, concealment and grace. she performs all these effortlessly through her ten fingernails. the source of all avatāras: lord nārāyaṇa represents the cosmic protective force. the ten avatāras (incarnations like matsya, kūrma, and kṛṣṇa) descend to restore cosmic balance. these ten great incarnations are merely minor, spontaneous expressions of her own ten finger-nails. she is the ultimate, primordial source from which all preserving, protecting, and liberating energies of the cosmos emerge.","esoteric":["The Source of All Avatāras: Lord Nārāyaṇa represents the cosmic protective force. The ten Avatāras (incarnations like Matsya, Kūrma, and Kṛṣṇa) descend to restore cosmic balance. these ten great incarnations are merely minor, spontaneous expressions of Her own ten finger-nails. She is the ultimate, primordial source from which all preserving, protecting, and liberating energies of the cosmos emerge."]},{"number":81,"name":"महापाशुपतास्त्राग्निनिर्धग्धासुरसैनिका","samasa":["• महच्च तत् पाशुपतं च यद् अस्त्रं (अद्वैतवृत्तियः वा) तस्य अग्निना निर्धग्धा असुरस्य सैनिका (आविद्यकवृत्तयः वा) यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["महापाशुपतास्त्राग्निनिर्धग्धासुरसैनिका means one who burned the army of demons with the fire of the Mahāpāśupata missile. The Pāśupata missile itself is capable of burning the whole world, and its presiding deity is Paramaśiva as Paśupati. Paśupati is connected with the three guṇas. The Mahāpāśupata missile is more powerful than the Pāśupata, and its presiding deity is Sadāśiva, who is beyond the three guṇas. Bhaṇḍa's army was burned by the Mahāpāśupata missile. Internally, the Mahāpāśupata fire represents the force by which Advaita grows through intense practice and burns the army of demonic ignorance. The Pāśupata mantra has six letters, while the Mahāpāśupata mantra is different."],"searchText":"81 महापाशुपतास्त्राग्निनिर्धग्धासुरसैनिका • महच्च तत् पाशुपतं च यद् अस्त्रं (अद्वैतवृत्तियः वा) तस्य अग्निना निर्धग्धा असुरस्य सैनिका (आविद्यकवृत्तयः वा) यया सा। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. महापाशुपतास्त्राग्निनिर्धग्धासुरसैनिका means one who burned the army of demons with the fire of the mahāpāśupata missile. the pāśupata missile itself is capable of burning the whole world, and its presiding deity is paramaśiva as paśupati. paśupati is connected with the three guṇas. the mahāpāśupata missile is more powerful than the pāśupata, and its presiding deity is sadāśiva, who is beyond the three guṇas. bhaṇḍa's army was burned by the mahāpāśupata missile. internally, the mahāpāśupata fire represents the force by which advaita grows through intense practice and burns the army of demonic ignorance. the pāśupata mantra has six letters, while the mahāpāśupata mantra is different. the fire of non-dual vision: the pāśupata weapon is the ultimate weapon of śiva, the lord of beasts (paśu). the \"army of demons\" represents the dualistic thoughts (āvidyaka-vṛttis) that bind the individual soul as a beast (pasu). when the fire of non-dual realization is released, it instantly burns away all dualistic concepts and attachments.","esoteric":["The Fire of Non-Dual Vision: The Pāśupata weapon is the ultimate weapon of Śiva, the lord of beasts (Paśu). The \"army of demons\" represents the dualistic thoughts (āvidyaka-vṛttis) that bind the individual soul as a beast (pasu). When the fire of non-dual realization is released, it instantly burns away all dualistic concepts and attachments."]},{"number":82,"name":"कामेश्वरास्त्रनिर्दग्धसभंडासुरशून्यका","samasa":["• कामेश्वरस्य यद् अस्त्रं तस्य अग्निना निर्दग्धं भंडासुरेण सहितं शून्यकाख्यं (नगरं) यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["नगरं — city"],"summary":["कामेश्वरास्त्रनिर्दग्धसभंडासुरशून्यका means one who burned Bhaṇḍāsura and his city Śūnyaka with the Kāmeśvara missile. Bhaṇḍāsura built Śoṇita and Śūnyaka as his capital cities. The Mahākāmeśvara missile is stronger than the Mahāpāśupata and completely destroyed Bhaṇḍāsura and his two cities. Śūnya means nil or zero, and the city became nil as its name suggests. Śoṇita means blood, which strengthens arrogance in the human mind; because the city was red like blood, it was called Śoṇita. Śūnyaka indicates the illusion that something exists where there is nothing. Bhaṇḍa and his cities were reduced to ashes without trace by the Kāmeśvarāstra. This name shows that when the jīva matures toward mokṣa, nothing remains except the śūnya-like residue that is also burned in the cit-flame of Kāmeśvara, leaving only the form of pure consciousness."],"searchText":"82 कामेश्वरास्त्रनिर्दग्धसभंडासुरशून्यका • कामेश्वरस्य यद् अस्त्रं तस्य अग्निना निर्दग्धं भंडासुरेण सहितं शून्यकाख्यं (नगरं) यया सा। नगरं — city कामेश्वरास्त्रनिर्दग्धसभंडासुरशून्यका means one who burned bhaṇḍāsura and his city śūnyaka with the kāmeśvara missile. bhaṇḍāsura built śoṇita and śūnyaka as his capital cities. the mahākāmeśvara missile is stronger than the mahāpāśupata and completely destroyed bhaṇḍāsura and his two cities. śūnya means nil or zero, and the city became nil as its name suggests. śoṇita means blood, which strengthens arrogance in the human mind; because the city was red like blood, it was called śoṇita. śūnyaka indicates the illusion that something exists where there is nothing. bhaṇḍa and his cities were reduced to ashes without trace by the kāmeśvarāstra. this name shows that when the jīva matures toward mokṣa, nothing remains except the śūnya-like residue that is also burned in the cit-flame of kāmeśvara, leaving only the form of pure consciousness. dissolving the illusion of the void: śūnyaka literally means \"the void\" or \"nothingness.\" it is the citadel of bhaṇḍāsura. while standard practices can dismantle individual ego-thoughts, the root impression of ignorance (mūlāvidyā) often retreats into a blank void of deep sleep or passive emptiness (śūnya). the kāmeśvarāstra is the weapon of supreme, self-luminous non-dual realization. it burns down not just the active ego, but the very \"void\" or blank canvas of ignorance, leaving only the pristine light of pure consciousness.","esoteric":["Dissolving the Illusion of the Void: Śūnyaka literally means \"the void\" or \"nothingness.\" It is the citadel of Bhaṇḍāsura. While standard practices can dismantle individual ego-thoughts, the root impression of ignorance (Mūlāvidyā) often retreats into a blank void of deep sleep or passive emptiness (Śūnya). The Kāmeśvarāstra is the weapon of supreme, self-luminous non-dual realization. It burns down not just the active ego, but the very \"void\" or blank canvas of ignorance, leaving only the pristine light of pure consciousness."]},{"number":83,"name":"ब्रह्मोपेन्द्रमहेन्द्रादिदेवसंस्तुतवैभवा","samasa":["• ब्रह्मोपेन्द्रमहेन्द्रादिभिः देवैः सम्यक् स्तुतं वैभवं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["देवैः — deva; divine being","वैभवं — glory"],"summary":["ब्रह्मोपेन्द्रमहेन्द्रादिदेवसंस्तुतवैभवा means one whose glory is praised by Brahmā, Upendra, Mahendra and other devas. Upendra is Viṣṇu in the form of Vāmana, born to Aditi, the mother of Indra, and therefore called the younger brother of Indra. Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Indra and other devas praise Śrīdevī by recognising Her all-pervading greatness and omnipotence. This praise is the celebration of Her being the Self of all. The names up to this point show Śrīdevī's resolve and power in fulfilling the purpose of the devas."],"searchText":"83 ब्रह्मोपेन्द्रमहेन्द्रादिदेवसंस्तुतवैभवा • ब्रह्मोपेन्द्रमहेन्द्रादिभिः देवैः सम्यक् स्तुतं वैभवं यस्याः सा। देवैः — deva; divine being वैभवं — glory ब्रह्मोपेन्द्रमहेन्द्रादिदेवसंस्तुतवैभवा means one whose glory is praised by brahmā, upendra, mahendra and other devas. upendra is viṣṇu in the form of vāmana, born to aditi, the mother of indra, and therefore called the younger brother of indra. brahmā, viṣṇu, indra and other devas praise śrīdevī by recognising her all-pervading greatness and omnipotence. this praise is the celebration of her being the self of all. the names up to this point show śrīdevī's resolve and power in fulfilling the purpose of the devas. the sovereign of all deities: brahmā (creation), viṣṇu (preservation), and indra (cosmic administration) are the supreme functional lords of the cosmos. by having her majesty praised by them, it signifies that even these primary cosmic intelligences recognize that their powers are derived entirely from her supreme, central authority.","esoteric":["The Sovereign of All Deities: Brahmā (Creation), Viṣṇu (Preservation), and Indra (Cosmic Administration) are the supreme functional lords of the cosmos. By having Her majesty praised by them, it signifies that even these primary cosmic intelligences recognize that their powers are derived entirely from Her supreme, central authority."]},{"number":84,"name":"हरनेत्राग्निसन्दग्धकामसञ्जीवनौषधिः","samasa":["• हरस्य नेत्रेण अग्निना सम्यक् दग्धस्य कामस्य सञ्जीवनौषधिः।"],"wordByWord":["कामस्य — desire; Kāma"],"summary":["हरनेत्राग्निसन्दग्धकामसञ्जीवनौषधिः means one who gave the life-restoring medicine to Kāma after he was burned by the fire of Hara's eye. Sañjīvinī is a herb capable of reviving the dead, and jīvātu is another name for it. After the destruction of Bhaṇḍāsura, Śrīdevī revived Kāma at the request of the devas. A child punished by the father goes to the mother for support; similarly Kāma, burned by Paramaśiva, received life again from Mother Śrīdevī. Hara is detached from worldly affairs and burned Kāma, who represents attachment. Śrīdevī attracted that same Hara toward Herself and made Him Kāmeśvara. When Kāmeśvara's glance joined Kāmeśvarī's, it became the medicine that gave Kāma rebirth. In another sense, She is the remedy that destroys ignorance and enables the jīva to reach the reality of God."],"searchText":"84 हरनेत्राग्निसन्दग्धकामसञ्जीवनौषधिः • हरस्य नेत्रेण अग्निना सम्यक् दग्धस्य कामस्य सञ्जीवनौषधिः। कामस्य — desire; kāma हरनेत्राग्निसन्दग्धकामसञ्जीवनौषधिः means one who gave the life-restoring medicine to kāma after he was burned by the fire of hara's eye. sañjīvinī is a herb capable of reviving the dead, and jīvātu is another name for it. after the destruction of bhaṇḍāsura, śrīdevī revived kāma at the request of the devas. a child punished by the father goes to the mother for support; similarly kāma, burned by paramaśiva, received life again from mother śrīdevī. hara is detached from worldly affairs and burned kāma, who represents attachment. śrīdevī attracted that same hara toward herself and made him kāmeśvara. when kāmeśvara's glance joined kāmeśvarī's, it became the medicine that gave kāma rebirth. in another sense, she is the remedy that destroys ignorance and enables the jīva to reach the reality of god. the resurrection of divine desire: when śiva's eye of pure transcendence burned cupid (worldly desire), the universe was threatened with absolute, cold stasis. she acts as the sañjīvana-auṣadhi (the life-giving medicine) to resurrect him. this represents the transmutation of desire. she does not resurrect carnal desire; rather, she revives desire in its highest, most auspicious form—as भक्ति(bhakti — love for the divine) and इच्छा (icchā — the creative will to manifest good in the world).","esoteric":["The Resurrection of Divine Desire: When Śiva's eye of pure transcendence burned Cupid (worldly desire), the universe was threatened with absolute, cold stasis. She acts as the Sañjīvana-auṣadhi (the life-giving medicine) to resurrect Him. This represents the transmutation of desire. She does not resurrect carnal desire; rather, She revives desire in its highest, most auspicious form—as भक्ति(Bhakti — love for the divine) and इच्छा (Icchā — the creative will to manifest good in the world)."]},{"number":85,"name":"श्रीमद्वाग्भवकूटैकस्वरूपमुखपङ्कजा","samasa":["• श्रीमद्वाग्भवनामकं कूटम् एव एकं स्वं रूपं यस्य तादृशं मुखपङ्कजं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["रूपं — form"],"summary":["श्रीमद्वाग्भवकूटैकस्वरूपमुखपङ्कजा means one whose lotus face is identical with the Śrīmad Vāgbhava-kūṭa, the first group of the Pañcadaśī mantra. The Śrīvidyā mantra has fifteen syllables arranged in three groups. The first group, called Vāgbhava-kūṭa, has five syllables. It has the special power of giving knowledge and is therefore called śrīmad. When Śrīdevī emerged from the sacrificial fire, Her face was first seen, and so the description of Her form begins there. Most of the organs through which the mind moves outward are in the face. This five-syllabled group forms Her face in the mantra-body, with speech as the principal element."],"searchText":"85 श्रीमद्वाग्भवकूटैकस्वरूपमुखपङ्कजा • श्रीमद्वाग्भवनामकं कूटम् एव एकं स्वं रूपं यस्य तादृशं मुखपङ्कजं यस्याः सा। रूपं — form श्रीमद्वाग्भवकूटैकस्वरूपमुखपङ्कजा means one whose lotus face is identical with the śrīmad vāgbhava-kūṭa, the first group of the pañcadaśī mantra. the śrīvidyā mantra has fifteen syllables arranged in three groups. the first group, called vāgbhava-kūṭa, has five syllables. it has the special power of giving knowledge and is therefore called śrīmad. when śrīdevī emerged from the sacrificial fire, her face was first seen, and so the description of her form begins there. most of the organs through which the mind moves outward are in the face. this five-syllabled group forms her face in the mantra-body, with speech as the principal element. the mantric face of speech: this initiates the mantra-uddhāra of the fifteen-syllabled पञ्चदशाक्षरी (pañcadaśākṣarī) mantra. the first part, वाग्भव कूट(vāgbhava-kūṭa), rules over speech, intellect, and creative expression. her face is identical to this section of the mantra. when a seeker meditates on her beautiful face, they are internally vibrating and activating the syllables that refine their speech, poetry, and cognitive wisdom.","esoteric":["The Mantric Face of Speech: This initiates the Mantra-Uddhāra of the fifteen-syllabled पञ्चदशाक्षरी (Pañcadaśākṣarī) mantra. The first part, वाग्भव कूट(Vāgbhava-kūṭa), rules over speech, intellect, and creative expression. Her face is identical to this section of the mantra. When a seeker meditates on Her beautiful face, they are internally vibrating and activating the syllables that refine their speech, poetry, and cognitive wisdom."]},{"number":86,"name":"कण्ठाधःकटिपर्यंतमध्यकूटस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• कण्ठस्य अधः कटिपर्यंतः यस्य मध्यस्य स एव कूटस्य स्वं रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मध्यस्य — middle","रूपं — form"],"summary":["कण्ठाधःकटिपर्यंतमध्यकूटस्वरूपिणी means one whose middle region, from below the neck to the waist, is the Madhyakūṭa or Kāmarāja-kūṭa. The second part of the Pañcadaśī mantra is called Madhyakūṭa or Kāmarāja-kūṭa and has six syllables. In Śrīdevī's mantra-form, the central portion below the neck and above the hips is this kūṭa. Wishes and desires are expressed through this part of the body; therefore it represents icchā-śakti, the power of will."],"searchText":"86 कण्ठाधःकटिपर्यंतमध्यकूटस्वरूपिणी • कण्ठस्य अधः कटिपर्यंतः यस्य मध्यस्य स एव कूटस्य स्वं रूपं यस्याः सा। मध्यस्य — middle रूपं — form कण्ठाधःकटिपर्यंतमध्यकूटस्वरूपिणी means one whose middle region, from below the neck to the waist, is the madhyakūṭa or kāmarāja-kūṭa. the second part of the pañcadaśī mantra is called madhyakūṭa or kāmarāja-kūṭa and has six syllables. in śrīdevī's mantra-form, the central portion below the neck and above the hips is this kūṭa. wishes and desires are expressed through this part of the body; therefore it represents icchā-śakti, the power of will. the mantric torso of love and will: the middle section of the mantra is the कामराज कूट (kāmarāja-kūṭa), which rules over desire, willpower, and the sustaining force of life.","esoteric":["The Mantric Torso of Love and Will: The middle section of the mantra is the कामराज कूट (Kāmarāja-kūṭa), which rules over desire, willpower, and the sustaining force of life."]},{"number":87,"name":"शक्तिकूटैकतापन्नकट्यधोभागधारिणी","samasa":["• शक्तिनामकेन कूटेन एकताम् आपन्नं कटेः अधोभागां धारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["शक्तिकूटैकतापन्नकट्यधोभागधारिणी means one whose lower body below the waist is identified with the Śaktikūṭa. The third part of the Pañcadaśī mantra has four syllables and forms the portion below Śrīdevī's hips in Her mantra-body. Kriyā-śakti, the energy of creation and action, comes from the lower part of the body. This third section is called Śaktikūṭa and is the form of kriyā-śakti. In the Pañcadaśī mantra, the Vāgbhava group is connected with knowledge, the Kāmarāja group with icchā-śakti and the fulfilment of what is sought, and the Śaktikūṭa with energies such as creation and action."],"searchText":"87 शक्तिकूटैकतापन्नकट्यधोभागधारिणी • शक्तिनामकेन कूटेन एकताम् आपन्नं कटेः अधोभागां धारयतीति। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. शक्तिकूटैकतापन्नकट्यधोभागधारिणी means one whose lower body below the waist is identified with the śaktikūṭa. the third part of the pañcadaśī mantra has four syllables and forms the portion below śrīdevī's hips in her mantra-body. kriyā-śakti, the energy of creation and action, comes from the lower part of the body. this third section is called śaktikūṭa and is the form of kriyā-śakti. in the pañcadaśī mantra, the vāgbhava group is connected with knowledge, the kāmarāja group with icchā-śakti and the fulfilment of what is sought, and the śaktikūṭa with energies such as creation and action. the mantric base of liberation: the final section of the mantra, शक्तिकूट (śakti-kūṭa), rules over dissolution, transcendence, and liberation (mokṣa). her lower limbs, which rest upon the earth, represent the terminal ground where the manifest energy resolves back into the absolute. meditating on her lower form completes the mantra, dissolving the physical boundaries of the seeker and ushering them into the non-dual state.","esoteric":["The Mantric Base of Liberation: The final section of the mantra, शक्तिकूट (Śakti-kūṭa), rules over dissolution, transcendence, and liberation (Mokṣa). Her lower limbs, which rest upon the earth, represent the terminal ground where the manifest energy resolves back into the absolute. Meditating on Her lower form completes the mantra, dissolving the physical boundaries of the seeker and ushering them into the non-dual state."]},{"number":88,"name":"मूलमन्त्रात्मिका","samasa":["• (चतुर्विधपुरुषार्थमूलकारणत्वात्) मूलं मन्त्र आत्मा (स्वरूपं) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मूलं — root; original","मन्त्र — mantra","आत्मा — self","स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature"],"summary":["मूलमन्त्रात्मिका means one who Herself is the mūla-mantra. Mantra means that which protects through repetition. The most important mantra is the Pañcadaśākṣarī. There is no difference between a mantra and its presiding deity; one who separates them is mistaken. Mūla means cause. Śrīdevī is the first cause of creation and is Herself in the form of Her own mantra. She is also the root cause of human purpose. The word mūla also points to the subtle kāmakalā, the primary root of Pañcadaśākṣarī itself. One who is in this form is Kāmakalāsvarūpiṇī. The inherent meaning of kāmakalā is to be learned from a proper teacher."],"searchText":"88 मूलमन्त्रात्मिका • (चतुर्विधपुरुषार्थमूलकारणत्वात्) मूलं मन्त्र आत्मा (स्वरूपं) यस्याः सा। मूलं — root; original मन्त्र — mantra आत्मा — self स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature मूलमन्त्रात्मिका means one who herself is the mūla-mantra. mantra means that which protects through repetition. the most important mantra is the pañcadaśākṣarī. there is no difference between a mantra and its presiding deity; one who separates them is mistaken. mūla means cause. śrīdevī is the first cause of creation and is herself in the form of her own mantra. she is also the root cause of human purpose. the word mūla also points to the subtle kāmakalā, the primary root of pañcadaśākṣarī itself. one who is in this form is kāmakalāsvarūpiṇī. the inherent meaning of kāmakalā is to be learned from a proper teacher. the identity of sound and deity: this is the ultimate declaration of mantra-śāstra. there is no difference between the deity and the mantra. the deity is not a separate entity residing in a far-off heaven; she isthe sound-formula itself. the fifteen syllables are the literal, sonic vibrations that constitute her dynamic body of grace, acting as the root cause of all human achievements (puruṣārthas).","esoteric":["The Identity of Sound and Deity: This is the ultimate declaration of Mantra-śāstra. there is no difference between the deity and the mantra. The deity is not a separate entity residing in a far-off heaven; She isthe sound-formula itself. The fifteen syllables are the literal, sonic vibrations that constitute Her dynamic body of grace, acting as the root cause of all human achievements (Puruṣārthas)."]},{"number":89,"name":"मूलकूटत्रयकलेवरा","samasa":["• मूलस्य कूटत्रयम् एव कलेवरं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मूलस्य — root; original"],"summary":["मूलकूटत्रयकलेवरा means one whose subtle body is identical with the mūla-mantra and its three groups of syllables. She has as Her body the three groups of the mantra, consisting respectively of five, six and four syllables. She also has the subtle kāmakalā, the root of these groups, as Her body. Kāmakalā has one bindu at the top, two bindus in the centre and a triangle at the bottom. Her body-profile is similar to this form."],"searchText":"89 मूलकूटत्रयकलेवरा • मूलस्य कूटत्रयम् एव कलेवरं यस्याः सा। मूलस्य — root; original मूलकूटत्रयकलेवरा means one whose subtle body is identical with the mūla-mantra and its three groups of syllables. she has as her body the three groups of the mantra, consisting respectively of five, six and four syllables. she also has the subtle kāmakalā, the root of these groups, as her body. kāmakalā has one bindu at the top, two bindus in the centre and a triangle at the bottom. her body-profile is similar to this form. the triune body of sound: this completes the mantric sequence. her body is the literal three sections (vāgbhava, kāmarāja, and śakti). this teaches the practitioner that when they visualize her form, they must perceive her not as flesh and bone, but as a living, breathing body of sacred, non-dual sound vibration.","esoteric":["The Triune Body of Sound: This completes the mantric sequence. Her body is the literal three sections (Vāgbhava, Kāmarāja, and Śakti). This teaches the practitioner that when they visualize Her form, they must perceive Her not as flesh and bone, but as a living, breathing body of sacred, non-dual sound vibration."]},{"number":90,"name":"कुलामृतैकरसिका","samasa":["• (कुः लीयते यस्मिन्निति कुलम्। कुलसम्बन्धलक्षणया सहस्रारात्स्रवदमृतं कुलामृतम्)। कुलामृतस्य रसिका।"],"wordByWord":["कुलम्। — family; kula tradition","रसिका। — enjoyer; relisher"],"summary":["कुलामृतैकरसिका means one who delights only in kulāmṛta, the nectar that flows through the awakened subtle path. Śrīdevī's gross and subtle forms have been described, and now the subtle energy called Kuṇḍalinī in every human being is discussed. The suṣumṇā nāḍī runs from the base of the body to the inner part of the skull through the centre of the body along the backbone. Kuṇḍalinī sleeps at the base in the form of a serpent coiled three and a half times, with its head downward. When awakened by yoga, it rises through suṣumṇā to the skull. There the energy melts, seeps down and flows through the body as nectar called kulāmṛta. Śrīdevī delights in this nectar. A yogi enjoys being drenched in its rain. Mūlādhāra is the abode of the pṛthvī-tattva."],"searchText":"90 कुलामृतैकरसिका • (कुः लीयते यस्मिन्निति कुलम्। कुलसम्बन्धलक्षणया सहस्रारात्स्रवदमृतं कुलामृतम्)। कुलामृतस्य रसिका। कुलम्। — family; kula tradition रसिका। — enjoyer; relisher कुलामृतैकरसिका means one who delights only in kulāmṛta, the nectar that flows through the awakened subtle path. śrīdevī's gross and subtle forms have been described, and now the subtle energy called kuṇḍalinī in every human being is discussed. the suṣumṇā nāḍī runs from the base of the body to the inner part of the skull through the centre of the body along the backbone. kuṇḍalinī sleeps at the base in the form of a serpent coiled three and a half times, with its head downward. when awakened by yoga, it rises through suṣumṇā to the skull. there the energy melts, seeps down and flows through the body as nectar called kulāmṛta. śrīdevī delights in this nectar. a yogi enjoys being drenched in its rain. mūlādhāra is the abode of the pṛthvī-tattva. the nectar of the crown: the kulāmṛta is the cool, ecstatic nectar that overflows from the sahasrāra when the kuṇḍalinī completes her ascent. she is rasikā because she takes delight in tasting this nectar of non-dual realization alongside the practitioner, validating their spiritual success.","esoteric":["The Nectar of the Crown: The Kulāmṛta is the cool, ecstatic nectar that overflows from the Sahasrāra when the Kuṇḍalinī completes Her ascent. She is Rasikā because She takes delight in tasting this nectar of non-dual realization alongside the practitioner, validating their spiritual success."]},{"number":91,"name":"कुलसङ्केतपालिनी","samasa":["• कुलस्य सङ्केतान् पालयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["कुलस्य — family; kula tradition"],"summary":["कुलसङ्केतपालिनी means one who guards the secret doctrine of the Kaulas. The energy called Kaula is kept in a secret place in the body, where it lies asleep. How it is awakened, raised upward, and made to cause kulāmṛta to flow through the nāḍīs of the body is not ordinary knowledge. The awakened Kuṇḍalinī gives various powers, and these matters are described in cryptic language in Tantrāśāstras so that only those who are fit can understand them. The knowledge of Kaula, or Kuṇḍalinī, is itself called Kaula. Śrīdevī protects this secret language from the unqualified. Ācāra is also called kula, and these ācāras are secret; Śrīdevī protects them. There are three secret ways in Her upāsanā: secret cakras, secret mantras, and secret worship."],"searchText":"91 कुलसङ्केतपालिनी • कुलस्य सङ्केतान् पालयतीति। कुलस्य — family; kula tradition कुलसङ्केतपालिनी means one who guards the secret doctrine of the kaulas. the energy called kaula is kept in a secret place in the body, where it lies asleep. how it is awakened, raised upward, and made to cause kulāmṛta to flow through the nāḍīs of the body is not ordinary knowledge. the awakened kuṇḍalinī gives various powers, and these matters are described in cryptic language in tantrāśāstras so that only those who are fit can understand them. the knowledge of kaula, or kuṇḍalinī, is itself called kaula. śrīdevī protects this secret language from the unqualified. ācāra is also called kula, and these ācāras are secret; śrīdevī protects them. there are three secret ways in her upāsanā: secret cakras, secret mantras, and secret worship. the keeper of the mystical codes: in śrī vidyā, the kula tradition involves distinct modes of internal worship, geometric layouts (śrī cakra), and mantra placement (nyāsa). the saṅketas are the highly classified, esoteric correspondences between the mantra, the diagram, and the human body. she is pālinī because she guards these mysteries from casual, insincere intellectual curiosity, revealing their protective power only to initiated practitioners who approach with reverence and mental purity.","esoteric":["The Keeper of the Mystical Codes: In Śrī Vidyā, the Kula tradition involves distinct modes of internal worship, geometric layouts (Śrī Cakra), and mantra placement (nyāsa). The saṅketas are the highly classified, esoteric correspondences between the mantra, the diagram, and the human body. She is Pālinī because She guards these mysteries from casual, insincere intellectual curiosity, revealing their protective power only to initiated practitioners who approach with reverence and mental purity."]},{"number":92,"name":"कुलाङ्गना","samasa":["• कुलसम्बन्धिनी अङ्गना।"],"wordByWord":["अङ्गना। — woman"],"summary":["कुलाङ्गना means one who belongs to a noble and chaste family. A lady of a good family protects the dignity and secrets of the family. She is a kulastrī and a pativratā, born in a good family and married into a good family. Such a kulastrī is normally not seen by outsiders. Similarly, Śrīdevī hides Herself behind the veil of avidyā. Śrīvidyā, the worship of Śrīdevī, is a supreme secret and is not to be revealed casually to others. Therefore She is called Kulāṅganā. Śrīvidyā is protected as a secret, but for those who are properly initiated and who follow it, it is known and intimate, just as a pativratā, unseen by outsiders, moves closely with her own people."],"searchText":"92 कुलाङ्गना • कुलसम्बन्धिनी अङ्गना। अङ्गना। — woman कुलाङ्गना means one who belongs to a noble and chaste family. a lady of a good family protects the dignity and secrets of the family. she is a kulastrī and a pativratā, born in a good family and married into a good family. such a kulastrī is normally not seen by outsiders. similarly, śrīdevī hides herself behind the veil of avidyā. śrīvidyā, the worship of śrīdevī, is a supreme secret and is not to be revealed casually to others. therefore she is called kulāṅganā. śrīvidyā is protected as a secret, but for those who are properly initiated and who follow it, it is known and intimate, just as a pativratā, unseen by outsiders, moves closely with her own people. the noble consort of the absolute: in worldly language, kulāṅganā refers to a modest woman of highly respectable lineage who stays loyal to her home. esoterically, the \"home\" is the kuṇḍalinī path. she is kulāṅganā because she never leaks her energy outward into the material world of distractions; she remains completely chaste, moving internally through her own dynamic path to unite with her singular consort, paramaśiva, at the crown.","esoteric":["The Noble Consort of the Absolute: In worldly language, kulāṅganā refers to a modest woman of highly respectable lineage who stays loyal to her home. Esoterically, the \"home\" is the Kuṇḍalinī path. She is Kulāṅganā because She never leaks Her energy outward into the material world of distractions; She remains completely chaste, moving internally through Her own dynamic path to unite with Her singular consort, Paramaśiva, at the crown."]},{"number":93,"name":"कुलान्तस्था","samasa":["• कुलस्य अन्तः तिष्ठतीति/ स्था।"],"wordByWord":["कुलस्य — family; kula tradition","अन्तः — inside"],"summary":["कुलान्तस्था means one who resides within kula. Kula can refer to the triad of mātṛ, māna and meya: the measurer, the means of knowing, and the object measured. Among these, She is in the form of māna, the intellect or means of knowledge. She can also be known through the Kula tantras, which explain methods of worship, methods of yoga, and related secrets. In good families, the family and its lineage are well known; Śrīdevī dwells as Śakti in such families, present in every house, street, village and nation. The suṣumṇā nāḍī is also called kula, and She resides in it. Kuṇḍalinī travels only through this nāḍī."],"searchText":"93 कुलान्तस्था • कुलस्य अन्तः तिष्ठतीति/ स्था। कुलस्य — family; kula tradition अन्तः — inside कुलान्तस्था means one who resides within kula. kula can refer to the triad of mātṛ, māna and meya: the measurer, the means of knowing, and the object measured. among these, she is in the form of māna, the intellect or means of knowledge. she can also be known through the kula tantras, which explain methods of worship, methods of yoga, and related secrets. in good families, the family and its lineage are well known; śrīdevī dwells as śakti in such families, present in every house, street, village and nation. the suṣumṇā nāḍī is also called kula, and she resides in it. kuṇḍalinī travels only through this nāḍī. the core of the energy system: as established in the agamas, kula denotes the manifest universe and the physical body with its network of nerve channels (nāḍīs). she is kulāntasthā because she sits at the absolute dead center of this network. she is the dormant energy at the base and the vibrant consciousness flowing through the central vertical axis, showing that the physical body is completely animated by her presence inside it.","esoteric":["The Core of the Energy System: As established in the Agamas, Kula denotes the manifest universe and the physical body with its network of nerve channels (nāḍīs). She is Kulāntasthā because She sits at the absolute dead center of this network. She is the dormant energy at the base and the vibrant consciousness flowing through the central vertical axis, showing that the physical body is completely animated by Her presence inside it."]},{"number":94,"name":"कौलिनी","samasa":["• कुले तिष्ठतीति।","• कुलेषु पूज्यत्वेन तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["कुले — family; kula tradition"],"summary":["कौलिनी means one who is the united form of Śiva and Śakti. Kula means Śakti, Akula is Śiva, and their unity is Kaula; She is of that form. The knowledge that recognises the apparent duality and relationship of Śiva and Śakti is Kaula, and one who possesses it is Kaulinī. Identifying the Śiva-cakras and Śakti-cakras separately and then recognising Śiva and Śakti as both distinct and united is called Kaula practice. Through yoga, Kuṇḍalinī is felt as Śiva-Śakti in the kula and akula cakras; this is Kaula-yoga, and She is connected with it. Kula-śakti is dynamic, while Akula, Śiva-śakti, is static. Their union occurs when the dynamic reaches and embraces the static. In external worship of Śrīcakra, the worshipper, Devī and devotion form one method called Kaula; She is worshipped through this method."],"searchText":"94 कौलिनी • कुले तिष्ठतीति। • कुलेषु पूज्यत्वेन तिष्ठतीति। कुले — family; kula tradition कौलिनी means one who is the united form of śiva and śakti. kula means śakti, akula is śiva, and their unity is kaula; she is of that form. the knowledge that recognises the apparent duality and relationship of śiva and śakti is kaula, and one who possesses it is kaulinī. identifying the śiva-cakras and śakti-cakras separately and then recognising śiva and śakti as both distinct and united is called kaula practice. through yoga, kuṇḍalinī is felt as śiva-śakti in the kula and akula cakras; this is kaula-yoga, and she is connected with it. kula-śakti is dynamic, while akula, śiva-śakti, is static. their union occurs when the dynamic reaches and embraces the static. in external worship of śrīcakra, the worshipper, devī and devotion form one method called kaula; she is worshipped through this method. the soul of the kaula path: kaulinī is the direct energy that dictates the kaulamethod of realization. while the samaya path leans toward pure internal meditation, the kaula path embraces the complete alignment of manifest objects and physical energy centers. she is kaulinībecause she sanctifies this path, converting the physical body from a trap of flesh into a direct instrument of absolute liberation.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Kaula Path: Kaulinī is the direct energy that dictates the Kaulamethod of realization. while the Samaya path leans toward pure internal meditation, the Kaula path embraces the complete alignment of manifest objects and physical energy centers. She is Kaulinībecause She sanctifies this path, converting the physical body from a trap of flesh into a direct instrument of absolute liberation."]},{"number":95,"name":"कुलयोगिनी","samasa":["• कुले योगः अस्या इति।"],"wordByWord":["कुले — family; kula tradition"],"summary":["कुलयोगिनी means one connected with Kula worship. The word kula has the many meanings explained in the previous names, and She is related to each of those meanings; therefore She is Kulayoginī. She is the Śakti connected with each of the six cakras beginning with Mūlādhāra. The union of Akula and Kula through yoga is called Kula-yoga, and She is reached through this. She also lays down the ways and procedures for contemplating Śrīdevī in Śrīcakra form. She grants the blessing of birth in a noble family."],"searchText":"95 कुलयोगिनी • कुले योगः अस्या इति। कुले — family; kula tradition कुलयोगिनी means one connected with kula worship. the word kula has the many meanings explained in the previous names, and she is related to each of those meanings; therefore she is kulayoginī. she is the śakti connected with each of the six cakras beginning with mūlādhāra. the union of akula and kula through yoga is called kula-yoga, and she is reached through this. she also lays down the ways and procedures for contemplating śrīdevī in śrīcakra form. she grants the blessing of birth in a noble family. the sovereign of the psychic network: a yoginī controls specific networks of energy. she is the kulayoginī because she links the individual bodily functions (vyaṣṭi) to the grand cosmic architecture (samaṣṭi). her \"union\" (yoga) ensures that the macrocosmic cycles of time, space, and breath are perfectly mirrored within the microscopic energy centers of the practitioner.","esoteric":["The Sovereign of the Psychic Network: A Yoginī controls specific networks of energy. She is the Kulayoginī because She links the individual bodily functions (Vyaṣṭi) to the grand cosmic architecture (Samaṣṭi). Her \"union\" (yoga) ensures that the macrocosmic cycles of time, space, and breath are perfectly mirrored within the microscopic energy centers of the practitioner."]},{"number":96,"name":"अकुला","samasa":["• न विद्यते कुलं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अकुला — beyond kula","कुलं — family; kula tradition"],"summary":["अकुला means one who is beyond kula. Kula also means parents, family, lineage and birthplace; Śrīdevī is beyond all of these, because She is beyond birth. Therefore She has no kula and is Akulā. The suṣumṇā nāḍī is also connected with this meaning, and She resides there. Akulācāra is beyond kulācāra and is commonly known as samayācāra. She is also in the form of samayācāra."],"searchText":"96 अकुला • न विद्यते कुलं यस्याः सा। अकुला — beyond kula कुलं — family; kula tradition अकुला means one who is beyond kula. kula also means parents, family, lineage and birthplace; śrīdevī is beyond all of these, because she is beyond birth. therefore she has no kula and is akulā. the suṣumṇā nāḍī is also connected with this meaning, and she resides there. akulācāra is beyond kulācāra and is commonly known as samayācāra. she is also in the form of samayācāra. the transcendent reality: this name forms a profound philosophical pair with the preceding names. while she is kaulinī (the manifest body/universe), she is simultaneously akulā—the formless, unconditioned, non-dual brahmansitting far beyond name, form, caste, or category. it matches the absolute state of paramaśiva, who is historically termed akula.","esoteric":["The Transcendent Reality: This name forms a profound philosophical pair with the preceding names. While She is Kaulinī (the manifest body/universe), She is simultaneously Akulā—the formless, unconditioned, non-dual Brahmansitting far beyond name, form, caste, or category. It matches the absolute state of Paramaśiva, who is historically termed Akula."]},{"number":97,"name":"समयान्तस्था","samasa":["• समयस्य अन्तः तिष्ठतीति/ स्था।"],"wordByWord":["समयस्य — samaya tradition","अन्तः — inside"],"summary":["समयान्तस्था means one who abides in the inner Samaya worship of Śiva and Śakti. Samaya is worship offered inwardly and jointly to Śiva and Śakti in the ether of the heart. External worship of a cakra is called Kula, while internal worship of the cakra through meditation is called Samaya. This worship is accepted as supreme, and She dwells in this type of Samaya. Śiva and Śakti are alike and equal; hence Śiva is called Samaya and Śakti is also called Samaya. Their equality is understood in five ways: equality of seat, equality of activity, equality of state or action, equality of name, and equality of form. Understanding these similarities and seeing no difference between Śiva and Śakti, worshipping them through meditation is the Samaya method."],"searchText":"97 समयान्तस्था • समयस्य अन्तः तिष्ठतीति/ स्था। समयस्य — samaya tradition अन्तः — inside समयान्तस्था means one who abides in the inner samaya worship of śiva and śakti. samaya is worship offered inwardly and jointly to śiva and śakti in the ether of the heart. external worship of a cakra is called kula, while internal worship of the cakra through meditation is called samaya. this worship is accepted as supreme, and she dwells in this type of samaya. śiva and śakti are alike and equal; hence śiva is called samaya and śakti is also called samaya. their equality is understood in five ways: equality of seat, equality of activity, equality of state or action, equality of name, and equality of form. understanding these similarities and seeing no difference between śiva and śakti, worshipping them through meditation is the samaya method. samaya means \"equal path\" or pure internal meditation where śiva and śakti are worshiped as completely equal within the space of the heart (dahara-ākāśa). she is samayāntasthā because she is the final realization achieved through this highly refined, purely mental internalization of worship.","esoteric":["Samaya means \"equal path\" or pure internal meditation where Śiva and Śakti are worshiped as completely equal within the space of the heart (Dahara-ākāśa). She is Samayāntasthā because She is the final realization achieved through this highly refined, purely mental internalization of worship."]},{"number":98,"name":"समयाचारतत्परा","samasa":["• समयाचारे तत्परा।"],"wordByWord":["तत्परा। — devoted"],"summary":["समयाचारतत्परा means one who is deeply devoted to samayācāra. Samayācāra is an internal form of worship. After proper initiation and purification, the aspirant worships Śrīdevī inwardly. Śrīdevī, sleeping in Mūlādhāra, awakens, adorns Herself in Svādhiṣṭhāna, emerges through Maṇipūra, receives worship and upacāras, and proceeds through the inner centres. She accepts worship at Anāhata, Viśuddhi and Ājñā, enjoys union with Śiva, and returns to Mūlādhāra. Enjoying this play of cit-śakti through imagination is samayācāra. As copper becomes gold through alchemy, the aspirant becomes Śrīdevī Herself through continuous contemplation. Without external tools of bāhya-pūjā, the aspirant imagines Śrīcakra within, experiences the union of Śiva and Śakti, and realises the unity of teacher, mantra, Śrīdevī, Śrīcakra and self."],"searchText":"98 समयाचारतत्परा • समयाचारे तत्परा। तत्परा। — devoted समयाचारतत्परा means one who is deeply devoted to samayācāra. samayācāra is an internal form of worship. after proper initiation and purification, the aspirant worships śrīdevī inwardly. śrīdevī, sleeping in mūlādhāra, awakens, adorns herself in svādhiṣṭhāna, emerges through maṇipūra, receives worship and upacāras, and proceeds through the inner centres. she accepts worship at anāhata, viśuddhi and ājñā, enjoys union with śiva, and returns to mūlādhāra. enjoying this play of cit-śakti through imagination is samayācāra. as copper becomes gold through alchemy, the aspirant becomes śrīdevī herself through continuous contemplation. without external tools of bāhya-pūjā, the aspirant imagines śrīcakra within, experiences the union of śiva and śakti, and realises the unity of teacher, mantra, śrīdevī, śrīcakra and self. the delight in internal devotion: this name confirms her affinity for pure, unadulterated internal contemplation. samayācāra removes the need for external physical rituals, lamps, or offerings, replacing them with steady mental focus within the crown or heart. she is tatparā (completely focused on this) because internal devotion strips away material duality, matching her true, non-dual essence.","esoteric":["The Delight in Internal Devotion: This name confirms Her affinity for pure, unadulterated internal contemplation. Samayācāra removes the need for external physical rituals, lamps, or offerings, replacing them with steady mental focus within the crown or heart. She is Tatparā (completely focused on this) because internal devotion strips away material duality, matching Her true, non-dual essence."]},{"number":99,"name":"मूलाधारैकनिलया","samasa":["• मूलाधारः एकः निलयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निलयः — abode"],"summary":["मूलाधारैकनिलया means one whose main residence is Mūlādhāra. The backbone is called merudaṇḍa, and the suṣumṇā nāḍī runs inside it. At the lowest part is Mūlādhāra, with Svādhiṣṭhāna above it, Maṇipūra near the lower abdomen, Anāhata in the chest, Viśuddhi in the neck, and Ājñā between the eyebrows. Above these six is the sahasrāra. The six cakras are grouped in pairs as agni, sūrya and candra kāṇḍas, and knots or granthis occur between these regions. The Mūlādhāra lotus has four petals. Kuṇḍalinī sleeps there, head downward, in the bindu called kulakuṇḍa within the karṇikā of this cakra. Mūlādhāra is so called because it is the base of Kuṇḍalinī and the root of suṣumṇā."],"searchText":"99 मूलाधारैकनिलया • मूलाधारः एकः निलयः यस्याः सा। निलयः — abode मूलाधारैकनिलया means one whose main residence is mūlādhāra. the backbone is called merudaṇḍa, and the suṣumṇā nāḍī runs inside it. at the lowest part is mūlādhāra, with svādhiṣṭhāna above it, maṇipūra near the lower abdomen, anāhata in the chest, viśuddhi in the neck, and ājñā between the eyebrows. above these six is the sahasrāra. the six cakras are grouped in pairs as agni, sūrya and candra kāṇḍas, and knots or granthis occur between these regions. the mūlādhāra lotus has four petals. kuṇḍalinī sleeps there, head downward, in the bindu called kulakuṇḍa within the karṇikā of this cakra. mūlādhāra is so called because it is the base of kuṇḍalinī and the root of suṣumṇā. the foundation of manifest existence: the mūlādhāra is the four-petaled root lotus at the base of the spine, governing the earth element. by calling it her eka-nilaya (primary home), the text positions her as the absolute root anchor of physical life. in her dormant state as the kuṇḍalinī snake, she sleeps here, holding up the physical structure of the practitioner before beginning her upward ascent.","esoteric":["The Foundation of Manifest Existence: The Mūlādhāra is the four-petaled root lotus at the base of the spine, governing the earth element. By calling it Her eka-nilaya (primary home), the text positions Her as the absolute root anchor of physical life. In Her dormant state as the Kuṇḍalinī snake, She sleeps here, holding up the physical structure of the practitioner before beginning Her upward ascent."]},{"number":100,"name":"ब्रह्मग्रन्थिविभेदिनी","samasa":["• ब्रह्मग्रन्थी विशेषेण भिनत्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["ब्रह्मग्रन्थिविभेदिनी means one who pierces the Brahmā-granthi. The first two cakras form the agni-kāṇḍa, connected with creation and with Brahmā. In the Samaya path, the six cakras are contemplated as Śrīcakra. The creation-cakra has three āvaraṇas: caturasra, ṣoḍaśadala and aṣṭadala. A granthi is a knot-like narrow passage between cakras. Kuṇḍalinī, rising from Mūlādhāra to Svādhiṣṭhāna and then to Maṇipūra, must pierce and pass through these knot-like passages. The first knot is Brahmā-granthi, in the region of Brahmā. These knots give Kuṇḍalinī a grip so that She does not fall while rising and also gains momentum upward. When Brahmā-granthi is pierced, the aspirant is freed from attachment to creation."],"searchText":"100 ब्रह्मग्रन्थिविभेदिनी • ब्रह्मग्रन्थी विशेषेण भिनत्तीति। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. ब्रह्मग्रन्थिविभेदिनी means one who pierces the brahmā-granthi. the first two cakras form the agni-kāṇḍa, connected with creation and with brahmā. in the samaya path, the six cakras are contemplated as śrīcakra. the creation-cakra has three āvaraṇas: caturasra, ṣoḍaśadala and aṣṭadala. a granthi is a knot-like narrow passage between cakras. kuṇḍalinī, rising from mūlādhāra to svādhiṣṭhāna and then to maṇipūra, must pierce and pass through these knot-like passages. the first knot is brahmā-granthi, in the region of brahmā. these knots give kuṇḍalinī a grip so that she does not fall while rising and also gains momentum upward. when brahmā-granthi is pierced, the aspirant is freed from attachment to creation. breaking the bondage of matter: in the vertical path of the suṣumṇā, there are three major psychic knots (granthis) that block the upward flow of energy. the first is the ब्रह्मग्रन्थि (brahmā-granthi), located just above the mūlādhāra center, which binds the soul to material attachments, physical desires, and inertia (tamas). as the kuṇḍalinī awakens, she acts as vibhedinī—piercing this knot cleanly, freeing the seeker's mind from physical bondage and allowing the energy to rise toward higher spiritual planes.","esoteric":["Breaking the Bondage of Matter: In the vertical path of the Suṣumṇā, there are three major psychic knots (granthis) that block the upward flow of energy. The first is the ब्रह्मग्रन्थि (Brahmā-granthi), located just above the Mūlādhāra center, which binds the soul to material attachments, physical desires, and inertia (tamas). As the Kuṇḍalinī awakens, She acts as Vibhedinī—piercing this knot cleanly, freeing the seeker's mind from physical bondage and allowing the energy to rise toward higher spiritual planes."]},{"number":101,"name":"मणिपूरान्तरुदिता","samasa":["• मणिभिः पूर्यते इति मणिपूरः। तस्य अन्तः उदिता।"],"wordByWord":["मणिभिः — jewel","मणिपूरः। — maṇipūra chakra","अन्तः — inside"],"summary":["मणिपूरान्तरुदिता means one who rises inside Maṇipūra. The lotus with ten petals near the navel is called Maṇipūra. It is also called the sthiti-cakra, the place of Viṣṇu and the sūrya-kāṇḍa. Kuṇḍalinī pierces the Brahmā-granthi in Mūlādhāra and Svādhiṣṭhāna and rises into Maṇipūra. There She receives upacāras from pādya up to the offering of jewels. Śrīdevī is decorated with various gems, or maṇis, and therefore this centre is called Maṇipūra. Since Śrīdevī rises here, She is called Maṇipūrāntaruditā."],"searchText":"101 मणिपूरान्तरुदिता • मणिभिः पूर्यते इति मणिपूरः। तस्य अन्तः उदिता। मणिभिः — jewel मणिपूरः। — maṇipūra chakra अन्तः — inside मणिपूरान्तरुदिता means one who rises inside maṇipūra. the lotus with ten petals near the navel is called maṇipūra. it is also called the sthiti-cakra, the place of viṣṇu and the sūrya-kāṇḍa. kuṇḍalinī pierces the brahmā-granthi in mūlādhāra and svādhiṣṭhāna and rises into maṇipūra. there she receives upacāras from pādya up to the offering of jewels. śrīdevī is decorated with various gems, or maṇis, and therefore this centre is called maṇipūra. since śrīdevī rises here, she is called maṇipūrāntaruditā. the awakening of the solar fire: the maṇipūra is the ten-petaled navel center, corresponding to the element of fire (agni). as the kuṇḍalinī cuts through the root barriers, she ascends and \"arises\" (uditā) in this solar center. this represents the dawning of clear inner focus, where the initial embers of spiritual practice turn into a steady, burning fire of dedication that refines the mind.","esoteric":["The Awakening of the Solar Fire: The Maṇipūra is the ten-petaled navel center, corresponding to the element of fire (agni). As the Kuṇḍalinī cuts through the root barriers, She ascends and \"arises\" (uditā) in this solar center. this represents the dawning of clear inner focus, where the initial embers of spiritual practice turn into a steady, burning fire of dedication that refines the mind."]},{"number":102,"name":"विष्णुग्रन्थिविभेदिनी","samasa":["• विष्णुग्रन्थिं विशिष्य भिनत्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["विष्णुग्रन्थिविभेदिनी means one who pierces the Viṣṇu-granthi. Kuṇḍalinī, rising out of Maṇipūra and proceeding toward Anāhata and Viśuddhi, passes through a very narrow path called Viṣṇu-granthi. This knot lies in the sustaining region connected with Viṣṇu. By piercing it, She conducts the aspirant beyond the sorrow connected with sthiti, or worldly maintenance and attachment. Thus She opens the path for the upward movement of Kuṇḍalinī through the subtle centres."],"searchText":"102 विष्णुग्रन्थिविभेदिनी • विष्णुग्रन्थिं विशिष्य भिनत्तीति। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. विष्णुग्रन्थिविभेदिनी means one who pierces the viṣṇu-granthi. kuṇḍalinī, rising out of maṇipūra and proceeding toward anāhata and viśuddhi, passes through a very narrow path called viṣṇu-granthi. this knot lies in the sustaining region connected with viṣṇu. by piercing it, she conducts the aspirant beyond the sorrow connected with sthiti, or worldly maintenance and attachment. thus she opens the path for the upward movement of kuṇḍalinī through the subtle centres. piercing the bondage of emotion: the second major psychic knot is the विष्णुग्रन्थि (viṣṇu-granthi), located near the heart (anāhata) center. this knot binds the seeker to emotional attachments, personal identity, and the desire for worldly action and recognition (rajas). by piercing this knot, she frees the heart from conditional, selfish attachments, transforming raw emotion into pure, universal love and devotion.","esoteric":["Piercing the Bondage of Emotion: The second major psychic knot is the विष्णुग्रन्थि (Viṣṇu-granthi), located near the heart (Anāhata) center. This knot binds the seeker to emotional attachments, personal identity, and the desire for worldly action and recognition (Rajas). By piercing this knot, She frees the heart from conditional, selfish attachments, transforming raw emotion into pure, universal love and devotion."]},{"number":103,"name":"आज्ञाचक्रान्तरालस्था","samasa":["• आज्ञाचक्रस्य अन्तराले तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["आज्ञाचक्रान्तरालस्था means one who abides within the Ājñā-cakra. The Ājñā-cakra is situated between the two eyebrows in the suṣumṇā nāḍī and has two petals. It is the place of the teacher who gives ājñā, or command; hence it is called Ājñā-cakra. Through the practice already completed, the mind becomes somewhat controlled and knowledge is gained. This centre is therefore connected with command, discipline and the rise of knowledge."],"searchText":"103 आज्ञाचक्रान्तरालस्था • आज्ञाचक्रस्य अन्तराले तिष्ठतीति। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. आज्ञाचक्रान्तरालस्था means one who abides within the ājñā-cakra. the ājñā-cakra is situated between the two eyebrows in the suṣumṇā nāḍī and has two petals. it is the place of the teacher who gives ājñā, or command; hence it is called ājñā-cakra. through the practice already completed, the mind becomes somewhat controlled and knowledge is gained. this centre is therefore connected with command, discipline and the rise of knowledge. the station of intuitive command: the ājñā cakra is the two-petaled center between the eyebrows, governing the mind and acting as the command post for intuitive knowledge. she sits antarāle (in the fine space between the two petals), representing the balance between the solar and lunar currents. at this point, the seeker's mind stops wavering, ready to follow the final commands of the inner self.","esoteric":["The Station of Intuitive Command: The Ājñā cakra is the two-petaled center between the eyebrows, governing the mind and acting as the command post for intuitive knowledge. She sits antarāle (in the fine space between the two petals), representing the balance between the solar and lunar currents. At this point, the seeker's mind stops wavering, ready to follow the final commands of the inner Self."]},{"number":104,"name":"रुद्रग्रन्थिविभेदिनी","samasa":["• रुद्रग्रन्थी विभिनत्तीति।","• तापसैः आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line."],"summary":["रुद्रग्रन्थिविभेदिनी means one who pierces the Rudra-granthi. This knot is between Viśuddhi and Ājñā, and Kuṇḍalinī must pierce it to pass upward. Śrīdevī is said to stay in the Ājñā-cakra, but Kuṇḍalinī reaches Ājñā from Mūlādhāra only after passing through the cakras and piercing the Rudra knot. In the Śrīvidyā mantra too, the groups are separated by the knots called hrīṃ. These three knots are called Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra granthis. Śrīdevī pierces these knots and moves through them. The deeper meaning is the unity of Śrīdevī, mantra, Śrīcakra, guru and self, with no difference among them."],"searchText":"104 रुद्रग्रन्थिविभेदिनी • रुद्रग्रन्थी विभिनत्तीति। • तापसैः आराध्या। word-by-word meaning could not be generated reliably from the available samāsa line. रुद्रग्रन्थिविभेदिनी means one who pierces the rudra-granthi. this knot is between viśuddhi and ājñā, and kuṇḍalinī must pierce it to pass upward. śrīdevī is said to stay in the ājñā-cakra, but kuṇḍalinī reaches ājñā from mūlādhāra only after passing through the cakras and piercing the rudra knot. in the śrīvidyā mantra too, the groups are separated by the knots called hrīṃ. these three knots are called brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra granthis. śrīdevī pierces these knots and moves through them. the deeper meaning is the unity of śrīdevī, mantra, śrīcakra, guru and self, with no difference among them. dissolving intellectual identity: the final psychic knot is the रुद्रग्रन्थि (rudra-granthi), located at the ājñā center. this knot binds the seeker to the subtle attachments of intellectual pride, spiritual visions, and the final boundary of individual ego. by piercing this knot, she dissolves the last remaining veil of duality, allowing the individual drop of consciousness to merge into the infinite ocean of the sahasrāra.","esoteric":["Dissolving Intellectual Identity: The final psychic knot is the रुद्रग्रन्थि (Rudra-granthi), located at the Ājñā center. This knot binds the seeker to the subtle attachments of intellectual pride, spiritual visions, and the final boundary of individual ego. By piercing this knot, She dissolves the last remaining veil of duality, allowing the individual drop of consciousness to merge into the infinite ocean of the Sahasrāra."]},{"number":105,"name":"सहस्राराम्बुजारूढा","samasa":["• सहस्रसङ्ख्यका अरा यस्य तद् अम्बुजं आरूढा।"],"wordByWord":["सहस्रसङ्ख्यका — numbered as one thousand","अरा — spokes; petals","अम्बुजं — lotus","आरूढा — ascended; mounted","सहस्राराम्बुजारूढा — She who has ascended the thousand-petalled lotus"],"summary":["सहस्राराम्बुजारूढा means one who ascends to the thousand-petalled lotus below the skull. Kuṇḍalinī is made to reach this place from Mūlādhāra after crossing all the cakras and piercing the knots. This is the place of Sadāśiva. Of the sixteen phases of the moon, fifteen wax and wane, while one is permanent; this permanent sixteenth phase is connected with this place. Sadāśiva's function of grace arises here. The thousand petals may also be understood as countless or infinite. Śrīdevī is contemplated here seated on the lap of Kāmeśvara with innumerable divine powers."],"searchText":"105 सहस्राराम्बुजारूढा • सहस्रसङ्ख्यका अरा यस्य तद् अम्बुजं आरूढा। सहस्रसङ्ख्यका — numbered as one thousand अरा — spokes; petals अम्बुजं — lotus आरूढा — ascended; mounted सहस्राराम्बुजारूढा — she who has ascended the thousand-petalled lotus सहस्राराम्बुजारूढा means one who ascends to the thousand-petalled lotus below the skull. kuṇḍalinī is made to reach this place from mūlādhāra after crossing all the cakras and piercing the knots. this is the place of sadāśiva. of the sixteen phases of the moon, fifteen wax and wane, while one is permanent; this permanent sixteenth phase is connected with this place. sadāśiva's function of grace arises here. the thousand petals may also be understood as countless or infinite. śrīdevī is contemplated here seated on the lap of kāmeśvara with innumerable divine powers. the summit of non-dual union: this marks the completion of the internal ascent. the sahasrāra is the thousand-petaled lotus at the crown of the head. when the kuṇḍalinī mounts (ārūḍhā) this summit, she unites with paramaśiva in absolute, unbroken stillness. this is the state of final liberation (mokṣa), where all dualistic concepts of space, time, and individuality vanish into pure bliss.","esoteric":["The Summit of Non-Dual Union: This marks the completion of the internal ascent. The Sahasrāra is the thousand-petaled lotus at the crown of the head. When the Kuṇḍalinī mounts (ārūḍhā) this summit, She unites with Paramaśiva in absolute, unbroken stillness. This is the state of final liberation (mokṣa), where all dualistic concepts of space, time, and individuality vanish into pure bliss."]},{"number":106,"name":"सुधासाराभिवर्षिणी","samasa":["• सुधायाः आसार अभिवर्षितुं शीलम् अस्या इति।"],"wordByWord":["सुधायाः — of nectar","आसार — shower; stream","अभिवर्षितुं — to shower","शीलम् — nature; habit","सुधासाराभिवर्षिणी — She who showers streams of nectar"],"summary":["सुधासाराभिवर्षिणी means one who showers the stream of nectar through all the nāḍīs from the candra-maṇḍala. Reaching this nectar-flow and enjoying indescribable bliss is the purpose of this upāsanā. When Kuṇḍalinī reaches the higher centre, nectar flows down and bathes the subtle channels of the body. This nectar is the cooling and blissful current associated with Śrīdevī's grace. Some traditions read the name as Sudhādhārābhivarṣiṇī, one who rains streams of nectar."],"searchText":"106 सुधासाराभिवर्षिणी • सुधायाः आसार अभिवर्षितुं शीलम् अस्या इति। सुधायाः — of nectar आसार — shower; stream अभिवर्षितुं — to shower शीलम् — nature; habit सुधासाराभिवर्षिणी — she who showers streams of nectar सुधासाराभिवर्षिणी means one who showers the stream of nectar through all the nāḍīs from the candra-maṇḍala. reaching this nectar-flow and enjoying indescribable bliss is the purpose of this upāsanā. when kuṇḍalinī reaches the higher centre, nectar flows down and bathes the subtle channels of the body. this nectar is the cooling and blissful current associated with śrīdevī's grace. some traditions read the name as sudhādhārābhivarṣiṇī, one who rains streams of nectar. the downpour of cosmic ecstasy: following the union at the crown, a cool, ecstatic nectar (sudhā) is released. she is abhivarṣiṇī because she showers this nectar down through the entire system of nerve channels (nāḍīs), rejuvenating every single cell and psychic layer of the practitioner with non-dual bliss.","esoteric":["The Downpour of Cosmic Ecstasy: Following the union at the crown, a cool, ecstatic nectar (sudhā) is released. She is Abhivarṣiṇī because She showers this nectar down through the entire system of nerve channels (nāḍīs), rejuvenating every single cell and psychic layer of the practitioner with non-dual bliss."]},{"number":107,"name":"तडिल्लतासमरुचिः","samasa":["• तडित् एव लता। तया समा रुचिः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["तडित् — lightning","लता — creeper","समा — equal; similar","रुचिः — lustre","तडिल्लतासमरुचिः — She whose lustre is like a lightning-creeper"],"summary":["तडिल्लतासमरुचिः means one who shines like a streak of lightning. The name is also read in some traditions as Taṭillatāsamaruci. The meaning remains that Śrīdevī glitters with the brilliance of lightning. Her radiance is sudden, bright and powerful, like a flash that illumines everything at once."],"searchText":"107 तडिल्लतासमरुचिः • तडित् एव लता। तया समा रुचिः यस्याः सा। तडित् — lightning लता — creeper समा — equal; similar रुचिः — lustre तडिल्लतासमरुचिः — she whose lustre is like a lightning-creeper तडिल्लतासमरुचिः means one who shines like a streak of lightning. the name is also read in some traditions as taṭillatāsamaruci. the meaning remains that śrīdevī glitters with the brilliance of lightning. her radiance is sudden, bright and powerful, like a flash that illumines everything at once. the flash of illumination: lightning flashes with intense, blinding brightness, piercing through pitch darkness in a fraction of a second. her luster is compared to lightning because the final dawning of self-knowledge (jñānodayā) does not happen slowly; it strikes the intellect instantly, completely burning away the long darkness of cosmic ignorance (avidyā) in a single flash of realization.","esoteric":["The Flash of Illumination: Lightning flashes with intense, blinding brightness, piercing through pitch darkness in a fraction of a second. Her luster is compared to lightning because the final dawning of self-knowledge (Jñānodayā) does not happen slowly; it strikes the intellect instantly, completely burning away the long darkness of cosmic ignorance (Avidyā) in a single flash of realization."]},{"number":108,"name":"षट्चक्रोपरिसंस्थिता","samasa":["• षडव्यवकानि चक्राणि। तेषां उपरि सम्यक् स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["चक्राणि — chakras; centres","उपरि — above","स्थिता — situated","षट्चक्रोपरिसंस्थिता — She who is established above the six chakras"],"summary":["षट्चक्रोपरिसंस्थिता means one who is established above the six cakras. The six cakras are Mūlādhāra, Svādhiṣṭhāna, Maṇipūra, Anāhata, Viśuddhi and Ājñā. Śrīdevī, as Kuṇḍalinī, rises through these centres and is established beyond them in the higher state. Having passed through the six cakras and their knots, She stands above their range."],"searchText":"108 षट्चक्रोपरिसंस्थिता • षडव्यवकानि चक्राणि। तेषां उपरि सम्यक् स्थिता। चक्राणि — chakras; centres उपरि — above स्थिता — situated षट्चक्रोपरिसंस्थिता — she who is established above the six chakras षट्चक्रोपरिसंस्थिता means one who is established above the six cakras. the six cakras are mūlādhāra, svādhiṣṭhāna, maṇipūra, anāhata, viśuddhi and ājñā. śrīdevī, as kuṇḍalinī, rises through these centres and is established beyond them in the higher state. having passed through the six cakras and their knots, she stands above their range. transcending the chakras: the ṣaṭ-cakra represents the physical and psychic architecture of human experience. while she animates these six centers, her ultimate, true home is above them (upari), in the sahasrāra. this establishes that the absolute nature of consciousness is transcendent—she supports the lower modes of life but remains unaffected by them.","esoteric":["Transcending the Chakras: The Ṣaṭ-cakra represents the physical and psychic architecture of human experience. While She animates these six centers, Her ultimate, true home is above them (upari), in the Sahasrāra. This establishes that the absolute nature of consciousness is transcendent—She supports the lower modes of life but remains unaffected by them."]},{"number":109,"name":"महासक्तिः","samasa":["• महे आसक्तिः यस्या सा।","• महती आ समन्तात् सक्तिः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महे — in the great; in festival/splendour","आसक्तिः — attachment; fondness","महती — great","सक्तिः — attachment; joinedness","महासक्तिः — She of great attachment or great power"],"summary":["महासक्तिः means one who has great delight or intense attachment. The word mahā can mean festival or splendour, and āsakti means immense joy or attachment. She is fond of the great festival of the union of Śiva and Śakti. She is also deeply pleased by worship performed as a festival. Mahat means vast, expanding in all directions; Her greatness spreads everywhere. Her union is present in all places and is visible even in an atom."],"searchText":"109 महासक्तिः • महे आसक्तिः यस्या सा। • महती आ समन्तात् सक्तिः यस्याः सा। महे — in the great; in festival/splendour आसक्तिः — attachment; fondness महती — great सक्तिः — attachment; joinedness महासक्तिः — she of great attachment or great power महासक्तिः means one who has great delight or intense attachment. the word mahā can mean festival or splendour, and āsakti means immense joy or attachment. she is fond of the great festival of the union of śiva and śakti. she is also deeply pleased by worship performed as a festival. mahat means vast, expanding in all directions; her greatness spreads everywhere. her union is present in all places and is visible even in an atom. on the transcendent plane, she holds an unbreakable attachment (mahā-āsakti) to śiva, ensuring their eternal union. on the manifest plane, her attachment takes the form of infinite, all-encompassing compassion (karuṇā) that acts like a magnetic pull, drawing every individual soul back toward the source of liberation.","esoteric":["On the transcendent plane, She holds an unbreakable attachment (Mahā-āsakti) to Śiva, ensuring their eternal union. On the manifest plane, Her attachment takes the form of infinite, all-encompassing compassion (Karuṇā) that acts like a magnetic pull, drawing every individual soul back toward the source of liberation."]},{"number":110,"name":"कुण्डलिनी","samasa":["• कुण्डले अस्याः स्त इति ।"],"wordByWord":["कुण्डले — coils; rings","कुण्डलिनी — She who is Kuṇḍalinī"],"summary":["कुण्डलिनी means one who is in the form of Kuṇḍalinī energy. She is like a serpent coiled three and a half times. The three full coils represent the letters A, U and M, and the half coil represents the half-mātrā; thus Kuṇḍalinī corresponds to Oṃ, the praṇava-mantra. She breathes like a serpent sleeping in Mūlādhāra, and this breath of Kuṇḍalinī, the energy of the soul, is prāṇa. The sound of this breath can be heard by closing the ears completely. The sleeping Kuṇḍalinī is awakened and led to brahmarandhra through ardent devotion, the fruits of worship, the blessings of the teacher, and yogic methods. When She reaches brahmarandhra, She rains nectar through the nāḍīs. The Vāgbhava-bīja is also called Kuṇḍalinī, so She may also be understood as that bīja."],"searchText":"110 कुण्डलिनी • कुण्डले अस्याः स्त इति । कुण्डले — coils; rings कुण्डलिनी — she who is kuṇḍalinī कुण्डलिनी means one who is in the form of kuṇḍalinī energy. she is like a serpent coiled three and a half times. the three full coils represent the letters a, u and m, and the half coil represents the half-mātrā; thus kuṇḍalinī corresponds to oṃ, the praṇava-mantra. she breathes like a serpent sleeping in mūlādhāra, and this breath of kuṇḍalinī, the energy of the soul, is prāṇa. the sound of this breath can be heard by closing the ears completely. the sleeping kuṇḍalinī is awakened and led to brahmarandhra through ardent devotion, the fruits of worship, the blessings of the teacher, and yogic methods. when she reaches brahmarandhra, she rains nectar through the nāḍīs. the vāgbhava-bīja is also called kuṇḍalinī, so she may also be understood as that bīja. the coiled power of evolution: this is the direct, structural title of the evolutionary force within the human body. as the kuṇḍalinī, she rests at the base center, coiled three and a half times like a snake. this coiled state represents potential energy. when awakened through systematic yoga and discrimination, this potential energy unfolds, straightening its path through the central channel to guide the practitioner toward non-dual liberation.","esoteric":["The Coiled Power of Evolution: This is the direct, structural title of the evolutionary force within the human body. As the Kuṇḍalinī, She rests at the base center, coiled three and a half times like a snake. This coiled state represents potential energy. When awakened through systematic yoga and discrimination, this potential energy unfolds, straightening its path through the central channel to guide the practitioner toward non-dual liberation."]},{"number":111,"name":"बिसतन्तुतनीयसी","samasa":["• बिसमेव तन्तुः तद्वत् तनीयसी।"],"wordByWord":["तन्तुः — fibre; thread","तनीयसी — very subtle; thinner","बिसतन्तुतनीयसी — She who is subtler than the fibre of a lotus stalk"],"summary":["बिसतन्तुतनीयसी means one who is as fine as the fibre of a lotus stalk. From Kulāmṛtaikarasikā onward, the subtle Kuṇḍalinī form of Śrīdevī is described. She is extremely subtle, like the delicate fibre inside a lotus stem. As Kuṇḍalinī, She rises from Mūlādhāra, pierces the inner knots, reaches brahmarandhra and causes nectar to flow through the nāḍīs. This subtle movement is connected with Śrīcakra-vidyā and with the awakening of inner knowledge. Those who adore Śrīdevī with control of the organs and inner worship can reach this stage. She is the subtle power by which nectar flows, knowledge is sustained, and liberation of body, soul and universe is sought."],"searchText":"111 बिसतन्तुतनीयसी • बिसमेव तन्तुः तद्वत् तनीयसी। तन्तुः — fibre; thread तनीयसी — very subtle; thinner बिसतन्तुतनीयसी — she who is subtler than the fibre of a lotus stalk बिसतन्तुतनीयसी means one who is as fine as the fibre of a lotus stalk. from kulāmṛtaikarasikā onward, the subtle kuṇḍalinī form of śrīdevī is described. she is extremely subtle, like the delicate fibre inside a lotus stem. as kuṇḍalinī, she rises from mūlādhāra, pierces the inner knots, reaches brahmarandhra and causes nectar to flow through the nāḍīs. this subtle movement is connected with śrīcakra-vidyā and with the awakening of inner knowledge. those who adore śrīdevī with control of the organs and inner worship can reach this stage. she is the subtle power by which nectar flows, knowledge is sustained, and liberation of body, soul and universe is sought. the infinite subtlety of awareness: the fiber inside a lotus stalk (bisa-tantu) is nearly invisible to the naked eye, yet it runs unbroken through the entire length of the stem. this represents the ultimate subtlety (sūkṣmatva) of the awakened kuṇḍalinī as she enters the central channel. consciousness is not a gross physical object; it is the finest, most microscopic thread of awareness that permeates the entire physical structure, completely uncatchable by the gross senses yet holding the entire network together.","esoteric":["The Infinite Subtlety of Awareness: the fiber inside a lotus stalk (bisa-tantu) is nearly invisible to the naked eye, yet it runs unbroken through the entire length of the stem. This represents the ultimate subtlety (sūkṣmatva) of the awakened Kuṇḍalinī as She enters the central channel. Consciousness is not a gross physical object; it is the finest, most microscopic thread of awareness that permeates the entire physical structure, completely uncatchable by the gross senses yet holding the entire network together."]},{"number":112,"name":"भवानी","samasa":["• भवस्य पत्नी।","• भवं (संसारं कामं वा) आनयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["भवस्य — of Bhava; of Shiva","पत्नी — wife","भवं — existence; worldly becoming","संसारं — worldly existence","कामं — desire","भवानी — She who is the consort of Bhava and who brings forth becoming"],"summary":["भवानी means one who gives life to bhava. The word bhava has three meanings: Lord Mahādeva, the cycle of human existence, and Kāma. She gives life to all three and is therefore Bhavānī. Since Lord Paramaśiva creates living beings, He is called Bhava, and His consort is Bhavānī. Among the eight forms of Paramaśiva, water is called Bhava, and She is the life-giving consort of that form. Bhavānī is also the name of Śrīdevī in the sacred place called Sthāneśvara. The name also suggests Her grace: when a devotee begins to call Her Bhavānī, She accepts the prayer as the wish to become one with Her and grants the rare state of union."],"searchText":"112 भवानी • भवस्य पत्नी। • भवं (संसारं कामं वा) आनयतीति। भवस्य — of bhava; of shiva पत्नी — wife भवं — existence; worldly becoming संसारं — worldly existence कामं — desire भवानी — she who is the consort of bhava and who brings forth becoming भवानी means one who gives life to bhava. the word bhava has three meanings: lord mahādeva, the cycle of human existence, and kāma. she gives life to all three and is therefore bhavānī. since lord paramaśiva creates living beings, he is called bhava, and his consort is bhavānī. among the eight forms of paramaśiva, water is called bhava, and she is the life-giving consort of that form. bhavānī is also the name of śrīdevī in the sacred place called sthāneśvara. the name also suggests her grace: when a devotee begins to call her bhavānī, she accepts the prayer as the wish to become one with her and grants the rare state of union. the quickener of existence: bhava means existence or the manifest universe. śiva in his absolute state remains unmoving, like a silent corpse (śava). she is bhavānī because she infuses life, movement, and reality into him, transforming him into bhava (the living lord of existence). as the root statement of the śāktaagamas goes: \"without her, he cannot even stir.\" she is the grand animator who brings the world into active being.","esoteric":["The Quickener of Existence: Bhava means existence or the manifest universe. Śiva in His absolute state remains unmoving, like a silent corpse (Śava). She is Bhavānī because She infuses life, movement, and reality into Him, transforming Him into Bhava (the living lord of existence). As the root statement of the ŚāktaAgamas goes: \"Without Her, He cannot even stir.\" She is the grand animator who brings the world into active being."]},{"number":113,"name":"भावनागम्या","samasa":["•  भावनया अगम्या।"],"wordByWord":["भावनया — by contemplation","अगम्या — reachable; knowable","भावनागम्या — She who is reached by contemplation"],"summary":["भावनागम्या means one who can be realised through devoted meditation. The forms of Śrīdevī having been described, the means of reaching Her are now indicated. Bhāvanā means sustained contemplation. As one thinks constantly, so one becomes; the example is a worm transformed by intense fixation. Meditation is of two kinds: meditation on sound and meditation on meaning. Meditation on sound worships sacred words and mantras as taught by the teacher. Meditation on meaning leads inward toward the reality indicated by those sounds. The name can also be interpreted in two ways: She is unreachable by ordinary becoming, or She is reachable through bhāvanā. Meditation with form is saguṇa-upāsanā; when it matures into meditation on meaning, it becomes nirguṇa-upāsanā. She is also attainable through the purified mind gained by righteous action."],"searchText":"113 भावनागम्या •  भावनया अगम्या। भावनया — by contemplation अगम्या — reachable; knowable भावनागम्या — she who is reached by contemplation भावनागम्या means one who can be realised through devoted meditation. the forms of śrīdevī having been described, the means of reaching her are now indicated. bhāvanā means sustained contemplation. as one thinks constantly, so one becomes; the example is a worm transformed by intense fixation. meditation is of two kinds: meditation on sound and meditation on meaning. meditation on sound worships sacred words and mantras as taught by the teacher. meditation on meaning leads inward toward the reality indicated by those sounds. the name can also be interpreted in two ways: she is unreachable by ordinary becoming, or she is reachable through bhāvanā. meditation with form is saguṇa-upāsanā; when it matures into meditation on meaning, it becomes nirguṇa-upāsanā. she is also attainable through the purified mind gained by righteous action. realization beyond the intellect: bhāvanā is not dry intellectual logic or physical ritualism; it is the steady, concentrated habituation of the mind to the non-dual truth (\"i am the absolute\"). she is completely inaccessible (agamyā) to physical eyes or external arguments. she becomes gamyā (attainable) only when the seeker's mind undergoes total internal transformation, dissolving objective thoughts into steady, loving meditation on the self.","esoteric":["Realization Beyond the Intellect: Bhāvanā is not dry intellectual logic or physical ritualism; it is the steady, concentrated habituation of the mind to the non-dual truth (\"I am the Absolute\"). She is completely inaccessible (agamyā) to physical eyes or external arguments. She becomes gamyā (attainable) only when the seeker's mind undergoes total internal transformation, dissolving objective thoughts into steady, loving meditation on the Self."]},{"number":114,"name":"भवारण्यकुठारिका","samasa":["• भवः एव आरण्यः। तस्य कुठारेव कुठारिका।"],"wordByWord":["भवः — worldly existence","आरण्यः — forest","कुठारिका — small axe","भवारण्यकुठारिका — She who is the axe to the forest of worldly existence"],"summary":["भवारण्यकुठारिका means one who is like an axe cutting down the forest of saṃsāra. The forest is dense with trees that grow again and again; similarly the cycle of worldly existence causes repeated birth through cravings for external objects. A forest is destroyed only when its trees are cut. In the same way, the forest of saṃsāra is destroyed only when desires for worldly objects are cut down. Śrīdevī is the axe that cuts these trees of bondage. When knowledge of Śrīdevī arises, attachment to worldly existence is severed."],"searchText":"114 भवारण्यकुठारिका • भवः एव आरण्यः। तस्य कुठारेव कुठारिका। भवः — worldly existence आरण्यः — forest कुठारिका — small axe भवारण्यकुठारिका — she who is the axe to the forest of worldly existence भवारण्यकुठारिका means one who is like an axe cutting down the forest of saṃsāra. the forest is dense with trees that grow again and again; similarly the cycle of worldly existence causes repeated birth through cravings for external objects. a forest is destroyed only when its trees are cut. in the same way, the forest of saṃsāra is destroyed only when desires for worldly objects are cut down. śrīdevī is the axe that cuts these trees of bondage. when knowledge of śrīdevī arises, attachment to worldly existence is severed. clearing the forest of bondage: the world of endless births and deaths (saṃsāra) is compared to a wild, tangled forest (bhava-āraṇya) because it is dark, full of hidden dangers (desires, delusions), and highly difficult to escape. she is the kuṭhārikā (the axe) because the dawn of her grace provides the exact intellectual sharpness needed to completely cut down the root of this ignorance, clearing the path to instant liberation.","esoteric":["Clearing the Forest of Bondage: The world of endless births and deaths (Saṃsāra) is compared to a wild, tangled forest (bhava-āraṇya) because it is dark, full of hidden dangers (desires, delusions), and highly difficult to escape. She is the kuṭhārikā (the axe) because the dawn of Her grace provides the exact intellectual sharpness needed to completely cut down the root of this ignorance, clearing the path to instant liberation."]},{"number":115,"name":"भद्रप्रिया","samasa":["• भद्रं प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["भद्रं — auspiciousness; good","प्रियं — dear","भद्रप्रिया — She who loves auspiciousness"],"summary":["भद्रप्रिया means one who is fond of everything auspicious. She delights in auspiciousness and is especially fond of granting auspicious things to Her devotees. The word bhadra also denotes a kind of elephant, and the name may also indicate Her affection for that noble species. Thus She is Bhadrāpriyā, the one who loves what is auspicious and gives auspiciousness."],"searchText":"115 भद्रप्रिया • भद्रं प्रियं यस्याः सा। भद्रं — auspiciousness; good प्रियं — dear भद्रप्रिया — she who loves auspiciousness भद्रप्रिया means one who is fond of everything auspicious. she delights in auspiciousness and is especially fond of granting auspicious things to her devotees. the word bhadra also denotes a kind of elephant, and the name may also indicate her affection for that noble species. thus she is bhadrāpriyā, the one who loves what is auspicious and gives auspiciousness. the affection for true welfare: bhadram in the vedas refers to the highest spiritual welfare and goodness. she is bhadrapriyā because she takes delight in the genuine well-being, virtue, and non-dual evolution of her devotees. she actively guides seekers away from harmful attachments, replacing them with the ultimate auspiciousness of a peaceful mind.","esoteric":["The Affection for True Welfare: Bhadram in the Vedas refers to the highest spiritual welfare and goodness. She is Bhadrapriyā because She takes delight in the genuine well-being, virtue, and non-dual evolution of Her devotees. She actively guides seekers away from harmful attachments, replacing them with the ultimate auspiciousness of a peaceful mind."]},{"number":116,"name":"भद्रमूर्तिः","samasa":["• भद्रा मूर्तिः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["भद्रा — auspicious","मूर्तिः — form","भद्रमूर्तिः — She whose form is auspicious"],"summary":["भद्रमूर्तिः means one who has an auspicious form. Brahman alone is truly auspicious, and Śrīdevī is of that auspicious nature. Maṅgala means felicity, the means to felicity, and that which instructs or brings it. She is beyond ordinary auspiciousness and is the auspiciousness of all auspicious things. Therefore Her very form is bhadra, sacred, blessed and beneficial."],"searchText":"116 भद्रमूर्तिः • भद्रा मूर्तिः यस्याः सा। भद्रा — auspicious मूर्तिः — form भद्रमूर्तिः — she whose form is auspicious भद्रमूर्तिः means one who has an auspicious form. brahman alone is truly auspicious, and śrīdevī is of that auspicious nature. maṅgala means felicity, the means to felicity, and that which instructs or brings it. she is beyond ordinary auspiciousness and is the auspiciousness of all auspicious things. therefore her very form is bhadra, sacred, blessed and beneficial. the embodiment of universal good: unlike worldly forms that contain mixtures of structural flaws or dualistic imperfections, her mūrti (whether manifest as the text, the mantra, the geometry, or the physical icon) is a pure, unadulterated field of auspicious energy. goring her form with focus releases nothing but harmony, working as a clearing agent that aligns the practitioner's body and mind with universal truth.","esoteric":["The Embodiment of Universal Good: Unlike worldly forms that contain mixtures of structural flaws or dualistic imperfections, Her mūrti (whether manifest as the text, the mantra, the geometry, or the physical icon) is a pure, unadulterated field of auspicious energy. Goring Her form with focus releases nothing but harmony, working as a clearing agent that aligns the practitioner's body and mind with universal truth."]},{"number":117,"name":"भक्तसौभाग्यदायिनी","samasa":["• भगः शोभना यस्यां तस्याः भावः सुष्ठु भाग्यं यस्य तस्य भावो वा सौभाग्यम्। भक्तेभ्यः सौभाग्यानि ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तेभ्यः — to devotees","सौभाग्यानि — good fortunes","भक्तसौभाग्यदायिनी — She who gives good fortune to devotees"],"summary":["भक्तसौभाग्यदायिनी means one who grants all-round prosperity and good fortune to Her devotees. Bhaga includes wealth, desire, praise, vigour, preparation, illumination, dignity and related forms of excellence. Since She possesses these, Her nature is saubhāgya, prosperity and blessedness. Saubhāgya also means exemplary fortune. One who contemplates these excellences receives saubhāgya from Her. The eight auspicious things used on holy occasions, such as sugarcane, peepul, sprouted cumin, coriander, cow's milk and its products, yellow objects, flowers and salt, are called saubhāgyāṣṭaka. She gives such auspiciousness and prosperity to Her devotees. Bhaga also means complete wealth, charity, glory, richness, relinquishment and liberation from bondage; She grants these to those devoted to Her."],"searchText":"117 भक्तसौभाग्यदायिनी • भगः शोभना यस्यां तस्याः भावः सुष्ठु भाग्यं यस्य तस्य भावो वा सौभाग्यम्। भक्तेभ्यः सौभाग्यानि ददातीति। भक्तेभ्यः — to devotees सौभाग्यानि — good fortunes भक्तसौभाग्यदायिनी — she who gives good fortune to devotees भक्तसौभाग्यदायिनी means one who grants all-round prosperity and good fortune to her devotees. bhaga includes wealth, desire, praise, vigour, preparation, illumination, dignity and related forms of excellence. since she possesses these, her nature is saubhāgya, prosperity and blessedness. saubhāgya also means exemplary fortune. one who contemplates these excellences receives saubhāgya from her. the eight auspicious things used on holy occasions, such as sugarcane, peepul, sprouted cumin, coriander, cow's milk and its products, yellow objects, flowers and salt, are called saubhāgyāṣṭaka. she gives such auspiciousness and prosperity to her devotees. bhaga also means complete wealth, charity, glory, richness, relinquishment and liberation from bondage; she grants these to those devoted to her. the giver of the ultimate fortune: in the exoteric world, saubhāgya refers to material wealth, happy relationships, and good luck. true saubhāgya is the dawning of the śrī vidyāknowledge and the active awakening of the inner kuṇḍalinī. she is the giver of this fortune because she transforms the dry life of a seeker into a rich, nectarine experience of self-realization, which is the ultimate prosperity.","esoteric":["The Giver of the Ultimate Fortune: In the exoteric world, saubhāgya refers to material wealth, happy relationships, and good luck. true saubhāgya is the dawning of the Śrī Vidyāknowledge and the active awakening of the inner Kuṇḍalinī. She is the giver of this fortune because She transforms the dry life of a seeker into a rich, nectarine experience of self-realization, which is the ultimate prosperity."]},{"number":118,"name":"भक्तिप्रिया","samasa":["• भक्तिः प्रिया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तिः — devotion","प्रिया — dear","भक्तिप्रिया — She who loves devotion"],"summary":["भक्तिप्रिया means one who is fond of devotion. Śrīdevī loves worship performed with devotion. Worship is of two kinds, primary and secondary. Primary devotion is a mental state of longing directed toward Īśvara, free from pride and selfishness, leaving no room in the mind for any other thought and forgetting the limited self. By reaching such devotion, one becomes fulfilled, immortal and content. One no longer desires, regrets, hates, longs for external pleasures, or clings to worldly interests. Devotion is like a seed returning to its parent tree, a needle reaching a magnet, a faithful wife reaching her husband, a creeper reaching a support, or a river reaching the ocean. The mind naturally reaching the Lord is devotion. Devotion is the chief means for knowledge and liberation, and uninterrupted contemplation of Brahman as one's own Self is also called devotion."],"searchText":"118 भक्तिप्रिया • भक्तिः प्रिया यस्याः सा। भक्तिः — devotion प्रिया — dear भक्तिप्रिया — she who loves devotion भक्तिप्रिया means one who is fond of devotion. śrīdevī loves worship performed with devotion. worship is of two kinds, primary and secondary. primary devotion is a mental state of longing directed toward īśvara, free from pride and selfishness, leaving no room in the mind for any other thought and forgetting the limited self. by reaching such devotion, one becomes fulfilled, immortal and content. one no longer desires, regrets, hates, longs for external pleasures, or clings to worldly interests. devotion is like a seed returning to its parent tree, a needle reaching a magnet, a faithful wife reaching her husband, a creeper reaching a support, or a river reaching the ocean. the mind naturally reaching the lord is devotion. devotion is the chief means for knowledge and liberation, and uninterrupted contemplation of brahman as one's own self is also called devotion. the reciprocity of love: she cannot be bought with rich gifts, elaborate external displays, or dry intellectual scholarship. the singular currency that catches her attention is bhakti—the complete, open-hearted surrender of the ego. she holds this dear because bhakti naturally thins out the walls of individual separation, allowing her non-dual presence to flood the seeker's heart instantly.","esoteric":["The Reciprocity of Love: She cannot be bought with rich gifts, elaborate external displays, or dry intellectual scholarship. The singular currency that catches Her attention is Bhakti—the complete, open-hearted surrender of the ego. She holds this dear because Bhakti naturally thins out the walls of individual separation, allowing Her non-dual presence to flood the seeker's heart instantly."]},{"number":119,"name":"भक्तिगम्या","samasa":["• भक्त्या गम्या।"],"wordByWord":["भक्त्या — by devotion","गम्या — reachable","भक्तिगम्या — She who is reached through devotion"],"summary":["भक्तिगम्या means one who is reached through devotion. Three meanings are possible: through true devotion She becomes present, She is attained, and She is recognised. The senses naturally turn outward, so ordinary people see external objects rather than the inner Self; the wise turn inward, seeking immortality, and behold the inner Self. Even though Brahman is not ordinarily perceivable, it can be comprehended through devotion and meditation. Gamya here means that She can be reached. To abide in Brahman is immortality, and such abiding is devotion. Devotion also reveals Her through Her characteristics: though She is subtle and not directly visible, Her form is recognised through truth, knowledge and the signs of the inner Self."],"searchText":"119 भक्तिगम्या • भक्त्या गम्या। भक्त्या — by devotion गम्या — reachable भक्तिगम्या — she who is reached through devotion भक्तिगम्या means one who is reached through devotion. three meanings are possible: through true devotion she becomes present, she is attained, and she is recognised. the senses naturally turn outward, so ordinary people see external objects rather than the inner self; the wise turn inward, seeking immortality, and behold the inner self. even though brahman is not ordinarily perceivable, it can be comprehended through devotion and meditation. gamya here means that she can be reached. to abide in brahman is immortality, and such abiding is devotion. devotion also reveals her through her characteristics: though she is subtle and not directly visible, her form is recognised through truth, knowledge and the signs of the inner self. the portal of devotion: intellectual analysis can map out the structural parameters of the mind, but it cannot touch the living essence of the absolute. she is bhaktigamyā because bhakti acts as the direct shortcut that bypasses the doubts and limits of the logical intellect, opening a clear, intuitive path straight into the heart of reality.","esoteric":["The Portal of Devotion: Intellectual analysis can map out the structural parameters of the mind, but it cannot touch the living essence of the Absolute. She is Bhaktigamyā because Bhakti acts as the direct shortcut that bypasses the doubts and limits of the logical intellect, opening a clear, intuitive path straight into the heart of reality."]},{"number":120,"name":"भक्तिवश्या","samasa":["• भक्त्या वश्या।","• भक्तेः वश्या (पराधीना)।"],"wordByWord":["भक्त्या — by devotion","वश्या — subdued; brought under control","पराधीना — dependent; subject to","भक्तिवश्या — She who is brought under control by devotion"],"summary":["भक्तिवश्या means one who can be won over through true devotion. The statement that God yields to devotion is illustrated by devotees such as Kaṇṇappa Nāyaṉār, Dhruva, Gajendra, Prahlāda, Śabarī and Kuchela. Without devotion, even Kāma, approaching Parameśvara with an inimical mind and shooting a flower-arrow, was burned to ashes. With devotion, however, the Lord blesses devotees without dwelling on their defects. True devotion alone pleases the divine, not merely birth, learning, strength, wealth, appearance or status. Therefore Śrīdevī becomes subject to the loving devotion of Her devotees and protects those who take refuge in Her."],"searchText":"120 भक्तिवश्या • भक्त्या वश्या। • भक्तेः वश्या (पराधीना)। भक्त्या — by devotion वश्या — subdued; brought under control पराधीना — dependent; subject to भक्तिवश्या — she who is brought under control by devotion भक्तिवश्या means one who can be won over through true devotion. the statement that god yields to devotion is illustrated by devotees such as kaṇṇappa nāyaṉār, dhruva, gajendra, prahlāda, śabarī and kuchela. without devotion, even kāma, approaching parameśvara with an inimical mind and shooting a flower-arrow, was burned to ashes. with devotion, however, the lord blesses devotees without dwelling on their defects. true devotion alone pleases the divine, not merely birth, learning, strength, wealth, appearance or status. therefore śrīdevī becomes subject to the loving devotion of her devotees and protects those who take refuge in her. the complete captivity by love: this name contains a stunning theological declaration: the supreme, omnipotent ruler of infinite universes, who is completely independent (svātantrya-śakti), willingly surrenders her autonomy and becomes parādhīnā (dependent) before the unselfish love of a true bhakta. the intensity of devotion dissolves the distance between the worshiper and the worshiped, making her completely one with the seeker's inner voice.","esoteric":["The Complete Captivity by Love: This name contains a stunning theological declaration: the supreme, omnipotent ruler of infinite universes, who is completely independent (Svātantrya-śakti), willingly surrenders Her autonomy and becomes parādhīnā (dependent) before the unselfish love of a true bhakta. The intensity of devotion dissolves the distance between the worshiper and the worshiped, making Her completely one with the seeker's inner voice."]},{"number":121,"name":"भयापहा","samasa":["• भयानि अपहन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["भयानि — fears","भयापहा — She who removes fear"],"summary":["भयापहा means one who removes all fear. She dispels every fear, including fear from water, earth, wilderness, danger, enemies and distress. One who reaches eternal bliss knows no fear. The very remembrance of Śrīdevī removes fear in frightening situations. Her names and deeds give courage in battle, forest, fire, flood, danger from thieves, enemies, rulers, weapons and suffering. Since there is nothing apart from Śrīdevī, true knowledge of Her removes the root of fear. She grants the knowledge of Brahman, the understanding that all is one and there is no second. Thus She removes the fear of saṃsāra, birth and death."],"searchText":"121 भयापहा • भयानि अपहन्तीति। भयानि — fears भयापहा — she who removes fear भयापहा means one who removes all fear. she dispels every fear, including fear from water, earth, wilderness, danger, enemies and distress. one who reaches eternal bliss knows no fear. the very remembrance of śrīdevī removes fear in frightening situations. her names and deeds give courage in battle, forest, fire, flood, danger from thieves, enemies, rulers, weapons and suffering. since there is nothing apart from śrīdevī, true knowledge of her removes the root of fear. she grants the knowledge of brahman, the understanding that all is one and there is no second. thus she removes the fear of saṃsāra, birth and death. the destruction of dualistic fear: as the upaniṣads explicitly declare: \"verily, fear arises only when there is a second entity\" (dvitīyād vai bhayaṃ bhavati). fear is a natural consequence of duality—the fear of loss, death, or judgment by another. she is bhayāpahā because she dissolves the very illusion of a \"second entity.\" by revealing that the entire universe is her own self-projection, she establishes the practitioner in the fearless, non-dual state of absolute safety.","esoteric":["The Destruction of Dualistic Fear: As the Upaniṣads explicitly declare: \"Verily, fear arises only when there is a second entity\" (Dvitīyād vai bhayaṃ bhavati). Fear is a natural consequence of duality—the fear of loss, death, or judgment by another. She is Bhayāpahā because She dissolves the very illusion of a \"second entity.\" By revealing that the entire universe is Her own self-projection, She establishes the practitioner in the fearless, non-dual state of absolute safety."]},{"number":122,"name":"शांभवी","samasa":["• शम्भोः इयं (पत्नी)।","• शाम्भवानां इयं (माता)।"],"wordByWord":["शम्भोः — of Shambhu; Shiva","पत्नी — wife","शाम्भवानां — of the followers/children of Shambhu","शांभवी — She who belongs to Shambhu"],"summary":["शांभवी means She who belongs to Śambhu. She is the consort and power of Śambhu, Lord Śiva, and is inseparable from Him. As Śāmbhavī, She is the auspicious Śakti connected with Śambhu and shares His nature."],"searchText":"122 शांभवी • शम्भोः इयं (पत्नी)। • शाम्भवानां इयं (माता)। शम्भोः — of shambhu; shiva पत्नी — wife शाम्भवानां — of the followers/children of shambhu शांभवी — she who belongs to shambhu शांभवी means she who belongs to śambhu. she is the consort and power of śambhu, lord śiva, and is inseparable from him. as śāmbhavī, she is the auspicious śakti connected with śambhu and shares his nature. the mudrā of silent awareness: beyond being the consort of śiva, śāmbhavī denotes the highest state of internal yoga—the शाम्भवी मुद्रा (śāmbhavī mudrā). in this state, the eyes are physically open, gazing outward, but the entire attention is fixed permanently inward on the non-dual self, completely unmoved by external modifications. she embodies this mudrā, representing the peak of quiet, stable baseline awareness.","esoteric":["The Mudrā of Silent Awareness: Beyond being the consort of Śiva, Śāmbhavī denotes the highest state of internal yoga—the शाम्भवी मुद्रा (Śāmbhavī Mudrā). In this state, the eyes are physically open, gazing outward, but the entire attention is fixed permanently inward on the non-dual Self, completely unmoved by external modifications. She embodies this mudrā, representing the peak of quiet, stable baseline awareness."]},{"number":123,"name":"शारदाराध्या","samasa":["• शारदया आराध्या।","• शारदे (ऋतौ) आराध्या।","• शारदा च असौ आराध्या च।"],"wordByWord":["शारदया — by Sharada","आराध्या — worshipped","शारदे — in autumn","ऋतौ — season","शारदाराध्या — She who is worshipped by Sharada or in the autumn season"],"summary":["शारदाराध्या means She who is worshipped by Śāradā, or She who is worshipped in the autumn season. Śāradā may indicate Sarasvatī, and the name therefore means one adored by Śāradā. It can also mean that She is specially worshipped during śarad, the clear autumn season."],"searchText":"123 शारदाराध्या • शारदया आराध्या। • शारदे (ऋतौ) आराध्या। • शारदा च असौ आराध्या च। शारदया — by sharada आराध्या — worshipped शारदे — in autumn ऋतौ — season शारदाराध्या — she who is worshipped by sharada or in the autumn season शारदाराध्या means she who is worshipped by śāradā, or she who is worshipped in the autumn season. śāradā may indicate sarasvatī, and the name therefore means one adored by śāradā. it can also mean that she is specially worshipped during śarad, the clear autumn season. the source of all learning: sāradā (sarasvatī) is the patron of arts, sciences, and classical learning. by being worshiped by her, it shows that all worldly knowledge bows down to the supreme spiritual knowledge (parā-vidyā) that lalitā represents. the autumn season (śarad) represents clarity, where the muddy waters of the monsoons settle and clear up. this maps onto the calm, clear intellect (śuddha-buddhi) where the divine presence is perfectly reflected and adored.","esoteric":["The Source of All Learning: Sāradā (Sarasvatī) is the patron of arts, sciences, and classical learning. By being worshiped by Her, it shows that all worldly knowledge bows down to the supreme spiritual knowledge (Parā-vidyā) that Lalitā represents. The autumn season (Śarad) represents clarity, where the muddy waters of the monsoons settle and clear up. This maps onto the calm, clear intellect (śuddha-buddhi) where the divine presence is perfectly reflected and adored."]},{"number":124,"name":"शर्वाणी","samasa":["• शर्वस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["शर्वस्य — of Sharva; Shiva","पत्नी — wife","शर्वाणी — She who is the consort of Sharva"],"summary":["शर्वाणी means the consort of Śarva, Lord Paramaśiva. One of the eight forms of Paramaśiva is the earth, and the consort of that form is called Sukeśī; their son is Aṅgāraka, Mars. Śarva is also understood as the one who destroys all beings during the great dissolution. As His consort and power, Śrīdevī is Śarvāṇī."],"searchText":"124 शर्वाणी • शर्वस्य पत्नी। शर्वस्य — of sharva; shiva पत्नी — wife शर्वाणी — she who is the consort of sharva शर्वाणी means the consort of śarva, lord paramaśiva. one of the eight forms of paramaśiva is the earth, and the consort of that form is called sukeśī; their son is aṅgāraka, mars. śarva is also understood as the one who destroys all beings during the great dissolution. as his consort and power, śrīdevī is śarvāṇī. the power of reabsorption: śarva is the specific form of lord śiva that rules over the element of earth and governs the cosmic phase of reabsorption and dissolution (saṃhāra). she is śarvāṇī because she is the kinetic energy that executes this reabsorption. she collapses the heavy, material elements of the universe back into their original, unmanifest potential, reminding the seeker to dissolve their physical attachments into the spiritual self.","esoteric":["The Power of Reabsorption: Śarva is the specific form of Lord Śiva that rules over the element of earth and governs the cosmic phase of reabsorption and dissolution (Saṃhāra). She is Śarvāṇī because She is the kinetic energy that executes this reabsorption. She collapses the heavy, material elements of the universe back into their original, unmanifest potential, reminding the seeker to dissolve their physical attachments into the spiritual self."]},{"number":125,"name":"शर्मदायिनी","samasa":["• शर्मं दातुं शीलम् अस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["शर्मं — happiness; peace","दातुं — to give","शीलम् — nature; habit","शर्मदायिनी — She who gives happiness and peace"],"summary":["शर्मदायिनी means the bestower of happiness. Śarma means happiness, peace and blessedness. Śrīdevī's nature is to give such happiness to Her devotees, and therefore She is Śarmadāyinī. She grants sukha, inward joy and auspicious well-being to those who worship Her."],"searchText":"125 शर्मदायिनी • शर्मं दातुं शीलम् अस्याः। शर्मं — happiness; peace दातुं — to give शीलम् — nature; habit शर्मदायिनी — she who gives happiness and peace शर्मदायिनी means the bestower of happiness. śarma means happiness, peace and blessedness. śrīdevī's nature is to give such happiness to her devotees, and therefore she is śarmadāyinī. she grants sukha, inward joy and auspicious well-being to those who worship her. the giver of unconditional peace: in vedic sanskrit, śarma denotes the highest state of safe, stable, and unconditional peace—far beyond temporary emotional happiness. she is śarmadāyinī because her presence acts as an immediate cooling agent, putting to rest the burning anxieties of worldly struggle and stabilizing the seeker in the profound comfort of self-realization.","esoteric":["The Giver of Unconditional Peace: In Vedic Sanskrit, Śarma denotes the highest state of safe, stable, and unconditional peace—far beyond temporary emotional happiness. She is Śarmadāyinī because Her presence acts as an immediate cooling agent, putting to rest the burning anxieties of worldly struggle and stabilizing the seeker in the profound comfort of self-realization."]},{"number":126,"name":"शाङ्करी","samasa":["• शस्य करः। तस्य स्त्री।","• शं करे यस्य तस्य स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["शस्य — of auspiciousness","करः — maker; doer","स्त्री — woman; consort","शाङ्करी — She who belongs to Shankara"],"summary":["शाङ्करी means the consort of Lord Śaṅkara. Śam means bliss, auspiciousness or propitiousness, and Śaṅkara is the one who gives it. Śāṅkarī is therefore the feminine counterpart and energy of Śaṅkara. She is connected with Yoga-nidrā and Viṣṇu-māyā in the Devī tradition. She is also understood as having the form of night."],"searchText":"126 शाङ्करी • शस्य करः। तस्य स्त्री। • शं करे यस्य तस्य स्त्री। शस्य — of auspiciousness करः — maker; doer स्त्री — woman; consort शाङ्करी — she who belongs to shankara शाङ्करी means the consort of lord śaṅkara. śam means bliss, auspiciousness or propitiousness, and śaṅkara is the one who gives it. śāṅkarī is therefore the feminine counterpart and energy of śaṅkara. she is connected with yoga-nidrā and viṣṇu-māyā in the devī tradition. she is also understood as having the form of night. the dynamic expression of welfare: śam means peace and spiritual welfare, and kara means the doer or causer. śaṅkara is the source of this peace. she is śāṅkarī because she is the active, dynamic expression that delivers this peace to the universe. she is the method, the grace, and the direct experience through which śiva's peaceful nature becomes real to the practitioner.","esoteric":["The Dynamic Expression of Welfare: Śam means peace and spiritual welfare, and kara means the doer or causer. Śaṅkara is the source of this peace. She is Śāṅkarī because She is the active, dynamic expression that delivers this peace to the universe. She is the method, the grace, and the direct experience through which Śiva's peaceful nature becomes real to the practitioner."]},{"number":127,"name":"श्रीकरी","samasa":["• श्रियः करी।","• श्रीकरः (विष्णुः)। तस्य इयम्।"],"wordByWord":["श्रियः — of Sri; prosperity","करी — maker; giver","विष्णुः — Vishnu","श्रीकरी — She who grants auspicious prosperity"],"summary":["श्रीकरी means one who gives prosperity. Śrī has many meanings: prosperity, wealth, Lakṣmī, auspiciousness, splendour, exultation, beauty and lustre. Śrīkarī is the feminine form of Śrīkara, the giver of affluence. Since Śrīdevī and Viṣṇu are inseparable, the name suits Śrīdevī. Time used in Śrīdevī worship may be described through special measures such as tattva-yuga, tattva-varṣa, kalā-māsa, tattva-dina, dina-nityā, tithi-nityā, vāsara and udaya-ghaṭikā. In the kaṭapayādi method, when the first letters of the day and udaya-ghaṭikā coincide, it is called a parva day or Śrīkarī. Thus She gives prosperity in both ordinary and ritual senses."],"searchText":"127 श्रीकरी • श्रियः करी। • श्रीकरः (विष्णुः)। तस्य इयम्। श्रियः — of sri; prosperity करी — maker; giver विष्णुः — vishnu श्रीकरी — she who grants auspicious prosperity श्रीकरी means one who gives prosperity. śrī has many meanings: prosperity, wealth, lakṣmī, auspiciousness, splendour, exultation, beauty and lustre. śrīkarī is the feminine form of śrīkara, the giver of affluence. since śrīdevī and viṣṇu are inseparable, the name suits śrīdevī. time used in śrīdevī worship may be described through special measures such as tattva-yuga, tattva-varṣa, kalā-māsa, tattva-dina, dina-nityā, tithi-nityā, vāsara and udaya-ghaṭikā. in the kaṭapayādi method, when the first letters of the day and udaya-ghaṭikā coincide, it is called a parva day or śrīkarī. thus she gives prosperity in both ordinary and ritual senses. the creator of spiritual radiance: śrī is not limited to physical money; it denotes beauty, symmetry, light, and spiritual radiance. she is śrīkarī because she introduces order, elegance, and light wherever she is invoked. she removes the poverty of the intellect, dressing the seeker's life in the rich splendor of clear understanding and universal harmony.","esoteric":["The Creator of Spiritual Radiance: Śrī is not limited to physical money; it denotes beauty, symmetry, light, and spiritual radiance. She is Śrīkarī because She introduces order, elegance, and light wherever She is invoked. She removes the poverty of the intellect, dressing the seeker's life in the rich splendor of clear understanding and universal harmony."]},{"number":128,"name":"साध्वी","samasa":["• साध्वी (पतिव्रता)।"],"wordByWord":["साध्वी — virtuous woman; faithful wife","पतिव्रता — faithful wife","साध्वी — She who is virtuous and faithful"],"summary":["साध्वी means one who is the paragon of virtue and fidelity. Śrīdevī's loyalty to Her consort is especially praised. When Dakṣa, Her father in one incarnation, insulted Her consort Lord Śiva, She could not tolerate it and gave up Her body. She later took birth as the daughter of Himavān, performed penance and obtained Lord Parameśvara as Her husband. This story shows Her unique chastity and steadfastness. She never takes another consort in any incarnation. Therefore Her pativratā-dharma is held to be greater than all others, and She is called Sādhvī."],"searchText":"128 साध्वी • साध्वी (पतिव्रता)। साध्वी — virtuous woman; faithful wife पतिव्रता — faithful wife साध्वी — she who is virtuous and faithful साध्वी means one who is the paragon of virtue and fidelity. śrīdevī's loyalty to her consort is especially praised. when dakṣa, her father in one incarnation, insulted her consort lord śiva, she could not tolerate it and gave up her body. she later took birth as the daughter of himavān, performed penance and obtained lord parameśvara as her husband. this story shows her unique chastity and steadfastness. she never takes another consort in any incarnation. therefore her pativratā-dharma is held to be greater than all others, and she is called sādhvī. the rectitude of pure consciousness: in common usage, sādhvī is a chaste wife. she is sādhvī because she never deviates from her essential nature as truth, and she remains completely, single-mindedly loyal to her union with śiva. she represents the perfect, unyielding stability of righteousness that balances and runs the cosmic law.","esoteric":["The Rectitude of Pure Consciousness: In common usage, sādhvī is a chaste wife. She is Sādhvī because She never deviates from Her essential nature as truth, and She remains completely, single-mindedly loyal to Her union with Śiva. She represents the perfect, unyielding stability of righteousness that balances and runs the cosmic law."]},{"number":129,"name":"शरच्चन्द्रनिभानना","samasa":["• शरत्कालिकेन चन्द्रेण निभः आननं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शरत्कालिकेन — autumnal","चन्द्रेण — moon","निभः — resemblance","आननं — face","शरच्चन्द्रनिभानना — She whose face resembles the autumn moon"],"summary":["शरच्चन्द्रनिभानना means one whose face shines like the autumn moon. Her face gives coolness, clarity and delight to those who behold Her, just as the clear full moon of autumn pleases the eyes and heart."],"searchText":"129 शरच्चन्द्रनिभानना • शरत्कालिकेन चन्द्रेण निभः आननं यस्याः सा। शरत्कालिकेन — autumnal चन्द्रेण — moon निभः — resemblance आननं — face शरच्चन्द्रनिभानना — she whose face resembles the autumn moon शरच्चन्द्रनिभानना means one whose face shines like the autumn moon. her face gives coolness, clarity and delight to those who behold her, just as the clear full moon of autumn pleases the eyes and heart. the face of pure, unclouded joy: the autumn moon (śarat-candra) is celebrated in indian literature because it shines through an atmosphere completely cleared of dust and storm clouds, radiating a cool, soft, and flawless white light. her face is compared to this moon because it represents the pristine, peaceful radiance of absolute consciousness, completely unclouded by the dust of worldly thoughts, bathing the seeker in cool, comforting grace.","esoteric":["The Face of Pure, Unclouded Joy: The autumn moon (śarat-candra) is celebrated in Indian literature because it shines through an atmosphere completely cleared of dust and storm clouds, radiating a cool, soft, and flawless white light. Her face is compared to this moon because it represents the pristine, peaceful radiance of absolute consciousness, completely unclouded by the dust of worldly thoughts, bathing the seeker in cool, comforting grace."]},{"number":130,"name":"शातोदरी","samasa":["• शातम् उदरं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शातम् — slender; thin","उदरं — belly","शातोदरी — She whose waist/belly is slender"],"summary":["शातोदरी means one who has a slender waist. Śāta means slim, and She has such a delicate waist. The name can also suggest the daughter of Himavān, the king of the Himalayas with hundreds of caves. A slender waist is considered a mark of beauty, and Śrīdevī is praised as possessing that graceful form."],"searchText":"130 शातोदरी • शातम् उदरं यस्याः सा। शातम् — slender; thin उदरं — belly शातोदरी — she whose waist/belly is slender शातोदरी means one who has a slender waist. śāta means slim, and she has such a delicate waist. the name can also suggest the daughter of himavān, the king of the himalayas with hundreds of caves. a slender waist is considered a mark of beauty, and śrīdevī is praised as possessing that graceful form. the container of the unmanifest universe: a slender abdomen represents physical beauty. esoterically, her abdomen is thinned out because during manifest creation, she projects the entire universe outward from within herself. the space within her belly represents the deep, silent repository where the entire cosmos is held in its unmanifest, potential state before the next cycle of creation begins.","esoteric":["The Container of the Unmanifest Universe: A slender abdomen represents physical beauty. Esoterically, Her abdomen is thinned out because during manifest creation, She projects the entire universe outward from within Herself. The space within Her belly represents the deep, silent repository where the entire cosmos is held in its unmanifest, potential state before the next cycle of creation begins."]},{"number":131,"name":"शान्तिमती","samasa":["• शान्तिरस्या अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["शान्तिमती — She who possesses peace"],"summary":["शान्तिमती means one who has a controlled and peaceful mind. She is tranquil and does not show vehemence toward Her devotees. The name is connected with Śāntā, Śānti and Śamātmikā, all indicating quietness, peace and inner restraint."],"searchText":"131 शान्तिमती • शान्तिरस्या अस्तीति। शान्तिमती — she who possesses peace शान्तिमती means one who has a controlled and peaceful mind. she is tranquil and does not show vehemence toward her devotees. the name is connected with śāntā, śānti and śamātmikā, all indicating quietness, peace and inner restraint. the ground of absolute stillness: peace (śānti) is not merely the temporary absence of mental noise; it is the fundamental nature of the unconditioned self (ātman). she is śāntimatī because she is the keeper of that absolute, unshakeable stillness that remain unaffected by the cosmic cycles of creation and destruction.","esoteric":["The Ground of Absolute Stillness: Peace (śānti) is not merely the temporary absence of mental noise; it is the fundamental nature of the unconditioned self (Ātman). She is Śāntimatī because She is the keeper of that absolute, unshakeable stillness that remain unaffected by the cosmic cycles of creation and destruction."]},{"number":132,"name":"निराधारा","samasa":["• आधाराः निष्क्रान्ताः यस्याः सा।","• निर्गतः आधारः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["आधाराः — supports","निष्क्रान्ताः — gone out; removed","निर्गतः — gone out; absent","निराधारा — She who is without support"],"summary":["निराधारा means one who has no support other than Herself and who is the support of all. Ādhāra can also indicate Mūlādhāra, from where She rises upward. The name also points to nirādhāra-pūjā, worship without external support such as an image. From this name onward, Śrīdevī's nirguṇa form and the results of meditating on it are explained. Worship may be external or internal; internal worship may be with support or without support. Sādhāra worship uses mental images and mantras taught by a teacher, while nirādhāra worship is by pure intellect, focusing on Śrīdevī as known through knowledge. In reality, pure intellect is the supreme Śrīdevī Herself. For the destruction of saṃsāra, She is worshipped as the Self, the witness, free from the glamour of manifoldness."],"searchText":"132 निराधारा • आधाराः निष्क्रान्ताः यस्याः सा। • निर्गतः आधारः यस्याः सा। आधाराः — supports निष्क्रान्ताः — gone out; removed निर्गतः — gone out; absent निराधारा — she who is without support निराधारा means one who has no support other than herself and who is the support of all. ādhāra can also indicate mūlādhāra, from where she rises upward. the name also points to nirādhāra-pūjā, worship without external support such as an image. from this name onward, śrīdevī's nirguṇa form and the results of meditating on it are explained. worship may be external or internal; internal worship may be with support or without support. sādhāra worship uses mental images and mantras taught by a teacher, while nirādhāra worship is by pure intellect, focusing on śrīdevī as known through knowledge. in reality, pure intellect is the supreme śrīdevī herself. for the destruction of saṃsāra, she is worshipped as the self, the witness, free from the glamour of manifoldness. the self-sustained absolute: every object in the manifest universe requires a base (ādhāra) to exist—the elements rest in space, bodies rest on earth. because she is the ultimate primordial cause (mūlaprakṛti) and space itself, there is nothing prior to her upon which she could rest. she is entirely self-supported and self-sustained (anādhāra), serving as the foundational support for the entire cosmos while resting on nothing but her own absolute being.","esoteric":["The Self-Sustained Absolute: Every object in the manifest universe requires a base (ādhāra) to exist—the elements rest in space, bodies rest on earth. Because She is the ultimate primordial cause (Mūlaprakṛti) and space itself, there is nothing prior to Her upon which She could rest. She is entirely self-supported and self-sustained (Anādhāra), serving as the foundational support for the entire cosmos while resting on nothing but Her own absolute being."]},{"number":133,"name":"निरञ्जना","samasa":["• निर्गतमञ्जनं यस्याः सा।","• नितरां रञ्जनं यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["रञ्जनं — colouring; attachment","निरञ्जना — She who is unstained"],"summary":["निरञ्जना means one who is free from every stain. Añjana means black collyrium used for the eyes; though used for beauty, it is still a stain. Here añjana indicates ignorance or illusion, because knowledge disappears through ignorance and darkness in the mind. Śrīdevī has no relation to ignorance or illusion. There are three kinds of bound souls: vijñānakevala, who sees the Self in the non-self and has arrogance as the impurity; pralayakevala, who also has the unperceivable impurity of karma causing new births; and sakala, who has the impurity of māyā and sees duality in all things. Śrīdevī is free from these impurities and therefore is Nirañjanā. The name can also mean one of great delight."],"searchText":"133 निरञ्जना • निर्गतमञ्जनं यस्याः सा। • नितरां रञ्जनं यस्यां सा। रञ्जनं — colouring; attachment निरञ्जना — she who is unstained निरञ्जना means one who is free from every stain. añjana means black collyrium used for the eyes; though used for beauty, it is still a stain. here añjana indicates ignorance or illusion, because knowledge disappears through ignorance and darkness in the mind. śrīdevī has no relation to ignorance or illusion. there are three kinds of bound souls: vijñānakevala, who sees the self in the non-self and has arrogance as the impurity; pralayakevala, who also has the unperceivable impurity of karma causing new births; and sakala, who has the impurity of māyā and sees duality in all things. śrīdevī is free from these impurities and therefore is nirañjanā. the name can also mean one of great delight. the flawless canvas: añjana means black collyrium or metaphorically, the stain of ignorance and limitation. she is nirañjanā because her primordial light remains completely unstained by the dualistic dynamics of the world. alternatively, as nitaraṃ rañjanam, she is the ultimate source of pure spiritual color and aesthetic ecstasy that fills the hearts of realized sages.","esoteric":["The Flawless Canvas: Añjana means black collyrium or metaphorically, the stain of ignorance and limitation. She is Nirañjanā because Her primordial light remains completely unstained by the dualistic dynamics of the world. Alternatively, as Nitaraṃ rañjanam, She is the ultimate source of pure spiritual color and aesthetic ecstasy that fills the hearts of realized sages."]},{"number":134,"name":"निर्लेपा","samasa":["• लेपात् निष्क्रान्ता।","• लेपः (कर्मसम्बन्धः ज्ञानेन) निर्गतः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["लेपः — taint; adhesion","कर्मसम्बन्धः — connection with action","निर्गतः — gone out; absent","निर्लेपा — She who is untouched by taint"],"summary":["निर्लेपा means one who is untouched by the results of actions. Śrīdevī is knowledge itself and therefore has no connection with karma. When one attains knowledge of Brahman, understood here as Śrīdevī, one becomes free from impurities. Just as a lotus leaf is not wetted by water, She is not affected by actions. Śrīdevī is free from the impurity called pralayakevala. By meditating on Her, one becomes free from impurities caused by action."],"searchText":"134 निर्लेपा • लेपात् निष्क्रान्ता। • लेपः (कर्मसम्बन्धः ज्ञानेन) निर्गतः यस्याः सा। लेपः — taint; adhesion कर्मसम्बन्धः — connection with action निर्गतः — gone out; absent निर्लेपा — she who is untouched by taint निर्लेपा means one who is untouched by the results of actions. śrīdevī is knowledge itself and therefore has no connection with karma. when one attains knowledge of brahman, understood here as śrīdevī, one becomes free from impurities. just as a lotus leaf is not wetted by water, she is not affected by actions. śrīdevī is free from the impurity called pralayakevala. by meditating on her, one becomes free from impurities caused by action. the untouched witness: just as a water drop slides across a lotus leaf without wetting it, her consciousness remains completely nirlepā—free from the sticky modifications of cosmic actions. even though she runs and maintains the entire karmic universe, the results of actions (karmaphala) never bind or stain her pristine essence.","esoteric":["The Untouched Witness: Just as a water drop slides across a lotus leaf without wetting it, Her consciousness remains completely Nirlepā—free from the sticky modifications of cosmic actions. Even though She runs and maintains the entire karmic universe, the results of actions (karmaphala) never bind or stain Her pristine essence."]},{"number":135,"name":"निर्मला","samasa":["• निर्गतानि मलानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मलानि — impurities","निर्मला — She who is pure"],"summary":["निर्मला means one who is free from all impurities. She has no impurity of arrogance and is therefore free from vijñānakevala impurity. She is free from tamas and from the impurity of ignorance or lack of true knowledge. Liberation is the aim of the soul, and this name, together with Nityamuktā, indicates the liberated nature of the Self. By meditating on this name, one becomes free from the impurity of arrogance."],"searchText":"135 निर्मला • निर्गतानि मलानि यस्याः सा। मलानि — impurities निर्मला — she who is pure निर्मला means one who is free from all impurities. she has no impurity of arrogance and is therefore free from vijñānakevala impurity. she is free from tamas and from the impurity of ignorance or lack of true knowledge. liberation is the aim of the soul, and this name, together with nityamuktā, indicates the liberated nature of the self. by meditating on this name, one becomes free from the impurity of arrogance. the transcendence of the three drosses: in śākta tantra, individual souls are bound by three types of mala (impurities): āṇava-mala (the illusion of being small and limited), māyīya-mala (the illusion of dualistic separation), and kārma-mala(the bondage of past actions). she is nirmalā because her supreme nature is eternally free from these three structural limitations, acting as the pure mirror that shows the seeker their own divine reality.","esoteric":["The Transcendence of the Three Drosses: In Śākta Tantra, individual souls are bound by three types of mala (impurities): Āṇava-mala (the illusion of being small and limited), Māyīya-mala (the illusion of dualistic separation), and Kārma-mala(the bondage of past actions). She is Nirmalā because Her supreme nature is eternally free from these three structural limitations, acting as the pure mirror that shows the seeker their own divine reality."]},{"number":136,"name":"नित्या","samasa":["• नित्या।"],"wordByWord":["नित्या — eternal","नित्या — She who is eternal"],"summary":["नित्या means one who is eternal. The Self is eternal, and therefore the view that the world vanishes every moment is not accepted here. In Śrīvidyā worship, fifteen tithi Nityā Devīs are mentioned, and Śrīdevī Herself is the sixteenth Mahānityā. These Nityā Devīs are connected with phases of the waxing and waning moon, but Śrīdevī is beyond all such measures of time. This name also indicates one of the Nityā Devīs. By meditating on Nityā, one becomes free from ruin and decay."],"searchText":"136 नित्या • नित्या। नित्या — eternal नित्या — she who is eternal नित्या means one who is eternal. the self is eternal, and therefore the view that the world vanishes every moment is not accepted here. in śrīvidyā worship, fifteen tithi nityā devīs are mentioned, and śrīdevī herself is the sixteenth mahānityā. these nityā devīs are connected with phases of the waxing and waning moon, but śrīdevī is beyond all such measures of time. this name also indicates one of the nityā devīs. by meditating on nityā, one becomes free from ruin and decay. the unmoving present: objects in time have a beginning, growth, decay, and death. she is nityā because she sits entirely outside the linear track of time. she is the constant, unmoving present that witnesses the rise and fall of universes without ever losing a single fraction of her completeness.","esoteric":["The Unmoving Present: Objects in time have a beginning, growth, decay, and death. She is Nityā because She sits entirely outside the linear track of time. She is the constant, unmoving present that witnesses the rise and fall of universes without ever losing a single fraction of Her completeness."]},{"number":137,"name":"निराकारा","samasa":["• निर्गतः आकारः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone out; absent","आकारः — form","निराकारा — She who is formless"],"summary":["निराकारा means one who is not limited by any form. Every visible form has some special feature, and the many forms of Śrīdevī seen by us are appearances. Her real nature is formless. Since She is omnipresent, no particular form or quality can limit Her. The name affirms that She is beyond all restricting forms."],"searchText":"137 निराकारा • निर्गतः आकारः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone out; absent आकारः — form निराकारा — she who is formless निराकारा means one who is not limited by any form. every visible form has some special feature, and the many forms of śrīdevī seen by us are appearances. her real nature is formless. since she is omnipresent, no particular form or quality can limit her. the name affirms that she is beyond all restricting forms. the infinite canvas: a defined shape requires a boundary that separates it from other things. because her supreme reality is all-pervading (sarva-vyāpinī), she cannot be pinned down by a physical outline. she is nirākārā (formless) in her parā state, which allows her to spontaneously project and assume all possible forms in the manifest universe without being limited by any of them.","esoteric":["The Infinite Canvas: A defined shape requires a boundary that separates it from other things. Because Her supreme reality is all-pervading (Sarva-vyāpinī), She cannot be pinned down by a physical outline. She is Nirākārā (formless) in Her Parā state, which allows Her to spontaneously project and assume all possible forms in the manifest universe without being limited by any of them."]},{"number":138,"name":"निराकुला","samasa":["• निर्गता आकुला यस्याः सा।","• निर्गतम् आकुलत्वं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["आकुलत्वं — agitation","निराकुला — She who is free from agitation"],"summary":["निराकुला means one who is never agitated. Though She is connected with ignorance as its controller, She is never disturbed by it. She remains distant from those whose minds are agitated, meaning that She can be reached only by those who possess clear and steady knowledge. Akula may also mean a void-like state, but She is not a mere void; She is omnipresent. Thus She is free from agitation and beyond emptiness."],"searchText":"138 निराकुला • निर्गता आकुला यस्याः सा। • निर्गतम् आकुलत्वं यस्याः सा। आकुलत्वं — agitation निराकुला — she who is free from agitation निराकुला means one who is never agitated. though she is connected with ignorance as its controller, she is never disturbed by it. she remains distant from those whose minds are agitated, meaning that she can be reached only by those who possess clear and steady knowledge. akula may also mean a void-like state, but she is not a mere void; she is omnipresent. thus she is free from agitation and beyond emptiness. the calm core of the cyclone: the manifest universe is a whirlwind of kinetic energy, changes, and emotional storms (ākula). she is nirākulā because her deepest identity sits at the dead center of this whirlwind—perfectly stable, clear, and serene, completely untouched by the outer waves of cosmic agitation.","esoteric":["The Calm Core of the Cyclone: The manifest universe is a whirlwind of kinetic energy, changes, and emotional storms (ākula). She is Nirākulā because Her deepest identity sits at the dead center of this whirlwind—perfectly stable, clear, and serene, completely untouched by the outer waves of cosmic agitation."]},{"number":139,"name":"निर्गुणा","samasa":["• निर्गताः गुणाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","गुणाः — qualities; gunas","निर्गुणा — She who is beyond the gunas"],"summary":["निर्गुणा means one who is beyond the three guṇas. The guṇas are sattva, rajas and tamas. The traits of deities belong to bodies and identities, but Śrīdevī is of the nature of cit and therefore has neither such qualities nor limiting identity. She is witness, pure, uncontaminated and beyond all attributes. Since qualities belong to the body and not to pure consciousness, She is nirguṇā."],"searchText":"139 निर्गुणा • निर्गताः गुणाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent गुणाः — qualities; gunas निर्गुणा — she who is beyond the gunas निर्गुणा means one who is beyond the three guṇas. the guṇas are sattva, rajas and tamas. the traits of deities belong to bodies and identities, but śrīdevī is of the nature of cit and therefore has neither such qualities nor limiting identity. she is witness, pure, uncontaminated and beyond all attributes. since qualities belong to the body and not to pure consciousness, she is nirguṇā. the substrate of qualities: the three guṇas are the building blocks of material nature (prakṛti). while she deploys these three qualities to construct the physical world, her primary, unmanifest identity (nirguṇa-brahman) remains completely unconditioned by them. she is the baseline awareness that witnesses the interaction of the qualities without being trapped by their modifications.","esoteric":["The Substrate of Qualities: The three Guṇas are the building blocks of material nature (Prakṛti). While She deploys these three qualities to construct the physical world, Her primary, unmanifest identity (Nirguṇa-Brahman) remains completely unconditioned by them. She is the baseline awareness that witnesses the interaction of the qualities without being trapped by their modifications."]},{"number":140,"name":"निष्कला","samasa":["• निर्गताः कलाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","कलाः — parts; phases","निष्कला — She who is without parts"],"summary":["निष्कला means one who is partless and an indivisible whole. The name rejects the idea that Brahman has parts or organs. The soul may appear as a part because of limiting adjuncts created by ignorance, just as space appears divided by pots or the moon appears many through reflections in different vessels. In reality, the soul is not different from Īśvara. When knowledge of Brahman removes ignorance and its limitations, only Brahman is seen. Meditation on Brahman without qualities is also niṣkala contemplation. Śrīdevī is that partless reality."],"searchText":"140 निष्कला • निर्गताः कलाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent कलाः — parts; phases निष्कला — she who is without parts निष्कला means one who is partless and an indivisible whole. the name rejects the idea that brahman has parts or organs. the soul may appear as a part because of limiting adjuncts created by ignorance, just as space appears divided by pots or the moon appears many through reflections in different vessels. in reality, the soul is not different from īśvara. when knowledge of brahman removes ignorance and its limitations, only brahman is seen. meditation on brahman without qualities is also niṣkala contemplation. śrīdevī is that partless reality. the partless whole: anything made of parts (sakala) can be broken down, divided, or destroyed over time. she is niṣkalā because she is an indivisible, homogenous mass of pure consciousness (akhaṇḍa-ekarasa). having no internal divisions, she is completely free from decay, existing eternally as a unified, perfect whole.","esoteric":["The Partless Whole: Anything made of parts (sakala) can be broken down, divided, or destroyed over time. She is Niṣkalā because She is an indivisible, homogenous mass of pure consciousness (Akhaṇḍa-Ekarasa). Having no internal divisions, She is completely free from decay, existing eternally as a unified, perfect whole."]},{"number":141,"name":"शान्ता","samasa":["• शान्ता (शमवती)।"],"wordByWord":["शान्ता — peaceful","शान्ता — She who is peaceful"],"summary":["शान्ता means one who is tranquil. She is without parts, without action and peaceful. She is connected with Śāntimatī, Śānti and Śamātmikā. The name can also be understood through the Sanskrit letters: the letter preceding śa is va, taken as the seed of nectar, so She is the form of the amṛta-bīja. If read as Aśāntā, with the prefix a understood differently, āśā means directions, and the meaning becomes that She is spread in all directions. Thus She is peaceful, nectar-like and all-pervading."],"searchText":"141 शान्ता • शान्ता (शमवती)। शान्ता — peaceful शान्ता — she who is peaceful शान्ता means one who is tranquil. she is without parts, without action and peaceful. she is connected with śāntimatī, śānti and śamātmikā. the name can also be understood through the sanskrit letters: the letter preceding śa is va, taken as the seed of nectar, so she is the form of the amṛta-bīja. if read as aśāntā, with the prefix a understood differently, āśā means directions, and the meaning becomes that she is spread in all directions. thus she is peaceful, nectar-like and all-pervading. the dynamic stillness: unlike passive dead space, her quietude (śāntā) is a dynamic, self-aware state of profound harmony. it represents the perfect stabilization of all mental and cosmic fluctuations, offering a serene sanctuary where the seeker's mind can find instant rest from the friction of worldly life.","esoteric":["The Dynamic Stillness: Unlike passive dead space, Her quietude (Śāntā) is a dynamic, self-aware state of profound harmony. It represents the perfect stabilization of all mental and cosmic fluctuations, offering a serene sanctuary where the seeker's mind can find instant rest from the friction of worldly life."]},{"number":142,"name":"निष्कामा","samasa":["• निर्गतः कामः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone out; absent","कामः — desire","निष्कामा — She who is free from desire"],"summary":["निष्कामा means one who is without desires. When all desires are already fulfilled, nothing remains to be desired. Śrīdevī is complete in Herself and therefore has no unfulfilled wish. Statements about divine will and resolve are to be understood as connected with limiting adjuncts and manifestation, not as ordinary desire. Her nature is fullness, and because She is pūrṇa, She is niṣkāmā."],"searchText":"142 निष्कामा • निर्गतः कामः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone out; absent कामः — desire निष्कामा — she who is free from desire निष्कामा means one who is without desires. when all desires are already fulfilled, nothing remains to be desired. śrīdevī is complete in herself and therefore has no unfulfilled wish. statements about divine will and resolve are to be understood as connected with limiting adjuncts and manifestation, not as ordinary desire. her nature is fullness, and because she is pūrṇa, she is niṣkāmā. the fullness of being: desire arises only when an entity feels incomplete or lacks something outside of itself. because she is pūrṇā (the infinite all-inclusive whole), there is nothing external to her that she could want or acquire. she is niṣkāmā because she rests in the complete satisfaction of her own self-contained fullness.","esoteric":["The Fullness of Being: Desire arises only when an entity feels incomplete or lacks something outside of itself. Because She is Pūrṇā (the infinite all-inclusive whole), there is nothing external to Her that She could want or acquire. She is Niṣkāmā because She rests in the complete satisfaction of Her own self-contained fullness."]},{"number":143,"name":"निरूपप्लवा","samasa":["• निर्गतः उपप्लवः (नाशः) यस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone out; absent","उपप्लवः — calamity; disturbance","नाशः — destruction","निरूपप्लवा — She who is free from disturbance"],"summary":["निरूपप्लवा means one who is free from destruction. Upaplava means destruction or disturbance, and She is free from it. The same meaning is related to Nirnāśā. If the name is split as nir, upa and plava, it can also be understood as She who creates the shower of nectar in the body, connecting the name with Sudhāsārābhivarṣiṇī and Bisatantutanīyasī. Thus She is beyond destruction and is also associated with the inner flow of nectar."],"searchText":"143 निरूपप्लवा • निर्गतः उपप्लवः (नाशः) यस्याः। निर्गतः — gone out; absent उपप्लवः — calamity; disturbance नाशः — destruction निरूपप्लवा — she who is free from disturbance निरूपप्लवा means one who is free from destruction. upaplava means destruction or disturbance, and she is free from it. the same meaning is related to nirnāśā. if the name is split as nir, upa and plava, it can also be understood as she who creates the shower of nectar in the body, connecting the name with sudhāsārābhivarṣiṇī and bisatantutanīyasī. thus she is beyond destruction and is also associated with the inner flow of nectar. the indestructible core: in sanskrit, upaplava refers to solar or lunar eclipses, signifying temporary darkening or structural crisis. she is nirūpaplavā because her inner sun of awareness never undergoes an eclipse or structural crisis. no cosmic event or cataclysm can shade, reduce, or disrupt her absolute clarity.","esoteric":["The Indestructible Core: In Sanskrit, upaplava refers to solar or lunar eclipses, signifying temporary darkening or structural crisis. She is Nirūpaplavā because Her inner sun of awareness never undergoes an eclipse or structural crisis. No cosmic event or cataclysm can shade, reduce, or disrupt Her absolute clarity."]},{"number":144,"name":"नित्यमुक्ता","samasa":["• नित्यं मुक्ता नित्यं मुञ्चति मुच्यते वा।","• नित्यं मुक्ताः यस्याः भक्ताः सा।","• नित्यमुक्तस्य भावः।"],"wordByWord":["मुक्ता — liberated","नित्यमुक्ता — She who is ever liberated"],"summary":["नित्यमुक्ता means one who is ever free from worldly bonds. Though Her devotees are bound to the world, She Herself is eternally free. She is the very form of liberation and has the nature of the nityamuktas, the eternally liberated. Her freedom is not produced at any time; it is always Her nature."],"searchText":"144 नित्यमुक्ता • नित्यं मुक्ता नित्यं मुञ्चति मुच्यते वा। • नित्यं मुक्ताः यस्याः भक्ताः सा। • नित्यमुक्तस्य भावः। मुक्ता — liberated नित्यमुक्ता — she who is ever liberated नित्यमुक्ता means one who is ever free from worldly bonds. though her devotees are bound to the world, she herself is eternally free. she is the very form of liberation and has the nature of the nityamuktas, the eternally liberated. her freedom is not produced at any time; it is always her nature. the sanctuary of freedom: some entities achieve freedom after a long period of bondage (mukta). she is nityamuktā because bondage has never touched her at any point in time. she is freedom itself. consequently, coming into contact with her energy instantly unbinds the seeker's mind, untying the knots of worldly conditioning.","esoteric":["The Sanctuary of Freedom: Some entities achieve freedom after a long period of bondage (mukta). She is Nityamuktā because bondage has never touched Her at any point in time. She is freedom itself. Consequently, coming into contact with Her energy instantly unbinds the seeker's mind, untying the knots of worldly conditioning."]},{"number":145,"name":"निर्विकारा","samasa":["• निर्गताः विकाराः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","विकाराः — modifications","निर्विकारा — She who is changeless"],"summary":["निर्विकारा means one who is not subject to change. The soul is witness to changes in the world but does not itself change. Nature changes and evolves into intellect, ego, organs, mind and elements, but pure consciousness remains unaffected. The Sāṅkhya system speaks of twenty-four principles beginning with nature and the soul as the twenty-fifth. Śrīdevī is described here as free from the many kinds of change belonging to these principles. In Śrīvidyā, She is the universal absolute, and the principles are understood without making matter independent of Her. She remains the changeless reality behind all changing categories."],"searchText":"145 निर्विकारा • निर्गताः विकाराः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent विकाराः — modifications निर्विकारा — she who is changeless निर्विकारा means one who is not subject to change. the soul is witness to changes in the world but does not itself change. nature changes and evolves into intellect, ego, organs, mind and elements, but pure consciousness remains unaffected. the sāṅkhya system speaks of twenty-four principles beginning with nature and the soul as the twenty-fifth. śrīdevī is described here as free from the many kinds of change belonging to these principles. in śrīvidyā, she is the universal absolute, and the principles are understood without making matter independent of her. she remains the changeless reality behind all changing categories. the changeless substrate: according to philosophy, there are six types of modifications (ṣaḍ-vikāra) that happen to matter: birth, existence, growth, alteration, decay, and death. she is nirvikārā because her consciousness remains absolutely changeless, serving as the stable screen upon which the moving movies of cosmic changes are projected.","esoteric":["The Changeless Substrate: According to philosophy, there are six types of modifications (ṣaḍ-vikāra) that happen to matter: birth, existence, growth, alteration, decay, and death. She is Nirvikārā because Her consciousness remains absolutely changeless, serving as the stable screen upon which the moving movies of cosmic changes are projected."]},{"number":146,"name":"निष्प्रपञ्चा","samasa":["• निर्गताः प्रपञ्चाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","प्रपञ्चाः — phenomenal manifestations","निष्प्रपञ्चा — She who is beyond the phenomenal world"],"summary":["निष्प्रपञ्चा means one who is beyond the whole expanded universe. Prapañca means collection, extension and expansion. Since Śrīdevī is complete in Herself and omnipresent, She is beyond these forms of worldly expansion. One thing expanding into many is prapañca, and contraction and expansion belong to changing things. Such worldly change is not seen in Śrīdevī, who is changeless. The name can also mean that the universe beginning with earth manifests from Her, while She Herself remains beyond manifestation."],"searchText":"146 निष्प्रपञ्चा • निर्गताः प्रपञ्चाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent प्रपञ्चाः — phenomenal manifestations निष्प्रपञ्चा — she who is beyond the phenomenal world निष्प्रपञ्चा means one who is beyond the whole expanded universe. prapañca means collection, extension and expansion. since śrīdevī is complete in herself and omnipresent, she is beyond these forms of worldly expansion. one thing expanding into many is prapañca, and contraction and expansion belong to changing things. such worldly change is not seen in śrīdevī, who is changeless. the name can also mean that the universe beginning with earth manifests from her, while she herself remains beyond manifestation. the transcendent matrix: prapañca refers to the manifest world built from the five elements, characterized by multiplicity and division. she is niṣprapañcābecause, in her absolute reality, all multiplicity dissolves into pure, undifferentiated unity. she supports the world as its creator, yet her true self remains untouched by cosmic complexity.","esoteric":["The Transcendent Matrix: Prapañca refers to the manifest world built from the five elements, characterized by multiplicity and division. She is Niṣprapañcābecause, in Her absolute reality, all multiplicity dissolves into pure, undifferentiated unity. She supports the world as its creator, yet Her true self remains untouched by cosmic complexity."]},{"number":147,"name":"निराश्रया","samasa":["• निर्गताः आश्रयाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","आश्रयाः — supports","निराश्रया — She who is without dependence"],"summary":["निराश्रया means one who is not dependent on anything or anyone. Everything depends on Her, but She does not depend on anything. She is self-established and independent. The name rejects the idea that the body or any external support is Brahman. Śrīdevī is beyond dependence and is the support on which all else rests."],"searchText":"147 निराश्रया • निर्गताः आश्रयाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent आश्रयाः — supports निराश्रया — she who is without dependence निराश्रया means one who is not dependent on anything or anyone. everything depends on her, but she does not depend on anything. she is self-established and independent. the name rejects the idea that the body or any external support is brahman. śrīdevī is beyond dependence and is the support on which all else rests. the ultimate sanctuary: an entity seeks a refuge (āśraya) when it feels weak, incomplete, or threatened. because she is the supreme powerhouse of all existence, she depends on nothing outside of herself. instead, she acts as the ultimate, unmoving refuge for all created beings while remaining completely self-contained.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Sanctuary: An entity seeks a refuge (āśraya) when it feels weak, incomplete, or threatened. Because She is the supreme powerhouse of all existence, She depends on nothing outside of Herself. Instead, She acts as the ultimate, unmoving refuge for all created beings while remaining completely self-contained."]},{"number":148,"name":"नित्यशुद्धा","samasa":["• नित्यं शुद्धा।"],"wordByWord":["शुद्धा — pure","नित्यशुद्धा — She who is eternally pure"],"summary":["नित्यशुद्धा means one who is eternally pure. She is free from impurity in all three times: past, present and future. She does not touch impurity, is greater than all, and is always pure. The body may be impure, but the indwelling Self is pure; Śrīdevī is of that eternally pure nature."],"searchText":"148 नित्यशुद्धा • नित्यं शुद्धा। शुद्धा — pure नित्यशुद्धा — she who is eternally pure नित्यशुद्धा means one who is eternally pure. she is free from impurity in all three times: past, present and future. she does not touch impurity, is greater than all, and is always pure. the body may be impure, but the indwelling self is pure; śrīdevī is of that eternally pure nature. the inherent purity: worldly purity is conditional and can be lost through defilement. she is nityaśuddhā because her purity is an absolute, non-negotiable aspect of her being. no matter how dense the material world becomes, her core light of awareness remains unsullied, working as an active clearing agent for anyone who contemplates her form.","esoteric":["The Inherent Purity: Worldly purity is conditional and can be lost through defilement. She is Nityaśuddhā because Her purity is an absolute, non-negotiable aspect of Her being. No matter how dense the material world becomes, Her core light of awareness remains unsullied, working as an active clearing agent for anyone who contemplates Her form."]},{"number":149,"name":"नित्यबुद्धा","samasa":["• नित्यं बुद्धा।"],"wordByWord":["बुद्धा — awakened; enlightened","नित्यबुद्धा — She who is eternally enlightened"],"summary":["नित्यबुद्धा means one who is always knowledgeable and wise. She is of the form of cit and therefore is always knowledge itself. Knowledge is inseparable from the knower. The deities worshipped in other paths are also forms of Śrīdevī. Through Her grace, purity and awakened knowledge become eternal. She is also worshipped as the deity present in the paths of different religious traditions."],"searchText":"149 नित्यबुद्धा • नित्यं बुद्धा। बुद्धा — awakened; enlightened नित्यबुद्धा — she who is eternally enlightened नित्यबुद्धा means one who is always knowledgeable and wise. she is of the form of cit and therefore is always knowledge itself. knowledge is inseparable from the knower. the deities worshipped in other paths are also forms of śrīdevī. through her grace, purity and awakened knowledge become eternal. she is also worshipped as the deity present in the paths of different religious traditions. the unwinking eye of awareness: human consciousness moves through cycles of waking, dreaming, and deep sleep. she is nityabuddhā because her supreme eye of awareness never closes, blinks, or forgets. she is the eternal, non-dual intelligence that illuminates all experiences, completely free from the sleep of ignorance.","esoteric":["The Unwinking Eye of Awareness: Human consciousness moves through cycles of waking, dreaming, and deep sleep. She is Nityabuddhā because Her supreme eye of awareness never closes, blinks, or forgets. She is the eternal, non-dual intelligence that illuminates all experiences, completely free from the sleep of ignorance."]},{"number":150,"name":"निरवद्या","samasa":["• निर्गतम् अवद्यं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अवद्यं — blemish","निरवद्या — She who is faultless"],"summary":["निरवद्या means one who is flawless and blemishless. Avadya means that which should not be revealed, and by extension a flaw or deficiency. Such flaws arise only from ignorance. Śrīdevī, being knowledge itself, is beyond all defects. Avadya is also the name of a hell; devotees of Śrīdevī are protected from such states and liberated from them. Therefore She is Niravadyā, free from all blemish and the remover of defect."],"searchText":"150 निरवद्या • निर्गतम् अवद्यं यस्याः सा। अवद्यं — blemish निरवद्या — she who is faultless निरवद्या means one who is flawless and blemishless. avadya means that which should not be revealed, and by extension a flaw or deficiency. such flaws arise only from ignorance. śrīdevī, being knowledge itself, is beyond all defects. avadya is also the name of a hell; devotees of śrīdevī are protected from such states and liberated from them. therefore she is niravadyā, free from all blemish and the remover of defect. the standard of flawless perfection: avadya refers to that which can be criticized or found lacking. because her nature is the complete integration of truth, beauty, and goodness (satyam-śivam-sundaram), there is no structural flaw or mismatch within her. she stands as the perfect, unblemished benchmark of reality.","esoteric":["The Standard of Flawless Perfection: Avadya refers to that which can be criticized or found lacking. Because Her nature is the complete integration of truth, beauty, and goodness (Satyam-Śivam-Sundaram), there is no structural flaw or mismatch within Her. She stands as the perfect, unblemished benchmark of reality."]},{"number":151,"name":"निरन्तरा","samasa":["• निर्गता अन्तराः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अन्तराः — intervals; gaps","निरन्तरा — She who is without interval or separation"],"summary":["निरन्तरा means one who is without interval or separation. She is continuous, unbroken and without any gap. Nothing stands apart from Her, and there is no interruption in Her presence."],"searchText":"151 निरन्तरा • निर्गता अन्तराः यस्याः सा। अन्तराः — intervals; gaps निरन्तरा — she who is without interval or separation निरन्तरा means one who is without interval or separation. she is continuous, unbroken and without any gap. nothing stands apart from her, and there is no interruption in her presence. the unbroken continuum: antara means a gap or separation. she is nirantarābecause she is a dense, seamless continuum of pure consciousness (akhaṇḍa-caitanya). there is no vacuum or point in space-time where she is absent, establishing her as the single thread running through all existence.","esoteric":["The Unbroken Continuum: Antara means a gap or separation. She is Nirantarābecause She is a dense, seamless continuum of pure consciousness (Akhaṇḍa-Caitanya). There is no vacuum or point in space-time where She is absent, establishing Her as the single thread running through all existence."]},{"number":152,"name":"निष्कारणा","samasa":["• निर्गतं कारणं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कारणं — cause","निष्कारणा — She who is without cause"],"summary":["निष्कारणा means one who is without cause. Śrīdevī Herself is the root cause of everything, and therefore She has no cause for Herself. She is the cause and chief of all causes, with no creator and no superior. The name can also be connected with the causal principle used in worship. When Śrīdevī is installed in Śrīcakra, She is contemplated as the form of causal bliss. She is complete in that causal reality and is associated with the bliss arising from it."],"searchText":"152 निष्कारणा • निर्गतं कारणं यस्याः सा। कारणं — cause निष्कारणा — she who is without cause निष्कारणा means one who is without cause. śrīdevī herself is the root cause of everything, and therefore she has no cause for herself. she is the cause and chief of all causes, with no creator and no superior. the name can also be connected with the causal principle used in worship. when śrīdevī is installed in śrīcakra, she is contemplated as the form of causal bliss. she is complete in that causal reality and is associated with the bliss arising from it. the causeless first cause: in the chain of cause and effect, every object is the effect of a prior cause. she is niṣkāraṇā because she sits at the very start of the chain—the uncaused cause (anādi). having no creator or parent before her, she is the independent source from which all secondary causes draw their power.","esoteric":["The Causeless First Cause: In the chain of cause and effect, every object is the effect of a prior cause. She is Niṣkāraṇā because She sits at the very start of the chain—the Uncaused Cause (Anādi). Having no creator or parent before Her, She is the independent source from which all secondary causes draw their power."]},{"number":153,"name":"निष्कलङ्का","samasa":["• निर्गताः कलङ्काः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","कलङ्काः — stains","निष्कलङ्का — She who is without stain"],"summary":["निष्कलङ्का means one who is not connected with any stain caused by sin. Sin cannot approach Śrīdevī, and therefore She is Niṣkalaṅkā. She is pure and untouched by sin. The name indicates absolute stainlessness and freedom from all blemish."],"searchText":"153 निष्कलङ्का • निर्गताः कलङ्काः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent कलङ्काः — stains निष्कलङ्का — she who is without stain निष्कलङ्का means one who is not connected with any stain caused by sin. sin cannot approach śrīdevī, and therefore she is niṣkalaṅkā. she is pure and untouched by sin. the name indicates absolute stainlessness and freedom from all blemish. the flawless mirror: kalaṅka represents a dark spot or moral blemish. while cosmic bodies like the moon hold structural spots, her sun of awareness is niṣkalaṅkā—a flawless, brilliant field of absolute clarity that contains no shadows or dark impressions.","esoteric":["The Flawless Mirror: Kalaṅka represents a dark spot or moral blemish. While cosmic bodies like the moon hold structural spots, Her sun of awareness is Niṣkalaṅkā—a flawless, brilliant field of absolute clarity that contains no shadows or dark impressions."]},{"number":154,"name":"निरुपाधिः","samasa":["• निर्गताः उपाधयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","उपाधयः — limiting adjuncts","निरुपाधिः — She who is without limiting adjuncts"],"summary":["निरुपाधिः means one who has no limitations. Upādhi is a limiting adjunct that makes something appear to have another character, as a crystal liṅga appears red when a hibiscus flower is placed near it. Similarly, ignorance creates differentiation in the mind and acts as a limitation. Śrīdevī is pure caitanya and has no limitation caused by ignorance. Upādhi may be complete or partial; She is free from both. Therefore She is Nirupādhiḥ."],"searchText":"154 निरुपाधिः • निर्गताः उपाधयः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent उपाधयः — limiting adjuncts निरुपाधिः — she who is without limiting adjuncts निरुपाधिः means one who has no limitations. upādhi is a limiting adjunct that makes something appear to have another character, as a crystal liṅga appears red when a hibiscus flower is placed near it. similarly, ignorance creates differentiation in the mind and acts as a limitation. śrīdevī is pure caitanya and has no limitation caused by ignorance. upādhi may be complete or partial; she is free from both. therefore she is nirupādhiḥ. the unconditioned absolute: an upādhi is a limiting condition that projects a false identity upon an object (like a red flower placed near a clear crystal makes the crystal look red). human identity is bound by upādhis like body, mind, and intellect. she is nirupādhiḥ because her core consciousness remains perfectly unconditioned and free from false colorings, existing in absolute autonomy.","esoteric":["The Unconditioned Absolute: An upādhi is a limiting condition that projects a false identity upon an object (like a red flower placed near a clear crystal makes the crystal look red). Human identity is bound by upādhis like body, mind, and intellect. She is Nirupādhiḥ because Her core consciousness remains perfectly unconditioned and free from false colorings, existing in absolute autonomy."]},{"number":155,"name":"निरीश्वरा","samasa":["• निर्गतः ईश्वरः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone out; absent","ईश्वरः — lord","निरीश्वरा — She who has no superior Lord"],"summary":["निरीश्वरा means one who has no superior or protector. She is the head of everything, so there is no one above Her. The name also relates to views that speak of reality with or without Īśvara; She includes and transcends both standpoints. Since She is supreme, independent and without any higher ruler, She is Nirīśvarā."],"searchText":"155 निरीश्वरा • निर्गतः ईश्वरः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone out; absent ईश्वरः — lord निरीश्वरा — she who has no superior lord निरीश्वरा means one who has no superior or protector. she is the head of everything, so there is no one above her. the name also relates to views that speak of reality with or without īśvara; she includes and transcends both standpoints. since she is supreme, independent and without any higher ruler, she is nirīśvarā. the supreme autonomy: this is a bold declaration of her absolute supremacy. in the hierarchy of cosmic powers, there is no master or controller sitting above her command post. she is the ultimate, independent authority (parameśvarī), ruling by the law of her own spontaneous will (svātantrya).","esoteric":["The Supreme Autonomy: This is a bold declaration of Her absolute supremacy. In the hierarchy of cosmic powers, there is no master or controller sitting above Her command post. She is the ultimate, independent authority (Parameśvarī), ruling by the law of Her own spontaneous will (Svātantrya)."]},{"number":156,"name":"नीरागा","samasa":["• निर्गताः रागाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone out; absent","रागाः — attachments; passions","नीरागा — She who is free from attachment"],"summary":["नीरागा means one who has no desires. From this point the teaching rejects the idea that the movements of mind, intellect, volition and ego belong to the Self. Desire, wrath, greed, delusion, pride and envy are impediments to be overcome by renunciation. One who mistakes these enemies as qualities of the soul is destroyed by following them; one who understands them as actions of the mind can control them or remain apart from them. Since Śrīdevī has already attained all that can be desired, She has no longing. She is beyond rāga and has no object of craving. Nīra also means water and aga means mountain; She is in both forms."],"searchText":"156 नीरागा • निर्गताः रागाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone out; absent रागाः — attachments; passions नीरागा — she who is free from attachment नीरागा means one who has no desires. from this point the teaching rejects the idea that the movements of mind, intellect, volition and ego belong to the self. desire, wrath, greed, delusion, pride and envy are impediments to be overcome by renunciation. one who mistakes these enemies as qualities of the soul is destroyed by following them; one who understands them as actions of the mind can control them or remain apart from them. since śrīdevī has already attained all that can be desired, she has no longing. she is beyond rāga and has no object of craving. nīra also means water and aga means mountain; she is in both forms. the quietude of the self: rāga represents the mental stickiness that binds the soul to objects. she is nīrāgā because she requires nothing outside of herself to experience joy, resting permanently in the calm, uncolored clarity of pure, non-dual subjectivity.","esoteric":["The Quietude of the Self: Rāga represents the mental stickiness that binds the soul to objects. She is Nīrāgā because She requires nothing outside of Herself to experience joy, resting permanently in the calm, uncolored clarity of pure, non-dual subjectivity."]},{"number":157,"name":"रागमथनी","samasa":["• रागं मथ्नातीति।"],"wordByWord":["रागं — attachment; passion","रागमथनी — She who destroys attachment"],"summary":["रागमथनी means one who churns and destroys attachment. She completely removes the desires and longings of Her devotees and gives them spiritual zeal. Just as churning brings out what is hidden in curd so that butter may be separated, She churns the mind of devotees and draws out serious desires. Rāga includes desire, aversion and strong attachment; She removes these from the heart."],"searchText":"157 रागमथनी • रागं मथ्नातीति। रागं — attachment; passion रागमथनी — she who destroys attachment रागमथनी means one who churns and destroys attachment. she completely removes the desires and longings of her devotees and gives them spiritual zeal. just as churning brings out what is hidden in curd so that butter may be separated, she churns the mind of devotees and draws out serious desires. rāga includes desire, aversion and strong attachment; she removes these from the heart. the destroyer of bondage: churning (mathana) requires applied force to break down a substance. she acts as rāgamathanī because her grace forcefully breaks down the sticky, binding attachments within the seeker's mind, freeing them from emotional dependence on worldly objects.","esoteric":["The Destroyer of Bondage: Churning (mathana) requires applied force to break down a substance. She acts as Rāgamathanī because Her grace forcefully breaks down the sticky, binding attachments within the seeker's mind, freeing them from emotional dependence on worldly objects."]},{"number":158,"name":"निर्मदा","samasa":["• निर्गतः मदः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone out; absent","मदः — pride","निर्मदा — She who is free from pride"],"summary":["निर्मदा means one who is without pride. Pride is the thought that one possesses something others do not, or has achieved something others could not, and then publicising it. Since Śrīdevī is not an object seen by others in this way, pride does not arise in Her. Though She may elsewhere be praised as supremely proud, there is no contradiction, because Brahman is described through seemingly opposite qualities: smaller than the smallest and greater than the greatest. Here the name teaches freedom from ordinary egoistic pride."],"searchText":"158 निर्मदा • निर्गतः मदः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone out; absent मदः — pride निर्मदा — she who is free from pride निर्मदा means one who is without pride. pride is the thought that one possesses something others do not, or has achieved something others could not, and then publicising it. since śrīdevī is not an object seen by others in this way, pride does not arise in her. though she may elsewhere be praised as supremely proud, there is no contradiction, because brahman is described through seemingly opposite qualities: smaller than the smallest and greater than the greatest. here the name teaches freedom from ordinary egoistic pride. the humility of the whole: pride (mada) arises when an individual compares themselves to others and feels superior. because she is the non-dual whole, there is no separate entity alongside her to compare herself against. she stands free from pride, resting in absolute, natural equilibrium.","esoteric":["The Humility of the Whole: Pride (mada) arises when an individual compares themselves to others and feels superior. Because She is the non-dual whole, there is no separate entity alongside Her to compare Herself against. She stands free from pride, resting in absolute, natural equilibrium."]},{"number":159,"name":"मदनाशिनी","samasa":["• मदं नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["मदं — pride","मदनाशिनी — She who destroys pride"],"summary":["मदनाशिनी means one who destroys pride. mada is pride, intoxication or arrogance, and She removes it from devotees. It may also be split as madana, the flower of the thorn-apple, and aśinī, one who eats; the flower dear to Parameśvara is also dear to Śrīdevī, because there is no difference between them. As alchemy transforms ordinary metal into gold, Her grace raises an ordinary devotee to a higher state. madana can also mean acute anxiety; She destroys that also."],"searchText":"159 मदनाशिनी • मदं नाशयतीति। मदं — pride मदनाशिनी — she who destroys pride मदनाशिनी means one who destroys pride. mada is pride, intoxication or arrogance, and she removes it from devotees. it may also be split as madana, the flower of the thorn-apple, and aśinī, one who eats; the flower dear to parameśvara is also dear to śrīdevī, because there is no difference between them. as alchemy transforms ordinary metal into gold, her grace raises an ordinary devotee to a higher state. madana can also mean acute anxiety; she destroys that also. the leveler of the ego: arrogance blocks spiritual evolution by freezing the intellect. she is madanāśinī because her presence acts as a powerful leveler that systematically dissolves the seeker's ego-driven pride, restoring the mental fluidity and humility needed to receive higher wisdom.","esoteric":["The Leveler of the Ego: Arrogance blocks spiritual evolution by freezing the intellect. She is Madanāśinī because Her presence acts as a powerful leveler that systematically dissolves the seeker's ego-driven pride, restoring the mental fluidity and humility needed to receive higher wisdom."]},{"number":160,"name":"निश्चिन्ता","samasa":["• निर्गता चिन्ता यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गता — gone away; absent","चिन्ता — anxiety; worry","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निश्चिन्ता — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गता चिन्ता यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निश्चिन्ता means one who is free from all anxieties. Cintā means recollection of thoughts, and especially painful recollection that becomes worry. Anxiety is compared to a funeral pyre: the pyre burns a dead body, while anxiety burns the living person. Cintā can also mean delusion or being cheated. Śrīdevī has no delusion and no painful mental agitation, and therefore She is Niścintā."],"searchText":"160 निश्चिन्ता • निर्गता चिन्ता यस्याः सा। निर्गता — gone away; absent चिन्ता — anxiety; worry यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निश्चिन्ता — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गता चिन्ता यस्याः सा। निश्चिन्ता means one who is free from all anxieties. cintā means recollection of thoughts, and especially painful recollection that becomes worry. anxiety is compared to a funeral pyre: the pyre burns a dead body, while anxiety burns the living person. cintā can also mean delusion or being cheated. śrīdevī has no delusion and no painful mental agitation, and therefore she is niścintā. the serene confidence of truth: worry (cintā) is a product of uncertainty and fear of the future. because she holds complete command over past, present, and future, there is no unpredictable event that could cause her anxiety. she remains perfectly relaxed in the quiet certainty of her absolute rule.","esoteric":["The Serene Confidence of Truth: Worry (cintā) is a product of uncertainty and fear of the future. Because She holds complete command over past, present, and future, there is no unpredictable event that could cause Her anxiety. She remains perfectly relaxed in the quiet certainty of Her absolute rule."]},{"number":161,"name":"निरहङ्कारा","samasa":["• निर्गतः अहङ्कारः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","अहङ्कारः — ego; self-sense","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निरहङ्कारा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः अहङ्कारः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निरहङ्कारा means one who is without ego. Ego is of three kinds: vaikārika, taijasa and bhūtādi, connected respectively with sattva, rajas and tamas. Since Śrīdevī is beyond the three guṇas, She has no ego related to any of them. She is pure consciousness and is not limited by the thought of individuality. Therefore She is Nirahaṅkārā."],"searchText":"161 निरहङ्कारा • निर्गतः अहङ्कारः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent अहङ्कारः — ego; self-sense यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निरहङ्कारा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः अहङ्कारः यस्याः सा। निरहङ्कारा means one who is without ego. ego is of three kinds: vaikārika, taijasa and bhūtādi, connected respectively with sattva, rajas and tamas. since śrīdevī is beyond the three guṇas, she has no ego related to any of them. she is pure consciousness and is not limited by the thought of individuality. therefore she is nirahaṅkārā. the universal i-consciousness: ahaṅkāra is the psychological faculty that draws a boundary line saying \"i am this limited body, and not that.\" she is nirahaṅkārā because she has no limited boundary line. her i-identity is पूर्णाहन्ता(pūrṇāhaṃtā — the infinite, universal i-consciousness) that encompasses all existence without exclusion.","esoteric":["The Universal I-Consciousness: Ahaṅkāra is the psychological faculty that draws a boundary line saying \"I am this limited body, and not that.\" She is Nirahaṅkārā because She has no limited boundary line. Her I-identity is पूर्णाहन्ता(Pūrṇāhaṃtā — the infinite, universal I-consciousness) that encompasses all existence without exclusion."]},{"number":162,"name":"निर्मोहा","samasa":["• निर्गताः मोहाः यस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","यस्याः — of whom; whose","निर्मोहा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः मोहाः यस्याः।"],"summary":["निर्मोहा means one who is free from bewilderment. moha is confusion, fascination, perplexity, wavering of mind, or mistaking one thing for another. Śrīdevī is beyond all such confusion. Her nature is clear knowledge, untouched by mental distraction."],"searchText":"162 निर्मोहा • निर्गताः मोहाः यस्याः। निर्गताः — gone away; absent यस्याः — of whom; whose निर्मोहा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः मोहाः यस्याः। निर्मोहा means one who is free from bewilderment. moha is confusion, fascination, perplexity, wavering of mind, or mistaking one thing for another. śrīdevī is beyond all such confusion. her nature is clear knowledge, untouched by mental distraction. the flawless clarity: delusion (moha) occurs when the mind mistakes the transient temporary world for the permanent reality. being the foundational truth itself, she is permanently free from confusion, radiating flawless clarity that cuts through the illusions of the world.","esoteric":["The Flawless Clarity: Delusion (moha) occurs when the mind mistakes the transient temporary world for the permanent reality. Being the foundational truth itself, She is permanently free from confusion, radiating flawless clarity that cuts through the illusions of the world."]},{"number":163,"name":"मोहनाशिनी","samasa":["• मोहं नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["नाशयतीति — destroys","मोहनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: मोहं नाशयतीति।"],"summary":["मोहनाशिनी means one who dispels all illusion. By imparting the knowledge of unity to Her devotees, She destroys bewilderment. For one who perceives oneness, there is no delusion and no sorrow. Thus She removes moha by revealing the truth of non-difference."],"searchText":"163 मोहनाशिनी • मोहं नाशयतीति। नाशयतीति — destroys मोहनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: मोहं नाशयतीति। मोहनाशिनी means one who dispels all illusion. by imparting the knowledge of unity to her devotees, she destroys bewilderment. for one who perceives oneness, there is no delusion and no sorrow. thus she removes moha by revealing the truth of non-difference. the dispeller of illusion: she acts as mohanāśinī because her grace acts like a bright light brought into a dark room. she instantly shatters the deep-seated delusions that keep the seeker bound to material attachments, illuminating the true nature of the eternal self.","esoteric":["The Dispeller of Illusion: She acts as Mohanāśinī because Her grace acts like a bright light brought into a dark room. She instantly shatters the deep-seated delusions that keep the seeker bound to material attachments, illuminating the true nature of the eternal Self."]},{"number":164,"name":"निर्ममा","samasa":["• निर्गतः ममत्वं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","ममत्वं — sense of mine-ness","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निर्ममा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः ममत्वं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निर्ममा means one who has no sense of mine. Self-interest implies separating things and thinking, “this is mine.” Since Śrīdevī is everything, there is no room in Her for such possessive thought. Therefore She is free from mamakāra, the notion of mine."],"searchText":"164 निर्ममा • निर्गतः ममत्वं यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent ममत्वं — sense of mine-ness यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निर्ममा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः ममत्वं यस्याः सा। निर्ममा means one who has no sense of mine. self-interest implies separating things and thinking, “this is mine.” since śrīdevī is everything, there is no room in her for such possessive thought. therefore she is free from mamakāra, the notion of mine. the freedom from ownership: possessiveness (mamatā) is the secondary branch of the ego that seeks to grab and control objects. because the entire universe belongs to her as her own expansion, she has no need to possess things in a limited way. she stands free from ownership, giving her grace unconditionally to all.","esoteric":["The Freedom from Ownership: Possessiveness (mamatā) is the secondary branch of the ego that seeks to grab and control objects. Because the entire universe belongs to Her as Her own expansion, She has no need to possess things in a limited way. She stands free from ownership, giving Her grace unconditionally to all."]},{"number":165,"name":"ममताहन्त्री","samasa":["• ममतायाः हन्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["हन्त्री — destroyer","ममताहन्त्री — meaning follows from the samasa: ममतायाः हन्त्री।"],"summary":["ममताहन्त्री means one who destroys the sense of mine. She removes the self-conceit by which a person clings to possessions and relationships as “mine.” The request of the Vaiśya in the Devī tradition shows the desire to be freed from “I” and “mine.” Śrīdevī destroys this possessiveness and turns the mind toward knowledge."],"searchText":"165 ममताहन्त्री • ममतायाः हन्त्री। हन्त्री — destroyer ममताहन्त्री — meaning follows from the samasa: ममतायाः हन्त्री। ममताहन्त्री means one who destroys the sense of mine. she removes the self-conceit by which a person clings to possessions and relationships as “mine.” the request of the vaiśya in the devī tradition shows the desire to be freed from “i” and “mine.” śrīdevī destroys this possessiveness and turns the mind toward knowledge. severing the ties of ownership: the sense of \"mine\" creates intense mental bondage and fear of loss. she is mamatāhantrī because she systematically cuts the tight cords of possessiveness in the seeker's heart, teaching them to see all things as passing expressions of the divine rather than personal property.","esoteric":["Severing the Ties of Ownership: The sense of \"mine\" creates intense mental bondage and fear of loss. She is Mamatāhantrī because She systematically cuts the tight cords of possessiveness in the seeker's heart, teaching them to see all things as passing expressions of the divine rather than personal property."]},{"number":166,"name":"निष्पापा","samasa":["• निर्गताः पापाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","पापाः — sins","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निष्पापा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः पापाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निष्पापा means one who is without sin. Sin and merit are created by deeds, which arise mainly from desires and actions. Since She is free from desire and has no binding action, She has neither sin nor merit. She is untouched by karma and has no longing for its fruits. Therefore She is Niṣpāpā."],"searchText":"166 निष्पापा • निर्गताः पापाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent पापाः — sins यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निष्पापा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः पापाः यस्याः सा। निष्पापा means one who is without sin. sin and merit are created by deeds, which arise mainly from desires and actions. since she is free from desire and has no binding action, she has neither sin nor merit. she is untouched by karma and has no longing for its fruits. therefore she is niṣpāpā. the field of absolute good: pāpa (sin) is an action born from ignorance and selfishness that generates negative mental impressions. because her nature is pure, non-dual light and unconditional love, there is no room for selfish distortion within her. she is pure goodness personified.","esoteric":["The Field of Absolute Good: Pāpa (sin) is an action born from ignorance and selfishness that generates negative mental impressions. Because Her nature is pure, non-dual light and unconditional love, there is no room for selfish distortion within Her. She is pure goodness personified."]},{"number":167,"name":"पापनाशिनी","samasa":["• पापान् नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["नाशयतीति — destroys","पापनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: पापान् नाशयतीति।"],"summary":["पापनाशिनी means one who destroys the sins of devotees. By repetition of Her mantra, worship, meditation and remembrance, She burns away the sins of devotees. Just as the tip of a reed is consumed in fire, sins are destroyed through Her grace. Her mantra and remembrance purify the devotee and remove accumulated wrongdoing."],"searchText":"167 पापनाशिनी • पापान् नाशयतीति। नाशयतीति — destroys पापनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: पापान् नाशयतीति। पापनाशिनी means one who destroys the sins of devotees. by repetition of her mantra, worship, meditation and remembrance, she burns away the sins of devotees. just as the tip of a reed is consumed in fire, sins are destroyed through her grace. her mantra and remembrance purify the devotee and remove accumulated wrongdoing. the fire of purification: past sins create deep karmic impressions (vāsanās) that weigh down the mind. she acts as pāpanāśinī because her grace acts like a roaring fire that instantly burns away the heaviest accumulations of past demerits, lightened the seeker's mental path.","esoteric":["The Fire of Purification: Past sins create deep karmic impressions (vāsanās) that weigh down the mind. She acts as Pāpanāśinī because Her grace acts like a roaring fire that instantly burns away the heaviest accumulations of past demerits, lightened the seeker's mental path."]},{"number":168,"name":"निष्क्रोधा","samasa":["• निर्गताः क्रोधाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","क्रोधाः — anger","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निष्क्रोधा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः क्रोधाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निष्क्रोधा means one who is without anger. She has no hatred toward anyone and does not become angry. Even when the Lord destroys the wicked for the protection of devotees, there is no hatred in that act. Destruction of evil is done with compassion, for correction and liberation. Śrīdevī is therefore free from anger, even while protecting the good and subduing the harmful."],"searchText":"168 निष्क्रोधा • निर्गताः क्रोधाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent क्रोधाः — anger यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निष्क्रोधा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः क्रोधाः यस्याः सा। निष्क्रोधा means one who is without anger. she has no hatred toward anyone and does not become angry. even when the lord destroys the wicked for the protection of devotees, there is no hatred in that act. destruction of evil is done with compassion, for correction and liberation. śrīdevī is therefore free from anger, even while protecting the good and subduing the harmful. the equanimity of the whole: anger arises when an external obstacle blocks an entity's desire. because there is nothing outside of her to oppose her will, anger can never rise within her nature. she remains perfectly balanced in universal equanimity.","esoteric":["The Equanimity of the Whole: Anger arises when an external obstacle blocks an entity's desire. Because there is nothing outside of Her to oppose Her will, anger can never rise within Her nature. She remains perfectly balanced in universal equanimity."]},{"number":169,"name":"क्रोधशमनी","samasa":["• क्रोधं शमयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["शमयतीति — pacifies; ends","क्रोधशमनी — meaning follows from the samasa: क्रोधं शमयतीति।"],"summary":["क्रोधशमनी means one who quiets anger. Every human being has inner enemies such as lust, anger, greed, delusion, pride and envy. Śrīdevī suppresses the anger of devotees and destroys lust in them. Anger destroys the fruit of sacrifice, offering and worship, just as water kept in an unbaked clay pot is lost. Anger leads to delusion, loss of memory, destruction of discrimination and ruin. She removes this destructive anger and protects the devotee’s inner discipline."],"searchText":"169 क्रोधशमनी • क्रोधं शमयतीति। शमयतीति — pacifies; ends क्रोधशमनी — meaning follows from the samasa: क्रोधं शमयतीति। क्रोधशमनी means one who quiets anger. every human being has inner enemies such as lust, anger, greed, delusion, pride and envy. śrīdevī suppresses the anger of devotees and destroys lust in them. anger destroys the fruit of sacrifice, offering and worship, just as water kept in an unbaked clay pot is lost. anger leads to delusion, loss of memory, destruction of discrimination and ruin. she removes this destructive anger and protects the devotee’s inner discipline. the cooling wave: anger burns up mental peace and clouds judgment. she acts as krodhaśamanī because her grace brings a powerful, cooling wave of peace that instantly puts out the flames of anger in the seeker's heart, replacing them with patience and understanding.","esoteric":["The Cooling Wave: Anger burns up mental peace and clouds judgment. She acts as Krodhaśamanī because Her grace brings a powerful, cooling wave of peace that instantly puts out the flames of anger in the seeker's heart, replacing them with patience and understanding."]},{"number":170,"name":"निर्लोभा","samasa":["• निर्गताः लोभाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","लोभाः — greed","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निर्लोभा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः लोभाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निर्लोभा means one who is free from greed. She is exceedingly liberal and therefore has no covetousness. Since She gives freely and lacks any desire to possess, She is Nirlobhā."],"searchText":"170 निर्लोभा • निर्गताः लोभाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent लोभाः — greed यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निर्लोभा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः लोभाः यस्याः सा। निर्लोभा means one who is free from greed. she is exceedingly liberal and therefore has no covetousness. since she gives freely and lacks any desire to possess, she is nirlobhā. the satisfied source: greed (lobha) is the constant urge to accumulate more, driven by a deep feeling of lack. being the inexhaustible source of all abundance, she can never experience lack. she remains perfectly resting in the satisfaction of her own fullness.","esoteric":["The Satisfied Source: Greed (lobha) is the constant urge to accumulate more, driven by a deep feeling of lack. Being the inexhaustible source of all abundance, She can never experience lack. She remains perfectly resting in the satisfaction of Her own fullness."]},{"number":171,"name":"लोभनाशिनी","samasa":["• लोभं नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["नाशयतीति — destroys","लोभनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: लोभं नाशयतीति।"],"summary":["लोभनाशिनी means one who destroys greed. Greed destroys all other good qualities, so it must be destroyed first. Śrīdevī destroys greed in the minds of Her devotees."],"searchText":"171 लोभनाशिनी • लोभं नाशयतीति। नाशयतीति — destroys लोभनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: लोभं नाशयतीति। लोभनाशिनी means one who destroys greed. greed destroys all other good qualities, so it must be destroyed first. śrīdevī destroys greed in the minds of her devotees. breaking the grip of avarice: greed keeps the mind running outward after material possessions. she is lobhanāśinī because her grace breaks this outward grip, helping the seeker realize that true wealth lies within the peace of their own consciousness.","esoteric":["Breaking the Grip of Avarice: Greed keeps the mind running outward after material possessions. She is Lobhanāśinī because Her grace breaks this outward grip, helping the seeker realize that true wealth lies within the peace of their own consciousness."]},{"number":172,"name":"निःसंशया","samasa":["• निर्गताः संशयाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","संशयाः — doubts","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निःसंशया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः संशयाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निःसंशया means one who is without doubt. Doubt is a state of mind that wavers between two alternatives. Since She is knowledge itself, such doubt is absent in Her."],"searchText":"172 निःसंशया • निर्गताः संशयाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent संशयाः — doubts यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निःसंशया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः संशयाः यस्याः सा। निःसंशया means one who is without doubt. doubt is a state of mind that wavers between two alternatives. since she is knowledge itself, such doubt is absent in her. the absolute certainty: doubt (saṃśaya) arises when the intellect cannot choose between conflicting ideas. because she is supreme, all-knowing clarity, she rests in absolute certainty, guiding seekers with an unyielding compass of truth.","esoteric":["The Absolute Certainty: Doubt (saṃśaya) arises when the intellect cannot choose between conflicting ideas. Because She is supreme, all-knowing clarity, She rests in absolute certainty, guiding seekers with an unyielding compass of truth."]},{"number":173,"name":"संशयघ्नी","samasa":["• संशयान् हन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["संशयघ्नी — meaning follows from the samasa: संशयान् हन्तीति।"],"summary":["संशयघ्नी means one who destroys doubt. Śrīdevī is in the form of the teacher and has the qualities of a true guru. A devotee should cultivate integrated contemplation of the self, mantra, goddess, yantra and teacher; this is the fivefold anusandhāna. A teacher must be free from doubt, able to teach the principles fully, clear the doubts of students, and remain without expectation or interest in wealth. Since Śrīdevī is the teacher, She has no doubts and removes all doubts of devotees."],"searchText":"173 संशयघ्नी • संशयान् हन्तीति। संशयघ्नी — meaning follows from the samasa: संशयान् हन्तीति। संशयघ्नी means one who destroys doubt. śrīdevī is in the form of the teacher and has the qualities of a true guru. a devotee should cultivate integrated contemplation of the self, mantra, goddess, yantra and teacher; this is the fivefold anusandhāna. a teacher must be free from doubt, able to teach the principles fully, clear the doubts of students, and remain without expectation or interest in wealth. since śrīdevī is the teacher, she has no doubts and removes all doubts of devotees. the sword of direct experience: doubt paralyzes spiritual action. she is saṃśayaghnī because her grace provides the seeker with direct, intuitive flashes of inner experience, cutting through intellectual doubts and establishing steady faith.","esoteric":["The Sword of Direct Experience: Doubt paralyzes spiritual action. She is Saṃśayaghnī because Her grace provides the seeker with direct, intuitive flashes of inner experience, cutting through intellectual doubts and establishing steady faith."]},{"number":174,"name":"निर्भवा","samasa":["• निर्गतः भवः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","भवः — worldly existence; becoming","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निर्भवा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः भवः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निर्भवा means one who is without origin. The Supreme Brahman is without beginning, and Śrīdevī is that beginningless reality. She is not produced by anything and has no prior cause."],"searchText":"174 निर्भवा • निर्गतः भवः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent भवः — worldly existence; becoming यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निर्भवा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः भवः यस्याः सा। निर्भवा means one who is without origin. the supreme brahman is without beginning, and śrīdevī is that beginningless reality. she is not produced by anything and has no prior cause. the unborn substrate: bhava is the continuous spinning of the wheel of transmigratory existence. she is nirbhavā because she stands entirely outside the wheel as its uncreated coordinator, completely unaffected by the movements of birth and death.","esoteric":["The Unborn Substrate: bhava is the continuous spinning of the wheel of transmigratory existence. She is Nirbhavā because She stands entirely outside the wheel as its uncreated coordinator, completely unaffected by the movements of birth and death."]},{"number":175,"name":"भवनाशिनी","samasa":["• भवं नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["नाशयतीति — destroys","भवनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भवं नाशयतीति।"],"summary":["भवनाशिनी means one who destroys worldly bondage. She lifts devotees out of the ocean of saṃsāra and removes the heat of worldly suffering. She grants the state beyond repeated birth and death. The name may also be understood as connected with a sacred river called Bhavanāśinī, whose form is identified with Her."],"searchText":"175 भवनाशिनी • भवं नाशयतीति। नाशयतीति — destroys भवनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भवं नाशयतीति। भवनाशिनी means one who destroys worldly bondage. she lifts devotees out of the ocean of saṃsāra and removes the heat of worldly suffering. she grants the state beyond repeated birth and death. the name may also be understood as connected with a sacred river called bhavanāśinī, whose form is identified with her. the grantor of liberation: the ultimate goal of spiritual practice is to escape the binding wheel of saṃsāra. she acts as bhavanāśinī because her grace provides the final illumination that breaks the wheel, liberating the seeker into eternal freedom.","esoteric":["The Grantor of Liberation: The ultimate goal of spiritual practice is to escape the binding wheel of saṃsāra. She acts as Bhavanāśinī because Her grace provides the final illumination that breaks the wheel, liberating the seeker into eternal freedom."]},{"number":176,"name":"निर्विकल्पा","samasa":["• निर्गताः विकल्पाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","विकल्पाः — mental alternatives; conceptual distinctions","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निर्विकल्पा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः विकल्पाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निर्विकल्पा means one who is without vikalpa, the notion produced by mere words without corresponding reality. vikalpa is an imagined idea, such as the horns of a rabbit or a horse. Śrīdevī is unconditioned eternal knowledge and is free from such mental constructions. Nirvikalpā also indicates the final stage of meditation, where no specific distinctions remain. Since everything is inseparable from Her, no theory or object stands opposed to Her. She is devoid of separateness, and all things are integrated in Her."],"searchText":"176 निर्विकल्पा • निर्गताः विकल्पाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent विकल्पाः — mental alternatives; conceptual distinctions यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निर्विकल्पा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः विकल्पाः यस्याः सा। निर्विकल्पा means one who is without vikalpa, the notion produced by mere words without corresponding reality. vikalpa is an imagined idea, such as the horns of a rabbit or a horse. śrīdevī is unconditioned eternal knowledge and is free from such mental constructions. nirvikalpā also indicates the final stage of meditation, where no specific distinctions remain. since everything is inseparable from her, no theory or object stands opposed to her. she is devoid of separateness, and all things are integrated in her. the state of direct realization: vikalpa is the movement of the mind among alternatives. she is nirvikalpā because she is unified, choice-less awareness prior to mental concepts, the steady state of nirvikalpa samādhi.","esoteric":["The State of Direct Realization: vikalpa is the movement of the mind among alternatives. She is Nirvikalpā because She is unified, choice-less awareness prior to mental concepts, the steady state of nirvikalpa samādhi."]},{"number":177,"name":"निराबाधा","samasa":["• निर्गतः बाधः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","बाधः — obstruction; affliction","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निराबाधा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः बाधः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निराबाधा means one whose mind is undisturbed. The mind is disturbed when it mistakes a shell for silver; that disturbance ends when the illusion vanishes. Since there is no object other than Śrīdevī, She has no such disturbance in mind."],"searchText":"177 निराबाधा • निर्गतः बाधः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent बाधः — obstruction; affliction यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निराबाधा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः बाधः यस्याः सा। निराबाधा means one whose mind is undisturbed. the mind is disturbed when it mistakes a shell for silver; that disturbance ends when the illusion vanishes. since there is no object other than śrīdevī, she has no such disturbance in mind. the absolute reality: in philosophy, a statement is bādhita if it is contradicted and proven false by a higher truth. she is nirābādhā because she is the ultimate truth that can never be negated, contradicted, or eclipsed by any higher reality.","esoteric":["The Absolute Reality: In philosophy, a statement is bādhita if it is contradicted and proven false by a higher truth. She is Nirābādhā because She is the ultimate truth that can never be negated, contradicted, or eclipsed by any higher reality."]},{"number":178,"name":"निर्भेदा","samasa":["• निर्गताः भेदाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","भेदाः — differences","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निर्भेदा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः भेदाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निर्भेदा means one who is without difference. Nothing exists in Her that can create a sense of difference in the mind. She is the supreme Śakti, infinite and free from all difference. The apparent difference between Śakti and the possessor of Śakti is removed by true knowledge; those who contemplate reality recognize non-separateness."],"searchText":"178 निर्भेदा • निर्गताः भेदाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent भेदाः — differences यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निर्भेदा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः भेदाः यस्याः सा। निर्भेदा means one who is without difference. nothing exists in her that can create a sense of difference in the mind. she is the supreme śakti, infinite and free from all difference. the apparent difference between śakti and the possessor of śakti is removed by true knowledge; those who contemplate reality recognize non-separateness. the non-dual whole: bheda represents the dualistic line drawn between self and other, subject and object. she is nirbhedā because her supreme reality is a unified whole of non-dual consciousness (advaita), containing no internal divisions.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Whole: bheda represents the dualistic line drawn between self and other, subject and object. She is Nirbhedā because Her supreme reality is a unified whole of non-dual consciousness (advaita), containing no internal divisions."]},{"number":179,"name":"भेदनाशिनी","samasa":["• भेदान् नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["नाशयतीति — destroys","भेदनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भेदान् नाशयतीति।"],"summary":["भेदनाशिनी means one who destroys the feeling of difference. She removes the sense of separation by creating knowledge of tattva, the true principle. Through that knowledge, the idea of difference is destroyed."],"searchText":"179 भेदनाशिनी • भेदान् नाशयतीति। नाशयतीति — destroys भेदनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भेदान् नाशयतीति। भेदनाशिनी means one who destroys the feeling of difference. she removes the sense of separation by creating knowledge of tattva, the true principle. through that knowledge, the idea of difference is destroyed. the illuminator of unity: the illusion of division (bheda) is the root cause of conflict and suffering. she acts as bhedanāśinī because her grace dissolves these false boundary lines, helping the seeker perceive the underlying unity that connects all life.","esoteric":["The Illuminator of Unity: The illusion of division (bheda) is the root cause of conflict and suffering. She acts as Bhedanāśinī because Her grace dissolves these false boundary lines, helping the seeker perceive the underlying unity that connects all life."]},{"number":180,"name":"निर्नाशा","samasa":["• निर्गतः नाशः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","नाशः — destruction","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निर्नाशा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः नाशः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निर्नाशा means one who is eternal, imperishable and endless. Nāśa means end or destruction, and She is without it. She is Brahman, truth, knowledge and infinity, and therefore She has no destruction."],"searchText":"180 निर्नाशा • निर्गतः नाशः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent नाशः — destruction यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निर्नाशा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः नाशः यस्याः सा। निर्नाशा means one who is eternal, imperishable and endless. nāśa means end or destruction, and she is without it. she is brahman, truth, knowledge and infinity, and therefore she has no destruction. the imperishable substrate: everything born in the material world must eventually face decay and death (nāśa). she is nirnāśā because her consciousness is an uncreated, imperishable reality that witnesses the collapse of cosmic eras while remaining completely untouched.","esoteric":["The Imperishable Substrate: Everything born in the material world must eventually face decay and death (nāśa). She is Nirnāśā because Her consciousness is an uncreated, imperishable reality that witnesses the collapse of cosmic eras while remaining completely untouched."]},{"number":181,"name":"मृत्युमथनी","samasa":["• मृत्युं मथ्नातीति।"],"wordByWord":["मृत्युमथनी — meaning follows from the samasa: मृत्युं मथ्नातीति।"],"summary":["मृत्युमथनी means one who saves devotees from death. As Parameśvara saved Mārkaṇḍeya from the god of death, Śrīdevī also saves Her devotees from death. Death belongs to the body and not to the soul; She makes devotees realize this truth. Like curd churned to obtain butter, She churns the fear of death, creates philosophical knowledge and removes that fear. Through contemplation, the devotee becomes identified with Her and attains the imperishable state."],"searchText":"181 मृत्युमथनी • मृत्युं मथ्नातीति। मृत्युमथनी — meaning follows from the samasa: मृत्युं मथ्नातीति। मृत्युमथनी means one who saves devotees from death. as parameśvara saved mārkaṇḍeya from the god of death, śrīdevī also saves her devotees from death. death belongs to the body and not to the soul; she makes devotees realize this truth. like curd churned to obtain butter, she churns the fear of death, creates philosophical knowledge and removes that fear. through contemplation, the devotee becomes identified with her and attains the imperishable state. the conqueror of death: fear of death binds all mortal beings. she acts as mṛtyumathanī because her grace elevates the seeker's mind to recognize their true, immortal identity as pure awareness, stripping death of its terrifying power.","esoteric":["The Conqueror of Death: Fear of death binds all mortal beings. She acts as Mṛtyumathanī because Her grace elevates the seeker's mind to recognize their true, immortal identity as pure awareness, stripping death of its terrifying power."]},{"number":182,"name":"निष्क्रिया","samasa":["• निर्गताः क्रियाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","क्रियाः — actions","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निष्क्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः क्रियाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निष्क्रिया means one who has no action to perform. Actions are of two kinds, ordained and prohibited, and She is beyond both. Being bodiless in Her supreme nature, She is unaffected by likes and dislikes. Without doing anything and without personal action, She is still the one through whose presence all action takes place."],"searchText":"182 निष्क्रिया • निर्गताः क्रियाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent क्रियाः — actions यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निष्क्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः क्रियाः यस्याः सा। निष्क्रिया means one who has no action to perform. actions are of two kinds, ordained and prohibited, and she is beyond both. being bodiless in her supreme nature, she is unaffected by likes and dislikes. without doing anything and without personal action, she is still the one through whose presence all action takes place. the silent witness: action (kriyā) implies a movement to achieve a goal that is not yet present. in her highest, unmanifest state (parā), she is completely actionless, resting as the quiet substrate that enables the dynamic universe to move.","esoteric":["The Silent Witness: Action (kriyā) implies a movement to achieve a goal that is not yet present. In Her highest, unmanifest state (parā), She is completely actionless, resting as the quiet substrate that enables the dynamic universe to move."]},{"number":183,"name":"निष्परिग्रहा","samasa":["• निर्गताः परिग्रहाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गताः — gone away; absent","परिग्रहाः — possessions; acquisitions","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निष्परिग्रहा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः परिग्रहाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निष्परिग्रहा means one who does not acquire or accept anything as a gift. Parigraha can mean attendants, spouse, gifts or root, and none of these applies to Her. Śrīdevī creates, protects and destroys the whole universe, yet receives nothing as a gift. She has no origin, so She is also without parigraha in the sense of a root or source."],"searchText":"183 निष्परिग्रहा • निर्गताः परिग्रहाः यस्याः सा। निर्गताः — gone away; absent परिग्रहाः — possessions; acquisitions यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निष्परिग्रहा — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गताः परिग्रहाः यस्याः सा। निष्परिग्रहा means one who does not acquire or accept anything as a gift. parigraha can mean attendants, spouse, gifts or root, and none of these applies to her. śrīdevī creates, protects and destroys the whole universe, yet receives nothing as a gift. she has no origin, so she is also without parigraha in the sense of a root or source. the perfect independence: parigraha refers to the anxious grabbing and holding of external things for security. being completely self-contained and perfect (pūrṇā), she requires no external support and stands in absolute independence.","esoteric":["The Perfect Independence: parigraha refers to the anxious grabbing and holding of external things for security. Being completely self-contained and perfect (pūrṇā), She requires no external support and stands in absolute independence."]},{"number":184,"name":"निस्तुला","samasa":["• निर्गतः तुलः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","तुलः — equal; comparison","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निस्तुला — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः तुलः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निस्तुला means one who is incomparable, unequal and peerless. There is nothing with which She can be compared, and therefore She cannot be weighed against anything else. She is without equal, without comparison and beyond all measure."],"searchText":"184 निस्तुला • निर्गतः तुलः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent तुलः — equal; comparison यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निस्तुला — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः तुलः यस्याः सा। निस्तुला means one who is incomparable, unequal and peerless. there is nothing with which she can be compared, and therefore she cannot be weighed against anything else. she is without equal, without comparison and beyond all measure. the incomparable absolute: a comparison requires two separate entities to match against each other. because she is the non-dual whole, there is no second entity that could equal her majesty. she stands completely unique and beyond all measures.","esoteric":["The Incomparable Absolute: A comparison requires two separate entities to match against each other. Because She is the non-dual whole, there is no second entity that could equal Her majesty. She stands completely unique and beyond all measures."]},{"number":185,"name":"नीलचिकुरा","samasa":["• नीलाः चिकुराः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["नीलाः — blue; dark","चिकुराः — locks of hair","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","नीलचिकुरा — meaning follows from the samasa: नीलाः चिकुराः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["नीलचिकुरा means one whose locks of hair are dark blue. The dark-blue hair is part of the description of Her beautiful form."],"searchText":"185 नीलचिकुरा • नीलाः चिकुराः यस्याः सा। नीलाः — blue; dark चिकुराः — locks of hair यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she नीलचिकुरा — meaning follows from the samasa: नीलाः चिकुराः यस्याः सा। नीलचिकुरा means one whose locks of hair are dark blue. the dark-blue hair is part of the description of her beautiful form. dark-blue hair indicates the beauty and radiance of her form.","esoteric":["Dark-blue hair indicates the beauty and radiance of Her form."]},{"number":186,"name":"निरपाया","samasa":["• निर्गतम् अपायं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतम् — gone away; absent","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निरपाया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतम् अपायं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निरपाया means one who is imperishable and free from danger. Apāya means danger, loss or decline. She is completely free from danger and cannot perish."],"searchText":"186 निरपाया • निर्गतम् अपायं यस्याः सा। निर्गतम् — gone away; absent यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निरपाया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतम् अपायं यस्याः सा। निरपाया means one who is imperishable and free from danger. apāya means danger, loss or decline. she is completely free from danger and cannot perish. the flawless security: worldly wealth and positions are constantly threatened by loss and decay (apāya). she is nirapāyā because her spiritual treasure is permanent, serving as an absolute, unshakeable sanctuary of safety.","esoteric":["The Flawless Security: Worldly wealth and positions are constantly threatened by loss and decay (apāya). She is Nirapāyā because Her spiritual treasure is permanent, serving as an absolute, unshakeable sanctuary of safety."]},{"number":187,"name":"निरत्यया","samasa":["• निर्गतः अत्ययः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतः — gone away; absent","अत्ययः — transgression; lapse","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निरत्यया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः अत्ययः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निरत्यया means one who is without transgression. Atyaya means transgression, punishment, obstruction, fault or emaciation. Śrīdevī sets limits for the universe and for those who perform creation, protection and destruction; She Herself never transgresses those limits."],"searchText":"187 निरत्यया • निर्गतः अत्ययः यस्याः सा। निर्गतः — gone away; absent अत्ययः — transgression; lapse यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निरत्यया — meaning follows from the samasa: निर्गतः अत्ययः यस्याः सा। निरत्यया means one who is without transgression. atyaya means transgression, punishment, obstruction, fault or emaciation. śrīdevī sets limits for the universe and for those who perform creation, protection and destruction; she herself never transgresses those limits. the immutable boundary: atyaya means crossing a boundary or passing into decay. she is niratyayā because her cosmic law and absolute being can never be stepped over or broken, existing as the immutable reality.","esoteric":["The Immutable Boundary: atyaya means crossing a boundary or passing into decay. She is Niratyayā because Her cosmic law and absolute being can never be stepped over or broken, existing as the immutable reality."]},{"number":188,"name":"दुर्लभा","samasa":["• दुःखेन लभ्यते इति।"],"wordByWord":["दुःखेन — with difficulty","लभ्यते — is obtained","दुर्लभा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुःखेन लभ्यते इति।"],"summary":["दुर्लभा means one who is difficult to attain, even for yogins. This name begins the description of Her qualified form, saguṇa. She is not easily attained without discipline and fitness."],"searchText":"188 दुर्लभा • दुःखेन लभ्यते इति। दुःखेन — with difficulty लभ्यते — is obtained दुर्लभा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुःखेन लभ्यते इति। दुर्लभा means one who is difficult to attain, even for yogins. this name begins the description of her qualified form, saguṇa. she is not easily attained without discipline and fitness. the filter of sincerity: she is durlabhā because her true, non-dual essence cannot be reached by casual, insincere, or outward-running minds. she requires the purification of the intellect, opening her gates only to genuine seekers.","esoteric":["The Filter of Sincerity: She is Durlabhā because Her true, non-dual essence cannot be reached by casual, insincere, or outward-running minds. She requires the purification of the intellect, opening Her gates only to genuine seekers."]},{"number":189,"name":"दुर्गमा अदुर्गमा","samasa":["• दुःखेन गम्यते इति।","• न विद्यते दुर्गमा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["दुःखेन — with difficulty","गम्यते — is reached","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","दुर्गमा अदुर्गमा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुःखेन गम्यते इति।"],"summary":["दुर्गमा अदुर्गमा means one who is hard to approach, and also one who is easily approachable. Even yogins cannot approach Her easily through achievements alone. Her path of devotion must be followed with concentration and control, like walking on the edge of a knife. When read as Adurgamā, the name means one who is easily approachable, and also one who killed the demon Durgama."],"searchText":"189 दुर्गमा अदुर्गमा • दुःखेन गम्यते इति। • न विद्यते दुर्गमा यस्याः सा। दुःखेन — with difficulty गम्यते — is reached यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she दुर्गमा अदुर्गमा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुःखेन गम्यते इति। दुर्गमा अदुर्गमा means one who is hard to approach, and also one who is easily approachable. even yogins cannot approach her easily through achievements alone. her path of devotion must be followed with concentration and control, like walking on the edge of a knife. when read as adurgamā, the name means one who is easily approachable, and also one who killed the demon durgama. the hidden path: she is durgamā because the internal path of the suṣumṇā is highly complex and guarded by inner knots. as adurgamā, once her grace is invoked, the barriers dissolve and the path becomes direct and easy.","esoteric":["The Hidden Path: She is Durgamā because the internal path of the suṣumṇā is highly complex and guarded by inner knots. As Adurgamā, once Her grace is invoked, the barriers dissolve and the path becomes direct and easy."]},{"number":190,"name":"दुर्गा","samasa":["• दुर्गा नाम्ना प्रसिद्धा।"],"wordByWord":["दुर्गा — Durga; the invincible goddess","दुर्गा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुर्गा नाम्ना प्रसिद्धा।"],"summary":["दुर्गा means one who is known as Durgā. As indicated in the previous name, She is Durgā because She killed the demon Durgama. She protects Indra and the other devas from fear and battle. She is also worshipped as the goddess who rescues devotees from difficulty, and as the nine-year-old form in kumārī worship."],"searchText":"190 दुर्गा • दुर्गा नाम्ना प्रसिद्धा। दुर्गा — durga; the invincible goddess दुर्गा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुर्गा नाम्ना प्रसिद्धा। दुर्गा means one who is known as durgā. as indicated in the previous name, she is durgā because she killed the demon durgama. she protects indra and the other devas from fear and battle. she is also worshipped as the goddess who rescues devotees from difficulty, and as the nine-year-old form in kumārī worship. the citadel of protection: durgā means a fort that is nearly impossible for enemies to breach. she is the fortress wall around her devotees. when a seeker takes refuge in her energy, she sets up an unbreachable wall of protection that keeps out negative forces.","esoteric":["The Citadel of Protection: Durgā means a fort that is nearly impossible for enemies to breach. She is the fortress wall around Her devotees. When a seeker takes refuge in Her energy, She sets up an unbreachable wall of protection that keeps out negative forces."]},{"number":191,"name":"दुःखहन्त्री","samasa":["• दुःखस्य हन्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["दुःखस्य — of sorrow","हन्त्री — destroyer","दुःखहन्त्री — meaning follows from the samasa: दुःखस्य हन्त्री।"],"summary":["दुःखहन्त्री means one who destroys sorrow. She removes sorrow and pain caused by worldly affairs and grants complete release from suffering."],"searchText":"191 दुःखहन्त्री • दुःखस्य हन्त्री। दुःखस्य — of sorrow हन्त्री — destroyer दुःखहन्त्री — meaning follows from the samasa: दुःखस्य हन्त्री। दुःखहन्त्री means one who destroys sorrow. she removes sorrow and pain caused by worldly affairs and grants complete release from suffering. the core of compassion: suffering (duḥkha) is a universal challenge of material life. she acts as duḥkhahantrī because her dawning presence targets the root cause of suffering, dissolving pain into the nectar of her bliss.","esoteric":["The Core of Compassion: Suffering (duḥkha) is a universal challenge of material life. She acts as Duḥkhahantrī because Her dawning presence targets the root cause of suffering, dissolving pain into the nectar of Her bliss."]},{"number":192,"name":"सुखप्रदा","samasa":["• सुखं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["सुखं — happiness","प्रकर्षेण — excellently; intensely","ददातीति — gives","सुखप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: सुखं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति।"],"summary":["सुखप्रदा means one who bestows happiness. It is not enough for sorrow to be removed; happiness is also needed. She gives happiness according to the devotee's state, either in this world, in the next world, or in both. Ardent devotees receive both enjoyment and liberation through Her grace."],"searchText":"192 सुखप्रदा • सुखं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति। सुखं — happiness प्रकर्षेण — excellently; intensely ददातीति — gives सुखप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: सुखं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति। सुखप्रदा means one who bestows happiness. it is not enough for sorrow to be removed; happiness is also needed. she gives happiness according to the devotee's state, either in this world, in the next world, or in both. ardent devotees receive both enjoyment and liberation through her grace. the bestower of true bliss: she does not merely grant short-term sensory pleasure; she provides sukha in its highest form, the permanent, unconditioned joy of the self (ātmānanda), stabilizing the mind in lasting satisfaction.","esoteric":["The Bestower of True Bliss: She does not merely grant short-term sensory pleasure; She provides sukha in its highest form, the permanent, unconditioned joy of the Self (ātmānanda), stabilizing the mind in lasting satisfaction."]},{"number":193,"name":"दुष्टदूरा","samasa":["• दुष्टानां दूरा।"],"wordByWord":["दुष्टानां — of the wicked","दूरा — far away","दुष्टदूरा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुष्टानां दूरा।"],"summary":["दुष्टदूरा means one who is beyond the reach of wicked people. For those whose minds are faulty, argumentative or impure, She remains distant and unattainable. She becomes reachable only when such defects are purified."],"searchText":"193 दुष्टदूरा • दुष्टानां दूरा। दुष्टानां — of the wicked दूरा — far away दुष्टदूरा — meaning follows from the samasa: दुष्टानां दूरा। दुष्टदूरा means one who is beyond the reach of wicked people. for those whose minds are faulty, argumentative or impure, she remains distant and unattainable. she becomes reachable only when such defects are purified. the distance from impurity: distance here is not physical space, but a mismatch of inner fitness. wicked minds (duṣṭa) run outward after selfish power. because her nature is pure, a corrupted intellect remains blind to her presence until it is purified.","esoteric":["The Distance from Impurity: Distance here is not physical space, but a mismatch of inner fitness. Wicked minds (duṣṭa) run outward after selfish power. Because Her nature is pure, a corrupted intellect remains blind to Her presence until it is purified."]},{"number":194,"name":"दुराचारशमनी","samasa":["• दुराचारं शमयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["शमयतीति — pacifies; ends","दुराचारशमनी — meaning follows from the samasa: दुराचारं शमयतीति।"],"summary":["दुराचारशमनी means one who puts an end to evil conduct. Evil customs are actions contrary to sacred discipline. She quickly destroys the sins committed by neglecting daily duties and by following prohibited acts."],"searchText":"194 दुराचारशमनी • दुराचारं शमयतीति। शमयतीति — pacifies; ends दुराचारशमनी — meaning follows from the samasa: दुराचारं शमयतीति। दुराचारशमनी means one who puts an end to evil conduct. evil customs are actions contrary to sacred discipline. she quickly destroys the sins committed by neglecting daily duties and by following prohibited acts. the restorer of righteousness: unrighteous conduct (durācāra) creates discord and pulls energy downward. she acts as durācāraśamanī because her grace pacifies harmful behavior and guides attention back toward harmony and right living (sadācāra).","esoteric":["The Restorer of Righteousness: Unrighteous conduct (durācāra) creates discord and pulls energy downward. She acts as Durācāraśamanī because Her grace pacifies harmful behavior and guides attention back toward harmony and right living (sadācāra)."]},{"number":195,"name":"दोषवर्जिता","samasa":["• दोषैः वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["दोषैः — by faults","वर्जिता — free from; devoid of","दोषवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: दोषैः वर्जिता।"],"summary":["दोषवर्जिता means one who is free from all faults. A fault is that which spoils the mind, speech and action through longing and aversion. Since She is free from longing and aversion, She is faultless."],"searchText":"195 दोषवर्जिता • दोषैः वर्जिता। दोषैः — by faults वर्जिता — free from; devoid of दोषवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: दोषैः वर्जिता। दोषवर्जिता means one who is free from all faults. a fault is that which spoils the mind, speech and action through longing and aversion. since she is free from longing and aversion, she is faultless. the flawless substrate: in philosophy, everything in nature contains variations of flaws (doṣa). being the uncreated primordial cause, she is above these limitations and remains a perfect, unblemished field of absolute purity.","esoteric":["The Flawless Substrate: In philosophy, everything in nature contains variations of flaws (doṣa). Being the uncreated primordial cause, She is above these limitations and remains a perfect, unblemished field of absolute purity."]},{"number":196,"name":"सर्वज्ञा","samasa":["• सर्वं जानातीति।"],"wordByWord":["जानातीति — knows","सर्वज्ञा — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वं जानातीति।"],"summary":["सर्वज्ञा means one who is omniscient. She perceives all and knows all. Since She knows everything, She is called Sarvajñā."],"searchText":"196 सर्वज्ञा • सर्वं जानातीति। जानातीति — knows सर्वज्ञा — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वं जानातीति। सर्वज्ञा means one who is omniscient. she perceives all and knows all. since she knows everything, she is called sarvajñā. the eye of cosmic intellect: her omniscience (sarvajñā) is not a collection of external facts; it is the natural result of being the substrate of all existence. because everything is an expansion of her own self, she knows all things from within as their inner witness.","esoteric":["The Eye of Cosmic Intellect: Her omniscience (sarvajñā) is not a collection of external facts; it is the natural result of being the substrate of all existence. Because everything is an expansion of Her own self, She knows all things from within as their inner witness."]},{"number":197,"name":"सान्द्रकरुणा","samasa":["• सान्द्रा करुणा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सान्द्रा — dense; intense","करुणा — compassion","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सान्द्रकरुणा — meaning follows from the samasa: सान्द्रा करुणा यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सान्द्रकरुणा means one who shows intense compassion."],"searchText":"197 सान्द्रकरुणा • सान्द्रा करुणा यस्याः सा। सान्द्रा — dense; intense करुणा — compassion यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सान्द्रकरुणा — meaning follows from the samasa: सान्द्रा करुणा यस्याः सा। सान्द्रकरुणा means one who shows intense compassion. the solid wave of grace: sāndra means dense or intensely packed, like cream. her compassion is not weak or intermittent; it is a dense wave of protective grace that fills every corner of space and supports any devotee who calls upon her.","esoteric":["The Solid Wave of Grace: Sāndra means dense or intensely packed, like cream. Her compassion is not weak or intermittent; it is a dense wave of protective grace that fills every corner of space and supports any devotee who calls upon Her."]},{"number":198,"name":"समानाधिकवर्जिता","samasa":["• समानाधिकाभ्यां वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["समानाधिकाभ्यां — from equal and superior","वर्जिता — free from; devoid of","समानाधिकवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: समानाधिकाभ्यां वर्जिता।"],"summary":["समानाधिकवर्जिता means one who has neither an equal nor a superior. No one is seen as equal to Her or greater than Her. She is beyond comparison and beyond subordination."],"searchText":"198 समानाधिकवर्जिता • समानाधिकाभ्यां वर्जिता। समानाधिकाभ्यां — from equal and superior वर्जिता — free from; devoid of समानाधिकवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: समानाधिकाभ्यां वर्जिता। समानाधिकवर्जिता means one who has neither an equal nor a superior. no one is seen as equal to her or greater than her. she is beyond comparison and beyond subordination. the absolute peak: if an entity has an equal, its power is limited; if it has a superior, it is subordinate. she stands as samānādhikavarjitā because she has no rival to challenge her and no master to command her.","esoteric":["The Absolute Peak: If an entity has an equal, its power is limited; if it has a superior, it is subordinate. She stands as Samānādhikavarjitā because She has no rival to challenge Her and no master to command Her."]},{"number":199,"name":"सर्वशक्तिमयी","samasa":["• सर्वाः शक्तयः अस्याः सन्तीति सर्वशक्तिमयी।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वाः — all","शक्तयः — powers","सन्तीति — exist","सर्वशक्तिमयी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वाः शक्तयः अस्याः सन्तीति सर्वशक्तिमयी।"],"summary":["सर्वशक्तिमयी means one who possesses all divine powers. The world is not different from Brahman, and the word māyā indicates non-difference. Śrīdevī is not different from the many śaktis. The energies of all devas are Her powers, and only through Her blessing do the devas possess their powers. Sarva may also mean infinite."],"searchText":"199 सर्वशक्तिमयी • सर्वाः शक्तयः अस्याः सन्तीति सर्वशक्तिमयी। सर्वाः — all शक्तयः — powers सन्तीति — exist सर्वशक्तिमयी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वाः शक्तयः अस्याः सन्तीति सर्वशक्तिमयी। सर्वशक्तिमयी means one who possesses all divine powers. the world is not different from brahman, and the word māyā indicates non-difference. śrīdevī is not different from the many śaktis. the energies of all devas are her powers, and only through her blessing do the devas possess their powers. sarva may also mean infinite. the powerhouse of the universe: every type of force in the universe, whether physical strength, mental willpower or spiritual light, is a small expression of her grand matrix. she holds all cosmic energies within her unified being.","esoteric":["The Powerhouse of the Universe: Every type of force in the universe, whether physical strength, mental willpower or spiritual light, is a small expression of Her grand matrix. She holds all cosmic energies within Her unified being."]},{"number":200,"name":"सर्वमङ्गला","samasa":["• सर्वाणि मङ्गलानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मङ्गलानि — auspicious things","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सर्वमङ्गला — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वाणि मङ्गलानि यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सर्वमङ्गला means one who is the root of all auspiciousness. She is the root of all auspicious things, grants all auspicious and desired blessings, and removes the distress of devotees. Sarvamaṅgalā may also be understood as a tithi nityā devī and as connected with the praṇava in Her mantra. She is cit-śakti, not different from Brahman, and gives good fortune to those who satisfy Her through meditation, praise, song and worship."],"searchText":"200 सर्वमङ्गला • सर्वाणि मङ्गलानि यस्याः सा। मङ्गलानि — auspicious things यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सर्वमङ्गला — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वाणि मङ्गलानि यस्याः सा। सर्वमङ्गला means one who is the root of all auspiciousness. she is the root of all auspicious things, grants all auspicious and desired blessings, and removes the distress of devotees. sarvamaṅgalā may also be understood as a tithi nityā devī and as connected with the praṇava in her mantra. she is cit-śakti, not different from brahman, and gives good fortune to those who satisfy her through meditation, praise, song and worship. the root of good fortune: she is the definition of good fortune. invoking her energy converts discord into harmony, ensuring that actions undertaken in her name move toward auspiciousness.","esoteric":["The Root of Good Fortune: She is the definition of good fortune. Invoking Her energy converts discord into harmony, ensuring that actions undertaken in Her name move toward auspiciousness."]},{"number":201,"name":"सद्गतिप्रदा","samasa":["• सतां गतिं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["सतां — of good people","गतिं — path; goal","प्रकर्षेण — excellently; intensely","ददातीति — gives","सद्गतिप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: सतां गतिं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति।"],"summary":["सद्गतिप्रदा means one who grants the good path and the good goal. Sadgati includes all blessed states, from heaven to mokṣa, according to the devotee's eligibility. Gati can mean goal, wisdom and the way to reach; She grants good knowledge, illumines the right path and leads the devotee to the eternal sat. Since She Herself is sat and also the goal, She is both the path and the destination. She destroys ignorance and gives self-luminous bliss."],"searchText":"201 सद्गतिप्रदा • सतां गतिं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति। सतां — of good people गतिं — path; goal प्रकर्षेण — excellently; intensely ददातीति — gives सद्गतिप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: सतां गतिं प्रकर्षेण ददातीति। सद्गतिप्रदा means one who grants the good path and the good goal. sadgati includes all blessed states, from heaven to mokṣa, according to the devotee's eligibility. gati can mean goal, wisdom and the way to reach; she grants good knowledge, illumines the right path and leads the devotee to the eternal sat. since she herself is sat and also the goal, she is both the path and the destination. she destroys ignorance and gives self-luminous bliss. the guide to liberation: sadgati is the high trajectory that leads a soul away from rebirth and toward liberation. she acts as sadgatipradā because she stands as the protective guide who ensures that the seeker's energy travels smoothly to its true destination.","esoteric":["The Guide to Liberation: sadgati is the high trajectory that leads a soul away from rebirth and toward liberation. She acts as Sadgatipradā because She stands as the protective guide who ensures that the seeker's energy travels smoothly to its true destination."]},{"number":202,"name":"सर्वेश्वरी","samasa":["• सर्वेषाम् ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["ईश्वरी — ruler; mistress","सर्वेश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वेषाम् ईश्वरी।"],"summary":["सर्वेश्वरी means one who is the mistress of the whole universe. Because She leads all beings onto the right path, She is Sarveśvarī. There is no place where Her control is obstructed; She is the Īśvarī of all. She is also one of the eight Vāgdevīs."],"searchText":"202 सर्वेश्वरी • सर्वेषाम् ईश्वरी। ईश्वरी — ruler; mistress सर्वेश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वेषाम् ईश्वरी। सर्वेश्वरी means one who is the mistress of the whole universe. because she leads all beings onto the right path, she is sarveśvarī. there is no place where her control is obstructed; she is the īśvarī of all. she is also one of the eight vāgdevīs. the royal command: this name declares her absolute dominion. all cosmic laws and living beings move under her command, establishing her as the sovereign ruler of the manifest universe.","esoteric":["The Royal Command: This name declares Her absolute dominion. All cosmic laws and living beings move under Her command, establishing Her as the sovereign ruler of the manifest universe."]},{"number":203,"name":"सर्वमयी","samasa":["• सर्वम् अस्याम् अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वम् — all","अस्याम् — in her","सर्वमयी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वम् अस्याम् अस्तीति।"],"summary":["सर्वमयी means one who is omnipresent and omnipotent. She is in the form of all things. The universe is made of thirty-six tattvas: the twenty-four ātmā or jaḍa tattvas, the seven vidyā or māyā tattvas, and the five Śiva tattvas. Worshipping Śrīdevī as the form of these thirty-six tattvas is called tattvatva, one of the six methods of reaching Her."],"searchText":"203 सर्वमयी • सर्वम् अस्याम् अस्तीति। सर्वम् — all अस्याम् — in her सर्वमयी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वम् अस्याम् अस्तीति। सर्वमयी means one who is omnipresent and omnipotent. she is in the form of all things. the universe is made of thirty-six tattvas: the twenty-four ātmā or jaḍa tattvas, the seven vidyā or māyā tattvas, and the five śiva tattvas. worshipping śrīdevī as the form of these thirty-six tattvas is called tattvatva, one of the six methods of reaching her. the non-dual matrix: this name declares her absolute immanence. she is not separate from the world; the world is her own visible body. every being is a wave appearing upon the single ocean of her consciousness.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Matrix: This name declares Her absolute immanence. She is not separate from the world; the world is Her own visible body. Every being is a wave appearing upon the single ocean of Her consciousness."]},{"number":204,"name":"सर्वमन्त्रस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• सर्वे मन्त्राः स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["मन्त्राः — mantras","स्वरूपम् — own form; essential nature","सर्वमन्त्रस्वरूपिणी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वे मन्त्राः स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति।"],"summary":["सर्वमन्त्रस्वरूपिणी means one who is the very essence of all mantras. There are many crores of mantras, and She is in the form of all of them. Her own form itself is mantra. She is also worshipped as the form of mantras in the method called mantratva, one of the six atvas."],"searchText":"204 सर्वमन्त्रस्वरूपिणी • सर्वे मन्त्राः स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति। मन्त्राः — mantras स्वरूपम् — own form; essential nature सर्वमन्त्रस्वरूपिणी — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वे मन्त्राः स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति। सर्वमन्त्रस्वरूपिणी means one who is the very essence of all mantras. there are many crores of mantras, and she is in the form of all of them. her own form itself is mantra. she is also worshipped as the form of mantras in the method called mantratva, one of the six atvas. the queen of sound: every mantra draws its power from her primary vibration. she is the underlying energy of all sacred sound formulas, making them effective when chanted with clear intent.","esoteric":["The Queen of Sound: Every mantra draws its power from Her primary vibration. She is the underlying energy of all sacred sound formulas, making them effective when chanted with clear intent."]},{"number":205,"name":"सर्वयन्त्रात्मिका","samasa":["• सर्वेषां यन्त्राणाम् आत्मिका।"],"wordByWord":["यन्त्राणाम् — of yantras","आत्मिका — embodiment; inner self","सर्वयन्त्रात्मिका — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वेषां यन्त्राणाम् आत्मिका।"],"summary":["सर्वयन्त्रात्मिका means one who is the inner self of all yantras. Yantras are forms made of lines that contain the concerned presiding deities within themselves. She is the life and essence of all such yantras."],"searchText":"205 सर्वयन्त्रात्मिका • सर्वेषां यन्त्राणाम् आत्मिका। यन्त्राणाम् — of yantras आत्मिका — embodiment; inner self सर्वयन्त्रात्मिका — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वेषां यन्त्राणाम् आत्मिका। सर्वयन्त्रात्मिका means one who is the inner self of all yantras. yantras are forms made of lines that contain the concerned presiding deities within themselves. she is the life and essence of all such yantras. the soul of sacred geometry: a yantra is a geometric layout that maps energy. she is the inner life of these diagrams, transforming them from drawings into active supports of spiritual power when aligned with meditation.","esoteric":["The Soul of Sacred Geometry: A yantra is a geometric layout that maps energy. She is the inner life of these diagrams, transforming them from drawings into active supports of spiritual power when aligned with meditation."]},{"number":206,"name":"सर्वतन्त्ररूपा","samasa":["• सर्वाणि तन्त्राणि एव रूपं (शरीरं) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["तन्त्राणि — tantras","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सर्वतन्त्ररूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वाणि तन्त्राणि एव रूपं (शरीरं) यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सर्वतन्त्ररूपा means one who is the spirit of all tantras in Her form. Since all tantras indicate Śrīdevī Herself and establish Her, She is in the form of all tantras. The sacred systems are understood as limbs of Her body, showing that every valid system abides in Her own form."],"searchText":"206 सर्वतन्त्ररूपा • सर्वाणि तन्त्राणि एव रूपं (शरीरं) यस्याः सा। तन्त्राणि — tantras रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सर्वतन्त्ररूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: सर्वाणि तन्त्राणि एव रूपं (शरीरं) यस्याः सा। सर्वतन्त्ररूपा means one who is the spirit of all tantras in her form. since all tantras indicate śrīdevī herself and establish her, she is in the form of all tantras. the sacred systems are understood as limbs of her body, showing that every valid system abides in her own form. the method personified: this teaching is the practical system of spiritual application. she is the very soul of these methods, showing that every genuine system of spiritual practice is a pathway for approaching her non-dual nature.","esoteric":["The Method Personified: this teaching is the practical system of spiritual application. She is the very soul of these methods, showing that every genuine system of spiritual practice is a pathway for approaching Her non-dual nature."]},{"number":207,"name":"मनोन्मनी","samasa":["• मनोन्मनाख्यशिवस्य शक्तिः।"],"wordByWord":["शक्तिः — power","मनोन्मनी — meaning follows from the samasa: मनोन्मनाख्यशिवस्य शक्तिः।"],"summary":["मनोन्मनी means one who is in the form of Manonmanī, transcendent consciousness. From the ājñācakra to the brahmarandhra there are subtle stations such as bindu, rodhinī, nāda, nādānta, śakti, vyāpinī, samanā, unmanī or Manonmanī, and mahābindu. The mahābindu, also called indu or the half-moon, is minute energy and is called Manonmanī. Śrīdevī is in the form of that unmanī. In yoga, when the mind is controlled, free from attachment to objects and fixed inward, it attains the state of unmanī. In meditation on Śrīdevī, when meditator and object of meditation are dissolved, the unmanī state arises and the ambrosia of wisdom is enjoyed."],"searchText":"207 मनोन्मनी • मनोन्मनाख्यशिवस्य शक्तिः। शक्तिः — power मनोन्मनी — meaning follows from the samasa: मनोन्मनाख्यशिवस्य शक्तिः। मनोन्मनी means one who is in the form of manonmanī, transcendent consciousness. from the ājñācakra to the brahmarandhra there are subtle stations such as bindu, rodhinī, nāda, nādānta, śakti, vyāpinī, samanā, unmanī or manonmanī, and mahābindu. the mahābindu, also called indu or the half-moon, is minute energy and is called manonmanī. śrīdevī is in the form of that unmanī. in yoga, when the mind is controlled, free from attachment to objects and fixed inward, it attains the state of unmanī. in meditation on śrīdevī, when meditator and object of meditation are dissolved, the unmanī state arises and the ambrosia of wisdom is enjoyed. beyond the mind: manonmanī represents a high state of yoga where the individual mind (manas) rises and dissolves into transcendent awareness (unmanī). she embodies this transition point, helping the seeker move beyond conceptual thought.","esoteric":["Beyond the Mind: Manonmanī represents a high state of yoga where the individual mind (manas) rises and dissolves into transcendent awareness (unmanī). She embodies this transition point, helping the seeker move beyond conceptual thought."]},{"number":208,"name":"माहेश्वरी","samasa":["• महेश्वरस्य इयम्।"],"wordByWord":["महेश्वरस्य — of Maheshvara","इयम् — belonging to him; his consort","माहेश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: महेश्वरस्य इयम्।"],"summary":["माहेश्वरी means one who is the consort and Śakti of Maheśvara, Paramaśiva. Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra perform creation, protection and destruction. Maheśvara stands above these three and transcends the three guṇas: rajas, tamas and sattva. His Śakti form is Māheśvarī. Maheśvara also means the lord of the bhūta gaṇas and the one honored by great practitioners; His consort is Māheśvarī."],"searchText":"208 माहेश्वरी • महेश्वरस्य इयम्। महेश्वरस्य — of maheshvara इयम् — belonging to him; his consort माहेश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: महेश्वरस्य इयम्। माहेश्वरी means one who is the consort and śakti of maheśvara, paramaśiva. brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra perform creation, protection and destruction. maheśvara stands above these three and transcends the three guṇas: rajas, tamas and sattva. his śakti form is māheśvarī. maheśvara also means the lord of the bhūta gaṇas and the one honored by great practitioners; his consort is māheśvarī. the power of absolute domain: as māheśvarī, she wields the immense sovereign majesty of the great lord and governs the major cosmic balances with absolute authority.","esoteric":["The Power of Absolute Domain: As Māheśvarī, She wields the immense sovereign majesty of the Great Lord and governs the major cosmic balances with absolute authority."]},{"number":209,"name":"महादेवी","samasa":["• महती च सा देवी च।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","सा — she","देवी — goddess","महादेवी — meaning follows from the samasa: महती च सा देवी च।"],"summary":["महादेवी means the great goddess. Mahatī means one whose body is immense and immeasurable. Śiva in His eighth form, the moon, is known as Mahādeva; His consort is Rohiṇī or Mahādevī. She possesses the entire energy of all devas and is the greatest of all devīs; therefore She is Mahādevī."],"searchText":"209 महादेवी • महती च सा देवी च। महती — great सा — she देवी — goddess महादेवी — meaning follows from the samasa: महती च सा देवी च। महादेवी means the great goddess. mahatī means one whose body is immense and immeasurable. śiva in his eighth form, the moon, is known as mahādeva; his consort is rohiṇī or mahādevī. she possesses the entire energy of all devas and is the greatest of all devīs; therefore she is mahādevī. the goddess supreme: while secondary deities rule over specific powers of nature, she is mahādevī, the overarching origin from whom all other feminine expressions draw their power.","esoteric":["The Goddess Supreme: While secondary deities rule over specific powers of nature, She is Mahādevī, the overarching origin from whom all other feminine expressions draw their power."]},{"number":210,"name":"महालक्ष्मी","samasa":["• महती च सा लक्ष्मी च।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","सा — she","लक्ष्मी — Lakshmi; prosperity","महालक्ष्मी — meaning follows from the samasa: महती च सा लक्ष्मी च।"],"summary":["महालक्ष्मी means the great Lakṣmī. She is Mahālakṣmī, the consort of Mahāviṣṇu, and is worshipped as the presiding deity at Karavīra in Kolhapur. Śrīdevī took the form of Mahālakṣmī with eighteen hands to kill Mahiṣāsura. Mahālakṣmī is also named as an element or form of Śrīdevī and is fit to be worshipped on the thirteenth lunar day."],"searchText":"210 महालक्ष्मी • महती च सा लक्ष्मी च। महती — great सा — she लक्ष्मी — lakshmi; prosperity महालक्ष्मी — meaning follows from the samasa: महती च सा लक्ष्मी च। महालक्ष्मी means the great lakṣmī. she is mahālakṣmī, the consort of mahāviṣṇu, and is worshipped as the presiding deity at karavīra in kolhapur. śrīdevī took the form of mahālakṣmī with eighteen hands to kill mahiṣāsura. mahālakṣmī is also named as an element or form of śrīdevī and is fit to be worshipped on the thirteenth lunar day. the origin of abundance: beyond material wealth, mahālakṣmī represents the deep wealth of spiritual clarity, beauty and cosmic order, illuminating the seeker's life with universal harmony.","esoteric":["The Origin of Abundance: Beyond material wealth, Mahālakṣmī represents the deep wealth of spiritual clarity, beauty and cosmic order, illuminating the seeker's life with universal harmony."]},{"number":211,"name":"मृडप्रिया","samasa":["• मृडस्य प्रिया।"],"wordByWord":["मृडस्य — of Mrida; Shiva","प्रिया — beloved","मृडप्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: मृडस्य प्रिया।"],"summary":["मृडप्रिया means one who is dear to Mṛḍa, Lord Śiva."],"searchText":"211 मृडप्रिया • मृडस्य प्रिया। मृडस्य — of mrida; shiva प्रिया — beloved मृडप्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: मृडस्य प्रिया। मृडप्रिया means one who is dear to mṛḍa, lord śiva. the comfort of the consort: mṛḍa is the compassionate form of śiva that forgives mistakes. she is his beloved, showing that her dynamic grace is aligned with divine mercy.","esoteric":["The Comfort of the Consort: Mṛḍa is the compassionate form of Śiva that forgives mistakes. She is His beloved, showing that Her dynamic grace is aligned with divine mercy."]},{"number":212,"name":"महारूपा","samasa":["• महद्रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महद्रूपं — great form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","महारूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: महद्रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["महारूपा means one who has a great and magnificent form. Supreme Brahman has four forms: puruṣa, the manifested gross elements, the unmanifest avyakta or pradhāna, and time. These are the root causes of creation, protection, destruction and fundamental principles; She is the root cause of all these and is greater than them. Mahat is the unmanifest state from which the world appears and into which it resolves; She is in the form of that mahat. Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Śiva perform creation, protection and destruction, and She assumes those great forms as well as the forms of yogins and siddhas."],"searchText":"212 महारूपा • महद्रूपं यस्याः सा। महद्रूपं — great form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she महारूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: महद्रूपं यस्याः सा। महारूपा means one who has a great and magnificent form. supreme brahman has four forms: puruṣa, the manifested gross elements, the unmanifest avyakta or pradhāna, and time. these are the root causes of creation, protection, destruction and fundamental principles; she is the root cause of all these and is greater than them. mahat is the unmanifest state from which the world appears and into which it resolves; she is in the form of that mahat. brahmā, viṣṇu and śiva perform creation, protection and destruction, and she assumes those great forms as well as the forms of yogins and siddhas. the cosmic body: her form is not limited to an icon; physical space, stars and galaxies are the visible layout of her grand cosmic body (viśvarūpa).","esoteric":["The Cosmic Body: Her form is not limited to an icon; physical space, stars and galaxies are the visible layout of Her grand cosmic body (viśvarūpa)."]},{"number":213,"name":"महापूज्या","samasa":["• महती च सा पूज्या च।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","सा — she","पूज्या — worshipful","महापूज्या — meaning follows from the samasa: महती च सा पूज्या च।"],"summary":["महापूज्या means one who is most worthy of worship. She is worshipped even by Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra, who are themselves worshipful. Being greater than the great and worthy of worship, She is Mahāpūjyā. Devas worship Her in different forms and yantras, including forms made of precious substances such as ruby and other materials. Remembering Her lotus feet destroys sins done knowingly or unknowingly."],"searchText":"213 महापूज्या • महती च सा पूज्या च। महती — great सा — she पूज्या — worshipful महापूज्या — meaning follows from the samasa: महती च सा पूज्या च। महापूज्या means one who is most worthy of worship. she is worshipped even by brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra, who are themselves worshipful. being greater than the great and worthy of worship, she is mahāpūjyā. devas worship her in different forms and yantras, including forms made of precious substances such as ruby and other materials. remembering her lotus feet destroys sins done knowingly or unknowingly. the ultimate adoration: all preliminary steps of worship find their destination at her feet. she is the highest altar of reality, where the distinction between worshipper and worshipped dissolves.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Adoration: All preliminary steps of worship find their destination at Her feet. She is the highest altar of reality, where the distinction between worshipper and worshipped dissolves."]},{"number":214,"name":"महापातकनाशिनी","samasa":["• महान्ति पातकानि नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","पातकानि — sins","नाशयतीति — destroys","महापातकनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: महान्ति पातकानि नाशयतीति।"],"summary":["महापातकनाशिनी means one who destroys great sins. The great sins include killing a brāhmaṇa, stealing, drinking alcohol, desiring the wife of an elder, and supporting those who commit such acts. Remembering the lotus feet of Śrīdevī destroys these sins and even the thought that tempts one to repeat them. Worshipping Her removes sinful tendencies and generates thoughts of good deeds."],"searchText":"214 महापातकनाशिनी • महान्ति पातकानि नाशयतीति। महान्ति — great पातकानि — sins नाशयतीति — destroys महापातकनाशिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: महान्ति पातकानि नाशयतीति। महापातकनाशिनी means one who destroys great sins. the great sins include killing a brāhmaṇa, stealing, drinking alcohol, desiring the wife of an elder, and supporting those who commit such acts. remembering the lotus feet of śrīdevī destroys these sins and even the thought that tempts one to repeat them. worshipping her removes sinful tendencies and generates thoughts of good deeds. the ultimate absolution: certain dark actions generate deep karmic weight (mahāpātaka) that is difficult to clear by ordinary means. her grace burns away even these deepest weights when approached with sincere devotion.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Absolution: Certain dark actions generate deep karmic weight (mahāpātaka) that is difficult to clear by ordinary means. Her grace burns away even these deepest weights when approached with sincere devotion."]},{"number":215,"name":"महामाया","samasa":["• महती च असौ माया च।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","च — and","असौ — this; that","माया — illusion; divine power","च। — and","महामाया — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महामाया means one who is in the form of great māyā. She creates delusion even among devas beginning with Brahmā. The seed letter hrīṃ is called māyā or śakti, and the complete energy of Śrīdevī is hidden in it. Hrīṃ is like a knot for the three kūṭas of the pañcadaśākṣarī mantra. Its parts contain the full power of the mantra, just as all parts of a tree are hidden in a seed. Māyā can also mean compassion; therefore Mahāmāyā also means one full of compassion."],"searchText":"215 महामाया • महती च असौ माया च। महती — great च — and असौ — this; that माया — illusion; divine power च। — and महामाया — the full name, understood through the samasa above महामाया means one who is in the form of great māyā. she creates delusion even among devas beginning with brahmā. the seed letter hrīṃ is called māyā or śakti, and the complete energy of śrīdevī is hidden in it. hrīṃ is like a knot for the three kūṭas of the pañcadaśākṣarī mantra. its parts contain the full power of the mantra, just as all parts of a tree are hidden in a seed. māyā can also mean compassion; therefore mahāmāyā also means one full of compassion. the coordinator of the cosmic play: māyā is the power that projects the universe upon awareness. she is mahāmāyā, holding the power both to bind the soul through duality and to release it through wisdom.","esoteric":["The Coordinator of the Cosmic Play: Māyā is the power that projects the universe upon awareness. She is Mahāmāyā, holding the power both to bind the soul through duality and to release it through wisdom."]},{"number":216,"name":"महासत्वा","samasa":["• महान्ति सत्वानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","सत्वानि — beings; realities; qualities","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महासत्वा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महासत्वा means one who is the supreme reality and full of sattva. Sattva means character, strength and state of existence; Śrīdevī has these in the highest degree. Sattva also means mind, and Her mind is so broad that She makes no distinction between any being, from Brahmā down to a worm. Sattva may also mean seat or the state by which individuality is shown; She is present in these forms in all things."],"searchText":"216 महासत्वा • महान्ति सत्वानि यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great सत्वानि — beings; realities; qualities यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महासत्वा — the full name, understood through the samasa above महासत्वा means one who is the supreme reality and full of sattva. sattva means character, strength and state of existence; śrīdevī has these in the highest degree. sattva also means mind, and her mind is so broad that she makes no distinction between any being, from brahmā down to a worm. sattva may also mean seat or the state by which individuality is shown; she is present in these forms in all things. the matrix of sattva: she is the dense repository of the sattva quality, providing the clean mental environment that enables seekers to experience spiritual clarity.","esoteric":["The Matrix of Sattva: She is the dense repository of the sattva quality, providing the clean mental environment that enables seekers to experience spiritual clarity."]},{"number":217,"name":"महाशक्तिः","samasa":["• महती शक्तिः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","शक्तिः — power; energy","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महाशक्तिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महाशक्तिः means one who has boundless energy. She has the power to administer the entire universe. Śakti means strength, and Śrīdevī's strength and weapons are so great that She is called Mahāśaktiḥ. This name is distinct from an earlier similar name by the difference between sa and śa."],"searchText":"217 महाशक्तिः • महती शक्तिः यस्याः सा। महती — great शक्तिः — power; energy यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महाशक्तिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above महाशक्तिः means one who has boundless energy. she has the power to administer the entire universe. śakti means strength, and śrīdevī's strength and weapons are so great that she is called mahāśaktiḥ. this name is distinct from an earlier similar name by the difference between sa and śa. the engine of the cosmos: she is the primary dynamic force that drives the universe and governs all energies with absolute supremacy.","esoteric":["The Engine of the Cosmos: She is the primary dynamic force that drives the universe and governs all energies with absolute supremacy."]},{"number":218,"name":"महारतिः","samasa":["• महती रतिः यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","रतिः — delight; love","यस्यां — in whom","सा। — she","महारतिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महारतिः means one who is great delight and affection. Rati means the mind's enjoyment and delight in an object. Such affection does not truly arise from the object but from the self of the enjoyer. That self-affection is Śrīdevī Herself in the form of the jīvātman. Because of ignorance, people seek affection outside, without knowing that it is within as the Self. One who knows this attains inner satisfaction. Śrīdevī is this form of rati, is more beautiful than Rati, and is the consort of Mahākāma."],"searchText":"218 महारतिः • महती रतिः यस्यां सा। महती — great रतिः — delight; love यस्यां — in whom सा। — she महारतिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above महारतिः means one who is great delight and affection. rati means the mind's enjoyment and delight in an object. such affection does not truly arise from the object but from the self of the enjoyer. that self-affection is śrīdevī herself in the form of the jīvātman. because of ignorance, people seek affection outside, without knowing that it is within as the self. one who knows this attains inner satisfaction. śrīdevī is this form of rati, is more beautiful than rati, and is the consort of mahākāma. the joy of the self: this delight is not short-term sensory pleasure; it is the deep, steady ecstasy of non-dual self-absorption (ātma-rati), satisfying the soul completely.","esoteric":["The Joy of the Self: This delight is not short-term sensory pleasure; it is the deep, steady ecstasy of non-dual self-absorption (ātma-rati), satisfying the soul completely."]},{"number":219,"name":"महाभोगा","samasa":["• महान् आभोगः यस्याः सा।","• महान् भोगः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान् — great","आभोगः — enjoyment; expanse","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","भोगः — enjoyment","महाभोगा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महाभोगा means one who is a great enjoyer. bhoga is the feeling of enjoying happiness, and any wealth that gives this feeling is bhoga. She has unlimited means of wealth and enjoys without obstruction. Abhoga also means extension; She is boundlessly extended as this universe and is therefore Mahābhogā."],"searchText":"219 महाभोगा • महान् आभोगः यस्याः सा। • महान् भोगः यस्याः सा। महान् — great आभोगः — enjoyment; expanse यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she भोगः — enjoyment महाभोगा — the full name, understood through the samasa above महाभोगा means one who is a great enjoyer. bhoga is the feeling of enjoying happiness, and any wealth that gives this feeling is bhoga. she has unlimited means of wealth and enjoys without obstruction. abhoga also means extension; she is boundlessly extended as this universe and is therefore mahābhogā. the integration of bhoga and mokṣa: her way does not force a dry choice between worldly life and liberation. she provides the rich delights of life (bhoga) while making them steps toward final freedom.","esoteric":["The Integration of bhoga and Mokṣa: Her way does not force a dry choice between worldly life and liberation. She provides the rich delights of life (bhoga) while making them steps toward final freedom."]},{"number":220,"name":"महैश्वर्या","samasa":["• महान्ति ऐश्वर्यं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","ऐश्वर्यं — sovereignty; lordship","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महैश्वर्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महैश्वर्या means one who possesses supreme sovereignty. Aiśvarya is the state of being īśvarī, the power and ability to rule others according to one's will. She possesses this capacity fully. Individual manifestations such as personality, beauty, innocence, fragrance and other special qualities are parts of īśvara's glory. Śrīdevī is integral to all these manifestations and is therefore Mahaiśvaryā."],"searchText":"220 महैश्वर्या • महान्ति ऐश्वर्यं यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great ऐश्वर्यं — sovereignty; lordship यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महैश्वर्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above महैश्वर्या means one who possesses supreme sovereignty. aiśvarya is the state of being īśvarī, the power and ability to rule others according to one's will. she possesses this capacity fully. individual manifestations such as personality, beauty, innocence, fragrance and other special qualities are parts of īśvara's glory. śrīdevī is integral to all these manifestations and is therefore mahaiśvaryā. the absolute dominion: her rule is unyielding and independent, governing all aspects of reality with absolute authority.","esoteric":["The Absolute Dominion: Her rule is unyielding and independent, governing all aspects of reality with absolute authority."]},{"number":221,"name":"महावीर्या","samasa":["• महान्ति वीर्याणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","वीर्याणि — strengths; powers; valours","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महावीर्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महावीर्या means one who is supreme in valour. Vīrya means vital power, might, glory and strength. Śrīdevī possesses all these in a great way."],"searchText":"221 महावीर्या • महान्ति वीर्याणि यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great वीर्याणि — strengths; powers; valours यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महावीर्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above महावीर्या means one who is supreme in valour. vīrya means vital power, might, glory and strength. śrīdevī possesses all these in a great way. the vital core: she holds the concentrated vital strength that fuels the processes of nature and drives them forward without exhaustion.","esoteric":["The Vital Core: She holds the concentrated vital strength that fuels the processes of nature and drives them forward without exhaustion."]},{"number":222,"name":"महाबला","samasa":["• महान्ति बलानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","बलानि — strengths; powers","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महाबला — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महाबला means one who has great might. Bala means army, strength, fragrance, taste, form, soul and other powers; Śrīdevī possesses all of these abundantly. Bala can also refer to the crow. Great yogins such as Bhuśuṇḍa worshipped Śrīdevī in that form and received great strength. Therefore She is Mahābalā."],"searchText":"222 महाबला • महान्ति बलानि यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great बलानि — strengths; powers यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महाबला — the full name, understood through the samasa above महाबला means one who has great might. bala means army, strength, fragrance, taste, form, soul and other powers; śrīdevī possesses all of these abundantly. bala can also refer to the crow. great yogins such as bhuśuṇḍa worshipped śrīdevī in that form and received great strength. therefore she is mahābalā. the unshaken base: her strength is absolute, supporting the entire weight of the universe without wavering.","esoteric":["The Unshaken Base: Her strength is absolute, supporting the entire weight of the universe without wavering."]},{"number":223,"name":"महबुद्धिः","samasa":["• महती च सा बुद्धिश्च।","• महती बुद्धिर्यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","च — and","सा — she","बुद्धिश्च। — and intellect; wisdom","सा। — she","महबुद्धिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महबुद्धिः means one who has great wisdom. Intellect is the understanding of inner consciousness, and She has the wisdom to understand everything at the subtlest level. By knowing Her, the whole universe is known, and from Her one obtains the highest intelligence. She is the very form of intellect. By worshipping Her, one gains great acumen."],"searchText":"223 महबुद्धिः • महती च सा बुद्धिश्च। • महती बुद्धिर्यस्याः सा। महती — great च — and सा — she बुद्धिश्च। — and intellect; wisdom सा। — she महबुद्धिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above महबुद्धिः means one who has great wisdom. intellect is the understanding of inner consciousness, and she has the wisdom to understand everything at the subtlest level. by knowing her, the whole universe is known, and from her one obtains the highest intelligence. she is the very form of intellect. by worshipping her, one gains great acumen. the origin of intuition: she is the overarching intelligence that governs cosmic law and gives seekers clear intuitive insight that refines understanding.","esoteric":["The Origin of Intuition: She is the overarching intelligence that governs cosmic law and gives seekers clear intuitive insight that refines understanding."]},{"number":224,"name":"महासिद्धिः","samasa":["• महती च सा सिद्धिश्च ।","• महती सिद्धिर्यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","च — and","सा — she","सिद्धिश्च — and attainment","सा। — she","महासिद्धिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महासिद्धिः means one who is the great siddhi and giver of siddhis. The eight siddhis are aṇimā, becoming minute; mahimā, becoming vast; garimā, becoming extremely heavy; laghimā, becoming almost weightless; prāpti, reaching all places; prākāmya, fulfilling desires; īśitva, controlling movable and immovable things; and vaśitva, subjugating all. Other siddhis include mastery over passions and freedom from being enslaved by happiness, sorrow, heat, cold, desire and aversion. She is the form of all these siddhis and grants them."],"searchText":"224 महासिद्धिः • महती च सा सिद्धिश्च । • महती सिद्धिर्यस्याः सा। महती — great च — and सा — she सिद्धिश्च — and attainment सा। — she महासिद्धिः — the full name, understood through the samasa above महासिद्धिः means one who is the great siddhi and giver of siddhis. the eight siddhis are aṇimā, becoming minute; mahimā, becoming vast; garimā, becoming extremely heavy; laghimā, becoming almost weightless; prāpti, reaching all places; prākāmya, fulfilling desires; īśitva, controlling movable and immovable things; and vaśitva, subjugating all. other siddhis include mastery over passions and freedom from being enslaved by happiness, sorrow, heat, cold, desire and aversion. she is the form of all these siddhis and grants them. the final destination: all minor spiritual powers are steps along the way. she is mahāsiddhi, the final stable state of self-realization that marks the completion of the journey.","esoteric":["The Final Destination: All minor spiritual powers are steps along the way. She is Mahāsiddhi, the final stable state of self-realization that marks the completion of the journey."]},{"number":225,"name":"महायोगेश्वरेश्वरी","samasa":["• महतां योगेश्वराणाम् ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["महतां — of the great","योगेश्वराणाम् — of the lords/masters of Yoga","ईश्वरी। — sovereign; mistress","महायोगेश्वरेश्वरी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महायोगेश्वरेश्वरी means the Īśvarī of all great yogeśvaras. Mahāyogas are the best methods of yoga, and their experts are mahāyogeśvaras; She is their head. Yoga is the integration of what appears differentiated. Yogeśvaras gain the quality of īśvara through yoga, and She grants that īśvara-quality to the great yogins."],"searchText":"225 महायोगेश्वरेश्वरी • महतां योगेश्वराणाम् ईश्वरी। महतां — of the great योगेश्वराणाम् — of the lords/masters of yoga ईश्वरी। — sovereign; mistress महायोगेश्वरेश्वरी — the full name, understood through the samasa above महायोगेश्वरेश्वरी means the īśvarī of all great yogeśvaras. mahāyogas are the best methods of yoga, and their experts are mahāyogeśvaras; she is their head. yoga is the integration of what appears differentiated. yogeśvaras gain the quality of īśvara through yoga, and she grants that īśvara-quality to the great yogins. the teacher of masters: the great masters of yoga (yogeśvaras) command inner energies. she stands above them as their supreme guide and the inner light that reveals their path.","esoteric":["The Teacher of Masters: The great masters of yoga (yogeśvaras) command inner energies. She stands above them as their supreme guide and the inner light that reveals their path."]},{"number":226,"name":"महातन्त्रा","samasa":["• महान्ति तन्त्राणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","तन्त्राणि — Tantras; systems of worship","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महातन्त्रा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महातन्त्रा means one who is worshipped through the great tantra. The methods of worship and the works that explain them are called tantras. Since each of these is great, She is Mahātantrā. Among them, Svatantra explains the worship of Śrīdevī exclusively and is a mahātantra. She is worshipped by this Mahātantra method. Parameśvara revealed many tantras for different deities and results, and then taught Śrīdevī the complete and independent Mahātantra called Svatantra, also known as Rājatantra."],"searchText":"226 महातन्त्रा • महान्ति तन्त्राणि यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great तन्त्राणि — tantras; systems of worship यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महातन्त्रा — the full name, understood through the samasa above महातन्त्रा means one who is worshipped through the great tantra. the methods of worship and the works that explain them are called tantras. since each of these is great, she is mahātantrā. among them, svatantra explains the worship of śrīdevī exclusively and is a mahātantra. she is worshipped by this mahātantra method. parameśvara revealed many tantras for different deities and results, and then taught śrīdevī the complete and independent mahātantra called svatantra, also known as rājatantra. the blueprint of practice: she rules the deep internal systems of spiritual transformation, turning the body and mind into pure vehicles of freedom.","esoteric":["The Blueprint of Practice: She rules the deep internal systems of spiritual transformation, turning the body and mind into pure vehicles of freedom."]},{"number":227,"name":"महामन्त्रा","samasa":["• महान्तः मन्त्राः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्तः — great","मन्त्राः — mantras","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महामन्त्रा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महामन्त्रा means one who is worshipped by great mantras. There are countless mantras used for worshipping Śrīdevī, including those of deities such as Bagalā, Kālī and Annapūrṇā. Among them, the greatest is the pañcadaśākṣarī mahāmantra called Śrīvidyā. Since She is worshipped by this mantra, She is Mahāmantrā."],"searchText":"227 महामन्त्रा • महान्तः मन्त्राः यस्याः सा। महान्तः — great मन्त्राः — mantras यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महामन्त्रा — the full name, understood through the samasa above महामन्त्रा means one who is worshipped by great mantras. there are countless mantras used for worshipping śrīdevī, including those of deities such as bagalā, kālī and annapūrṇā. among them, the greatest is the pañcadaśākṣarī mahāmantra called śrīvidyā. since she is worshipped by this mantra, she is mahāmantrā. the seed of power: she is the force behind the highest mantras, rendering them vibrant when aligned with focus and devotion.","esoteric":["The Seed of Power: She is the force behind the highest mantras, rendering them vibrant when aligned with focus and devotion."]},{"number":228,"name":"महायन्त्रा","samasa":["• महान्ति यन्त्राणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","यन्त्राणि — yantras","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महायन्त्रा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महायन्त्रा means one who has many great yantras used for Her worship. A yantra is a drawing made of lines, circles, lotus-petal shapes, rectangles, triangles and intersection points. Yantras are two-dimensional; when height is added, the form is called Meru. The three-dimensional Śrīcakra with the bindu at the top is Meru, and a partial form is called ardha-Meru. Great yantras such as Śrīcakra, Pūjācakra, Padmacakra, Amṛtakaṭa yantra, Meru, Siddhavajra yantra and liṅga are Her forms; therefore She is Mahāyantrā."],"searchText":"228 महायन्त्रा • महान्ति यन्त्राणि यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great यन्त्राणि — yantras यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महायन्त्रा — the full name, understood through the samasa above महायन्त्रा means one who has many great yantras used for her worship. a yantra is a drawing made of lines, circles, lotus-petal shapes, rectangles, triangles and intersection points. yantras are two-dimensional; when height is added, the form is called meru. the three-dimensional śrīcakra with the bindu at the top is meru, and a partial form is called ardha-meru. great yantras such as śrīcakra, pūjācakra, padmacakra, amṛtakaṭa yantra, meru, siddhavajra yantra and liṅga are her forms; therefore she is mahāyantrā. the central axis: she is the central power holding the layout of the śrīcakra, organizing the cosmic paths with absolute balance.","esoteric":["The Central Axis: She is the central power holding the layout of the Śrīcakra, organizing the cosmic paths with absolute balance."]},{"number":229,"name":"महासना","samasa":["• महान्ति आसनानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["महान्ति — great","आसनानि — seats; postures","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","महासना — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महासना means one who has a great seat. The thirty-six tattvas beginning with earth, created by Her, are Her seat. These tattvas, whether taken individually, in combination, or all together, form the seat of Śrīdevī. She also has the hearts of great people as Her seat. She is seated on great seats such as Pañcabrahmāsana, Cakrarājaratha and siṃhāsana; therefore She is Mahāsanā."],"searchText":"229 महासना • महान्ति आसनानि यस्याः सा। महान्ति — great आसनानि — seats; postures यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she महासना — the full name, understood through the samasa above महासना means one who has a great seat. the thirty-six tattvas beginning with earth, created by her, are her seat. these tattvas, whether taken individually, in combination, or all together, form the seat of śrīdevī. she also has the hearts of great people as her seat. she is seated on great seats such as pañcabrahmāsana, cakrarājaratha and siṃhāsana; therefore she is mahāsanā. the summit base: her seat is composed of the highest cosmic principles, serving as a stable support for spiritual elevation.","esoteric":["The Summit Base: Her seat is composed of the highest cosmic principles, serving as a stable support for spiritual elevation."]},{"number":230,"name":"महायागक्रमाराध्या","samasa":["• महान् च असौ यागः स एव क्रमः। तेन आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["महान् — great","च — and","असौ — this; that","यागः — sacrifice; worship","एव — itself; alone","क्रमः। — method; sequence","तेन — by that; through that","आराध्या। — to be worshipped","महायागक्रमाराध्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महायागक्रमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by the sequence of the great sacrifice. Mahāyāga is the worship of Śrīdevī together with the sixty-four yoginīs and gives quicker results than other methods. In this worship, the body is contemplated as Śrīdevī, with the organs and inner consciousness as yoginīs. Kramā means energy, arrangement, movement and shaking; as yāgakramā, She is worshipped through the powerful method called Mahāyāga."],"searchText":"230 महायागक्रमाराध्या • महान् च असौ यागः स एव क्रमः। तेन आराध्या। महान् — great च — and असौ — this; that यागः — sacrifice; worship एव — itself; alone क्रमः। — method; sequence तेन — by that; through that आराध्या। — to be worshipped महायागक्रमाराध्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above महायागक्रमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by the sequence of the great sacrifice. mahāyāga is the worship of śrīdevī together with the sixty-four yoginīs and gives quicker results than other methods. in this worship, the body is contemplated as śrīdevī, with the organs and inner consciousness as yoginīs. kramā means energy, arrangement, movement and shaking; as yāgakramā, she is worshipped through the powerful method called mahāyāga. the internal homa: the great sacrifice (mahāyāga) is the internal process where the seeker offers limited personal thoughts into the fire of pure awareness. she is worshipped through this sequence because this non-dual sacrifice dissolves individual separation.","esoteric":["The Internal Homa: The great sacrifice (mahāyāga) is the internal process where the seeker offers limited personal thoughts into the fire of pure awareness. She is worshipped through this sequence because this non-dual sacrifice dissolves individual separation."]},{"number":231,"name":"महाभैरवपूजिता","samasa":["• महान् च असौ भैरवश्च। तेन पूजिता।"],"wordByWord":["महान् — great","च — and","असौ — this; that","भैरवश्च। — and Bhairava","तेन — by that; through that","पूजिता। — worshipped","महाभैरवपूजिता — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महाभैरवपूजिता means one who is worshipped by Mahābhairava. Bhairava indicates the one who performs creation, preservation and destruction, and therefore points to Paramaśiva. Mahābhairava worships Śrīdevī as mantra-śakti and caused Her to manifest from the fire altar of consciousness through the great sacrifice. Bhairava may also mean a group of frightened women; She is worshipped by them as well."],"searchText":"231 महाभैरवपूजिता • महान् च असौ भैरवश्च। तेन पूजिता। महान् — great च — and असौ — this; that भैरवश्च। — and bhairava तेन — by that; through that पूजिता। — worshipped महाभैरवपूजिता — the full name, understood through the samasa above महाभैरवपूजिता means one who is worshipped by mahābhairava. bhairava indicates the one who performs creation, preservation and destruction, and therefore points to paramaśiva. mahābhairava worships śrīdevī as mantra-śakti and caused her to manifest from the fire altar of consciousness through the great sacrifice. bhairava may also mean a group of frightened women; she is worshipped by them as well. the absolute reciprocity: mahābhairava is the grand absolute aspect of transcendent consciousness. his worship of her shows that dynamic energy and witness-awareness mutually adore each other and maintain the ultimate cosmic balance.","esoteric":["The Absolute Reciprocity: Mahābhairava is the grand absolute aspect of transcendent consciousness. His worship of Her shows that dynamic energy and witness-awareness mutually adore each other and maintain the ultimate cosmic balance."]},{"number":232,"name":"महेश्वरमहाकल्पमहाताण्डवसाक्षिणी","samasa":["• महेश्वरस्य महाकल्पे यन्महाताण्डवं तस्य साक्षिणी।"],"wordByWord":["महेश्वरस्य — of Maheshvara","महाकल्पे — in the great cosmic cycle","यन्महाताण्डवं — the great Tandava which","तस्य — of that; his","साक्षिणी। — witness","महेश्वरमहाकल्पमहाताण्डवसाक्षिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महेश्वरमहाकल्पमहाताण्डवसाक्षिणी means one who witnesses the great cosmic dance of Maheśvara at the end of the creative cycle. Mahākalpa is the great dissolution in which the universe is submerged into the Lord. Maheśvara performs the mahātāṇḍava at that time, and Śrīdevī remains the sole witness from creation until complete destruction. When Maheśvara performs tāṇḍava, Śrīdevī performs lāsya. Through their compassionate movement, the fifth function, anugraha, begins and the universe is recreated."],"searchText":"232 महेश्वरमहाकल्पमहाताण्डवसाक्षिणी • महेश्वरस्य महाकल्पे यन्महाताण्डवं तस्य साक्षिणी। महेश्वरस्य — of maheshvara महाकल्पे — in the great cosmic cycle यन्महाताण्डवं — the great tandava which तस्य — of that; his साक्षिणी। — witness महेश्वरमहाकल्पमहाताण्डवसाक्षिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above महेश्वरमहाकल्पमहाताण्डवसाक्षिणी means one who witnesses the great cosmic dance of maheśvara at the end of the creative cycle. mahākalpa is the great dissolution in which the universe is submerged into the lord. maheśvara performs the mahātāṇḍava at that time, and śrīdevī remains the sole witness from creation until complete destruction. when maheśvara performs tāṇḍava, śrīdevī performs lāsya. through their compassionate movement, the fifth function, anugraha, begins and the universe is recreated. the sole survivor of dissolution: when the manifest universe dissolves in mahākalpa and maheśvara performs the mahātāṇḍava, she stands as sākṣiṇī, the unmoving awareness that remains untouched by the end of time.","esoteric":["The Sole Survivor of Dissolution: When the manifest universe dissolves in mahākalpa and Maheśvara performs the mahātāṇḍava, She stands as Sākṣiṇī, the unmoving awareness that remains untouched by the end of time."]},{"number":233,"name":"महाकामेशमहिषी","samasa":["• महतः कामस्य ईशस्य महिषी।"],"wordByWord":["महतः — of the great","कामस्य — of Kama; desire","ईशस्य — of the Lord","महिषी। — queen; consort","महाकामेशमहिषी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महाकामेशमहिषी means one who is the consort and crowned queen of Mahākāmeśvara. She is the great empress of Mahākāmeśvara and shares His supreme sovereignty."],"searchText":"233 महाकामेशमहिषी • महतः कामस्य ईशस्य महिषी। महतः — of the great कामस्य — of kama; desire ईशस्य — of the lord महिषी। — queen; consort महाकामेशमहिषी — the full name, understood through the samasa above महाकामेशमहिषी means one who is the consort and crowned queen of mahākāmeśvara. she is the great empress of mahākāmeśvara and shares his supreme sovereignty. the authority of will: a mahiṣī is the crowned queen with sovereign authority. as the mahiṣī of the supreme lord of consciousness, she holds authority over the creation and deployment of cosmic law.","esoteric":["The Authority of Will: A mahiṣī is the crowned queen with sovereign authority. As the mahiṣī of the supreme Lord of consciousness, She holds authority over the creation and deployment of cosmic law."]},{"number":234,"name":"महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी","samasa":["• त्रयाणां पुरं तदात्मिका च सा महती च सा सुन्दरी च।"],"wordByWord":["त्रयाणां — of three","पुरं — city; body; state","तदात्मिका — having that as her nature","च — and","सा — she","महती — great","सुन्दरी — beautiful one","च। — and","महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी means the great Tripurasundarī. She takes the three forms of knower, knowledge and known. The intellect differs according to the person and object, but divine knowledge is the base and root cause of all knowledge. She is that Mahātripurā, unchanged by becoming knower or known, and She is also supreme beauty. Her beauty is so great that it cannot be found in any of the three worlds."],"searchText":"234 महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी • त्रयाणां पुरं तदात्मिका च सा महती च सा सुन्दरी च। त्रयाणां — of three पुरं — city; body; state तदात्मिका — having that as her nature च — and सा — she महती — great सुन्दरी — beautiful one च। — and महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी — the full name, understood through the samasa above महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी means the great tripurasundarī. she takes the three forms of knower, knowledge and known. the intellect differs according to the person and object, but divine knowledge is the base and root cause of all knowledge. she is that mahātripurā, unchanged by becoming knower or known, and she is also supreme beauty. her beauty is so great that it cannot be found in any of the three worlds. the sovereign of the three states: tripurā refers to the three states of consciousness, the three worlds and the three parts of mantra. she is sundarī because she harmonizes these three dimensions as the transcendent fourth state, turīya.","esoteric":["The Sovereign of the Three States: Tripurā refers to the three states of consciousness, the three worlds and the three parts of mantra. She is Sundarī because She harmonizes these three dimensions as the transcendent fourth state, turīya."]},{"number":235,"name":"चतुःषष्ट्युपचाराढ्या","samasa":["• चतुरधिका षष्टिः तावद्भिः उपचारैः आढ्या।"],"wordByWord":["चतुरधिका — four more than","षष्टिः — sixty","तावद्भिः — by that many","उपचारैः — offerings; services","आढ्या। — endowed with","चतुःषष्ट्युपचाराढ्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चतुःषष्ट्युपचाराढ्या means one who is worshipped with sixty-four services. Ordinary worship may use five or sixteen upacāras, but Her worship expands this to sixty-four offerings. The five offerings are sandal, flowers, incense, lamp and food. The sixteen include meditation, invocation, seat, washing of feet, arghya, water, bathing, clothing, fragrance, flowers, incense, lamp, food, ārati, circumambulation and prostration. The sixty-four services elaborate these with bathing, adornment, garments, ornaments, weapons, footwear, seat, nectar, tāmbūla, auspicious lights, umbrella, fan, mirror, music, sandal, flowers, incense, lamp and food. If all items are not available, flowers or unbroken colored rice may be used with mental offering."],"searchText":"235 चतुःषष्ट्युपचाराढ्या • चतुरधिका षष्टिः तावद्भिः उपचारैः आढ्या। चतुरधिका — four more than षष्टिः — sixty तावद्भिः — by that many उपचारैः — offerings; services आढ्या। — endowed with चतुःषष्ट्युपचाराढ्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above चतुःषष्ट्युपचाराढ्या means one who is worshipped with sixty-four services. ordinary worship may use five or sixteen upacāras, but her worship expands this to sixty-four offerings. the five offerings are sandal, flowers, incense, lamp and food. the sixteen include meditation, invocation, seat, washing of feet, arghya, water, bathing, clothing, fragrance, flowers, incense, lamp, food, ārati, circumambulation and prostration. the sixty-four services elaborate these with bathing, adornment, garments, ornaments, weapons, footwear, seat, nectar, tāmbūla, auspicious lights, umbrella, fan, mirror, music, sandal, flowers, incense, lamp and food. if all items are not available, flowers or unbroken colored rice may be used with mental offering. the sacredness of art and action: the sixty-four offerings show that worship includes refined service, beauty, adornment, sound, food and gesture. every careful act becomes an offering to her presence.","esoteric":["The Sacredness of Art and Action: The sixty-four offerings show that worship includes refined service, beauty, adornment, sound, food and gesture. Every careful act becomes an offering to Her presence."]},{"number":236,"name":"चतुष्षष्टिकलामयी","samasa":["• चतुरधिका षष्टिः कलाः अस्या अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["चतुरधिका — four more than","षष्टिः — sixty","कलाः — arts; digits; powers","अस्या — of her","अस्तीति। — exists; is present","चतुष्षष्टिकलामयी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चतुष्षष्टिकलामयी means one who embodies the sixty-four arts. She has all arts in Her form. The sixty-four arts are listed in different ways and include knowledge of scripts and languages, writing, drawing, composing verses, repeating what is heard, games, sacred knowledge, auxiliary sciences, systems of philosophy, grammar, astronomy, poetry, drama, magic, training animals and vehicles, bodily marks, cooking, removing poison, music, dancing, singing, alchemy, testing gems, thieving, pulse-reading and disappearance. Kalā can also mean tantra, and She has all these as Her form."],"searchText":"236 चतुष्षष्टिकलामयी • चतुरधिका षष्टिः कलाः अस्या अस्तीति। चतुरधिका — four more than षष्टिः — sixty कलाः — arts; digits; powers अस्या — of her अस्तीति। — exists; is present चतुष्षष्टिकलामयी — the full name, understood through the samasa above चतुष्षष्टिकलामयी means one who embodies the sixty-four arts. she has all arts in her form. the sixty-four arts are listed in different ways and include knowledge of scripts and languages, writing, drawing, composing verses, repeating what is heard, games, sacred knowledge, auxiliary sciences, systems of philosophy, grammar, astronomy, poetry, drama, magic, training animals and vehicles, bodily marks, cooking, removing poison, music, dancing, singing, alchemy, testing gems, thieving, pulse-reading and disappearance. kalā can also mean tantra, and she has all these as her form. the matrix of culture and intellect: she is the underlying repository of all intellectual and artistic faculties. every science, song, craft and refined skill explores a part of her expressive power.","esoteric":["The Matrix of Culture and Intellect: She is the underlying repository of all intellectual and artistic faculties. Every science, song, craft and refined skill explores a part of Her expressive power."]},{"number":237,"name":"महाचतुष्षष्टिकोटियोगिनीगणसेविता","samasa":["• चतुष्षष्टिकोटिसङ्ख्यकाः योगिनीनां गणाः। तैः महद्भिः सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["चतुष्षष्टिकोटिसङ्ख्यकाः — numbering sixty-four crores","योगिनीनां — of Yoginis","गणाः। — hosts; groups","महद्भिः — by great","सेविता। — served; worshipped","महाचतुष्षष्टिकोटियोगिनीगणसेविता — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["महाचतुष्षष्टिकोटियोगिनीगणसेविता means one who is served by the hosts of sixty-four crore yoginīs. In the middle layer of Śrīcakra are eight prakaṭa yoginīs identified with the Mātṛkā devīs: Brāhmī, Māheśvarī, Kaumārī, Vaiṣṇavī, Vārāhī, Māhendrī, Cāmuṇḍā and Mahālakṣmī. Each has eight allied yoginīs, and each of those has one crore attendants, making sixty-four crores. Mahā may also mean nine; across the nine āvaraṇas, the number becomes 576 crores. Śrīdevī is served and worshipped by these yoginīs."],"searchText":"237 महाचतुष्षष्टिकोटियोगिनीगणसेविता • चतुष्षष्टिकोटिसङ्ख्यकाः योगिनीनां गणाः। तैः महद्भिः सेविता। चतुष्षष्टिकोटिसङ्ख्यकाः — numbering sixty-four crores योगिनीनां — of yoginis गणाः। — hosts; groups महद्भिः — by great सेविता। — served; worshipped महाचतुष्षष्टिकोटियोगिनीगणसेविता — the full name, understood through the samasa above महाचतुष्षष्टिकोटियोगिनीगणसेविता means one who is served by the hosts of sixty-four crore yoginīs. in the middle layer of śrīcakra are eight prakaṭa yoginīs identified with the mātṛkā devīs: brāhmī, māheśvarī, kaumārī, vaiṣṇavī, vārāhī, māhendrī, cāmuṇḍā and mahālakṣmī. each has eight allied yoginīs, and each of those has one crore attendants, making sixty-four crores. mahā may also mean nine; across the nine āvaraṇas, the number becomes 576 crores. śrīdevī is served and worshipped by these yoginīs. the grid of cosmic forces: the sixty-four crores of yoginīs represent vast streams of kinetic power. she sits at the center of this network as its commanding presence, served by every current of energy.","esoteric":["The Grid of Cosmic Forces: The sixty-four crores of yoginīs represent vast streams of kinetic power. She sits at the center of this network as its commanding presence, served by every current of energy."]},{"number":238,"name":"मनुविद्या","samasa":["• मनुविद्या।"],"wordByWord":["मनुविद्या। — the Vidya of Manu","मनुविद्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["मनुविद्या means one who is in the form of the vidyā adored by Manu. Śrīvidyā was adored by twelve devotees: Manu, Candra, Kubera, Lopāmudrā, Agastya, Manmatha, Agni, Sūrya, Indra, स्कन्द, Śiva and Durvāsas. Each realized a form of mantra through penance and worshipped Her. Manu is foremost among them, and Śrīdevī is the form of the Śrīvidyā mantra revealed through him."],"searchText":"238 मनुविद्या • मनुविद्या। मनुविद्या। — the vidya of manu मनुविद्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above मनुविद्या means one who is in the form of the vidyā adored by manu. śrīvidyā was adored by twelve devotees: manu, candra, kubera, lopāmudrā, agastya, manmatha, agni, sūrya, indra, स्कन्द, śiva and durvāsas. each realized a form of mantra through penance and worshipped her. manu is foremost among them, and śrīdevī is the form of the śrīvidyā mantra revealed through him. the lineage of the primordial lawgiver: manu is the primordial lawgiver of cosmic order. manu-vidyā identifies her with the wisdom that sustains moral and structural balance across human eras.","esoteric":["The Lineage of the Primordial Lawgiver: Manu is the primordial lawgiver of cosmic order. Manu-vidyā identifies Her with the wisdom that sustains moral and structural balance across human eras."]},{"number":239,"name":"चन्द्रविद्या","samasa":["• चन्द्रविद्या।"],"wordByWord":["चन्द्रविद्या। — the Vidya of Chandra","चन्द्रविद्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चन्द्रविद्या means the vidyā adored by Candra. Candra is the second of the twelve devotees connected with Śrīvidyā, and this name refers to the form of vidyā associated with him."],"searchText":"239 चन्द्रविद्या • चन्द्रविद्या। चन्द्रविद्या। — the vidya of chandra चन्द्रविद्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above चन्द्रविद्या means the vidyā adored by candra. candra is the second of the twelve devotees connected with śrīvidyā, and this name refers to the form of vidyā associated with him. the path of lunar bliss: candra-vidyā is the lunar path of śrīvidyā. it emphasizes cool, soothing inner bliss and balances the fires of intellect and action.","esoteric":["The Path of Lunar Bliss: Candra-vidyā is the lunar path of Śrīvidyā. It emphasizes cool, soothing inner bliss and balances the fires of intellect and action."]},{"number":240,"name":"चन्द्रमण्डलमध्यगा","samasa":["• चन्द्रमण्डलस्य मध्यं गच्छन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["चन्द्रमण्डलस्य — of the lunar disc","मध्यं — middle; centre","गच्छन्तीति। — goes; abides","चन्द्रमण्डलमध्यगा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चन्द्रमण्डलमध्यगा means one who dwells in the centre of the moon's disc. The full moon is contemplated as Her abode. Śrīdevī, awakened from the mūlādhāra, pierces the six cakras and reaches the Lord. Contemplating Her in the lunar disc on a full-moon day and worshipping Her with the sahasranāma grants long life free from disease. The moon's disc is also understood as Śrīcakra itself, and She is meditated upon there during Śrīvidyā sandhyāvandana."],"searchText":"240 चन्द्रमण्डलमध्यगा • चन्द्रमण्डलस्य मध्यं गच्छन्तीति। चन्द्रमण्डलस्य — of the lunar disc मध्यं — middle; centre गच्छन्तीति। — goes; abides चन्द्रमण्डलमध्यगा — the full name, understood through the samasa above चन्द्रमण्डलमध्यगा means one who dwells in the centre of the moon's disc. the full moon is contemplated as her abode. śrīdevī, awakened from the mūlādhāra, pierces the six cakras and reaches the lord. contemplating her in the lunar disc on a full-moon day and worshipping her with the sahasranāma grants long life free from disease. the moon's disc is also understood as śrīcakra itself, and she is meditated upon there during śrīvidyā sandhyāvandana. the core of the crown nectar: in subtle yoga, the candra-maṇḍala is the radiant lunar orb in the sahasrāra. she sits at its core, generating supreme life-giving spiritual joy.","esoteric":["The Core of the Crown Nectar: In subtle yoga, the candra-maṇḍala is the radiant lunar orb in the sahasrāra. She sits at its core, generating supreme life-giving spiritual joy."]},{"number":241,"name":"चारुरूपा","samasa":["• चारु रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["चारु — beautiful; charming","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","चारुरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चारुरूपा means one who has a beautiful form. Her beauty is indicated by names such as Tripurasundarī, Lalitā and Sundarī."],"searchText":"241 चारुरूपा • चारु रूपं यस्याः सा। चारु — beautiful; charming रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she चारुरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above चारुरूपा means one who has a beautiful form. her beauty is indicated by names such as tripurasundarī, lalitā and sundarī. the harmony of reality: cāru implies beauty that satisfies the mind and brings peace. her form embodies the harmony of truth and balances the thoughts of the observer.","esoteric":["The Harmony of Reality: Cāru implies beauty that satisfies the mind and brings peace. Her form embodies the harmony of truth and balances the thoughts of the observer."]},{"number":242,"name":"चारुहासा","samasa":["• चारु हासं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["चारु — beautiful; charming","हासं — smile","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","चारुहासा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चारुहासा means one who has a charming smile. Her smile is like the moon and points to a stage of awakened consciousness, prabodha, that gives the highest bliss and is to be known from a teacher."],"searchText":"242 चारुहासा • चारु हासं यस्याः सा। चारु — beautiful; charming हासं — smile यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she चारुहासा — the full name, understood through the samasa above चारुहासा means one who has a charming smile. her smile is like the moon and points to a stage of awakened consciousness, prabodha, that gives the highest bliss and is to be known from a teacher. the smile of liberation: her gentle smile represents the dawn of spiritual awakening. when she smiles upon the seeker's intellect, ignorance lifts and the light of realization appears.","esoteric":["The Smile of Liberation: Her gentle smile represents the dawn of spiritual awakening. When She smiles upon the seeker's intellect, ignorance lifts and the light of realization appears."]},{"number":243,"name":"चारुचन्द्रकलाधरा","samasa":["• चार्व्याः चन्द्रस्य कलायाः धरा।"],"wordByWord":["चार्व्याः — of the beautiful","चन्द्रस्य — of the moon","कलायाः — of the digit/crescent","धरा। — bearer","चारुचन्द्रकलाधरा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चारुचन्द्रकलाधरा means one who wears a beautiful crescent moon in Her crown. Cāru can indicate that which neither waxes nor wanes, and candrakalā is the everlasting lunar digit; in that sense She is the basis of the candrakalā. The name also recalls the princess Candrakalā, whose happiness came through Śrīdevī's grace."],"searchText":"243 चारुचन्द्रकलाधरा • चार्व्याः चन्द्रस्य कलायाः धरा। चार्व्याः — of the beautiful चन्द्रस्य — of the moon कलायाः — of the digit/crescent धरा। — bearer चारुचन्द्रकलाधरा — the full name, understood through the samasa above चारुचन्द्रकलाधरा means one who wears a beautiful crescent moon in her crown. cāru can indicate that which neither waxes nor wanes, and candrakalā is the everlasting lunar digit; in that sense she is the basis of the candrakalā. the name also recalls the princess candrakalā, whose happiness came through śrīdevī's grace. the beacon of time and balance: the crescent moon digit (candrakalā) represents time and the balance of nāda. by wearing it on her head, she rules the cycles of time while remaining still beyond time.","esoteric":["The Beacon of Time and Balance: The crescent moon digit (candrakalā) represents time and the balance of nāda. By wearing it on Her head, She rules the cycles of time while remaining still beyond time."]},{"number":244,"name":"चराचरजगन्नाथा","samasa":["• चरं चाचरं च चराचरं जगत्। तस्य नाथा।"],"wordByWord":["चरं — moving; animate","चाचरं — and unmoving; inanimate","च — and","चराचरं — moving and unmoving","जगत्। — world","तस्य — of that; his","नाथा। — mistress; ruler","चराचरजगन्नाथा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चराचरजगन्नाथा means one who is the mistress of the moving and unmoving world. The world has both dynamic and inert forms, and She is the head of both."],"searchText":"244 चराचरजगन्नाथा • चरं चाचरं च चराचरं जगत्। तस्य नाथा। चरं — moving; animate चाचरं — and unmoving; inanimate च — and चराचरं — moving and unmoving जगत्। — world तस्य — of that; his नाथा। — mistress; ruler चराचरजगन्नाथा — the full name, understood through the samasa above चराचरजगन्नाथा means one who is the mistress of the moving and unmoving world. the world has both dynamic and inert forms, and she is the head of both. the universal guardian: cara represents moving beings, while acara represents unmoving forms. as nāthā, she provides the order, support and consciousness for both.","esoteric":["The Universal Guardian: Cara represents moving beings, while acara represents unmoving forms. As Nāthā, She provides the order, support and consciousness for both."]},{"number":245,"name":"चक्रराजनिकेतना","samasa":["• चक्रराजम् एव निकेतनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["चक्रराजम् — the king of Chakras; Sri Chakra","एव — itself; alone","निकेतनं — abode","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","चक्रराजनिकेतना — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चक्रराजनिकेतना means one who abides in Śrīcakra. Śrīcakra is called Cakrarāja, the king of cakras, because it contains the nine cakras from Trailokyamohana to Sarvānandamaya. She dwells in it with all Her attendants."],"searchText":"245 चक्रराजनिकेतना • चक्रराजम् एव निकेतनं यस्याः सा। चक्रराजम् — the king of chakras; sri chakra एव — itself; alone निकेतनं — abode यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she चक्रराजनिकेतना — the full name, understood through the samasa above चक्रराजनिकेतना means one who abides in śrīcakra. śrīcakra is called cakrarāja, the king of cakras, because it contains the nine cakras from trailokyamohana to sarvānandamaya. she dwells in it with all her attendants. the abode of geometry: śrīcakra is her house of patterns. every enclosure, triangle and bindu represents a layer of her consciousness and a path for the seeker.","esoteric":["The Abode of Geometry: Śrīcakra is Her house of patterns. Every enclosure, triangle and bindu represents a layer of Her consciousness and a path for the seeker."]},{"number":246,"name":"पार्वती","samasa":["• पर्वतस्यापत्यं स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["पर्वतस्यापत्यं — daughter of the mountain","स्त्री। — female; woman","पार्वती — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["पार्वती means the daughter of Mount Himavān, king of mountains. She is also called Śailendratanayā."],"searchText":"246 पार्वती • पर्वतस्यापत्यं स्त्री। पर्वतस्यापत्यं — daughter of the mountain स्त्री। — female; woman पार्वती — the full name, understood through the samasa above पार्वती means the daughter of mount himavān, king of mountains. she is also called śailendratanayā. the solid base of energy: mountains represent stability, height and strength. as pārvatī, her dynamic energy is anchored in the highest spiritual steadiness.","esoteric":["The Solid Base of Energy: Mountains represent stability, height and strength. As Pārvatī, Her dynamic energy is anchored in the highest spiritual steadiness."]},{"number":247,"name":"पद्मनयना","samasa":["• पद्म इव नयने यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पद्म — lotus","इव — like","नयने — eyes","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","पद्मनयना — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["पद्मनयना means one whose eyes are like lotuses."],"searchText":"247 पद्मनयना • पद्म इव नयने यस्याः सा। पद्म — lotus इव — like नयने — eyes यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she पद्मनयना — the full name, understood through the samasa above पद्मनयना means one whose eyes are like lotuses. the glance of open awareness: lotuses open to the sun and remain clean above muddy water. her lotus eyes suggest compassion and pure awareness looking upon all beings.","esoteric":["The Glance of Open Awareness: Lotuses open to the sun and remain clean above muddy water. Her lotus eyes suggest compassion and pure awareness looking upon all beings."]},{"number":248,"name":"पद्मरागसमप्रभा","samasa":["• पद्मरागस्य समा प्रभा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पद्मरागस्य — of ruby","समा — equal; similar","प्रभा — lustre","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","पद्मरागसमप्रभा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["पद्मरागसमप्रभा means one who shines like ruby. Padma also means lotus, and Her lustre is comparable to the red colour of the lotus."],"searchText":"248 पद्मरागसमप्रभा • पद्मरागस्य समा प्रभा यस्याः सा। पद्मरागस्य — of ruby समा — equal; similar प्रभा — lustre यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she पद्मरागसमप्रभा — the full name, understood through the samasa above पद्मरागसमप्रभा means one who shines like ruby. padma also means lotus, and her lustre is comparable to the red colour of the lotus. the fire of pure awareness: the ruby-like padmarāga glow is deep red and luminous. she radiates this crimson light as the warmth and vitality of consciousness.","esoteric":["The Fire of Pure Awareness: The ruby-like padmarāga glow is deep red and luminous. She radiates this crimson light as the warmth and vitality of consciousness."]},{"number":249,"name":"पञ्चप्रेतासनासीना","samasa":["• पञ्च प्रेताः वा पञ्चानां प्रेतानां समूहः एव आसनं तस्मिन् आसीना।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्च — five","प्रेताः — corpses","वा — or","पञ्चानां — of five","प्रेतानां — of corpses","समूहः — group","एव — itself; alone","आसनं — seat","तस्मिन् — in that","आसीना। — seated","पञ्चप्रेतासनासीना — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["पञ्चप्रेतासनासीना means one seated on a throne formed of five corpses. The five forms of Śiva, namely Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra, Īśāna and Sadāśiva, arise from Brahman and perform creation, protection, destruction, concealment and grace by Śrīdevī's command. During dissolution they are relieved of their functions and merge in Her; deprived of power, they are called corpses. Sadāśiva becomes the seat plank and the other four become its legs. Their śaktis are Vāmā, Jyeṣṭhā, Raudrī and others; without these śaktis they cannot act. When Śakti unites with Paramaśiva, it becomes the samarasyā form without difference."],"searchText":"249 पञ्चप्रेतासनासीना • पञ्च प्रेताः वा पञ्चानां प्रेतानां समूहः एव आसनं तस्मिन् आसीना। पञ्च — five प्रेताः — corpses वा — or पञ्चानां — of five प्रेतानां — of corpses समूहः — group एव — itself; alone आसनं — seat तस्मिन् — in that आसीना। — seated पञ्चप्रेतासनासीना — the full name, understood through the samasa above पञ्चप्रेतासनासीना means one seated on a throne formed of five corpses. the five forms of śiva, namely brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra, īśāna and sadāśiva, arise from brahman and perform creation, protection, destruction, concealment and grace by śrīdevī's command. during dissolution they are relieved of their functions and merge in her; deprived of power, they are called corpses. sadāśiva becomes the seat plank and the other four become its legs. their śaktis are vāmā, jyeṣṭhā, raudrī and others; without these śaktis they cannot act. when śakti unites with paramaśiva, it becomes the samarasyā form without difference. the lord of inactive principles: the five pretas are brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra, īśvara and sadāśiva when separated from active energy. without her śakti, even these cosmic principles are inert; she sits upon them as the power that awakens and directs them.","esoteric":["The Lord of Inactive Principles: The five pretas are Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra, Īśvara and Sadāśiva when separated from active energy. Without Her śakti, even these cosmic principles are inert; She sits upon them as the power that awakens and directs them."]},{"number":250,"name":"पञ्चब्रह्मस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• पञ्च ब्रह्माणः स्वरूपं अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्च — five","ब्रह्माणः — Brahmas","स्वरूपं — essential form","अस्याः — of her","अस्तीति। — exists; is present","पञ्चब्रह्मस्वरूपिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["पञ्चब्रह्मस्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the five Brahmans. Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra, Īśāna and Paramaśiva are the five Brahmans and form Her seat; She is their very form. The five faces of Parameśvara, Īśāna, Tatpuruṣa, Aghora, Vāmadeva and Sadyojāta, are also called the five Brahmans, and She is their form. Soul, nature, intellect, ego and mind are also forms of Brahman, and She is present in those five forms. She is in the form of anything composed of five elements."],"searchText":"250 पञ्चब्रह्मस्वरूपिणी • पञ्च ब्रह्माणः स्वरूपं अस्याः अस्तीति। पञ्च — five ब्रह्माणः — brahmas स्वरूपं — essential form अस्याः — of her अस्तीति। — exists; is present पञ्चब्रह्मस्वरूपिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above पञ्चब्रह्मस्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the five brahmans. brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra, īśāna and paramaśiva are the five brahmans and form her seat; she is their very form. the five faces of parameśvara, īśāna, tatpuruṣa, aghora, vāmadeva and sadyojāta, are also called the five brahmans, and she is their form. soul, nature, intellect, ego and mind are also forms of brahman, and she is present in those five forms. she is in the form of anything composed of five elements. the core of cosmic functions: this complements the previous name. in her active state, she projects herself as the five great cosmic duties: creation, preservation, destruction, concealment and grace.","esoteric":["The Core of Cosmic Functions: This complements the previous name. In Her active state, She projects Herself as the five great cosmic duties: creation, preservation, destruction, concealment and grace."]},{"number":251,"name":"चिन्मयी","samasa":["• चिद् एव।"],"wordByWord":["चिद् — pure consciousness","एव। — itself; alone","चिन्मयी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["चिन्मयी means one who is in the form of cit, pure consciousness itself. The word cit means knowledge. She is knowledge itself, pure knowledge without distinction between knower, known and intellect."],"searchText":"251 चिन्मयी • चिद् एव। चिद् — pure consciousness एव। — itself; alone चिन्मयी — the full name, understood through the samasa above चिन्मयी means one who is in the form of cit, pure consciousness itself. the word cit means knowledge. she is knowledge itself, pure knowledge without distinction between knower, known and intellect. the homogeneous light: she does not merely possess consciousness; she is consciousness itself. her core identity is clean, non-dual light that illumines all thoughts.","esoteric":["The Homogeneous Light: She does not merely possess consciousness; She is consciousness itself. Her core identity is clean, non-dual light that illumines all thoughts."]},{"number":252,"name":"परमानन्दा","samasa":["• परमश्च असौ आनन्दा च।"],"wordByWord":["परमश्च — and supreme","असौ — this; that","आनन्दा — bliss","च। — and","परमानन्दा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["परमानन्दा means one who is supreme bliss. She is the completely contented form, and nothing is greater than this bliss."],"searchText":"252 परमानन्दा • परमश्च असौ आनन्दा च। परमश्च — and supreme असौ — this; that आनन्दा — bliss च। — and परमानन्दा — the full name, understood through the samasa above परमानन्दा means one who is supreme bliss. she is the completely contented form, and nothing is greater than this bliss. unconditioned ecstasy: worldly happiness depends on external objects and passes quickly. she is paramānandā because her joy is independent of external conditions, the steady self-contained ecstasy of non-dual reality.","esoteric":["Unconditioned Ecstasy: Worldly happiness depends on external objects and passes quickly. She is Paramānandā because Her joy is independent of external conditions, the steady self-contained ecstasy of non-dual reality."]},{"number":253,"name":"विज्ञानघनरूपिणी","samasa":["• विज्ञानमेव घनं रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति।","• विज्ञानैः (जीवैः) घनं रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["विज्ञानमेव — knowledge itself","घनं — solid mass; compact","अस्याः — of her","अस्तीति। — exists; is present","विज्ञानघनरूपिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["विज्ञानघनरूपिणी means one who is wisdom personified. She is the essence of consciousness. The soul, as vijñāna reflected in the intellect, is the self; the aggregate of such souls is vijñānaghana. Śrīdevī is in that form. Hiraṇyagarbha is the collective synthesis of souls, and She is also in that form."],"searchText":"253 विज्ञानघनरूपिणी • विज्ञानमेव घनं रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति। • विज्ञानैः (जीवैः) घनं रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति। विज्ञानमेव — knowledge itself घनं — solid mass; compact अस्याः — of her अस्तीति। — exists; is present विज्ञानघनरूपिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above विज्ञानघनरूपिणी means one who is wisdom personified. she is the essence of consciousness. the soul, as vijñāna reflected in the intellect, is the self; the aggregate of such souls is vijñānaghana. śrīdevī is in that form. hiraṇyagarbha is the collective synthesis of souls, and she is also in that form. the solid mass of awareness: ghana means dense and uniform. her awareness has no hollow pockets or gaps of ignorance; it is a completely packed field of pure intuitive wisdom.","esoteric":["The Solid Mass of Awareness: Ghana means dense and uniform. Her awareness has no hollow pockets or gaps of ignorance; it is a completely packed field of pure intuitive wisdom."]},{"number":254,"name":"ध्यानध्यातृध्येयरूपा","samasa":["• ध्यानं च ध्याता च ध्येयश्च रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["ध्यानं — meditation","च — and","ध्याता — meditator","ध्येयश्च — and the object meditated upon","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","ध्यानध्यातृध्येयरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["ध्यानध्यातृध्येयरूपा means one who is the form of meditation, meditator and object of meditation. Meditation is the mind's understanding of Śrīdevī, imagining Her form and merging into it. Just as knowledge has a threefold structure, She is the form of this entire triad."],"searchText":"254 ध्यानध्यातृध्येयरूपा • ध्यानं च ध्याता च ध्येयश्च रूपं यस्याः सा। ध्यानं — meditation च — and ध्याता — meditator ध्येयश्च — and the object meditated upon रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she ध्यानध्यातृध्येयरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above ध्यानध्यातृध्येयरूपा means one who is the form of meditation, meditator and object of meditation. meditation is the mind's understanding of śrīdevī, imagining her form and merging into it. just as knowledge has a threefold structure, she is the form of this entire triad. the dissolution of the triad: in practice there is the meditator, the process of meditation and the divine object. sādhana reaches completion when this tripuṭī dissolves into non-dual unity. she is all three parts.","esoteric":["The Dissolution of the Triad: In practice there is the meditator, the process of meditation and the divine object. Sādhana reaches completion when this tripuṭī dissolves into non-dual unity. She is all three parts."]},{"number":255,"name":"धर्माधर्मविवर्जिता","samasa":["• धर्मश्चाधर्मश्च ताभ्यां विशेषेण वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["धर्मश्चाधर्मश्च — dharma and adharma","ताभ्यां — from/by those two","विशेषेण — especially; completely","वर्जिता। — devoid of","धर्माधर्मविवर्जिता — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["धर्माधर्मविवर्जिता means one who is beyond dharma and adharma. Dharma can mean restraint, social and spiritual discipline, quality, character, or bondage. Breaking such limits is adharma. Śrīdevī is not bound by these distinctions. She is not limited by any quality, character, bondage, or release from bondage. She is beyond both dharma and adharma."],"searchText":"255 धर्माधर्मविवर्जिता • धर्मश्चाधर्मश्च ताभ्यां विशेषेण वर्जिता। धर्मश्चाधर्मश्च — dharma and adharma ताभ्यां — from/by those two विशेषेण — especially; completely वर्जिता। — devoid of धर्माधर्मविवर्जिता — the full name, understood through the samasa above धर्माधर्मविवर्जिता means one who is beyond dharma and adharma. dharma can mean restraint, social and spiritual discipline, quality, character, or bondage. breaking such limits is adharma. śrīdevī is not bound by these distinctions. she is not limited by any quality, character, bondage, or release from bondage. she is beyond both dharma and adharma. the beyond-moral absolute: dharma and adharma govern individual action in the dualistic world. as the supreme whole, she supports these rules without being conditioned by merit and demerit.","esoteric":["The Beyond-Moral Absolute: Dharma and adharma govern individual action in the dualistic world. As the supreme whole, She supports these rules without being conditioned by merit and demerit."]},{"number":256,"name":"विश्वरूपा","samasa":["• विश्वं रूपं यस्याः सा।","• श्वा इव वृत्तिः विगतं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वं — the universe","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","इव — like","विश्वरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["विश्वरूपा means one whose form is the universe. In creation, subtle principles arise from nature and become gross elements. Consciousness manifesting through gross, subtle and causal vehicles is called Viśva, Taijasa and Prājña; collectively these are Vaiśvānara, Hiraṇyagarbha and Īśvara. The waking, dream and deep-sleep states are connected with creation, protection and destruction. Further states connected with concealment and grace are also included. Śrīdevī is the form of all these states and of the universe itself. Viśva also indicates Brahman as the cause and non-different form of the world, and as that which pervades all."],"searchText":"256 विश्वरूपा • विश्वं रूपं यस्याः सा। • श्वा इव वृत्तिः विगतं यस्याः सा। विश्वं — the universe रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she इव — like विश्वरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above विश्वरूपा means one whose form is the universe. in creation, subtle principles arise from nature and become gross elements. consciousness manifesting through gross, subtle and causal vehicles is called viśva, taijasa and prājña; collectively these are vaiśvānara, hiraṇyagarbha and īśvara. the waking, dream and deep-sleep states are connected with creation, protection and destruction. further states connected with concealment and grace are also included. śrīdevī is the form of all these states and of the universe itself. viśva also indicates brahman as the cause and non-different form of the world, and as that which pervades all. the immanent body: she is not separate from creation. every galaxy, planet, tree and atom is within her immense cosmic form; material space itself is her visible body.","esoteric":["The Immanent Body: She is not separate from creation. Every galaxy, planet, tree and atom is within Her immense cosmic form; material space itself is Her visible body."]},{"number":257,"name":"जागरिणी","samasa":["• जागर अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["जागर — waking state","अस्याः — of her","अस्तीति। — exists; is present","जागरिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["जागरिणी means one who is in the waking state of the soul. Jāgara means waking, and jāgariṇī is the soul in the conscious state. Her name in this state is Viśvarūpā; therefore She is Jāgariṇī."],"searchText":"257 जागरिणी • जागर अस्याः अस्तीति। जागर — waking state अस्याः — of her अस्तीति। — exists; is present जागरिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above जागरिणी means one who is in the waking state of the soul. jāgara means waking, and jāgariṇī is the soul in the conscious state. her name in this state is viśvarūpā; therefore she is jāgariṇī. the lord of the outward eye: she rules jāgrat-avasthā, the waking state, where the mind looks outward through the gross senses and interacts with physical matter.","esoteric":["The Lord of the Outward Eye: She rules jāgrat-avasthā, the waking state, where the mind looks outward through the gross senses and interacts with physical matter."]},{"number":258,"name":"स्वपन्ती","samasa":["• स्वपितीति।"],"wordByWord":["स्वपितीति। — sleeps; dreams","स्वपन्ती — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["स्वपन्ती means one who is in the dreaming state, where the soul is connected with the subtle body."],"searchText":"258 स्वपन्ती • स्वपितीति। स्वपितीति। — sleeps; dreams स्वपन्ती — the full name, understood through the samasa above स्वपन्ती means one who is in the dreaming state, where the soul is connected with the subtle body. the designer of the subtle canvas: she rules svapna-avasthā, the dreaming state, where the gross senses rest and the mind builds an inner universe from impressions.","esoteric":["The Designer of the Subtle Canvas: She rules svapna-avasthā, the dreaming state, where the gross senses rest and the mind builds an inner universe from impressions."]},{"number":259,"name":"तैजसात्मिका","samasa":["• तैजसाः आत्मा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["तैजसाः — Taijasa; dream-state self","आत्मा — self","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","तैजसात्मिका — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["तैजसात्मिका means one whose self is Taijasa. Śrīdevī is in the dream state, where the individual soul is called Taijasa. In the collective form of souls, Taijasa is called Hiraṇyagarbha, and She is also that form."],"searchText":"259 तैजसात्मिका • तैजसाः आत्मा यस्याः सा। तैजसाः — taijasa; dream-state self आत्मा — self यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she तैजसात्मिका — the full name, understood through the samasa above तैजसात्मिका means one whose self is taijasa. śrīdevī is in the dream state, where the individual soul is called taijasa. in the collective form of souls, taijasa is called hiraṇyagarbha, and she is also that form. the subtle state: taijasa belongs to the dream state, svapna-avasthā, where the mind experiences objects formed from impressions and light. she is the witness and essence of this luminous subtle layer.","esoteric":["The Subtle State: Taijasa belongs to the dream state, svapna-avasthā, where the mind experiences objects formed from impressions and light. She is the witness and essence of this luminous subtle layer."]},{"number":260,"name":"सुप्ता","samasa":["• सुप्ता।"],"wordByWord":["सुप्ता — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["सुप्ता means one who is in the sleep state of the soul."],"searchText":"260 सुप्ता • सुप्ता। सुप्ता — the full name, understood through the samasa above सुप्ता means one who is in the sleep state of the soul. the dormant power: she represents suṣupti, the state of deep dreamless sleep in which mental modifications, names and forms rest in an unmanifest causal condition.","esoteric":["The Dormant Power: She represents suṣupti, the state of deep dreamless sleep in which mental modifications, names and forms rest in an unmanifest causal condition."]},{"number":261,"name":"प्राज्ञात्मिका","samasa":["• प्राज्ञस्य आत्मिका।"],"wordByWord":["प्राज्ञस्य — of Prajna; deep-sleep self","आत्मिका। — whose nature is","प्राज्ञात्मिका — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["प्राज्ञात्मिका means one whose self is Prājña. In deep sleep, the soul connected with the body is called Prājña, and She is that form. Deep sleep includes the experiences of not knowing, the sense of individuality, and happiness remembered on waking as good sleep. The collective form of all such souls is Īśvara, and She is also that form."],"searchText":"261 प्राज्ञात्मिका • प्राज्ञस्य आत्मिका। प्राज्ञस्य — of prajna; deep-sleep self आत्मिका। — whose nature is प्राज्ञात्मिका — the full name, understood through the samasa above प्राज्ञात्मिका means one whose self is prājña. in deep sleep, the soul connected with the body is called prājña, and she is that form. deep sleep includes the experiences of not knowing, the sense of individuality, and happiness remembered on waking as good sleep. the collective form of all such souls is īśvara, and she is also that form. the causal state: prājña belongs to suṣupti, the deep sleep state, where distinctions and mental movements dissolve into causal awareness. she is that underlying causal presence and the witness of the sleeping mind.","esoteric":["The Causal State: Prājña belongs to suṣupti, the deep sleep state, where distinctions and mental movements dissolve into causal awareness. She is that underlying causal presence and the witness of the sleeping mind."]},{"number":262,"name":"तुर्या","samasa":["• तुर्या।"],"wordByWord":["तुर्या। — the fourth state","तुर्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["तुर्या means one who is the soul in the fourth state. The fourth state is the understanding that clearly distinguishes waking, dream and deep sleep and the souls associated with them: Viśva, Taijasa and Prājña. The bliss of this state makes the knower recognize it as the true state. Even while the other states continue according to worldly tendencies, one established in turya is not affected by them. Śrīdevī is this fourth state."],"searchText":"262 तुर्या • तुर्या। तुर्या। — the fourth state तुर्या — the full name, understood through the samasa above तुर्या means one who is the soul in the fourth state. the fourth state is the understanding that clearly distinguishes waking, dream and deep sleep and the souls associated with them: viśva, taijasa and prājña. the bliss of this state makes the knower recognize it as the true state. even while the other states continue according to worldly tendencies, one established in turya is not affected by them. śrīdevī is this fourth state. transcendence of triads: turyā is the consciousness that underlies, pervades and transcends waking, dream and deep sleep. she is the self-luminous fourth, the non-dual awareness on which the other states appear and disappear.","esoteric":["Transcendence of Triads: Turyā is the consciousness that underlies, pervades and transcends waking, dream and deep sleep. She is the self-luminous fourth, the non-dual awareness on which the other states appear and disappear."]},{"number":263,"name":"सर्वावस्थाविवर्जिता","samasa":["• सर्वाभिः अवस्थाभिः विशेषेण वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वाभिः — by all","अवस्थाभिः — states","विशेषेण — especially; completely","वर्जिता। — devoid of","सर्वावस्थाविवर्जिता — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["सर्वावस्थाविवर्जिता means one who is free from all states. Beyond waking, dream, deep sleep and the fourth is the transcendental condition, which is not really a state. Crossing all states, the soul merges in the Supreme Being, Śrīdevī, where there is no individual or collective form. This is beyond mind and speech and can be known only by experience."],"searchText":"263 सर्वावस्थाविवर्जिता • सर्वाभिः अवस्थाभिः विशेषेण वर्जिता। सर्वाभिः — by all अवस्थाभिः — states विशेषेण — especially; completely वर्जिता। — devoid of सर्वावस्थाविवर्जिता — the full name, understood through the samasa above सर्वावस्थाविवर्जिता means one who is free from all states. beyond waking, dream, deep sleep and the fourth is the transcendental condition, which is not really a state. crossing all states, the soul merges in the supreme being, śrīdevī, where there is no individual or collective form. this is beyond mind and speech and can be known only by experience. beyond the states: though she appears as waking, dream, deep sleep and turyā, she is ultimately turyātīta, untouched by all modifications and conditions. states belong to change; she remains the immutable reality.","esoteric":["Beyond the States: Though She appears as waking, dream, deep sleep and turyā, She is ultimately turyātīta, untouched by all modifications and conditions. States belong to change; She remains the immutable reality."]},{"number":264,"name":"सृष्टिकर्त्री","samasa":["• सृष्टेः कर्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["सृष्टेः — of creation","कर्त्री। — doer; creator","सृष्टिकर्त्री — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["सृष्टिकर्त्री means one who performs the task of creation. Creation is the function of Īśvara when rajas predominates. To distinguish forms such as Brahmā from the Supreme Being is māyā."],"searchText":"264 सृष्टिकर्त्री • सृष्टेः कर्त्री। सृष्टेः — of creation कर्त्री। — doer; creator सृष्टिकर्त्री — the full name, understood through the samasa above सृष्टिकर्त्री means one who performs the task of creation. creation is the function of īśvara when rajas predominates. to distinguish forms such as brahmā from the supreme being is māyā. the creative power: though creation is commonly connected with brahmā, the ultimate power belongs to her. she is the śakti that enables the projection of the universe.","esoteric":["The Creative Power: Though creation is commonly connected with Brahmā, the ultimate power belongs to Her. She is the śakti that enables the projection of the universe."]},{"number":265,"name":"ब्रह्मरूपा","samasa":["• ब्रह्मब्रह्मा रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["ब्रह्मब्रह्मा — Brahman/Brahma","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","ब्रह्मरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["ब्रह्मरूपा means one who is in the form of Brahmā. Brahmā performs the work of creation and is a distinguished form of Śrīdevī appearing through māyā."],"searchText":"265 ब्रह्मरूपा • ब्रह्मब्रह्मा रूपं यस्याः सा। ब्रह्मब्रह्मा — brahman/brahma रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she ब्रह्मरूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above ब्रह्मरूपा means one who is in the form of brahmā. brahmā performs the work of creation and is a distinguished form of śrīdevī appearing through māyā. the personal creator: she manifests as brahmā for the work of creation, while remaining the deeper reality on which the universe appears.","esoteric":["The Personal Creator: She manifests as Brahmā for the work of creation, while remaining the deeper reality on which the universe appears."]},{"number":266,"name":"गोप्त्री","samasa":["• गोप्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["गोप्त्री। — protector","गोप्त्री — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["गोप्त्री means one who performs the task of protection. Śrīdevī takes up the function of sustaining the created universe when sattva predominates."],"searchText":"266 गोप्त्री • गोप्त्री। गोप्त्री। — protector गोप्त्री — the full name, understood through the samasa above गोप्त्री means one who performs the task of protection. śrīdevī takes up the function of sustaining the created universe when sattva predominates. sustenance of the cosmos: as the inner sustaining force, she preserves cosmic order during manifestation and keeps the laws of nature and karma in balance.","esoteric":["Sustenance of the Cosmos: As the inner sustaining force, She preserves cosmic order during manifestation and keeps the laws of nature and karma in balance."]},{"number":267,"name":"गोविन्दरूपिणी","samasa":["• गोविन्दस्य रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["गोविन्दस्य — of Govinda","अस्याः — of her","अस्तीति। — exists; is present","गोविन्दरूपिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["गोविन्दरूपिणी means one who is in the form of Govinda, Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu, the protector of the universe in whom sattva predominates, is also Śrīdevī. Go means speech, and Govinda means one who can be understood by speech. The Supreme Being is beyond speech, yet as Govinda, in the protecting function, He responds to the cry of the soul. Govinda can also mean the one who protects and raises the earth, lord of cows, one reached through speech, and one understood through Vedānta."],"searchText":"267 गोविन्दरूपिणी • गोविन्दस्य रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति। गोविन्दस्य — of govinda अस्याः — of her अस्तीति। — exists; is present गोविन्दरूपिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above गोविन्दरूपिणी means one who is in the form of govinda, viṣṇu. viṣṇu, the protector of the universe in whom sattva predominates, is also śrīdevī. go means speech, and govinda means one who can be understood by speech. the supreme being is beyond speech, yet as govinda, in the protecting function, he responds to the cry of the soul. govinda can also mean the one who protects and raises the earth, lord of cows, one reached through speech, and one understood through vedānta. cosmic preservation: to sustain the universe, she assumes sattva-guṇa and manifests as govinda, viṣṇu, the all-pervading protector. go can refer to speech, earth or the senses, and govinda is the one who knows, protects and is reached through them.","esoteric":["Cosmic Preservation: To sustain the universe, She assumes sattva-guṇa and manifests as Govinda, Viṣṇu, the all-pervading protector. Go can refer to speech, earth or the senses, and Govinda is the one who knows, protects and is reached through them."]},{"number":268,"name":"संहारिणी","samasa":["• संहारिणी। संहारं करोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["संहारं — dissolution; destruction","करोतीति। — does; performs","संहारिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["संहारिणी means one who performs the task of destruction. Destruction is the reduction of the universe back into atoms and is the third cosmic function. This is Śrīdevī's function in the form of Īśvara when tamas predominates; therefore She is Saṃhāriṇī."],"searchText":"268 संहारिणी • संहारिणी। संहारं करोतीति। संहारं — dissolution; destruction करोतीति। — does; performs संहारिणी — the full name, understood through the samasa above संहारिणी means one who performs the task of destruction. destruction is the reduction of the universe back into atoms and is the third cosmic function. this is śrīdevī's function in the form of īśvara when tamas predominates; therefore she is saṃhāriṇī. the act of reabsorption: she reabsorbs names, forms and elements back into herself at the end of a cosmic cycle. internally, she dissolves duality and draws the mind back to the heart.","esoteric":["The Act of Reabsorption: She reabsorbs names, forms and elements back into Herself at the end of a cosmic cycle. Internally, She dissolves duality and draws the mind back to the heart."]},{"number":269,"name":"रुद्ररूपा","samasa":["• रुद्रः रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["रुद्रः — Rudra","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा। — she","रुद्ररूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above"],"summary":["रुद्ररूपा means one who is in the form of Rudra. When tamas predominates, Śrīdevī's form is called Rudra, and that form destroys the world. Rudra also means one who drives away sorrow; ru means sorrow and drāvayati means removes. Rudra can also make others cry through separation in destruction. The sun is also called Rudra, for at dissolution it burns the world before the rains submerge it. Rudra is also called the weeper because he arose from Brahmā's forehead and cried loudly."],"searchText":"269 रुद्ररूपा • रुद्रः रूपं यस्याः सा। रुद्रः — rudra रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा। — she रुद्ररूपा — the full name, understood through the samasa above रुद्ररूपा means one who is in the form of rudra. when tamas predominates, śrīdevī's form is called rudra, and that form destroys the world. rudra also means one who drives away sorrow; ru means sorrow and drāvayati means removes. rudra can also make others cry through separation in destruction. the sun is also called rudra, for at dissolution it burns the world before the rains submerge it. rudra is also called the weeper because he arose from brahmā's forehead and cried loudly. the principle of dissolution: for saṃhāra, she assumes tamo-guṇa and manifests as rudra. this fierce form is ultimately compassionate because it dissolves bondage and finite limitation.","esoteric":["The Principle of Dissolution: For saṃhāra, She assumes tamo-guṇa and manifests as Rudra. This fierce form is ultimately compassionate because it dissolves bondage and finite limitation."]},{"number":270,"name":"तिरोधानकरी","samasa":["• तिरोधानं करोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["तिरोधानं — concealment; disappearance","करोतीति — makes; manifests","तिरोधानकरी — meaning follows from the samasa: तिरोधानं करोतीति।"],"summary":["तिरोधानकरी means one who causes disappearance. Tirodhāna is complete dissolution, the absorption of even atoms into finer states and the integration of ego, intelligence and intellect back into nature in the reverse order of creation. Śrīdevī performs this function. Tiraskariṇī is also the name of one of Her attendants; She is in that form and hides Her form from those without devotion."],"searchText":"270 तिरोधानकरी • तिरोधानं करोतीति। तिरोधानं — concealment; disappearance करोतीति — makes; manifests तिरोधानकरी — meaning follows from the samasa: तिरोधानं करोतीति। तिरोधानकरी means one who causes disappearance. tirodhāna is complete dissolution, the absorption of even atoms into finer states and the integration of ego, intelligence and intellect back into nature in the reverse order of creation. śrīdevī performs this function. tiraskariṇī is also the name of one of her attendants; she is in that form and hides her form from those without devotion. the power of māyā: tirodhāna is the fourth cosmic function, where infinite consciousness conceals its true nature from individual souls. she creates the limitation of ego, time and space, allowing the differentiated universe to appear.","esoteric":["The Power of Māyā: Tirodhāna is the fourth cosmic function, where infinite consciousness conceals its true nature from individual souls. She creates the limitation of ego, time and space, allowing the differentiated universe to appear."]},{"number":271,"name":"ईश्वरी","samasa":["• ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["ईश्वरी — ruler; mistress","ईश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: ईश्वरी।"],"summary":["ईश्वरी means one who is in the form of Īśvara. Īśvara performs the fourth function, tirodhāna, and is completely associated with sattva. Śrīdevī is in that form. Īśvara's qualities are lordship, activity, independence and consciousness; since Śrīdevī possesses these fully, She is called Īśvarī."],"searchText":"271 ईश्वरी • ईश्वरी। ईश्वरी — ruler; mistress ईश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: ईश्वरी। ईश्वरी means one who is in the form of īśvara. īśvara performs the fourth function, tirodhāna, and is completely associated with sattva. śrīdevī is in that form. īśvara's qualities are lordship, activity, independence and consciousness; since śrīdevī possesses these fully, she is called īśvarī. the lord of concealment: she is the sovereign power associated with tirodhāna, the act of concealment. the name also denotes her unobstructed freedom of will (svātantrya-śakti), by which she directs the universe.","esoteric":["The Lord of Concealment: She is the sovereign power associated with tirodhāna, the act of concealment. The name also denotes Her unobstructed freedom of will (svātantrya-śakti), by which She directs the universe."]},{"number":272,"name":"सदाशिवा","samasa":["• सदा शिवा।"],"wordByWord":["सदा — always","शिवा — auspicious; Shiva-form","सदाशिवा — meaning follows from the samasa: सदा शिवा।"],"summary":["सदाशिवा means one who is in the form of Sadāśiva. Sad means always, and Śiva means auspicious. Taking the form of Sadāśiva, Śrīdevī performs the fifth function, anugraha, the bestowal of grace."],"searchText":"272 सदाशिवा • सदा शिवा। सदा — always शिवा — auspicious; shiva-form सदाशिवा — meaning follows from the samasa: सदा शिवा। सदाशिवा means one who is in the form of sadāśiva. sad means always, and śiva means auspicious. taking the form of sadāśiva, śrīdevī performs the fifth function, anugraha, the bestowal of grace. the presiding deity of grace: she manifests as sadāśiva, the fifth cosmic principle. as sadāśiva, her nature is eternal auspiciousness and the benevolent power from which liberation flows.","esoteric":["The Presiding Deity of Grace: She manifests as Sadāśiva, the fifth cosmic principle. As Sadāśiva, Her nature is eternal auspiciousness and the benevolent power from which liberation flows."]},{"number":273,"name":"अनुग्रहदा","samasa":["• अनुग्रहं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["अनुग्रहं — grace; favour","ददातीति — gives","अनुग्रहदा — meaning follows from the samasa: अनुग्रहं ददातीति।"],"summary":["अनुग्रहदा means one who confers blessings. After complete dissolution, the universe again assumes the form of primordial atoms; this process is anugraha, the function of Śrīdevī as Paramaśiva. Tirodhāna and anugraha mean bondage and release. Īśvara and Paramaśiva are the external and internal manifestations connected with these functions. Īśvara works within prescribed laws in ways outwardly seen, while Sadāśiva acts inwardly with compassion so that souls do not suffer excessively. Both are forms of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"273 अनुग्रहदा • अनुग्रहं ददातीति। अनुग्रहं — grace; favour ददातीति — gives अनुग्रहदा — meaning follows from the samasa: अनुग्रहं ददातीति। अनुग्रहदा means one who confers blessings. after complete dissolution, the universe again assumes the form of primordial atoms; this process is anugraha, the function of śrīdevī as paramaśiva. tirodhāna and anugraha mean bondage and release. īśvara and paramaśiva are the external and internal manifestations connected with these functions. īśvara works within prescribed laws in ways outwardly seen, while sadāśiva acts inwardly with compassion so that souls do not suffer excessively. both are forms of śrīdevī. the bestowal of liberation: anugraha is the descent of grace that breaks concealment and awakens the individual soul. through this grace, ignorance dissolves and mokṣa is bestowed.","esoteric":["The Bestowal of Liberation: anugraha is the descent of grace that breaks concealment and awakens the individual soul. Through this grace, ignorance dissolves and mokṣa is bestowed."]},{"number":274,"name":"पञ्चकृत्यपरायणा","samasa":["• पञ्चासु कृत्येषु परम् अयनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्चासु — in five","कृत्येषु — functions; acts","परम् — supreme","अयनं — abode; course","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","पञ्चकृत्यपरायणा — meaning follows from the samasa: पञ्चासु कृत्येषु परम् अयनं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["पञ्चकृत्यपरायणा means one who is devoted to the five functions. She has complete interest and involvement in creation, protection, destruction, concealment and grace. These five functions depend on Her. Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra, Īśvara and Paramaśiva perform them as forms and śaktis of Śrīdevī. They carry out their duties only by Her permission and command."],"searchText":"274 पञ्चकृत्यपरायणा • पञ्चासु कृत्येषु परम् अयनं यस्याः सा। पञ्चासु — in five कृत्येषु — functions; acts परम् — supreme अयनं — abode; course यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she पञ्चकृत्यपरायणा — meaning follows from the samasa: पञ्चासु कृत्येषु परम् अयनं यस्याः सा। पञ्चकृत्यपरायणा means one who is devoted to the five functions. she has complete interest and involvement in creation, protection, destruction, concealment and grace. these five functions depend on her. brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra, īśvara and paramaśiva perform them as forms and śaktis of śrīdevī. they carry out their duties only by her permission and command. the harmonizer of the five acts: the five operations are sṛṣṭi, sthiti, saṃhāra, tirodhāna and anugraha. she remains absorbed in maintaining this cosmic rhythm.","esoteric":["The Harmonizer of the Five Acts: The five operations are sṛṣṭi, sthiti, saṃhāra, tirodhāna and anugraha. She remains absorbed in maintaining this cosmic rhythm."]},{"number":275,"name":"भानुमण्डलमध्यस्था","samasa":["• भानोः यत् मण्डलं तस्य मध्ये तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["भानोः — of the Sun","मण्डलं — disc; orbit","भानुमण्डलमध्यस्था — meaning follows from the samasa: भानोः यत् मण्डलं तस्य मध्ये तिष्ठतीति।"],"summary":["भानुमण्डलमध्यस्था means one who is in the middle of the solar orb. She is worshipped by meditating on Her in the sun's disc. The golden being seen within the sun is the Supreme Lord Parameśvara, and this name indicates that Śrīdevī is in that form. Bhānumaṇḍala is also understood as the anāhata cakra, where Śrīdevī is present as Kuṇḍalinī."],"searchText":"275 भानुमण्डलमध्यस्था • भानोः यत् मण्डलं तस्य मध्ये तिष्ठतीति। भानोः — of the sun मण्डलं — disc; orbit भानुमण्डलमध्यस्था — meaning follows from the samasa: भानोः यत् मण्डलं तस्य मध्ये तिष्ठतीति। भानुमण्डलमध्यस्था means one who is in the middle of the solar orb. she is worshipped by meditating on her in the sun's disc. the golden being seen within the sun is the supreme lord parameśvara, and this name indicates that śrīdevī is in that form. bhānumaṇḍala is also understood as the anāhata cakra, where śrīdevī is present as kuṇḍalinī. the solar center: she dwells as the innermost light within the solar orb. in the subtle body, bhānumaṇḍala is connected with the anāhata center, where she shines as kuṇḍalinī.","esoteric":["The Solar Center: She dwells as the innermost light within the solar orb. In the subtle body, bhānumaṇḍala is connected with the anāhata center, where She shines as Kuṇḍalinī."]},{"number":276,"name":"भैरवी","samasa":["• भैरवस्य पत्नी।","• भीरूणां (स्त्रीणां) संहतिः।"],"wordByWord":["भैरवस्य — of Bhairava","पत्नी — wife; consort","भैरवी — meaning follows from the samasa: भैरवस्य पत्नी।"],"summary":["भैरवी means the consort of Bhairava. Bhairava performs the three functions and has a terrific form; She is His energy. Bhīru can mean woman, and women collectively may be called bhairavam; since She is in that form, She is Bhairavī. A form of Her mantra is also known as Bhairavī, and a twelve-year-old girl is worshipped by this name."],"searchText":"276 भैरवी • भैरवस्य पत्नी। • भीरूणां (स्त्रीणां) संहतिः। भैरवस्य — of bhairava पत्नी — wife; consort भैरवी — meaning follows from the samasa: भैरवस्य पत्नी। भैरवी means the consort of bhairava. bhairava performs the three functions and has a terrific form; she is his energy. bhīru can mean woman, and women collectively may be called bhairavam; since she is in that form, she is bhairavī. a form of her mantra is also known as bhairavī, and a twelve-year-old girl is worshipped by this name. the power of bhairava: bhairava governs the cosmic cycle, and bhairavī is his non-dual dynamic power. to ego-bound beings she may appear fearsome, but to the wise she removes the fear of death.","esoteric":["The Power of Bhairava: Bhairava governs the cosmic cycle, and Bhairavī is His non-dual dynamic power. To ego-bound beings She may appear fearsome, but to the wise She removes the fear of death."]},{"number":277,"name":"भगमालिनी","samasa":["• भगं मलतीति।"],"wordByWord":["भगं — bhaga; fortune; splendour; power","मलतीति — wears like a garland; possesses","भगमालिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भगं मलतीति।"],"summary":["भगमालिनी means one who is in the form of Bhagamālinī. Bhaga includes qualities such as discrimination, dispassion, effort, excellence, fame, glory, liberation, lordliness, magnanimity, power, prosperity, omniscience, righteousness, supremacy, wisdom and creative power. Śrīdevī possesses all these qualities and is therefore Bhagamālinī. She is also the tithi nityā devī connected with the second day of the bright lunar half and the fourteenth day of the dark lunar half, and one among the deities of the eighth āvaraṇa."],"searchText":"277 भगमालिनी • भगं मलतीति। भगं — bhaga; fortune; splendour; power मलतीति — wears like a garland; possesses भगमालिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भगं मलतीति। भगमालिनी means one who is in the form of bhagamālinī. bhaga includes qualities such as discrimination, dispassion, effort, excellence, fame, glory, liberation, lordliness, magnanimity, power, prosperity, omniscience, righteousness, supremacy, wisdom and creative power. śrīdevī possesses all these qualities and is therefore bhagamālinī. she is also the tithi nityā devī connected with the second day of the bright lunar half and the fourteenth day of the dark lunar half, and one among the deities of the eighth āvaraṇa. the garland of divine attributes: bhaga refers to divine splendors such as lordship, dharma, fame, wealth, wisdom and dispassion. she wears these qualities like a garland and radiates creative power.","esoteric":["The Garland of Divine Attributes: Bhaga refers to divine splendors such as lordship, dharma, fame, wealth, wisdom and dispassion. She wears these qualities like a garland and radiates creative power."]},{"number":278,"name":"पद्मासना","samasa":["• पद्मम् एव आसनं यस्याः सा।","• पद्मां (लक्ष्मीं) सनति।","• पद्मम् अस्यति।"],"wordByWord":["पद्मम् — lotus","आसनं — seat","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","पद्मां — Lakshmi; lotus-like prosperity","पद्मासना — meaning follows from the samasa: पद्मम् एव आसनं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["पद्मासना means one whose seat is the lotus. Brahmā, Sarasvatī and Lakṣmī have lotuses as their seats, and Śrīdevī is in all these three forms. The lotus has nature as its leaves, categories as its filaments and knowledge as its stalk; She has such a lotus as Her seat. Padmāsana is also a yogic posture, and She is in that form. She distributes padma, wealth or Lakṣmī, to devotees. Padma may also mean bindu, on which She is seated."],"searchText":"278 पद्मासना • पद्मम् एव आसनं यस्याः सा। • पद्मां (लक्ष्मीं) सनति। • पद्मम् अस्यति। पद्मम् — lotus आसनं — seat यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she पद्मां — lakshmi; lotus-like prosperity पद्मासना — meaning follows from the samasa: पद्मम् एव आसनं यस्याः सा। पद्मासना means one whose seat is the lotus. brahmā, sarasvatī and lakṣmī have lotuses as their seats, and śrīdevī is in all these three forms. the lotus has nature as its leaves, categories as its filaments and knowledge as its stalk; she has such a lotus as her seat. padmāsana is also a yogic posture, and she is in that form. she distributes padma, wealth or lakṣmī, to devotees. padma may also mean bindu, on which she is seated. yogic absorption: as padmāsanā, she sits in meditative stillness within the lotus centers of the subtle body. she also dispenses both worldly and spiritual abundance.","esoteric":["Yogic Absorption: As Padmāsanā, She sits in meditative stillness within the lotus centers of the subtle body. She also dispenses both worldly and spiritual abundance."]},{"number":279,"name":"भगवती","samasa":["• भगाः अस्यां सन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["भगाः — divine excellences","अस्यां — in her","सन्तीति — exist","भगवती — meaning follows from the samasa: भगाः अस्यां सन्तीति।"],"summary":["भगवती means one who possesses prosperity and the power of Īśvara. Bhaga has the qualities given in the previous names, and Śrīdevī possesses all those qualities without deficiency. Since She knows the origin and dissolution of beings, their coming and going, and knowledge and ignorance, She is called Bhagavatī."],"searchText":"279 भगवती • भगाः अस्यां सन्तीति। भगाः — divine excellences अस्यां — in her सन्तीति — exist भगवती — meaning follows from the samasa: भगाः अस्यां सन्तीति। भगवती means one who possesses prosperity and the power of īśvara. bhaga has the qualities given in the previous names, and śrīdevī possesses all those qualities without deficiency. since she knows the origin and dissolution of beings, their coming and going, and knowledge and ignorance, she is called bhagavatī. the knower of the cosmos: bhagavatī is the one who knows the origin, dissolution, movement, knowledge and ignorance of beings. she is the worshipful personal form of absolute brahman.","esoteric":["The Knower of the Cosmos: Bhagavatī is the one who knows the origin, dissolution, movement, knowledge and ignorance of beings. She is the worshipful personal form of absolute Brahman."]},{"number":280,"name":"पद्मनाभसहोदरी","samasa":["• पद्मनाभस्य सहोदरी। '"],"wordByWord":["पद्मनाभस्य — of Padmanabha; Vishnu","सहोदरी — sister","पद्मनाभसहोदरी — meaning follows from the samasa: पद्मनाभस्य सहोदरी। '"],"summary":["पद्मनाभसहोदरी means the sister of Padmanābha, Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu is called Padmanābha because the lotus arose from His navel. Śrīdevī created three pairs: Brahmā and Lakṣmī in golden colour, Viṣṇu and Śrīdevī in blue colour, and Śiva and Sarasvatī in white colour; their colours indicate the three guṇas. In this account, Viṣṇu and Śrīdevī are siblings. She is also identified with Subhadrā, sister of Śrīkṛṣṇa, and with the sister of the enemy of Kaṃsa. The name also contains hidden mantra syllables through Padma, Nābha and Sahodarī."],"searchText":"280 पद्मनाभसहोदरी • पद्मनाभस्य सहोदरी। ' पद्मनाभस्य — of padmanabha; vishnu सहोदरी — sister पद्मनाभसहोदरी — meaning follows from the samasa: पद्मनाभस्य सहोदरी। ' पद्मनाभसहोदरी means the sister of padmanābha, viṣṇu. viṣṇu is called padmanābha because the lotus arose from his navel. śrīdevī created three pairs: brahmā and lakṣmī in golden colour, viṣṇu and śrīdevī in blue colour, and śiva and sarasvatī in white colour; their colours indicate the three guṇas. in this account, viṣṇu and śrīdevī are siblings. she is also identified with subhadrā, sister of śrīkṛṣṇa, and with the sister of the enemy of kaṃsa. the name also contains hidden mantra syllables through padma, nābha and sahodarī. the shared womb of nature: she is nārāyaṇī, sister of viṣṇu. viṣṇu represents protective consciousness, while she is the active śakti that makes protection effective; both share the sustaining sattva quality.","esoteric":["The Shared Womb of Nature: She is Nārāyaṇī, sister of Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu represents protective consciousness, while She is the active śakti that makes protection effective; both share the sustaining sattva quality."]},{"number":281,"name":"उन्मेषनिमिषोत्पन्नविपन्नभुवनावली","samasa":["• उन्मेषनिमिषाभ्यामेव उत्पन्ना विपन्नाश्च भुवनानाम् आवल्यः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["भुवनानाम् — of worlds","आवल्यः — series; rows","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","उन्मेषनिमिषोत्पन्नविपन्नभुवनावली — meaning follows from the samasa: उन्मेषनिमिषाभ्यामेव उत्पन्ना विपन्नाश्च भुवनानाम् आवल्यः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["उन्मेषनिमिषोत्पन्नविपन्नभुवनावली means one whose opening and closing of eyes bring worlds into being and make them disappear. Unmeṣa means opening the eyes, and nimeṣa means closing them. These movements indicate creation and dissolution, showing that worlds arise and disappear effortlessly by Her mere will."],"searchText":"281 उन्मेषनिमिषोत्पन्नविपन्नभुवनावली • उन्मेषनिमिषाभ्यामेव उत्पन्ना विपन्नाश्च भुवनानाम् आवल्यः यस्याः सा। भुवनानाम् — of worlds आवल्यः — series; rows यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she उन्मेषनिमिषोत्पन्नविपन्नभुवनावली — meaning follows from the samasa: उन्मेषनिमिषाभ्यामेव उत्पन्ना विपन्नाश्च भुवनानाम् आवल्यः यस्याः सा। उन्मेषनिमिषोत्पन्नविपन्नभुवनावली means one whose opening and closing of eyes bring worlds into being and make them disappear. unmeṣa means opening the eyes, and nimeṣa means closing them. these movements indicate creation and dissolution, showing that worlds arise and disappear effortlessly by her mere will. effortless cosmic cycles: creation and reabsorption require no labour from her; they correspond to unmeṣa, outward manifestation, and nimeṣa, inward withdrawal. her blink spans cosmic time.","esoteric":["Effortless Cosmic Cycles: Creation and reabsorption require no labour from Her; they correspond to unmeṣa, outward manifestation, and nimeṣa, inward withdrawal. Her blink spans cosmic time."]},{"number":282,"name":"सहस्रशीर्षवदना","samasa":["• सहस्राणि शीर्षाणि च वदनानि च यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सहस्राणि — thousands","शीर्षाणि — heads","वदनानि — faces","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सहस्रशीर्षवदना — meaning follows from the samasa: सहस्राणि शीर्षाणि च वदनानि च यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सहस्रशीर्षवदना means one who has thousands of heads and faces. This describes Her cosmic form, in which all heads and faces belong to Her universal body."],"searchText":"282 सहस्रशीर्षवदना • सहस्राणि शीर्षाणि च वदनानि च यस्याः सा। सहस्राणि — thousands शीर्षाणि — heads वदनानि — faces यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सहस्रशीर्षवदना — meaning follows from the samasa: सहस्राणि शीर्षाणि च वदनानि च यस्याः सा। सहस्रशीर्षवदना means one who has thousands of heads and faces. this describes her cosmic form, in which all heads and faces belong to her universal body. the cosmic person: since she is the inner self of all beings, every head and face belongs to her vast cosmic form (virāṭ-rūpa).","esoteric":["The Cosmic Person: Since She is the inner self of all beings, every head and face belongs to Her vast cosmic form (virāṭ-rūpa)."]},{"number":283,"name":"सहस्राक्षी","samasa":["• सहस्राणि अक्षीणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सहस्राणि — thousands","अक्षीणि — eyes","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सहस्राक्षी — meaning follows from the samasa: सहस्राणि अक्षीणि यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सहस्राक्षी means one who has thousands of eyes. This describes Her cosmic form and all-pervading vision."],"searchText":"283 सहस्राक्षी • सहस्राणि अक्षीणि यस्याः सा। सहस्राणि — thousands अक्षीणि — eyes यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सहस्राक्षी — meaning follows from the samasa: सहस्राणि अक्षीणि यस्याः सा। सहस्राक्षी means one who has thousands of eyes. this describes her cosmic form and all-pervading vision. the infinite witness: as the ultimate seer (draṣṭā), she witnesses all actions, thoughts and changes across all planes. every eye functions through her consciousness.","esoteric":["The Infinite Witness: As the ultimate seer (draṣṭā), She witnesses all actions, thoughts and changes across all planes. Every eye functions through Her consciousness."]},{"number":284,"name":"सहस्रपात्","samasa":["• सहस्राः पादाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पादाः — feet","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सहस्रपात् — meaning follows from the samasa: सहस्राः पादाः यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सहस्रपात् means one who has thousands of feet. This means She pervades all beings and all worlds."],"searchText":"284 सहस्रपात् • सहस्राः पादाः यस्याः सा। पादाः — feet यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सहस्रपात् — meaning follows from the samasa: सहस्राः पादाः यस्याः सा। सहस्रपात् means one who has thousands of feet. this means she pervades all beings and all worlds. all-pervading motion: she is the kriyā-śakti that moves the universe. all movement proceeds through her, and no place is outside her presence.","esoteric":["All-Pervading Motion: She is the kriyā-śakti that moves the universe. All movement proceeds through Her, and no place is outside Her presence."]},{"number":285,"name":"आब्रह्मकीटजननी","samasa":["• आ ब्रह्मणः कीटपर्यन्तानां जननी।"],"wordByWord":["ब्रह्मणः — from Brahma","जननी — mother","आब्रह्मकीटजननी — meaning follows from the samasa: आ ब्रह्मणः कीटपर्यन्तानां जननी।"],"summary":["आब्रह्मकीटजननी means one who is the mother of all beings, from Brahmā down to a worm."],"searchText":"285 आब्रह्मकीटजननी • आ ब्रह्मणः कीटपर्यन्तानां जननी। ब्रह्मणः — from brahma जननी — mother आब्रह्मकीटजननी — meaning follows from the samasa: आ ब्रह्मणः कीटपर्यन्तानां जननी। आब्रह्मकीटजननी means one who is the mother of all beings, from brahmā down to a worm. equal origin of being: from brahmā to the smallest creature, all beings arise from the same causal womb. she is the mother of every level of manifestation.","esoteric":["Equal Origin of Being: From Brahmā to the smallest creature, all beings arise from the same causal womb. She is the mother of every level of manifestation."]},{"number":286,"name":"वर्णाश्रमविधायिनी","samasa":["• वर्णाश्च आश्रमाश्च तेषां विधायिनी।"],"wordByWord":["विधायिनी — ordainer","वर्णाश्रमविधायिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: वर्णाश्च आश्रमाश्च तेषां विधायिनी।"],"summary":["वर्णाश्रमविधायिनी means one who established varṇa and āśrama. After creating beings from Brahmā down to worms, She gave sacred commands to guide them on the right path. Through karma, She established dharma for human beings by dividing society into four varṇas and four āśramas. Action prescribed according to one's station, joined with knowledge of the Self, leads toward liberation. From dharma arises devotion, and through devotion the supreme is attained."],"searchText":"286 वर्णाश्रमविधायिनी • वर्णाश्च आश्रमाश्च तेषां विधायिनी। विधायिनी — ordainer वर्णाश्रमविधायिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: वर्णाश्च आश्रमाश्च तेषां विधायिनी। वर्णाश्रमविधायिनी means one who established varṇa and āśrama. after creating beings from brahmā down to worms, she gave sacred commands to guide them on the right path. through karma, she established dharma for human beings by dividing society into four varṇas and four āśramas. action prescribed according to one's station, joined with knowledge of the self, leads toward liberation. from dharma arises devotion, and through devotion the supreme is attained. the basis of dharma: social and spiritual order is arranged for gradual evolution. she aligns duties with qualities and actions so that beings can move toward liberation.","esoteric":["The Basis of Dharma: Social and spiritual order is arranged for gradual evolution. She aligns duties with qualities and actions so that beings can move toward liberation."]},{"number":287,"name":"निजाज्ञारूपनिगमा","samasa":["• याः निजां (स्वीयाम्) आज्ञां रूपयन्ति तादृशाः निगमा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","निजाज्ञारूपनिगमा — meaning follows from the samasa: याः निजां (स्वीयाम्) आज्ञां रूपयन्ति तादृशाः निगमा यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["निजाज्ञारूपनिगमा means one whose commands are the nigamas. The revealed injunctions tell human beings what to do and what to avoid, setting out the goal, means and practical directions. These commands also define the limits of varṇa and āśrama. The nigamas arise from Śrīdevī as Her own command."],"searchText":"287 निजाज्ञारूपनिगमा • याः निजां (स्वीयाम्) आज्ञां रूपयन्ति तादृशाः निगमा यस्याः सा। यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she निजाज्ञारूपनिगमा — meaning follows from the samasa: याः निजां (स्वीयाम्) आज्ञां रूपयन्ति तादृशाः निगमा यस्याः सा। निजाज्ञारूपनिगमा means one whose commands are the nigamas. the revealed injunctions tell human beings what to do and what to avoid, setting out the goal, means and practical directions. these commands also define the limits of varṇa and āśrama. the nigamas arise from śrīdevī as her own command. the commands of the empress: the nigamas are her royal command. to follow them is to align with her will and cosmic harmony.","esoteric":["The Commands of the Empress: The nigamas are Her royal command. To follow them is to align with Her will and cosmic harmony."]},{"number":288,"name":"पुण्यापुण्यफलप्रदा","samasa":["• पुण्यस्य अपुण्यस्य च फले प्रकरषेण ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["पुण्यस्य — of merit","अपुण्यस्य — of demerit","फले — fruits","ददातीति — gives","पुण्यापुण्यफलप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: पुण्यस्य अपुण्यस्य च फले प्रकरषेण ददातीति।"],"summary":["पुण्यापुण्यफलप्रदा means one who gives the fruits of righteous and unrighteous actions. Śrīdevī determines the results of good and bad actions arising from ordained and prohibited conduct. The name uses puṇya and apuṇya, not puṇya and pāpa, because apuṇya can appear righteous to a person acting from ignorance or ego. She directly grants the fruits of both righteous and unrighteous deeds."],"searchText":"288 पुण्यापुण्यफलप्रदा • पुण्यस्य अपुण्यस्य च फले प्रकरषेण ददातीति। पुण्यस्य — of merit अपुण्यस्य — of demerit फले — fruits ददातीति — gives पुण्यापुण्यफलप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: पुण्यस्य अपुण्यस्य च फले प्रकरषेण ददातीति। पुण्यापुण्यफलप्रदा means one who gives the fruits of righteous and unrighteous actions. śrīdevī determines the results of good and bad actions arising from ordained and prohibited conduct. the name uses puṇya and apuṇya, not puṇya and pāpa, because apuṇya can appear righteous to a person acting from ignorance or ego. she directly grants the fruits of both righteous and unrighteous deeds. the law of karma: she is the neutral cosmic intelligence that returns the fruits of action to the doer. joy follows puṇya, and corrective experience follows apuṇya, preserving moral balance.","esoteric":["The Law of Karma: She is the neutral cosmic intelligence that returns the fruits of action to the doer. Joy follows puṇya, and corrective experience follows apuṇya, preserving moral balance."]},{"number":289,"name":"श्रुतिसीमन्तसिन्धूरीकृतपादाब्जधूलिका","samasa":["• श्रुतीनां सीमन्ताः सिन्धूरवत् (तदन्तर्गतरहस्यार्थवत्) कृता पादाब्जयोः धूलिः यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["सीमन्ताः — parting of the hair; crest-line","सिन्धूरवत् — like vermilion","पादाब्जयोः — of the lotus feet","धूलिः — dust","सा — she","श्रुतिसीमन्तसिन्धूरीकृतपादाब्जधूलिका — meaning follows from the samasa: श्रुतीनां सीमन्ताः सिन्धूरवत् (तदन्तर्गतरहस्यार्थवत्) कृता पादाब्जयोः धूलिः यया सा।"],"summary":["श्रुतिसीमन्तसिन्धूरीकृतपादाब्जधूलिका means one whose lotus-foot dust becomes vermilion on the parting line of the śrutis. The śrutis are imagined as women who wear the dust of Her lotus feet as sindūra on their heads. This indicates that the highest secret meaning of revealed wisdom culminates at Her feet."],"searchText":"289 श्रुतिसीमन्तसिन्धूरीकृतपादाब्जधूलिका • श्रुतीनां सीमन्ताः सिन्धूरवत् (तदन्तर्गतरहस्यार्थवत्) कृता पादाब्जयोः धूलिः यया सा। सीमन्ताः — parting of the hair; crest-line सिन्धूरवत् — like vermilion पादाब्जयोः — of the lotus feet धूलिः — dust सा — she श्रुतिसीमन्तसिन्धूरीकृतपादाब्जधूलिका — meaning follows from the samasa: श्रुतीनां सीमन्ताः सिन्धूरवत् (तदन्तर्गतरहस्यार्थवत्) कृता पादाब्जयोः धूलिः यया सा। श्रुतिसीमन्तसिन्धूरीकृतपादाब्जधूलिका means one whose lotus-foot dust becomes vermilion on the parting line of the śrutis. the śrutis are imagined as women who wear the dust of her lotus feet as sindūra on their heads. this indicates that the highest secret meaning of revealed wisdom culminates at her feet. the crown of knowledge: the śrutis are personified as divine women, and the dust of her feet rests on the highest part of their heads. the highest knowledge is fulfilled at her feet.","esoteric":["The Crown of Knowledge: The śrutis are personified as divine women, and the dust of Her feet rests on the highest part of their heads. The highest knowledge is fulfilled at Her feet."]},{"number":290,"name":"सकलागमसन्दोहशुक्तिसम्पुटमौक्तिका","samasa":["• सकलाश्च ते आगमाश्च तेषां सन्दोहाः एव शुक्तयः ताभिः सम्पुटं मौक्तिकं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सन्दोहाः — collections","शुक्तयः — shells","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","सकलागमसन्दोहशुक्तिसम्पुटमौक्तिका — meaning follows from the samasa: सकलाश्च ते आगमाश्च तेषां सन्दोहाः एव शुक्तयः ताभिः सम्पुटं मौक्तिकं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["सकलागमसन्दोहशुक्तिसम्पुटमौक्तिका means one who is the pearl enclosed in the shell-caskets formed by the collections of all āgamas. The āgamas are like shells, and Śrīdevī is the pearl hidden within them."],"searchText":"290 सकलागमसन्दोहशुक्तिसम्पुटमौक्तिका • सकलाश्च ते आगमाश्च तेषां सन्दोहाः एव शुक्तयः ताभिः सम्पुटं मौक्तिकं यस्याः सा। सन्दोहाः — collections शुक्तयः — shells यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she सकलागमसन्दोहशुक्तिसम्पुटमौक्तिका — meaning follows from the samasa: सकलाश्च ते आगमाश्च तेषां सन्दोहाः एव शुक्तयः ताभिः सम्पुटं मौक्तिकं यस्याः सा। सकलागमसन्दोहशुक्तिसम्पुटमौक्तिका means one who is the pearl enclosed in the shell-caskets formed by the collections of all āgamas. the āgamas are like shells, and śrīdevī is the pearl hidden within them. the hidden essence: just as a pearl rests within a shell, her true nature is the precious inner essence within all āgamic structures. the outer forms are the container; she is the pearl.","esoteric":["The Hidden Essence: Just as a pearl rests within a shell, Her true nature is the precious inner essence within all āgamic structures. The outer forms are the container; She is the pearl."]},{"number":291,"name":"पुरुषार्थप्रदा","samasa":["• पुरुषार्थान् प्रकर्षेण ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["पुरुषार्थान् — human aims","प्रकर्षेण — excellently; completely","ददातीति — gives","पुरुषार्थप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: पुरुषार्थान् प्रकर्षेण ददातीति।"],"summary":["पुरुषार्थप्रदा means one who bestows the four aims of human life. The four puruṣārthas are dharma, artha, kāma and mokṣa: virtue, wealth, enjoyment and liberation. A human being obtains all four only through the blessings of Śrīdevī. Worship of unconditioned Brahman and its fruit also arise only through Her blessing."],"searchText":"291 पुरुषार्थप्रदा • पुरुषार्थान् प्रकर्षेण ददातीति। पुरुषार्थान् — human aims प्रकर्षेण — excellently; completely ददातीति — gives पुरुषार्थप्रदा — meaning follows from the samasa: पुरुषार्थान् प्रकर्षेण ददातीति। पुरुषार्थप्रदा means one who bestows the four aims of human life. the four puruṣārthas are dharma, artha, kāma and mokṣa: virtue, wealth, enjoyment and liberation. a human being obtains all four only through the blessings of śrīdevī. worship of unconditioned brahman and its fruit also arise only through her blessing. the giver of the four aims: she grants dharma, artha, kāma and mokṣa in proper balance. she gives both worldly support and liberation according to the seeker's fitness.","esoteric":["The Giver of the Four Aims: She grants dharma, artha, kāma and mokṣa in proper balance. She gives both worldly support and liberation according to the seeker's fitness."]},{"number":292,"name":"पूर्णा","samasa":["• पूर्णा।"],"wordByWord":["पूर्णा — full; complete","पूर्णा — meaning follows from the samasa: पूर्णा।"],"summary":["पूर्णा means one who is the all-encompassing whole. She is free from limitation by time, place and circumstance. As Brahman, Śrīdevī is fully present in everything and everywhere. Pūrṇā also refers to the fifth, tenth and fifteenth nityā devīs, the fourteenth bright lunar night, and a sacred river."],"searchText":"292 पूर्णा • पूर्णा। पूर्णा — full; complete पूर्णा — meaning follows from the samasa: पूर्णा। पूर्णा means one who is the all-encompassing whole. she is free from limitation by time, place and circumstance. as brahman, śrīdevī is fully present in everything and everywhere. pūrṇā also refers to the fifth, tenth and fifteenth nityā devīs, the fourteenth bright lunar night, and a sacred river. the indivisible absolute: she lacks nothing, contains everything and is complete in herself. nothing can increase or diminish her fullness.","esoteric":["The Indivisible Absolute: She lacks nothing, contains everything and is complete in Herself. Nothing can increase or diminish Her fullness."]},{"number":293,"name":"भोगिनी","samasa":["• भोगः अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["भोगः — enjoyment","भोगिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भोगः अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"summary":["भोगिनी means one who is the enjoyer. Bhoga means bliss, and She enjoys it; She is both bliss and the enjoyer. Bhoga can also mean the body of a serpent, and Śrīdevī is Kuṇḍalinī energy in the human body in the form of a female serpent. Bhoginī is also the name of a nāgakanyā."],"searchText":"293 भोगिनी • भोगः अस्याः अस्तीति। भोगः — enjoyment भोगिनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भोगः अस्याः अस्तीति। भोगिनी means one who is the enjoyer. bhoga means bliss, and she enjoys it; she is both bliss and the enjoyer. bhoga can also mean the body of a serpent, and śrīdevī is kuṇḍalinī energy in the human body in the form of a female serpent. bhoginī is also the name of a nāgakanyā. the cosmic enjoyer: she is bhoginī, the enjoyer of bliss, while remaining unattached. she is also the serpent power moving as kuṇḍalinī within the body.","esoteric":["The Cosmic Enjoyer: She is Bhoginī, the enjoyer of bliss, while remaining unattached. She is also the serpent power moving as Kuṇḍalinī within the body."]},{"number":294,"name":"भुवनेश्वरी","samasa":["• भुवनानाम् ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["भुवनानाम् — of worlds","ईश्वरी — ruler; mistress","भुवनेश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: भुवनानाम् ईश्वरी।"],"summary":["भुवनेश्वरी means the sovereign ruler of the fourteen worlds. The seven lower worlds, the earth, and the six higher worlds together form the fourteen worlds, and She guides them according to Her will. The word bhuvana can mean earth, heaven, water and other realms; She is the head of all. The māyā-bīja hrīṃ is also called the Bhuvaneśvarī bīja, and She is its presiding deity. Its letters indicate space, fire and water, which She creates and through which the world arises."],"searchText":"294 भुवनेश्वरी • भुवनानाम् ईश्वरी। भुवनानाम् — of worlds ईश्वरी — ruler; mistress भुवनेश्वरी — meaning follows from the samasa: भुवनानाम् ईश्वरी। भुवनेश्वरी means the sovereign ruler of the fourteen worlds. the seven lower worlds, the earth, and the six higher worlds together form the fourteen worlds, and she guides them according to her will. the word bhuvana can mean earth, heaven, water and other realms; she is the head of all. the māyā-bīja hrīṃ is also called the bhuvaneśvarī bīja, and she is its presiding deity. its letters indicate space, fire and water, which she creates and through which the world arises. sovereignty over the worlds: she is the queen governing all realms of manifestation. as bhuvaneśvarī, she is also connected with hrīṃ, the bīja that sustains the matrix of space.","esoteric":["Sovereignty over the Worlds: She is the queen governing all realms of manifestation. As Bhuvaneśvarī, She is also connected with hrīṃ, the bīja that sustains the matrix of space."]},{"number":295,"name":"अम्बिका","samasa":["• अम्बा एव अम्बिका।"],"wordByWord":["अम्बा — mother","अम्बिका — meaning follows from the samasa: अम्बा एव अम्बिका।"],"summary":["अम्बिका means the great mother. Ammā, ambā and ambikā are affectionate words for mother. Since Śrīdevī is the mother of the entire universe, She is Ambikā. Ambikā also means mother of the world, goddess of speech, earth, Rudrāṇī, and the aggregate of the three śaktis: icchā, jñāna and kriyā. Ambikā can also mean night or sleep; as night and sleep, She embraces beings like a mother and gives rest and peace."],"searchText":"295 अम्बिका • अम्बा एव अम्बिका। अम्बा — mother अम्बिका — meaning follows from the samasa: अम्बा एव अम्बिका। अम्बिका means the great mother. ammā, ambā and ambikā are affectionate words for mother. since śrīdevī is the mother of the entire universe, she is ambikā. ambikā also means mother of the world, goddess of speech, earth, rudrāṇī, and the aggregate of the three śaktis: icchā, jñāna and kriyā. ambikā can also mean night or sleep; as night and sleep, she embraces beings like a mother and gives rest and peace. the accessible mother: ambikā is the loving mother of every soul. she also gathers the powers of will, knowledge and action into one protective maternal form.","esoteric":["The Accessible Mother: Ambikā is the loving mother of every soul. She also gathers the powers of will, knowledge and action into one protective maternal form."]},{"number":296,"name":"अनादिनिधना","samasa":["• आदिः निधनं च न विद्यते यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["आदिः — beginning","निधनं — end","न — not","विद्यते — exists","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","अनादिनिधना — meaning follows from the samasa: आदिः निधनं च न विद्यते यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["अनादिनिधना means one who has neither beginning nor end. The Supreme Being is without beginning and end, unlike human beings who arise and pass away within time. This distinction helps point to Śrīdevī's transcendence. Nidhana can also mean destruction or obstruction to worship. She protects devotees from obstacles such as inability, false satisfaction, misleading attainments and the bonds arising from ignorance; therefore She is Anādinidhanā."],"searchText":"296 अनादिनिधना • आदिः निधनं च न विद्यते यस्याः सा। आदिः — beginning निधनं — end न — not विद्यते — exists यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she अनादिनिधना — meaning follows from the samasa: आदिः निधनं च न विद्यते यस्याः सा। अनादिनिधना means one who has neither beginning nor end. the supreme being is without beginning and end, unlike human beings who arise and pass away within time. this distinction helps point to śrīdevī's transcendence. nidhana can also mean destruction or obstruction to worship. she protects devotees from obstacles such as inability, false satisfaction, misleading attainments and the bonds arising from ignorance; therefore she is anādinidhanā. beyond linear time: time-bound things have origin and end. she is the consciousness from which time itself appears, existing before beginning and after end.","esoteric":["Beyond Linear Time: Time-bound things have origin and end. She is the consciousness from which time itself appears, existing before beginning and after end."]},{"number":297,"name":"हरिब्रह्मेन्द्रसेविता","samasa":["• हरिश्च ब्रह्म च इन्द्रश्च तैः सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["ब्रह्म — Brahma","सेविता — served; worshipped","हरिब्रह्मेन्द्रसेविता — meaning follows from the samasa: हरिश्च ब्रह्म च इन्द्रश्च तैः सेविता।"],"summary":["हरिब्रह्मेन्द्रसेविता means one who is served by Hari, Brahmā and Indra. In Śrīcakra, the cintāmaṇigṛha is Her dwelling. Around it are the seats of Viṣṇu, Brahmā, Indra and other guardians, who constantly meditate on Śrīdevī. Since even Hari, Brahmā and Indra adore Her, Her devotees need not worship them separately."],"searchText":"297 हरिब्रह्मेन्द्रसेविता • हरिश्च ब्रह्म च इन्द्रश्च तैः सेविता। ब्रह्म — brahma सेविता — served; worshipped हरिब्रह्मेन्द्रसेविता — meaning follows from the samasa: हरिश्च ब्रह्म च इन्द्रश्च तैः सेविता। हरिब्रह्मेन्द्रसेविता means one who is served by hari, brahmā and indra. in śrīcakra, the cintāmaṇigṛha is her dwelling. around it are the seats of viṣṇu, brahmā, indra and other guardians, who constantly meditate on śrīdevī. since even hari, brahmā and indra adore her, her devotees need not worship them separately. the power behind the gods: the great deities receive their authority through her grace. their powers function as reflections of her supreme command.","esoteric":["The Power Behind the Gods: The great deities receive their authority through Her grace. Their powers function as reflections of Her supreme command."]},{"number":298,"name":"नारायणी","samasa":["• नारायणस्य इयं पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["नारायणस्य — of Narayana","पत्नी — wife; consort","नारायणी — meaning follows from the samasa: नारायणस्य इयं पत्नी।"],"summary":["नारायणी means one who is called Nārāyaṇī. Nara can indicate Brahman, and waters are called nāra because they emanate from Brahman. Since Viṣṇu has water as His abode, He is Nārāyaṇa, and Nārāyaṇī is related to Him as sister. Nārāyaṇa may also indicate Śiva, in which case Nārāyaṇī is Śiva's consort. There is no difference between Nārāyaṇa and Śrīdevī: in Ardhanārī, She is the left half, and in Śaṅkaranārāyaṇa, Nārāyaṇa is the left half. She is also indicated by names such as Govindarūpiṇī, Mukundā and Viṣṇurūpiṇī."],"searchText":"298 नारायणी • नारायणस्य इयं पत्नी। नारायणस्य — of narayana पत्नी — wife; consort नारायणी — meaning follows from the samasa: नारायणस्य इयं पत्नी। नारायणी means one who is called nārāyaṇī. nara can indicate brahman, and waters are called nāra because they emanate from brahman. since viṣṇu has water as his abode, he is nārāyaṇa, and nārāyaṇī is related to him as sister. nārāyaṇa may also indicate śiva, in which case nārāyaṇī is śiva's consort. there is no difference between nārāyaṇa and śrīdevī: in ardhanārī, she is the left half, and in śaṅkaranārāyaṇa, nārāyaṇa is the left half. she is also indicated by names such as govindarūpiṇī, mukundā and viṣṇurūpiṇī. the refuge of souls: nāra can mean souls and ayana means refuge or path. nārāyaṇī is the dynamic śakti identical with that refuge, showing no difference between pervasive consciousness and its power.","esoteric":["The Refuge of Souls: Nāra can mean souls and ayana means refuge or path. Nārāyaṇī is the dynamic śakti identical with that refuge, showing no difference between pervasive consciousness and its power."]},{"number":299,"name":"नादरूपा","samasa":["• नाद एव रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","नादरूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: नाद एव रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["नादरूपा means one who is in the form of sound. Sound has four stages: parā, manifest only in prāṇa; paśyantī, manifest in the mind; madhyamā, manifest in the organs; and vaikharī, manifest as articulated speech. All four occur as names of Śrīdevī. Between madhyamā and vaikharī are nine subtle sounds connected with letters, and nāda pervades them as their cause. In the bīja hrīṃ, the final half-letter resonates in an extended way. Above the bindu are subtle stages such as ardhacandra, rodhinī, nāda, nādānta, śakti, vyāpikā, samanā and unmanī; Śrīdevī is the nāda among them."],"searchText":"299 नादरूपा • नाद एव रूपं यस्याः सा। रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she नादरूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: नाद एव रूपं यस्याः सा। नादरूपा means one who is in the form of sound. sound has four stages: parā, manifest only in prāṇa; paśyantī, manifest in the mind; madhyamā, manifest in the organs; and vaikharī, manifest as articulated speech. all four occur as names of śrīdevī. between madhyamā and vaikharī are nine subtle sounds connected with letters, and nāda pervades them as their cause. in the bīja hrīṃ, the final half-letter resonates in an extended way. above the bindu are subtle stages such as ardhacandra, rodhinī, nāda, nādānta, śakti, vyāpikā, samanā and unmanī; śrīdevī is the nāda among them. primal vibration: before sound becomes audible speech, it exists as subtle nāda. she is that primary vibration from which mantra, syllable and language unfold.","esoteric":["Primal Vibration: Before sound becomes audible speech, it exists as subtle nāda. She is that primary vibration from which mantra, syllable and language unfold."]},{"number":300,"name":"नामरूपविवर्जिता","samasa":["• नामरूपाभ्यां विवर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["विवर्जिता — free from; devoid of","नामरूपविवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: नामरूपाभ्यां विवर्जिता।"],"summary":["नामरूपविवर्जिता means one who is without name and form. Everything in the world is identified by name and form, but She is beyond both and cannot be indicated by them. Created things are known through five aspects: existence, knowledge, bliss or affection, name and form. The first three relate cit to the world; the last two are illusory. Only Brahman is beyond name and form, and therefore Śrīdevī is beyond name and form."],"searchText":"300 नामरूपविवर्जिता • नामरूपाभ्यां विवर्जिता। विवर्जिता — free from; devoid of नामरूपविवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: नामरूपाभ्यां विवर्जिता। नामरूपविवर्जिता means one who is without name and form. everything in the world is identified by name and form, but she is beyond both and cannot be indicated by them. created things are known through five aspects: existence, knowledge, bliss or affection, name and form. the first three relate cit to the world; the last two are illusory. only brahman is beyond name and form, and therefore śrīdevī is beyond name and form. the transcendent absolute: though she assumes names and forms for worship, her true nature is the unconditioned brahman beyond mental definition and physical shape.","esoteric":["The Transcendent Absolute: Though She assumes names and forms for worship, Her true nature is the unconditioned Brahman beyond mental definition and physical shape."]},{"number":301,"name":"ह्रींकारी","samasa":["• ह्रीं करोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["ह्रीं — Hrim seed-syllable","करोतीति — makes; manifests","ह्रींकारी — meaning follows from the samasa: ह्रीं करोतीति।"],"summary":["ह्रींकारी means one who is in the form of the hrīṃ bīja. Hrī means modesty, shyness and bashfulness; one who produces this is Hrīṃkārī. Śrīdevī is present as bashfulness in all beings. Because She performs creation, protection and destruction, She is also called Hrīṃkārī. Hrīṃ is one of Her names, the māyā-bīja and the Bhuvaneśvarī bīja. In the Pañcadaśī mantra it occurs at the end of every section. Oṃ is the general praṇava, while hrīṃ is the śākta praṇava."],"searchText":"301 ह्रींकारी • ह्रीं करोतीति। ह्रीं — hrim seed-syllable करोतीति — makes; manifests ह्रींकारी — meaning follows from the samasa: ह्रीं करोतीति। ह्रींकारी means one who is in the form of the hrīṃ bīja. hrī means modesty, shyness and bashfulness; one who produces this is hrīṃkārī. śrīdevī is present as bashfulness in all beings. because she performs creation, protection and destruction, she is also called hrīṃkārī. hrīṃ is one of her names, the māyā-bīja and the bhuvaneśvarī bīja. in the pañcadaśī mantra it occurs at the end of every section. oṃ is the general praṇava, while hrīṃ is the śākta praṇava. the cosmic sound form: hrīṃ is the bīja of sacred modesty and containment. as hrīṃkārī, she animates the vibration between unmanifest brahman and the manifest universe.","esoteric":["The Cosmic Sound Form: Hrīṃ is the bīja of sacred modesty and containment. As Hrīṃkārī, She animates the vibration between unmanifest Brahman and the manifest universe."]},{"number":302,"name":"ह्रीमती","samasa":["• ह्रीः अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["ह्रीः — modesty; sacred Hri power","ह्रीमती — meaning follows from the samasa: ह्रीः अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"summary":["ह्रीमती means one who has modesty. Śrīdevī is indicated as modesty, mind, satisfaction, interest and nourishment. Those born in good families, educated well, of good character and in noble company feel ashamed to do wrong actions; that shame restrains them. Śrīdevī is the form of this inner modesty."],"searchText":"302 ह्रीमती • ह्रीः अस्याः अस्तीति। ह्रीः — modesty; sacred hri power ह्रीमती — meaning follows from the samasa: ह्रीः अस्याः अस्तीति। ह्रीमती means one who has modesty. śrīdevī is indicated as modesty, mind, satisfaction, interest and nourishment. those born in good families, educated well, of good character and in noble company feel ashamed to do wrong actions; that shame restrains them. śrīdevī is the form of this inner modesty. cosmic modesty: hrī is the divine veil and conscience within beings. as hrīmatī, she guides the heart away from transgression and toward purity.","esoteric":["Cosmic Modesty: Hrī is the divine veil and conscience within beings. As Hrīmatī, She guides the heart away from transgression and toward purity."]},{"number":303,"name":"हृद्या","samasa":["• हृदि भवा।"],"wordByWord":["हृदि — in the heart","भवा — dwelling; being","हृद्या — meaning follows from the samasa: हृदि भवा।"],"summary":["हृद्या means one who abides in the heart. She lives in the hearts of ascetics and devotees. The name can also mean one who is delightful and pleasing to the mind."],"searchText":"303 हृद्या • हृदि भवा। हृदि — in the heart भवा — dwelling; being हृद्या — meaning follows from the samasa: हृदि भवा। हृद्या means one who abides in the heart. she lives in the hearts of ascetics and devotees. the name can also mean one who is delightful and pleasing to the mind. the heart substratum: hṛdaya is the inner spiritual heart, the space of consciousness. she is the light residing there and is approached through inward meditation.","esoteric":["The Heart Substratum: Hṛdaya is the inner spiritual heart, the space of consciousness. She is the light residing there and is approached through inward meditation."]},{"number":304,"name":"हेयोपादेयवर्जिता","samasa":["• हातुम् उपादातुं च योग्ये हेयोपादेये। ताभ्यां वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["हेयोपादेये — what is to be rejected and accepted","वर्जिता — free from","हेयोपादेयवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: हातुम् उपादातुं च योग्ये हेयोपादेये। ताभ्यां वर्जिता।"],"summary":["हेयोपादेयवर्जिता means one who has nothing to reject or accept. Injunctions and prohibitions apply to those who are ignorant; since Śrīdevī is knowledge itself, She is beyond them. Heya is what is to be abandoned, and upādeya is what is to be accepted. She has no interest, disinterest or aversion, and therefore nothing to accept, reject or regret."],"searchText":"304 हेयोपादेयवर्जिता • हातुम् उपादातुं च योग्ये हेयोपादेये। ताभ्यां वर्जिता। हेयोपादेये — what is to be rejected and accepted वर्जिता — free from हेयोपादेयवर्जिता — meaning follows from the samasa: हातुम् उपादातुं च योग्ये हेयोपादेये। ताभ्यां वर्जिता। हेयोपादेयवर्जिता means one who has nothing to reject or accept. injunctions and prohibitions apply to those who are ignorant; since śrīdevī is knowledge itself, she is beyond them. heya is what is to be abandoned, and upādeya is what is to be accepted. she has no interest, disinterest or aversion, and therefore nothing to accept, reject or regret. beyond attraction and repulsion: acceptance and rejection arise only when something appears separate from the self. since she is the non-dual whole, nothing is outside her to gain or discard.","esoteric":["Beyond Attraction and Repulsion: Acceptance and rejection arise only when something appears separate from the self. Since She is the non-dual whole, nothing is outside Her to gain or discard."]},{"number":305,"name":"राजराजार्चिता","samasa":["• राज्ञां राज्ञा अर्चिता।"],"wordByWord":["राज्ञां — of kings","राज्ञा — by the king","अर्चिता — worshipped","राजराजार्चिता — meaning follows from the samasa: राज्ञां राज्ञा अर्चिता।"],"summary":["राजराजार्चिता means one who is worshipped by Rājarāja. Rājarāja can indicate the twelve presiding deities of various mantras beginning with Manu and Candra; they worship Śrīdevī. She may also be understood as the form of the different Śrīvidyā traditions taught by them. Rājarāja also refers to Kubera, king of kings, who dwells in Śrīcakra with his attendants and adores Her."],"searchText":"305 राजराजार्चिता • राज्ञां राज्ञा अर्चिता। राज्ञां — of kings राज्ञा — by the king अर्चिता — worshipped राजराजार्चिता — meaning follows from the samasa: राज्ञां राज्ञा अर्चिता। राजराजार्चिता means one who is worshipped by rājarāja. rājarāja can indicate the twelve presiding deities of various mantras beginning with manu and candra; they worship śrīdevī. she may also be understood as the form of the different śrīvidyā traditions taught by them. rājarāja also refers to kubera, king of kings, who dwells in śrīcakra with his attendants and adores her. the worship of kubera: even the king of wealth bows before her. material sovereignty and mantra lineages both receive their sustaining power through her worship.","esoteric":["The Worship of Kubera: Even the king of wealth bows before Her. Material sovereignty and mantra lineages both receive their sustaining power through Her worship."]},{"number":306,"name":"राज्ञी","samasa":["• राज्ञी।"],"wordByWord":["राज्ञी — queen","राज्ञी — meaning follows from the samasa: राज्ञी।"],"summary":["राज्ञी means one who is queen. Śrīdevī is the empress of Rājarājeśvara, Mahākāmeśvara. She is also the most beautiful."],"searchText":"306 राज्ञी • राज्ञी। राज्ञी — queen राज्ञी — meaning follows from the samasa: राज्ञी। राज्ञी means one who is queen. śrīdevī is the empress of rājarājeśvara, mahākāmeśvara. she is also the most beautiful. the supreme sovereign: she is lalitā mahātripurasundarī, the empress who governs the cosmos from the cintāmaṇigṛha. all laws, elements and deities operate under her command.","esoteric":["The Supreme Sovereign: She is Lalitā Mahātripurasundarī, the empress who governs the cosmos from the cintāmaṇigṛha. All laws, elements and deities operate under Her command."]},{"number":307,"name":"रम्या","samasa":["• रम्या। (सौन्दर्यवती)।"],"wordByWord":["रम्या — beautiful; pleasing","रम्या — meaning follows from the samasa: रम्या। (सौन्दर्यवती)।"],"summary":["रम्या means one who is most beautiful."],"searchText":"307 रम्या • रम्या। (सौन्दर्यवती)। रम्या — beautiful; pleasing रम्या — meaning follows from the samasa: रम्या। (सौन्दर्यवती)। रम्या means one who is most beautiful. the origin of delight: she is the embodiment of beauty and bliss. whatever appears beautiful or delightful reflects a small part of her inherent splendor.","esoteric":["The Origin of Delight: She is the embodiment of beauty and bliss. Whatever appears beautiful or delightful reflects a small part of Her inherent splendor."]},{"number":308,"name":"राजीवलोचना","samasa":["• राजीव इव लोचने यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["राजीव — lotus; deer; fish","लोचने — eyes","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","राजीवलोचना — meaning follows from the samasa: राजीव इव लोचने यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["राजीवलोचना means one whose eyes are like deer, fish and red lotus. Rājīva can mean deer, fish and red lotus, and Her eyes are likened to all these. Rājīva can also mean one dependent on a king; She looks with affection and blessings upon the devotees of Her consort Rājarājeśvara."],"searchText":"308 राजीवलोचना • राजीव इव लोचने यस्याः सा। राजीव — lotus; deer; fish लोचने — eyes यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she राजीवलोचना — meaning follows from the samasa: राजीव इव लोचने यस्याः सा। राजीवलोचना means one whose eyes are like deer, fish and red lotus. rājīva can mean deer, fish and red lotus, and her eyes are likened to all these. rājīva can also mean one dependent on a king; she looks with affection and blessings upon the devotees of her consort rājarājeśvara. the lotus sight: her lotus-like eyes shower compassion and peace. her gaze is open, pure and untouched by worldly impurity.","esoteric":["The Lotus Sight: Her lotus-like eyes shower compassion and peace. Her gaze is open, pure and untouched by worldly impurity."]},{"number":309,"name":"रञ्जनी","samasa":["• भक्तान् रञ्जयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तान् — devotees","रञ्जयतीति — delights; colours","रञ्जनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भक्तान् रञ्जयतीति।"],"summary":["रञ्जनी means one who delights Her devotees. She delights them by giving bliss in this world and liberation in the other world. Rañjayati also means to make red, and Śrīdevī's colour is red; by Her presence, even pure Paramaśiva is coloured red, as a red flower colours crystal."],"searchText":"309 रञ्जनी • भक्तान् रञ्जयतीति। भक्तान् — devotees रञ्जयतीति — delights; colours रञ्जनी — meaning follows from the samasa: भक्तान् रञ्जयतीति। रञ्जनी means one who delights her devotees. she delights them by giving bliss in this world and liberation in the other world. rañjayati also means to make red, and śrīdevī's colour is red; by her presence, even pure paramaśiva is coloured red, as a red flower colours crystal. coloring the mind: to color the mind is to fill it with divine consciousness. she saturates the devotee's heart with the red glow of devotion and bliss.","esoteric":["Coloring the Mind: To color the mind is to fill it with divine consciousness. She saturates the devotee's heart with the red glow of devotion and bliss."]},{"number":310,"name":"रमणी","samasa":["• भक्तान् रमयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तान् — devotees","रमयतीति — causes to rejoice","रमणी — meaning follows from the samasa: भक्तान् रमयतीति।"],"summary":["रमणी means one who moves closely and delightfully with devotees. Because of Her greatness, devotees might approach Her with fear, amazement and awe. By making Herself simple and approachable, She allows devotees to come near without fear."],"searchText":"310 रमणी • भक्तान् रमयतीति। भक्तान् — devotees रमयतीति — causes to rejoice रमणी — meaning follows from the samasa: भक्तान् रमयतीति। रमणी means one who moves closely and delightfully with devotees. because of her greatness, devotees might approach her with fear, amazement and awe. by making herself simple and approachable, she allows devotees to come near without fear. the rest within consciousness: she brings delight to practitioners and ends restless wandering through saṃsāra. in her presence, the mind finds its natural joy and rest.","esoteric":["The Rest Within Consciousness: She brings delight to practitioners and ends restless wandering through saṃsāra. In Her presence, the mind finds its natural joy and rest."]},{"number":311,"name":"रस्या","samasa":["• रसयितुं योग्या।"],"wordByWord":["रसयितुं — to taste; to relish","योग्या — fit; worthy","रस्या — meaning follows from the samasa: रसयितुं योग्या।"],"summary":["रस्या means one who is to be tasted as the essence of bliss. Rasa is the feeling that follows continuous experience in the mind; when tasteful it is rasa, and when tasteless it is virasa. The universal absolute is rasa, the essence. As juice is drawn from fruit and enjoyed, the subtle essence is drawn from the gross and enjoyed. In this way Śrīdevī is to be experienced as rasa."],"searchText":"311 रस्या • रसयितुं योग्या। रसयितुं — to taste; to relish योग्या — fit; worthy रस्या — meaning follows from the samasa: रसयितुं योग्या। रस्या means one who is to be tasted as the essence of bliss. rasa is the feeling that follows continuous experience in the mind; when tasteful it is rasa, and when tasteless it is virasa. the universal absolute is rasa, the essence. as juice is drawn from fruit and enjoyed, the subtle essence is drawn from the gross and enjoyed. in this way śrīdevī is to be experienced as rasa. the ultimate experience: she is the essential sweetness behind experience. she is tasted inwardly as the nectar of non-dual bliss in deep realization.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Experience: She is the essential sweetness behind experience. She is tasted inwardly as the nectar of non-dual bliss in deep realization."]},{"number":312,"name":"रणत्किङ्किणिमेखला","samasa":["• रणन्त्यः किङ्किण्यः यस्यां तादृशी मेखला यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["रणन्त्यः — tinkling; sounding","किङ्किण्यः — small bells","मेखला — girdle","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","रणत्किङ्किणिमेखला — meaning follows from the samasa: रणन्त्यः किङ्किण्यः यस्यां तादृशी मेखला यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["रणत्किङ्किणिमेखला means one who wears a girdle with tinkling bells. Her waist-belt is adorned with kiṅkiṇī bells that sound as She moves."],"searchText":"312 रणत्किङ्किणिमेखला • रणन्त्यः किङ्किण्यः यस्यां तादृशी मेखला यस्याः सा। रणन्त्यः — tinkling; sounding किङ्किण्यः — small bells मेखला — girdle यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she रणत्किङ्किणिमेखला — meaning follows from the samasa: रणन्त्यः किङ्किण्यः यस्यां तादृशी मेखला यस्याः सा। रणत्किङ्किणिमेखला means one who wears a girdle with tinkling bells. her waist-belt is adorned with kiṅkiṇī bells that sound as she moves. the sound of the girdle: the tinkling kiṅkiṇī bells suggest subtle sacred sound. her movement is accompanied by delicate nāda that awakens inner awareness.","esoteric":["The Sound of the Girdle: The tinkling kiṅkiṇī bells suggest subtle sacred sound. Her movement is accompanied by delicate nāda that awakens inner awareness."]},{"number":313,"name":"रमा","samasa":["• रमा।"],"wordByWord":["रमा — Lakshmi; delight","रमा — meaning follows from the samasa: रमा।"],"summary":["रमा means one who is in the form of Lakṣmī. She appears in forms such as Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī. The fourth Sanskrit vowel e is indicated by this name, and it is the third letter in the Pañcadaśī mantra. The related name Ratirūpā may be remembered. In Mahāṣoḍhā Nyāsa, She is also indicated in the form of a river."],"searchText":"313 रमा • रमा। रमा — lakshmi; delight रमा — meaning follows from the samasa: रमा। रमा means one who is in the form of lakṣmī. she appears in forms such as lakṣmī and sarasvatī. the fourth sanskrit vowel e is indicated by this name, and it is the third letter in the pañcadaśī mantra. the related name ratirūpā may be remembered. in mahāṣoḍhā nyāsa, she is also indicated in the form of a river. the principle of lakṣmī: she is not separate from lakṣmī, called ramā. wealth, beauty and sovereignty are forms of her expansive power.","esoteric":["The Principle of Lakṣmī: She is not separate from Lakṣmī, called Ramā. Wealth, beauty and sovereignty are forms of Her expansive power."]},{"number":314,"name":"राकेन्दुवदना","samasa":["• राकेन्दुवत् वदनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["राकेन्दुवत् — like the full moon","वदनं — face","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","राकेन्दुवदना — meaning follows from the samasa: राकेन्दुवत् वदनं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["राकेन्दुवदना means one whose face is like the full moon. Just as people are pleased again and again by seeing the ocean, an elephant and the moon, Her face gives inexhaustible joy. The moon also suggests both circular fullness and crescent beauty."],"searchText":"314 राकेन्दुवदना • राकेन्दुवत् वदनं यस्याः सा। राकेन्दुवत् — like the full moon वदनं — face यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she राकेन्दुवदना — meaning follows from the samasa: राकेन्दुवत् वदनं यस्याः सा। राकेन्दुवदना means one whose face is like the full moon. just as people are pleased again and again by seeing the ocean, an elephant and the moon, her face gives inexhaustible joy. the moon also suggests both circular fullness and crescent beauty. the coolness of grace: her full-moon face radiates soothing nectar-like light. it cools the heat of sorrow and gives peace to the devotee.","esoteric":["The Coolness of Grace: Her full-moon face radiates soothing nectar-like light. It cools the heat of sorrow and gives peace to the devotee."]},{"number":315,"name":"रतिरूपा","samasa":["• रतिः एव रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["रतिः — Rati; love; delight","रूपं — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","रतिरूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: रतिः एव रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["रतिरूपा means one who is in the form of Rati, the consort of Kāma. Rati is interest, attraction and involvement in an object; until the desired thing is obtained, people do not find peace. Rati helps Kāma by creating love and interest. Śrīdevī’s energy appears in the form of Rati, and therefore She is Ratirūpā. The name also connects with the Kāmākalā letter eṃ, formed by the union of e, bindu and anusvāra."],"searchText":"315 रतिरूपा • रतिः एव रूपं यस्याः सा। रतिः — rati; love; delight रूपं — form यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she रतिरूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: रतिः एव रूपं यस्याः सा। रतिरूपा means one who is in the form of rati, the consort of kāma. rati is interest, attraction and involvement in an object; until the desired thing is obtained, people do not find peace. rati helps kāma by creating love and interest. śrīdevī’s energy appears in the form of rati, and therefore she is ratirūpā. the name also connects with the kāmākalā letter eṃ, formed by the union of e, bindu and anusvāra. the essence of delight: rati is the capacity for joy, attraction and pleasure. she manifests as that capacity within living beings.","esoteric":["The Essence of Delight: Rati is the capacity for joy, attraction and pleasure. She manifests as that capacity within living beings."]},{"number":316,"name":"रतिप्रिया","samasa":["• रतिः प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["रतिः — Rati; love; delight","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","रतिप्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: रतिः प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["रतिप्रिया means one who is beloved of Rati, the wife of Kāma. Rati also means copulation and erotic art. The name indicates the delight of union with Her consort Kāmeśvara in the Sahasrāra. It also shows that the love and attraction between husband and wife arise because woman is a part of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"316 रतिप्रिया • रतिः प्रियं यस्याः सा। रतिः — rati; love; delight यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she रतिप्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: रतिः प्रियं यस्याः सा। रतिप्रिया means one who is beloved of rati, the wife of kāma. rati also means copulation and erotic art. the name indicates the delight of union with her consort kāmeśvara in the sahasrāra. it also shows that the love and attraction between husband and wife arise because woman is a part of śrīdevī. the love of divine delight: she is pleased by the intense loving delight of inward union. rati directed toward the divine becomes a path to her.","esoteric":["The Love of Divine Delight: She is pleased by the intense loving delight of inward union. Rati directed toward the divine becomes a path to Her."]},{"number":317,"name":"रक्षाकरी","samasa":["• रक्षां करोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["रक्षां — protection","करोतीति — makes; manifests","रक्षाकरी — meaning follows from the samasa: रक्षां करोतीति।"],"summary":["रक्षाकरी means the protector. She performs the work of guarding and protecting. Rakṣā also means the holy ashes from a sacrificial fire. Just as offerings in the fire become ash, Śrīdevī burns everything into ash; in this sense She performs both protection and destruction."],"searchText":"317 रक्षाकरी • रक्षां करोतीति। रक्षां — protection करोतीति — makes; manifests रक्षाकरी — meaning follows from the samasa: रक्षां करोतीति। रक्षाकरी means the protector. she performs the work of guarding and protecting. rakṣā also means the holy ashes from a sacrificial fire. just as offerings in the fire become ash, śrīdevī burns everything into ash; in this sense she performs both protection and destruction. the absolute shield: she protects the devotee from outer danger and inner downfall. her grace guards the mind from doubt, pride and scattering.","esoteric":["The Absolute Shield: She protects the devotee from outer danger and inner downfall. Her grace guards the mind from doubt, pride and scattering."]},{"number":318,"name":"राक्षसघ्नी","samasa":["• राक्षसान् हन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["राक्षसान् — demons","हन्तीति — kills","राक्षसघ्नी — meaning follows from the samasa: राक्षसान् हन्तीति।"],"summary":["राक्षसघ्नी means slayer of demons. She destroys wicked and demonic forces for the protection of the good. The related name Daityahantrī also has this sense."],"searchText":"318 राक्षसघ्नी • राक्षसान् हन्तीति। राक्षसान् — demons हन्तीति — kills राक्षसघ्नी — meaning follows from the samasa: राक्षसान् हन्तीति। राक्षसघ्नी means slayer of demons. she destroys wicked and demonic forces for the protection of the good. the related name daityahantrī also has this sense. destroyer of inner demons: rākṣasas also represent dark forces in the mind such as anger, greed, lust and delusion. as rākṣasaghnī, she removes these impurities and restores dharma.","esoteric":["Destroyer of Inner Demons: Rākṣasas also represent dark forces in the mind such as anger, greed, lust and delusion. As Rākṣasaghnī, She removes these impurities and restores dharma."]},{"number":319,"name":"रामा","samasa":["• रमन्ते अस्यां योगिनः।"],"wordByWord":["रमन्ते — delight","अस्यां — in her","योगिनः — yogins","रामा — meaning follows from the samasa: रमन्ते अस्यां योगिनः।"],"summary":["रामा means woman, and also one who delights yogins. All feminine words indicate Śrīdevī. When women are pleased, divine forces are pleased and the family prospers; when they are displeased, the family declines. Since yogins delight in meditating on and worshipping Śrīdevī, She is called Rāmā. The root ram means to delight."],"searchText":"319 रामा • रमन्ते अस्यां योगिनः। रमन्ते — delight अस्यां — in her योगिनः — yogins रामा — meaning follows from the samasa: रमन्ते अस्यां योगिनः। रामा means woman, and also one who delights yogins. all feminine words indicate śrīdevī. when women are pleased, divine forces are pleased and the family prospers; when they are displeased, the family declines. since yogins delight in meditating on and worshipping śrīdevī, she is called rāmā. the root ram means to delight. the refuge of yogins: yogins delight in the infinite and find their rest in her consciousness. she is the inward place of joy where seekers find peace.","esoteric":["The Refuge of Yogins: Yogins delight in the infinite and find their rest in Her consciousness. She is the inward place of joy where seekers find peace."]},{"number":320,"name":"रमणलम्पटा","samasa":["• रमणेषु लम्पटा।"],"wordByWord":["रमणेषु — in union with the beloved","लम्पटा — deeply attached","रमणलम्पटा — meaning follows from the samasa: रमणेषु लम्पटा।"],"summary":["रमणलम्पटा means one devoted to Her husband. She is absorbed in union with Her consort Kāmeśvara in the Sahasrāra. The name also indicates that every woman’s devotion to her husband arises because she is part of Śrīdevī. Ramaṇa means enjoyment or play, and lampaṭā means devoted."],"searchText":"320 रमणलम्पटा • रमणेषु लम्पटा। रमणेषु — in union with the beloved लम्पटा — deeply attached रमणलम्पटा — meaning follows from the samasa: रमणेषु लम्पटा। रमणलम्पटा means one devoted to her husband. she is absorbed in union with her consort kāmeśvara in the sahasrāra. the name also indicates that every woman’s devotion to her husband arises because she is part of śrīdevī. ramaṇa means enjoyment or play, and lampaṭā means devoted. the union of śiva and śakti: ramaṇa refers to kāmeśvara. lampaṭā signifies her unbroken absorption in non-dual union with him.","esoteric":["The Union of Śiva and Śakti: Ramaṇa refers to Kāmeśvara. Lampaṭā signifies Her unbroken absorption in non-dual union with Him."]},{"number":321,"name":"काम्या","samasa":["• [ज्ञानेन प्राप्तव्यत्वेन मुमुक्षुभिः] काम्या।"],"wordByWord":["काम्या — desired; worthy of being sought","काम्या — meaning follows from the samasa: [ज्ञानेन प्राप्तव्यत्वेन मुमुक्षुभिः] काम्या।"],"summary":["काम्या means one who is greatly desired. Those who seek liberation desire to attain Her through knowledge. Kāmyā is also the deity of the twelfth night of the dark fortnight of the lunar month. In Śrīvidyā practice the twelfth day of the dark fortnight and the fourth day of the bright fortnight have the same presiding deity, Bheruṇḍā; another reckoning calls the presiding deity of the fourth bright night Viśvarūpā and of the twelfth dark night Kāmyā."],"searchText":"321 काम्या • [ज्ञानेन प्राप्तव्यत्वेन मुमुक्षुभिः] काम्या। काम्या — desired; worthy of being sought काम्या — meaning follows from the samasa: [ज्ञानेन प्राप्तव्यत्वेन मुमुक्षुभिः] काम्या। काम्या means one who is greatly desired. those who seek liberation desire to attain her through knowledge. kāmyā is also the deity of the twelfth night of the dark fortnight of the lunar month. in śrīvidyā practice the twelfth day of the dark fortnight and the fourth day of the bright fortnight have the same presiding deity, bheruṇḍā; another reckoning calls the presiding deity of the fourth bright night viśvarūpā and of the twelfth dark night kāmyā. the ultimate goal of the seeker: ordinary desires aim at passing objects. for the seeker of liberation, she alone is truly worth desiring.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Goal of the Seeker: Ordinary desires aim at passing objects. For the seeker of liberation, She alone is truly worth desiring."]},{"number":322,"name":"कामकलारूपा","samasa":["• कामकला रूपं यस्या सा।","• कामा च असौ कलारूपा च।"],"wordByWord":["कामकला — Kamakala","रूपं — form","सा — she","कामकलारूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: कामकला रूपं यस्या सा।"],"summary":["कामकलारूपा means one who is in the form of Kāmākalā. The names Mūlamantrātmikā and Mūlakūṭatrayakalebarā are related to this idea. Kāmākalā consists of three bindus, one above and two at the sides, and hārdakalā in triangular form below. This is expressed by the letter eṃ and indicates the union of Śiva and Śakti. The first bindu is called kāma and hārdakalā is called kalā. Śrīdevī has the names Kāmā and Kalā, and therefore She is Kāmākalā."],"searchText":"322 कामकलारूपा • कामकला रूपं यस्या सा। • कामा च असौ कलारूपा च। कामकला — kamakala रूपं — form सा — she कामकलारूपा — meaning follows from the samasa: कामकला रूपं यस्या सा। कामकलारूपा means one who is in the form of kāmākalā. the names mūlamantrātmikā and mūlakūṭatrayakalebarā are related to this idea. kāmākalā consists of three bindus, one above and two at the sides, and hārdakalā in triangular form below. this is expressed by the letter eṃ and indicates the union of śiva and śakti. the first bindu is called kāma and hārdakalā is called kalā. śrīdevī has the names kāmā and kalā, and therefore she is kāmākalā. the triadic bindu structure: kāmākalā is formed of three bindus and the underlying kalā. it is the creative formula of śiva and śakti united.","esoteric":["The Triadic Bindu Structure: Kāmākalā is formed of three bindus and the underlying kalā. It is the creative formula of Śiva and Śakti united."]},{"number":323,"name":"कदम्बकुसुमप्रिया","samasa":["• कदम्बकुसुमानि प्रियानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कदम्बकुसुमानि — Kadamba flowers","प्रियानि — dear","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","कदम्बकुसुमप्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: कदम्बकुसुमानि प्रियानि यस्याः सा।"],"summary":["कदम्बकुसुमप्रिया means one who is fond of kadamba flowers. Because She is fond of kadamba trees, a kadamba grove is established outside Her cintāmaṇigṛha. The name also indicates Mīnākṣī of Madurai. Kadamba can symbolize the mind, and kadamba flower can symbolize the expansion of the mind. Knowledge and expansion are inseparable; therefore Śrīdevī, who is the integrated form of knowledge of subjects and tattvas, is fond of the kadamba flower as the expansion of mind."],"searchText":"323 कदम्बकुसुमप्रिया • कदम्बकुसुमानि प्रियानि यस्याः सा। कदम्बकुसुमानि — kadamba flowers प्रियानि — dear यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she कदम्बकुसुमप्रिया — meaning follows from the samasa: कदम्बकुसुमानि प्रियानि यस्याः सा। कदम्बकुसुमप्रिया means one who is fond of kadamba flowers. because she is fond of kadamba trees, a kadamba grove is established outside her cintāmaṇigṛha. the name also indicates mīnākṣī of madurai. kadamba can symbolize the mind, and kadamba flower can symbolize the expansion of the mind. knowledge and expansion are inseparable; therefore śrīdevī, who is the integrated form of knowledge of subjects and tattvas, is fond of the kadamba flower as the expansion of mind. the kadamba grove: kadamba flowers represent the blossoming of the mind. offering them signifies the surrender of a fully opened heart and intellect to her.","esoteric":["The Kadamba Grove: Kadamba flowers represent the blossoming of the mind. Offering them signifies the surrender of a fully opened heart and intellect to Her."]},{"number":324,"name":"कल्याणी","samasa":["• [मङ्गलस्वरूपत्वात्] कल्याणी।"],"wordByWord":["मङ्गलस्वरूपत्वात् — because of auspicious nature","कल्याणी — auspicious one","कल्याणी — meaning follows from the samasa: [मङ्गलस्वरूपत्वात्] कल्याणी।"],"summary":["कल्याणी means one who is auspicious. Śrīdevī is complete auspiciousness. Kalya can mean good words and ana can mean to utter, so Kalyāṇī can mean one who always speaks good words. She is worshipped as Kalyāṇī on Malaya mountain. Auspiciousness is happiness, from ordinary human happiness up to the happiness of Brahmā; all are tiny drops of complete bliss. Śrīdevī is complete bliss, the blemishless Brahman of knowledge and bliss."],"searchText":"324 कल्याणी • [मङ्गलस्वरूपत्वात्] कल्याणी। मङ्गलस्वरूपत्वात् — because of auspicious nature कल्याणी — auspicious one कल्याणी — meaning follows from the samasa: [मङ्गलस्वरूपत्वात्] कल्याणी। कल्याणी means one who is auspicious. śrīdevī is complete auspiciousness. kalya can mean good words and ana can mean to utter, so kalyāṇī can mean one who always speaks good words. she is worshipped as kalyāṇī on malaya mountain. auspiciousness is happiness, from ordinary human happiness up to the happiness of brahmā; all are tiny drops of complete bliss. śrīdevī is complete bliss, the blemishless brahman of knowledge and bliss. the essence of well-being: she is auspiciousness itself. remembering her removes inauspiciousness, negative thought and obstruction, bringing clarity and welfare.","esoteric":["The Essence of Well-being: She is auspiciousness itself. Remembering Her removes inauspiciousness, negative thought and obstruction, bringing clarity and welfare."]},{"number":325,"name":"जगतीकन्दा","samasa":["• जगत्याः कन्दं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["जगत्याः — of the world; of the universe","कन्दं — root; bulb; source of support","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","जगतीकन्दा — she whose root or source is the universe, or who is the root-cause of the universe"],"summary":["जगतीकन्दा means one who is the root cause of the universe. The word कन्द has meanings such as root of a plant, cloud, and that which fills. A root supports the whole plant and gives it strength. In the same way, Śrīdevī supports and strengthens the whole world."],"searchText":"325 जगतीकन्दा • जगत्याः कन्दं यस्याः सा। जगत्याः — of the world; of the universe कन्दं — root; bulb; source of support यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she जगतीकन्दा — she whose root or source is the universe, or who is the root-cause of the universe जगतीकन्दा means one who is the root cause of the universe. the word कन्द has meanings such as root of a plant, cloud, and that which fills. a root supports the whole plant and gives it strength. in the same way, śrīdevī supports and strengthens the whole world. the cosmic root: just as a plant is supported by its root, the universe rests upon her causal power. she is the foundation from which creation grows.","esoteric":["The Cosmic Root: Just as a plant is supported by its root, the universe rests upon Her causal power. She is the foundation from which creation grows."]},{"number":326,"name":"करुणारससागरा","samasa":["• करुणा एव रसः येषु सागरेषु तादृशाः सागराः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["करुणा — compassion","रसः — essence; fluid; rasa","सागरा — oceans","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","करुणारससागरा — she whose oceans have compassion as their essence"],"summary":["करुणारससागरा means one who is the ocean of compassion. Śrīdevī is like an ocean whose water is compassion, and Her compassion is greater than an ocean. Her compassion for devotees is without deceit, partiality, quarrel or expectation. Her eyes are described as waves of compassion. Her compassion is like an ocean of nectar of liberation, flows through Her gracious glance, and is Her very body."],"searchText":"326 करुणारससागरा • करुणा एव रसः येषु सागरेषु तादृशाः सागराः यस्याः सा। करुणा — compassion रसः — essence; fluid; rasa सागरा — oceans यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she करुणारससागरा — she whose oceans have compassion as their essence करुणारससागरा means one who is the ocean of compassion. śrīdevī is like an ocean whose water is compassion, and her compassion is greater than an ocean. her compassion for devotees is without deceit, partiality, quarrel or expectation. her eyes are described as waves of compassion. her compassion is like an ocean of nectar of liberation, flows through her gracious glance, and is her very body. the ocean of mercy: her compassion is vast, deep and inexhaustible. it is not a passing emotion but a shoreless sea of grace.","esoteric":["The Ocean of Mercy: Her compassion is vast, deep and inexhaustible. It is not a passing emotion but a shoreless sea of grace."]},{"number":327,"name":"कलावती","samasa":["• (चतुःषष्टिसङ्ख्याः) कला अस्यां सन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["चतुःषष्टिसङ्ख्याः — sixty-four in number","कलाः — arts; kalas","अस्याम् — in her","सन्ति — exist","कलावती — she who possesses the arts"],"summary":["कलावती means one who embodies the sixty-four arts. She is the form and origin of all the arts described under Catuḥṣaṣṭikalāmayī."],"searchText":"327 कलावती • (चतुःषष्टिसङ्ख्याः) कला अस्यां सन्तीति। चतुःषष्टिसङ्ख्याः — sixty-four in number कलाः — arts; kalas अस्याम् — in her सन्ति — exist कलावती — she who possesses the arts कलावती means one who embodies the sixty-four arts. she is the form and origin of all the arts described under catuḥṣaṣṭikalāmayī. the sixty-four arts: she is the origin and master of the catuḥṣaṣṭi kalās, the arts that shape culture, skill and refinement.","esoteric":["The Sixty-Four Arts: She is the origin and master of the catuḥṣaṣṭi kalās, the arts that shape culture, skill and refinement."]},{"number":328,"name":"कलालापा","samasa":["• कल एव आलापः यस्याः सा।","• कं लालावत् आपः यस्याः सकाशात् सा।"],"wordByWord":["कला — art; also sweet sound","आलापः — speech; conversation","यस्याः — of whom; whose","कलालापा — she whose speech itself is art","कम् — Brahman","लाला — saliva; natural flow","आपः — attainment"],"summary":["कलालापा means one whose conversation is art. Everything Śrīdevī speaks is an art. Kalā can mean sweet-sounding and ālāpa means speech, so Kalālāpā means one who has sweet speech. Kam means Brahman, lālā means saliva, and āpa means attainment; just as saliva flows naturally when one thinks of tasty food, attainment of Brahman becomes natural through Her grace and leads along the path of liberation."],"searchText":"328 कलालापा • कल एव आलापः यस्याः सा। • कं लालावत् आपः यस्याः सकाशात् सा। कला — art; also sweet sound आलापः — speech; conversation यस्याः — of whom; whose कलालापा — she whose speech itself is art कम् — brahman लाला — saliva; natural flow आपः — attainment कलालापा means one whose conversation is art. everything śrīdevī speaks is an art. kalā can mean sweet-sounding and ālāpa means speech, so kalālāpā means one who has sweet speech. kam means brahman, lālā means saliva, and āpa means attainment; just as saliva flows naturally when one thinks of tasty food, attainment of brahman becomes natural through her grace and leads along the path of liberation. the sweetness of speech: her speech is sweet, artistic and filled with truth. through her grace, the movement toward brahman becomes natural.","esoteric":["The Sweetness of Speech: Her speech is sweet, artistic and filled with truth. Through Her grace, the movement toward Brahman becomes natural."]},{"number":329,"name":"कान्ता","samasa":["• कान्ता [कमनीयत्वात्]।","• कम् एव अन्तः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कान्ता — beautiful; beloved","कमनीयत्वात् — because of loveliness","कम् — Brahman","अन्तः — end; final state","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["कान्ता means one who is beautiful. Since She is effulgent, She appears as supreme beauty; lustre is the beauty and brightness of the body. Kam means Brahman and anta means final, so unconditioned Brahman is Her final form. This points to Śrīdevī’s form beyond qualities, while She makes both saguṇa and nirguṇa forms perceptible. Kāntā is also the presiding deity of the eleventh night of the dark fortnight of the lunar month."],"searchText":"329 कान्ता • कान्ता [कमनीयत्वात्]। • कम् एव अन्तः यस्याः सा। कान्ता — beautiful; beloved कमनीयत्वात् — because of loveliness कम् — brahman अन्तः — end; final state यस्याः — of whom; whose कान्ता means one who is beautiful. since she is effulgent, she appears as supreme beauty; lustre is the beauty and brightness of the body. kam means brahman and anta means final, so unconditioned brahman is her final form. this points to śrīdevī’s form beyond qualities, while she makes both saguṇa and nirguṇa forms perceptible. kāntā is also the presiding deity of the eleventh night of the dark fortnight of the lunar month. the supreme beauty: she is the ultimate beloved, drawing hearts by her radiance. as the final point of brahman, she is where the search for beauty and happiness ends.","esoteric":["The Supreme Beauty: She is the ultimate beloved, drawing hearts by Her radiance. As the final point of Brahman, She is where the search for beauty and happiness ends."]},{"number":330,"name":"कादम्बरीप्रिया","samasa":["• कादम्बरी (उत्तमा मदिरा) प्रिया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कादम्बरी — mead; high-quality liquor","प्रिया — dear; beloved","यस्याः — of whom; whose","कादम्बरीप्रिया — she to whom kadambari is dear"],"summary":["कादम्बरीप्रिया means one who is fond of mead. In Navāvaraṇa pūjā there are five articles beginning with ma: madhu, māṃsa, matsya, mudrā and maithuna. Mead is one of the consecrated offerings made to Śrīdevī and then consumed according to eligibility. Those not restricted from such articles may use them; others should use substitutes while keeping the corresponding tattvas in mind. Śrīdevī is fond of excellent mead. Related names include Samayācāratatparā, Vāruṇīmadavihvalā, Kaulamārgatatparasevitā, Madhuprītā, Mādhvīpānālasā, Madhumatī, Savyāpasavyamārgasthā and Dakṣiṇādakṣiṇārādhyā."],"searchText":"330 कादम्बरीप्रिया • कादम्बरी (उत्तमा मदिरा) प्रिया यस्याः सा। कादम्बरी — mead; high-quality liquor प्रिया — dear; beloved यस्याः — of whom; whose कादम्बरीप्रिया — she to whom kadambari is dear कादम्बरीप्रिया means one who is fond of mead. in navāvaraṇa pūjā there are five articles beginning with ma: madhu, māṃsa, matsya, mudrā and maithuna. mead is one of the consecrated offerings made to śrīdevī and then consumed according to eligibility. those not restricted from such articles may use them; others should use substitutes while keeping the corresponding tattvas in mind. śrīdevī is fond of excellent mead. related names include samayācāratatparā, vāruṇīmadavihvalā, kaulamārgatatparasevitā, madhuprītā, mādhvīpānālasā, madhumatī, savyāpasavyamārgasthā and dakṣiṇādakṣiṇārādhyā. the wine of divine intoxication: kādambarī also suggests the inner nectar of realization. she delights in the bliss that dissolves ego and turns the mind toward her.","esoteric":["The Wine of Divine Intoxication: Kādambarī also suggests the inner nectar of realization. She delights in the bliss that dissolves ego and turns the mind toward Her."]},{"number":331,"name":"वरदा","samasa":["• वरान् ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["वरान् — boons","ददाति — gives","वरदा — giver of boons"],"summary":["वरदा means one who bestows boons. She grants boons to Brahmā, Viṣṇu and other devotees. Her uplifted hand ever confers boons and fulfils the desires of devas, daityas and ascetics. Even without displaying the gesture of boon-giving, Śrīdevī grants devotees more than they desire. From the root vṛ, to choose, She is Varadā, the giver of what is chosen. Worshipped with concentration on the ninth lunar day, She becomes the giver of boons to all worlds."],"searchText":"331 वरदा • वरान् ददातीति। वरान् — boons ददाति — gives वरदा — giver of boons वरदा means one who bestows boons. she grants boons to brahmā, viṣṇu and other devotees. her uplifted hand ever confers boons and fulfils the desires of devas, daityas and ascetics. even without displaying the gesture of boon-giving, śrīdevī grants devotees more than they desire. from the root vṛ, to choose, she is varadā, the giver of what is chosen. worshipped with concentration on the ninth lunar day, she becomes the giver of boons to all worlds. the ultimate gift: other deities may grant limited boons such as long life, wealth or power. she grants the highest boon, ātma-dāna, the gift of her own self, which gives liberation.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Gift: Other deities may grant limited boons such as long life, wealth or power. She grants the highest boon, Ātma-dāna, the gift of Her own self, which gives liberation."]},{"number":332,"name":"वामनयना","samasa":["• वामानि नयनानि यस्याः सा।","• वामं नयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["वामानि — beautiful; graceful; also left","नयनानि — eyes; means of knowledge","यस्याः — of whom; whose","वामं — the left path; also fruit of action","नयति — leads","वामनयना — she with beautiful eyes; she who leads by the left path"],"summary":["वामनयना means one who has beautiful or graceful eyes. Vāma means beauty, and नयनम् means eyes or proof; the name can mean one with beautiful eyes, beautiful proofs, or a beautiful means of understanding. Vāma also means left-handed, and She leads devotees who follow the left-handed path. Vāma can also mean the fruits of actions, so She makes devotees reap the fruits of their actions. In Mātṛkā Nyāsa, the bīja for the left eye is eṃ; since this is a Kāmākalā bīja, the name may also indicate Kāmākalā."],"searchText":"332 वामनयना • वामानि नयनानि यस्याः सा। • वामं नयतीति। वामानि — beautiful; graceful; also left नयनानि — eyes; means of knowledge यस्याः — of whom; whose वामं — the left path; also fruit of action नयति — leads वामनयना — she with beautiful eyes; she who leads by the left path वामनयना means one who has beautiful or graceful eyes. vāma means beauty, and नयनम् means eyes or proof; the name can mean one with beautiful eyes, beautiful proofs, or a beautiful means of understanding. vāma also means left-handed, and she leads devotees who follow the left-handed path. vāma can also mean the fruits of actions, so she makes devotees reap the fruits of their actions. in mātṛkā nyāsa, the bīja for the left eye is eṃ; since this is a kāmākalā bīja, the name may also indicate kāmākalā. the guide to liberation: beyond her beautiful eyes, the root nī means to lead. as vāmanayanā, she leads the practitioner toward the highest spiritual beauty, liberation.","esoteric":["The Guide to Liberation: Beyond Her beautiful eyes, the root nī means to lead. As Vāmanayanā, She leads the practitioner toward the highest spiritual beauty, liberation."]},{"number":333,"name":"वारुणीमदविह्वला","samasa":["• वारुण्याः मदेन विह्वला।","• वरुणस्य इयं वारुणीमान् तस्य इव अविह्वला।"],"wordByWord":["वारुण्याः — of Vāruṇī liquor; of Varuṇa-related power","मदेन — by intoxication; by bliss","विह्वला — overwhelmed; perturbed","अविह्वला — not fatigued or exhausted"],"summary":["वारुणीमदविह्वला means one who is moved by Vāruṇī, the intoxicating wine of spiritual bliss. Vāruṇī is a liquor obtained from date fruit and is linked with Varuṇa. The expression indicates forgetting external objects and simply enjoying, as in Svātmārāma. The Brahmavidyā taught by Varuṇa to Bhṛgu is called Vāruṇī. The name may also be split as Vāruṇīmat and Avihvalā: by Her grace, Ādiśeṣa, connected with the region of Varuṇa, is not fatigued in supporting the universe. Vāruṇī is also a nāḍī connected with Vāyu in the body; Śrīdevī removes weariness and exhaustion from devotees."],"searchText":"333 वारुणीमदविह्वला • वारुण्याः मदेन विह्वला। • वरुणस्य इयं वारुणीमान् तस्य इव अविह्वला। वारुण्याः — of vāruṇī liquor; of varuṇa-related power मदेन — by intoxication; by bliss विह्वला — overwhelmed; perturbed अविह्वला — not fatigued or exhausted वारुणीमदविह्वला means one who is moved by vāruṇī, the intoxicating wine of spiritual bliss. vāruṇī is a liquor obtained from date fruit and is linked with varuṇa. the expression indicates forgetting external objects and simply enjoying, as in svātmārāma. the brahmavidyā taught by varuṇa to bhṛgu is called vāruṇī. the name may also be split as vāruṇīmat and avihvalā: by her grace, ādiśeṣa, connected with the region of varuṇa, is not fatigued in supporting the universe. vāruṇī is also a nāḍī connected with vāyu in the body; śrīdevī removes weariness and exhaustion from devotees. the wine of spiritual bliss: vāruṇī is the inward intoxication in which external objects are forgotten. she governs this blissful absorption and removes fatigue from devotees.","esoteric":["The Wine of Spiritual Bliss: Vāruṇī is the inward intoxication in which external objects are forgotten. She governs this blissful absorption and removes fatigue from devotees."]},{"number":334,"name":"विश्वाधिका","samasa":["• विश्वाधिका। विश्वस्मात् अधिका।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वस्मात् — than the universe","अधिका — greater; beyond","विश्वाधिका — she who transcends the universe"],"summary":["विश्वाधिका means one who transcends the whole world. She is beyond the thirty-six tattvas from earth up to Śiva. Since She is the united form of Śiva and Śakti and is in the form of Sadākhya-tattva, She is Viśvādhikā. Śrīdevī is beyond waking, dream and deep sleep, and even beyond the turīya state."],"searchText":"334 विश्वाधिका • विश्वाधिका। विश्वस्मात् अधिका। विश्वस्मात् — than the universe अधिका — greater; beyond विश्वाधिका — she who transcends the universe विश्वाधिका means one who transcends the whole world. she is beyond the thirty-six tattvas from earth up to śiva. since she is the united form of śiva and śakti and is in the form of sadākhya-tattva, she is viśvādhikā. śrīdevī is beyond waking, dream and deep sleep, and even beyond the turīya state. surpassing the manifested: though the universe is her own projection, she is not limited by it. her essential nature remains untouched by cosmic change.","esoteric":["Surpassing the Manifested: Though the universe is Her own projection, She is not limited by it. Her essential nature remains untouched by cosmic change."]},{"number":335,"name":"वेदवेद्या","samasa":["• वेदैः वेद्या।"],"wordByWord":["वेदैः — by the Vedas","वेद्या — to be known; knowable","वेदवेद्या — she who is known through the Vedas"],"summary":["वेदवेद्या means one who can be known through the Vedas. She can be realized through the Ṛg, Yajur, Sāma and Atharva Vedas. In Śrī Nagara, the dwelling place of Śrīdevī, the four Vedas are the four entrances, and one reaches Her by passing through them. In the bindu at the centre of Śrīcakra, the Āmnāya deities connected with the four Vedas are worshipped. Since She is recognized through these vidyās, Śrīdevī is Vedavedyā."],"searchText":"335 वेदवेद्या • वेदैः वेद्या। वेदैः — by the vedas वेद्या — to be known; knowable वेदवेद्या — she who is known through the vedas वेदवेद्या means one who can be known through the vedas. she can be realized through the ṛg, yajur, sāma and atharva vedas. in śrī nagara, the dwelling place of śrīdevī, the four vedas are the four entrances, and one reaches her by passing through them. in the bindu at the centre of śrīcakra, the āmnāya deities connected with the four vedas are worshipped. since she is recognized through these vidyās, śrīdevī is vedavedyā. the ultimate subject of revelation: the vedas have her as their final meaning. their rituals, vidyās and deities ultimately point toward śrīdevī, the supreme non-dual consciousness.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Subject of Revelation: The Vedas have Her as their final meaning. Their rituals, vidyās and deities ultimately point toward Śrīdevī, the supreme non-dual consciousness."]},{"number":336,"name":"विन्ध्याचलनिवासिनी","samasa":["• विन्ध्याख्ये अचले निवासतीति।"],"wordByWord":["विन्ध्याख्ये — called Vindhya","अचले — mountain","निवसति — dwells","विन्ध्याचलनिवासिनी — she who dwells in the Vindhya mountain"],"summary":["विन्ध्याचलनिवासिनी means one who resides in the Vindhya mountains. Śrīdevī incarnated during the Vaivasvata Manvantara in the house of Nandagopa, from the womb of Yaśodā, to destroy the demons Śumbha and Niśumbha. After that, She dwelt in the Vindhya mountains."],"searchText":"336 विन्ध्याचलनिवासिनी • विन्ध्याख्ये अचले निवासतीति। विन्ध्याख्ये — called vindhya अचले — mountain निवसति — dwells विन्ध्याचलनिवासिनी — she who dwells in the vindhya mountain विन्ध्याचलनिवासिनी means one who resides in the vindhya mountains. śrīdevī incarnated during the vaivasvata manvantara in the house of nandagopa, from the womb of yaśodā, to destroy the demons śumbha and niśumbha. after that, she dwelt in the vindhya mountains. the vindhya abode: she resides in the vindhya mountain range as a fierce protective deity. internally, the unmoving mountain suggests the firm base from which her power rises.","esoteric":["The Vindhya Abode: She resides in the Vindhya mountain range as a fierce protective deity. Internally, the unmoving mountain suggests the firm base from which Her power rises."]},{"number":337,"name":"विधात्री","samasa":["• विदधातीति।","• विधातुः पत्नी वा।"],"wordByWord":["विदधाति — supports; arranges; ordains","विधातुः — of Vidhātā, Brahmā","पत्नी — wife; consort","विधात्री — supporter; ordainer; consort of Brahmā"],"summary":["विधात्री means one who supports the universe. Since She supports and nourishes the universe, She is Vidhātrī. Vidhātā means Brahmā, and his consort is Vidhātrī. The word may also be connected with dhātrī, myrobalan, because She is fond of myrobalans. Dhātrī also means mother, who bears the child in her womb and releases it at the proper time. As the great mother, She is Vidhātrī."],"searchText":"337 विधात्री • विदधातीति। • विधातुः पत्नी वा। विदधाति — supports; arranges; ordains विधातुः — of vidhātā, brahmā पत्नी — wife; consort विधात्री — supporter; ordainer; consort of brahmā विधात्री means one who supports the universe. since she supports and nourishes the universe, she is vidhātrī. vidhātā means brahmā, and his consort is vidhātrī. the word may also be connected with dhātrī, myrobalan, because she is fond of myrobalans. dhātrī also means mother, who bears the child in her womb and releases it at the proper time. as the great mother, she is vidhātrī. the ordainer of fate: she supports, nourishes and orders the universe. the lines of destiny and the care of beings operate through her sustaining power.","esoteric":["The Ordainer of Fate: She supports, nourishes and orders the universe. The lines of destiny and the care of beings operate through Her sustaining power."]},{"number":338,"name":"वेदजननी","samasa":["• वेदानां जननी।"],"wordByWord":["वेदानाम् — of the Vedas","जननी — mother; origin","वेदजननी — mother of the Vedas"],"summary":["वेदजननी means one who is the mother of the Vedas. Since the Vedas arise from Her and reveal Her, She is their mother. As the origin of sacred knowledge and as the one known through the Vedas, She is called Vedajananī."],"searchText":"338 वेदजननी • वेदानां जननी। वेदानाम् — of the vedas जननी — mother; origin वेदजननी — mother of the vedas वेदजननी means one who is the mother of the vedas. since the vedas arise from her and reveal her, she is their mother. as the origin of sacred knowledge and as the one known through the vedas, she is called vedajananī. the mother of revelation: the vedas are eternal and not authored by human minds. they arise from her naturally, like breath, at the beginning of cosmic manifestation.","esoteric":["The Mother of Revelation: The Vedas are eternal and not authored by human minds. They arise from Her naturally, like breath, at the beginning of cosmic manifestation."]},{"number":339,"name":"विष्णुमाया","samasa":["• विष्णोः माया।"],"wordByWord":["विष्णोः — of Viṣṇu","माया — power of manifestation; divine power","विष्णुमाया — the Māyā of Viṣṇu"],"summary":["विष्णुमाया means one who is the māyā of Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu is the all-pervading principle, and māyā is the power through which names, forms and the universe are projected. Śrīdevī, as the power of Viṣṇu, is called Viṣṇumāyā. This also indicates that the sustaining function of the universe operates through Her power."],"searchText":"339 विष्णुमाया • विष्णोः माया। विष्णोः — of viṣṇu माया — power of manifestation; divine power विष्णुमाया — the māyā of viṣṇu विष्णुमाया means one who is the māyā of viṣṇu. viṣṇu is the all-pervading principle, and māyā is the power through which names, forms and the universe are projected. śrīdevī, as the power of viṣṇu, is called viṣṇumāyā. this also indicates that the sustaining function of the universe operates through her power. the projective power: she is the mysterious power of viṣṇu that projects name and form over consciousness. she makes the non-dual appear as many and also holds the key to removing that illusion.","esoteric":["The Projective Power: She is the mysterious power of Viṣṇu that projects name and form over consciousness. She makes the non-dual appear as many and also holds the key to removing that illusion."]},{"number":340,"name":"विलासिनी","samasa":["• विलासः अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["विलासः — sport; graceful play; shining expression","अस्याः — of her","अस्ति — exists","विलासिनी — she who possesses divine sport or graceful play"],"summary":["विलासिनी means one who is sportive and graceful. Vilāsa denotes play, graceful movement and manifestation. The universe is Her divine play, and Her beauty, actions and manifestations are expressions of that play. She is therefore called Vilāsinī."],"searchText":"340 विलासिनी • विलासः अस्याः अस्तीति। विलासः — sport; graceful play; shining expression अस्याः — of her अस्ति — exists विलासिनी — she who possesses divine sport or graceful play विलासिनी means one who is sportive and graceful. vilāsa denotes play, graceful movement and manifestation. the universe is her divine play, and her beauty, actions and manifestations are expressions of that play. she is therefore called vilāsinī. the universe as play: projection, maintenance and dissolution of worlds are effortless play for her. her cosmic action is graceful vilāsa.","esoteric":["The Universe as Play: Projection, maintenance and dissolution of worlds are effortless play for Her. Her cosmic action is graceful vilāsa."]},{"number":341,"name":"क्षेत्रस्वरूपा","samasa":["• क्षेत्रं स्वं रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["क्षेत्रं — field; body; matter","स्वं रूपं — own form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","क्षेत्रस्वरूपा — she whose own form is the field"],"summary":["क्षेत्रस्वरूपा means one whose body is the field of matter and the bodies of all beings. Kṣetram is a field prepared for cultivation by removing weeds, ploughing and watering. Similarly, a place prepared through mantra, tantra and yantra for attaining divinity is called kṣetra. The thirty-six categories from earth to Śiva form Her body. Therefore Parameśvara is called Kṣetrajña, the knower of the field."],"searchText":"341 क्षेत्रस्वरूपा • क्षेत्रं स्वं रूपं यस्याः सा। क्षेत्रं — field; body; matter स्वं रूपं — own form यस्याः — of whom; whose क्षेत्रस्वरूपा — she whose own form is the field क्षेत्रस्वरूपा means one whose body is the field of matter and the bodies of all beings. kṣetram is a field prepared for cultivation by removing weeds, ploughing and watering. similarly, a place prepared through mantra, tantra and yantra for attaining divinity is called kṣetra. the thirty-six categories from earth to śiva form her body. therefore parameśvara is called kṣetrajña, the knower of the field. the material field: kṣetra is the mutable universe, the physical body and the field of matter. this world is her own visible and tangible form.","esoteric":["The Material Field: Kṣetra is the mutable universe, the physical body and the field of matter. This world is Her own visible and tangible form."]},{"number":342,"name":"क्षेत्रेशी","samasa":["• क्षेत्रस्य यः ईशः तस्य इयम्।"],"wordByWord":["क्षेत्रस्य — of the field; of matter","ईशः — lord; ruler","तस्य इयम् — she who belongs to him; his power or consort","क्षेत्रेशी — ruler of the field; consort of Kṣetreśa"],"summary":["क्षेत्रेशी means one who is the ruler of matter, or the consort of Kṣetreśa, Śiva. There is no difference between Śrīdevī and Parameśvara. Śakti and Bhagavān are one in essence, and therefore She is the ruler of kṣetra."],"searchText":"342 क्षेत्रेशी • क्षेत्रस्य यः ईशः तस्य इयम्। क्षेत्रस्य — of the field; of matter ईशः — lord; ruler तस्य इयम् — she who belongs to him; his power or consort क्षेत्रेशी — ruler of the field; consort of kṣetreśa क्षेत्रेशी means one who is the ruler of matter, or the consort of kṣetreśa, śiva. there is no difference between śrīdevī and parameśvara. śakti and bhagavān are one in essence, and therefore she is the ruler of kṣetra. the owner of the field: she manifests as kṣetra and also rules it as īśvarī. the field operates under her command.","esoteric":["The Owner of the Field: She manifests as kṣetra and also rules it as Īśvarī. The field operates under Her command."]},{"number":343,"name":"क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञपालिनी","samasa":["• क्षेत्रं क्षेत्रज्ञं च पालयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["क्षेत्रं — field; body; matter","क्षेत्रज्ञं — knower of the field","च — and","पालयति — protects","क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञपालिनी — she who protects both matter and the knower of matter"],"summary":["क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञपालिनी means one who protects matter and the knower of matter. Kṣetram is the body, and kṣetrajña is the soul. She protects both. The twenty-four tattvas are kṣetras, and the puruṣa who enjoys them is the kṣetrajña. Śrīdevī alone takes the form of all these kṣetras and kṣetrajñas."],"searchText":"343 क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञपालिनी • क्षेत्रं क्षेत्रज्ञं च पालयतीति। क्षेत्रं — field; body; matter क्षेत्रज्ञं — knower of the field च — and पालयति — protects क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञपालिनी — she who protects both matter and the knower of matter क्षेत्रक्षेत्रज्ञपालिनी means one who protects matter and the knower of matter. kṣetram is the body, and kṣetrajña is the soul. she protects both. the twenty-four tattvas are kṣetras, and the puruṣa who enjoys them is the kṣetrajña. śrīdevī alone takes the form of all these kṣetras and kṣetrajñas. sustaining matter and soul: she sustains the objective field so that experience can occur and protects the knowing soul through its journey in saṃsāra.","esoteric":["Sustaining Matter and Soul: She sustains the objective field so that experience can occur and protects the knowing soul through its journey in saṃsāra."]},{"number":344,"name":"क्षयवृद्धिविनिर्मुक्ता","samasa":["• क्षयवृद्धिभ्यां विनिर्मुक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["क्षय — decay; reduction","वृद्धि — growth; increase","विनिर्मुक्ता — completely free from","क्षयवृद्धिविनिर्मुक्ता — she who is free from growth and decay"],"summary":["क्षयवृद्धिविनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from decay and growth. Growth and decay belong to kṣetra. Though She is related to kṣetra and is its ruler and protector along with kṣetrajña, She is free from growth and decay. Weapons do not cut the soul, fire does not burn it, water does not wet it, and wind does not dry it. She is not bound by actions or their results; Her glory neither increases nor decreases by action."],"searchText":"344 क्षयवृद्धिविनिर्मुक्ता • क्षयवृद्धिभ्यां विनिर्मुक्ता। क्षय — decay; reduction वृद्धि — growth; increase विनिर्मुक्ता — completely free from क्षयवृद्धिविनिर्मुक्ता — she who is free from growth and decay क्षयवृद्धिविनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from decay and growth. growth and decay belong to kṣetra. though she is related to kṣetra and is its ruler and protector along with kṣetrajña, she is free from growth and decay. weapons do not cut the soul, fire does not burn it, water does not wet it, and wind does not dry it. she is not bound by actions or their results; her glory neither increases nor decreases by action. beyond material change: decay and growth belong to material objects and bodies. as eternal changeless consciousness, she remains constant and untouched by all modification.","esoteric":["Beyond Material Change: Decay and growth belong to material objects and bodies. As eternal changeless consciousness, She remains constant and untouched by all modification."]},{"number":345,"name":"क्षेत्रपालसमर्चिता","samasa":["• क्षेत्रं पालयति तेन समयग् अर्चिता।"],"wordByWord":["क्षेत्रं — field; sacred precinct; body","पालः — protector","सम्यक् अर्चिता — well worshipped","क्षेत्रपालसमर्चिता — she who is well worshipped by Kṣetrapāla"],"summary":["क्षेत्रपालसमर्चिता means one who is worshipped by Kṣetrapāla. Kālī was created by Śiva to slay Dārukāsura. After the demon was killed, Her wrath did not subside, and Śiva took the form of a crying infant. She suckled the child, who drank the fire of Her anger with the milk. This child is Kṣetrapāla, an incarnation of Śiva, and he worshipped Śrīdevī. Kṣetrapāla also protects the wealth of those who recite the sahasranāma. Literally, kṣetra is a sacrificial precinct and pāla is its protector; kṣetra can also mean the body, whose protectors are fire, air, sun and others."],"searchText":"345 क्षेत्रपालसमर्चिता • क्षेत्रं पालयति तेन समयग् अर्चिता। क्षेत्रं — field; sacred precinct; body पालः — protector सम्यक् अर्चिता — well worshipped क्षेत्रपालसमर्चिता — she who is well worshipped by kṣetrapāla क्षेत्रपालसमर्चिता means one who is worshipped by kṣetrapāla. kālī was created by śiva to slay dārukāsura. after the demon was killed, her wrath did not subside, and śiva took the form of a crying infant. she suckled the child, who drank the fire of her anger with the milk. this child is kṣetrapāla, an incarnation of śiva, and he worshipped śrīdevī. kṣetrapāla also protects the wealth of those who recite the sahasranāma. literally, kṣetra is a sacrificial precinct and pāla is its protector; kṣetra can also mean the body, whose protectors are fire, air, sun and others. the guardian’s worship: kṣetrapāla guards sacred precincts and boundaries. even this guardian receives his power by worshipping her.","esoteric":["The Guardian’s Worship: Kṣetrapāla guards sacred precincts and boundaries. Even this guardian receives his power by worshipping Her."]},{"number":346,"name":"विजया","samasa":["• विशिष्टः जयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विशिष्टः — special; excellent","जयः — victory","यस्याः — of whom; whose","विजया — she whose victory is special; victorious one"],"summary":["विजया means one who is victorious. The word vijaya means special victory. She is victorious over all obstacles, demons, ignorance and forces opposed to dharma. The name also indicates the victory obtained by devotees through Her grace."],"searchText":"346 विजया • विशिष्टः जयः यस्याः सा। विशिष्टः — special; excellent जयः — victory यस्याः — of whom; whose विजया — she whose victory is special; victorious one विजया means one who is victorious. the word vijaya means special victory. she is victorious over all obstacles, demons, ignorance and forces opposed to dharma. the name also indicates the victory obtained by devotees through her grace. the triumphant power: her victory is not temporary. as the supreme reality, she remains victorious over ignorance, delusion and death, and grants victory to those aligned with her.","esoteric":["The Triumphant Power: Her victory is not temporary. As the supreme reality, She remains victorious over ignorance, delusion and death, and grants victory to those aligned with Her."]},{"number":347,"name":"विमला","samasa":["• विगतः मलः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विगतः — gone; removed","मलः — impurity; blemish","यस्याः — of whom; whose","विमला — she who is free from impurity"],"summary":["विमला means one who is without impurity. The word mala means impurity. Since no impurity belongs to Her, She is Vimalā. She is pure consciousness, untouched by the impurities that bind the soul."],"searchText":"347 विमला • विगतः मलः यस्याः सा। विगतः — gone; removed मलः — impurity; blemish यस्याः — of whom; whose विमला — she who is free from impurity विमला means one who is without impurity. the word mala means impurity. since no impurity belongs to her, she is vimalā. she is pure consciousness, untouched by the impurities that bind the soul. free from the three impurities: she is untouched by āṇavamala, the taint of limitation; māyīyamala, the taint of differentiated perception; and kārmamala, the taint of binding action. she remains pure awareness.","esoteric":["Free from the Three Impurities: She is untouched by āṇavamala, the taint of limitation; māyīyamala, the taint of differentiated perception; and kārmamala, the taint of binding action. She remains pure awareness."]},{"number":348,"name":"वन्द्या","samasa":["• वन्दितुं योग्या।"],"wordByWord":["वन्दितुम् — to be saluted; to be worshipped","योग्या — worthy","वन्द्या — worthy of worship"],"summary":["वन्द्या means one who is worthy of worship. She is to be worshipped by all because She is the origin, support and goal of the universe. Devas, sages and devotees bow to Her."],"searchText":"348 वन्द्या • वन्दितुं योग्या। वन्दितुम् — to be saluted; to be worshipped योग्या — worthy वन्द्या — worthy of worship वन्द्या means one who is worthy of worship. she is to be worshipped by all because she is the origin, support and goal of the universe. devas, sages and devotees bow to her. the object of universal salutation: she is the origin of life and light. bowing to her dissolves pride and turns the mind toward its highest refuge.","esoteric":["The Object of Universal Salutation: She is the origin of life and light. Bowing to Her dissolves pride and turns the mind toward its highest refuge."]},{"number":349,"name":"वन्दारुजनवत्सला","samasa":["• वन्दारून् जनान् वत्सवत् लातीति।"],"wordByWord":["वन्दारून् — those who bow or worship","जनान् — people","वत्सवत् — like calves; with affection","लाति — protects; nourishes","वन्दारुजनवत्सला — she who loves and protects worshipping people like her children"],"summary":["वन्दारुजनवत्सला means one who is affectionate to those who bow to Her. Vatsalā is one who shows a mother’s love toward her child. Śrīdevī shows such tenderness to worshippers and protects those who bow down to Her."],"searchText":"349 वन्दारुजनवत्सला • वन्दारून् जनान् वत्सवत् लातीति। वन्दारून् — those who bow or worship जनान् — people वत्सवत् — like calves; with affection लाति — protects; nourishes वन्दारुजनवत्सला — she who loves and protects worshipping people like her children वन्दारुजनवत्सला means one who is affectionate to those who bow to her. vatsalā is one who shows a mother’s love toward her child. śrīdevī shows such tenderness to worshippers and protects those who bow down to her. maternal tenderness: vatsalā means spontaneous motherly affection. she protects and nourishes devotees who bow to her with humility.","esoteric":["Maternal Tenderness: Vatsalā means spontaneous motherly affection. She protects and nourishes devotees who bow to Her with humility."]},{"number":350,"name":"वाग्वादिनी","samasa":["• वाचं वदतीति।","• वाचं वादयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["वाचम् — speech; word","वदति — speaks","वादयति — causes to speak; makes speech function","वाग्वादिनी — she who speaks, and who causes speech to arise"],"summary":["वाग्वादिनी means one who speaks or causes speech. She is the power behind speech and enables speech to function. As Vāk, She is the origin of words, meaning and expression."],"searchText":"350 वाग्वादिनी • वाचं वदतीति। • वाचं वादयतीति। वाचम् — speech; word वदति — speaks वादयति — causes to speak; makes speech function वाग्वादिनी — she who speaks, and who causes speech to arise वाग्वादिनी means one who speaks or causes speech. she is the power behind speech and enables speech to function. as vāk, she is the origin of words, meaning and expression. the power of articulation: she causes speech and language to manifest. she is the inner voice that turns thought into clear expression.","esoteric":["The Power of Articulation: She causes speech and language to manifest. She is the inner voice that turns thought into clear expression."]},{"number":351,"name":"वामकेशी","samasa":["• वामाः केशाः यस्याः सा।","• वामाः एव वामकाः ये तेषाम् ईशस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["वामाः — beautiful; also left-sided","केशाः — hair","यस्याः — of whom; whose","ईशस्य पत्नी — consort of the Lord","वामकेशी — she with beautiful hair; consort of the Lord of the Vāmaka group"],"summary":["वामकेशी means one who has beautiful hair. The name also has another interpretation connected with Vāmaka and the Lord. In the simple sense, Her hair is beautiful and auspicious."],"searchText":"351 वामकेशी • वामाः केशाः यस्याः सा। • वामाः एव वामकाः ये तेषाम् ईशस्य पत्नी। वामाः — beautiful; also left-sided केशाः — hair यस्याः — of whom; whose ईशस्य पत्नी — consort of the lord वामकेशी — she with beautiful hair; consort of the lord of the vāmaka group वामकेशी means one who has beautiful hair. the name also has another interpretation connected with vāmaka and the lord. in the simple sense, her hair is beautiful and auspicious. the consort of vāmakeśvara: she is connected with vāmakeśvara. her beautiful hair also suggests rays of energy streaming outward into manifestation.","esoteric":["The Consort of Vāmakeśvara: She is connected with Vāmakeśvara. Her beautiful hair also suggests rays of energy streaming outward into manifestation."]},{"number":352,"name":"वह्निमण्डलवासिनी","samasa":["• वह्नेः यत् मण्डलं तत्र वसतीति।"],"wordByWord":["वह्नेः — of fire","मण्डलं — circle; orb","तत्र — there","वसति — dwells","वह्निमण्डलवासिनी — she who dwells in the circle of fire"],"summary":["वह्निमण्डलवासिनी means one who dwells in the circle of fire. Fire is sacred and purifying. She is contemplated as dwelling in the fire-orb, and the worship connected with fire and inner radiance is indicated by this name."],"searchText":"352 वह्निमण्डलवासिनी • वह्नेः यत् मण्डलं तत्र वसतीति। वह्नेः — of fire मण्डलं — circle; orb तत्र — there वसति — dwells वह्निमण्डलवासिनी — she who dwells in the circle of fire वह्निमण्डलवासिनी means one who dwells in the circle of fire. fire is sacred and purifying. she is contemplated as dwelling in the fire-orb, and the worship connected with fire and inner radiance is indicated by this name. the fire centre: vahnimaṇḍala is the circle of sacred fire. she dwells in that purifying fire and burns the devotee’s impurities through inner radiance.","esoteric":["The Fire Centre: Vahnimaṇḍala is the circle of sacred fire. She dwells in that purifying fire and burns the devotee’s impurities through inner radiance."]},{"number":353,"name":"भक्तिमत्कल्पलतिका","samasa":["• भक्तिमतां कल्पलतिका इव।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तिमताम् — of those who possess devotion","कल्पलतिका — wish-fulfilling creeper","इव — like","भक्तिमत्कल्पलतिका — she who is like a wish-fulfilling creeper for devotees"],"summary":["भक्तिमत्कल्पलतिका means one who is like a wish-fulfilling creeper to devotees. Kalpalatikā is a creeper that grants what is desired. She fulfils the true aspirations of devotees. Latikā also suggests a fragrant, mind-soothing creeper, and Śrīdevī is like such a soothing creeper to Her devotees."],"searchText":"353 भक्तिमत्कल्पलतिका • भक्तिमतां कल्पलतिका इव। भक्तिमताम् — of those who possess devotion कल्पलतिका — wish-fulfilling creeper इव — like भक्तिमत्कल्पलतिका — she who is like a wish-fulfilling creeper for devotees भक्तिमत्कल्पलतिका means one who is like a wish-fulfilling creeper to devotees. kalpalatikā is a creeper that grants what is desired. she fulfils the true aspirations of devotees. latikā also suggests a fragrant, mind-soothing creeper, and śrīdevī is like such a soothing creeper to her devotees. the wishing creeper: like a kalpalatā, she fulfils the needs of those with genuine devotion, giving both worldly support and the fruit of liberation.","esoteric":["The Wishing Creeper: Like a kalpalatā, She fulfils the needs of those with genuine devotion, giving both worldly support and the fruit of liberation."]},{"number":354,"name":"पशुपाशविमोचनी","samasa":["• पशोः पाशं विमोचयतीति।","• पशूनां पाशे (पिपासाशनाये) विशिष्य मोचयतीति।","• पशुपस्य आशा येषां ते पशुपाशाः। तान् विशेषण मोचयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["पशोः — of the pashu, the bound soul or ignorant being","पाशं — bondage; fetter","विमोचयति — releases completely","पशूनाम् — of ignorant beings","पिपासा-अशनाये — thirst and hunger","विशिष्य — especially; completely","पशुपाशविमोचनी — she who releases bound souls from their bonds"],"summary":["पशुपाशविमोचनी means one who releases bound beings from bondage. Paśus are those who lack the conviction of non-separation and see the deity as different from themselves. Pāśa can indicate hunger and thirst, and more broadly the afflictions that bind the soul. These include avidyā, asmitā, rāga, dveṣa and abhiniveśa: ignorance, egoism, desire, hatred and clinging attachment. Other bonds such as cruelty, doubt, fear, shame, disgust, race, fame and caste are also included. Śrīdevī releases ignorant beings from all these bonds."],"searchText":"354 पशुपाशविमोचनी • पशोः पाशं विमोचयतीति। • पशूनां पाशे (पिपासाशनाये) विशिष्य मोचयतीति। • पशुपस्य आशा येषां ते पशुपाशाः। तान् विशेषण मोचयतीति। पशोः — of the pashu, the bound soul or ignorant being पाशं — bondage; fetter विमोचयति — releases completely पशूनाम् — of ignorant beings पिपासा-अशनाये — thirst and hunger विशिष्य — especially; completely पशुपाशविमोचनी — she who releases bound souls from their bonds पशुपाशविमोचनी means one who releases bound beings from bondage. paśus are those who lack the conviction of non-separation and see the deity as different from themselves. pāśa can indicate hunger and thirst, and more broadly the afflictions that bind the soul. these include avidyā, asmitā, rāga, dveṣa and abhiniveśa: ignorance, egoism, desire, hatred and clinging attachment. other bonds such as cruelty, doubt, fear, shame, disgust, race, fame and caste are also included. śrīdevī releases ignorant beings from all these bonds. the soul and the tether: paśu is the bound individual soul, and pāśa is the rope of ignorance, ego and karma. as paśupāśavimocanī, she releases the soul from bondage.","esoteric":["The Soul and the Tether: Paśu is the bound individual soul, and pāśa is the rope of ignorance, ego and karma. As Paśupāśavimocanī, She releases the soul from bondage."]},{"number":355,"name":"संहृताशेषपाषण्डा","samasa":["• संहृताः अशेषाः पाषण्डाः यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["संहृताः — destroyed; removed","अशेषाः — without remainder; all","पाषण्डाः — heretics; deniers of sacred dharma","यया — by whom","संहृताशेषपाषण्डा — she by whom all heresy is destroyed"],"summary":["संहृताशेषपाषण्डा means one who destroys all pāṣaṇḍas, those opposed to true spiritual values. Pāṣaṇḍa denotes false or distorted paths that cut people off from righteousness and right understanding. In another form it is written pākhaṇḍa, with the sense of cutting away from true knowledge. Śrīdevī destroys such falsehood and restores right vision."],"searchText":"355 संहृताशेषपाषण्डा • संहृताः अशेषाः पाषण्डाः यया सा। संहृताः — destroyed; removed अशेषाः — without remainder; all पाषण्डाः — heretics; deniers of sacred dharma यया — by whom संहृताशेषपाषण्डा — she by whom all heresy is destroyed संहृताशेषपाषण्डा means one who destroys all pāṣaṇḍas, those opposed to true spiritual values. pāṣaṇḍa denotes false or distorted paths that cut people off from righteousness and right understanding. in another form it is written pākhaṇḍa, with the sense of cutting away from true knowledge. śrīdevī destroys such falsehood and restores right vision. the destruction of delusion: pāṣaṇḍa is distorted understanding that leads beings away from truth. she destroys these false views and replaces blindness with real knowledge.","esoteric":["The Destruction of Delusion: Pāṣaṇḍa is distorted understanding that leads beings away from truth. She destroys these false views and replaces blindness with real knowledge."]},{"number":356,"name":"सदाचारप्रवर्तिका","samasa":["• सदाचारस्य प्रवर्तिका।"],"wordByWord":["सत् — good; noble; auspicious","आचारस्य — of conduct; practice","प्रवर्तिका — promoter; one who sets in motion","सदाचारप्रवर्तिका — she who promotes right conduct"],"summary":["सदाचारप्रवर्तिका means one who inspires right conduct. Because She destroys wickedness, She turns people toward right action. Sat means great or auspicious, and ācāra means conduct; therefore She directs people toward great and auspicious conduct. She gives the inclination to follow righteous discipline, ritual duty and knowledge of Brahman. The dharma taught by Brahmā, Manu, Vyāsa and others remains established until dissolution through Her power."],"searchText":"356 सदाचारप्रवर्तिका • सदाचारस्य प्रवर्तिका। सत् — good; noble; auspicious आचारस्य — of conduct; practice प्रवर्तिका — promoter; one who sets in motion सदाचारप्रवर्तिका — she who promotes right conduct सदाचारप्रवर्तिका means one who inspires right conduct. because she destroys wickedness, she turns people toward right action. sat means great or auspicious, and ācāra means conduct; therefore she directs people toward great and auspicious conduct. she gives the inclination to follow righteous discipline, ritual duty and knowledge of brahman. the dharma taught by brahmā, manu, vyāsa and others remains established until dissolution through her power. the instiller of right conduct: sadācāra is clean ethical and spiritual discipline. she acts as the inner conscience that moves seekers toward purity, duty and higher meditation.","esoteric":["The Instiller of Right Conduct: Sadācāra is clean ethical and spiritual discipline. She acts as the inner conscience that moves seekers toward purity, duty and higher meditation."]},{"number":357,"name":"तापत्रयाग्निसंतप्तसमाह्लादनचन्द्रिका","samasa":["• तापानां त्रयं यस्य तेन अग्निना सम्यक् तप्तानां सम्यग् आह्लादनेन चन्द्रिका इव।"],"wordByWord":["तापत्रय — the three sufferings","अग्नि — fire","संतप्त — scorched; afflicted","समाह्लादन — complete soothing; delighting","चन्द्रिका — moonlight","तापत्रयाग्निसंतप्तसमाह्लादनचन्द्रिका — she who soothes like moonlight those scorched by the fire of the three afflictions"],"summary":["तापत्रयाग्निसंतप्तसमाह्लादनचन्द्रिका means one who soothes, like moonlight, those scorched by the fire of the three distresses. The three sufferings are ādhyātmika, ādhibhautika and ādhidaivika. Ādhyātmika arises from the body, senses, mind, intellect, ego and volition. Ādhibhautika comes from the world and the elements. Ādhidaivika comes from unseen or divine causes beyond human control. These belong to the cycle of life, and Śrīdevī makes the suffering soul happy by removing pain through Her moon-like compassion."],"searchText":"357 तापत्रयाग्निसंतप्तसमाह्लादनचन्द्रिका • तापानां त्रयं यस्य तेन अग्निना सम्यक् तप्तानां सम्यग् आह्लादनेन चन्द्रिका इव। तापत्रय — the three sufferings अग्नि — fire संतप्त — scorched; afflicted समाह्लादन — complete soothing; delighting चन्द्रिका — moonlight तापत्रयाग्निसंतप्तसमाह्लादनचन्द्रिका — she who soothes like moonlight those scorched by the fire of the three afflictions तापत्रयाग्निसंतप्तसमाह्लादनचन्द्रिका means one who soothes, like moonlight, those scorched by the fire of the three distresses. the three sufferings are ādhyātmika, ādhibhautika and ādhidaivika. ādhyātmika arises from the body, senses, mind, intellect, ego and volition. ādhibhautika comes from the world and the elements. ādhidaivika comes from unseen or divine causes beyond human control. these belong to the cycle of life, and śrīdevī makes the suffering soul happy by removing pain through her moon-like compassion. the cooling moonlight: the three fires of suffering burn the mind. her compassion is candrikā, soothing moonlight that cools distress and restores peace.","esoteric":["The Cooling Moonlight: The three fires of suffering burn the mind. Her compassion is candrikā, soothing moonlight that cools distress and restores peace."]},{"number":358,"name":"तरुणी","samasa":["• नित्यतारुणवत्वात् तरुणी।"],"wordByWord":["नित्य — eternal; always","तारुणवत्वात् — because of youthfulness","तरुणी — ever young"],"summary":["तरुणी means one who is ever young. Śrīdevī has no growth or reduction, because She has no beginning or end. If there were a beginning there would be growth, and if there were an end there would be decline; She has neither. She is eternal and present in all three times. Names such as Nityā, Pūrṇā and Nityayauvanā convey the same sense. She is without ageing and is immortal."],"searchText":"358 तरुणी • नित्यतारुणवत्वात् तरुणी। नित्य — eternal; always तारुणवत्वात् — because of youthfulness तरुणी — ever young तरुणी means one who is ever young. śrīdevī has no growth or reduction, because she has no beginning or end. if there were a beginning there would be growth, and if there were an end there would be decline; she has neither. she is eternal and present in all three times. names such as nityā, pūrṇā and nityayauvanā convey the same sense. she is without ageing and is immortal. eternally youthful: she is nityatāruṇyavatī, always fresh and young. unlike material bodies, her consciousness never ages, decays or loses vitality.","esoteric":["Eternally Youthful: She is Nityatāruṇyavatī, always fresh and young. Unlike material bodies, Her consciousness never ages, decays or loses vitality."]},{"number":359,"name":"तापसाराध्या","samasa":["• तापसैः आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["तापसैः — by ascetics; by those practising austerity","आराध्या — worshipped; to be adored","तापसाराध्या — she who is worshipped by ascetics"],"summary":["तापसाराध्या means one who is worshipped by ascetics. Tapa can also mean saṃsāra, the condition of misery; sāra means essence or depth; and dhyā means meditation. Śrīdevī, who is the root cause of saṃsāra, is the essential object of meditation."],"searchText":"359 तापसाराध्या • तापसैः आराध्या। तापसैः — by ascetics; by those practising austerity आराध्या — worshipped; to be adored तापसाराध्या — she who is worshipped by ascetics तापसाराध्या means one who is worshipped by ascetics. tapa can also mean saṃsāra, the condition of misery; sāra means essence or depth; and dhyā means meditation. śrīdevī, who is the root cause of saṃsāra, is the essential object of meditation. the object of deep penance: she is approached through tapas, concentrated discipline that burns away distraction. ascetics worship her as the goal of inward absorption.","esoteric":["The Object of Deep Penance: She is approached through tapas, concentrated discipline that burns away distraction. Ascetics worship Her as the goal of inward absorption."]},{"number":360,"name":"तनुमध्या","samasa":["• तनुः मध्यः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["तनुः — slender; thin","मध्यः — waist; middle","यस्याः — of whom; whose","सा — she","तनुमध्या — she whose waist is slender"],"summary":["तनुमध्या means one who has a slender waist. The beauty and slenderness of Śrīdevī’s middle portion is indicated here. Tanumadhyā is also the deity worshipped in Kāñcī, the consort of Bilveśvara, dwelling on the bank of the river Nīvā. Tanumadhyā is also the name of a metre with six letters in each foot and twenty-four letters in all."],"searchText":"360 तनुमध्या • तनुः मध्यः यस्याः सा। तनुः — slender; thin मध्यः — waist; middle यस्याः — of whom; whose सा — she तनुमध्या — she whose waist is slender तनुमध्या means one who has a slender waist. the beauty and slenderness of śrīdevī’s middle portion is indicated here. tanumadhyā is also the deity worshipped in kāñcī, the consort of bilveśvara, dwelling on the bank of the river nīvā. tanumadhyā is also the name of a metre with six letters in each foot and twenty-four letters in all. the subtle middle: madhya is the middle point, and tanu means slender or subtle. her form indicates the subtle junction between manifestation and the unmanifest.","esoteric":["The Subtle Middle: Madhya is the middle point, and tanu means slender or subtle. Her form indicates the subtle junction between manifestation and the unmanifest."]},{"number":361,"name":"तमोपहा","samasa":["• तमः अपहन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["तमः — darkness; ignorance","अपहन्ति — removes; destroys","तमोपहा — remover of darkness"],"summary":["तमोपहा means one who removes darkness. She removes from devotees the darkness called ignorance. Those who cling to ignorance enter blind darkness; Śrīdevī dispels that darkness and gives knowledge."],"searchText":"361 तमोपहा • तमः अपहन्तीति। तमः — darkness; ignorance अपहन्ति — removes; destroys तमोपहा — remover of darkness तमोपहा means one who removes darkness. she removes from devotees the darkness called ignorance. those who cling to ignorance enter blind darkness; śrīdevī dispels that darkness and gives knowledge. the destruction of ignorance: tamas is darkness and spiritual ignorance. as tamopahā, she shines like the inner sun and removes the veil over the self.","esoteric":["The Destruction of Ignorance: Tamas is darkness and spiritual ignorance. As Tamopahā, She shines like the inner sun and removes the veil over the self."]},{"number":362,"name":"चितिः","samasa":["• चितिः।"],"wordByWord":["चितिः — consciousness; knowledge; awareness"],"summary":["चितिः means one who is in the form of knowledge. Cit is independent and is the cause of the establishment of the universe. Śrīdevī is called Cit because She is the life of those who desire life. As Citi, She is the conscious form that pervades the whole universe."],"searchText":"362 चितिः • चितिः। चितिः — consciousness; knowledge; awareness चितिः means one who is in the form of knowledge. cit is independent and is the cause of the establishment of the universe. śrīdevī is called cit because she is the life of those who desire life. as citi, she is the conscious form that pervades the whole universe. pure awareness: she is consciousness itself, not merely one who possesses consciousness. she is the changeless light that illumines thought, movement and experience.","esoteric":["Pure Awareness: She is consciousness itself, not merely one who possesses consciousness. She is the changeless light that illumines thought, movement and experience."]},{"number":363,"name":"तत्पदलक्ष्यार्था","samasa":["• तत् इति पदेन लक्षणीयः अर्थः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["तत् — that; the word Tat","पदेन — by the word","लक्षणीयः — indicated indirectly; implied","अर्थः — meaning","यस्याः — of whom; whose","तत्पदलक्ष्यार्था — she who is the implied meaning of the word Tat"],"summary":["तत्पदलक्ष्यार्था means one who is the implied meaning of the word tat. In the mahāvākya tat tvam asi, tat indicates Brahman as the cause of creation and other cosmic functions. Its implied meaning is that same Brahman in pure form, free from function. Śrīdevī is the Brahman indicated by that implied meaning."],"searchText":"363 तत्पदलक्ष्यार्था • तत् इति पदेन लक्षणीयः अर्थः यस्याः सा। तत् — that; the word tat पदेन — by the word लक्षणीयः — indicated indirectly; implied अर्थः — meaning यस्याः — of whom; whose तत्पदलक्ष्यार्था — she who is the implied meaning of the word tat तत्पदलक्ष्यार्था means one who is the implied meaning of the word tat. in the mahāvākya tat tvam asi, tat indicates brahman as the cause of creation and other cosmic functions. its implied meaning is that same brahman in pure form, free from function. śrīdevī is the brahman indicated by that implied meaning. the implied meaning of tat: the literal meaning points to īśvara as cosmic cause. the implied meaning is pure non-dual consciousness, and she is that reality.","esoteric":["The Implied Meaning of Tat: The literal meaning points to Īśvara as cosmic cause. The implied meaning is pure non-dual consciousness, and She is that reality."]},{"number":364,"name":"चिदेकरसरूपिणी","samasa":["• चिदेव रसः येषां तानि रूपाणि अस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["चित् — consciousness","एव — alone; indeed","रसः — essence","रूपिणी — she whose form is","चिदेकरसरूपिणी — she whose forms have consciousness alone as their essence"],"summary":["चिदेकरसरूपिणी means one whose form is the single essence of consciousness. Bliss, consciousness and intellect are inseparable from Her. Though She appears in different forms, Her conscious form is full of knowledge, and knowledge itself is the single essence. She is never separated from cit; though attributes make them appear different, they are really one."],"searchText":"364 चिदेकरसरूपिणी • चिदेव रसः येषां तानि रूपाणि अस्याः इति। चित् — consciousness एव — alone; indeed रसः — essence रूपिणी — she whose form is चिदेकरसरूपिणी — she whose forms have consciousness alone as their essence चिदेकरसरूपिणी means one whose form is the single essence of consciousness. bliss, consciousness and intellect are inseparable from her. though she appears in different forms, her conscious form is full of knowledge, and knowledge itself is the single essence. she is never separated from cit; though attributes make them appear different, they are really one. homogeneous reality: her whole manifestation has one underlying essence, pure cit. matter and mind are modifications of that single conscious reality.","esoteric":["Homogeneous Reality: Her whole manifestation has one underlying essence, pure cit. Matter and mind are modifications of that single conscious reality."]},{"number":365,"name":"स्वात्मानन्दलवीभूतब्रह्माद्यानन्दसन्ततिः","samasa":["• स्वस्याः आत्मारूपः यः आनन्दः तस्य लवीभूताः ब्रह्मादीनां सन्ततयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्वस्याः — of her own","आत्मारूपः — in the form of the Self","आनन्दः — bliss","लवीभूताः — become a tiny particle","ब्रह्मादीनाम् — of Brahma and others","सन्ततयः — streams; continuities","स्वात्मानन्दलवीभूतब्रह्माद्यानन्दसन्ततिः — she whose own Self-bliss makes the bliss of Brahma and others only a minute particle"],"summary":["स्वात्मानन्दलवीभूतब्रह्माद्यानन्दसन्ततिः means that the bliss of Brahmā and others is only a minute particle of Her own bliss. The gods who perform creation, protection and destruction, along with Indra and other devas, experience bliss, but it is only a drop beside the bliss of Śrīdevī. Other beings live on a mere part of this bliss. Even the highest graded bliss remains limited; Her bliss is the unlimited bliss of Brahman. Lava means a particle, so all other blisses are tiny particles of Her own Self-bliss."],"searchText":"365 स्वात्मानन्दलवीभूतब्रह्माद्यानन्दसन्ततिः • स्वस्याः आत्मारूपः यः आनन्दः तस्य लवीभूताः ब्रह्मादीनां सन्ततयः यस्याः सा। स्वस्याः — of her own आत्मारूपः — in the form of the self आनन्दः — bliss लवीभूताः — become a tiny particle ब्रह्मादीनाम् — of brahma and others सन्ततयः — streams; continuities स्वात्मानन्दलवीभूतब्रह्माद्यानन्दसन्ततिः — she whose own self-bliss makes the bliss of brahma and others only a minute particle स्वात्मानन्दलवीभूतब्रह्माद्यानन्दसन्ततिः means that the bliss of brahmā and others is only a minute particle of her own bliss. the gods who perform creation, protection and destruction, along with indra and other devas, experience bliss, but it is only a drop beside the bliss of śrīdevī. other beings live on a mere part of this bliss. even the highest graded bliss remains limited; her bliss is the unlimited bliss of brahman. lava means a particle, so all other blisses are tiny particles of her own self-bliss. the ocean and the drop: the bliss of brahmā and other great beings is only a tiny drop. she is the unlimited ocean of self-bliss.","esoteric":["The Ocean and the Drop: The bliss of Brahmā and other great beings is only a tiny drop. She is the unlimited ocean of Self-bliss."]},{"number":366,"name":"परा","samasa":["• परानन्दाभिधे तन्त्रे प्रसिद्धत्वाच्च सा परा।"],"wordByWord":["परा — supreme; transcendent; the highest form of speech","परानन्द — supreme bliss","प्रसिद्धत्वात् — because of being well known"],"summary":["परा means one who is in the form of Parā, the transcendent sound. Speech has four forms: Parā, Paśyantī, Madhyamā and Vaikharī. Physical uttered speech is only the gross form, while subtler sound indicates unconditioned Brahman. In manifestation, bindu, nāda and bīja are stages of sound and creation. In the body, the causal bindu is in the mūlādhāra and is known as Śakti or Kuṇḍalinī. The first motionless sound in the mūlādhāra is Parā speech, from which the later stages arise. Śrīdevī is present in all four grades of speech."],"searchText":"366 परा • परानन्दाभिधे तन्त्रे प्रसिद्धत्वाच्च सा परा। परा — supreme; transcendent; the highest form of speech परानन्द — supreme bliss प्रसिद्धत्वात् — because of being well known परा means one who is in the form of parā, the transcendent sound. speech has four forms: parā, paśyantī, madhyamā and vaikharī. physical uttered speech is only the gross form, while subtler sound indicates unconditioned brahman. in manifestation, bindu, nāda and bīja are stages of sound and creation. in the body, the causal bindu is in the mūlādhāra and is known as śakti or kuṇḍalinī. the first motionless sound in the mūlādhāra is parā speech, from which the later stages arise. śrīdevī is present in all four grades of speech. the unmanifest sound: parā is the highest and most subtle stage of sound. it rests in the mūlādhāra as silent potential before thought or audible speech arises.","esoteric":["The Unmanifest Sound: Parā is the highest and most subtle stage of sound. It rests in the mūlādhāra as silent potential before thought or audible speech arises."]},{"number":367,"name":"प्रत्यक्चितीरूपा","samasa":["• प्रतिकूलम् अञ्चतीति प्रतिची। सा च सा चिती च प्रत्यक्चिती। सा रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रत्यक् — inward; turned toward the Self","चिती — consciousness; knowledge","रूपा — form","प्रत्यक्चितीरूपा — she who is in the form of inner consciousness"],"summary":["प्रत्यक्चितीरूपा means one who is in the form of inner consciousness. The senses naturally move outward. Parā, the great subtle form of sound, is recognized only by the mind turned inward. This inward turning is pratyak. With inward attention, the mind recognizes Parā-knowledge as Brahman without distinction of matter, energy and qualities. Thus Śrīdevī is pratyakciti, the great inward knowledge."],"searchText":"367 प्रत्यक्चितीरूपा • प्रतिकूलम् अञ्चतीति प्रतिची। सा च सा चिती च प्रत्यक्चिती। सा रूपं यस्याः सा। प्रत्यक् — inward; turned toward the self चिती — consciousness; knowledge रूपा — form प्रत्यक्चितीरूपा — she who is in the form of inner consciousness प्रत्यक्चितीरूपा means one who is in the form of inner consciousness. the senses naturally move outward. parā, the great subtle form of sound, is recognized only by the mind turned inward. this inward turning is pratyak. with inward attention, the mind recognizes parā-knowledge as brahman without distinction of matter, energy and qualities. thus śrīdevī is pratyakciti, the great inward knowledge. the inward gaze: pratyak is the reversal of attention from outer objects toward awareness itself. she is the inner consciousness recognized when the mind rests inwardly.","esoteric":["The Inward Gaze: pratyak is the reversal of attention from outer objects toward awareness itself. She is the inner consciousness recognized when the mind rests inwardly."]},{"number":368,"name":"पश्यन्ती","samasa":["• पश्यतीति पश्यन्ती।"],"wordByWord":["पश्यति — sees","पश्यन्ती — she who sees; the second subtle stage of speech"],"summary":["पश्यन्ती means one who is in the form of Paśyantī, speech in the inaudible stage. The second stage of speech after Parā is Paśyantī, and She is that form. Because She sees all and sees all in Herself, She is called Paśyantī. Since She rises above the path of action, She is also called Uttīrṇā."],"searchText":"368 पश्यन्ती • पश्यतीति पश्यन्ती। पश्यति — sees पश्यन्ती — she who sees; the second subtle stage of speech पश्यन्ती means one who is in the form of paśyantī, speech in the inaudible stage. the second stage of speech after parā is paśyantī, and she is that form. because she sees all and sees all in herself, she is called paśyantī. since she rises above the path of action, she is also called uttīrṇā. the visualized thought: paśyantī is sound before audible speech, appearing as luminous inner vision or unified thought. she is the witness of that primal creative vision.","esoteric":["The Visualized Thought: Paśyantī is sound before audible speech, appearing as luminous inner vision or unified thought. She is the witness of that primal creative vision."]},{"number":369,"name":"परदेवता","samasa":["• परा च असौ देवता च।"],"wordByWord":["परा — supreme","देवता — deity; object of worship","परदेवता — the supreme deity"],"summary":["परदेवता means one who is the object of supreme devotion. She is worshipped as the supreme deity and as the ultimate Godhead to be meditated upon."],"searchText":"369 परदेवता • परा च असौ देवता च। परा — supreme देवता — deity; object of worship परदेवता — the supreme deity परदेवता means one who is the object of supreme devotion. she is worshipped as the supreme deity and as the ultimate godhead to be meditated upon. the supreme deity: she is paradevatā, the ultimate object of worship. all devotion reaches completion in her.","esoteric":["The Supreme Deity: She is Paradevatā, the ultimate object of worship. All devotion reaches completion in Her."]},{"number":370,"name":"मध्यमा","samasa":["• मध्ये स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["मध्ये — in the middle","स्थिता — situated","मध्यमा — the middle stage of speech"],"summary":["मध्यमा means one who is in the form of Madhyamā, speech in the middle stage of external expression. This stage is not like Paśyantī, which stops immediately after rising, nor like Vaikharī, where articulation is fully developed. It is the intermediate stage between them and is therefore called Madhyamā."],"searchText":"370 मध्यमा • मध्ये स्थिता। मध्ये — in the middle स्थिता — situated मध्यमा — the middle stage of speech मध्यमा means one who is in the form of madhyamā, speech in the middle stage of external expression. this stage is not like paśyantī, which stops immediately after rising, nor like vaikharī, where articulation is fully developed. it is the intermediate stage between them and is therefore called madhyamā. the mental articulation: madhyamā is the inner middle stage of speech. here unified thought becomes words and concepts, though speech is still internal and silent.","esoteric":["The Mental Articulation: Madhyamā is the inner middle stage of speech. Here unified thought becomes words and concepts, though speech is still internal and silent."]},{"number":371,"name":"वैखरीरूपा","samasa":["• विशेषेण खरः विखरः। तस्य इयम् एव रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विशेषेण — specially; distinctly","खरः — hard; audible sound","वैखरी — uttered speech","रूपा — form","वैखरीरूपा — she who is in the form of articulated speech"],"summary":["वैखरीरूपा means one who is in the form of Vaikharī, audible uttered speech. Vaikharī is the hard and manifest form of letters, issuing as sound through the throat and mouth. Scattered sound, carried by air and made dense through articulation, becomes words. Vaikharī clearly enters the cavity of the ear and is connected with the air that brings sound from the heart through the throat."],"searchText":"371 वैखरीरूपा • विशेषेण खरः विखरः। तस्य इयम् एव रूपं यस्याः सा। विशेषेण — specially; distinctly खरः — hard; audible sound वैखरी — uttered speech रूपा — form वैखरीरूपा — she who is in the form of articulated speech वैखरीरूपा means one who is in the form of vaikharī, audible uttered speech. vaikharī is the hard and manifest form of letters, issuing as sound through the throat and mouth. scattered sound, carried by air and made dense through articulation, becomes words. vaikharī clearly enters the cavity of the ear and is connected with the air that brings sound from the heart through the throat. audible communication: vaikharī is gross sound shaped by throat, tongue, teeth and lips. every spoken word, sentence and mantra is her voice in audible expression.","esoteric":["Audible Communication: Vaikharī is gross sound shaped by throat, tongue, teeth and lips. Every spoken word, sentence and mantra is Her voice in audible expression."]},{"number":372,"name":"भक्तमानसहंसिका","samasa":["• भक्तानां मानसे हंसीव हंसिका।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तानाम् — of devotees","मानसे — in the mind; in the Mānasa lake-like mind","हंसी इव — like a swan","हंसिका — female swan","भक्तमानसहंसिका — she who is like a swan in the minds of devotees"],"summary":["भक्तमानसहंसिका means one who is the swan in the lake-like minds of devotees. The pure minds of devotees are like the sacred Mānasa lake where swans dwell, and Śrīdevī is the swan dwelling there. She is visible inwardly to devotees, while remaining unseen by those without devotion."],"searchText":"372 भक्तमानसहंसिका • भक्तानां मानसे हंसीव हंसिका। भक्तानाम् — of devotees मानसे — in the mind; in the mānasa lake-like mind हंसी इव — like a swan हंसिका — female swan भक्तमानसहंसिका — she who is like a swan in the minds of devotees भक्तमानसहंसिका means one who is the swan in the lake-like minds of devotees. the pure minds of devotees are like the sacred mānasa lake where swans dwell, and śrīdevī is the swan dwelling there. she is visible inwardly to devotees, while remaining unseen by those without devotion. sporting in the heart: a swan moves in clear water, and she dwells in the clear lake of the devotee’s mind. when the mind is serene, her presence plays there as haṃsa, the breath of life.","esoteric":["Sporting in the Heart: A swan moves in clear water, and She dwells in the clear lake of the devotee’s mind. When the mind is serene, Her presence plays there as haṃsa, the breath of life."]},{"number":373,"name":"कामेश्वरप्राणनाडी","samasa":["• कामेश्वरस्य प्राणनाडीव।"],"wordByWord":["कामेश्वरस्य — of Kāmeśvara","प्राणनाडी — life-current; vital nerve","इव — like","कामेश्वरप्राणनाडी — she who is like the life-current of Kāmeśvara"],"summary":["कामेश्वरप्राणनाडी means one who is the life-current of Kāmeśvara. Prāṇa is the life principle, and a nāḍī carries that vital force. Śrīdevī is so inseparably connected with Kāmeśvara that She is described as His very prāṇanāḍī."],"searchText":"373 कामेश्वरप्राणनाडी • कामेश्वरस्य प्राणनाडीव। कामेश्वरस्य — of kāmeśvara प्राणनाडी — life-current; vital nerve इव — like कामेश्वरप्राणनाडी — she who is like the life-current of kāmeśvara कामेश्वरप्राणनाडी means one who is the life-current of kāmeśvara. prāṇa is the life principle, and a nāḍī carries that vital force. śrīdevī is so inseparably connected with kāmeśvara that she is described as his very prāṇanāḍī. the vital breath of śiva: kāmeśvara is foundational consciousness, and she is the prāṇanāḍī that animates him. they are inseparable like fire and heat.","esoteric":["The Vital Breath of Śiva: Kāmeśvara is foundational consciousness, and She is the prāṇanāḍī that animates Him. They are inseparable like fire and heat."]},{"number":374,"name":"कृतज्ञा","samasa":["• कृते जानातीति।"],"wordByWord":["कृते — what has been done; action performed","जानाति — knows","कृतज्ञा — she who knows what has been done; grateful one"],"summary":["कृतज्ञा means one who knows what has been done. She knows even the smallest service or worship performed by devotees. She is grateful in the highest sense and never ignores devotion shown to Her."],"searchText":"374 कृतज्ञा • कृते जानातीति। कृते — what has been done; action performed जानाति — knows कृतज्ञा — she who knows what has been done; grateful one कृतज्ञा means one who knows what has been done. she knows even the smallest service or worship performed by devotees. she is grateful in the highest sense and never ignores devotion shown to her. remembering small devotions: she remembers even the smallest hidden act of devotion, surrender or worship. every step toward her is received and returned with grace.","esoteric":["Remembering Small Devotions: She remembers even the smallest hidden act of devotion, surrender or worship. Every step toward Her is received and returned with grace."]},{"number":375,"name":"कामपूजिता","samasa":["• कामेन पूजिता।"],"wordByWord":["कामेन — by Kāma; by desire; by Kāmeśvara","पूजिता — worshipped","कामपूजिता — she who is worshipped by Kāma"],"summary":["कामपूजिता means one who is worshipped by Kāma. Kāma may indicate the deity of desire or Kāmeśvara. She is worshipped by him and is also the supreme object sought by desire when desire becomes purified."],"searchText":"375 कामपूजिता • कामेन पूजिता। कामेन — by kāma; by desire; by kāmeśvara पूजिता — worshipped कामपूजिता — she who is worshipped by kāma कामपूजिता means one who is worshipped by kāma. kāma may indicate the deity of desire or kāmeśvara. she is worshipped by him and is also the supreme object sought by desire when desire becomes purified. purified desire: kāma worships her, and desire becomes sacred when turned toward her. the creative drive is purified and directed toward union with the divine.","esoteric":["Purified Desire: Kāma worships Her, and desire becomes sacred when turned toward Her. The creative drive is purified and directed toward union with the divine."]},{"number":376,"name":"शृङ्गाररससम्पूर्णा","samasa":["• शृङ्गाराख्यरसेन सम्यक् पूर्णा।","• शृङ्गम् अररं यस्याः सा शृङ्गाररा। सा एव सम्पूर्णेन ब्रह्मणा सह ससम्पूर्णा च।"],"wordByWord":["शृङ्गाररस — the rasa of love and beauty","सम्पूर्णा — completely full","ब्रह्मणा सह — together with Brahman","शृङ्गाररससम्पूर्णा — she who is full of the rasa of love and beauty"],"summary":["शृङ्गाररससम्पूर्णा means one who is filled with the rasa of love and beauty. Śṛṅgāra is the rasa of love, and Śrīdevī is complete in this rasa. The name also allows a deeper understanding in which Her completeness is linked with Brahman."],"searchText":"376 शृङ्गाररससम्पूर्णा • शृङ्गाराख्यरसेन सम्यक् पूर्णा। • शृङ्गम् अररं यस्याः सा शृङ्गाररा। सा एव सम्पूर्णेन ब्रह्मणा सह ससम्पूर्णा च। शृङ्गाररस — the rasa of love and beauty सम्पूर्णा — completely full ब्रह्मणा सह — together with brahman शृङ्गाररससम्पूर्णा — she who is full of the rasa of love and beauty शृङ्गाररससम्पूर्णा means one who is filled with the rasa of love and beauty. śṛṅgāra is the rasa of love, and śrīdevī is complete in this rasa. the name also allows a deeper understanding in which her completeness is linked with brahman. the sentiment of union: śṛṅgāra is the rasa of love and attraction. in its highest sense, it is the love between the individual soul and the universal self, or between śiva and śakti.","esoteric":["The Sentiment of Union: Śṛṅgāra is the rasa of love and attraction. In its highest sense, it is the love between the individual soul and the universal self, or between Śiva and Śakti."]},{"number":377,"name":"जया","samasa":["• जयस्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["जय — victory","स्वरूपा — whose nature is","जया — victory itself"],"summary":["जया means one who is victory itself. She is the victorious power, and through Her grace the devotee gains victory over inner and outer obstacles."],"searchText":"377 जया • जयस्वरूपा। जय — victory स्वरूपा — whose nature is जया — victory itself जया means one who is victory itself. she is the victorious power, and through her grace the devotee gains victory over inner and outer obstacles. the energy of success: she is victory itself. through her power, righteousness triumphs over unrighteousness and devotees overcome obstacles.","esoteric":["The Energy of Success: She is victory itself. Through Her power, righteousness triumphs over unrighteousness and devotees overcome obstacles."]},{"number":378,"name":"जालन्धरस्थिता","samasa":["• जालन्धरे स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["जालन्धरे — in Jālandhara","स्थिता — situated","जालन्धरस्थिता — she who abides in Jālandhara"],"summary":["जालन्धरस्थिता means one who is situated in Jālandhara. Jālandhara is one of the sacred seats connected with worship. She is present there and is worshipped in that pīṭha."],"searchText":"378 जालन्धरस्थिता • जालन्धरे स्थिता। जालन्धरे — in jālandhara स्थिता — situated जालन्धरस्थिता — she who abides in jālandhara जालन्धरस्थिता means one who is situated in jālandhara. jālandhara is one of the sacred seats connected with worship. she is present there and is worshipped in that pīṭha. the jālandhara seat: she is present in the sacred jālandhara pīṭha. internally, jālandhara also recalls the throat lock that contains and redirects upward-moving vital force.","esoteric":["The Jālandhara Seat: She is present in the sacred Jālandhara pīṭha. Internally, Jālandhara also recalls the throat lock that contains and redirects upward-moving vital force."]},{"number":379,"name":"ओड्याणपीठनिलया","samasa":["• ओड्याणाख्यं पीठम् एव निलयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["ओड्याणाख्यम् — called Oḍyāṇa","पीठम् — sacred seat","निलयः — abode","यस्याः — of whom; whose","ओड्याणपीठनिलया — she whose abode is the Oḍyāṇa pīṭha"],"summary":["ओड्याणपीठनिलया means one whose abode is the Oḍyāṇa pīṭha. Oḍyāṇa is an important pīṭha of Śrīdevī worship. She is contemplated as dwelling there."],"searchText":"379 ओड्याणपीठनिलया • ओड्याणाख्यं पीठम् एव निलयः यस्याः सा। ओड्याणाख्यम् — called oḍyāṇa पीठम् — sacred seat निलयः — abode यस्याः — of whom; whose ओड्याणपीठनिलया — she whose abode is the oḍyāṇa pīṭha ओड्याणपीठनिलया means one whose abode is the oḍyāṇa pīṭha. oḍyāṇa is an important pīṭha of śrīdevī worship. she is contemplated as dwelling there. the oḍyāṇa seat: she dwells in oḍyāṇa pīṭha. in inner worship it is contemplated as a central sacred seat from which her creative power radiates.","esoteric":["The Oḍyāṇa Seat: She dwells in Oḍyāṇa pīṭha. In inner worship it is contemplated as a central sacred seat from which Her creative power radiates."]},{"number":380,"name":"बिन्दुमण्डलवासिनी","samasa":["• बिन्दुः एव मण्डलं तस्मिन् वसतीति।"],"wordByWord":["बिन्दुः — bindu; point","मण्डलं — circle; field","तस्मिन् — in that","वसति — dwells","बिन्दुमण्डलवासिनी — she who dwells in the bindu-maṇḍala"],"summary":["बिन्दुमण्डलवासिनी means one who dwells in the bindu-maṇḍala. It is the central and most subtle point in the Śrīcakra. Śrīdevī is contemplated as dwelling in that supreme centre."],"searchText":"380 बिन्दुमण्डलवासिनी • बिन्दुः एव मण्डलं तस्मिन् वसतीति। बिन्दुः — bindu; point मण्डलं — circle; field तस्मिन् — in that वसति — dwells बिन्दुमण्डलवासिनी — she who dwells in the bindu-maṇḍala बिन्दुमण्डलवासिनी means one who dwells in the bindu-maṇḍala. it is the central and most subtle point in the śrīcakra. śrīdevī is contemplated as dwelling in that supreme centre. the centre point: the central point is the subtle central point of śrīcakra. she resides there as the condensed union of śiva and śakti before manifestation expands.","esoteric":["The Centre Point: The central point is the subtle central point of Śrīcakra. She resides there as the condensed union of Śiva and Śakti before manifestation expands."]},{"number":381,"name":"रहोयागक्रमाराध्या","samasa":["• रहसि यागः तस्य तत्र वा क्रमेण आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["रहसि — in secret","यागः — worship; sacrifice","क्रमेण — according to prescribed order","आराध्या — to be worshipped","रहोयागक्रमाराध्या — she who is worshipped by the secret ritual order"],"summary":["रहोयागक्रमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by the procedure of secret worship. Rahoyāga is worship performed in secrecy according to the prescribed order. It is an inner form of worship directed to Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"381 रहोयागक्रमाराध्या • रहसि यागः तस्य तत्र वा क्रमेण आराध्या। रहसि — in secret यागः — worship; sacrifice क्रमेण — according to prescribed order आराध्या — to be worshipped रहोयागक्रमाराध्या — she who is worshipped by the secret ritual order रहोयागक्रमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by the procedure of secret worship. rahoyāga is worship performed in secrecy according to the prescribed order. it is an inner form of worship directed to śrīdevī. internal sacrifice: rahoyāga is inward worship. the practitioner offers ego, thoughts and sense-functions into the fire of pure consciousness.","esoteric":["Internal Sacrifice: Rahoyāga is inward worship. The practitioner offers ego, thoughts and sense-functions into the fire of pure consciousness."]},{"number":382,"name":"रहस्तर्पणतर्पिता","samasa":["• रहसि (कृतेन) तर्पणेन तर्पिता।"],"wordByWord":["रहसि — secretly","तर्पणेन — by offering of satisfaction; libation","तर्पिता — satisfied","रहस्तर्पणतर्पिता — she who is pleased by secret tarpaṇa"],"summary":["रहस्तर्पणतर्पिता means one who is satisfied by secret tarpaṇa. She is pleased by offerings made in the inner and secret mode of worship."],"searchText":"382 रहस्तर्पणतर्पिता • रहसि (कृतेन) तर्पणेन तर्पिता। रहसि — secretly तर्पणेन — by offering of satisfaction; libation तर्पिता — satisfied रहस्तर्पणतर्पिता — she who is pleased by secret tarpaṇa रहस्तर्पणतर्पिता means one who is satisfied by secret tarpaṇa. she is pleased by offerings made in the inner and secret mode of worship. the inner libation: rahastarpaṇa is secret inward offering. the bliss and nectar of inner absorption are offered back to her.","esoteric":["The Inner Libation: Rahastarpaṇa is secret inward offering. The bliss and nectar of inner absorption are offered back to Her."]},{"number":383,"name":"सद्यःप्रसादिनी","samasa":["• सद्यः एव प्रसीदतीति।"],"wordByWord":["सद्यः — immediately","प्रसीदति — becomes gracious; is pleased","सद्यःप्रसादिनी — she who grants grace immediately"],"summary":["सद्यःप्रसादिनी means one who is pleased immediately. Śrīdevī responds quickly to sincere worship and devotion. Her grace is immediate when She is approached with proper devotion."],"searchText":"383 सद्यःप्रसादिनी • सद्यः एव प्रसीदतीति। सद्यः — immediately प्रसीदति — becomes gracious; is pleased सद्यःप्रसादिनी — she who grants grace immediately सद्यःप्रसादिनी means one who is pleased immediately. śrīdevī responds quickly to sincere worship and devotion. her grace is immediate when she is approached with proper devotion. immediate grace: she responds at once to sincere devotion and surrender. her grace quickly clears obstruction and illumines the heart.","esoteric":["Immediate Grace: She responds at once to sincere devotion and surrender. Her grace quickly clears obstruction and illumines the heart."]},{"number":384,"name":"विश्वसाक्षिणी","samasa":["• विश्वस्य साक्षिणी।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वस्य — of the universe","साक्षिणी — witness","विश्वसाक्षिणी — witness of the universe"],"summary":["विश्वसाक्षिणी means one who is the witness of the universe. She is the witness-consciousness before which the whole universe appears and functions."],"searchText":"384 विश्वसाक्षिणी • विश्वस्य साक्षिणी। विश्वस्य — of the universe साक्षिणी — witness विश्वसाक्षिणी — witness of the universe विश्वसाक्षिणी means one who is the witness of the universe. she is the witness-consciousness before which the whole universe appears and functions. the cosmic witness: the universe moves through creation, maintenance and dissolution before her. she remains the constant witness and the light that makes perception possible.","esoteric":["The Cosmic Witness: The universe moves through creation, maintenance and dissolution before Her. She remains the constant witness and the light that makes perception possible."]},{"number":385,"name":"साक्षिवर्जिता","samasa":["• साक्षिणः वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["साक्षिणः — witness","वर्जिता — devoid of; beyond","साक्षिवर्जिता — beyond any witness"],"summary":["साक्षिवर्जिता means one who has no witness beyond Herself. She is the witness of all, but there is no other witness to Her. Since She is the ultimate consciousness, She is beyond being witnessed by another."],"searchText":"385 साक्षिवर्जिता • साक्षिणः वर्जिता। साक्षिणः — witness वर्जिता — devoid of; beyond साक्षिवर्जिता — beyond any witness साक्षिवर्जिता means one who has no witness beyond herself. she is the witness of all, but there is no other witness to her. since she is the ultimate consciousness, she is beyond being witnessed by another. the absolute subject: she witnesses everything, yet none stands beyond her to witness her. she is the final consciousness that can never become an object.","esoteric":["The Absolute Subject: She witnesses everything, yet none stands beyond Her to witness Her. She is the final consciousness that can never become an object."]},{"number":386,"name":"षडङ्गदेवतायुक्ता","samasa":["• षण्णाम् अङ्गानां देवताभिः युक्ता।","• षण्णाम् अङ्गानां देवता। तेन युक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["षण्णाम् — of six","अङ्गानाम् — limbs; auxiliaries","देवताभिः — with deities","युक्ता — joined; endowed","षडङ्गदेवतायुक्ता — she who is united with the deities of the six limbs"],"summary":["षडङ्गदेवतायुक्ता means one who is accompanied by the deities of the six limbs. The six limbs connected with mantra and worship have their presiding deities. She is united with those deities and is worshipped together with them."],"searchText":"386 षडङ्गदेवतायुक्ता • षण्णाम् अङ्गानां देवताभिः युक्ता। • षण्णाम् अङ्गानां देवता। तेन युक्ता। षण्णाम् — of six अङ्गानाम् — limbs; auxiliaries देवताभिः — with deities युक्ता — joined; endowed षडङ्गदेवतायुक्ता — she who is united with the deities of the six limbs षडङ्गदेवतायुक्ता means one who is accompanied by the deities of the six limbs. the six limbs connected with mantra and worship have their presiding deities. she is united with those deities and is worshipped together with them. the six limbs: the mantra limbs are hṛdaya, śiras, śikhā, kavaca, netra and astra. she is accompanied by the deities presiding over these six limbs.","esoteric":["The Six Limbs: The mantra limbs are hṛdaya, śiras, śikhā, kavaca, netra and astra. She is accompanied by the deities presiding over these six limbs."]},{"number":387,"name":"षाड्गुण्यपरिपूरिता","samasa":["• षण्णां गुणानां समूहः तेन परितः पूरिता।"],"wordByWord":["षण्णाम् — of six","गुणानाम् — qualities","समूहः — aggregate","परिपूरिता — completely filled","षाड्गुण्यपरिपूरिता — she who is fully endowed with the six qualities"],"summary":["षाड्गुण्यपरिपूरिता means one who is filled with the six divine qualities. The six qualities are complete lordly excellences. Śrīdevī is fully endowed with them."],"searchText":"387 षाड्गुण्यपरिपूरिता • षण्णां गुणानां समूहः तेन परितः पूरिता। षण्णाम् — of six गुणानाम् — qualities समूहः — aggregate परिपूरिता — completely filled षाड्गुण्यपरिपूरिता — she who is fully endowed with the six qualities षाड्गुण्यपरिपूरिता means one who is filled with the six divine qualities. the six qualities are complete lordly excellences. śrīdevī is fully endowed with them. the six virtues: she is filled with aiśvarya, vīrya, yaśas, śrī, jñāna and vairāgya: sovereignty, power, fame, prosperity, knowledge and dispassion.","esoteric":["The Six Virtues: She is filled with aiśvarya, vīrya, yaśas, śrī, jñāna and vairāgya: sovereignty, power, fame, prosperity, knowledge and dispassion."]},{"number":388,"name":"नित्यक्लिन्ना","samasa":["• नित्यं क्लिन्ना।"],"wordByWord":["नित्यम् — always","क्लिन्ना — moist; melted; softened with compassion","नित्यक्लिन्ना — ever softened; ever compassionate"],"summary":["नित्यक्लिन्ना means one who is always softened or melted. The name indicates constant compassion and tenderness toward devotees. It is also connected with the nityā called Nityaklinnā in Śrīvidyā worship."],"searchText":"388 नित्यक्लिन्ना • नित्यं क्लिन्ना। नित्यम् — always क्लिन्ना — moist; melted; softened with compassion नित्यक्लिन्ना — ever softened; ever compassionate नित्यक्लिन्ना means one who is always softened or melted. the name indicates constant compassion and tenderness toward devotees. it is also connected with the nityā called nityaklinnā in śrīvidyā worship. perpetual compassion: her heart never dries into indifference. she is always softened with mercy and tenderness for devotees.","esoteric":["Perpetual Compassion: Her heart never dries into indifference. She is always softened with mercy and tenderness for devotees."]},{"number":389,"name":"निरुपमा","samasa":["• निर्गता उपमा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गता — gone; absent","उपमा — comparison; equal","यस्याः — of whom; whose","निरुपमा — she who has no comparison"],"summary":["निरुपमा means one who is incomparable. There is no object or being equal to Her, and no comparison can adequately describe Her."],"searchText":"389 निरुपमा • निर्गता उपमा यस्याः सा। निर्गता — gone; absent उपमा — comparison; equal यस्याः — of whom; whose निरुपमा — she who has no comparison निरुपमा means one who is incomparable. there is no object or being equal to her, and no comparison can adequately describe her. beyond comparison: comparison requires another equal object. since she is unique and non-dual, nothing can stand beside her as an equal or analogy.","esoteric":["Beyond Comparison: Comparison requires another equal object. Since She is unique and non-dual, nothing can stand beside Her as an equal or analogy."]},{"number":390,"name":"निर्वाणसुखदायिनी","samasa":["• निर्वाणस्य सुखं ददातीति।","• निर्गतं बाणं यस्मिन् सुखे तत् सुखं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["निर्वाणस्य — of liberation","सुखम् — happiness; bliss","ददाति — gives","निर्वाणसुखदायिनी — giver of the happiness of liberation"],"summary":["निर्वाणसुखदायिनी means one who grants the bliss of nirvāṇa. Nirvāṇa is liberation, the state beyond bondage, and Śrīdevī grants that supreme happiness to the devotee. The name can also be understood as nir-bāṇa, freedom from the arrow of desire or suffering, and She grants that freedom."],"searchText":"390 निर्वाणसुखदायिनी • निर्वाणस्य सुखं ददातीति। • निर्गतं बाणं यस्मिन् सुखे तत् सुखं ददातीति। निर्वाणस्य — of liberation सुखम् — happiness; bliss ददाति — gives निर्वाणसुखदायिनी — giver of the happiness of liberation निर्वाणसुखदायिनी means one who grants the bliss of nirvāṇa. nirvāṇa is liberation, the state beyond bondage, and śrīdevī grants that supreme happiness to the devotee. the name can also be understood as nir-bāṇa, freedom from the arrow of desire or suffering, and she grants that freedom. the bliss of liberation: worldly happiness is brief, but nirvāṇasukha is lasting freedom from bondage. she grants that final spiritual happiness.","esoteric":["The Bliss of Liberation: Worldly happiness is brief, but nirvāṇasukha is lasting freedom from bondage. She grants that final spiritual happiness."]},{"number":391,"name":"नित्याषोडशिकारूपा","samasa":["• नित्याश्च ताः षोडशिकाश्च तासां रूपाणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["नित्याः — eternal deities; nityās","षोडशिकाः — the sixteen forms","रूपाणि — forms","यस्याः — of whom; whose","नित्याषोडशिकारूपा — she whose forms are the sixteen nityās"],"summary":["नित्याषोडशिकारूपा means one who is in the form of the sixteen nityās. The sixteen nityā deities are forms of Śrīdevī. She is their collective and essential form."],"searchText":"391 नित्याषोडशिकारूपा • नित्याश्च ताः षोडशिकाश्च तासां रूपाणि यस्याः सा। नित्याः — eternal deities; nityās षोडशिकाः — the sixteen forms रूपाणि — forms यस्याः — of whom; whose नित्याषोडशिकारूपा — she whose forms are the sixteen nityās नित्याषोडशिकारूपा means one who is in the form of the sixteen nityās. the sixteen nityā deities are forms of śrīdevī. she is their collective and essential form. the sixteen nityās: the sixteen nityās are rays of śrīdevī connected with lunar time. she is their collective form and embodies all sixteen phases.","esoteric":["The Sixteen Nityās: The sixteen nityās are rays of Śrīdevī connected with lunar time. She is their collective form and embodies all sixteen phases."]},{"number":392,"name":"श्रीकण्ठार्धशरीरिणी","samasa":["• श्रीः कण्ठे यस्य सः श्रीकण्ठः। तस्य अर्धं शरीरम् अस्याः अस्तीति।","• श्रीकण्ठेन अर्धशरीरम् अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["श्रीकण्ठः — Śiva, the auspicious-throated one","अर्धम् — half","शरीरम् — body","अस्याः — of her","श्रीकण्ठार्धशरीरिणी — she who shares half the body of Śrīkaṇṭha"],"summary":["श्रीकण्ठार्धशरीरिणी means one who has half the body of Śrīkaṇṭha. Śrīkaṇṭha is Śiva. Śrīdevī shares His body and is inseparable from Him. The name expresses the Ardhanārīśvara principle, the unity of Śiva and Śakti."],"searchText":"392 श्रीकण्ठार्धशरीरिणी • श्रीः कण्ठे यस्य सः श्रीकण्ठः। तस्य अर्धं शरीरम् अस्याः अस्तीति। • श्रीकण्ठेन अर्धशरीरम् अस्याः अस्तीति। श्रीकण्ठः — śiva, the auspicious-throated one अर्धम् — half शरीरम् — body अस्याः — of her श्रीकण्ठार्धशरीरिणी — she who shares half the body of śrīkaṇṭha श्रीकण्ठार्धशरीरिणी means one who has half the body of śrīkaṇṭha. śrīkaṇṭha is śiva. śrīdevī shares his body and is inseparable from him. the name expresses the ardhanārīśvara principle, the unity of śiva and śakti. the fusion of being: she is the left half of śiva’s form. consciousness and dynamic energy are not separate; they are united in one body.","esoteric":["The Fusion of Being: She is the left half of Śiva’s form. Consciousness and dynamic energy are not separate; they are united in one body."]},{"number":393,"name":"प्रभावती","samasa":["• प्रभा अस्या अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["प्रभा — light; radiance","अस्ति — exists","प्रभावती — she who possesses radiance"],"summary":["प्रभावती means one who is radiant. Prabhā is light and splendour. Śrīdevī possesses supreme radiance."],"searchText":"393 प्रभावती • प्रभा अस्या अस्तीति। प्रभा — light; radiance अस्ति — exists प्रभावती — she who possesses radiance प्रभावती means one who is radiant. prabhā is light and splendour. śrīdevī possesses supreme radiance. the owner of splendour: she possesses radiance. whatever shines, whether object, star or intellect, shines by a fraction of her prabhā.","esoteric":["The Owner of Splendour: She possesses radiance. Whatever shines, whether object, star or intellect, shines by a fraction of Her prabhā."]},{"number":394,"name":"प्रभारूपा","samasa":["• प्रभा एव रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रभा — radiance","एव — itself","रूपम् — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","प्रभारूपा — she whose form is radiance"],"summary":["प्रभारूपा means one whose form is radiance. She is not merely radiant; radiance itself is Her form."],"searchText":"394 प्रभारूपा • प्रभा एव रूपं यस्याः सा। प्रभा — radiance एव — itself रूपम् — form यस्याः — of whom; whose प्रभारूपा — she whose form is radiance प्रभारूपा means one whose form is radiance. she is not merely radiant; radiance itself is her form. identity with light: she does not merely possess light as an attribute. her essential form is pure luminous radiance.","esoteric":["Identity with Light: She does not merely possess light as an attribute. Her essential form is pure luminous radiance."]},{"number":395,"name":"प्रसिद्धा","samasa":["• (सर्वैः अहम् इति वेद्यत्वात्) प्रसिद्धा।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वैः — by all","अहम् इति — as “I”","वेद्यत्वात् — because of being known","प्रसिद्धा — well known; evident"],"summary":["प्रसिद्धा means one who is well known. She is known by all as the inner “I”. Because the awareness “I am” is common to all experience, She is famous and evident as the Self."],"searchText":"395 प्रसिद्धा • (सर्वैः अहम् इति वेद्यत्वात्) प्रसिद्धा। सर्वैः — by all अहम् इति — as “i” वेद्यत्वात् — because of being known प्रसिद्धा — well known; evident प्रसिद्धा means one who is well known. she is known by all as the inner “i”. because the awareness “i am” is common to all experience, she is famous and evident as the self. the most immediate intimacy: she is known as the self-evident feeling “i am.” no external proof is needed for this inner presence.","esoteric":["The Most Immediate Intimacy: She is known as the self-evident feeling “I am.” No external proof is needed for this inner presence."]},{"number":396,"name":"परमेश्वरी","samasa":["• परमा च सा ईश्वरी च।"],"wordByWord":["परमा — supreme","ईश्वरी — ruler; goddess","परमेश्वरी — supreme ruler"],"summary":["परमेश्वरी means one who is the supreme ruler. She is the highest Īśvarī, the supreme sovereign power beyond all other rulers."],"searchText":"396 परमेश्वरी • परमा च सा ईश्वरी च। परमा — supreme ईश्वरी — ruler; goddess परमेश्वरी — supreme ruler परमेश्वरी means one who is the supreme ruler. she is the highest īśvarī, the supreme sovereign power beyond all other rulers. the ultimate sovereign: she is the supreme ruler over all causes, worlds and spiritual paths. her sovereignty is complete independence, svātantrya.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Sovereign: She is the supreme ruler over all causes, worlds and spiritual paths. Her sovereignty is complete independence, svātantrya."]},{"number":397,"name":"मूलप्रकृतिः","samasa":["• मूला प्रकृतिः।","• मूलस्य प्रकृतिः।"],"wordByWord":["मूला — root; original","प्रकृतिः — primordial nature","मूलप्रकृतिः — the root primordial nature"],"summary":["मूलप्रकृतिः means one who is the original Prakṛti. She is the root nature from which manifestation proceeds. As Mūlaprakṛti, She is the origin of all names and forms."],"searchText":"397 मूलप्रकृतिः • मूला प्रकृतिः। • मूलस्य प्रकृतिः। मूला — root; original प्रकृतिः — primordial nature मूलप्रकृतिः — the root primordial nature मूलप्रकृतिः means one who is the original prakṛti. she is the root nature from which manifestation proceeds. as mūlaprakṛti, she is the origin of all names and forms. the primordial womb: mūlaprakṛti is the unmanifest equilibrium of sattva, rajas and tamas. she is the root material and kinetic cause of manifestation.","esoteric":["The Primordial Womb: Mūlaprakṛti is the unmanifest equilibrium of sattva, rajas and tamas. She is the root material and kinetic cause of manifestation."]},{"number":398,"name":"अव्यक्ता","samasa":["• न व्यक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["न — not","व्यक्ता — manifest","अव्यक्ता — unmanifest"],"summary":["अव्यक्ता means one who is unmanifest. Before manifestation, She remains beyond perception and description. She is the unmanifest origin."],"searchText":"398 अव्यक्ता • न व्यक्ता। न — not व्यक्ता — manifest अव्यक्ता — unmanifest अव्यक्ता means one who is unmanifest. before manifestation, she remains beyond perception and description. she is the unmanifest origin. beyond sensory perception: in her unmanifest state, she is not grasped by the senses or ordinary mind. she remains hidden before names and forms appear.","esoteric":["Beyond Sensory Perception: In Her unmanifest state, She is not grasped by the senses or ordinary mind. She remains hidden before names and forms appear."]},{"number":399,"name":"व्यक्ताऽव्यक्तस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• व्यक्तं च अव्यक्तं स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["व्यक्तम् — manifest","अव्यक्तम् — unmanifest","स्वरूपम् — essential form","अस्याः — of her","व्यक्ताऽव्यक्तस्वरूपिणी — she whose form is both manifest and unmanifest"],"summary":["व्यक्ताऽव्यक्तस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is both manifest and unmanifest. She appears as the manifested universe and also remains as the unmanifest cause. Both states are Her own form."],"searchText":"399 व्यक्ताऽव्यक्तस्वरूपिणी • व्यक्तं च अव्यक्तं स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति। व्यक्तम् — manifest अव्यक्तम् — unmanifest स्वरूपम् — essential form अस्याः — of her व्यक्ताऽव्यक्तस्वरूपिणी — she whose form is both manifest and unmanifest व्यक्ताऽव्यक्तस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is both manifest and unmanifest. she appears as the manifested universe and also remains as the unmanifest cause. both states are her own form. the total synthesis: she is both avyakta, the hidden cause, and vyakta, the visible universe. the root and the manifest tree are both her.","esoteric":["The Total Synthesis: She is both avyakta, the hidden cause, and vyakta, the visible universe. The root and the manifest tree are both Her."]},{"number":400,"name":"व्यापिनी","samasa":["• व्याप्नोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["व्याप्नोति — pervades","व्यापिनी — all-pervading one"],"summary":["व्यापिनी means one who pervades everything. She pervades all objects, beings, states and worlds as their inner reality."],"searchText":"400 व्यापिनी • व्याप्नोतीति। व्याप्नोति — pervades व्यापिनी — all-pervading one व्यापिनी means one who pervades everything. she pervades all objects, beings, states and worlds as their inner reality. absolute omnipresence: she is absent nowhere. she pervades every object, being, state and thought as the inner fabric of existence.","esoteric":["Absolute Omnipresence: She is absent nowhere. She pervades every object, being, state and thought as the inner fabric of existence."]},{"number":401,"name":"विविधाकारा","samasa":["• विविधाः आकाराः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विविधाः — various; manifold","आकाराः — forms","यस्याः — of whom; whose","विविधाकारा — she who has manifold forms"],"summary":["विविधाकारा means one who has various forms. The many forms seen in the universe are forms of Śrīdevī. She appears in countless shapes according to the needs of creation and worship."],"searchText":"401 विविधाकारा • विविधाः आकाराः यस्याः सा। विविधाः — various; manifold आकाराः — forms यस्याः — of whom; whose विविधाकारा — she who has manifold forms विविधाकारा means one who has various forms. the many forms seen in the universe are forms of śrīdevī. she appears in countless shapes according to the needs of creation and worship. the infinite manifestation: her one essence appears as countless forms. no single appearance can limit her, because every form is within her play.","esoteric":["The Infinite Manifestation: Her one essence appears as countless forms. No single appearance can limit Her, because every form is within Her play."]},{"number":402,"name":"विद्याऽविद्यास्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• विद्या च अविद्या च स्वरूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["विद्या — knowledge","अविद्या — ignorance","स्वरूपम् — form","अस्याः — of her","विद्याऽविद्यास्वरूपिणी — she whose form is knowledge and ignorance"],"summary":["विद्याऽविद्यास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of knowledge and ignorance. Vidyā leads to liberation, while avidyā is the basis of bondage and manifestation. Both function within Her power and are forms of Her cosmic play."],"searchText":"402 विद्याऽविद्यास्वरूपिणी • विद्या च अविद्या च स्वरूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति। विद्या — knowledge अविद्या — ignorance स्वरूपम् — form अस्याः — of her विद्याऽविद्यास्वरूपिणी — she whose form is knowledge and ignorance विद्याऽविद्यास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of knowledge and ignorance. vidyā leads to liberation, while avidyā is the basis of bondage and manifestation. both function within her power and are forms of her cosmic play. knowledge and ignorance: as vidyā, she leads inward to liberation. as avidyā, she enables the appearance of difference and worldly experience.","esoteric":["Knowledge and Ignorance: As vidyā, She leads inward to liberation. As avidyā, She enables the appearance of difference and worldly experience."]},{"number":403,"name":"महाकामेशनयनकुमुदाह्लादकौमुदी","samasa":["• महाकामेशस्य नयने एव कुमुदे। तयोः आह्लादे कौमुदी इव।"],"wordByWord":["महाकामेशस्य — of Mahākāmeśa","नयने — eyes","कुमुदे — water-lilies","आह्लादे — in delighting","कौमुदी — moonlight","महाकामेशनयनकुमुदाह्लादकौमुदी — she who is moonlight delighting the water-lily eyes of Mahākāmeśa"],"summary":["महाकामेशनयनकुमुदाह्लादकौमुदी means one who is like moonlight that delights the lily-like eyes of Mahākāmeśa. The eyes of Mahākāmeśa are like kumuda flowers, which bloom in moonlight. Śrīdevī is the moonlight that gives delight to those eyes."],"searchText":"403 महाकामेशनयनकुमुदाह्लादकौमुदी • महाकामेशस्य नयने एव कुमुदे। तयोः आह्लादे कौमुदी इव। महाकामेशस्य — of mahākāmeśa नयने — eyes कुमुदे — water-lilies आह्लादे — in delighting कौमुदी — moonlight महाकामेशनयनकुमुदाह्लादकौमुदी — she who is moonlight delighting the water-lily eyes of mahākāmeśa महाकामेशनयनकुमुदाह्लादकौमुदी means one who is like moonlight that delights the lily-like eyes of mahākāmeśa. the eyes of mahākāmeśa are like kumuda flowers, which bloom in moonlight. śrīdevī is the moonlight that gives delight to those eyes. the radiance of delight: like moonlight opening the kumuda, her beauty delights the eyes of mahākāmeśvara. she is the bliss of their union.","esoteric":["The Radiance of Delight: Like moonlight opening the kumuda, Her beauty delights the eyes of Mahākāmeśvara. She is the bliss of their union."]},{"number":404,"name":"भक्तहार्दतमोभेदभानुमद्भानुसंततिः","samasa":["• भक्तानां हृदि भावनी यानि तमांसि तेषां भेदे भानुमतः भानुसंततिः।"],"wordByWord":["भक्तानाम् — of devotees","हार्द — in the heart","तमः — darkness","भेद — breaking; removing","भानुमत् — sun-like","भानुसंततिः — stream of rays","भक्तहार्दतमोभेदभानुमद्भानुसंततिः — she who is a stream of sun-rays removing the darkness in devotees’ hearts"],"summary":["भक्तहार्दतमोभेदभानुमद्भानुसंततिः means one who removes the darkness in devotees’ hearts like rays of the sun. The darkness in the heart is ignorance and sorrow. Her grace shines like sunlight and dispels that inner darkness."],"searchText":"404 भक्तहार्दतमोभेदभानुमद्भानुसंततिः • भक्तानां हृदि भावनी यानि तमांसि तेषां भेदे भानुमतः भानुसंततिः। भक्तानाम् — of devotees हार्द — in the heart तमः — darkness भेद — breaking; removing भानुमत् — sun-like भानुसंततिः — stream of rays भक्तहार्दतमोभेदभानुमद्भानुसंततिः — she who is a stream of sun-rays removing the darkness in devotees’ hearts भक्तहार्दतमोभेदभानुमद्भानुसंततिः means one who removes the darkness in devotees’ hearts like rays of the sun. the darkness in the heart is ignorance and sorrow. her grace shines like sunlight and dispels that inner darkness. the solar dispersion: ignorance and sorrow in the heart are like darkness. her grace is like sunlight, dispersing them and filling the heart with clarity.","esoteric":["The Solar Dispersion: Ignorance and sorrow in the heart are like darkness. Her grace is like sunlight, dispersing them and filling the heart with clarity."]},{"number":405,"name":"शिवदूती","samasa":["• शिवः दूतः यस्याः सा।","• शिवस्य दूती।"],"wordByWord":["शिवः — Śiva","दूतः — messenger","यस्याः — of whom; whose","शिवदूती — she for whom Śiva is messenger; or the messenger of Śiva"],"summary":["शिवदूती means one whose messenger is Śiva, or one who is the messenger of Śiva. The name recalls the form in which Śiva Himself acts as Her messenger. It also indicates Her inseparable relation with Śiva."],"searchText":"405 शिवदूती • शिवः दूतः यस्याः सा। • शिवस्य दूती। शिवः — śiva दूतः — messenger यस्याः — of whom; whose शिवदूती — she for whom śiva is messenger; or the messenger of śiva शिवदूती means one whose messenger is śiva, or one who is the messenger of śiva. the name recalls the form in which śiva himself acts as her messenger. it also indicates her inseparable relation with śiva. the supreme command: śiva acts as her messenger, showing her sovereignty and her inseparable relation with him.","esoteric":["The Supreme Command: Śiva acts as Her messenger, showing Her sovereignty and Her inseparable relation with Him."]},{"number":406,"name":"शिवाराध्या","samasa":["• शिवेन आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["शिवेन — by Śiva","आराध्या — worshipped; adored","शिवाराध्या — she who is worshipped by Śiva"],"summary":["शिवाराध्या means one who is worshipped by Śiva. Even Śiva worships Her. This establishes Her supreme status as the power of Śiva Himself."],"searchText":"406 शिवाराध्या • शिवेन आराध्या। शिवेन — by śiva आराध्या — worshipped; adored शिवाराध्या — she who is worshipped by śiva शिवाराध्या means one who is worshipped by śiva. even śiva worships her. this establishes her supreme status as the power of śiva himself. the contemplation of consciousness: śiva worships her as his own creative power and bliss. she is the object of adoration even for śiva.","esoteric":["The Contemplation of Consciousness: Śiva worships Her as His own creative power and bliss. She is the object of adoration even for Śiva."]},{"number":407,"name":"शिवमूर्तिः","samasa":["• शिवः एव मूर्तिः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शिवः — Śiva; auspiciousness","एव — itself","मूर्तिः — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose","शिवमूर्तिः — she whose form is Śiva"],"summary":["शिवमूर्तिः means one whose form is Śiva. She is not different from Śiva. Her form is auspiciousness itself and is identical with Śiva-consciousness."],"searchText":"407 शिवमूर्तिः • शिवः एव मूर्तिः यस्याः सा। शिवः — śiva; auspiciousness एव — itself मूर्तिः — form यस्याः — of whom; whose शिवमूर्तिः — she whose form is śiva शिवमूर्तिः means one whose form is śiva. she is not different from śiva. her form is auspiciousness itself and is identical with śiva-consciousness. non-dual identity: her very form is śiva. śiva and śakti are inseparable aspects of one indivisible reality.","esoteric":["Non-Dual Identity: Her very form is Śiva. Śiva and Śakti are inseparable aspects of one indivisible reality."]},{"number":408,"name":"शिवङ्करी","samasa":["• शिवं करोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["शिवम् — auspiciousness; welfare","करोति — makes; does","शिवङ्करी — she who causes auspiciousness"],"summary":["शिवङ्करी means one who does good and makes all auspicious. She confers welfare and auspiciousness on devotees and turns life toward the good."],"searchText":"408 शिवङ्करी • शिवं करोतीति। शिवम् — auspiciousness; welfare करोति — makes; does शिवङ्करी — she who causes auspiciousness शिवङ्करी means one who does good and makes all auspicious. she confers welfare and auspiciousness on devotees and turns life toward the good. the dispenser of peace: she creates welfare, auspiciousness and inner peace. by removing harmful tendencies, she turns the soul toward śiva.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of Peace: She creates welfare, auspiciousness and inner peace. By removing harmful tendencies, She turns the soul toward Śiva."]},{"number":409,"name":"शिवप्रिया","samasa":["• शिवस्य प्रिया।","• शिवः प्रियः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शिवस्य — of Śiva","प्रिया — beloved","शिवः — Śiva","प्रियः — dear","शिवप्रिया — beloved of Śiva; she to whom Śiva is dear"],"summary":["शिवप्रिया means one who is dear to Śiva. She is beloved of Śiva, and Śiva is dear to Her. The name expresses the mutual unity and love of Śiva and Śakti."],"searchText":"409 शिवप्रिया • शिवस्य प्रिया। • शिवः प्रियः यस्याः सा। शिवस्य — of śiva प्रिया — beloved शिवः — śiva प्रियः — dear शिवप्रिया — beloved of śiva; she to whom śiva is dear शिवप्रिया means one who is dear to śiva. she is beloved of śiva, and śiva is dear to her. the name expresses the mutual unity and love of śiva and śakti. the inseparable bond: she is eternally dear to śiva. their love shows the inseparability of consciousness and energy.","esoteric":["The Inseparable Bond: She is eternally dear to Śiva. Their love shows the inseparability of consciousness and energy."]},{"number":410,"name":"शिवपरा","samasa":["• शिवः एव परः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शिवः — Śiva","एव — alone","परः — supreme goal","यस्याः — of whom; whose","शिवपरा — she whose supreme object is Śiva"],"summary":["शिवपरा means one for whom Śiva is supreme. She is established in Śiva as the supreme reality. The name also shows Her non-difference from Śiva."],"searchText":"410 शिवपरा • शिवः एव परः यस्याः सा। शिवः — śiva एव — alone परः — supreme goal यस्याः — of whom; whose शिवपरा — she whose supreme object is śiva शिवपरा means one for whom śiva is supreme. she is established in śiva as the supreme reality. the name also shows her non-difference from śiva. perpetual orientation: her power leads everything back into the peaceful consciousness of śiva. she remains completely absorbed in him.","esoteric":["Perpetual Orientation: Her power leads everything back into the peaceful consciousness of Śiva. She remains completely absorbed in Him."]},{"number":411,"name":"शिष्टेष्टा","samasa":["• शिष्टैः इष्टा।","• शिष्टानि इष्टानि यस्याः सा।","• शिष्टानाम् इष्टा।","• शिष्टाः इष्टाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शिष्टैः — by the cultured and righteous","इष्टा — loved; worshipped; desired","शिष्टानाम् — of the noble","शिष्टेष्टा — she who is loved and worshipped by the noble"],"summary":["शिष्टेष्टा means one who is loved and worshipped by the noble and cultured. Śiṣṭa means the righteous, learned and disciplined. She is their chosen deity and object of worship."],"searchText":"411 शिष्टेष्टा • शिष्टैः इष्टा। • शिष्टानि इष्टानि यस्याः सा। • शिष्टानाम् इष्टा। • शिष्टाः इष्टाः यस्याः सा। शिष्टैः — by the cultured and righteous इष्टा — loved; worshipped; desired शिष्टानाम् — of the noble शिष्टेष्टा — she who is loved and worshipped by the noble शिष्टेष्टा means one who is loved and worshipped by the noble and cultured. śiṣṭa means the righteous, learned and disciplined. she is their chosen deity and object of worship. the adoration of the wise: śiṣṭas are disciplined and refined seekers. she is their desired deity and holds them dear, protecting their spiritual progress.","esoteric":["The Adoration of the Wise: Śiṣṭas are disciplined and refined seekers. She is their desired deity and holds them dear, protecting their spiritual progress."]},{"number":412,"name":"शिष्टपूजिता","samasa":["• शिष्टैः पूजिता।"],"wordByWord":["शिष्टैः — by the noble; by the disciplined","पूजिता — worshipped","शिष्टपूजिता — worshipped by the noble"],"summary":["शिष्टपूजिता means one who is worshipped by noble persons. The śiṣṭas, those who follow right knowledge and conduct, worship Her."],"searchText":"412 शिष्टपूजिता • शिष्टैः पूजिता। शिष्टैः — by the noble; by the disciplined पूजिता — worshipped शिष्टपूजिता — worshipped by the noble शिष्टपूजिता means one who is worshipped by noble persons. the śiṣṭas, those who follow right knowledge and conduct, worship her. the worship of the noble: her worship is cherished by the righteous, learned and disciplined. their devotion confirms her place as the object of right understanding and conduct.","esoteric":["The Worship of the Noble: Her worship is cherished by the righteous, learned and disciplined. Their devotion confirms Her place as the object of right understanding and conduct."]},{"number":413,"name":"अप्रमेया","samasa":["• न प्रमेया।"],"wordByWord":["न — not","प्रमेया — measurable; knowable as an object of proof","अप्रमेया — immeasurable; not an object of limited knowledge"],"summary":["अप्रमेया means one who is immeasurable. She cannot be measured by ordinary means of knowledge. Being the very basis of knowledge, She cannot be known as a limited object."],"searchText":"413 अप्रमेया • न प्रमेया। न — not प्रमेया — measurable; knowable as an object of proof अप्रमेया — immeasurable; not an object of limited knowledge अप्रमेया means one who is immeasurable. she cannot be measured by ordinary means of knowledge. being the very basis of knowledge, she cannot be known as a limited object. beyond proof: objects are measured by pramāṇa, means of knowledge. she is the consciousness behind those means and is the knower, never a limited known object.","esoteric":["Beyond Proof: Objects are measured by pramāṇa, means of knowledge. She is the consciousness behind those means and is the knower, never a limited known object."]},{"number":414,"name":"स्वप्रकाशा","samasa":["• स्वः प्रकाशः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्वः — self; own","प्रकाशः — light; illumination","यस्याः — of whom; whose","स्वप्रकाशा — self-luminous one"],"summary":["स्वप्रकाशा means one who is self-luminous. She shines by Herself and does not need another light to reveal Her. As consciousness, She reveals all things and is self-revealed."],"searchText":"414 स्वप्रकाशा • स्वः प्रकाशः यस्याः सा। स्वः — self; own प्रकाशः — light; illumination यस्याः — of whom; whose स्वप्रकाशा — self-luminous one स्वप्रकाशा means one who is self-luminous. she shines by herself and does not need another light to reveal her. as consciousness, she reveals all things and is self-revealed. independent light: she needs no external lamp, intellect or proof to reveal her. like the sun, she is known through her own light.","esoteric":["Independent Light: She needs no external lamp, intellect or proof to reveal Her. Like the sun, She is known through Her own light."]},{"number":415,"name":"मनोवाचामगोचरा","samasa":["• मनांसि च वाचश्च तेषां तासां च अगोचरा।"],"wordByWord":["• मनांसि — minds.","• वाचः — words, speech.","• तेषाम् / तासाम् — of them.","• अगोचरा — beyond the field or range of perception.","• मनोवाचामगोचरा — She who is beyond the range of mind and speech."],"summary":["मनोवाचामगोचरा means one who is beyond the range of mind and speech. She cannot be fully grasped by mind or expressed by speech. No object of thought or word is found in Her. Mind, speech and the organs can know only limited objects, but Śrīdevī is limitless, boundless and infinite. With the previous name, the name may also indicate that She is beyond immature mind and speech, and is approached by purified mind and speech."],"searchText":"415 मनोवाचामगोचरा • मनांसि च वाचश्च तेषां तासां च अगोचरा। • मनांसि — minds. • वाचः — words, speech. • तेषाम् / तासाम् — of them. • अगोचरा — beyond the field or range of perception. • मनोवाचामगोचरा — she who is beyond the range of mind and speech. मनोवाचामगोचरा means one who is beyond the range of mind and speech. she cannot be fully grasped by mind or expressed by speech. no object of thought or word is found in her. mind, speech and the organs can know only limited objects, but śrīdevī is limitless, boundless and infinite. with the previous name, the name may also indicate that she is beyond immature mind and speech, and is approached by purified mind and speech. transcendence of conceptions: words and ordinary thought cannot contain her immensity. she remains the witness behind mental concepts and verbal definitions.","esoteric":["Transcendence of Conceptions: Words and ordinary thought cannot contain Her immensity. She remains the witness behind mental concepts and verbal definitions."]},{"number":416,"name":"चिच्छक्तिः","samasa":["• चित्शक्तिः।"],"wordByWord":["• चित् — consciousness, knowledge.","• शक्तिः — power, energy.","• चिच्छक्तिः — the power of consciousness."],"summary":["चिच्छक्तिः means one who is the power of cit. Cicchakti, the power that removes ignorance, is also called caitanya. Since Śrīdevī is knowledge itself, She is Cicchakti. This power is present in all beings; without it, a being is like a corpse. As cit-śakti, She is the living conscious power in all. Cit can also mean comparison, and the knowledge gained by comparison is Śrīdevī Herself."],"searchText":"416 चिच्छक्तिः • चित्शक्तिः। • चित् — consciousness, knowledge. • शक्तिः — power, energy. • चिच्छक्तिः — the power of consciousness. चिच्छक्तिः means one who is the power of cit. cicchakti, the power that removes ignorance, is also called caitanya. since śrīdevī is knowledge itself, she is cicchakti. this power is present in all beings; without it, a being is like a corpse. as cit-śakti, she is the living conscious power in all. cit can also mean comparison, and the knowledge gained by comparison is śrīdevī herself. kinetic consciousness: she is conscious power, not inert force. she is brahman’s capacity to know, experience and manifest without losing purity.","esoteric":["Kinetic Consciousness: She is conscious power, not inert force. She is Brahman’s capacity to know, experience and manifest without losing purity."]},{"number":417,"name":"चेतनारूपा","samasa":["• चेतना रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• चेतना — consciousness, sentience, inner awareness.","• रूपम् — form.","• यस्याः सा — whose; she whose.","• चेतनारूपा — She whose form is consciousness."],"summary":["चेतनारूपा means one who is in the form of consciousness, caitanya. The conscious energy in all beings is Śrīdevī. Cetanā is the inner sense through which objects shown by eye, ear and mind are recognized. Its presence is known through its action. Pure cit-śakti is caitanya, the conscious principle that guides the senses."],"searchText":"417 चेतनारूपा • चेतना रूपं यस्याः सा। • चेतना — consciousness, sentience, inner awareness. • रूपम् — form. • यस्याः सा — whose; she whose. • चेतनारूपा — she whose form is consciousness. चेतनारूपा means one who is in the form of consciousness, caitanya. the conscious energy in all beings is śrīdevī. cetanā is the inner sense through which objects shown by eye, ear and mind are recognized. its presence is known through its action. pure cit-śakti is caitanya, the conscious principle that guides the senses. the animating pulse: cetanā is the spark of life and intelligence. every thought, movement and perception occurs through her living presence.","esoteric":["The Animating Pulse: Cetanā is the spark of life and intelligence. Every thought, movement and perception occurs through Her living presence."]},{"number":418,"name":"जडशक्तिः","samasa":["• जडाशक्तिः।"],"wordByWord":["• जडा — inert, insentient, mechanical.","• शक्तिः — power, energy.","• जडशक्तिः — the power operating in inert creation."],"summary":["जडशक्तिः means one who manifests as the forces of inanimate creation. A modification of māyā, related to the power that creates the animate world, is creative energy. The energies of beings are difficult to grasp; the creative energies of Brahman are even harder to grasp and are in Brahman like heat in fire. Brahman is the instrumental cause, while these creative energies are the material cause. An object becomes itself by its own energy."],"searchText":"418 जडशक्तिः • जडाशक्तिः। • जडा — inert, insentient, mechanical. • शक्तिः — power, energy. • जडशक्तिः — the power operating in inert creation. जडशक्तिः means one who manifests as the forces of inanimate creation. a modification of māyā, related to the power that creates the animate world, is creative energy. the energies of beings are difficult to grasp; the creative energies of brahman are even harder to grasp and are in brahman like heat in fire. brahman is the instrumental cause, while these creative energies are the material cause. an object becomes itself by its own energy. the matrix of matter: she is jaḍaśakti, the power appearing as inert matter and mechanical force. the physical universe is also built through her energy.","esoteric":["The Matrix of Matter: She is jaḍaśakti, the power appearing as inert matter and mechanical force. The physical universe is also built through Her energy."]},{"number":419,"name":"जडात्मिका","samasa":["• जडं दृश्यमत्रम् आत्मा यस्याः मायायाः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• जडम् — inert, insentient.","• दृश्यमात्रम् — mere visible object, object of perception.","• आत्मा — inner essence, nature.","• माया — māyā.","• जडात्मिका — She who is the inner essence of inert manifestation."],"summary":["जडात्मिका means one who is the innermost essence of all mechanical forces. The static universe is a special form of cosmic manifestation, and She is its inner essence."],"searchText":"419 जडात्मिका • जडं दृश्यमत्रम् आत्मा यस्याः मायायाः सा। • जडम् — inert, insentient. • दृश्यमात्रम् — mere visible object, object of perception. • आत्मा — inner essence, nature. • माया — māyā. • जडात्मिका — she who is the inner essence of inert manifestation. जडात्मिका means one who is the innermost essence of all mechanical forces. the static universe is a special form of cosmic manifestation, and she is its inner essence. the objective universe: jaḍa is the dense field of seen objects. she embodies this material layer through her power of māyā.","esoteric":["The Objective Universe: Jaḍa is the dense field of seen objects. She embodies this material layer through Her power of māyā."]},{"number":420,"name":"गायत्री","samasa":["• छन्दसां चतुर्विंशत्यक्षरं गायत्री।","• गायन्तं त्रायते यस्मादिति।","• गायनाद् गमनाद् वा।","• गायति च त्रायते च।","• गायनात्मत्वात्।","• गोपकन्या ब्रह्मणः कनिष्ठपत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["• छन्दसाम् — among metres.","• चतुर्विंशत्यक्षरम् — having twenty-four syllables.","• गायन्तम् — the one who sings or recites.","• त्रायते — protects.","• गायनात् — from singing.","• गमनात् — from going or movement.","• गायति — sings.","• त्रायते — protects.","• गोपकन्या — daughter of a cowherd / guardian of sacred knowledge.","• ब्रह्मणः कनिष्ठपत्नी — the junior wife of Brahmā."],"summary":["गायत्री means one who is in the form of Gāyatrī. The Gāyatrī mantra is mother of mantras, and the Gāyatrī metre has twenty-four characters. Gāyatrī protects those who recite Her mantra: gāyantaṃ trāyate, She protects the one who sings or chants. She is also linked with song, hearing and protection. Śrīdevī is in the form of Gāyatrī and, in another interpretation, in the form of the three guṇas."],"searchText":"420 गायत्री • छन्दसां चतुर्विंशत्यक्षरं गायत्री। • गायन्तं त्रायते यस्मादिति। • गायनाद् गमनाद् वा। • गायति च त्रायते च। • गायनात्मत्वात्। • गोपकन्या ब्रह्मणः कनिष्ठपत्नी। • छन्दसाम् — among metres. • चतुर्विंशत्यक्षरम् — having twenty-four syllables. • गायन्तम् — the one who sings or recites. • त्रायते — protects. • गायनात् — from singing. • गमनात् — from going or movement. • गायति — sings. • त्रायते — protects. • गोपकन्या — daughter of a cowherd / guardian of sacred knowledge. • ब्रह्मणः कनिष्ठपत्नी — the junior wife of brahmā. गायत्री means one who is in the form of gāyatrī. the gāyatrī mantra is mother of mantras, and the gāyatrī metre has twenty-four characters. gāyatrī protects those who recite her mantra: gāyantaṃ trāyate, she protects the one who sings or chants. she is also linked with song, hearing and protection. śrīdevī is in the form of gāyatrī and, in another interpretation, in the form of the three guṇas. the mother of mantras: she is gāyatrī, the protective mantra power. she guards the one who chants and turns the intellect toward light.","esoteric":["The Mother of Mantras: She is Gāyatrī, the protective mantra power. She guards the one who chants and turns the intellect toward light."]},{"number":421,"name":"व्याहृतिः","samasa":["• उच्चारणरूपा।","• मन्त्रविशेषणरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["• उच्चारण — utterance, pronunciation.","• रूपा — form.","• मन्त्रविशेषण — qualifying or special mantra-expression.","• व्याहृतिः — sacred utterance/invocation."],"summary":["व्याहृतिः means one who is in the form of vyāhṛtis, sacred invocations. Special mantras are called vyāhṛtis. Before creation, Brahmā chanted Oṃ and then bhūḥ, bhuvaḥ and suvaḥ; creation expanded into seven worlds: bhūḥ, bhuvaḥ, suvaḥ, mahaḥ, janaḥ, tapaḥ and satyam. Therefore Oṃ and the names of these worlds are vyāhṛtis, and She is in that form. Vyāhṛti can also mean pronunciation."],"searchText":"421 व्याहृतिः • उच्चारणरूपा। • मन्त्रविशेषणरूपा। • उच्चारण — utterance, pronunciation. • रूपा — form. • मन्त्रविशेषण — qualifying or special mantra-expression. • व्याहृतिः — sacred utterance/invocation. व्याहृतिः means one who is in the form of vyāhṛtis, sacred invocations. special mantras are called vyāhṛtis. before creation, brahmā chanted oṃ and then bhūḥ, bhuvaḥ and suvaḥ; creation expanded into seven worlds: bhūḥ, bhuvaḥ, suvaḥ, mahaḥ, janaḥ, tapaḥ and satyam. therefore oṃ and the names of these worlds are vyāhṛtis, and she is in that form. vyāhṛti can also mean pronunciation. the sacred utterance: vyāhṛtis are cosmic utterances such as bhūḥ, bhuvaḥ and suvaḥ. she is the sound-power that projects and names the worlds.","esoteric":["The Sacred Utterance: Vyāhṛtis are cosmic utterances such as bhūḥ, bhuvaḥ and suvaḥ. She is the sound-power that projects and names the worlds."]},{"number":422,"name":"संध्या","samasa":["• सम्यग् ध्यायन्ति अस्याम्।","• सम्यग्ध्येयत्वात्।"],"wordByWord":["• सम्यक् — properly, completely.","• ध्यायन्ति — they meditate.","• अस्याम् — in her, upon her.","• ध्येयत्वात् — because she is fit to be meditated upon.","• संध्या — Sandhyā, junction, twilight meditation."],"summary":["संध्या means one who is in the form of Sandhyā, the deity of twilight. Sandhyā means junction, meditation, and the meeting of day and night. Morning and evening are such junctions, and noon and midnight are also treated as junctions. True sandhyā worship is meditation on the unity of consciousness. Sandhyā is also the mind-born daughter of Brahmā, later known as Arundhatī. She is connected with the integration of Iḍā, Piṅgalā and Suṣumṇā, and with the forms Mahākālī, Mahālakṣmī and Ekavīrā."],"searchText":"422 संध्या • सम्यग् ध्यायन्ति अस्याम्। • सम्यग्ध्येयत्वात्। • सम्यक् — properly, completely. • ध्यायन्ति — they meditate. • अस्याम् — in her, upon her. • ध्येयत्वात् — because she is fit to be meditated upon. • संध्या — sandhyā, junction, twilight meditation. संध्या means one who is in the form of sandhyā, the deity of twilight. sandhyā means junction, meditation, and the meeting of day and night. morning and evening are such junctions, and noon and midnight are also treated as junctions. true sandhyā worship is meditation on the unity of consciousness. sandhyā is also the mind-born daughter of brahmā, later known as arundhatī. she is connected with the integration of iḍā, piṅgalā and suṣumṇā, and with the forms mahākālī, mahālakṣmī and ekavīrā. the hour of union: sandhyā is the junction where transition becomes worship. internally, she is the meeting of iḍā, piṅgalā and suṣumṇā in meditative absorption.","esoteric":["The Hour of Union: Sandhyā is the junction where transition becomes worship. Internally, She is the meeting of Iḍā, Piṅgalā and Suṣumṇā in meditative absorption."]},{"number":423,"name":"द्विजवृन्दनिषेविता","samasa":["• द्विजानां वृन्दम्। तैः निषेविता उपास्या।"],"wordByWord":["• द्विजानाम् — of the twice-born.","• वृन्दम् — group, assembly.","• तैः — by them.","• निषेविता — served, worshipped.","• उपास्या — to be worshipped."],"summary":["द्विजवृन्दनिषेविता means one who is worshipped by groups of the twice-born. She is meditated upon by brāhmaṇas, kṣatriyas and vaiśyas, whose second birth occurs through upanayana for understanding Gāyatrī. She is worshipped because She is Sandhyā. Dvija can also mean birds, and birds returning to their nests suggest beings entering deep sleep after waking and dream. Thus this name may also indicate deep sleep."],"searchText":"423 द्विजवृन्दनिषेविता • द्विजानां वृन्दम्। तैः निषेविता उपास्या। • द्विजानाम् — of the twice-born. • वृन्दम् — group, assembly. • तैः — by them. • निषेविता — served, worshipped. • उपास्या — to be worshipped. द्विजवृन्दनिषेविता means one who is worshipped by groups of the twice-born. she is meditated upon by brāhmaṇas, kṣatriyas and vaiśyas, whose second birth occurs through upanayana for understanding gāyatrī. she is worshipped because she is sandhyā. dvija can also mean birds, and birds returning to their nests suggest beings entering deep sleep after waking and dream. thus this name may also indicate deep sleep. the double birth: dvija means twice-born, first by physical birth and then by sacred discipline. such disciplined seekers worship her as their central deity.","esoteric":["The Double Birth: Dvija means twice-born, first by physical birth and then by sacred discipline. Such disciplined seekers worship Her as their central deity."]},{"number":424,"name":"तत्त्वासना","samasa":["• षट्त्रिंशत् तत्त्वानि आसनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• षट्त्रिंशत् — thirty-six.","• तत्त्वानि — cosmic principles or elements.","• आसनम् — seat.","• यस्याः सा — whose; she whose.","• तत्त्वासना — She whose seat is constituted by the tattvas."],"summary":["तत्त्वासना means one whose seat is made of the cosmic elements or tattvas. Different systems count tattvas differently, but Śākta and Śaiva traditions accept thirty-six tattvas from Śiva to pṛthivī. Śrīdevī has these thirty-six tattvas as Her yogic seat. Another meaning is that She pushes out or transcends the tattvas, remaining beyond them even when they are destroyed."],"searchText":"424 तत्त्वासना • षट्त्रिंशत् तत्त्वानि आसनं यस्याः सा। • षट्त्रिंशत् — thirty-six. • तत्त्वानि — cosmic principles or elements. • आसनम् — seat. • यस्याः सा — whose; she whose. • तत्त्वासना — she whose seat is constituted by the tattvas. तत्त्वासना means one whose seat is made of the cosmic elements or tattvas. different systems count tattvas differently, but śākta and śaiva traditions accept thirty-six tattvas from śiva to pṛthivī. śrīdevī has these thirty-six tattvas as her yogic seat. another meaning is that she pushes out or transcends the tattvas, remaining beyond them even when they are destroyed. the throne of tattvas: the thirty-six tattvas form her seat. she rules the whole ladder of manifestation and also transcends it.","esoteric":["The Throne of Tattvas: The thirty-six tattvas form Her seat. She rules the whole ladder of manifestation and also transcends it."]},{"number":425,"name":"तत्","samasa":["• तत्पदस्य बुद्धिविपरिवृत्तिविषये शक्तिः।","• तत्पदवाच्या।","• तस्मै नमः।"],"wordByWord":["• तत् — That; the transcendent principle referred to in the Mahavakya.","• पदस्य — of the word.","• बुद्धिविपरिवृत्तिविषये — in the field of the transformation or revolution of intellect.","• शक्तिः — power.","• वाच्या — directly denoted.","• तस्मै नमः — salutation to That."],"summary":["तत् means one who is in the form of tat, “That.” The word tat signifies the movement of mind, as Śrīdevī moves in the buddhis of all souls. She is indicated by the word tat. In nāmāvalī usage, this name appears as tasmai namaḥ."],"searchText":"425 तत् • तत्पदस्य बुद्धिविपरिवृत्तिविषये शक्तिः। • तत्पदवाच्या। • तस्मै नमः। • तत् — that; the transcendent principle referred to in the mahavakya. • पदस्य — of the word. • बुद्धिविपरिवृत्तिविषये — in the field of the transformation or revolution of intellect. • शक्तिः — power. • वाच्या — directly denoted. • तस्मै नमः — salutation to that. तत् means one who is in the form of tat, “that.” the word tat signifies the movement of mind, as śrīdevī moves in the buddhis of all souls. she is indicated by the word tat. in nāmāvalī usage, this name appears as tasmai namaḥ. the direct designation: tat points to the transcendent cause and absolute brahman. as tat, she is beyond limiting personal descriptions.","esoteric":["The Direct Designation: Tat points to the transcendent cause and absolute Brahman. As Tat, She is beyond limiting personal descriptions."]},{"number":426,"name":"त्वम्","samasa":["• त्वम्पदवाच्या।","• त्वम्पदवाच्या।","• तुभ्यं नमः।"],"wordByWord":["• त्वम् — Thou; you.","• पदवाच्या — denoted by the word.","• तुभ्यम् नमः — salutation to you."],"summary":["त्वम् means “thou.” Among the thirty-six tattvas, Śiva-tattva is Para Saṃvit, the supreme being without quality or blemish. Śiva-tattva and Śakti-tattva are one in Para Saṃvit. When Śrīdevī is Parabrahman, She is prakāśa-vimarśa-sāmarasya-rūpiṇī, the unity of illumination and self-awareness. This knowledge includes aham, idam, etat and tat. In nāmāvalī usage, this name appears as tubhyaṃ namaḥ."],"searchText":"426 त्वम् • त्वम्पदवाच्या। • त्वम्पदवाच्या। • तुभ्यं नमः। • त्वम् — thou; you. • पदवाच्या — denoted by the word. • तुभ्यम् नमः — salutation to you. त्वम् means “thou.” among the thirty-six tattvas, śiva-tattva is para saṃvit, the supreme being without quality or blemish. śiva-tattva and śakti-tattva are one in para saṃvit. when śrīdevī is parabrahman, she is prakāśa-vimarśa-sāmarasya-rūpiṇī, the unity of illumination and self-awareness. this knowledge includes aham, idam, etat and tat. in nāmāvalī usage, this name appears as tubhyaṃ namaḥ. the immediate presence: tat is “that,” while tvam is “thou.” she is not distant only; she is the inner reality present in the seeker.","esoteric":["The Immediate Presence: Tat is “That,” while tvam is “thou.” She is not distant only; She is the inner reality present in the seeker."]},{"number":427,"name":"अयी","samasa":["• अयी। जनमातृत्वात् जनैः आमन्त्रणीया।"],"wordByWord":["• अयी — Ayī; affectionate form of address to the Mother.","• जनमातृत्वात् — because she is the mother of all beings.","• जनैः — by people.","• आमन्त्रणीया — to be called or invoked."],"summary":["अयी means one who is called ayī. The word is a tender form of calling, like a child calling the mother."],"searchText":"427 अयी • अयी। जनमातृत्वात् जनैः आमन्त्रणीया। • अयी — ayī; affectionate form of address to the mother. • जनमातृत्वात् — because she is the mother of all beings. • जनैः — by people. • आमन्त्रणीया — to be called or invoked. अयी means one who is called ayī. the word is a tender form of calling, like a child calling the mother. the spontaneous cry: ayī is a tender call to the mother. she responds to the simple cry of love arising from the heart.","esoteric":["The Spontaneous Cry: Ayī is a tender call to the mother. She responds to the simple cry of love arising from the heart."]},{"number":428,"name":"पञ्चकोशांतरस्थिता","samasa":["• पञ्चसङ्ख्याकाः कोशाः। तेषाम् अन्तरे स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["• पञ्चसङ्ख्याकाः — numbering five.","• कोशाः — sheaths.","• तेषाम् — of them.","• अन्तरे — inside, within.","• स्थिता — situated, abiding.","• पञ्चकोशांतरस्थिता — She who dwells amidst the five kośas, the psychological sheaths of the personality."],"summary":["पञ्चकोशांतरस्थिता means one who dwells within the five kośas. In worship, five pañcikās are contemplated as five Lakṣmīs, five sheaths, five kalpalatās, five kāmadhenus and five gems. The bodily five sheaths are annamaya, prāṇamaya, manomaya, vijñānamaya and ānandamaya. Each is covered by the previous one. Śrīdevī is present within these kośas and is the truth beyond and within them."],"searchText":"428 पञ्चकोशांतरस्थिता • पञ्चसङ्ख्याकाः कोशाः। तेषाम् अन्तरे स्थिता। • पञ्चसङ्ख्याकाः — numbering five. • कोशाः — sheaths. • तेषाम् — of them. • अन्तरे — inside, within. • स्थिता — situated, abiding. • पञ्चकोशांतरस्थिता — she who dwells amidst the five kośas, the psychological sheaths of the personality. पञ्चकोशांतरस्थिता means one who dwells within the five kośas. in worship, five pañcikās are contemplated as five lakṣmīs, five sheaths, five kalpalatās, five kāmadhenus and five gems. the bodily five sheaths are annamaya, prāṇamaya, manomaya, vijñānamaya and ānandamaya. each is covered by the previous one. śrīdevī is present within these kośas and is the truth beyond and within them. the hidden jewel: the five kośas are food, vital energy, mind, intellect and bliss sheaths. she dwells at their centre as the innermost reality.","esoteric":["The Hidden Jewel: The five kośas are food, vital energy, mind, intellect and bliss sheaths. She dwells at their centre as the innermost reality."]},{"number":429,"name":"निस्सीममहिमा","samasa":["• निष्कान्तः सीमानं सीमां वा निःसीमा नीःसीमो वा महिमा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• निष्कान्तः — gone beyond, free from.","• सीमानं — limit.","• सीमां — boundary.","• निःसीमा — without limit.","• महिमा — glory, greatness.","• निस्सीममहिमा — She whose glory is boundless."],"summary":["निस्सीममहिमा means one whose glory is boundless. Sīmā means boundary, and nissīma means without boundary. Her greatness and glory are limitless."],"searchText":"429 निस्सीममहिमा • निष्कान्तः सीमानं सीमां वा निःसीमा नीःसीमो वा महिमा यस्याः सा। • निष्कान्तः — gone beyond, free from. • सीमानं — limit. • सीमां — boundary. • निःसीमा — without limit. • महिमा — glory, greatness. • निस्सीममहिमा — she whose glory is boundless. निस्सीममहिमा means one whose glory is boundless. sīmā means boundary, and nissīma means without boundary. her greatness and glory are limitless. boundless glory: her mahimā has no boundary, limit or measure. it extends beyond space, time and capacity.","esoteric":["Boundless Glory: Her mahimā has no boundary, limit or measure. It extends beyond space, time and capacity."]},{"number":430,"name":"नित्ययौवना","samasa":["• नित्यं यौवनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• नित्यं — always, eternally.","• यौवनं — youth.","• नित्ययौवना — She who is eternally young."],"summary":["नित्ययौवना means one who is eternally young. She is youthful without growth, decline or deterioration."],"searchText":"430 नित्ययौवना • नित्यं यौवनं यस्याः सा। • नित्यं — always, eternally. • यौवनं — youth. • नित्ययौवना — she who is eternally young. नित्ययौवना means one who is eternally young. she is youthful without growth, decline or deterioration. the dynamic freshness: her youth is untouched by age or decay. her consciousness remains perpetually fresh, vibrant and vital.","esoteric":["The Dynamic Freshness: Her youth is untouched by age or decay. Her consciousness remains perpetually fresh, vibrant and vital."]},{"number":431,"name":"मदशालिनी","samasa":["• मदेन शालते इति।"],"wordByWord":["• मदेन — by bliss, exhilaration, or divine intoxication.","• शालते — shines, abides, is endowed.","• मदशालिनी — She who shines with the intoxication of bliss."],"summary":["मदशालिनी means one who is filled with the intoxication of bliss. Mada here means absorption in bliss, with no interest in anything else. She shines in that state, with the mind submerged in bliss and rapture."],"searchText":"431 मदशालिनी • मदेन शालते इति। • मदेन — by bliss, exhilaration, or divine intoxication. • शालते — shines, abides, is endowed. • मदशालिनी — she who shines with the intoxication of bliss. मदशालिनी means one who is filled with the intoxication of bliss. mada here means absorption in bliss, with no interest in anything else. she shines in that state, with the mind submerged in bliss and rapture. the intoxication of fullness: her intoxication is the joy of absolute self-satisfaction, ātmarati. she lacks nothing, seeks nothing outside herself, and remains delighted in her own infinite fullness.","esoteric":["The Intoxication of Fullness: Her intoxication is the joy of absolute self-satisfaction, Ātmarati. She lacks nothing, seeks nothing outside Herself, and remains delighted in Her own infinite fullness."]},{"number":432,"name":"मदघूर्णितरक्ताक्षी","samasa":["• मदेन घूर्णितानि रक्तानि च अक्षीणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• मदेन — by bliss, exhilaration, or divine intoxication.","• घूर्णितानि — made to roll or revolve.","• रक्तानि — reddish.","• अक्षीणि — eyes.","• मदघूर्णितरक्ताक्षी — She whose reddish eyes roll owing to the exuberance of bliss."],"summary":["मदघूर्णितरक्ताक्षी means one whose reddish eyes roll through the exuberance of bliss. Ghūrṇana means turning away from outside matters or revolving. Because of bliss, Her naturally reddish eyes become further red-tinged and turn inward, without interest in external things."],"searchText":"432 मदघूर्णितरक्ताक्षी • मदेन घूर्णितानि रक्तानि च अक्षीणि यस्याः सा। • मदेन — by bliss, exhilaration, or divine intoxication. • घूर्णितानि — made to roll or revolve. • रक्तानि — reddish. • अक्षीणि — eyes. • मदघूर्णितरक्ताक्षी — she whose reddish eyes roll owing to the exuberance of bliss. मदघूर्णितरक्ताक्षी means one whose reddish eyes roll through the exuberance of bliss. ghūrṇana means turning away from outside matters or revolving. because of bliss, her naturally reddish eyes become further red-tinged and turn inward, without interest in external things. the gaze of samādhi: the rolling, reddened eyes show attention drawn away from outer objects and gathered inward. the redness also suggests the intensity of her compassion while she abides in non-dual bliss.","esoteric":["The Gaze of Samādhi: The rolling, reddened eyes show attention drawn away from outer objects and gathered inward. The redness also suggests the intensity of Her compassion while She abides in non-dual bliss."]},{"number":433,"name":"मदपाटलगंडभूः","samasa":["• मदपाटलवत्यौ गण्डभूवौ यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• गण्डभूवौ — cheek-regions.","• मदपाटलगंडभूः — She whose cheek-regions are rosy through bliss."],"summary":["मदपाटलगंडभूः means one whose cheeks are rosy through bliss. Her cheeks are whitish-red or rosy because Her mind is full of bliss. Pāṭala means rosy, or the colour of the trumpet flower. Mada can also mean wine, making Her cheeks reddish. Mada can also indicate the musk deer, suggesting that Her cheek-regions are decorated with pāṭala designs drawn with musk."],"searchText":"433 मदपाटलगंडभूः • मदपाटलवत्यौ गण्डभूवौ यस्याः सा। • गण्डभूवौ — cheek-regions. • मदपाटलगंडभूः — she whose cheek-regions are rosy through bliss. मदपाटलगंडभूः means one whose cheeks are rosy through bliss. her cheeks are whitish-red or rosy because her mind is full of bliss. pāṭala means rosy, or the colour of the trumpet flower. mada can also mean wine, making her cheeks reddish. mada can also indicate the musk deer, suggesting that her cheek-regions are decorated with pāṭala designs drawn with musk. the flush of bliss: the rosy glow on her cheeks is the outward sign of inner ānanda. it shows warm, overflowing delight and the welcoming beauty of the divine mother.","esoteric":["The Flush of Bliss: The rosy glow on Her cheeks is the outward sign of inner ānanda. It shows warm, overflowing delight and the welcoming beauty of the divine mother."]},{"number":434,"name":"चन्दनद्रवदिग्धाङ्गी","samasa":["• चन्दनस्य द्रवेण दिग्धानि अङ्गानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• चन्दनस्य — of sandal paste.","• द्रवेण — with liquid or paste.","• दिग्धानि — anointed, smeared.","• अङ्गानि — limbs.","• चन्दनद्रवदिग्धाङ्गी — She whose limbs are anointed with liquid sandal paste."],"summary":["चन्दनद्रवदिग्धाङ्गी means one whose limbs are anointed with liquid sandal paste. Candana is sandalwood, drava is liquid or paste, digdha means smeared or anointed, and aṅga means limb. Thus Her body is adorned with sandal paste."],"searchText":"434 चन्दनद्रवदिग्धाङ्गी • चन्दनस्य द्रवेण दिग्धानि अङ्गानि यस्याः सा। • चन्दनस्य — of sandal paste. • द्रवेण — with liquid or paste. • दिग्धानि — anointed, smeared. • अङ्गानि — limbs. • चन्दनद्रवदिग्धाङ्गी — she whose limbs are anointed with liquid sandal paste. चन्दनद्रवदिग्धाङ्गी means one whose limbs are anointed with liquid sandal paste. candana is sandalwood, drava is liquid or paste, digdha means smeared or anointed, and aṅga means limb. thus her body is adorned with sandal paste. the cooling presence: sandal paste is cooling and soothing. her sandal-anointed limbs indicate a compassionate power that cools the heat and distress of worldly life.","esoteric":["The Cooling Presence: Sandal paste is cooling and soothing. Her sandal-anointed limbs indicate a compassionate power that cools the heat and distress of worldly life."]},{"number":435,"name":"चाम्पेयकुसुमप्रिया","samasa":["• चाम्पेयकुसुमं प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• चाम्पेयकुसुमं — campaka flower.","• प्रियं — dear, beloved.","• चाम्पेयकुसुमप्रिया — She who loves campaka flowers."],"summary":["चाम्पेयकुसुमप्रिया means one who loves champaka flowers. Campaka flowers are dear to Her, and She is adorned and worshipped with fragrant flower garlands that include campaka blossoms."],"searchText":"435 चाम्पेयकुसुमप्रिया • चाम्पेयकुसुमं प्रियं यस्याः सा। • चाम्पेयकुसुमं — campaka flower. • प्रियं — dear, beloved. • चाम्पेयकुसुमप्रिया — she who loves campaka flowers. चाम्पेयकुसुमप्रिया means one who loves champaka flowers. campaka flowers are dear to her, and she is adorned and worshipped with fragrant flower garlands that include campaka blossoms. the golden flower: the champaka flower is bright, fragrant and refined. offering it signifies devotion made fragrant and beautiful, pleasing her gracious nature.","esoteric":["The Golden Flower: The champaka flower is bright, fragrant and refined. Offering it signifies devotion made fragrant and beautiful, pleasing Her gracious nature."]},{"number":436,"name":"कुशला","samasa":["• सृष्ट्यादिनिर्माणकौशलवत्त्वात् कुशला।","• कुशं (जलं) लाति (आदत्ते) इति।","• कुत्सितः शलः (चन्द्रमा) यस्याः अग्रे इति।"],"wordByWord":["• सृष्ट्यादिनिर्माणकौशलवत्त्वात् — because She possesses skill in creation and the rest.","• कुशला — skilful, auspicious."],"summary":["कुशला means one who is skilful and auspicious. She possesses perfect skill in the creation, maintenance and ordering of the universe. Another interpretation takes kuśa as water and lā as taking or accepting, giving the sense of Kuśalā."],"searchText":"436 कुशला • सृष्ट्यादिनिर्माणकौशलवत्त्वात् कुशला। • कुशं (जलं) लाति (आदत्ते) इति। • कुत्सितः शलः (चन्द्रमा) यस्याः अग्रे इति। • सृष्ट्यादिनिर्माणकौशलवत्त्वात् — because she possesses skill in creation and the rest. • कुशला — skilful, auspicious. कुशला means one who is skilful and auspicious. she possesses perfect skill in the creation, maintenance and ordering of the universe. another interpretation takes kuśa as water and lā as taking or accepting, giving the sense of kuśalā. the perfect skill: she is kuśalā because her cosmic activity is carried out with flawless skill. creation, preservation and guidance proceed through her unfailing order.","esoteric":["The Perfect Skill: She is Kuśalā because Her cosmic activity is carried out with flawless skill. Creation, preservation and guidance proceed through Her unfailing order."]},{"number":437,"name":"कोमलाकारा","samasa":["• कोमलः आकारः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• कोमलः — soft, delicate.","• आकारः — form.","• कोमलाकारा — She who has a soft form."],"summary":["कोमलाकारा means one whose form is soft. Her form is tender, delicate and beautiful."],"searchText":"437 कोमलाकारा • कोमलः आकारः यस्याः सा। • कोमलः — soft, delicate. • आकारः — form. • कोमलाकारा — she who has a soft form. कोमलाकारा means one whose form is soft. her form is tender, delicate and beautiful. the gentle form: her form is soft and approachable for devotees. even while she holds supreme power, she appears with tenderness, beauty and maternal grace.","esoteric":["The Gentle Form: Her form is soft and approachable for devotees. Even while She holds supreme power, She appears with tenderness, beauty and maternal grace."]},{"number":438,"name":"कुरुकुल्ला","samasa":["• कुरुकुल्लाख्यदेवी। अहङ्कारचित्तमयप्राकारयोः मध्ये विमर्शमयवाप्याम् अधिकृता इत्यर्थः।"],"wordByWord":["• कुरुकुल्लाख्यदेवी — the goddess called Kurukullā.","• कुरुकुल्ला — She who has the form of Kurukullā."],"summary":["कुरुकुल्ला means one who has the form of the deity Kurukullā. In Śrī Nagara, between the enclosures of ahaṃkāra and citta, there is a well called Vimarśa. Kurukullā Devī is the presiding deity of that well."],"searchText":"438 कुरुकुल्ला • कुरुकुल्लाख्यदेवी। अहङ्कारचित्तमयप्राकारयोः मध्ये विमर्शमयवाप्याम् अधिकृता इत्यर्थः। • कुरुकुल्लाख्यदेवी — the goddess called kurukullā. • कुरुकुल्ला — she who has the form of kurukullā. कुरुकुल्ला means one who has the form of the deity kurukullā. in śrī nagara, between the enclosures of ahaṃkāra and citta, there is a well called vimarśa. kurukullā devī is the presiding deity of that well. the guardian of reflection: kurukullā presides over the vimarśa-vāpī, the well of reflective awareness between ahaṃkāra and citta. she governs the inward movement of thought toward the centre.","esoteric":["The Guardian of Reflection: Kurukullā presides over the Vimarśa-vāpī, the well of reflective awareness between ahaṃkāra and citta. She governs the inward movement of thought toward the centre."]},{"number":439,"name":"कुलेश्वरी","samasa":["• कुलस्य (सजातीयमातृमानमेयानां समूहस्य) ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["• कुलस्य — of the kula.","• ईश्वरी — ruler, mistress.","• कुलेश्वरी — She who is the ruler of the triad."],"summary":["कुलेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the triad. Kula here indicates the triad of the knower, the means of knowledge and the object known. She is the sovereign of this whole field of experience."],"searchText":"439 कुलेश्वरी • कुलस्य (सजातीयमातृमानमेयानां समूहस्य) ईश्वरी। • कुलस्य — of the kula. • ईश्वरी — ruler, mistress. • कुलेश्वरी — she who is the ruler of the triad. कुलेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the triad. kula here indicates the triad of the knower, the means of knowledge and the object known. she is the sovereign of this whole field of experience. the ruler of kula: kula is the triad of mātṛ, māna and meya: knower, knowing and known. she rules this complete structure of experience and illumines it from within.","esoteric":["The Ruler of Kula: Kula is the triad of mātṛ, māna and meya: knower, knowing and known. She rules this complete structure of experience and illumines it from within."]},{"number":440,"name":"कुलकुण्डालया ","samasa":["• कुलकुण्डम् (मूलाधारकर्णिकायां बिन्दुः) एव आलयः यस्याः सा। कुण्डलिनीत्यर्थः।"],"wordByWord":["• कुलकुण्डम् — the kula-kuṇḍa, the subtle centre at the mūlādhāra.","• मूलाधारकर्णिकायां — in the pericarp of the mūlādhāra.","• बिन्दुः — bindu, point.","• आलयः — abode.","• कुलकुण्डालया — She whose abode is the kula-kuṇḍa."],"summary":["कुलकुण्डालया means one whose abode is the kula-kuṇḍa. The kula-kuṇḍa is the subtle bindu in the pericarp of the mūlādhāra. She dwells there as Kuṇḍalinī."],"searchText":"440 कुलकुण्डालया  • कुलकुण्डम् (मूलाधारकर्णिकायां बिन्दुः) एव आलयः यस्याः सा। कुण्डलिनीत्यर्थः। • कुलकुण्डम् — the kula-kuṇḍa, the subtle centre at the mūlādhāra. • मूलाधारकर्णिकायां — in the pericarp of the mūlādhāra. • बिन्दुः — bindu, point. • आलयः — abode. • कुलकुण्डालया — she whose abode is the kula-kuṇḍa. कुलकुण्डालया means one whose abode is the kula-kuṇḍa. the kula-kuṇḍa is the subtle bindu in the pericarp of the mūlādhāra. she dwells there as kuṇḍalinī. the seat of kuṇḍalinī: the kula-kuṇḍa is the subtle centre in the four-petalled mūlādhāra. she resides there as kuṇḍalinī, the coiled power waiting to rise.","esoteric":["The Seat of Kuṇḍalinī: The kula-kuṇḍa is the subtle centre in the four-petalled mūlādhāra. She resides there as Kuṇḍalinī, the coiled power waiting to rise."]},{"number":441,"name":"कौलमार्गतत्परसेविता","samasa":["• कौलमार्गः। ◦ कुलसम्बन्धी कौलः (स्वस्ववंशपरम्पराप्राप्तः) मार्गः। ◦ तन्त्रोदितं कौलमार्गम्।","• तस्मिन् तत्परैः सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["• कौलमार्गः — the Kaula path.","• तस्मिन् — in that.","• तत्परैः — by those devoted to it.","• सेविता — served, worshipped.","• कौलमार्गतत्परसेविता — She who is served by those devoted to the Kaula path."],"summary":["कौलमार्गतत्परसेविता means one who is worshipped by those devoted to the Kaula path. Kaula-mārga is the path connected with kula and received through one’s lineage. She is served by those who are fully dedicated to that traditional mode of worship."],"searchText":"441 कौलमार्गतत्परसेविता • कौलमार्गः। ◦ कुलसम्बन्धी कौलः (स्वस्ववंशपरम्पराप्राप्तः) मार्गः। ◦ तन्त्रोदितं कौलमार्गम्। • तस्मिन् तत्परैः सेविता। • कौलमार्गः — the kaula path. • तस्मिन् — in that. • तत्परैः — by those devoted to it. • सेविता — served, worshipped. • कौलमार्गतत्परसेविता — she who is served by those devoted to the kaula path. कौलमार्गतत्परसेविता means one who is worshipped by those devoted to the kaula path. kaula-mārga is the path connected with kula and received through one’s lineage. she is served by those who are fully dedicated to that traditional mode of worship. the kaula path: kaula-mārga is a lineage path that sees no separation between the spiritual and the embodied. she is served by practitioners wholly intent on that path.","esoteric":["The Kaula Path: Kaula-mārga is a lineage path that sees no separation between the spiritual and the embodied. She is served by practitioners wholly intent on that path."]},{"number":442,"name":"कुमारगणनाथाम्बा","samasa":["• कुमारस्य गणनाथस्य च अम्बा।","• कुत्सितः मारगणः येषां तन्नाथान् अम्बते (बध्नाति) इति।"],"wordByWord":["• कुमारस्य — of Kumāra.","• गणनाथस्य — of Gaṇanātha.","• अम्बा — mother.","• कुमारगणनाथाम्बा — the mother of Kumāra and Gaṇanātha."],"summary":["कुमारगणनाथाम्बा means the mother of Kumāra and Gaṇanātha. She is the mother of Kumāra, also known as Kārttikeya, and of Gaṇanātha, Gaṇapati. Another interpretation is that She binds or restrains those whose impulses are impure."],"searchText":"442 कुमारगणनाथाम्बा • कुमारस्य गणनाथस्य च अम्बा। • कुत्सितः मारगणः येषां तन्नाथान् अम्बते (बध्नाति) इति। • कुमारस्य — of kumāra. • गणनाथस्य — of gaṇanātha. • अम्बा — mother. • कुमारगणनाथाम्बा — the mother of kumāra and gaṇanātha. कुमारगणनाथाम्बा means the mother of kumāra and gaṇanātha. she is the mother of kumāra, also known as kārttikeya, and of gaṇanātha, gaṇapati. another interpretation is that she binds or restrains those whose impulses are impure. the mother of divine powers: as mother of kumāra and gaṇanātha, she gives rise to dynamic action and obstacle-removing intelligence. she also restrains harmful impulses and turns the seeker inward.","esoteric":["The Mother of Divine Powers: As mother of Kumāra and Gaṇanātha, She gives rise to dynamic action and obstacle-removing intelligence. She also restrains harmful impulses and turns the seeker inward."]},{"number":443,"name":"तुष्टिः","samasa":["• सन्तोषरूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• सन्तोषरूपिणी — having the form of contentment.","• तुष्टिः — She who has the form of contentment."],"summary":["तुष्टिः means one who has the form of contentment. Tuṣṭi is satisfaction and contentment. Śrīdevī is praised as contentment, nourishment, wisdom, fortitude, tranquillity, benevolence and beauty. Whoever possesses these qualities may be understood to have received Her special blessing."],"searchText":"443 तुष्टिः • सन्तोषरूपिणी। • सन्तोषरूपिणी — having the form of contentment. • तुष्टिः — she who has the form of contentment. तुष्टिः means one who has the form of contentment. tuṣṭi is satisfaction and contentment. śrīdevī is praised as contentment, nourishment, wisdom, fortitude, tranquillity, benevolence and beauty. whoever possesses these qualities may be understood to have received her special blessing. the form of contentment: she is santoṣarūpiṇī, the energy of true satisfaction. contentment does not depend on finite objects; it arises as her presence in a peaceful mind.","esoteric":["The Form of Contentment: She is santoṣarūpiṇī, the energy of true satisfaction. Contentment does not depend on finite objects; it arises as Her presence in a peaceful mind."]},{"number":444,"name":"पुष्टिः","samasa":["• पोषणकारिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• पोषणकारिणी — one who nourishes.","• पुष्टिः — She who is complete."],"summary":["पुष्टिः means one who is complete and nourishing. Her form is full of thrivingness, nourishment, plenty and completeness in all limbs and constituent parts of the body. This name is to be understood with the preceding name."],"searchText":"444 पुष्टिः • पोषणकारिणी। • पोषणकारिणी — one who nourishes. • पुष्टिः — she who is complete. पुष्टिः means one who is complete and nourishing. her form is full of thrivingness, nourishment, plenty and completeness in all limbs and constituent parts of the body. this name is to be understood with the preceding name. the nourishing principle: she is poṣaṇakāriṇī, the power that nourishes and sustains. she supports physical life, inner strength and spiritual growth.","esoteric":["The Nourishing Principle: She is poṣaṇakāriṇī, the power that nourishes and sustains. She supports physical life, inner strength and spiritual growth."]},{"number":445,"name":"मतिः","samasa":["• बुद्धिरूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• बुद्धिरूपिणी — having the form of intellect.","• मतिः — She who has the form of intellect."],"summary":["मतिः means one who has the form of intellect. Mati is understanding, thought and discernment. She is the faculty by which the mind grasps meaning and turns toward truth."],"searchText":"445 मतिः • बुद्धिरूपिणी। • बुद्धिरूपिणी — having the form of intellect. • मतिः — she who has the form of intellect. मतिः means one who has the form of intellect. mati is understanding, thought and discernment. she is the faculty by which the mind grasps meaning and turns toward truth. the discerning intellect: she manifests as buddhirūpiṇī, the inner faculty of clear understanding. through her, thought becomes capable of discrimination and right direction.","esoteric":["The Discerning Intellect: She manifests as buddhirūpiṇī, the inner faculty of clear understanding. Through Her, thought becomes capable of discrimination and right direction."]},{"number":446,"name":"धृतिः","samasa":["• धैर्यरूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• धैर्यरूपिणी — having the form of firmness or fortitude.","• धृतिः — She who is fortitude"],"summary":["धृतिः means one who is fortitude. Dhṛti indicates boldness, firmness and steadiness. It is the power of remaining firm and enduring without collapse."],"searchText":"446 धृतिः • धैर्यरूपिणी। • धैर्यरूपिणी — having the form of firmness or fortitude. • धृतिः — she who is fortitude धृतिः means one who is fortitude. dhṛti indicates boldness, firmness and steadiness. it is the power of remaining firm and enduring without collapse. unshakable endurance: she is dhairyarūpiṇī, the inner strength that holds the mind steady. through her, courage and firmness remain even amid difficulty.","esoteric":["Unshakable Endurance: She is dhairyarūpiṇī, the inner strength that holds the mind steady. Through Her, courage and firmness remain even amid difficulty."]},{"number":447,"name":"शान्तिः","samasa":["• शान्तिरूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• शान्तिरूपिणी — having the form of peace.","• शान्तिः — She who is in the form of tranquillity."],"summary":["शान्तिः means one who is in the form of tranquillity. Śānti is peace, control and the quieting of agitation. It is the release of the organs from attachment to worldly affairs and the resulting peace of mind."],"searchText":"447 शान्तिः • शान्तिरूपिणी। • शान्तिरूपिणी — having the form of peace. • शान्तिः — she who is in the form of tranquillity. शान्तिः means one who is in the form of tranquillity. śānti is peace, control and the quieting of agitation. it is the release of the organs from attachment to worldly affairs and the resulting peace of mind. the still mind: she is śāntirūpiṇī, the state in which agitation and mental disturbance become quiet. her presence is known as deep peace and inward rest.","esoteric":["The Still Mind: She is śāntirūpiṇī, the state in which agitation and mental disturbance become quiet. Her presence is known as deep peace and inward rest."]},{"number":448,"name":"स्वस्तिमती","samasa":["• सुष्ठु अस्तिः (सत्ता) तद्वती।","• सत्यस्य सत्यम्।"],"wordByWord":["• स्वस्तिमती — She who is in the form of eternal truth and auspiciousness."],"summary":["स्वस्तिमती means one who is in the form of eternal truth and auspiciousness. Suṣṭhu means properly or beautifully, and sattā means existence. One who possesses this pure existence is Svastimatī. Svasti also means immortality, benediction, welfare, holiness and auspiciousness."],"searchText":"448 स्वस्तिमती • सुष्ठु अस्तिः (सत्ता) तद्वती। • सत्यस्य सत्यम्। • स्वस्तिमती — she who is in the form of eternal truth and auspiciousness. स्वस्तिमती means one who is in the form of eternal truth and auspiciousness. suṣṭhu means properly or beautifully, and sattā means existence. one who possesses this pure existence is svastimatī. svasti also means immortality, benediction, welfare, holiness and auspiciousness. the auspicious existence: svasti points to pure, auspicious being. she possesses unbroken sattā, the ground of existence that gives welfare, blessing and immortality.","esoteric":["The Auspicious Existence: Svasti points to pure, auspicious being. She possesses unbroken sattā, the ground of existence that gives welfare, blessing and immortality."]},{"number":449,"name":"कान्तिः","samasa":["• देदीप्यमाना।","• इच्छाशक्तिः।"],"wordByWord":["• देदीप्यमाना — shining brightly.","• कान्तिः — She who is radiance."],"summary":["कान्तिः means one who is radiance. The sun, moon and other lights shine because of the effulgence of the Supreme Being. Kānti also indicates icchāśakti, the power of divine will."],"searchText":"449 कान्तिः • देदीप्यमाना। • इच्छाशक्तिः। • देदीप्यमाना — shining brightly. • कान्तिः — she who is radiance. कान्तिः means one who is radiance. the sun, moon and other lights shine because of the effulgence of the supreme being. kānti also indicates icchāśakti, the power of divine will. the luminous will: she is radiant light and icchāśakti, the primal will behind manifestation. her brilliance is the light by which all other lights shine.","esoteric":["The Luminous Will: She is radiant light and icchāśakti, the primal will behind manifestation. Her brilliance is the light by which all other lights shine."]},{"number":450,"name":"नन्दिनी","samasa":["• नन्दयितृत्वात्।","• नन्दस्य पुत्री।","• कामधेनुवंशोद्भवा गोविशेषः।","• गङ्गास्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["• नन्दयितृत्वात् — because She causes joy.","• नन्दिनी — She who causes joy."],"summary":["नन्दिनी means one who causes joy. Nandinī is also a cow born in the lineage of Kāmadhenu, and She is also in the form of the river Gaṅgā."],"searchText":"450 नन्दिनी • नन्दयितृत्वात्। • नन्दस्य पुत्री। • कामधेनुवंशोद्भवा गोविशेषः। • गङ्गास्वरूपा। • नन्दयितृत्वात् — because she causes joy. • नन्दिनी — she who causes joy. नन्दिनी means one who causes joy. nandinī is also a cow born in the lineage of kāmadhenu, and she is also in the form of the river gaṅgā. the cause of joy: she delights and gladdens beings. as nandinī, she is associated with nourishing abundance and the purifying flow of gaṅgā.","esoteric":["The Cause of Joy: She delights and gladdens beings. As Nandinī, She is associated with nourishing abundance and the purifying flow of Gaṅgā."]},{"number":451,"name":"विघ्ननाशिनी","samasa":["• विशेषेण घ्नन्तीति विघ्नाः। तान्नाशयितुं शीलम् अस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["• विघ्नाः — obstacles.","• विघ्ननाशिनी — She who removes obstacles."],"summary":["विघ्ननाशिनी means one who destroys obstacles. She removes all obstacles in Śrīvidyā upāsanā. She is in the form of Mahāgaṇapati, who destroys obstacles; therefore Gaṇapati is worshipped at the beginning of all activities."],"searchText":"451 विघ्ननाशिनी • विशेषेण घ्नन्तीति विघ्नाः। तान्नाशयितुं शीलम् अस्याः। • विघ्नाः — obstacles. • विघ्ननाशिनी — she who removes obstacles. विघ्ननाशिनी means one who destroys obstacles. she removes all obstacles in śrīvidyā upāsanā. she is in the form of mahāgaṇapati, who destroys obstacles; therefore gaṇapati is worshipped at the beginning of all activities. the clearance of blockages: in practice, obstacles include laziness, doubt, distraction and disease. as vighnanāśinī, she dissolves these blockages and opens the path for the practitioner.","esoteric":["The Clearance of Blockages: In practice, obstacles include laziness, doubt, distraction and disease. As Vighnanāśinī, She dissolves these blockages and opens the path for the practitioner."]},{"number":452,"name":"तेजोवती","samasa":["• तेजसाम् आदित्यादीनाम् आधारभूतत्वात्।"],"wordByWord":["• तेजसाम् — of lights, splendours.","• आधारभूतत्वात् — because she is the support.","• तेजोवती — She who has splendor."],"summary":["तेजोवती means one who has splendour. She is the support of all lights and radiance, including the sun, moon and fire."],"searchText":"452 तेजोवती • तेजसाम् आदित्यादीनाम् आधारभूतत्वात्। • तेजसाम् — of lights, splendours. • आधारभूतत्वात् — because she is the support. • तेजोवती — she who has splendor. तेजोवती means one who has splendour. she is the support of all lights and radiance, including the sun, moon and fire. the support of light: she is the basis of all brilliance. the power of the sun, moon and fire to shine is an expression of her splendour.","esoteric":["The Support of Light: She is the basis of all brilliance. The power of the sun, moon and fire to shine is an expression of Her splendour."]},{"number":453,"name":"त्रिनयना","samasa":["• त्रीणि सोमसूर्याग्निरूपाणि नयनानि यस्याः सा।","• वौषट् इति शब्दस्य संज्ञा त्रिनयना। तद्रूपा।","• त्रीणि प्रमाणानि नयति (प्रापयति) इति।","• त्रीणि प्रत्यक्षानुमानशब्दरूपाणि प्रमाणानि यस्याः सा।","• त्रीन् मार्गान् (दक्षिणोत्तरब्रह्ममार्गान्) प्रति अधिकारिणः नयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• त्रीणि — three.","• सोमसूर्याग्निरूपाणि — in the forms of moon, sun and fire.","• नयनानि — eyes.","• त्रिनयना — She who has three eyes."],"summary":["त्रिनयना means one who has three eyes. Her three eyes are in the forms of the moon, sun and fire. The name is also connected with the three means of knowledge: pratyakṣa, anumāna and śabda. She leads qualified devotees through the three paths called dakṣiṇa, uttara and brahma."],"searchText":"453 त्रिनयना • त्रीणि सोमसूर्याग्निरूपाणि नयनानि यस्याः सा। • वौषट् इति शब्दस्य संज्ञा त्रिनयना। तद्रूपा। • त्रीणि प्रमाणानि नयति (प्रापयति) इति। • त्रीणि प्रत्यक्षानुमानशब्दरूपाणि प्रमाणानि यस्याः सा। • त्रीन् मार्गान् (दक्षिणोत्तरब्रह्ममार्गान्) प्रति अधिकारिणः नयतीति। • त्रीणि — three. • सोमसूर्याग्निरूपाणि — in the forms of moon, sun and fire. • नयनानि — eyes. • त्रिनयना — she who has three eyes. त्रिनयना means one who has three eyes. her three eyes are in the forms of the moon, sun and fire. the name is also connected with the three means of knowledge: pratyakṣa, anumāna and śabda. she leads qualified devotees through the three paths called dakṣiṇa, uttara and brahma. the three eyes: her eyes are moon, sun and fire, illumining time and experience. she also governs pratyakṣa, anumāna and śabda, and guides seekers through the appropriate spiritual path.","esoteric":["The Three Eyes: Her eyes are moon, sun and fire, illumining time and experience. She also governs pratyakṣa, anumāna and śabda, and guides seekers through the appropriate spiritual path."]},{"number":454,"name":"लोलाक्षीकामरूपिणी","samasa":["• लोलाक्षीणां (स्त्रीणां) यः कामः तद्रूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• कामः — desire.","• तद्रूपिणी — having that form.","• लोलाक्षीकामरूपिणी — She who is in the form of the desire of beautiful-eyed women."],"summary":["लोलाक्षीकामरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the desire of beautiful-eyed women. She is in the form of Yogeśvarī, the deity connected with desire. Some traditions split this as two names, Lolākṣī and Kāmarūpiṇī."],"searchText":"454 लोलाक्षीकामरूपिणी • लोलाक्षीणां (स्त्रीणां) यः कामः तद्रूपिणी। • कामः — desire. • तद्रूपिणी — having that form. • लोलाक्षीकामरूपिणी — she who is in the form of the desire of beautiful-eyed women. लोलाक्षीकामरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the desire of beautiful-eyed women. she is in the form of yogeśvarī, the deity connected with desire. some traditions split this as two names, lolākṣī and kāmarūpiṇī. the power of desire: she is the force of attraction, beauty and love. desire, when turned inward and purified, becomes a movement toward the divine.","esoteric":["The Power of Desire: She is the force of attraction, beauty and love. Desire, when turned inward and purified, becomes a movement toward the divine."]},{"number":455,"name":"मालिनी","samasa":["• मालावत्त्वात्।"],"wordByWord":["• मालिनी — She who wears a garland; also a metrical name."],"summary":["मालिनी means one who wears a garland. Mālinī is also the name of a metre of fifteen letters. It is also used for a florist woman, the city of Campā, Gaurī and the river Gaṅgā. Mālinī is also described as a girl of seven years."],"searchText":"455 मालिनी • मालावत्त्वात्। • मालिनी — she who wears a garland; also a metrical name. मालिनी means one who wears a garland. mālinī is also the name of a metre of fifteen letters. it is also used for a florist woman, the city of campā, gaurī and the river gaṅgā. mālinī is also described as a girl of seven years. the garland of letters: her garland is the varṇamālā, the sequence of sacred letters from a to kṣa. as mālinī, she wears the sound-structure through which mantra and expression arise.","esoteric":["The Garland of Letters: Her garland is the varṇamālā, the sequence of sacred letters from a to kṣa. As Mālinī, She wears the sound-structure through which mantra and expression arise."]},{"number":456,"name":"हंसिनी","samasa":["• हंसाः (यतिविशेषाः) अस्याम् अभेदेन सन्तीति।","• हंस इति अजपामन्त्रः। तद्रूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• हंसाः — haṃsas, swans or ascetics.","• अजपामन्त्रः — the ajapā mantra.","• तद्रूपिणी — having that form.","• हंसिनी — She who is in the form of haṃsa or the ajapā mantra."],"summary":["हंसिनी means one who is in the form of haṃsa. Haṃsa can refer to great ascetics called paramahaṃsas, who meditate on Her. The movement of inhalation and exhalation is called the haṃsa mantra or ajapā mantra. Since this mantra is connected with Śrīdevī, She is Haṃsinī."],"searchText":"456 हंसिनी • हंसाः (यतिविशेषाः) अस्याम् अभेदेन सन्तीति। • हंस इति अजपामन्त्रः। तद्रूपिणी। • हंसाः — haṃsas, swans or ascetics. • अजपामन्त्रः — the ajapā mantra. • तद्रूपिणी — having that form. • हंसिनी — she who is in the form of haṃsa or the ajapā mantra. हंसिनी means one who is in the form of haṃsa. haṃsa can refer to great ascetics called paramahaṃsas, who meditate on her. the movement of inhalation and exhalation is called the haṃsa mantra or ajapā mantra. since this mantra is connected with śrīdevī, she is haṃsinī. the ajapā mantra: haṃsa is the natural mantra of the breath, haṃ with exhalation and sa with inhalation. she is present in this unuttered mantra that moves through life itself.","esoteric":["The Ajapā Mantra: Haṃsa is the natural mantra of the breath, haṃ with exhalation and sa with inhalation. She is present in this unuttered mantra that moves through life itself."]},{"number":457,"name":"माता","samasa":["• सर्वजनयितृत्वात्।"],"wordByWord":["• माता — mother.","• सर्वजनयितृत्वात् — because She gives birth to all."],"summary":["माता means mother. Śrīdevī is in the form of the mother. All mantras originate from Her, and She is the motherly origin of beings. The presiding deity of certain lunar days is also called Nityā, whose mantra has the cryptic name Mātā."],"searchText":"457 माता • सर्वजनयितृत्वात्। • माता — mother. • सर्वजनयितृत्वात् — because she gives birth to all. माता means mother. śrīdevī is in the form of the mother. all mantras originate from her, and she is the motherly origin of beings. the presiding deity of certain lunar days is also called nityā, whose mantra has the cryptic name mātā. the primordial mother: she is the universal mother from whom beings arise. as mātā, she gives refuge, nourishment and protection to all.","esoteric":["The Primordial Mother: She is the universal mother from whom beings arise. As Mātā, She gives refuge, nourishment and protection to all."]},{"number":458,"name":"मलयाचलवासिनी","samasa":["• मलयाचले वसतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• मलयाचले — on the Malaya mountain.","• वसतीति — dwells.","• मलयाचलवासिनी — She who resides on the Malaya mountain."],"summary":["मलयाचलवासिनी means one who resides on the Malaya mountain. The Malaya mountain is associated with Kerala and with fragrant sandalwood groves. She is worshipped as the deity dwelling there."],"searchText":"458 मलयाचलवासिनी • मलयाचले वसतीति। • मलयाचले — on the malaya mountain. • वसतीति — dwells. • मलयाचलवासिनी — she who resides on the malaya mountain. मलयाचलवासिनी means one who resides on the malaya mountain. the malaya mountain is associated with kerala and with fragrant sandalwood groves. she is worshipped as the deity dwelling there. the fragrant mountain: malaya is known for sandalwood. her dwelling there suggests cooling grace, spiritual fragrance and purity that soothe the heat of worldly tendencies.","esoteric":["The Fragrant Mountain: Malaya is known for sandalwood. Her dwelling there suggests cooling grace, spiritual fragrance and purity that soothe the heat of worldly tendencies."]},{"number":459,"name":"सुमुखी","samasa":["• शोभनं मुखं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• शोभनं — beautiful, auspicious.","• मुखं — face.","• सुमुखी — She who has a beautiful face."],"summary":["सुमुखी means one who has a beautiful face. Sumukhī is also a metre in music. The name indicates Her auspicious and handsome countenance, full of grace and beauty."],"searchText":"459 सुमुखी • शोभनं मुखं यस्याः सा। • शोभनं — beautiful, auspicious. • मुखं — face. • सुमुखी — she who has a beautiful face. सुमुखी means one who has a beautiful face. sumukhī is also a metre in music. the name indicates her auspicious and handsome countenance, full of grace and beauty. the welcoming face: her face is beautiful, auspicious and benevolent. she appears to devotees with a countenance that encourages approach and devotion.","esoteric":["The Welcoming Face: Her face is beautiful, auspicious and benevolent. She appears to devotees with a countenance that encourages approach and devotion."]},{"number":460,"name":"नलिनी","samasa":["• करचरणमुखनेत्राद्यवयवानां कमलरूपत्वात्।","• भागीरथीरूपत्वात्। नन्दिनी नलिनी गङ्गेति तदीयद्वादशनामसु गणनात्।","• नलः राजा यस्याम् उपासनया तादात्म्येन निविष्टः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• कमलरूपत्वात् — because of having lotus-like form.","• नलिनी — She who is like a lotus flower."],"summary":["नलिनी means one who is like a lotus flower. Her hands, feet, face, eyes and other limbs are like lotuses; therefore Śrīdevī Herself is described as a lotus. Nalinī is also one of the names of the river Gaṅgā. Nala, a king, is also connected with this name through devotion."],"searchText":"460 नलिनी • करचरणमुखनेत्राद्यवयवानां कमलरूपत्वात्। • भागीरथीरूपत्वात्। नन्दिनी नलिनी गङ्गेति तदीयद्वादशनामसु गणनात्। • नलः राजा यस्याम् उपासनया तादात्म्येन निविष्टः सा। • कमलरूपत्वात् — because of having lotus-like form. • नलिनी — she who is like a lotus flower. नलिनी means one who is like a lotus flower. her hands, feet, face, eyes and other limbs are like lotuses; therefore śrīdevī herself is described as a lotus. nalinī is also one of the names of the river gaṅgā. nala, a king, is also connected with this name through devotion. the lotus form: her hands, feet, face and eyes have the beauty of blossomed lotuses. as nalinī, she is also linked with the purifying flow of gaṅgā.","esoteric":["The Lotus Form: Her hands, feet, face and eyes have the beauty of blossomed lotuses. As Nalinī, She is also linked with the purifying flow of Gaṅgā."]},{"number":461,"name":"सुभ्रूः","samasa":["• शोभने भ्रुवौ यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• भ्रुवौ — eyebrows.","• सुभ्रूः — She who has beautiful eyebrows."],"summary":["सुभ्रूः means one who has beautiful eyebrows. Her eyebrows are praised for their beauty. In the time taken for Her eyebrows to rise and fall, many four-yuga cycles may pass."],"searchText":"461 सुभ्रूः • शोभने भ्रुवौ यस्याः सा। • भ्रुवौ — eyebrows. • सुभ्रूः — she who has beautiful eyebrows. सुभ्रूः means one who has beautiful eyebrows. her eyebrows are praised for their beauty. in the time taken for her eyebrows to rise and fall, many four-yuga cycles may pass. the brows of command: her eyebrows indicate subtle command and direction. a mere movement of her glance can set vast cycles of time and cosmic order in motion.","esoteric":["The Brows of Command: Her eyebrows indicate subtle command and direction. A mere movement of Her glance can set vast cycles of time and cosmic order in motion."]},{"number":462,"name":"शोभना","samasa":["• सौन्दर्यशीलत्वात्।"],"wordByWord":["• सौन्दर्यशीलत्वात् — because of the nature of beauty.","• शोभना — She who is all radiant with beauty."],"summary":["शोभना means one who is radiant with beauty. Her nature is beauty and auspicious splendour."],"searchText":"462 शोभना • सौन्दर्यशीलत्वात्। • सौन्दर्यशीलत्वात् — because of the nature of beauty. • शोभना — she who is all radiant with beauty. शोभना means one who is radiant with beauty. her nature is beauty and auspicious splendour. the quality of beauty: she is śobhanā because beauty belongs to her nature. her presence turns existence toward harmony, grace and auspiciousness.","esoteric":["The Quality of Beauty: She is Śobhanā because beauty belongs to Her nature. Her presence turns existence toward harmony, grace and auspiciousness."]},{"number":463,"name":"सुरनायिका","samasa":["• सुराणां नायिकेश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["• सुरनायिका — She who is the leader of the devas."],"summary":["सुरनायिका means one who is the leader of the devas. She is the supreme power and ruler of the devas, guiding the divine forces."],"searchText":"463 सुरनायिका • सुराणां नायिकेश्वरी। • सुरनायिका — she who is the leader of the devas. सुरनायिका means one who is the leader of the devas. she is the supreme power and ruler of the devas, guiding the divine forces. the leader of the devas: the devas represent powers of light, order and dharma. she is their nāyikā, the sovereign force that guides and empowers them.","esoteric":["The Leader of the Devas: The devas represent powers of light, order and dharma. She is their nāyikā, the sovereign force that guides and empowers them."]},{"number":464,"name":"कालकण्ठी","samasa":["• कालः कण्ठो यस्य ईश्वरस्य तस्य स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["• कालः — dark, black, time.","• कालकण्ठी — She who is the consort of Kālakaṇṭha; She whose throat has a soft tone."],"summary":["कालकण्ठी means one who is the consort of Kālakaṇṭha. Kāla can mean dark, black or time, and kaṇṭha means throat. Another interpretation is that a soft, low sound proceeds from Her throat, showing the sweetness of Her voice."],"searchText":"464 कालकण्ठी • कालः कण्ठो यस्य ईश्वरस्य तस्य स्त्री। • कालः — dark, black, time. • कालकण्ठी — she who is the consort of kālakaṇṭha; she whose throat has a soft tone. कालकण्ठी means one who is the consort of kālakaṇṭha. kāla can mean dark, black or time, and kaṇṭha means throat. another interpretation is that a soft, low sound proceeds from her throat, showing the sweetness of her voice. the dark-throated power: she is united with kālakaṇṭha, the dark-throated śiva. she is also the sweetness and subtle resonance of divine speech arising from the throat.","esoteric":["The Dark-Throated Power: She is united with Kālakaṇṭha, the dark-throated Śiva. She is also the sweetness and subtle resonance of divine speech arising from the throat."]},{"number":465,"name":"कान्तिमती","samasa":["• कान्तिः अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["• कान्तिः — lustre, beauty.","• कान्तिमती — the name understood through the samasa above."],"summary":["कान्तिमती means one who possesses radiance. This name continues the meaning of Kānti, indicating splendour, beauty and shining presence."],"searchText":"465 कान्तिमती • कान्तिः अस्याः अस्तीति। • कान्तिः — lustre, beauty. • कान्तिमती — the name understood through the samasa above. कान्तिमती means one who possesses radiance. this name continues the meaning of kānti, indicating splendour, beauty and shining presence. the inherent glow: she possesses lasting beauty and lustre. her radiance draws the devotee inward with warmth and auspicious brilliance.","esoteric":["The Inherent Glow: She possesses lasting beauty and lustre. Her radiance draws the devotee inward with warmth and auspicious brilliance."]},{"number":466,"name":"क्षोभिणी","samasa":["• परमेश्वरौ सृष्ट्यौन्मुख्येन क्षोभयतीति।","• मनः क्षोभात् कांश्चिद् गणानजनयद् इति।"],"wordByWord":["• क्षोभिणी — She who stirs or agitates."],"summary":["क्षोभिणी means one who stirs or agitates. She stirs Parameśvara toward creation and causes movement in what is otherwise still. She also gives rise to certain gaṇas through the stirring of Her mind."],"searchText":"466 क्षोभिणी • परमेश्वरौ सृष्ट्यौन्मुख्येन क्षोभयतीति। • मनः क्षोभात् कांश्चिद् गणानजनयद् इति। • क्षोभिणी — she who stirs or agitates. क्षोभिणी means one who stirs or agitates. she stirs parameśvara toward creation and causes movement in what is otherwise still. she also gives rise to certain gaṇas through the stirring of her mind. the stirring power: before manifestation there is stillness. as kṣobhiṇī, she introduces the movement by which creation begins and latent powers become active.","esoteric":["The Stirring Power: Before manifestation there is stillness. As Kṣobhiṇī, She introduces the movement by which creation begins and latent powers become active."]},{"number":467,"name":"सूक्ष्मरूपिणी","samasa":["• सूक्ष्मं रूपम् अस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["• सूक्ष्मं — subtle.","• रूपम् — form.","• सूक्ष्मरूपिणी — She whose form is subtle."],"summary":["सूक्ष्मरूपिणी means one whose form is very subtle and not easily recognized. Her gross, subtle and subtler forms are distinguished, and here the subtle form is indicated. Since She has no ordinary material cause like sound and the rest, She is subtle."],"searchText":"467 सूक्ष्मरूपिणी • सूक्ष्मं रूपम् अस्याः इति। • सूक्ष्मं — subtle. • रूपम् — form. • सूक्ष्मरूपिणी — she whose form is subtle. सूक्ष्मरूपिणी means one whose form is very subtle and not easily recognized. her gross, subtle and subtler forms are distinguished, and here the subtle form is indicated. since she has no ordinary material cause like sound and the rest, she is subtle. the subtle form: beyond gross visible form, she is subtle presence. she is known through refined awareness, inner vibration and the subtle current of kuṇḍalinī.","esoteric":["The Subtle Form: Beyond gross visible form, She is subtle presence. She is known through refined awareness, inner vibration and the subtle current of Kuṇḍalinī."]},{"number":468,"name":"वज्रेश्वरी","samasa":["• षष्ठीतिथिनित्या जालन्धरपीठाधिष्ठात्री।","• वज्राख्यानद्याः अधिपतिः।"],"wordByWord":["• वज्रेश्वरी — the deity Vajreśvarī."],"summary":["वज्रेश्वरी means one who is Vajreśvarī. Vajreśvarī is the presiding deity of the sixth day of the bright lunar fortnight and the tenth day of the dark lunar fortnight. She is also connected with Jālandhara Pīṭha and with the vajra."],"searchText":"468 वज्रेश्वरी • षष्ठीतिथिनित्या जालन्धरपीठाधिष्ठात्री। • वज्राख्यानद्याः अधिपतिः। • वज्रेश्वरी — the deity vajreśvarī. वज्रेश्वरी means one who is vajreśvarī. vajreśvarī is the presiding deity of the sixth day of the bright lunar fortnight and the tenth day of the dark lunar fortnight. she is also connected with jālandhara pīṭha and with the vajra. the vajra power: vajreśvarī is diamond-like strength and protection. her energy is firm, brilliant and difficult for hostile forces to penetrate.","esoteric":["The Vajra Power: Vajreśvarī is diamond-like strength and protection. Her energy is firm, brilliant and difficult for hostile forces to penetrate."]},{"number":469,"name":"वामदेवी","samasa":["• वामः वननीयः देवः वामदेवः। तस्य स्त्री।","• वामा (सुन्दरी) च सा देवी च।","• वामानां (कर्मफलानां) देवी।"],"wordByWord":["• वामः — beautiful, worthy of worship, or the fruits of action.","• वामदेवः — Vāmadeva.","• वामदेवी — She who is Vāmadevī."],"summary":["वामदेवी means one who is Vāmadevī. Vāma can mean worthy of worship, beautiful, the left side, or the fruits of actions. She is the consort or power of Vāmadeva, the beautiful Devī, the deity presiding over the fruits of actions, and the goddess of those devoted to the vāma path."],"searchText":"469 वामदेवी • वामः वननीयः देवः वामदेवः। तस्य स्त्री। • वामा (सुन्दरी) च सा देवी च। • वामानां (कर्मफलानां) देवी। • वामः — beautiful, worthy of worship, or the fruits of action. • वामदेवः — vāmadeva. • वामदेवी — she who is vāmadevī. वामदेवी means one who is vāmadevī. vāma can mean worthy of worship, beautiful, the left side, or the fruits of actions. she is the consort or power of vāmadeva, the beautiful devī, the deity presiding over the fruits of actions, and the goddess of those devoted to the vāma path. the vāma power: she is the beautiful and worshipful power of vāmadeva. as the deity of karmic fruits, she measures and assigns the consequences of actions.","esoteric":["The Vāma Power: She is the beautiful and worshipful power of Vāmadeva. As the deity of karmic fruits, She measures and assigns the consequences of actions."]},{"number":470,"name":"वयोवस्थाविवर्जिता","samasa":["• वयोविशेषाणामवस्थाभिः विवर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["• विवर्जिता — free from.","• वयोवस्थाविवर्जिता — She who is devoid of old age and other changes."],"summary":["वयोवस्थाविवर्जिता means one who is free from the states of age. She is devoid of old age and other changes. Being eternal, She is untouched by the stages of life such as childhood, youth and old age."],"searchText":"470 वयोवस्थाविवर्जिता • वयोविशेषाणामवस्थाभिः विवर्जिता। • विवर्जिता — free from. • वयोवस्थाविवर्जिता — she who is devoid of old age and other changes. वयोवस्थाविवर्जिता means one who is free from the states of age. she is devoid of old age and other changes. being eternal, she is untouched by the stages of life such as childhood, youth and old age. beyond age: bodies pass through birth, growth, youth, decline and death. her true form is eternal consciousness, untouched by these changes.","esoteric":["Beyond Age: Bodies pass through birth, growth, youth, decline and death. Her true form is eternal consciousness, untouched by these changes."]},{"number":471,"name":"सिद्धेश्वरी","samasa":["• सिद्धानाम् ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["• सिद्धानाम् — of siddhas.","• ईश्वरी — ruler, mistress.","• सिद्धेश्वरी — She who is the goddess of siddhas."],"summary":["सिद्धेश्वरी means one who is the goddess of siddhas, the spiritual adepts. Siddhas are those who have gained powers such as aṇimā and mahimā through worship and discipline. Such powers are meant as aids for controlling the mind, doing penance and attaining self-knowledge, not for worldly use. She is the queen of such siddhas."],"searchText":"471 सिद्धेश्वरी • सिद्धानाम् ईश्वरी। • सिद्धानाम् — of siddhas. • ईश्वरी — ruler, mistress. • सिद्धेश्वरी — she who is the goddess of siddhas. सिद्धेश्वरी means one who is the goddess of siddhas, the spiritual adepts. siddhas are those who have gained powers such as aṇimā and mahimā through worship and discipline. such powers are meant as aids for controlling the mind, doing penance and attaining self-knowledge, not for worldly use. she is the queen of such siddhas. the mistress of siddhas: a siddha is an adept who has mastered inner powers and uses them for self-knowledge. she is their ruler and the power behind their attainment.","esoteric":["The Mistress of Siddhas: A siddha is an adept who has mastered inner powers and uses them for self-knowledge. She is their ruler and the power behind their attainment."]},{"number":472,"name":"सिद्धविद्या","samasa":["• सिद्धा च सा विद्या च।"],"wordByWord":["• सिद्धा — perfected, accomplished.","• विद्या — knowledge, sacred wisdom.","• सिद्धविद्या — She who is the perfected vidyā."],"summary":["सिद्धविद्या means one who is the perfected vidyā. A mantra protects the one who chants it; when the presiding deity is female, it is called vidyā. Some mantras need examination for suitability, but certain mantras give results at all times. Śrīdevī is in the form of Siddhavidyā, the accomplished vidyā that grants its fruits."],"searchText":"472 सिद्धविद्या • सिद्धा च सा विद्या च। • सिद्धा — perfected, accomplished. • विद्या — knowledge, sacred wisdom. • सिद्धविद्या — she who is the perfected vidyā. सिद्धविद्या means one who is the perfected vidyā. a mantra protects the one who chants it; when the presiding deity is female, it is called vidyā. some mantras need examination for suitability, but certain mantras give results at all times. śrīdevī is in the form of siddhavidyā, the accomplished vidyā that grants its fruits. the proven vidyā: her mantra is siddha, inherently accomplished and potent. when properly received and practiced, it bears fruit without uncertainty.","esoteric":["The Proven Vidyā: Her mantra is siddha, inherently accomplished and potent. When properly received and practiced, it bears fruit without uncertainty."]},{"number":473,"name":"सिद्धमाता","samasa":["• सिद्धानां माता रक्षकत्वात्।"],"wordByWord":["• माता — mother.","• रक्षकत्वात् — because of protecting.","• सिद्धमाता — She who is the mother and guard of Siddhas (aspirants)."],"summary":["सिद्धमाता means one who is the mother and protector of siddhas. She guards spiritual adepts and aspirants who have attained siddhi."],"searchText":"473 सिद्धमाता • सिद्धानां माता रक्षकत्वात्। • माता — mother. • रक्षकत्वात् — because of protecting. • सिद्धमाता — she who is the mother and guard of siddhas (aspirants). सिद्धमाता means one who is the mother and protector of siddhas. she guards spiritual adepts and aspirants who have attained siddhi. the mother of the perfected: even siddhas remain her children. she protects their attainment, removes pride and guides them toward final absorption.","esoteric":["The Mother of the Perfected: Even siddhas remain Her children. She protects their attainment, removes pride and guides them toward final absorption."]},{"number":474,"name":"यशस्विनी","samasa":[],"wordByWord":["• यशस्विनी — She who possesses fame and glory."],"summary":["यशस्विनी means one who possesses fame and glory. Yaśas is glory, renown and splendour. She is endowed with supreme glory."],"searchText":"474 यशस्विनी • यशस्विनी — she who possesses fame and glory. यशस्विनी means one who possesses fame and glory. yaśas is glory, renown and splendour. she is endowed with supreme glory. the glory of being: she possesses yaśas, the splendour of victorious and auspicious existence. her glory shines through all divine accomplishment.","esoteric":["The Glory of Being: She possesses yaśas, the splendour of victorious and auspicious existence. Her glory shines through all divine accomplishment."]},{"number":475,"name":"विशुद्धिचक्रनिलया","samasa":["• विशुद्धिचक्रम् एव निलयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• विशुद्धिचक्रम् — the Viśuddhi chakra.","• निलयः — abode.","• विशुद्धिचक्रनिलया — She whose abode is the Viśuddhi chakra."],"summary":["विशुद्धिचक्रनिलया means one who dwells in the Viśuddhi chakra. This chakra is in the cavity of the throat. There the soul becomes purified by seeing Brahman in the form of a swan. Her abode is in the pericarp of the sixteen-petalled lotus."],"searchText":"475 विशुद्धिचक्रनिलया • विशुद्धिचक्रम् एव निलयः यस्याः सा। • विशुद्धिचक्रम् — the viśuddhi chakra. • निलयः — abode. • विशुद्धिचक्रनिलया — she whose abode is the viśuddhi chakra. विशुद्धिचक्रनिलया means one who dwells in the viśuddhi chakra. this chakra is in the cavity of the throat. there the soul becomes purified by seeing brahman in the form of a swan. her abode is in the pericarp of the sixteen-petalled lotus. the throat centre: viśuddhi is the sixteen-petalled throat chakra. it is connected with space, purity, refined speech and subtle discrimination.","esoteric":["The Throat Centre: Viśuddhi is the sixteen-petalled throat chakra. It is connected with space, purity, refined speech and subtle discrimination."]},{"number":476,"name":"आरक्तवर्णा","samasa":["• आरक्तो वर्णो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• आरक्तवर्णा — She whose colour is rosy-red."],"summary":["आरक्तवर्णा means one whose colour is rosy-red. Her colour is like that of the trumpet flower. The initial a is prefixed in this name."],"searchText":"476 आरक्तवर्णा • आरक्तो वर्णो यस्याः सा। • आरक्तवर्णा — she whose colour is rosy-red. आरक्तवर्णा means one whose colour is rosy-red. her colour is like that of the trumpet flower. the initial a is prefixed in this name. the rosy hue: her soft red glow indicates living energy and auspicious beauty in the viśuddhi centre.","esoteric":["The Rosy Hue: Her soft red glow indicates living energy and auspicious beauty in the Viśuddhi centre."]},{"number":477,"name":"त्रिलोचना","samasa":["• त्रीणि लोचनानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• त्रीणि — three.","• लोचनानि — eyes.","• त्रिलोचना — She who has three eyes."],"summary":["त्रिलोचना means one who has three eyes. The meaning follows directly from the compound: She is endowed with three eyes."],"searchText":"477 त्रिलोचना • त्रीणि लोचनानि यस्याः सा। • त्रीणि — three. • लोचनानि — eyes. • त्रिलोचना — she who has three eyes. त्रिलोचना means one who has three eyes. the meaning follows directly from the compound: she is endowed with three eyes. the triple sight: her three eyes illumine the inner field. they signify complete awareness across time, perception and transformation.","esoteric":["The Triple Sight: Her three eyes illumine the inner field. They signify complete awareness across time, perception and transformation."]},{"number":478,"name":"खट्वाङ्गादिप्रहरणा","samasa":["• खटाङ्गम् आदिः येषां तानि प्रहरणानि (आयुधानि) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• आदिः — beginning with.","• प्रहरणानि — weapons.","• आयुधानि — weapons.","• खट्वाङ्गादिप्रहरणा — She whose weapons begin with the khaṭvāṅga."],"summary":["खट्वाङ्गादिप्रहरणा means one whose weapons begin with the khaṭvāṅga. A khaṭvāṅga is a club with a human skull at its end. It may also be understood as the leg of a cot used as a weapon."],"searchText":"478 खट्वाङ्गादिप्रहरणा • खटाङ्गम् आदिः येषां तानि प्रहरणानि (आयुधानि) यस्याः सा। • आदिः — beginning with. • प्रहरणानि — weapons. • आयुधानि — weapons. • खट्वाङ्गादिप्रहरणा — she whose weapons begin with the khaṭvāṅga. खट्वाङ्गादिप्रहरणा means one whose weapons begin with the khaṭvāṅga. a khaṭvāṅga is a club with a human skull at its end. it may also be understood as the leg of a cot used as a weapon. the ascetic weapon: the khaṭvāṅga indicates a fierce power that cuts attachment to the body and fear of death. her weapons protect the inward path.","esoteric":["The Ascetic Weapon: The khaṭvāṅga indicates a fierce power that cuts attachment to the body and fear of death. Her weapons protect the inward path."]},{"number":479,"name":"वदनैकसमन्विता","samasa":["• वदनं च तद् एकं च तेन समन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["• समन्विता — endowed with.","• वदनैकसमन्विता — She who is endowed with one face."],"summary":["वदनैकसमन्विता means one who has one face. This single face is connected with the ether tattva."],"searchText":"479 वदनैकसमन्विता • वदनं च तद् एकं च तेन समन्विता। • समन्विता — endowed with. • वदनैकसमन्विता — she who is endowed with one face. वदनैकसमन्विता means one who has one face. this single face is connected with the ether tattva. the single face: her one face represents gathered focus and the unified expression of the space principle at the throat centre.","esoteric":["The Single Face: Her one face represents gathered focus and the unified expression of the space principle at the throat centre."]},{"number":480,"name":"पायसान्नप्रिया","samasa":["• पायसश्च तदन्नं च प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• पायसश्च — sweet milk-rice.","• प्रियं — dear, beloved.","• पायसान्नप्रिया — She who loves pāyasānna."],"summary":["पायसान्नप्रिया means one who loves pāyasānna. Pāyasānna, also called paramānna, is a nourishing preparation of milk and rice that supports the growth of the body."],"searchText":"480 पायसान्नप्रिया • पायसश्च तदन्नं च प्रियं यस्याः सा। • पायसश्च — sweet milk-rice. • प्रियं — dear, beloved. • पायसान्नप्रिया — she who loves pāyasānna. पायसान्नप्रिया means one who loves pāyasānna. pāyasānna, also called paramānna, is a nourishing preparation of milk and rice that supports the growth of the body. the cooling food: pāyasa is soothing and nourishing. its association here suggests cooling, stabilising nourishment for the throat centre.","esoteric":["The Cooling Food: Pāyasa is soothing and nourishing. Its association here suggests cooling, stabilising nourishment for the throat centre."]},{"number":481,"name":"त्वक्स्था","samasa":["• त्वचि तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• त्वचि — in the skin.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established.","• त्वक्स्था — She who is the deity of the organ of touch."],"summary":["त्वक्स्था means one who abides in the skin. She is the deity of the organ of touch."],"searchText":"481 त्वक्स्था • त्वचि तिष्ठतीति। • त्वचि — in the skin. • तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established. • त्वक्स्था — she who is the deity of the organ of touch. त्वक्स्था means one who abides in the skin. she is the deity of the organ of touch. the touch principle: as tvaksthā, she presides over skin and tactile awareness. the sense of touch is animated by her presence.","esoteric":["The Touch Principle: As Tvaksthā, She presides over skin and tactile awareness. The sense of touch is animated by Her presence."]},{"number":482,"name":"पशुलोकभयङ्करी","samasa":["• अद्वैतविद्याविहीनाः पशवः एव लोकाः। तेषां भयं करोतीति। (द्वितीयाद्वै भयं भवति)।"],"wordByWord":["• पशवः — bound beings, ignorant ones.","• लोकाः — people.","• पशुलोकभयङ्करी — She who is frightful to the ignorant."],"summary":["पशुलोकभयङ्करी means one who is frightful to the ignorant. Paśus are those who lack the knowledge of non-duality. To those bound by such ignorance, She appears fearsome."],"searchText":"482 पशुलोकभयङ्करी • अद्वैतविद्याविहीनाः पशवः एव लोकाः। तेषां भयं करोतीति। (द्वितीयाद्वै भयं भवति)। • पशवः — bound beings, ignorant ones. • लोकाः — people. • पशुलोकभयङ्करी — she who is frightful to the ignorant. पशुलोकभयङ्करी means one who is frightful to the ignorant. paśus are those who lack the knowledge of non-duality. to those bound by such ignorance, she appears fearsome. the terror of duality: paśu means a bound being caught in separation and ignorance. for such a mind, divine truth appears as fear; for the non-dual knower, she is not frightening.","esoteric":["The Terror of Duality: Paśu means a bound being caught in separation and ignorance. For such a mind, divine truth appears as fear; for the non-dual knower, She is not frightening."]},{"number":483,"name":"अमृतादिमहाशक्तिसंवृता","samasa":["• अमृताख्या शक्तिः आदिः यासां महाशक्तीनां ताभिः संवृता।"],"wordByWord":["• अमृताख्या — called Amṛtā.","• शक्तिः — śakti, power.","• आदिः — beginning with.","• संवृता — surrounded.","• अमृतादिमहाशक्तिसंवृता — She who is surrounded by the great śaktis beginning with Amṛtā."],"summary":["अमृतादिमहाशक्तिसंवृता means one who is surrounded by the great śaktis beginning with Amṛtā. Around Śrīdevī are sixteen śaktis, one for each petal and one for each letter of the sixteen-petalled Viśuddhi lotus."],"searchText":"483 अमृतादिमहाशक्तिसंवृता • अमृताख्या शक्तिः आदिः यासां महाशक्तीनां ताभिः संवृता। • अमृताख्या — called amṛtā. • शक्तिः — śakti, power. • आदिः — beginning with. • संवृता — surrounded. • अमृतादिमहाशक्तिसंवृता — she who is surrounded by the great śaktis beginning with amṛtā. अमृतादिमहाशक्तिसंवृता means one who is surrounded by the great śaktis beginning with amṛtā. around śrīdevī are sixteen śaktis, one for each petal and one for each letter of the sixteen-petalled viśuddhi lotus. the sixteen powers: the viśuddhi chakra has sixteen petals. she is surrounded by the sixteen śaktis beginning with amṛtā, forming a complete circle of vowel power.","esoteric":["The Sixteen Powers: The Viśuddhi chakra has sixteen petals. She is surrounded by the sixteen śaktis beginning with Amṛtā, forming a complete circle of vowel power."]},{"number":484,"name":"डाकिनीश्वरी","samasa":["• डाकिन्याख्या ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["• डाकिन्याख्या — called Ḍākinī.","• ईश्वरी — ruler, mistress.","• डाकिनीश्वरी — She who is called Ḍākinīśvarī."],"summary":["डाकिनीश्वरी means one who is called Ḍākinīśvarī. She possesses the nine attributes belonging to the preceding Viśuddhi chakra names."],"searchText":"484 डाकिनीश्वरी • डाकिन्याख्या ईश्वरी। • डाकिन्याख्या — called ḍākinī. • ईश्वरी — ruler, mistress. • डाकिनीश्वरी — she who is called ḍākinīśvarī. डाकिनीश्वरी means one who is called ḍākinīśvarī. she possesses the nine attributes belonging to the preceding viśuddhi chakra names. the viśuddhi śakti: as ḍākinīśvarī, she is the presiding śakti of the viśuddhi chakra and gathers the attributes of that centre into herself.","esoteric":["The Viśuddhi Śakti: As Ḍākinīśvarī, She is the presiding śakti of the Viśuddhi chakra and gathers the attributes of that centre into Herself."]},{"number":485,"name":"अनाहताब्जनिलया","samasa":["• हृत्पद्मे यद् अनाहताख्यचक्रम् तद् एव निलयः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• अनाहताख्यचक्रम् — the chakra called Anāhata.","• निलयः — abode.","• अनाहताब्जनिलया — She who abides in the Anāhata lotus."],"summary":["अनाहताब्जनिलया means one who abides in the Anāhata lotus. This is the twelve-petalled lotus in the heart and is the place of the air element."],"searchText":"485 अनाहताब्जनिलया • हृत्पद्मे यद् अनाहताख्यचक्रम् तद् एव निलयः यस्याः सा। • अनाहताख्यचक्रम् — the chakra called anāhata. • निलयः — abode. • अनाहताब्जनिलया — she who abides in the anāhata lotus. अनाहताब्जनिलया means one who abides in the anāhata lotus. this is the twelve-petalled lotus in the heart and is the place of the air element. the heart lotus: anāhata is the twelve-petalled heart centre. it is connected with air, inner balance and the subtle unstruck sound.","esoteric":["The Heart Lotus: Anāhata is the twelve-petalled heart centre. It is connected with air, inner balance and the subtle unstruck sound."]},{"number":486,"name":"श्यामाभा","samasa":["• श्यामा आभा (कान्तिः) यस्याः सा।","• श्यामया (षोडशवार्षिक्या) तुल्या।"],"wordByWord":["• श्यामा — dark, blue-green, sixteen-year-old maiden.","• आभा — lustre.","• कान्तिः — lustre, beauty.","• श्यामाभा — She who shines with a dark blue-green complexion."],"summary":["श्यामाभा means one who shines with a dark blue-green complexion. Her colour is like that of clouds. Śyāmā can also mean a girl of sixteen years, and She is in that form."],"searchText":"486 श्यामाभा • श्यामा आभा (कान्तिः) यस्याः सा। • श्यामया (षोडशवार्षिक्या) तुल्या। • श्यामा — dark, blue-green, sixteen-year-old maiden. • आभा — lustre. • कान्तिः — lustre, beauty. • श्यामाभा — she who shines with a dark blue-green complexion. श्यामाभा means one who shines with a dark blue-green complexion. her colour is like that of clouds. śyāmā can also mean a girl of sixteen years, and she is in that form. the luminous dark hue: her greenish-blue radiance suits the heart centre and the life-giving quality of air. it is dark, shining and full of vitality.","esoteric":["The Luminous Dark Hue: Her greenish-blue radiance suits the heart centre and the life-giving quality of air. It is dark, shining and full of vitality."]},{"number":487,"name":"वदनद्वया","samasa":["• वदनयोर्द्वयं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• वदनद्वया — She who has two faces."],"summary":["वदनद्वया means one who has two faces. The two faces indicate the ether and air tattvas."],"searchText":"487 वदनद्वया • वदनयोर्द्वयं यस्याः सा। • वदनद्वया — she who has two faces. वदनद्वया means one who has two faces. the two faces indicate the ether and air tattvas. the dual face: at the heart centre, her two faces suggest balanced awareness of inward feeling and outward relation, held in one harmony.","esoteric":["The Dual Face: At the heart centre, Her two faces suggest balanced awareness of inward feeling and outward relation, held in one harmony."]},{"number":488,"name":"दंष्ट्रोज्ज्वला","samasa":["• दंष्ट्राभिः उज्ज्वला।"],"wordByWord":["• दंष्ट्राभिः — with tusks or fangs.","• उज्ज्वला — shining.","• दंष्ट्रोज्ज्वला — She who shines with fangs."],"summary":["दंष्ट्रोज्ज्वला means one who shines with fangs. Her fangs are radiant and indicate a fierce protective form."],"searchText":"488 दंष्ट्रोज्ज्वला • दंष्ट्राभिः उज्ज्वला। • दंष्ट्राभिः — with tusks or fangs. • उज्ज्वला — shining. • दंष्ट्रोज्ज्वला — she who shines with fangs. दंष्ट्रोज्ज्वला means one who shines with fangs. her fangs are radiant and indicate a fierce protective form. the fierce radiance: her shining fangs show the power that cuts through fear, delusion and harmful attachment in the heart.","esoteric":["The Fierce Radiance: Her shining fangs show the power that cuts through fear, delusion and harmful attachment in the heart."]},{"number":489,"name":"अक्षमालादिधरा","samasa":["• अक्षमाला आदिः येषां तेषां आयुधानां धरा।"],"wordByWord":["• अक्षमाला — rosary.","• आदिः — beginning with.","• धरा — bearing.","• अक्षमालादिधरा — She who bears a rosary and other emblems."],"summary":["अक्षमालादिधरा means one who bears a rosary and other emblems. The garland of Sanskrit letters beginning with a and ending with kṣa is called akṣamālā. It is used for counting while chanting mantras. She bears the rosary, trident, skull and ḍamaru. Akṣa can also mean the wheel of a chariot, so it may indicate the chakra weapon."],"searchText":"489 अक्षमालादिधरा • अक्षमाला आदिः येषां तेषां आयुधानां धरा। • अक्षमाला — rosary. • आदिः — beginning with. • धरा — bearing. • अक्षमालादिधरा — she who bears a rosary and other emblems. अक्षमालादिधरा means one who bears a rosary and other emblems. the garland of sanskrit letters beginning with a and ending with kṣa is called akṣamālā. it is used for counting while chanting mantras. she bears the rosary, trident, skull and ḍamaru. akṣa can also mean the wheel of a chariot, so it may indicate the chakra weapon. the rosary of sound: akṣamālā indicates continuous japa and concentration. it also recalls the garland of letters through which mantra is counted and awakened.","esoteric":["The Rosary of Sound: Akṣamālā indicates continuous japa and concentration. It also recalls the garland of letters through which mantra is counted and awakened."]},{"number":490,"name":"रुधिरसंस्थिता","samasa":["• रुधिरे (शोणिते) संस्थिता तदभिमानित्वेन।"],"wordByWord":["• रुधिरे — in blood.","• संस्थिता — established, abiding.","• रुधिरसंस्थिता — She who abides in the blood."],"summary":["रुधिरसंस्थिता means one who is established in the blood. She is the presiding deity of the blood portion of the body."],"searchText":"490 रुधिरसंस्थिता • रुधिरे (शोणिते) संस्थिता तदभिमानित्वेन। • रुधिरे — in blood. • संस्थिता — established, abiding. • रुधिरसंस्थिता — she who abides in the blood. रुधिरसंस्थिता means one who is established in the blood. she is the presiding deity of the blood portion of the body. the blood principle: she abides in rudhira, the blood. through this vital tissue, her presence supports circulation, life and the air principle of the heart centre.","esoteric":["The Blood Principle: She abides in rudhira, the blood. Through this vital tissue, Her presence supports circulation, life and the air principle of the heart centre."]},{"number":491,"name":"कालरात्र्यादिशक्त्योघवृता","samasa":["• कालरात्र्याख्या शक्तिः आदिः यासां तासां ओघेन (समूहेन) वृता।"],"wordByWord":["• कालरात्र्याख्या — called Kālarātri.","• शक्तिः — śakti, power.","• आदिः — beginning with.","• ओघेन — by a group or multitude.","• वृता — surrounded.","• कालरात्र्यादिशक्त्योघवृता — She who is surrounded by the host of śaktis beginning with Kālarātri."],"summary":["कालरात्र्यादिशक्त्योघवृता means one who is surrounded by the host of śaktis beginning with Kālarātri. Kālarātri is a śakti connected with destructive power. Kālarātri also denotes the night before death, known through a warning dream. She may also be understood as being in the form of Kālarātri."],"searchText":"491 कालरात्र्यादिशक्त्योघवृता • कालरात्र्याख्या शक्तिः आदिः यासां तासां ओघेन (समूहेन) वृता। • कालरात्र्याख्या — called kālarātri. • शक्तिः — śakti, power. • आदिः — beginning with. • ओघेन — by a group or multitude. • वृता — surrounded. • कालरात्र्यादिशक्त्योघवृता — she who is surrounded by the host of śaktis beginning with kālarātri. कालरात्र्यादिशक्त्योघवृता means one who is surrounded by the host of śaktis beginning with kālarātri. kālarātri is a śakti connected with destructive power. kālarātri also denotes the night before death, known through a warning dream. she may also be understood as being in the form of kālarātri. the twelve petal powers: the anāhata lotus has twelve petals. she is surrounded by the attendant śaktis beginning with kālarātri, forming a protective circle around the heart centre.","esoteric":["The Twelve Petal Powers: The Anāhata lotus has twelve petals. She is surrounded by the attendant śaktis beginning with Kālarātri, forming a protective circle around the heart centre."]},{"number":492,"name":"स्निग्धौदनप्रिया","samasa":["• स्निग्धः ओदनः प्रियो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• स्निग्धः — unctuous, moist.","• ओदनः — cooked rice.","• स्निग्धौदनप्रिया — She who loves rice mixed with ghee."],"summary":["स्निग्धौदनप्रिया means one who loves rice mixed with ghee. This food is nourishing, enriches the blood and gives energy."],"searchText":"492 स्निग्धौदनप्रिया • स्निग्धः ओदनः प्रियो यस्याः सा। • स्निग्धः — unctuous, moist. • ओदनः — cooked rice. • स्निग्धौदनप्रिया — she who loves rice mixed with ghee. स्निग्धौदनप्रिया means one who loves rice mixed with ghee. this food is nourishing, enriches the blood and gives energy. the nourishing rice: snigdha-odana is moist, smooth and sustaining. it suggests nourishment that steadies the heart centre and supports the vitality of the body.","esoteric":["The Nourishing Rice: Snigdha-odana is moist, smooth and sustaining. It suggests nourishment that steadies the heart centre and supports the vitality of the body."]},{"number":493,"name":"महावीरेन्द्रवरदा","samasa":["• महान्तेभ्यः वीरेन्द्रेभ्यः वरं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["• महान्तेभ्यः — to the great.","• वीरेन्द्रेभ्यः — to chiefs of heroes.","• वरं — boon.","• महावीरेन्द्रवरदा — She who grants boons to great heroic adepts."],"summary":["महावीरेन्द्रवरदा means one who grants boons to great heroic adepts. Mahāvīra can mean a vessel used in soma sacrifice. It also refers to those who constantly drink the nectar of Brahman, know Brahman, and directly realize Brahman as the Self and witness of all. Vīrendras are those who realize the fourth state even within waking, dream and deep sleep. She granted boons to Indra and Prahlāda."],"searchText":"493 महावीरेन्द्रवरदा • महान्तेभ्यः वीरेन्द्रेभ्यः वरं ददातीति। • महान्तेभ्यः — to the great. • वीरेन्द्रेभ्यः — to chiefs of heroes. • वरं — boon. • महावीरेन्द्रवरदा — she who grants boons to great heroic adepts. महावीरेन्द्रवरदा means one who grants boons to great heroic adepts. mahāvīra can mean a vessel used in soma sacrifice. it also refers to those who constantly drink the nectar of brahman, know brahman, and directly realize brahman as the self and witness of all. vīrendras are those who realize the fourth state even within waking, dream and deep sleep. she granted boons to indra and prahlāda. the boon-giver to heroes: mahāvīras are heroic practitioners who conquer inner fear and realize the self. to such vīrendras, she grants the highest boons and spiritual sovereignty.","esoteric":["The Boon-Giver to Heroes: Mahāvīras are heroic practitioners who conquer inner fear and realize the Self. To such vīrendras, She grants the highest boons and spiritual sovereignty."]},{"number":494,"name":"राकिण्यम्बास्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• राकिणीनाम् अम्बायाः स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["• स्वरूपम् — form.","• राकिण्यम्बास्वरूपिणी — She who is in the form of Rākiṇī Ambā."],"summary":["राकिण्यम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of Rākiṇī Ambā. She is the Rākiṇī Yoginī associated with the Anāhata chakra."],"searchText":"494 राकिण्यम्बास्वरूपिणी • राकिणीनाम् अम्बायाः स्वरूपम् अस्याः इति। • स्वरूपम् — form. • राकिण्यम्बास्वरूपिणी — she who is in the form of rākiṇī ambā. राकिण्यम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of rākiṇī ambā. she is the rākiṇī yoginī associated with the anāhata chakra. the heart śakti: as rākiṇī ambā, she presides over the anāhata centre and gathers the attributes of the twelve-petalled heart lotus into herself.","esoteric":["The Heart Śakti: As Rākiṇī Ambā, She presides over the Anāhata centre and gathers the attributes of the twelve-petalled heart lotus into Herself."]},{"number":495,"name":"मणिपूराब्जनिलया","samasa":["• मणिपूराख्यम् अब्जं निलयो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• मणिपूराख्यम् — called Maṇipūra.","• मणिपूराब्जनिलया — She whose abode is the Maṇipūra lotus."],"summary":["मणिपूराब्जनिलया means one who dwells in the Maṇipūra lotus. Maṇipūra is the ten-petalled lotus in the region of the navel."],"searchText":"495 मणिपूराब्जनिलया • मणिपूराख्यम् अब्जं निलयो यस्याः सा। • मणिपूराख्यम् — called maṇipūra. • मणिपूराब्जनिलया — she whose abode is the maṇipūra lotus. मणिपूराब्जनिलया means one who dwells in the maṇipūra lotus. maṇipūra is the ten-petalled lotus in the region of the navel. the jewel city: maṇipūra is the navel centre, connected with fire, digestion and inner heat. she dwells there as the radiant power that collects and purifies energy.","esoteric":["The Jewel City: Maṇipūra is the navel centre, connected with fire, digestion and inner heat. She dwells there as the radiant power that collects and purifies energy."]},{"number":496,"name":"वदनत्रयसंयुता","samasa":["• वदनानां त्रयेण संयुता।"],"wordByWord":["• वदनत्रयसंयुता — She who has three faces."],"summary":["वदनत्रयसंयुता means one who has three faces. The abdomen is the place of water, and Her three faces explain the three tattvas: ether, air and water."],"searchText":"496 वदनत्रयसंयुता • वदनानां त्रयेण संयुता। • वदनत्रयसंयुता — she who has three faces. वदनत्रयसंयुता means one who has three faces. the abdomen is the place of water, and her three faces explain the three tattvas: ether, air and water. the three faces: her three faces show mastery over the elements active in this centre. they also suggest the gathered power of perception, digestion and transformation.","esoteric":["The Three Faces: Her three faces show mastery over the elements active in this centre. They also suggest the gathered power of perception, digestion and transformation."]},{"number":497,"name":"वज्रादिकायुधोपेता","samasa":["• वज्रादिकैः चतुर्भिः आयुधैः उपैता।"],"wordByWord":["• वज्रादिकैः — with vajra and others.","• उपैता — endowed with.","• वज्रादिकायुधोपेता — She who is armed with the vajra and other weapons."],"summary":["वज्रादिकायुधोपेता means one who is armed with the vajra and other weapons. In Her four hands She holds the vajra, śakti, daṇḍa and abhaya."],"searchText":"497 वज्रादिकायुधोपेता • वज्रादिकैः चतुर्भिः आयुधैः उपैता। • वज्रादिकैः — with vajra and others. • उपैता — endowed with. • वज्रादिकायुधोपेता — she who is armed with the vajra and other weapons. वज्रादिकायुधोपेता means one who is armed with the vajra and other weapons. in her four hands she holds the vajra, śakti, daṇḍa and abhaya. the vajra weapons: the vajra and other weapons represent firmness, force and protection. they cut through impurity and defend the inner fire of the navel centre.","esoteric":["The Vajra Weapons: The vajra and other weapons represent firmness, force and protection. They cut through impurity and defend the inner fire of the navel centre."]},{"number":498,"name":"डामर्यादिभिरावृता","samasa":["• डामर्याद्याभिः दशभिः शक्तिभिः आवृता।"],"wordByWord":["• डामर्याद्याभिः — with Ḍāmarī and others.","• दशभिः — with ten.","• आवृता — surrounded.","• डामर्यादिभिरावृता — She who is surrounded by Ḍāmarī and others."],"summary":["डामर्यादिभिरावृता means one who is surrounded by Ḍāmarī and others. She is encircled by ten devīs: Ḍāmarī, Ḍhaṅkāriṇī, Nāriṇī, Tāmasī, Sthāṇvī, Dakṣāyaṇī, Dhātrī, Nārī, Pārvatī and Phaṭkāriṇī."],"searchText":"498 डामर्यादिभिरावृता • डामर्याद्याभिः दशभिः शक्तिभिः आवृता। • डामर्याद्याभिः — with ḍāmarī and others. • दशभिः — with ten. • आवृता — surrounded. • डामर्यादिभिरावृता — she who is surrounded by ḍāmarī and others. डामर्यादिभिरावृता means one who is surrounded by ḍāmarī and others. she is encircled by ten devīs: ḍāmarī, ḍhaṅkāriṇī, nāriṇī, tāmasī, sthāṇvī, dakṣāyaṇī, dhātrī, nārī, pārvatī and phaṭkāriṇī. the ten petal powers: the maṇipūra chakra has ten petals. she sits at the centre, surrounded by the ten śaktis beginning with ḍāmarī.","esoteric":["The Ten Petal Powers: The Maṇipūra chakra has ten petals. She sits at the centre, surrounded by the ten śaktis beginning with Ḍāmarī."]},{"number":499,"name":"रक्त्रवर्णा","samasa":["• रक्तो वर्णो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• रक्त्रवर्णा — She who is red or blood-coloured."],"summary":["रक्त्रवर्णा means one who is red or blood-coloured. Her complexion is the colour of blood-red radiance."],"searchText":"499 रक्त्रवर्णा • रक्तो वर्णो यस्याः सा। • रक्त्रवर्णा — she who is red or blood-coloured. रक्त्रवर्णा means one who is red or blood-coloured. her complexion is the colour of blood-red radiance. the crimson radiance: her red colour shows heat, force and the fiery energy of the maṇipūra centre.","esoteric":["The Crimson Radiance: Her red colour shows heat, force and the fiery energy of the Maṇipūra centre."]},{"number":500,"name":"मांसनिष्ठा","samasa":["• मांसे नितरां तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• मांसे — in flesh.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established.","• मांसनिष्ठा — She who is established in flesh."],"summary":["मांसनिष्ठा means one who is established in flesh. She is associated with the flesh or muscle tissue of the body. This name concludes the sixth kalā called Ruci."],"searchText":"500 मांसनिष्ठा • मांसे नितरां तिष्ठतीति। • मांसे — in flesh. • तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established. • मांसनिष्ठा — she who is established in flesh. मांसनिष्ठा means one who is established in flesh. she is associated with the flesh or muscle tissue of the body. this name concludes the sixth kalā called ruci. the muscle principle: she abides in māṃsa, the bodily tissue of flesh and muscle. through it she supports strength, movement and the fire-centred vitality of the body.","esoteric":["The Muscle Principle: She abides in māṃsa, the bodily tissue of flesh and muscle. Through it She supports strength, movement and the fire-centred vitality of the body."]},{"number":501,"name":"गुडान्नप्रीतमानसा","samasa":["• गुडेन मिश्रमन्नं तेन प्रीतं मानसं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• गुडेन — with jaggery.","• मिश्रमन्नं — rice or food mixed with it.","• तेन — by that.","• प्रीतं — pleased.","• मानसं — mind.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• गुडान्नप्रीतमानसा — She whose mind is pleased by rice cooked with jaggery."],"summary":["गुडान्नप्रीतमानसा means one whose mind is pleased by rice cooked with jaggery. She is satisfied by guḍānna, rice mixed or cooked with jaggery."],"searchText":"501 गुडान्नप्रीतमानसा • गुडेन मिश्रमन्नं तेन प्रीतं मानसं यस्याः सा। • गुडेन — with jaggery. • मिश्रमन्नं — rice or food mixed with it. • तेन — by that. • प्रीतं — pleased. • मानसं — mind. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • गुडान्नप्रीतमानसा — she whose mind is pleased by rice cooked with jaggery. गुडान्नप्रीतमानसा means one whose mind is pleased by rice cooked with jaggery. she is satisfied by guḍānna, rice mixed or cooked with jaggery. the sweet offering: guḍānna is sweet, nourishing and grounding. it satisfies her in the maṇipūra sequence and balances the heat of the navel centre.","esoteric":["The Sweet Offering: Guḍānna is sweet, nourishing and grounding. It satisfies Her in the Maṇipūra sequence and balances the heat of the navel centre."]},{"number":502,"name":"समस्तभक्तसुखदा","samasa":["• समस्तेभ्यो भक्तेभ्यो सुखं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["• समस्तेभ्यो — to all.","• भक्तेभ्यो — to devotees.","• सुखं — happiness.","• ददातीति — gives.","• समस्तभक्तसुखदा — She who gives happiness to all devotees."],"summary":["समस्तभक्तसुखदा means one who gives happiness to all devotees. She bestows joy and well-being on every devotee."],"searchText":"502 समस्तभक्तसुखदा • समस्तेभ्यो भक्तेभ्यो सुखं ददातीति। • समस्तेभ्यो — to all. • भक्तेभ्यो — to devotees. • सुखं — happiness. • ददातीति — gives. • समस्तभक्तसुखदा — she who gives happiness to all devotees. समस्तभक्तसुखदा means one who gives happiness to all devotees. she bestows joy and well-being on every devotee. the giver of happiness: her grace reaches all devotees in keeping with their capacity. she grants comfort, joy and the deeper happiness of spiritual nearness.","esoteric":["The Giver of Happiness: Her grace reaches all devotees in keeping with their capacity. She grants comfort, joy and the deeper happiness of spiritual nearness."]},{"number":503,"name":"लाकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• लाकिन्याख्याया अम्बायाः स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["• लाकिन्याख्याया — called Lākiṇī.","• अम्बायाः — of the Mother.","• स्वरूपमस्याः — her form.","• अस्तीति — is.","• लाकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी — She who is in the form of Lākiṇī Ambā."],"summary":["लाकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of Lākiṇī Ambā. She is Lākiṇī Devī, the presiding form connected with Maṇipūra."],"searchText":"503 लाकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी • लाकिन्याख्याया अम्बायाः स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति। • लाकिन्याख्याया — called lākiṇī. • अम्बायाः — of the mother. • स्वरूपमस्याः — her form. • अस्तीति — is. • लाकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी — she who is in the form of lākiṇī ambā. लाकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of lākiṇī ambā. she is lākiṇī devī, the presiding form connected with maṇipūra. the navel śakti: as lākiṇī ambā, she gathers the qualities of the ten-petalled maṇipūra lotus and rules the fire-centred navel region.","esoteric":["The Navel Śakti: As Lākiṇī Ambā, She gathers the qualities of the ten-petalled Maṇipūra lotus and rules the fire-centred navel region."]},{"number":504,"name":"स्वाधिष्ठानाम्बुजगता","samasa":["• स्वाधिष्ठानाख्यम् अम्बुजं गता।"],"wordByWord":["• स्वाधिष्ठानाख्यम् — called Svādhiṣṭhāna.","• अम्बुजं — lotus.","• गता — gone to, residing in.","• स्वाधिष्ठानाम्बुजगता — She who dwells in the Svādhiṣṭhāna lotus."],"summary":["स्वाधिष्ठानाम्बुजगता means one who abides in the Svādhiṣṭhāna lotus. This chakra is in the lower abdomen of the body."],"searchText":"504 स्वाधिष्ठानाम्बुजगता • स्वाधिष्ठानाख्यम् अम्बुजं गता। • स्वाधिष्ठानाख्यम् — called svādhiṣṭhāna. • अम्बुजं — lotus. • गता — gone to, residing in. • स्वाधिष्ठानाम्बुजगता — she who dwells in the svādhiṣṭhāna lotus. स्वाधिष्ठानाम्बुजगता means one who abides in the svādhiṣṭhāna lotus. this chakra is in the lower abdomen of the body. the svādhiṣṭhāna lotus: she moves to the six-petalled svādhiṣṭhāna centre, associated with the lower abdomen, water and vital continuity.","esoteric":["The Svādhiṣṭhāna Lotus: She moves to the six-petalled Svādhiṣṭhāna centre, associated with the lower abdomen, water and vital continuity."]},{"number":505,"name":"चतुर्वक्त्रमनोहरा","samasa":["• चतुर्भिः वक्त्रैः मनः हरतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• चतुर्भिः — with four.","• वक्त्रैः — faces.","• मनः — mind.","• हरतीति — captivates.","• चतुर्वक्त्रमनोहरा — She who enchants with four faces."],"summary":["चतुर्वक्त्रमनोहरा means one who enchants with Her four faces. Svādhiṣṭhāna is the place of water. Therefore, beginning with ether and ending with water, the four primary elements are represented by Her four faces."],"searchText":"505 चतुर्वक्त्रमनोहरा • चतुर्भिः वक्त्रैः मनः हरतीति। • चतुर्भिः — with four. • वक्त्रैः — faces. • मनः — mind. • हरतीति — captivates. • चतुर्वक्त्रमनोहरा — she who enchants with four faces. चतुर्वक्त्रमनोहरा means one who enchants with her four faces. svādhiṣṭhāna is the place of water. therefore, beginning with ether and ending with water, the four primary elements are represented by her four faces. the four faces: her four faces show the ordering of the four elements from ether through water. they make the svādhiṣṭhāna form beautiful and captivating.","esoteric":["The Four Faces: Her four faces show the ordering of the four elements from ether through water. They make the Svādhiṣṭhāna form beautiful and captivating."]},{"number":506,"name":"शूलाद्यायुधसम्पन्ना","samasa":["• शूलादिभिः आयुधैः सम्पन्ना।"],"wordByWord":["• शूलादिभिः — with trident and others.","• आयुधैः — weapons.","• सम्पन्ना — endowed.","• शूलाद्यायुधसम्पन्ना — She who is endowed with weapons beginning with the trident."],"summary":["शूलाद्यायुधसम्पन्ना means one who has weapons such as the trident. Her weapons include the trident, noose, skull and goad."],"searchText":"506 शूलाद्यायुधसम्पन्ना • शूलादिभिः आयुधैः सम्पन्ना। • शूलादिभिः — with trident and others. • आयुधैः — weapons. • सम्पन्ना — endowed. • शूलाद्यायुधसम्पन्ना — she who is endowed with weapons beginning with the trident. शूलाद्यायुधसम्पन्ना means one who has weapons such as the trident. her weapons include the trident, noose, skull and goad. the trident and weapons: her weapons show discipline and protection. the trident pierces the three guṇas and subdues lower impulses.","esoteric":["The Trident and Weapons: Her weapons show discipline and protection. The trident pierces the three guṇas and subdues lower impulses."]},{"number":507,"name":"पीतवर्णा","samasa":["• पीतो वर्णो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• पीतो — yellow.","• वर्णो — colour.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• पीतवर्णा — She whose colour is yellow."],"summary":["पीतवर्णा means one whose hue is yellow or golden. Pīta also means saffron flower, so She may also be understood as rosy like the saffron flower."],"searchText":"507 पीतवर्णा • पीतो वर्णो यस्याः सा। • पीतो — yellow. • वर्णो — colour. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • पीतवर्णा — she whose colour is yellow. पीतवर्णा means one whose hue is yellow or golden. pīta also means saffron flower, so she may also be understood as rosy like the saffron flower. the golden hue: her yellow radiance is steady, luminous and auspicious. it gives brightness and balance to the svādhiṣṭhāna centre.","esoteric":["The Golden Hue: Her yellow radiance is steady, luminous and auspicious. It gives brightness and balance to the Svādhiṣṭhāna centre."]},{"number":508,"name":"अतिगर्विता","samasa":["• अतीव सौन्दर्यादिकृतो गर्वो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• अतीव — exceedingly.","• सौन्दर्यादिकृतो — caused by beauty and the like.","• गर्वो — pride, dignity.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• अतिगर्विता — She who is very proud or dignified."],"summary":["अतिगर्विता means one who is very proud or dignified. Her pride is the dignity born of Her beauty and sovereignty, not ordinary arrogance."],"searchText":"508 अतिगर्विता • अतीव सौन्दर्यादिकृतो गर्वो यस्याः सा। • अतीव — exceedingly. • सौन्दर्यादिकृतो — caused by beauty and the like. • गर्वो — pride, dignity. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • अतिगर्विता — she who is very proud or dignified. अतिगर्विता means one who is very proud or dignified. her pride is the dignity born of her beauty and sovereignty, not ordinary arrogance. the dignity of sovereignty: her garva is majesty and self-possession. she stands complete in her own beauty, authority and independence.","esoteric":["The Dignity of Sovereignty: Her garva is majesty and self-possession. She stands complete in Her own beauty, authority and independence."]},{"number":509,"name":"मेदोनिष्ठा","samasa":["• मेदसि निष्ठा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• मेदसि — in fat tissue.","• निष्ठा — established, abiding.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• मेदोनिष्ठा — She who is established in fat tissue."],"summary":["मेदोनिष्ठा means one who is established in the fatty tissues of the body. She resides in or presides over medas, the fat tissue. Since She is the presiding deity of this tissue, the previous name mentions dignity or pride."],"searchText":"509 मेदोनिष्ठा • मेदसि निष्ठा यस्याः सा। • मेदसि — in fat tissue. • निष्ठा — established, abiding. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • मेदोनिष्ठा — she who is established in fat tissue. मेदोनिष्ठा means one who is established in the fatty tissues of the body. she resides in or presides over medas, the fat tissue. since she is the presiding deity of this tissue, the previous name mentions dignity or pride. the fat-tissue principle: she abides in medas, the tissue of fat and lubrication. through it she supports bodily reserve, protection and the water principle.","esoteric":["The Fat-Tissue Principle: She abides in medas, the tissue of fat and lubrication. Through it She supports bodily reserve, protection and the water principle."]},{"number":510,"name":"मधुप्रीता","samasa":["• मधुना प्रीता।"],"wordByWord":["• मधुना — with honey or mead.","• प्रीता — pleased.","• मधुप्रीता — She who is pleased by madhu."],"summary":["मधुप्रीता means one who is pleased by madhu. Madhu can mean mead or honey. An offering with madhu pleases the great Devī."],"searchText":"510 मधुप्रीता • मधुना प्रीता। • मधुना — with honey or mead. • प्रीता — pleased. • मधुप्रीता — she who is pleased by madhu. मधुप्रीता means one who is pleased by madhu. madhu can mean mead or honey. an offering with madhu pleases the great devī. the sweet nectar: madhu is sweet, liquid and pleasing. in inner worship it suggests the nectar-like essence of devotion offered back to her.","esoteric":["The Sweet Nectar: Madhu is sweet, liquid and pleasing. In inner worship it suggests the nectar-like essence of devotion offered back to Her."]},{"number":511,"name":"बन्धिन्यादिसमन्विता","samasa":["• बन्धिन्यादिभिः समन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["• बन्धिन्यादिभिः — with Bandhinī and others.","• समन्विता — endowed, accompanied.","• बन्धिन्यादिसमन्विता — She who is accompanied by Bandhinī and others."],"summary":["बन्धिन्यादिसमन्विता means one who is accompanied by Bandhinī and others. The six deities beginning with Bandhinī are Bandhinī, Bhadrakālī, Mahāmāyā, Yaśasvinī, Raktā and Lamboṣṭhī."],"searchText":"511 बन्धिन्यादिसमन्विता • बन्धिन्यादिभिः समन्विता। • बन्धिन्यादिभिः — with bandhinī and others. • समन्विता — endowed, accompanied. • बन्धिन्यादिसमन्विता — she who is accompanied by bandhinī and others. बन्धिन्यादिसमन्विता means one who is accompanied by bandhinī and others. the six deities beginning with bandhinī are bandhinī, bhadrakālī, mahāmāyā, yaśasvinī, raktā and lamboṣṭhī. the six petal powers: the svādhiṣṭhāna lotus has six petals. she is surrounded by the attendant śaktis beginning with bandhinī, forming the sixfold circle of that centre.","esoteric":["The Six Petal Powers: The Svādhiṣṭhāna lotus has six petals. She is surrounded by the attendant śaktis beginning with Bandhinī, forming the sixfold circle of that centre."]},{"number":512,"name":"दध्यन्नासक्तहृदया","samasa":["• दधिसिक्ते अन्ने आसक्तं हृदयं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• दधिसिक्ते — soaked with curd.","• अन्ने — in rice or food.","• आसक्तं — attached, fond of.","• हृदयं — heart.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• दध्यन्नासक्तहृदया — She whose heart is fond of curd rice."],"summary":["दध्यन्नासक्तहृदया means one whose heart is fond of curd rice. She is attached to dadhyanna, rice mixed with curd."],"searchText":"512 दध्यन्नासक्तहृदया • दधिसिक्ते अन्ने आसक्तं हृदयं यस्याः सा। • दधिसिक्ते — soaked with curd. • अन्ने — in rice or food. • आसक्तं — attached, fond of. • हृदयं — heart. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • दध्यन्नासक्तहृदया — she whose heart is fond of curd rice. दध्यन्नासक्तहृदया means one whose heart is fond of curd rice. she is attached to dadhyanna, rice mixed with curd. the cooling food: curd rice is cooling, nourishing and stabilising. it suits the svādhiṣṭhāna centre, calming and steadying its fluid nature.","esoteric":["The Cooling Food: Curd rice is cooling, nourishing and stabilising. It suits the Svādhiṣṭhāna centre, calming and steadying its fluid nature."]},{"number":513,"name":"काकिनीरूपधारिणी","samasa":["• काकिन्या रूपं धारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• काकिन्या — of Kākiṇī.","• रूपं — form.","• धारयतीति — bears, assumes.","• काकिनीरूपधारिणी — She who assumes the form of Kākiṇī."],"summary":["काकिनीरूपधारिणी means one who assumes the form of Kākiṇī. She bears the form of Kākiṇī, the śakti connected with the Svādhiṣṭhāna centre."],"searchText":"513 काकिनीरूपधारिणी • काकिन्या रूपं धारयतीति। • काकिन्या — of kākiṇī. • रूपं — form. • धारयतीति — bears, assumes. • काकिनीरूपधारिणी — she who assumes the form of kākiṇī. काकिनीरूपधारिणी means one who assumes the form of kākiṇī. she bears the form of kākiṇī, the śakti connected with the svādhiṣṭhāna centre. the pelvic śakti: as kākiṇī, she gathers the qualities of the svādhiṣṭhāna lotus and presides over that centre.","esoteric":["The Pelvic Śakti: As Kākiṇī, She gathers the qualities of the Svādhiṣṭhāna lotus and presides over that centre."]},{"number":514,"name":"मूलाधाराम्बुजारूढा","samasa":["• मूलाधाराख्ये अम्बुजे आरूढा।"],"wordByWord":["• मूलाधाराख्ये — called Mūlādhāra.","• अम्बुजे — in the lotus.","• आरूढा — mounted, ascended.","• मूलाधाराम्बुजारूढा — She who dwells in the Mūlādhāra lotus."],"summary":["मूलाधाराम्बुजारूढा means one who dwells in the Mūlādhāra lotus. Mūlādhāra is in the lower part of the body, and She resides in the lotus there."],"searchText":"514 मूलाधाराम्बुजारूढा • मूलाधाराख्ये अम्बुजे आरूढा। • मूलाधाराख्ये — called mūlādhāra. • अम्बुजे — in the lotus. • आरूढा — mounted, ascended. • मूलाधाराम्बुजारूढा — she who dwells in the mūlādhāra lotus. मूलाधाराम्बुजारूढा means one who dwells in the mūlādhāra lotus. mūlādhāra is in the lower part of the body, and she resides in the lotus there. the root foundation: mūlādhāra is the four-petalled root centre. it is connected with earth, bodily structure and the base of the subtle energy system.","esoteric":["The Root Foundation: Mūlādhāra is the four-petalled root centre. It is connected with earth, bodily structure and the base of the subtle energy system."]},{"number":515,"name":"पञ्चवक्त्रा","samasa":["• पञ्चसङ्ख्यानि वक्त्राणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• पञ्चसङ्ख्यानि — numbering five.","• वक्त्राणि — faces.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• पञ्चवक्त्रा — She who has five faces."],"summary":["पञ्चवक्त्रा means one who has five faces. Mūlādhāra is the place of the earth tattva. Her five faces indicate the five primary elements from ether to earth."],"searchText":"515 पञ्चवक्त्रा • पञ्चसङ्ख्यानि वक्त्राणि यस्याः सा। • पञ्चसङ्ख्यानि — numbering five. • वक्त्राणि — faces. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • पञ्चवक्त्रा — she who has five faces. पञ्चवक्त्रा means one who has five faces. mūlādhāra is the place of the earth tattva. her five faces indicate the five primary elements from ether to earth. the five faces: her five faces correspond to the five mahābhūtas. at the root centre, she holds the full material field in stable order.","esoteric":["The Five Faces: Her five faces correspond to the five mahābhūtas. At the root centre, She holds the full material field in stable order."]},{"number":516,"name":"अस्थिसंस्थिता","samasa":["• अस्थिषु सम्यक् स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["• अस्थिषु — in the bones.","• सम्यक् — fully, properly.","• स्थिता — situated.","• अस्थिसंस्थिता — She who is established in the bones."],"summary":["अस्थिसंस्थिता means one who is established in the bones. She presides over the bones of living beings."],"searchText":"516 अस्थिसंस्थिता • अस्थिषु सम्यक् स्थिता। • अस्थिषु — in the bones. • सम्यक् — fully, properly. • स्थिता — situated. • अस्थिसंस्थिता — she who is established in the bones. अस्थिसंस्थिता means one who is established in the bones. she presides over the bones of living beings. the bone principle: she abides in asthi, the skeletal structure. through this dense tissue she supports firmness, shape and the earth quality of the body.","esoteric":["The Bone Principle: She abides in asthi, the skeletal structure. Through this dense tissue She supports firmness, shape and the earth quality of the body."]},{"number":517,"name":"अङ्कुशादिप्रहरणा","samasa":["• अङ्कुशादीनि प्रहरणानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• अङ्कुशादीनि — goad and others.","• प्रहरणानि — weapons.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• अङ्कुशादिप्रहरणा — She whose weapons begin with the goad."],"summary":["अङ्कुशादिप्रहरणा means one who is armed with the goad and other weapons. She has a lotus, book and the knowledge-sign, or mudrā, in Her hands."],"searchText":"517 अङ्कुशादिप्रहरणा • अङ्कुशादीनि प्रहरणानि यस्याः सा। • अङ्कुशादीनि — goad and others. • प्रहरणानि — weapons. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • अङ्कुशादिप्रहरणा — she whose weapons begin with the goad. अङ्कुशादिप्रहरणा means one who is armed with the goad and other weapons. she has a lotus, book and the knowledge-sign, or mudrā, in her hands. the goad of restraint: the aṅkuśa restrains and redirects unruly forces. at the root centre, her weapons steady raw energy and turn it toward discipline.","esoteric":["The Goad of Restraint: The aṅkuśa restrains and redirects unruly forces. At the root centre, Her weapons steady raw energy and turn it toward discipline."]},{"number":518,"name":"वरदादिनिषेविता","samasa":["• वरदादिभिः चतुर्भिः शक्तिभिः निषेविता।"],"wordByWord":["• वरदादिभिः — by Varadā and others.","• चतुर्भिः — with four.","• शक्तिभिः — with śaktis.","• निषेविता — served, attended.","• वरदादिनिषेविता — She who is attended by Varadā and other śaktis."],"summary":["वरदादिनिषेविता means one who is attended by Varadā and other śaktis. The four śaktis are Varadā, Śrī, Śaṇḍā and Sarasvatī."],"searchText":"518 वरदादिनिषेविता • वरदादिभिः चतुर्भिः शक्तिभिः निषेविता। • वरदादिभिः — by varadā and others. • चतुर्भिः — with four. • शक्तिभिः — with śaktis. • निषेविता — served, attended. • वरदादिनिषेविता — she who is attended by varadā and other śaktis. वरदादिनिषेविता means one who is attended by varadā and other śaktis. the four śaktis are varadā, śrī, śaṇḍā and sarasvatī. the four petal powers: the mūlādhāra lotus has four petals. she is attended by the four śaktis beginning with varadā.","esoteric":["The Four Petal Powers: The Mūlādhāra lotus has four petals. She is attended by the four śaktis beginning with Varadā."]},{"number":519,"name":"मुद्गौदनासक्तचित्ता","samasa":["• मुद्गसूपमिश्र ओदने आसक्तं चित्तं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• मुद्गसूपमिश्र — mixed with green-gram soup.","• ओदने — in cooked rice.","• आसक्तं — attached, fond of.","• चित्तं — mind.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• मुद्गौदनासक्तचित्ता — She whose mind is fond of rice mixed with green gram."],"summary":["मुद्गौदनासक्तचित्ता means one whose mind is fond of rice mixed with green gram. This food is called poṅgal, prepared from rice and green gram."],"searchText":"519 मुद्गौदनासक्तचित्ता • मुद्गसूपमिश्र ओदने आसक्तं चित्तं यस्याः सा। • मुद्गसूपमिश्र — mixed with green-gram soup. • ओदने — in cooked rice. • आसक्तं — attached, fond of. • चित्तं — mind. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • मुद्गौदनासक्तचित्ता — she whose mind is fond of rice mixed with green gram. मुद्गौदनासक्तचित्ता means one whose mind is fond of rice mixed with green gram. this food is called poṅgal, prepared from rice and green gram. the grounding food: mudga-odana is rice with green gram. it is nourishing and stabilising, fitting the earthy quality of the mūlādhāra centre.","esoteric":["The Grounding Food: Mudga-odana is rice with green gram. It is nourishing and stabilising, fitting the earthy quality of the Mūlādhāra centre."]},{"number":520,"name":"साकिन्याम्बास्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• साकिन्यम्बायाः स्वरूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["• साकिन्यम्बायाः — of Sākiṇī Ambā.","• स्वरूपम् — form.","• अस्याः — of Her.","• अस्तीति — is.","• साकिन्याम्बास्वरूपिणी — She who is in the form of Sākiṇī Ambā."],"summary":["साकिन्याम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of Sākiṇī Ambā. She is the Sākiṇī form associated with the Mūlādhāra centre."],"searchText":"520 साकिन्याम्बास्वरूपिणी • साकिन्यम्बायाः स्वरूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति। • साकिन्यम्बायाः — of sākiṇī ambā. • स्वरूपम् — form. • अस्याः — of her. • अस्तीति — is. • साकिन्याम्बास्वरूपिणी — she who is in the form of sākiṇī ambā. साकिन्याम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of sākiṇī ambā. she is the sākiṇī form associated with the mūlādhāra centre. the root śakti: as sākiṇī ambā, she gathers the qualities of the mūlādhāra lotus and presides over the root centre.","esoteric":["The Root Śakti: As Sākiṇī Ambā, She gathers the qualities of the Mūlādhāra lotus and presides over the root centre."]},{"number":521,"name":"आज्ञाचक्राब्जनिलया","samasa":["• आज्ञाचक्राब्जमेव निलयो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• निलयो — abode.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• आज्ञाचक्राब्जनिलया — She whose abode is the Ājñā chakra lotus."],"summary":["आज्ञाचक्राब्जनिलया means one who resides in the Ājñā chakra lotus between the eyebrows."],"searchText":"521 आज्ञाचक्राब्जनिलया • आज्ञाचक्राब्जमेव निलयो यस्याः सा। • निलयो — abode. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • आज्ञाचक्राब्जनिलया — she whose abode is the ājñā chakra lotus. आज्ञाचक्राब्जनिलया means one who resides in the ājñā chakra lotus between the eyebrows. the command centre: ājñā is the two-petalled lotus between the eyebrows. it is connected with mind, insight and inner command.","esoteric":["The Command Centre: Ājñā is the two-petalled lotus between the eyebrows. It is connected with mind, insight and inner command."]},{"number":522,"name":"शुक्लवर्णा","samasa":["• शुक्लो वर्णो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• शुक्लो — white.","• वर्णो — colour.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• शुक्लवर्णा — She whose colour is white."],"summary":["शुक्लवर्णा means one who is white in complexion. Her colour is pure white."],"searchText":"522 शुक्लवर्णा • शुक्लो वर्णो यस्याः सा। • शुक्लो — white. • वर्णो — colour. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • शुक्लवर्णा — she whose colour is white. शुक्लवर्णा means one who is white in complexion. her colour is pure white. the white radiance: her white complexion signifies purity, clarity and the cleansing of the mind principle in the ājñā centre.","esoteric":["The White Radiance: Her white complexion signifies purity, clarity and the cleansing of the mind principle in the Ājñā centre."]},{"number":523,"name":"षडानना","samasa":["• षट्संख्यकानि आननानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• षट्संख्यकानि — numbering six.","• आननानि — faces.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• षडानना — She who has six faces."],"summary":["षडानना means one who has six faces. Ājñā chakra is the place of the mind. Her six faces show the energy of the five primary elements together with the mind, and indicate Her control over the chakras from Viśuddhi to Mūlādhāra."],"searchText":"523 षडानना • षट्संख्यकानि आननानि यस्याः सा। • षट्संख्यकानि — numbering six. • आननानि — faces. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • षडानना — she who has six faces. षडानना means one who has six faces. ājñā chakra is the place of the mind. her six faces show the energy of the five primary elements together with the mind, and indicate her control over the chakras from viśuddhi to mūlādhāra. the six faces: her six faces gather the five elements and mind into one command point. they show oversight of the lower centres from viśuddhi to mūlādhāra.","esoteric":["The Six Faces: Her six faces gather the five elements and mind into one command point. They show oversight of the lower centres from Viśuddhi to Mūlādhāra."]},{"number":524,"name":"मज्जासंस्था","samasa":["• मज्ज्ञि आसमन्तात् सम्यक् तिष्ठतीति। (मज्जधात्वभिमानिनीत्यर्थः)।"],"wordByWord":["• मज्ज्ञि — in marrow.","• आसमन्तात् — on all sides, completely.","• सम्यक् — fully, properly.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established.","• मज्जधात्वभिमानिनीत्यर्थः — meaning: the presiding deity of the marrow tissue.","• मज्जासंस्था — the complete name, understood through the samasa above."],"summary":["मज्जासंस्था means one who is established in the marrow. She is the presiding deity of bone marrow."],"searchText":"524 मज्जासंस्था • मज्ज्ञि आसमन्तात् सम्यक् तिष्ठतीति। (मज्जधात्वभिमानिनीत्यर्थः)। • मज्ज्ञि — in marrow. • आसमन्तात् — on all sides, completely. • सम्यक् — fully, properly. • तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established. • मज्जधात्वभिमानिनीत्यर्थः — meaning: the presiding deity of the marrow tissue. • मज्जासंस्था — the complete name, understood through the samasa above. मज्जासंस्था means one who is established in the marrow. she is the presiding deity of bone marrow. the marrow principle: she abides in majjā, the marrow tissue. this points to subtle bodily depth and the inner support of vitality and perception.","esoteric":["The Marrow Principle: She abides in majjā, the marrow tissue. This points to subtle bodily depth and the inner support of vitality and perception."]},{"number":525,"name":"हंसवतीमुख्यशक्तिसमन्विता","samasa":["• हंसवती एव मुख्या आदिः ययोः ताभ्यां शक्तिभिः समन्विता।"],"wordByWord":["• हंसवती — Haṃsavatī.","• एव — itself, indeed.","• मुख्या — chief, principal.","• आदिः — beginning with.","• ययोः — of which two.","• ताभ्यां — by those two.","• शक्तिभिः — with śaktis.","• समन्विता — endowed, accompanied.","• हंसवतीमुख्यशक्तिसमन्विता — She who is accompanied by the śaktis headed by Haṃsavatī."],"summary":["हंसवतीमुख्यशक्तिसमन्विता means one who is accompanied by the śaktis headed by Haṃsavatī. She is surrounded by Haṃsavatī and the other śakti of the two-petalled Ājñā chakra."],"searchText":"525 हंसवतीमुख्यशक्तिसमन्विता • हंसवती एव मुख्या आदिः ययोः ताभ्यां शक्तिभिः समन्विता। • हंसवती — haṃsavatī. • एव — itself, indeed. • मुख्या — chief, principal. • आदिः — beginning with. • ययोः — of which two. • ताभ्यां — by those two. • शक्तिभिः — with śaktis. • समन्विता — endowed, accompanied. • हंसवतीमुख्यशक्तिसमन्विता — she who is accompanied by the śaktis headed by haṃsavatī. हंसवतीमुख्यशक्तिसमन्विता means one who is accompanied by the śaktis headed by haṃsavatī. she is surrounded by haṃsavatī and the other śakti of the two-petalled ājñā chakra. the two petal powers: the ājñā lotus has two petals. haṃsavatī and kṣamāvatī are the attendant śaktis linked with its twofold power.","esoteric":["The Two Petal Powers: The Ājñā lotus has two petals. Haṃsavatī and Kṣamāvatī are the attendant śaktis linked with its twofold power."]},{"number":526,"name":"हरिद्रान्नैकरसिका","samasa":["• हरिद्रामिश्रे अन्ने एकः (मुख्यः) रसः (प्रीतिः) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• हरिद्रामिश्रे — mixed with turmeric.","• अन्ने — in rice or food.","• एकः — one.","• मुख्यः — main.","• रसः — taste, relish.","• प्रीतिः — delight, fondness.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• हरिद्रान्नैकरसिका — She whose chief delight is turmeric rice."],"summary":["हरिद्रान्नैकरसिका means one whose chief delight is turmeric rice. She is fond of rice mixed with turmeric."],"searchText":"526 हरिद्रान्नैकरसिका • हरिद्रामिश्रे अन्ने एकः (मुख्यः) रसः (प्रीतिः) यस्याः सा। • हरिद्रामिश्रे — mixed with turmeric. • अन्ने — in rice or food. • एकः — one. • मुख्यः — main. • रसः — taste, relish. • प्रीतिः — delight, fondness. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • हरिद्रान्नैकरसिका — she whose chief delight is turmeric rice. हरिद्रान्नैकरसिका means one whose chief delight is turmeric rice. she is fond of rice mixed with turmeric. the turmeric rice: haridrānna is bright, cleansing and auspicious. it suits the clarity and sharpness of the ājñā centre.","esoteric":["The Turmeric Rice: Haridrānna is bright, cleansing and auspicious. It suits the clarity and sharpness of the Ājñā centre."]},{"number":527,"name":"हाकिनीरूपधारिणी","samasa":["• हाकिन्याख्यायाः देव्या रूपं धारयितुं शीलमिति।"],"wordByWord":["• हाकिन्याख्यायाः — called Hākiṇī.","• देव्या — of the goddess.","• रूपं — form.","• धारयितुं — to assume.","• शीलमिति — having the nature of.","• हाकिनीरूपधारिणी — She who assumes the form of Hākiṇī."],"summary":["हाकिनीरूपधारिणी means one who assumes the form of Hākiṇī. She is Hākiṇī, the śakti connected with the Ājñā chakra."],"searchText":"527 हाकिनीरूपधारिणी • हाकिन्याख्यायाः देव्या रूपं धारयितुं शीलमिति। • हाकिन्याख्यायाः — called hākiṇī. • देव्या — of the goddess. • रूपं — form. • धारयितुं — to assume. • शीलमिति — having the nature of. • हाकिनीरूपधारिणी — she who assumes the form of hākiṇī. हाकिनीरूपधारिणी means one who assumes the form of hākiṇī. she is hākiṇī, the śakti connected with the ājñā chakra. the brow śakti: as hākiṇī, she presides over the ājñā centre and gathers its qualities of mind, command and insight.","esoteric":["The Brow Śakti: As Hākiṇī, She presides over the Ājñā centre and gathers its qualities of mind, command and insight."]},{"number":528,"name":"सहस्रदलपद्मस्था","samasa":["• सहस्रदले पद्मे (ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे) तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• सहस्रदले — in the thousand-petalled.","• पद्मे — in the lotus.","• ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे — in the brahmarandhra.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established.","• सहस्रदलपद्मस्था — She who abides in the thousand-petalled lotus."],"summary":["सहस्रदलपद्मस्था means one who abides in the thousand-petalled lotus. This lotus is in the brahmarandhra and is the highest lotus in the subtle body."],"searchText":"528 सहस्रदलपद्मस्था • सहस्रदले पद्मे (ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे) तिष्ठतीति। • सहस्रदले — in the thousand-petalled. • पद्मे — in the lotus. • ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे — in the brahmarandhra. • तिष्ठतीति — abides, is established. • सहस्रदलपद्मस्था — she who abides in the thousand-petalled lotus. सहस्रदलपद्मस्था means one who abides in the thousand-petalled lotus. this lotus is in the brahmarandhra and is the highest lotus in the subtle body. the thousand-petalled lotus: she abides in the crown lotus, the highest subtle centre. there the lower distinctions resolve into pure awareness.","esoteric":["The Thousand-Petalled Lotus: She abides in the crown lotus, the highest subtle centre. There the lower distinctions resolve into pure awareness."]},{"number":529,"name":"सर्ववर्णोपशोभिता","samasa":["• सर्वैः वर्णैः (पाटलश्यामरक्तपीतादिरूपैः) उपशोभिता। चित्रवर्णा इत्यर्थः।","• सर्वाणि वर्णानि (अक्षराणि) यासां ताभिः शक्तिभिः उप समीपे शोभिता।"],"wordByWord":["• सर्वैः — with all.","• वर्णैः — colours or letters.","• पाटलश्यामरक्तपीतादिरूपैः — having forms such as pink, dark, red and yellow.","• उपशोभिता — adorned, made beautiful.","• चित्रवर्णा — variegated in colour.","• इत्यर्थः — this is the meaning.","• सर्वाणि — all.","• वर्णानि — letters or colours.","• अक्षराणि — letters.","• यासां — whose.","• ताभिः — by them.","• शक्तिभिः — with śaktis.","• उप — near.","• समीपे — near, close by.","• शोभिता — adorned.","• सर्ववर्णोपशोभिता — She who shines adorned by all colours or letters."],"summary":["सर्ववर्णोपशोभिता means one who shines adorned by all colours or letters. All colours and all letters are included in Her retinue and form."],"searchText":"529 सर्ववर्णोपशोभिता • सर्वैः वर्णैः (पाटलश्यामरक्तपीतादिरूपैः) उपशोभिता। चित्रवर्णा इत्यर्थः। • सर्वाणि वर्णानि (अक्षराणि) यासां ताभिः शक्तिभिः उप समीपे शोभिता। • सर्वैः — with all. • वर्णैः — colours or letters. • पाटलश्यामरक्तपीतादिरूपैः — having forms such as pink, dark, red and yellow. • उपशोभिता — adorned, made beautiful. • चित्रवर्णा — variegated in colour. • इत्यर्थः — this is the meaning. • सर्वाणि — all. • वर्णानि — letters or colours. • अक्षराणि — letters. • यासां — whose. • ताभिः — by them. • शक्तिभिः — with śaktis. • उप — near. • समीपे — near, close by. • शोभिता — adorned. • सर्ववर्णोपशोभिता — she who shines adorned by all colours or letters. सर्ववर्णोपशोभिता means one who shines adorned by all colours or letters. all colours and all letters are included in her retinue and form. the full spectrum: in the crown, all colours and letters are gathered into her radiance. she shines as the complete field of light and sound.","esoteric":["The Full Spectrum: In the crown, all colours and letters are gathered into Her radiance. She shines as the complete field of light and sound."]},{"number":530,"name":"सर्वायुधधरा","samasa":["• सर्वेषाम् आयुधानां धरा।"],"wordByWord":["• सर्वेषाम् — of all.","• आयुधानां — weapons.","• धरा — bearer.","• सर्वायुधधरा — She who bears all weapons."],"summary":["सर्वायुधधरा means one who bears all weapons. She is armed with every weapon."],"searchText":"530 सर्वायुधधरा • सर्वेषाम् आयुधानां धरा। • सर्वेषाम् — of all. • आयुधानां — weapons. • धरा — bearer. • सर्वायुधधरा — she who bears all weapons. सर्वायुधधरा means one who bears all weapons. she is armed with every weapon. the complete arsenal: she holds all divine weapons, showing total power to protect, restrain and destroy ignorance.","esoteric":["The Complete Arsenal: She holds all divine weapons, showing total power to protect, restrain and destroy ignorance."]},{"number":531,"name":"शुक्लसंस्थिता","samasa":["• शुक्ले (वीर्याख्यधातौ) सम्यक् (तदभिमानितया) स्थिता।","• [भविष्योत्तरपुराणे कथिते] शुक्लसंज्ञे ध्यानविशेषे स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["• शुक्ले — in śukla, the white vital principle.","• वीर्याख्यधातौ — in the bodily tissue called semen.","• सम्यक् — fully, properly.","• तदभिमानितया — as its presiding deity.","• स्थिता — situated.","• शुक्लसंज्ञे — called Śukla.","• ध्यानविशेषे — in a particular meditation.","• शुक्लसंस्थिता — She who is established in śukla."],"summary":["शुक्लसंस्थिता means one who is established in śukla. She is the presiding deity of semen, the white vital principle. Śukla is also the name of a special meditation, and She may be understood as being established in that form."],"searchText":"531 शुक्लसंस्थिता • शुक्ले (वीर्याख्यधातौ) सम्यक् (तदभिमानितया) स्थिता। • [भविष्योत्तरपुराणे कथिते] शुक्लसंज्ञे ध्यानविशेषे स्थिता। • शुक्ले — in śukla, the white vital principle. • वीर्याख्यधातौ — in the bodily tissue called semen. • सम्यक् — fully, properly. • तदभिमानितया — as its presiding deity. • स्थिता — situated. • शुक्लसंज्ञे — called śukla. • ध्यानविशेषे — in a particular meditation. • शुक्लसंस्थिता — she who is established in śukla. शुक्लसंस्थिता means one who is established in śukla. she is the presiding deity of semen, the white vital principle. śukla is also the name of a special meditation, and she may be understood as being established in that form. the essence of vitality: she governs śukla, the concentrated vital essence of the body. she is also connected with śukla-dhyāna, the pure white meditation of stillness and clarity.","esoteric":["The Essence of Vitality: She governs śukla, the concentrated vital essence of the body. She is also connected with śukla-dhyāna, the pure white meditation of stillness and clarity."]},{"number":532,"name":"सर्वतोमुखी","samasa":["• सर्वतः मुखानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• सर्वतः — on all sides.","• मुखानि — faces.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• सर्वतोमुखी — She who has faces on all sides."],"summary":["सर्वतोमुखी means one who has faces in all directions. She has eyes, heads and mouths everywhere, and is present facing all sides."],"searchText":"532 सर्वतोमुखी • सर्वतः मुखानि यस्याः सा। • सर्वतः — on all sides. • मुखानि — faces. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • सर्वतोमुखी — she who has faces on all sides. सर्वतोमुखी means one who has faces in all directions. she has eyes, heads and mouths everywhere, and is present facing all sides. the omnidirectional vision: she is not limited by direction or angle. she sees, receives and responds everywhere at once.","esoteric":["The Omnidirectional Vision: She is not limited by direction or angle. She sees, receives and responds everywhere at once."]},{"number":533,"name":"सर्वौदनप्रीतचित्ता","samasa":["• सर्वैः ओदनैः प्रीतं चित्तं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• सर्वैः — with all.","• ओदनैः — with rice preparations.","• प्रीतं — pleased.","• चित्तं — mind.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• सर्वौदनप्रीतचित्ता — She whose mind is pleased by all rice preparations."],"summary":["सर्वौदनप्रीतचित्ता means one whose mind is pleased by all kinds of rice. From pāyasa rice to turmeric rice and other preparations, She is pleased with every kind of odana."],"searchText":"533 सर्वौदनप्रीतचित्ता • सर्वैः ओदनैः प्रीतं चित्तं यस्याः सा। • सर्वैः — with all. • ओदनैः — with rice preparations. • प्रीतं — pleased. • चित्तं — mind. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • सर्वौदनप्रीतचित्ता — she whose mind is pleased by all rice preparations. सर्वौदनप्रीतचित्ता means one whose mind is pleased by all kinds of rice. from pāyasa rice to turmeric rice and other preparations, she is pleased with every kind of odana. the complete nourishment: at the crown, all earlier food distinctions are gathered together. she accepts every form of nourishment as part of one complete offering.","esoteric":["The Complete Nourishment: At the crown, all earlier food distinctions are gathered together. She accepts every form of nourishment as part of one complete offering."]},{"number":534,"name":"याकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी","samasa":["• याकिन्याख्यायाः अम्बायाः स्वरूपं अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["• याकिन्याख्यायाः — called Yākiṇī.","• अम्बायाः — of the Mother.","• स्वरूपं — form.","• अस्याः — of Her.","• अस्तीति — is.","• याकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी — She who is in the form of Yākiṇī Ambā."],"summary":["याकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who appears in the form of Yākiṇī Ambā. She is Yākiṇī, the form connected with the Sahasrāra. She also has the quality of delighting in Paramaśiva."],"searchText":"534 याकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी • याकिन्याख्यायाः अम्बायाः स्वरूपं अस्याः अस्तीति। • याकिन्याख्यायाः — called yākiṇī. • अम्बायाः — of the mother. • स्वरूपं — form. • अस्याः — of her. • अस्तीति — is. • याकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी — she who is in the form of yākiṇī ambā. याकिन्यम्बास्वरूपिणी means one who appears in the form of yākiṇī ambā. she is yākiṇī, the form connected with the sahasrāra. she also has the quality of delighting in paramaśiva. the crown śakti: as yākiṇī ambā, she gathers the qualities of the sahasrāra and presides over the crown as the culmination of the subtle centres.","esoteric":["The Crown Śakti: As Yākiṇī Ambā, She gathers the qualities of the Sahasrāra and presides over the crown as the culmination of the subtle centres."]},{"number":535,"name":"स्वाहा","samasa":["• स्वाहार्थरूपा।","• सुष्ठु आहूयते अनया इति।","• स्वान् आजिहीते (स्वीयत्वेन सम्यग्जानाति) इति।"],"wordByWord":["• स्वाहार्थरूपा — having the form of the meaning of Svāhā.","• सुष्ठु — well, properly.","• आहूयते — is invoked.","• अनया — by this.","• इति — thus.","• स्वान् — one’s own.","• आजिहीते — calls, brings near.","• स्वीयत्वेन — as one’s own.","• सम्यग्जानाति — knows properly.","• स्वाहा — She who is in the form of Svāhā."],"summary":["स्वाहा means one who is in the form of Svāhā. Svāhā is the sacred exclamation with which oblations are offered in the sacrificial fire for the gods."],"searchText":"535 स्वाहा • स्वाहार्थरूपा। • सुष्ठु आहूयते अनया इति। • स्वान् आजिहीते (स्वीयत्वेन सम्यग्जानाति) इति। • स्वाहार्थरूपा — having the form of the meaning of svāhā. • सुष्ठु — well, properly. • आहूयते — is invoked. • अनया — by this. • इति — thus. • स्वान् — one’s own. • आजिहीते — calls, brings near. • स्वीयत्वेन — as one’s own. • सम्यग्जानाति — knows properly. • स्वाहा — she who is in the form of svāhā. स्वाहा means one who is in the form of svāhā. svāhā is the sacred exclamation with which oblations are offered in the sacrificial fire for the gods. the fire offering: svāhā is the mantra-power that carries offerings into the sacrificial fire. as svāhā, she transforms the offering into subtle divine nourishment.","esoteric":["The Fire Offering: Svāhā is the mantra-power that carries offerings into the sacrificial fire. As Svāhā, She transforms the offering into subtle divine nourishment."]},{"number":536,"name":"स्वधा","samasa":["• सुष्ठु आधीयते अनया इति।","• सुष्ठु अं (विष्णुं स्वान् वा) दधातीति।"],"wordByWord":["• सुष्ठु — well, properly.","• आधीयते — is placed or offered.","• अनया — by this.","• इति — thus.","• अं — the syllable or being indicated by am.","• विष्णुं — Viṣṇu.","• स्वान् — one’s own.","• वा — or.","• दधातीति — holds, sustains.","• स्वधा — She who is in the form of Svadhā."],"summary":["स्वधा means one who is in the form of Svadhā. Svāhā and Svadhā are used in offerings: Svāhā for the gods in the sacrificial fire, and Svadhā for the ancestors. She is also in the form of the devīs represented by Svāhā and Svadhā."],"searchText":"536 स्वधा • सुष्ठु आधीयते अनया इति। • सुष्ठु अं (विष्णुं स्वान् वा) दधातीति। • सुष्ठु — well, properly. • आधीयते — is placed or offered. • अनया — by this. • इति — thus. • अं — the syllable or being indicated by am. • विष्णुं — viṣṇu. • स्वान् — one’s own. • वा — or. • दधातीति — holds, sustains. • स्वधा — she who is in the form of svadhā. स्वधा means one who is in the form of svadhā. svāhā and svadhā are used in offerings: svāhā for the gods in the sacrificial fire, and svadhā for the ancestors. she is also in the form of the devīs represented by svāhā and svadhā. the ancestral offering: svadhā is the mantra-power by which offerings reach the ancestors. as svadhā, she sustains the ancestral line and keeps its order nourished.","esoteric":["The Ancestral Offering: Svadhā is the mantra-power by which offerings reach the ancestors. As Svadhā, She sustains the ancestral line and keeps its order nourished."]},{"number":537,"name":"अमतिः","samasa":["• अविद्या।","• [अल्पार्थे नञ् इत्यनेन] वृत्त्यात्मकविद्यारूपा।","• अविद्यापूर्वा प्राथमिकी (विद्यापूर्वा च क्रमप्राप्ता) सृष्टिरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["• अविद्या — ignorance.","• अल्पार्थे — in a minor or secondary sense.","• नञ् — the negative particle nañ.","• इत्यनेन — by this.","• वृत्त्यात्मकविद्यारूपा — a form of knowledge as mental modification.","• अविद्यापूर्वा — preceded by avidyā.","• प्राथमिकी — primary, initial.","• विद्यापूर्वा — preceded by vidyā.","• च — and.","• क्रमप्राप्ता — arrived in sequence.","• सृष्टिरूपा — in the form of creation.","• अमतिः — She who is in the form of non-understanding or primordial movement."],"summary":["अमतिः means one who is in the form of ignorance or non-understanding. Amati is explained as avidyā, and also as a form of knowledge functioning through mental modifications. It may also indicate the primordial movement connected with creation."],"searchText":"537 अमतिः • अविद्या। • [अल्पार्थे नञ् इत्यनेन] वृत्त्यात्मकविद्यारूपा। • अविद्यापूर्वा प्राथमिकी (विद्यापूर्वा च क्रमप्राप्ता) सृष्टिरूपा। • अविद्या — ignorance. • अल्पार्थे — in a minor or secondary sense. • नञ् — the negative particle nañ. • इत्यनेन — by this. • वृत्त्यात्मकविद्यारूपा — a form of knowledge as mental modification. • अविद्यापूर्वा — preceded by avidyā. • प्राथमिकी — primary, initial. • विद्यापूर्वा — preceded by vidyā. • च — and. • क्रमप्राप्ता — arrived in sequence. • सृष्टिरूपा — in the form of creation. • अमतिः — she who is in the form of non-understanding or primordial movement. अमतिः means one who is in the form of ignorance or non-understanding. amati is explained as avidyā, and also as a form of knowledge functioning through mental modifications. it may also indicate the primordial movement connected with creation. the veil of non-understanding: as amati, she is the power behind the absence or limitation of active intellect. even ignorance and the first stirring of creation stand within her power.","esoteric":["The Veil of Non-Understanding: As Amati, She is the power behind the absence or limitation of active intellect. Even ignorance and the first stirring of creation stand within Her power."]},{"number":538,"name":"मेधा","samasa":["• विदिताखिलवेदसारा।","• धीर्धारणवती बुद्धिविशेषरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["• विदिताखिलवेदसारा — one who knows the essence of all sacred knowledge.","• धीर्धारणवती — intelligence that retains.","• बुद्धिविशेषरूपा — in the form of a special intellect.","• मेधा — She who is retentive intelligence."],"summary":["मेधा means one who is in the form of medhā, retentive intelligence. Medhā is the power that grasps and retains the essence of sacred knowledge."],"searchText":"538 मेधा • विदिताखिलवेदसारा। • धीर्धारणवती बुद्धिविशेषरूपा। • विदिताखिलवेदसारा — one who knows the essence of all sacred knowledge. • धीर्धारणवती — intelligence that retains. • बुद्धिविशेषरूपा — in the form of a special intellect. • मेधा — she who is retentive intelligence. मेधा means one who is in the form of medhā, retentive intelligence. medhā is the power that grasps and retains the essence of sacred knowledge. the power of retention: medhā is not ordinary memory. it is the refined intelligence that grasps, holds and preserves essential knowledge without distortion.","esoteric":["The Power of Retention: Medhā is not ordinary memory. It is the refined intelligence that grasps, holds and preserves essential knowledge without distortion."]},{"number":539,"name":"श्रुतिः","samasa":["• वेदरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["• वेदरूपा — in the form of sacred revelation.","• श्रुतिः — She who is in the form of śruti."],"summary":["श्रुतिः means one who is in the form of śruti. Śruti is sacred knowledge heard and received through revelation."],"searchText":"539 श्रुतिः • वेदरूपा। • वेदरूपा — in the form of sacred revelation. • श्रुतिः — she who is in the form of śruti. श्रुतिः means one who is in the form of śruti. śruti is sacred knowledge heard and received through revelation. the heard wisdom: as śruti, she is revealed knowledge itself. she is the living sound of truth heard in inward absorption.","esoteric":["The Heard Wisdom: As Śruti, She is revealed knowledge itself. She is the living sound of truth heard in inward absorption."]},{"number":540,"name":"स्मृतिः","samasa":["• स्मरते सर्वकार्याणीति।"],"wordByWord":["• स्मरते — remembers.","• सर्वकार्याणीति — all actions.","• स्मृतिः — She who is in the form of smṛti."],"summary":["स्मृतिः means one who is in the form of smṛti. Śruti means hearing, and smṛti means recollection. She is in the form of knowledge gained through both hearing and remembrance."],"searchText":"540 स्मृतिः • स्मरते सर्वकार्याणीति। • स्मरते — remembers. • सर्वकार्याणीति — all actions. • स्मृतिः — she who is in the form of smṛti. स्मृतिः means one who is in the form of smṛti. śruti means hearing, and smṛti means recollection. she is in the form of knowledge gained through both hearing and remembrance. the power of remembrance: smṛti is memory that preserves knowledge and conduct. as smṛti, she holds order, recollection and continuity within the mind.","esoteric":["The Power of Remembrance: Smṛti is memory that preserves knowledge and conduct. As Smṛti, She holds order, recollection and continuity within the mind."]},{"number":541,"name":"अनुत्तमा","samasa":["• यदपेक्षयोत्तममन्यद्वस्तु नास्ति सा।","• न नुत्ता परप्रेरिता मा बुद्धिरैश्वर्यं वा यस्या सा।"],"wordByWord":["• यदपेक्षयोत्तममन्यद्वस्तु — a thing superior in comparison with whom.","• नास्ति — does not exist.","• सा — she.","• न — not.","• नुत्ता — praised or prompted.","• परप्रेरिता — impelled by another.","• मा — measure, knowledge or power.","• बुद्धिरैश्वर्यं — intellect or lordship.","• वा — or.","• यस्या — whose.","• अनुत्तमा — She who has none superior."],"summary":["अनुत्तमा means one who has none superior to Her. Nothing is higher than Her. She is not dependent on praise, external prompting or any other authority."],"searchText":"541 अनुत्तमा • यदपेक्षयोत्तममन्यद्वस्तु नास्ति सा। • न नुत्ता परप्रेरिता मा बुद्धिरैश्वर्यं वा यस्या सा। • यदपेक्षयोत्तममन्यद्वस्तु — a thing superior in comparison with whom. • नास्ति — does not exist. • सा — she. • न — not. • नुत्ता — praised or prompted. • परप्रेरिता — impelled by another. • मा — measure, knowledge or power. • बुद्धिरैश्वर्यं — intellect or lordship. • वा — or. • यस्या — whose. • अनुत्तमा — she who has none superior. अनुत्तमा means one who has none superior to her. nothing is higher than her. she is not dependent on praise, external prompting or any other authority. the unsurpassed one: she is anuttamā because no reality stands above her. her sovereignty is independent, complete and final.","esoteric":["The Unsurpassed One: She is Anuttamā because no reality stands above Her. Her sovereignty is independent, complete and final."]},{"number":542,"name":"पुण्यकीर्तिः","samasa":["• पुण्या पुण्यप्रदा कीर्तिर्यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• पुण्या — holy, meritorious.","• पुण्यप्रदा — bestower of merit.","• कीर्तिर्यस्याः — whose fame.","• सा — she.","• पुण्यकीर्तिः — She whose fame is holy and meritorious."],"summary":["पुण्यकीर्तिः means one whose fame is holy and meritorious. Her praise itself is auspicious and bestows merit."],"searchText":"542 पुण्यकीर्तिः • पुण्या पुण्यप्रदा कीर्तिर्यस्याः सा। • पुण्या — holy, meritorious. • पुण्यप्रदा — bestower of merit. • कीर्तिर्यस्याः — whose fame. • सा — she. • पुण्यकीर्तिः — she whose fame is holy and meritorious. पुण्यकीर्तिः means one whose fame is holy and meritorious. her praise itself is auspicious and bestows merit. the purifying renown: her fame is puṇya. hearing, repeating and celebrating her glory purifies the mind and creates merit.","esoteric":["The Purifying Renown: Her fame is puṇya. Hearing, repeating and celebrating Her glory purifies the mind and creates merit."]},{"number":543,"name":"पुण्यलभ्या","samasa":["• पुण्यैः लभ्या।"],"wordByWord":["• पुण्यैः — through merit.","• लभ्या — attainable.","• पुण्यलभ्या — She who is attainable through merit."],"summary":["पुण्यलभ्या means one who can be attained through virtue and righteousness. Puṇya is merit from good actions, and through such puṇya Her blessings are attained. The righteous and wisdom-devoted behold Her, not those ruled by desire."],"searchText":"543 पुण्यलभ्या • पुण्यैः लभ्या। • पुण्यैः — through merit. • लभ्या — attainable. • पुण्यलभ्या — she who is attainable through merit. पुण्यलभ्या means one who can be attained through virtue and righteousness. puṇya is merit from good actions, and through such puṇya her blessings are attained. the righteous and wisdom-devoted behold her, not those ruled by desire. the attainment through merit: she is reached through puṇya, purity and right conduct. ego, deception and desire do not open the way to her.","esoteric":["The Attainment Through Merit: She is reached through puṇya, purity and right conduct. Ego, deception and desire do not open the way to Her."]},{"number":544,"name":"पुण्यश्रवणकीर्तना","samasa":["• पुण्ये विहितकर्मरूपे श्रवणकीर्तने यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• पुण्ये — in merit.","• विहितकर्मरूपे — in the form of prescribed action.","• श्रवणकीर्तने — hearing and chanting.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• पुण्यश्रवणकीर्तना — She whose hearing and chanting are meritorious."],"summary":["पुण्यश्रवणकीर्तना means one whose hearing and chanting are meritorious. Listening to and reciting Her names are themselves holy acts."],"searchText":"544 पुण्यश्रवणकीर्तना • पुण्ये विहितकर्मरूपे श्रवणकीर्तने यस्याः सा। • पुण्ये — in merit. • विहितकर्मरूपे — in the form of prescribed action. • श्रवणकीर्तने — hearing and chanting. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • पुण्यश्रवणकीर्तना — she whose hearing and chanting are meritorious. पुण्यश्रवणकीर्तना means one whose hearing and chanting are meritorious. listening to and reciting her names are themselves holy acts. the merit of sound: hearing and chanting her names purify the inner field. śravaṇa and kīrtana become direct acts of alignment with her.","esoteric":["The Merit of Sound: Hearing and chanting Her names purify the inner field. Śravaṇa and kīrtana become direct acts of alignment with Her."]},{"number":545,"name":"पुलोमजार्चिता","samasa":["• पुलोमतो जातया (इन्द्राण्या) अर्चिता"],"wordByWord":["• पुलोमतो — from Puloma.","• जातया — born of.","• इन्द्राण्या — by Indrāṇī.","• अर्चिता — worshipped.","• पुलोमजार्चिता — She who is worshipped by Pulomajā."],"summary":["पुलोमजार्चिता means one who is worshipped by Pulomajā. Pulomajā is Indrāṇī, the daughter of Puloma."],"searchText":"545 पुलोमजार्चिता • पुलोमतो जातया (इन्द्राण्या) अर्चिता • पुलोमतो — from puloma. • जातया — born of. • इन्द्राण्या — by indrāṇī. • अर्चिता — worshipped. • पुलोमजार्चिता — she who is worshipped by pulomajā. पुलोमजार्चिता means one who is worshipped by pulomajā. pulomajā is indrāṇī, the daughter of puloma. the worship of pulomajā: indrāṇī, the queenly daughter of puloma, worships her. this shows her supremacy even among celestial powers.","esoteric":["The Worship of Pulomajā: Indrāṇī, the queenly daughter of Puloma, worships Her. This shows Her supremacy even among celestial powers."]},{"number":546,"name":"बन्धमोचनी","samasa":["• बन्धं मोचयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• बन्धं — bondage.","• मोचयतीति — releases.","• बन्धमोचनी — She who releases bondage."],"summary":["बन्धमोचनी means one who releases beings from bondage. She frees beings from the bonds that hold them in limitation."],"searchText":"546 बन्धमोचनी • बन्धं मोचयतीति। • बन्धं — bondage. • मोचयतीति — releases. • बन्धमोचनी — she who releases bondage. बन्धमोचनी means one who releases beings from bondage. she frees beings from the bonds that hold them in limitation. the liberator from bondage: bandha is the bondage of ego, attachment and repeated birth. as bandhamocanī, she breaks these bonds and grants freedom.","esoteric":["The Liberator from Bondage: Bandha is the bondage of ego, attachment and repeated birth. As Bandhamocanī, She breaks these bonds and grants freedom."]},{"number":547,"name":"बन्धुरालका बर्बरालका","samasa":["• बन्धुरा बर्बरा अलकाः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• बन्धुरा — beautiful.","• बर्बरा — curly.","• अलकाः — locks of hair.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• बन्धुरालका बर्बरालका — She whose tresses are charming and curly."],"summary":["बन्धुरालका बर्बरालका means one who has charming, curly tresses. Her locks of hair are beautiful, curled and graceful."],"searchText":"547 बन्धुरालका बर्बरालका • बन्धुरा बर्बरा अलकाः यस्याः सा। • बन्धुरा — beautiful. • बर्बरा — curly. • अलकाः — locks of hair. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • बन्धुरालका बर्बरालका — she whose tresses are charming and curly. बन्धुरालका बर्बरालका means one who has charming, curly tresses. her locks of hair are beautiful, curled and graceful. the curled tresses: her curly hair suggests beauty, charm and the graceful movement of energy. the locks appear as flowing waves of divine splendour.","esoteric":["The Curled Tresses: Her curly hair suggests beauty, charm and the graceful movement of energy. The locks appear as flowing waves of divine splendour."]},{"number":548,"name":"विमर्शरूपिणी","samasa":["• विमर्शः एव रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["• विमर्शः — reflective consciousness, self-awareness.","• एव — itself, indeed.","• अस्याः — of Her.","• अस्तीति — is.","• विमर्शरूपिणी — She who is in the form of vimarśa."],"summary":["विमर्शरूपिणी means one who is in the form of vimarśa. Vimarśa is the self-awareness aspect of consciousness, without which pure prakāśa cannot appear as experience."],"searchText":"548 विमर्शरूपिणी • विमर्शः एव रूपम् अस्याः अस्तीति। • विमर्शः — reflective consciousness, self-awareness. • एव — itself, indeed. • अस्याः — of her. • अस्तीति — is. • विमर्शरूपिणी — she who is in the form of vimarśa. विमर्शरूपिणी means one who is in the form of vimarśa. vimarśa is the self-awareness aspect of consciousness, without which pure prakāśa cannot appear as experience. the self-aware light: prakāśa is self-luminous consciousness, and vimarśa is its self-awareness. she is that reflective power by which consciousness knows and manifests.","esoteric":["The Self-Aware Light: Prakāśa is self-luminous consciousness, and vimarśa is its self-awareness. She is that reflective power by which consciousness knows and manifests."]},{"number":549,"name":"विद्या","samasa":["• मोक्षप्रदज्ञानस्वरूपत्वाद्विद्या।"],"wordByWord":["• मोक्षप्रदज्ञानस्वरूपत्वाद्विद्या — vidyā because She is knowledge that grants liberation.","• विद्या — She who is liberating knowledge."],"summary":["विद्या means one who is liberating knowledge. She is the vidyā that grants mokṣa. Vidyā is the supreme knowledge by which the products of māyā are discerned and wisdom is recognized."],"searchText":"549 विद्या • मोक्षप्रदज्ञानस्वरूपत्वाद्विद्या। • मोक्षप्रदज्ञानस्वरूपत्वाद्विद्या — vidyā because she is knowledge that grants liberation. • विद्या — she who is liberating knowledge. विद्या means one who is liberating knowledge. she is the vidyā that grants mokṣa. vidyā is the supreme knowledge by which the products of māyā are discerned and wisdom is recognized. the knowledge of liberation: she is parāvidyā, direct knowledge that removes separation and reveals the self. through her, māyā is discerned and mokṣa becomes possible.","esoteric":["The Knowledge of Liberation: She is parāvidyā, direct knowledge that removes separation and reveals the Self. Through Her, māyā is discerned and mokṣa becomes possible."]},{"number":550,"name":"वियदादिजगत्प्रसूः","samasa":["• वियद्व्योम आदिर्यस्य तज्जगत्प्रसूते इति।"],"wordByWord":["• वियद्व्योम — ether or space.","• आदिर्यस्य — beginning with which.","• तज्जगत्प्रसूते — mother of that world.","• इति — thus.","• वियदादिजगत्प्रसूः — She who is the mother of the universe beginning with ether."],"summary":["वियदादिजगत्प्रसूः means one who is the mother of the universe beginning with ether. Ether, air, fire, water and earth are the primary elements of the manifest universe. Ether appears near yet becomes subtle and beyond grasp; likewise the Supreme Being seems understood yet remains beyond capture."],"searchText":"550 वियदादिजगत्प्रसूः • वियद्व्योम आदिर्यस्य तज्जगत्प्रसूते इति। • वियद्व्योम — ether or space. • आदिर्यस्य — beginning with which. • तज्जगत्प्रसूते — mother of that world. • इति — thus. • वियदादिजगत्प्रसूः — she who is the mother of the universe beginning with ether. वियदादिजगत्प्रसूः means one who is the mother of the universe beginning with ether. ether, air, fire, water and earth are the primary elements of the manifest universe. ether appears near yet becomes subtle and beyond grasp; likewise the supreme being seems understood yet remains beyond capture. the mother of elements: the universe unfolds from space into air, fire, water and earth. she is the primal mother before the first element and the ground of all manifestation.","esoteric":["The Mother of Elements: The universe unfolds from space into air, fire, water and earth. She is the primal mother before the first element and the ground of all manifestation."]},{"number":551,"name":"सर्वव्याधिप्रशमनी","samasa":["• सर्वेषां व्याधीनां प्रशमनी।"],"wordByWord":["• सर्वेषां — of all.","• व्याधीनां — of diseases.","• प्रशमनी — pacifier, remover.","• सर्वव्याधिप्रशमनी — She who pacifies all diseases."],"summary":["सर्वव्याधिप्रशमनी means one who cures or alleviates all illnesses and diseases. She pacifies every kind of disease."],"searchText":"551 सर्वव्याधिप्रशमनी • सर्वेषां व्याधीनां प्रशमनी। • सर्वेषां — of all. • व्याधीनां — of diseases. • प्रशमनी — pacifier, remover. • सर्वव्याधिप्रशमनी — she who pacifies all diseases. सर्वव्याधिप्रशमनी means one who cures or alleviates all illnesses and diseases. she pacifies every kind of disease. the healer of all diseases: vyādhi includes bodily illness and the deeper sickness of saṃsāric wandering. she cools suffering, removes disease and restores wholeness.","esoteric":["The Healer of All Diseases: Vyādhi includes bodily illness and the deeper sickness of saṃsāric wandering. She cools suffering, removes disease and restores wholeness."]},{"number":552,"name":"सर्वमृत्युनिवारिणी","samasa":["• सर्वमृत्यून् निवारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• सर्वमृत्यून् — all deaths.","• निवारयतीति — wards off.","• सर्वमृत्युनिवारिणी — She who wards off all forms of death."],"summary":["सर्वमृत्युनिवारिणी means one who dispels all forms of death. This includes untimely death and death through old age. Untimely death may arise from accident or fatal disease, and She prevents it. The fruits of actions are also called mṛtyus; She saves one from these by making one realize the Self and reach the nectar-like state."],"searchText":"552 सर्वमृत्युनिवारिणी • सर्वमृत्यून् निवारयतीति। • सर्वमृत्यून् — all deaths. • निवारयतीति — wards off. • सर्वमृत्युनिवारिणी — she who wards off all forms of death. सर्वमृत्युनिवारिणी means one who dispels all forms of death. this includes untimely death and death through old age. untimely death may arise from accident or fatal disease, and she prevents it. the fruits of actions are also called mṛtyus; she saves one from these by making one realize the self and reach the nectar-like state. the shield against mortality: she protects against apamṛtyu, untimely death, and also grants the deathless state by dissolving ego and leading the seeker beyond fear.","esoteric":["The Shield Against Mortality: She protects against apamṛtyu, untimely death, and also grants the deathless state by dissolving ego and leading the seeker beyond fear."]},{"number":553,"name":"अग्रगण्या","samasa":["• अग्रे गणयितुम् अर्हा।","• गणं लब्ध्री गण्या। अग्रे च सा गण्या च।"],"wordByWord":["• अग्रे — first, foremost.","• गणयितुम् — to be counted.","• अर्हा — worthy.","• गणं — group, category.","• लब्ध्री — attainer.","• गण्या — to be counted.","• च — and.","• सा — she.","• अग्रगण्या — She who deserves to be counted first."],"summary":["अग्रगण्या means one who deserves to be counted first. She is foremost among all and is worthy of being placed at the head of any enumeration."],"searchText":"553 अग्रगण्या • अग्रे गणयितुम् अर्हा। • गणं लब्ध्री गण्या। अग्रे च सा गण्या च। • अग्रे — first, foremost. • गणयितुम् — to be counted. • अर्हा — worthy. • गणं — group, category. • लब्ध्री — attainer. • गण्या — to be counted. • च — and. • सा — she. • अग्रगण्या — she who deserves to be counted first. अग्रगण्या means one who deserves to be counted first. she is foremost among all and is worthy of being placed at the head of any enumeration. the first principle: she is counted first because she stands before all dependent realities. everything else follows after her.","esoteric":["The First Principle: She is counted first because She stands before all dependent realities. Everything else follows after Her."]},{"number":554,"name":"अचिन्त्यरूपा","samasa":["• चिन्तयितुम् अशक्यं रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• चिन्तयितुम् — to think.","• अशक्यं — impossible.","• रूपं — form.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• अचिन्त्यरूपा — She whose form is beyond thought."],"summary":["अचिन्त्यरूपा means one whose form is beyond thought. Her nature cannot be grasped by ordinary mental conception."],"searchText":"554 अचिन्त्यरूपा • चिन्तयितुम् अशक्यं रूपं यस्याः सा। • चिन्तयितुम् — to think. • अशक्यं — impossible. • रूपं — form. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • अचिन्त्यरूपा — she whose form is beyond thought. अचिन्त्यरूपा means one whose form is beyond thought. her nature cannot be grasped by ordinary mental conception. beyond thought: the mind grasps limited objects, but her true form is not limited by time, space or attributes. she is realized directly, not confined by concepts.","esoteric":["Beyond Thought: The mind grasps limited objects, but Her true form is not limited by time, space or attributes. She is realized directly, not confined by concepts."]},{"number":555,"name":"कलिकल्मषनाशिनी","samasa":["• कलियुगे कल्मषानां नाशिनी।"],"wordByWord":["• कलियुगे — in the Kali age.","• कल्मषानां — of impurities or sins.","• नाशिनी — destroyer.","• कलिकल्मषनाशिनी — She who destroys the impurities of the Kali age."],"summary":["कलिकल्मषनाशिनी means one who destroys the sins and impurities of the Kali age."],"searchText":"555 कलिकल्मषनाशिनी • कलियुगे कल्मषानां नाशिनी। • कलियुगे — in the kali age. • कल्मषानां — of impurities or sins. • नाशिनी — destroyer. • कलिकल्मषनाशिनी — she who destroys the impurities of the kali age. कलिकल्मषनाशिनी means one who destroys the sins and impurities of the kali age. the purifier of the kali age: the kali age is marked by distraction, decline and impurity. her name destroys these distortions and purifies the seeker.","esoteric":["The Purifier of the Kali Age: The Kali age is marked by distraction, decline and impurity. Her name destroys these distortions and purifies the seeker."]},{"number":556,"name":"कात्यायनी","samasa":["• कतो नामर्षिः तस्यापत्यं स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["• कतो — from the sage named Kātyāyana.","• नामर्षिः — the sage so named.","• तस्यापत्यं — his descendant or offspring.","• स्त्री — female.","• कात्यायनी — She who is Kātyāyanī."],"summary":["कात्यायनी means one who is the daughter of the sage Kātyāyana. She is the deity formed from the collective brightness of all the devas, and She destroys Mahiṣāsura. She is also worshipped as Kātyāyanī in sacred places, and the gopikās worshipped Her during Mārgaśīrṣa month and obtained Kṛṣṇa as their husband. Kātyāyanī is also counted among the nine names of Durgā."],"searchText":"556 कात्यायनी • कतो नामर्षिः तस्यापत्यं स्त्री। • कतो — from the sage named kātyāyana. • नामर्षिः — the sage so named. • तस्यापत्यं — his descendant or offspring. • स्त्री — female. • कात्यायनी — she who is kātyāyanī. कात्यायनी means one who is the daughter of the sage kātyāyana. she is the deity formed from the collective brightness of all the devas, and she destroys mahiṣāsura. she is also worshipped as kātyāyanī in sacred places, and the gopikās worshipped her during mārgaśīrṣa month and obtained kṛṣṇa as their husband. kātyāyanī is also counted among the nine names of durgā. the warrior light: kātyāyanī is the unified force of divine radiance gathered into a protective warrior form. she arises when scattered powers must become one victorious śakti.","esoteric":["The Warrior Light: Kātyāyanī is the unified force of divine radiance gathered into a protective warrior form. She arises when scattered powers must become one victorious śakti."]},{"number":557,"name":"कालहन्त्री","samasa":["• कालस्य मृत्योर्हन्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["• कालस्य — of Time or death.","• मृत्योः — of death.","• हन्त्री — destroyer.","• कालहन्त्री — She who destroys Time or death."],"summary":["कालहन्त्री means one who is the destroyer of Time or Death. She is the destroyer even of Kāla, the power of death."],"searchText":"557 कालहन्त्री • कालस्य मृत्योर्हन्त्री। • कालस्य — of time or death. • मृत्योः — of death. • हन्त्री — destroyer. • कालहन्त्री — she who destroys time or death. कालहन्त्री means one who is the destroyer of time or death. she is the destroyer even of kāla, the power of death. the destroyer of time: kāla consumes all created beings, but she stands beyond kāla. by revealing deathless awareness, she cuts the fear of time and death.","esoteric":["The Destroyer of Time: Kāla consumes all created beings, but She stands beyond Kāla. By revealing deathless awareness, She cuts the fear of time and death."]},{"number":558,"name":"कमलाक्षनिषेविता","samasa":["• कमलाक्षेण विष्णुना नितरां सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["• कमलाक्षेण — by the lotus-eyed one.","• विष्णुना — by Viṣṇu.","• सेविता — worshipped.","• कमलाक्षनिषेविता — She who is worshipped by Kamalākṣa, Viṣṇu."],"summary":["कमलाक्षनिषेविता means one who is specially worshipped by lotus-eyed Mahāviṣṇu. Viṣṇu worships Her and thereby attains the state of Viṣṇu. The account of Viṣṇu worshipping with lotuses and offering his own eye when one lotus was short is also connected with this name. Since Śiva and Śakti are not different, that worship is also worship of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"558 कमलाक्षनिषेविता • कमलाक्षेण विष्णुना नितरां सेविता। • कमलाक्षेण — by the lotus-eyed one. • विष्णुना — by viṣṇu. • सेविता — worshipped. • कमलाक्षनिषेविता — she who is worshipped by kamalākṣa, viṣṇu. कमलाक्षनिषेविता means one who is specially worshipped by lotus-eyed mahāviṣṇu. viṣṇu worships her and thereby attains the state of viṣṇu. the account of viṣṇu worshipping with lotuses and offering his own eye when one lotus was short is also connected with this name. since śiva and śakti are not different, that worship is also worship of śrīdevī. the power worshipped by viṣṇu: kamalākṣa worships her as the ground of sustaining power. through her energy, preservation and cosmic order are maintained.","esoteric":["The Power Worshipped by Viṣṇu: Kamalākṣa worships Her as the ground of sustaining power. Through Her energy, preservation and cosmic order are maintained."]},{"number":559,"name":"ताम्बूलपूरितमुखी","samasa":["• ताम्बूलेन पूरितं मुखं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• ताम्बूलेन — with tāmbūla, betel leaf.","• पूरितं — filled.","• मुखं — mouth or face.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• ताम्बूलपूरितमुखी — She whose mouth is filled with tāmbūla."],"summary":["ताम्बूलपूरितमुखी means one whose mouth is filled with tāmbūla, betel leaves. The fragrance from Her mouth is a mark of royal enjoyment and auspicious beauty. Poets gained poetic excellence by receiving the juice of Her tāmbūla."],"searchText":"559 ताम्बूलपूरितमुखी • ताम्बूलेन पूरितं मुखं यस्याः सा। • ताम्बूलेन — with tāmbūla, betel leaf. • पूरितं — filled. • मुखं — mouth or face. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • ताम्बूलपूरितमुखी — she whose mouth is filled with tāmbūla. ताम्बूलपूरितमुखी means one whose mouth is filled with tāmbūla, betel leaves. the fragrance from her mouth is a mark of royal enjoyment and auspicious beauty. poets gained poetic excellence by receiving the juice of her tāmbūla. the fragrant mouth: tāmbūla reddens the mouth and gives fragrance. her tāmbūla-filled mouth suggests auspicious beauty, sweetness of speech and the giving of poetic power.","esoteric":["The Fragrant Mouth: Tāmbūla reddens the mouth and gives fragrance. Her tāmbūla-filled mouth suggests auspicious beauty, sweetness of speech and the giving of poetic power."]},{"number":560,"name":"दाडिमीकुसुमप्रभा","samasa":["• दाडिमीवृक्षस्य कुसुमस्येव प्रभा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• दाडिमीवृक्षस्य — of the pomegranate tree.","• कुसुमस्येव — like the flower.","• प्रभा — lustre.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• दाडिमीकुसुमप्रभा — She whose lustre is like a pomegranate flower."],"summary":["दाडिमीकुसुमप्रभा means one whose lustre is like the hue of a pomegranate flower. Her complexion has the vivid red colour of the brilliant pomegranate blossom."],"searchText":"560 दाडिमीकुसुमप्रभा • दाडिमीवृक्षस्य कुसुमस्येव प्रभा यस्याः सा। • दाडिमीवृक्षस्य — of the pomegranate tree. • कुसुमस्येव — like the flower. • प्रभा — lustre. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • दाडिमीकुसुमप्रभा — she whose lustre is like a pomegranate flower. दाडिमीकुसुमप्रभा means one whose lustre is like the hue of a pomegranate flower. her complexion has the vivid red colour of the brilliant pomegranate blossom. the crimson flower: the pomegranate blossom is intensely red and radiant. her colour shows vibrant will, beauty and auspicious energy.","esoteric":["The Crimson Flower: The pomegranate blossom is intensely red and radiant. Her colour shows vibrant will, beauty and auspicious energy."]},{"number":561,"name":"मृगाक्षी","samasa":["• मृगस्य अक्षिणी इव अक्षिणी यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• मृगस्य — of a deer.","• अक्षिणी — eyes.","• इव — as if.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• मृगाक्षी — She whose eyes are like those of a deer."],"summary":["मृगाक्षी means one who has eyes like those of a deer. Deer eyes move on all sides and are not fixed in one place; such wavering eyes add beauty. Her eyes move in this way so that Her compassionate glance may fall upon devotees on every side."],"searchText":"561 मृगाक्षी • मृगस्य अक्षिणी इव अक्षिणी यस्याः सा। • मृगस्य — of a deer. • अक्षिणी — eyes. • इव — as if. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • मृगाक्षी — she whose eyes are like those of a deer. मृगाक्षी means one who has eyes like those of a deer. deer eyes move on all sides and are not fixed in one place; such wavering eyes add beauty. her eyes move in this way so that her compassionate glance may fall upon devotees on every side. the deer-like gaze: her eyes are gentle, wide and compassionate. their restless grace also soothes the deer-like movement of the mind.","esoteric":["The Deer-Like Gaze: Her eyes are gentle, wide and compassionate. Their restless grace also soothes the deer-like movement of the mind."]},{"number":562,"name":"मोहिनी","samasa":["• मोहयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• मोहयतीति — enchants, deludes.","• मोहिनी — She who enchants."],"summary":["मोहिनी means one who enchants or bewitches. She deludes the entire universe through Her beauty and is therefore called Mohinī. Viṣṇu assumed the Mohinī form by meditating upon Śrīdevī. Mohinī is also connected with sacred reckonings of time and with the deity at Nivāsapura on the banks of the Pravara."],"searchText":"562 मोहिनी • मोहयतीति। • मोहयतीति — enchants, deludes. • मोहिनी — she who enchants. मोहिनी means one who enchants or bewitches. she deludes the entire universe through her beauty and is therefore called mohinī. viṣṇu assumed the mohinī form by meditating upon śrīdevī. mohinī is also connected with sacred reckonings of time and with the deity at nivāsapura on the banks of the pravara. the enchanting power: as mohinī, she veils the non-dual truth and makes the universe appear as many. this enchantment sustains the play of creation.","esoteric":["The Enchanting Power: As Mohinī, She veils the non-dual truth and makes the universe appear as many. This enchantment sustains the play of creation."]},{"number":563,"name":"मुख्या","samasa":["• मुखे सर्वादौ भवा।"],"wordByWord":["• मुखे — at the beginning or in the face.","• सर्वादौ — first of all.","• भवा — being, existing.","• मुख्या — She who is first or principal."],"summary":["मुख्या means one who is the first or principal. When a child is born, the face is the first part to appear; therefore what is first is called mukhya. She is first among all that has originated and foremost among all deities."],"searchText":"563 मुख्या • मुखे सर्वादौ भवा। • मुखे — at the beginning or in the face. • सर्वादौ — first of all. • भवा — being, existing. • मुख्या — she who is first or principal. मुख्या means one who is the first or principal. when a child is born, the face is the first part to appear; therefore what is first is called mukhya. she is first among all that has originated and foremost among all deities. the principal cause: she is mukhyā because she stands at the head of the causal order. before all secondary forces, she is the primary principle.","esoteric":["The Principal Cause: She is Mukhyā because She stands at the head of the causal order. Before all secondary forces, She is the primary principle."]},{"number":564,"name":"मृडानी","samasa":["• मृडस्य परमशिवस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["• मृडस्य — of Mṛḍa, Śiva.","• परमशिवस्य — of Paramaśiva.","• पत्नी — wife, consort.","• मृडानी — She who is the consort of Mṛḍa."],"summary":["मृडानी means one who is the consort of Mṛḍa, Paramaśiva. The root mṛḍ indicates giving happiness. Since Paramaśiva gives happiness to all, He is called Mṛḍa, and She is His consort, Mṛḍānī. Mṛḍānī is also indicated in Mahāṣoḍhānyāsa in the form of Pakṣa."],"searchText":"564 मृडानी • मृडस्य परमशिवस्य पत्नी। • मृडस्य — of mṛḍa, śiva. • परमशिवस्य — of paramaśiva. • पत्नी — wife, consort. • मृडानी — she who is the consort of mṛḍa. मृडानी means one who is the consort of mṛḍa, paramaśiva. the root mṛḍ indicates giving happiness. since paramaśiva gives happiness to all, he is called mṛḍa, and she is his consort, mṛḍānī. mṛḍānī is also indicated in mahāṣoḍhānyāsa in the form of pakṣa. the power of mercy: mṛḍa is the giver of happiness and compassion. as mṛḍānī, she is the śakti that expresses mercy, joy and forgiveness.","esoteric":["The Power of Mercy: Mṛḍa is the giver of happiness and compassion. As Mṛḍānī, She is the śakti that expresses mercy, joy and forgiveness."]},{"number":565,"name":"मित्ररूपिणी","samasa":["• मित्राणां सूर्याणामिव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["• मित्राणां — of Mitras, suns or friends.","• सूर्याणामिव — like the suns.","• रूपमस्याः — Her form.","• अस्तीति — is.","• मित्ररूपिणी — She who is in the form of Mitra."],"summary":["मित्ररूपिणी means one who is in the form of the Sun or in the form of a friend. Mitra is one of the twelve names of the Sun, so She is the illuminating and sustaining principle. In Śrīvidyā tantra, fire indicates Śiva, Moon indicates Śrīdevī, and Sun indicates their unified form. Mitra also means friend; thus She is the friendly Self."],"searchText":"565 मित्ररूपिणी • मित्राणां सूर्याणामिव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। • मित्राणां — of mitras, suns or friends. • सूर्याणामिव — like the suns. • रूपमस्याः — her form. • अस्तीति — is. • मित्ररूपिणी — she who is in the form of mitra. मित्ररूपिणी means one who is in the form of the sun or in the form of a friend. mitra is one of the twelve names of the sun, so she is the illuminating and sustaining principle. in śrīvidyā tantra, fire indicates śiva, moon indicates śrīdevī, and sun indicates their unified form. mitra also means friend; thus she is the friendly self. the solar friend: as mitra, she shines as life-giving solar radiance and also as the friendly self that guides the soul out of darkness.","esoteric":["The Solar Friend: As Mitra, She shines as life-giving solar radiance and also as the friendly Self that guides the soul out of darkness."]},{"number":566,"name":"नित्यतृप्ता","samasa":["• नित्यं तृप्ता।","• नित्येन स्वरूपानन्देन तृप्ता।"],"wordByWord":["• नित्यं — always, eternally.","• तृप्ता — satisfied.","• नित्येन — by the eternal.","• स्वरूपानन्देन — by the bliss of Her own nature.","• नित्यतृप्ता — She who is eternally content."],"summary":["नित्यतृप्ता means one who is eternally content. She is complete in every respect and needs nothing. Therefore She is always satisfied, contented by the eternal bliss of Her own true nature."],"searchText":"566 नित्यतृप्ता • नित्यं तृप्ता। • नित्येन स्वरूपानन्देन तृप्ता। • नित्यं — always, eternally. • तृप्ता — satisfied. • नित्येन — by the eternal. • स्वरूपानन्देन — by the bliss of her own nature. • नित्यतृप्ता — she who is eternally content. नित्यतृप्ता means one who is eternally content. she is complete in every respect and needs nothing. therefore she is always satisfied, contented by the eternal bliss of her own true nature. eternal fulness: her satisfaction does not depend on anything outside herself. she is always fulfilled in svarūpānanda, the bliss of her own nature.","esoteric":["Eternal Fulness: Her satisfaction does not depend on anything outside Herself. She is always fulfilled in svarūpānanda, the bliss of Her own nature."]},{"number":567,"name":"भक्तनिधिः","samasa":["• भक्तानां निधिः।"],"wordByWord":["• भक्तानां — of devotees.","• निधिः — treasure.","• भक्तनिधिः — She who is the treasure of devotees."],"summary":["भक्तनिधिः means one who is a treasure for devotees. She grants what devotees ask and gives even more than what is asked."],"searchText":"567 भक्तनिधिः • भक्तानां निधिः। • भक्तानां — of devotees. • निधिः — treasure. • भक्तनिधिः — she who is the treasure of devotees. भक्तनिधिः means one who is a treasure for devotees. she grants what devotees ask and gives even more than what is asked. the devotee’s treasure: a nidhi is inexhaustible wealth. for devotees, she is the hidden treasure that removes spiritual poverty and grants inner abundance.","esoteric":["The Devotee’s Treasure: A nidhi is inexhaustible wealth. For devotees, She is the hidden treasure that removes spiritual poverty and grants inner abundance."]},{"number":568,"name":"नियन्त्री","samasa":["• जगन्नियामक्त्वात् नियन्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["• नियन्त्री — controller, governor.","• नियन्त्री — She who guides and controls."],"summary":["नियन्त्री means one who guides and controls the universe. Because She governs and directs the whole universe, She is called Niyantrī."],"searchText":"568 नियन्त्री • जगन्नियामक्त्वात् नियन्त्री। • नियन्त्री — controller, governor. • नियन्त्री — she who guides and controls. नियन्त्री means one who guides and controls the universe. because she governs and directs the whole universe, she is called niyantrī. the cosmic controller: she is the inner governor of order, karma, nature and time. the universe moves under her direction.","esoteric":["The Cosmic Controller: She is the inner governor of order, karma, nature and time. The universe moves under Her direction."]},{"number":569,"name":"निखिलेश्वरी","samasa":["• निखिलस्य ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["• निखिलस्य — of all.","• ईश्वरी — ruler, sovereign.","• निखिलेश्वरी — She who is the ruler of all."],"summary":["निखिलेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of all. Since She controls the universe, She is the sovereign ruler of everything."],"searchText":"569 निखिलेश्वरी • निखिलस्य ईश्वरी। • निखिलस्य — of all. • ईश्वरी — ruler, sovereign. • निखिलेश्वरी — she who is the ruler of all. निखिलेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of all. since she controls the universe, she is the sovereign ruler of everything. sovereignty over all: nikhila means all without remainder. her rule extends over every part of reality.","esoteric":["Sovereignty Over All: Nikhila means all without remainder. Her rule extends over every part of reality."]},{"number":570,"name":"मैत्र्यादिवासनालभ्या","samasa":["• मैत्र्यादिभिः वासनाभिः लभ्या।"],"wordByWord":["• मैत्र्यादिभिः — by friendliness and the like.","• वासनाभिः — by dispositions or tendencies.","• लभ्या — attainable.","• मैत्र्यादिवासनालभ्या — She who is attained through dispositions such as friendliness."],"summary":["मैत्र्यादिवासनालभ्या means one who is attained through dispositions such as friendliness. Bad tendencies should be removed and good dispositions cultivated: friendship toward the happy, compassion toward the suffering, joy in the righteous, and indifference toward the sinful. These four dispositions are maitrī, karuṇā, muditā and upekṣā. They purify the mind and make Śrīdevī easy to attain."],"searchText":"570 मैत्र्यादिवासनालभ्या • मैत्र्यादिभिः वासनाभिः लभ्या। • मैत्र्यादिभिः — by friendliness and the like. • वासनाभिः — by dispositions or tendencies. • लभ्या — attainable. • मैत्र्यादिवासनालभ्या — she who is attained through dispositions such as friendliness. मैत्र्यादिवासनालभ्या means one who is attained through dispositions such as friendliness. bad tendencies should be removed and good dispositions cultivated: friendship toward the happy, compassion toward the suffering, joy in the righteous, and indifference toward the sinful. these four dispositions are maitrī, karuṇā, muditā and upekṣā. they purify the mind and make śrīdevī easy to attain. the ethical access path: maitrī, karuṇā, muditā and upekṣā cleanse the mind of jealousy, cruelty and agitation. through these dispositions, her light becomes easier to receive.","esoteric":["The Ethical Access Path: Maitrī, karuṇā, muditā and upekṣā cleanse the mind of jealousy, cruelty and agitation. Through these dispositions, Her light becomes easier to receive."]},{"number":571,"name":"महाप्रलयसाक्षिणी","samasa":["• महाप्रलये साक्षिणी।"],"wordByWord":["• महाप्रलये — in the great dissolution.","• साक्षिणी — witness.","• महाप्रलयसाक्षिणी — She who is the witness of the great dissolution."],"summary":["महाप्रलयसाक्षिणी means one who is the witness of the great dissolution. In the great dissolution, Brahmā and others dissolve, while Śrīdevī alone remains as the witness. A witness does not participate in the action and is not affected by its result. She is the witness of the great pralaya."],"searchText":"571 महाप्रलयसाक्षिणी • महाप्रलये साक्षिणी। • महाप्रलये — in the great dissolution. • साक्षिणी — witness. • महाप्रलयसाक्षिणी — she who is the witness of the great dissolution. महाप्रलयसाक्षिणी means one who is the witness of the great dissolution. in the great dissolution, brahmā and others dissolve, while śrīdevī alone remains as the witness. a witness does not participate in the action and is not affected by its result. she is the witness of the great pralaya. the witness of dissolution: during mahāpralaya, elements, time and beings dissolve. she remains as the silent sākṣiṇī, untouched and independent.","esoteric":["The Witness of Dissolution: During mahāpralaya, elements, time and beings dissolve. She remains as the silent sākṣiṇī, untouched and independent."]},{"number":572,"name":"पराशक्तिः","samasa":["• परा शक्तिः।","• परायाः (मन्त्रस्य शक्तिः।"],"wordByWord":["• परा — supreme.","• शक्तिः — power, energy.","• परायाः — of Parā or of the supreme mantra.","• मन्त्रस्य — of the mantra.","• पराशक्तिः — She who is the supreme power."],"summary":["पराशक्तिः means one who is the Supreme Power. Certain bodily elements are described as arising from Śakti and others from Śiva, and the tenth principle is called Parāśakti. Parāśakti also means very great energy. Śiva attains manifest greatness only through union with Śakti. His supreme Śakti is known in manifold forms, and whatever energy is found in any substance is Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"572 पराशक्तिः • परा शक्तिः। • परायाः (मन्त्रस्य शक्तिः। • परा — supreme. • शक्तिः — power, energy. • परायाः — of parā or of the supreme mantra. • मन्त्रस्य — of the mantra. • पराशक्तिः — she who is the supreme power. पराशक्तिः means one who is the supreme power. certain bodily elements are described as arising from śakti and others from śiva, and the tenth principle is called parāśakti. parāśakti also means very great energy. śiva attains manifest greatness only through union with śakti. his supreme śakti is known in manifold forms, and whatever energy is found in any substance is śrīdevī. the supreme energy: she is parāśakti, the primordial kinetic power of brahman. through her, non-dual awareness expresses will, manifests worlds and reveals its beauty.","esoteric":["The Supreme Energy: She is Parāśakti, the primordial kinetic power of Brahman. Through Her, non-dual awareness expresses will, manifests worlds and reveals its beauty."]},{"number":573,"name":"परानिष्ठा","samasa":["• परा निष्ठा।","• परायां निष्ठा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• परा — supreme.","• निष्ठा — final state, establishment.","• परायां — in the supreme.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• परानिष्ठा — She who is the supreme final establishment."],"summary":["परानिष्ठा means one who is the final end of speech, action and thought. All actions culminate in knowledge. The highest state is firm knowledge, supported by teacher, reasoning and experience, that the Self alone is pure non-dual Brahman. This is the highest culmination of teaching and direct experience."],"searchText":"573 परानिष्ठा • परा निष्ठा। • परायां निष्ठा यस्याः सा। • परा — supreme. • निष्ठा — final state, establishment. • परायां — in the supreme. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • परानिष्ठा — she who is the supreme final establishment. परानिष्ठा means one who is the final end of speech, action and thought. all actions culminate in knowledge. the highest state is firm knowledge, supported by teacher, reasoning and experience, that the self alone is pure non-dual brahman. this is the highest culmination of teaching and direct experience. the ultimate establishment: parāniṣṭhā is firm absorption in the supreme. in that state, the mind rests in non-dual brahman without wandering.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Establishment: Parāniṣṭhā is firm absorption in the supreme. In that state, the mind rests in non-dual Brahman without wandering."]},{"number":574,"name":"प्रज्ञानघनरूपिणी","samasa":["• प्रकृष्टेन ज्ञानेन घनं रूपमस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["• प्रकृष्टेन — by supreme, excellent.","• ज्ञानेन — knowledge.","• घनं — compact, solid mass.","• रूपमस्याः — Her form.","• प्रज्ञानघनरूपिणी — She whose form is a compact mass of supreme knowledge."],"summary":["प्रज्ञानघनरूपिणी means one who is of the form of pure, concentrated, supreme knowledge. Pra means superior and beyond ordinary mental modification. Jñāna is eternal wisdom. Ghana means compact, solid and not contaminated by ignorance. She is the solidified form of supreme wisdom, like a mass of one taste throughout."],"searchText":"574 प्रज्ञानघनरूपिणी • प्रकृष्टेन ज्ञानेन घनं रूपमस्याः इति। • प्रकृष्टेन — by supreme, excellent. • ज्ञानेन — knowledge. • घनं — compact, solid mass. • रूपमस्याः — her form. • प्रज्ञानघनरूपिणी — she whose form is a compact mass of supreme knowledge. प्रज्ञानघनरूपिणी means one who is of the form of pure, concentrated, supreme knowledge. pra means superior and beyond ordinary mental modification. jñāna is eternal wisdom. ghana means compact, solid and not contaminated by ignorance. she is the solidified form of supreme wisdom, like a mass of one taste throughout. the mass of consciousness: prajñānaghana is consciousness without gaps, division or foreign element. her form is dense, pure awareness throughout.","esoteric":["The Mass of Consciousness: Prajñānaghana is consciousness without gaps, division or foreign element. Her form is dense, pure awareness throughout."]},{"number":575,"name":"माध्वीपानालसा","samasa":["• माध्व्या पानेनालसा।"],"wordByWord":["• माध्व्या — by mādhvī drink.","• पानेन — by drinking.","• अलसा — languid.","• माध्वीपानालसा — She who is languid from drinking mādhvī."],"summary":["माध्वीपानालसा means one who is languid after drinking mādhvī. Mādhvī is a drink mixed with grapes and honey. In this setting madhu or liquor indicates supreme bliss, so the name means She is immersed in the bliss of the Supreme Self."],"searchText":"575 माध्वीपानालसा • माध्व्या पानेनालसा। • माध्व्या — by mādhvī drink. • पानेन — by drinking. • अलसा — languid. • माध्वीपानालसा — she who is languid from drinking mādhvī. माध्वीपानालसा means one who is languid after drinking mādhvī. mādhvī is a drink mixed with grapes and honey. in this setting madhu or liquor indicates supreme bliss, so the name means she is immersed in the bliss of the supreme self. the ecstasy of bliss: mādhvī here points to the nectar of supreme bliss. filled with that inner nectar, her active power becomes relaxed in ecstatic absorption.","esoteric":["The Ecstasy of Bliss: Mādhvī here points to the nectar of supreme bliss. Filled with that inner nectar, Her active power becomes relaxed in ecstatic absorption."]},{"number":576,"name":"मत्ता","samasa":["• मत्ता इव।","• मद्भावः (अहम्भावः)।"],"wordByWord":["• मत्ता — intoxicated.","• इव — as if.","• मद्भावः — state of I-ness or self-sense.","• अहम्भावः — ego-sense.","• मत्ता — She who appears intoxicated."],"summary":["मत्ता means one who appears intoxicated or unconscious. As in the previous name, this indicates the state caused by divine drink, understood as supreme bliss. Mat also indicates the Self and the sense of “I”; She is the pure I-sense of Paramaśiva."],"searchText":"576 मत्ता • मत्ता इव। • मद्भावः (अहम्भावः)। • मत्ता — intoxicated. • इव — as if. • मद्भावः — state of i-ness or self-sense. • अहम्भावः — ego-sense. • मत्ता — she who appears intoxicated. मत्ता means one who appears intoxicated or unconscious. as in the previous name, this indicates the state caused by divine drink, understood as supreme bliss. mat also indicates the self and the sense of “i”; she is the pure i-sense of paramaśiva. the bliss-filled i-sense: she is mattā because she is filled with the ecstasy of her own infinite being. her intoxication is pure awareness of “i am.”","esoteric":["The Bliss-Filled I-Sense: She is Mattā because She is filled with the ecstasy of Her own infinite being. Her intoxication is pure awareness of “I am.”"]},{"number":577,"name":"मातृकावर्णरूपिणी","samasa":["• मातृका (अकारादिक्षकारान्ताः)। तासां वर्णाः। तान्येव रूपं स्वरूपमस्याः इति।","• मातृकावर्णा (एकपञ्चाशत्) एव रूपमस्या इति।","• मातृकावर्णा एव रूपा निरूपका वाचका यस्याः इति।","• मातृकावर्णान् रूपयति (जनयति) इति।"],"wordByWord":["• मातृका — letters of the alphabet.","• अकारादिक्षकारान्ताः — from a to kṣa.","• तासां — of them.","• वर्णाः — letters or colours.","• तान्येव — those very.","• स्वरूपमस्याः — Her own form.","• एव — itself.","• यस्याः — whose.","• रूपयति — forms, manifests.","• जनयति — generates.","• मातृकावर्णरूपिणी — She who is in the form of the mātṛkā letters."],"summary":["मातृकावर्णरूपिणी means one who is in the form of all Sanskrit letters. She is in the form of the fifty-one letters. Letters give form and colour to words and are therefore called varṇas. She is the śakti that gives individuality to letters, the garland of letters, sound-Brahman, and the origin of the mātṛkā letters."],"searchText":"577 मातृकावर्णरूपिणी • मातृका (अकारादिक्षकारान्ताः)। तासां वर्णाः। तान्येव रूपं स्वरूपमस्याः इति। • मातृकावर्णा (एकपञ्चाशत्) एव रूपमस्या इति। • मातृकावर्णा एव रूपा निरूपका वाचका यस्याः इति। • मातृकावर्णान् रूपयति (जनयति) इति। • मातृका — letters of the alphabet. • अकारादिक्षकारान्ताः — from a to kṣa. • तासां — of them. • वर्णाः — letters or colours. • तान्येव — those very. • स्वरूपमस्याः — her own form. • एव — itself. • यस्याः — whose. • रूपयति — forms, manifests. • जनयति — generates. • मातृकावर्णरूपिणी — she who is in the form of the mātṛkā letters. मातृकावर्णरूपिणी means one who is in the form of all sanskrit letters. she is in the form of the fifty-one letters. letters give form and colour to words and are therefore called varṇas. she is the śakti that gives individuality to letters, the garland of letters, sound-brahman, and the origin of the mātṛkā letters. the letter matrix: mātṛkā is the array of sacred letters from a to kṣa. she is that phonic grid through which names, mantras and forms arise.","esoteric":["The Letter Matrix: Mātṛkā is the array of sacred letters from a to kṣa. She is that phonic grid through which names, mantras and forms arise."]},{"number":578,"name":"महाकैलासनिलया","samasa":["• महाकैलास एव निलयो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• महाकैलास — great Kailāsa.","• एव — itself.","• निलयः — abode.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• महाकैलासनिलया — She whose abode is Mahākailāsa."],"summary":["महाकैलासनिलया means one who resides in great Kailāsa. Mahākailāsa is beyond ordinary Kailāsa, the abode of Paramaśiva. The word mahā indicates greatness. Kailāsa is also interpreted as the Sahasrāra in the brahmarandhra, where Śiva in the form of bindu resides."],"searchText":"578 महाकैलासनिलया • महाकैलास एव निलयो यस्याः सा। • महाकैलास — great kailāsa. • एव — itself. • निलयः — abode. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • महाकैलासनिलया — she whose abode is mahākailāsa. महाकैलासनिलया means one who resides in great kailāsa. mahākailāsa is beyond ordinary kailāsa, the abode of paramaśiva. the word mahā indicates greatness. kailāsa is also interpreted as the sahasrāra in the brahmarandhra, where śiva in the form of bindu resides. the great kailāsa: mahākailāsa is the supreme inner summit where śiva and śakti rest in non-dual union. internally, it corresponds to the luminous crown centre.","esoteric":["The Great Kailāsa: Mahākailāsa is the supreme inner summit where Śiva and Śakti rest in non-dual union. Internally, it corresponds to the luminous crown centre."]},{"number":579,"name":"मृणालमृदुदोर्लता","samasa":["• मृणालमिव (बिसतन्तुः इव) मृद्व्यो दोर्लता यस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["• मृणालमिव — like a lotus fibre or stalk.","• बिसतन्तुः — lotus fibre.","• इव — as if.","• दोर्लता — creeper-like arms.","• यस्याः — whose.","• मृणालमृदुदोर्लता — She whose creeper-like arms are soft like lotus stalks."],"summary":["मृणालमृदुदोर्लता means one whose arms are soft and slender like lotus stalks. Her subtle fineness and slenderness are praised through the image of lotus fibre."],"searchText":"579 मृणालमृदुदोर्लता • मृणालमिव (बिसतन्तुः इव) मृद्व्यो दोर्लता यस्याः। • मृणालमिव — like a lotus fibre or stalk. • बिसतन्तुः — lotus fibre. • इव — as if. • दोर्लता — creeper-like arms. • यस्याः — whose. • मृणालमृदुदोर्लता — she whose creeper-like arms are soft like lotus stalks. मृणालमृदुदोर्लता means one whose arms are soft and slender like lotus stalks. her subtle fineness and slenderness are praised through the image of lotus fibre. the soft arms of grace: her arms hold cosmic implements, yet they are soft like mṛṇāla. her power works through gentleness and maternal grace.","esoteric":["The Soft Arms of Grace: Her arms hold cosmic implements, yet they are soft like mṛṇāla. Her power works through gentleness and maternal grace."]},{"number":580,"name":"महनीया","samasa":["• पूज्यत्वात् महनीया।"],"wordByWord":["• पूज्यत्वात् — because of being worthy of worship.","• महनीया — venerable.","• महनीया — She who is worthy of worship."],"summary":["महनीया means one who is worthy of worship by all. She deserves worship and honour."],"searchText":"580 महनीया • पूज्यत्वात् महनीया। • पूज्यत्वात् — because of being worthy of worship. • महनीया — venerable. • महनीया — she who is worthy of worship. महनीया means one who is worthy of worship by all. she deserves worship and honour. the venerable one: her very presence commands reverence. meditation on her worthiness creates humility and devotion.","esoteric":["The Venerable One: Her very presence commands reverence. Meditation on Her worthiness creates humility and devotion."]},{"number":581,"name":"दयामूर्तिः","samasa":["• दयैव मूर्तिः स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• दयैव — compassion itself.","• मूर्तिः — form, embodiment.","• स्वरूपं — nature, form.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• दयामूर्तिः — She whose form is compassion."],"summary":["दयामूर्तिः means one who is the personification of mercy and compassion. Her eyes move with waves of compassion, and compassion protects even those whose faults would otherwise disqualify them."],"searchText":"581 दयामूर्तिः • दयैव मूर्तिः स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। • दयैव — compassion itself. • मूर्तिः — form, embodiment. • स्वरूपं — nature, form. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • दयामूर्तिः — she whose form is compassion. दयामूर्तिः means one who is the personification of mercy and compassion. her eyes move with waves of compassion, and compassion protects even those whose faults would otherwise disqualify them. compassion incarnate: she does not merely perform merciful acts; compassion itself is her form. even correction and dissolution operate for the growth of beings.","esoteric":["Compassion Incarnate: She does not merely perform merciful acts; compassion itself is Her form. Even correction and dissolution operate for the growth of beings."]},{"number":582,"name":"महासाम्राज्यशालिनी","samasa":["• महत् च तत् साम्राज्यं च। तस्य शालिनी।"],"wordByWord":["• महत् — great.","• च — and.","• तत् — that.","• साम्राज्यं — empire.","• शालिनी — possessing.","• महासाम्राज्यशालिनी — She who possesses a great empire."],"summary":["महासाम्राज्यशालिनी means one who possesses a vast empire. A samrāṭ controls many kings; a mahāsamrāṭ controls many samrāṭs. This name is apt because She is not different from Parameśvara and is the empress of the dominion of Mahākailāsa."],"searchText":"582 महासाम्राज्यशालिनी • महत् च तत् साम्राज्यं च। तस्य शालिनी। • महत् — great. • च — and. • तत् — that. • साम्राज्यं — empire. • शालिनी — possessing. • महासाम्राज्यशालिनी — she who possesses a great empire. महासाम्राज्यशालिनी means one who possesses a vast empire. a samrāṭ controls many kings; a mahāsamrāṭ controls many samrāṭs. this name is apt because she is not different from parameśvara and is the empress of the dominion of mahākailāsa. empress of the vast realm: her empire is not limited territory. she rules the whole field of manifestation, law and liberation with supreme authority.","esoteric":["Empress of the Vast Realm: Her empire is not limited territory. She rules the whole field of manifestation, law and liberation with supreme authority."]},{"number":583,"name":"आत्मविद्या","samasa":["• आत्मनः विद्या।"],"wordByWord":["• आत्मनः — of the Self.","• विद्या — knowledge, doctrine.","• आत्मविद्या — She who is knowledge of the Self."],"summary":["आत्मविद्या means one who is the doctrine that helps one understand the Self. This vidyā teaches the form of Brahman. She bestows the knowledge of Brahman, and this name is also connected with Turīya Gāyatrī of Mahāṣoḍhānyāsa."],"searchText":"583 आत्मविद्या • आत्मनः विद्या। • आत्मनः — of the self. • विद्या — knowledge, doctrine. • आत्मविद्या — she who is knowledge of the self. आत्मविद्या means one who is the doctrine that helps one understand the self. this vidyā teaches the form of brahman. she bestows the knowledge of brahman, and this name is also connected with turīya gāyatrī of mahāṣoḍhānyāsa. the knowledge of the self: as ātmavidyā, she reveals the identity of the individual self with the universal self. realizing her is recognizing one’s true nature.","esoteric":["The Knowledge of the Self: As Ātmavidyā, She reveals the identity of the individual self with the universal Self. Realizing Her is recognizing one’s true nature."]},{"number":584,"name":"महाविद्या","samasa":["• महती (सर्वानर्थनिवारका) च असौ विद्या च।"],"wordByWord":["• महती — great.","• सर्वानर्थनिवारका — remover of all misfortunes.","• च — and.","• विद्या — knowledge, doctrine.","• महाविद्या — She who is the great vidyā."],"summary":["महाविद्या means one who is the great doctrine. Ātmavidyā is great because it teaches Brahman and is therefore called Mahāvidyā. She is also Mahatī, the great one, because She removes all sorrows. Navadurgā Vidyā or Vanadurgā Vidyā, and Caṇḍī Navākṣarī Vidyā, are also connected with this name."],"searchText":"584 महाविद्या • महती (सर्वानर्थनिवारका) च असौ विद्या च। • महती — great. • सर्वानर्थनिवारका — remover of all misfortunes. • च — and. • विद्या — knowledge, doctrine. • महाविद्या — she who is the great vidyā. महाविद्या means one who is the great doctrine. ātmavidyā is great because it teaches brahman and is therefore called mahāvidyā. she is also mahatī, the great one, because she removes all sorrows. navadurgā vidyā or vanadurgā vidyā, and caṇḍī navākṣarī vidyā, are also connected with this name. the great vidyā: she is mahāvidyā because her knowledge removes the deepest sorrow and confusion. her path leads from suffering to freedom.","esoteric":["The Great Vidyā: She is Mahāvidyā because Her knowledge removes the deepest sorrow and confusion. Her path leads from suffering to freedom."]},{"number":585,"name":"श्रीविद्या","samasa":["• श्रीश्चासौ विद्या च।"],"wordByWord":["• श्रीश्चासौ — She who is Śrī.","• विद्या — knowledge, doctrine.","• च — and.","• श्रीविद्या — She who is Śrīvidyā."],"summary":["श्रीविद्या means one who is in the form of Pañcadaśī Vidyā. Vidyā has four forms: Yajña Vidyā, Mahāvidyā, Guhyavidyā and Ātmavidyā. She is all these forms and bestows liberation. Each group of the Pañcadaśī mantra gives the meaning of the Gāyatrī mantra. It is called Śrīvidyā because it gives extraordinary meanings in very few letters, and Śrīvidyā alone is the path to liberation."],"searchText":"585 श्रीविद्या • श्रीश्चासौ विद्या च। • श्रीश्चासौ — she who is śrī. • विद्या — knowledge, doctrine. • च — and. • श्रीविद्या — she who is śrīvidyā. श्रीविद्या means one who is in the form of pañcadaśī vidyā. vidyā has four forms: yajña vidyā, mahāvidyā, guhyavidyā and ātmavidyā. she is all these forms and bestows liberation. each group of the pañcadaśī mantra gives the meaning of the gāyatrī mantra. it is called śrīvidyā because it gives extraordinary meanings in very few letters, and śrīvidyā alone is the path to liberation. the śrīvidyā form: she is the living body of the pañcadaśī and ṣoḍaśī mantric current. śrīvidyā unites worldly auspiciousness with final liberation.","esoteric":["The Śrīvidyā Form: She is the living body of the Pañcadaśī and Ṣoḍaśī mantric current. Śrīvidyā unites worldly auspiciousness with final liberation."]},{"number":586,"name":"कामसेविता","samasa":["• कामेन सेविता (उपासिता)।"],"wordByWord":["• कामेन — by Kāma.","• सेविता — worshipped.","• उपासिता — adored.","• कामसेविता — She who is worshipped by Kāma."],"summary":["कामसेविता means one who is adored by Kāma. Kāma here indicates Mahākāmeśvara, who worshipped Her. Mahākāmeśvara and Kāmeśvarī mutually acted as teacher and disciple. Kāma also indicates the bodiless god of love, the presiding seer of Kādi Vidyā, another form of Pañcadaśī Vidyā. Kāmadeva worshipped Śrīdevī and received Her blessings; his power succeeds only through Her gracious glance."],"searchText":"586 कामसेविता • कामेन सेविता (उपासिता)। • कामेन — by kāma. • सेविता — worshipped. • उपासिता — adored. • कामसेविता — she who is worshipped by kāma. कामसेविता means one who is adored by kāma. kāma here indicates mahākāmeśvara, who worshipped her. mahākāmeśvara and kāmeśvarī mutually acted as teacher and disciple. kāma also indicates the bodiless god of love, the presiding seer of kādi vidyā, another form of pañcadaśī vidyā. kāmadeva worshipped śrīdevī and received her blessings; his power succeeds only through her gracious glance. the kāma lineage: kāma can indicate kāmadeva and also paramaśiva. both point to her as the power worshipped at the heart of desire, mantra and cosmic play.","esoteric":["The Kāma Lineage: Kāma can indicate Kāmadeva and also Paramaśiva. Both point to Her as the power worshipped at the heart of desire, mantra and cosmic play."]},{"number":587,"name":"श्रीषोडशाक्षरीविद्या","samasa":["• षोडशानामक्षराणां समाहारः षोडशाक्षरी। श्रीयुक्ता षोडशाक्षरी। सा च असौ विद्या च।","• श्रीः इति षोडशमक्षरं यस्यां तादृशी च असौ विद्या च।"],"wordByWord":["• समाहारः — collection.","• षोडशाक्षरी — sixteen-lettered.","• श्रीयुक्ता — endowed with Śrī.","• सा — she.","• च — and.","• विद्या — knowledge, doctrine.","• श्रीषोडशाक्षरीविद्या — She who is the Śrī Ṣoḍaśākṣarī Vidyā."],"summary":["श्रीषोडशाक्षरीविद्या means one who is in the form of the sixteen-lettered mantra. By adding one seed-letter to the Pañcadaśī mantra, the sixteen-lettered vidyā is obtained. Mahāṣoḍaśī has different versions in mantra-śāstra and must be learned through a proper teacher. Ātmavidyā, Mahāvidyā, Śrīvidyā and this name indicate successive forms of sacred knowledge, including the mantra-form and Parabrahman-form of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"587 श्रीषोडशाक्षरीविद्या • षोडशानामक्षराणां समाहारः षोडशाक्षरी। श्रीयुक्ता षोडशाक्षरी। सा च असौ विद्या च। • श्रीः इति षोडशमक्षरं यस्यां तादृशी च असौ विद्या च। • समाहारः — collection. • षोडशाक्षरी — sixteen-lettered. • श्रीयुक्ता — endowed with śrī. • सा — she. • च — and. • विद्या — knowledge, doctrine. • श्रीषोडशाक्षरीविद्या — she who is the śrī ṣoḍaśākṣarī vidyā. श्रीषोडशाक्षरीविद्या means one who is in the form of the sixteen-lettered mantra. by adding one seed-letter to the pañcadaśī mantra, the sixteen-lettered vidyā is obtained. mahāṣoḍaśī has different versions in mantra-śāstra and must be learned through a proper teacher. ātmavidyā, mahāvidyā, śrīvidyā and this name indicate successive forms of sacred knowledge, including the mantra-form and parabrahman-form of śrīdevī. the sixteen-syllabled vidyā: she is the ṣoḍaśī mantra, the sixteenfold completion of the śrīvidyā current. it is a guarded mantra-form of liberation.","esoteric":["The Sixteen-Syllabled Vidyā: She is the Ṣoḍaśī mantra, the sixteenfold completion of the Śrīvidyā current. It is a guarded mantra-form of liberation."]},{"number":588,"name":"त्रिकूटा","samasa":["• त्रयाणां (ब्रह्मादीनामवस्थापीठलोकगुणादीनां वा) कूटं (समूहः) यस्यां सा।","• वाग्भवादिकूटत्रयाभिन्ना।"],"wordByWord":["• त्रयाणां — of three.","• कूटं — group, section.","• समूहः — collection.","• सा — she.","• वाग्भवादिकूटत्रयाभिन्ना — non-different from the three kūṭas beginning with Vāgbhava.","• त्रिकूटा — She who has three kūṭas."],"summary":["त्रिकूटा means one who has three groups or kūṭas. Oṃ has three parts: A, U and M. There are three deities, three worlds, three states of the soul, three bodies, three guṇas, three times and three mantra-kāṇḍas. In Śrīvidyā, the three kūṭas are Vāgbhava-kūṭa, Kāmarāja-kūṭa and Śakti-kūṭa. She is the form of all that exists in groups of three."],"searchText":"588 त्रिकूटा • त्रयाणां (ब्रह्मादीनामवस्थापीठलोकगुणादीनां वा) कूटं (समूहः) यस्यां सा। • वाग्भवादिकूटत्रयाभिन्ना। • त्रयाणां — of three. • कूटं — group, section. • समूहः — collection. • सा — she. • वाग्भवादिकूटत्रयाभिन्ना — non-different from the three kūṭas beginning with vāgbhava. • त्रिकूटा — she who has three kūṭas. त्रिकूटा means one who has three groups or kūṭas. oṃ has three parts: a, u and m. there are three deities, three worlds, three states of the soul, three bodies, three guṇas, three times and three mantra-kāṇḍas. in śrīvidyā, the three kūṭas are vāgbhava-kūṭa, kāmarāja-kūṭa and śakti-kūṭa. she is the form of all that exists in groups of three. the three mantric peaks: she is the triadic structure of śrīvidyā: vāgbhava-kūṭa, kāmarāja-kūṭa and śakti-kūṭa. these three peaks map mantra, form and consciousness.","esoteric":["The Three Mantric Peaks: She is the triadic structure of Śrīvidyā: Vāgbhava-kūṭa, Kāmarāja-kūṭa and Śakti-kūṭa. These three peaks map mantra, form and consciousness."]},{"number":589,"name":"कामकोटिका","samasa":["• कामः (परशिवः) एव कोटिः (एकदेशः) यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• कामः — Kāma, desire or Paramaśiva.","• परशिवः — Paramaśiva.","• एव — itself.","• कोटिः — limit, point, section.","• एकदेशः — one part.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• कामकोटिका — She who is Kāmakotikā."],"summary":["कामकोटिका means one who is in the form of Kāmakoti. Since the Supreme Being is the unified form of Śiva and Śakti, Śrīdevī is called Kāmakotikā. She is also identified with the Kāmakoti Pīṭha at Kāñcīpuram. She is the limit or culmination of kāma, understood as the highest desire, liberation. This is also interpreted as residence in Śrīcakra."],"searchText":"589 कामकोटिका • कामः (परशिवः) एव कोटिः (एकदेशः) यस्याः सा। • कामः — kāma, desire or paramaśiva. • परशिवः — paramaśiva. • एव — itself. • कोटिः — limit, point, section. • एकदेशः — one part. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • कामकोटिका — she who is kāmakotikā. कामकोटिका means one who is in the form of kāmakoti. since the supreme being is the unified form of śiva and śakti, śrīdevī is called kāmakotikā. she is also identified with the kāmakoti pīṭha at kāñcīpuram. she is the limit or culmination of kāma, understood as the highest desire, liberation. this is also interpreted as residence in śrīcakra. the apex of kāma: kāma is the highest attraction toward union, and koṭi is the limit or summit. she is the culmination where śiva and śakti are one.","esoteric":["The Apex of Kāma: Kāma is the highest attraction toward union, and koṭi is the limit or summit. She is the culmination where Śiva and Śakti are one."]},{"number":590,"name":"कटाक्षकिङ्करीभूतकमलाकोटिसेविता","samasa":["• कटाक्षस्य किङ्करीभूताभिः कमलानां (लक्ष्मीणां) कोटिभिः सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["• कटाक्षस्य — of the glance.","• किङ्करीभूताभिः — made into attendants.","• कमलानां — of Lakṣmīs.","• लक्ष्मीणां — of Lakṣmīs.","• कोटिभिः — by crores.","• सेविता — worshipped.","• कटाक्षकिङ्करीभूतकमलाकोटिसेविता — She who is served by crores of Lakṣmīs made attendants by Her glance."],"summary":["कटाक्षकिङ्करीभूतकमलाकोटिसेविता means one who is served by crores of Lakṣmīs made attendants by Her mere glance. If the glance of Lakṣmī for even a moment makes one wealthy, the greatness of Śrīdevī, served by crores of Lakṣmīs, is beyond imagination. If Her benign glance falls on a devotee, crores of Lakṣmīs attend him."],"searchText":"590 कटाक्षकिङ्करीभूतकमलाकोटिसेविता • कटाक्षस्य किङ्करीभूताभिः कमलानां (लक्ष्मीणां) कोटिभिः सेविता। • कटाक्षस्य — of the glance. • किङ्करीभूताभिः — made into attendants. • कमलानां — of lakṣmīs. • लक्ष्मीणां — of lakṣmīs. • कोटिभिः — by crores. • सेविता — worshipped. • कटाक्षकिङ्करीभूतकमलाकोटिसेविता — she who is served by crores of lakṣmīs made attendants by her glance. कटाक्षकिङ्करीभूतकमलाकोटिसेविता means one who is served by crores of lakṣmīs made attendants by her mere glance. if the glance of lakṣmī for even a moment makes one wealthy, the greatness of śrīdevī, served by crores of lakṣmīs, is beyond imagination. if her benign glance falls on a devotee, crores of lakṣmīs attend him. the ground of abundance: lakṣmī herself is a form of wealth and grace, yet countless lakṣmīs become attendants through her side-glance. her grace brings boundless material and spiritual wealth.","esoteric":["The Ground of Abundance: Lakṣmī herself is a form of wealth and grace, yet countless Lakṣmīs become attendants through Her side-glance. Her grace brings boundless material and spiritual wealth."]},{"number":591,"name":"शिरःस्थिता","samasa":["• शिरसि ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["• शिरसि — in the head.","• ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे — in the brahmarandhra.","• स्थिता — situated.","• शिरःस्थिता — She who resides in the head."],"summary":["शिरःस्थिता means one who resides in the head. She resides in the brahmarandhra, assuming the form of a teacher. She is also in the form of the final mahābindu in the sound m of the seed hrīṃ, to be learned through a teacher."],"searchText":"591 शिरःस्थिता • शिरसि ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे स्थिता। • शिरसि — in the head. • ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे — in the brahmarandhra. • स्थिता — situated. • शिरःस्थिता — she who resides in the head. शिरःस्थिता means one who resides in the head. she resides in the brahmarandhra, assuming the form of a teacher. she is also in the form of the final mahābindu in the sound m of the seed hrīṃ, to be learned through a teacher. the crown station: she resides in the brahmarandhra at the peak of the head, as pure white light and the giver of nectar flowing through the subtle channels.","esoteric":["The Crown Station: She resides in the brahmarandhra at the peak of the head, as pure white light and the giver of nectar flowing through the subtle channels."]},{"number":592,"name":"चन्द्रनिभा","samasa":["• (ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे) चन्द्रस्य निभा (सदृशी)।"],"wordByWord":["• ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे — in the brahmarandhra.","• चन्द्रस्य — of the Moon.","• निभा — similarity, likeness.","• सदृशी — similar.","• चन्द्रनिभा — She whose lustre is like the Moon."],"summary":["चन्द्रनिभा means one whose lustre is like the Moon. In the lower part of the brahmarandhra there is a moon connected with the third division of Pañcadaśī Vidyā; therefore She is called Candranibhā."],"searchText":"592 चन्द्रनिभा • (ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे) चन्द्रस्य निभा (सदृशी)। • ब्रह्मरन्ध्रे — in the brahmarandhra. • चन्द्रस्य — of the moon. • निभा — similarity, likeness. • सदृशी — similar. • चन्द्रनिभा — she whose lustre is like the moon. चन्द्रनिभा means one whose lustre is like the moon. in the lower part of the brahmarandhra there is a moon connected with the third division of pañcadaśī vidyā; therefore she is called candranibhā. the moonlike radiance: at the head centre, her light is cool, white and soothing like the full moon, calming inner heat and restlessness.","esoteric":["The Moonlike Radiance: At the head centre, Her light is cool, white and soothing like the full moon, calming inner heat and restlessness."]},{"number":593,"name":"भालस्था","samasa":["• भाले तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• भाले — in the forehead.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides.","• भालस्था — She who resides in the forehead."],"summary":["भालस्था means one who resides in the forehead. She abides in the Ājñā chakra in the forehead in the form of the bindu of the syllable hrīṃ."],"searchText":"593 भालस्था • भाले तिष्ठतीति। • भाले — in the forehead. • तिष्ठतीति — abides. • भालस्था — she who resides in the forehead. भालस्था means one who resides in the forehead. she abides in the ājñā chakra in the forehead in the form of the bindu of the syllable hrīṃ. the forehead station: at the forehead, she shines as the bindu of inner command, vision and discernment.","esoteric":["The Forehead Station: At the forehead, She shines as the bindu of inner command, vision and discernment."]},{"number":594,"name":"इन्द्रधनुष्प्रभा","samasa":["• इन्द्रधनुः इव प्रकर्षेण भातीति।"],"wordByWord":["• इन्द्रधनुः — rainbow, Indra’s bow.","• इव — as if.","• प्रकर्षेण — excellently.","• भातीति — shines.","• इन्द्रधनुष्प्रभा — She whose brightness is like a rainbow."],"summary":["इन्द्रधनुष्प्रभा means one whose brightness is like a rainbow. Indradhanuḥ means the bow of Indra, the rainbow. The bindu and crescent in the forehead are forms of light; the bindu shines like a lamp, with the crescent above it."],"searchText":"594 इन्द्रधनुष्प्रभा • इन्द्रधनुः इव प्रकर्षेण भातीति। • इन्द्रधनुः — rainbow, indra’s bow. • इव — as if. • प्रकर्षेण — excellently. • भातीति — shines. • इन्द्रधनुष्प्रभा — she whose brightness is like a rainbow. इन्द्रधनुष्प्रभा means one whose brightness is like a rainbow. indradhanuḥ means the bow of indra, the rainbow. the bindu and crescent in the forehead are forms of light; the bindu shines like a lamp, with the crescent above it. the rainbow light: at the forehead, her radiance appears as many-coloured light, like pure light dividing into subtle channels of perception.","esoteric":["The Rainbow Light: At the forehead, Her radiance appears as many-coloured light, like pure light dividing into subtle channels of perception."]},{"number":595,"name":"हृदयस्था","samasa":["• हृदये तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• हृदये — in the heart.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides.","• हृदयस्था — She who resides in the heart."],"summary":["हृदयस्था means one who resides in the heart. She is to be meditated upon in the heart. Here the heart indicates the parā-bīja, and the entire moving and unmoving universe is present there in seed-form."],"searchText":"595 हृदयस्था • हृदये तिष्ठतीति। • हृदये — in the heart. • तिष्ठतीति — abides. • हृदयस्था — she who resides in the heart. हृदयस्था means one who resides in the heart. she is to be meditated upon in the heart. here the heart indicates the parā-bīja, and the entire moving and unmoving universe is present there in seed-form. the heart station: she rests in the heart as witness-light, devotion and emotional balance. in that subtle heart, the universe exists in seed-form.","esoteric":["The Heart Station: She rests in the heart as witness-light, devotion and emotional balance. In that subtle heart, the universe exists in seed-form."]},{"number":596,"name":"रविप्रख्या","samasa":["• रवेः प्रख्या (सदृशा)।"],"wordByWord":["• रवेः — of the Sun.","• प्रख्या — likeness.","• रविप्रख्या — She whose brightness is like the Sun."],"summary":["रविप्रख्या means one who has brightness like the Sun. In the heart there is a solar disc connected with the second division of the Pañcadaśī mantra. Therefore Śrīdevī is called Raviprakhyā."],"searchText":"596 रविप्रख्या • रवेः प्रख्या (सदृशा)। • रवेः — of the sun. • प्रख्या — likeness. • रविप्रख्या — she whose brightness is like the sun. रविप्रख्या means one who has brightness like the sun. in the heart there is a solar disc connected with the second division of the pañcadaśī mantra. therefore śrīdevī is called raviprakhyā. the solar heart: her heart-radiance is warm and brilliant like the sun, burning away fear, doubt and inner obstruction.","esoteric":["The Solar Heart: Her heart-radiance is warm and brilliant like the sun, burning away fear, doubt and inner obstruction."]},{"number":597,"name":"त्रिकोणान्तरदीपिका","samasa":["• (मूलाधारे) त्रिकोणस्य आन्तरे दीपिका।"],"wordByWord":["• त्रिकोणस्य — of the triangle.","• आन्तरे — inside.","• दीपिका — lamp/light.","• त्रिकोणान्तरदीपिका — She who is the lamp within the triangle."],"summary":["त्रिकोणान्तरदीपिका means one who is like a light within a triangle. In the pericarp of the Mūlādhāra there is a triangle, and within it a disc of fire connected with the first division of the Pañcadaśī mantra. Fire in Mūlādhāra, the Sun in the heart and the Moon below the brahmarandhra together form the threefold ancient mantra."],"searchText":"597 त्रिकोणान्तरदीपिका • (मूलाधारे) त्रिकोणस्य आन्तरे दीपिका। • त्रिकोणस्य — of the triangle. • आन्तरे — inside. • दीपिका — lamp/light. • त्रिकोणान्तरदीपिका — she who is the lamp within the triangle. त्रिकोणान्तरदीपिका means one who is like a light within a triangle. in the pericarp of the mūlādhāra there is a triangle, and within it a disc of fire connected with the first division of the pañcadaśī mantra. fire in mūlādhāra, the sun in the heart and the moon below the brahmarandhra together form the threefold ancient mantra. the lamp of the root: in the mūlādhāra triangle, she shines like a steady lamp. this is the dormant kuṇḍalinī fire that holds the body’s vitality.","esoteric":["The Lamp of the Root: In the Mūlādhāra triangle, She shines like a steady lamp. This is the dormant Kuṇḍalinī fire that holds the body’s vitality."]},{"number":598,"name":"दाक्षायणी","samasa":["• दक्षस्य कन्या।","• दाक्षायणयज्ञरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["• दक्षस्य — of Dakṣa.","• कन्या — daughter.","• दाक्षायणयज्ञरूपा — in the form of the Dākṣāyaṇa sacrifice.","• दाक्षायणी — She who is the daughter of Dakṣa."],"summary":["दाक्षायणी means one who is the daughter of Dakṣa. Dākṣāyaṇī means the wife of Śiva and also refers to Rohiṇī and other constellations, daughters of Dakṣa Prajāpati. Dākṣāyaṇa is also a sacrifice involving repetition of darśa and pūrṇamāsa rites; She is in that form too."],"searchText":"598 दाक्षायणी • दक्षस्य कन्या। • दाक्षायणयज्ञरूपा। • दक्षस्य — of dakṣa. • कन्या — daughter. • दाक्षायणयज्ञरूपा — in the form of the dākṣāyaṇa sacrifice. • दाक्षायणी — she who is the daughter of dakṣa. दाक्षायणी means one who is the daughter of dakṣa. dākṣāyaṇī means the wife of śiva and also refers to rohiṇī and other constellations, daughters of dakṣa prajāpati. dākṣāyaṇa is also a sacrifice involving repetition of darśa and pūrṇamāsa rites; she is in that form too. the daughter of dakṣa: as dākṣāyaṇī, she appears as satī and also as the principle that gives sacred action its inner validity.","esoteric":["The Daughter of Dakṣa: As Dākṣāyaṇī, She appears as Satī and also as the principle that gives sacred action its inner validity."]},{"number":599,"name":"दैत्यहन्त्री","samasa":["• दैत्यानां भण्डासुरादीनां हन्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["• दैत्यानां — of demons.","• भण्डासुरादीनां — of Bhaṇḍāsura and others.","• हन्त्री — destroyer.","• दैत्यहन्त्री — She who destroys demons."],"summary":["दैत्यहन्त्री means one who slays demons such as Bhaṇḍāsura. She destroys hostile and demonic forces."],"searchText":"599 दैत्यहन्त्री • दैत्यानां भण्डासुरादीनां हन्त्री। • दैत्यानां — of demons. • भण्डासुरादीनां — of bhaṇḍāsura and others. • हन्त्री — destroyer. • दैत्यहन्त्री — she who destroys demons. दैत्यहन्त्री means one who slays demons such as bhaṇḍāsura. she destroys hostile and demonic forces. the destroyer of inner demons: daityas also represent ego, pride and inner chaos. as daityahantrī, she destroys those distortions and restores dharma.","esoteric":["The Destroyer of Inner Demons: Daityas also represent ego, pride and inner chaos. As Daityahantrī, She destroys those distortions and restores dharma."]},{"number":600,"name":"दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी","samasa":["• दक्षस्य (दक्षयोः) यज्ञं विनाशयितुं शीलमस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["• दक्षस्य — of Dakṣa.","• यज्ञं — sacrifice.","• विनाशयितुं — to destroy.","• शीलमस्याः — Her nature is.","• दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी — She who destroyed Dakṣa’s sacrifice."],"summary":["दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी means one who destroyed the sacrifice of Dakṣa. Dakṣa, out of ego, did not honour Śiva or give Him His proper offering; therefore the sacrifice was destroyed. Though Śiva and His attendants performed the destruction, Śrīdevī was the instrument of that destruction, and so the name belongs to Her."],"searchText":"600 दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी • दक्षस्य (दक्षयोः) यज्ञं विनाशयितुं शीलमस्याः। • दक्षस्य — of dakṣa. • यज्ञं — sacrifice. • विनाशयितुं — to destroy. • शीलमस्याः — her nature is. • दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी — she who destroyed dakṣa’s sacrifice. दक्षयज्ञविनाशिनी means one who destroyed the sacrifice of dakṣa. dakṣa, out of ego, did not honour śiva or give him his proper offering; therefore the sacrifice was destroyed. though śiva and his attendants performed the destruction, śrīdevī was the instrument of that destruction, and so the name belongs to her. the destroyer of egoic ritual: dakṣa’s sacrifice lacked honour for śiva and was driven by pride. she dismantles ritual action that is empty of humility and true consciousness.","esoteric":["The Destroyer of Egoic Ritual: Dakṣa’s sacrifice lacked honour for Śiva and was driven by pride. She dismantles ritual action that is empty of humility and true consciousness."]},{"number":601,"name":"दरान्दोलितदीर्घाक्षी","samasa":["• दरम् (ईषद्यथा स्यात्तथा) आन्दोलितानि (चञ्चलानि) दीर्घाणि अक्षीणि यस्याः सा।","• दरम् (भयम्) आन्दोलितं (नाशितं) यैः तादृशदीर्घाक्षीणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• दरम् — slightly or fear.","• आन्दोलितानि — moving, wavering.","• चञ्चलानि — restless.","• दीर्घाणि — long.","• अक्षीणि — eyes.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• भयम् — fear.","• नाशितं — destroyed.","• दरान्दोलितदीर्घाक्षी — She whose long eyes move slightly and remove fear."],"summary":["दरान्दोलितदीर्घाक्षी means one whose long eyes, reaching up to the ears, slightly move. Dara means a little, so Her eyes gently move on all sides. Eyes extending to the ears are considered best. Dara also means fear; Her eyes remove fear. Her long wavering eyes allow Her compassionate glance to fall on all devotees."],"searchText":"601 दरान्दोलितदीर्घाक्षी • दरम् (ईषद्यथा स्यात्तथा) आन्दोलितानि (चञ्चलानि) दीर्घाणि अक्षीणि यस्याः सा। • दरम् (भयम्) आन्दोलितं (नाशितं) यैः तादृशदीर्घाक्षीणि यस्याः सा। • दरम् — slightly or fear. • आन्दोलितानि — moving, wavering. • चञ्चलानि — restless. • दीर्घाणि — long. • अक्षीणि — eyes. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • भयम् — fear. • नाशितं — destroyed. • दरान्दोलितदीर्घाक्षी — she whose long eyes move slightly and remove fear. दरान्दोलितदीर्घाक्षी means one whose long eyes, reaching up to the ears, slightly move. dara means a little, so her eyes gently move on all sides. eyes extending to the ears are considered best. dara also means fear; her eyes remove fear. her long wavering eyes allow her compassionate glance to fall on all devotees. the fear-removing eyes: her long, gently moving eyes show living compassion. their glance reaches all directions and removes fear from the heart.","esoteric":["The Fear-Removing Eyes: Her long, gently moving eyes show living compassion. Their glance reaches all directions and removes fear from the heart."]},{"number":602,"name":"दरहासोज्ज्वलन्मुखी","samasa":["• दरहासेन उज्ज्वलत् मुखं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• दरहासेन — by a gentle smile.","• उज्ज्वलत् — shining.","• मुखं — mouth or face.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• दरहासोज्ज्वलन्मुखी — She whose face shines with a gentle smile."],"summary":["दरहासोज्ज्वलन्मुखी means one whose face shines with a smile. Darahāsa means a gentle smile. Her physical beauty and inner bliss are both indicated by this smile. Dara also means fear; in battle, Her terrible laughter destroys demons."],"searchText":"602 दरहासोज्ज्वलन्मुखी • दरहासेन उज्ज्वलत् मुखं यस्याः सा। • दरहासेन — by a gentle smile. • उज्ज्वलत् — shining. • मुखं — mouth or face. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • दरहासोज्ज्वलन्मुखी — she whose face shines with a gentle smile. दरहासोज्ज्वलन्मुखी means one whose face shines with a smile. darahāsa means a gentle smile. her physical beauty and inner bliss are both indicated by this smile. dara also means fear; in battle, her terrible laughter destroys demons. the luminous smile: her gentle smile is the dawn of vidyā. it lights the mind, removes doubt and fills consciousness with joy.","esoteric":["The Luminous Smile: Her gentle smile is the dawn of vidyā. It lights the mind, removes doubt and fills consciousness with joy."]},{"number":603,"name":"गुरुमूर्तिः","samasa":["• गुरुरेव मूर्तिः शरीरं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["• गुरुरेव — the Guru himself.","• मूर्तिः — form, embodiment.","• शरीरं — body.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• गुरुमूर्तिः — She whose form is the Guru."],"summary":["गुरुमूर्तिः means one who assumes the form of a teacher. The teacher, mantra and deity are one and should not be seen as different. Śrīcakra and the Self are also to be understood in the same non-different way. Gu means darkness of ignorance, and ru removes it; therefore guru means one who removes ignorance. Śrīdevī comes as the Guru and gives mantra-upadeśa."],"searchText":"603 गुरुमूर्तिः • गुरुरेव मूर्तिः शरीरं यस्याः सा। • गुरुरेव — the guru himself. • मूर्तिः — form, embodiment. • शरीरं — body. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • गुरुमूर्तिः — she whose form is the guru. गुरुमूर्तिः means one who assumes the form of a teacher. the teacher, mantra and deity are one and should not be seen as different. śrīcakra and the self are also to be understood in the same non-different way. gu means darkness of ignorance, and ru removes it; therefore guru means one who removes ignorance. śrīdevī comes as the guru and gives mantra-upadeśa. the guru form: she appears as the guru to transmit mantra and remove ignorance. the guru is her functional form for guiding the seeker to liberation.","esoteric":["The Guru Form: She appears as the Guru to transmit mantra and remove ignorance. The Guru is Her functional form for guiding the seeker to liberation."]},{"number":604,"name":"गुणनिधिः","samasa":["• गुणानां निधिः।","• गुणा व्यूहरूपा निधिसंख्या यस्याः सा।","• गुणो रज्जुः सा चेह नौकाबन्धनी वटीरिकानाम्नी लक्षणया गृह्यते। सा नितरां धीयतेऽस्यामिति गुणनिधिः (मात्स्यकालीपुराणम्)।"],"wordByWord":["• गुणानां — of qualities.","• निधिः — treasure.","• यस्याः — whose.","• सा — she.","• गुणनिधिः — She who is the treasure-house of qualities."],"summary":["गुणनिधिः means one who is the treasure-house of qualities. The three guṇas, sattva, rajas and tamas, have countless modifications, and She is the repository of all such qualities. Guṇa can also mean aggregate or vyūha; nine such vyūhas are described, and She is their form. Guṇa can also mean rope, connected with Her stabilising power."],"searchText":"604 गुणनिधिः • गुणानां निधिः। • गुणा व्यूहरूपा निधिसंख्या यस्याः सा। • गुणो रज्जुः सा चेह नौकाबन्धनी वटीरिकानाम्नी लक्षणया गृह्यते। सा नितरां धीयतेऽस्यामिति गुणनिधिः (मात्स्यकालीपुराणम्)। • गुणानां — of qualities. • निधिः — treasure. • यस्याः — whose. • सा — she. • गुणनिधिः — she who is the treasure-house of qualities. गुणनिधिः means one who is the treasure-house of qualities. the three guṇas, sattva, rajas and tamas, have countless modifications, and she is the repository of all such qualities. guṇa can also mean aggregate or vyūha; nine such vyūhas are described, and she is their form. guṇa can also mean rope, connected with her stabilising power. the storehouse of qualities: she contains all guṇas and their countless forms. as the treasure of qualities, she is also the stabilising force that holds beings steady.","esoteric":["The Storehouse of Qualities: She contains all guṇas and their countless forms. As the treasure of qualities, She is also the stabilising force that holds beings steady."]},{"number":605,"name":"गोमाता","samasa":["• गवां धेनूनां माता।"],"wordByWord":["• गवां — of cows.","• धेनूनां — of cows.","• माता — mother.","• गोमाता — She who is the mother of cows."],"summary":["गोमाता means one who is in the form of Kāmadhenu, the divine cow, mother of all cows or greatest of cows. Go also means speech, rays and heaven; She is the root form of all these."],"searchText":"605 गोमाता • गवां धेनूनां माता। • गवां — of cows. • धेनूनां — of cows. • माता — mother. • गोमाता — she who is the mother of cows. गोमाता means one who is in the form of kāmadhenu, the divine cow, mother of all cows or greatest of cows. go also means speech, rays and heaven; she is the root form of all these. the mother of go: go can indicate cow, speech, light, earth and the senses. as gomātā, she nourishes all these as the wish-fulfilling mother.","esoteric":["The Mother of Go: Go can indicate cow, speech, light, earth and the senses. As Gomātā, She nourishes all these as the wish-fulfilling mother."]},{"number":606,"name":"गुहजन्मभूः","samasa":["• गुहस्य स्कन्दस्य जन्मभूः।","• गुहा जीवाः तेषां जन्मभूः।"],"wordByWord":["• गुहस्य — of Guha.","• जन्मभूः — birthplace, mother-origin.","• गुहा — hidden beings, souls.","• जीवाः — souls.","• तेषां — of them.","• गुहजन्मभूः — She who is the mother-origin of Guha and hidden beings."],"summary":["गुहजन्मभूः means one who is the mother of Guha, Lord Muruga or Subrahmaṇya. The root guh means to cover. Souls veiled by ignorance are called guhas. As sparks arise from hot iron, souls arise from the Self; therefore She is also the origin of such guhas."],"searchText":"606 गुहजन्मभूः • गुहस्य स्कन्दस्य जन्मभूः। • गुहा जीवाः तेषां जन्मभूः। • गुहस्य — of guha. • जन्मभूः — birthplace, mother-origin. • गुहा — hidden beings, souls. • जीवाः — souls. • तेषां — of them. • गुहजन्मभूः — she who is the mother-origin of guha and hidden beings. गुहजन्मभूः means one who is the mother of guha, lord muruga or subrahmaṇya. the root guh means to cover. souls veiled by ignorance are called guhas. as sparks arise from hot iron, souls arise from the self; therefore she is also the origin of such guhas. the mother of guha: she is the mother of guha, the hidden one. she is also the ground from which the hidden individual souls arise.","esoteric":["The Mother of Guha: She is the mother of Guha, the hidden one. She is also the ground from which the hidden individual souls arise."]},{"number":607,"name":"देवेशी","samasa":["• देवानाम् ईशी।"],"wordByWord":["• देवानाम् — of the gods.","• ईशी — ruler.","• देवेशी — She who is ruler of the gods."],"summary":["देवेशी means one who is the ruler of the gods. She is the head of all divine powers such as Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Śiva and others."],"searchText":"607 देवेशी • देवानाम् ईशी। • देवानाम् — of the gods. • ईशी — ruler. • देवेशी — she who is ruler of the gods. देवेशी means one who is the ruler of the gods. she is the head of all divine powers such as brahmā, viṣṇu, śiva and others. the ruler of the devas: the devas are powers of light and order. she is their sovereign and the power behind their functions.","esoteric":["The Ruler of the Devas: The devas are powers of light and order. She is their sovereign and the power behind their functions."]},{"number":608,"name":"दण्डनीतिस्था","samasa":["• दण्डनीतौ तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["• दण्डनीतौ — in the science of punishment and governance.","• तिष्ठतीति — abides.","• दण्डनीतिस्था — She who abides in daṇḍanīti."],"summary":["दण्डनीतिस्था means one who administers justice by punishing the wicked. Daṇḍanīti is the science that describes offences and the corresponding punishments. Because She restrains, corrects and guides beings along the right path, She is called Daṇḍanītisthā."],"searchText":"608 दण्डनीतिस्था • दण्डनीतौ तिष्ठतीति। • दण्डनीतौ — in the science of punishment and governance. • तिष्ठतीति — abides. • दण्डनीतिस्था — she who abides in daṇḍanīti. दण्डनीतिस्था means one who administers justice by punishing the wicked. daṇḍanīti is the science that describes offences and the corresponding punishments. because she restrains, corrects and guides beings along the right path, she is called daṇḍanītisthā. the moral law: daṇḍanīti is corrective justice and right governance. she stands within this order, ensuring that action returns fitting consequence.","esoteric":["The Moral Law: Daṇḍanīti is corrective justice and right governance. She stands within this order, ensuring that action returns fitting consequence."]},{"number":609,"name":"दहराकाशरूपिणी","samasa":["• दहरमाकाशं रूपमस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["• रूपमस्याः — Her form.","• दहराकाशरूपिणी — She whose form is the subtle inner ether."],"summary":["दहराकाशरूपिणी means one who is the subtle ether in the cave of the heart. In the heart of every being there is a subtle hidden space, and She dwells there as the inner ether. This daharākāśa is the subtle inner space identified with Brahman."],"searchText":"609 दहराकाशरूपिणी • दहरमाकाशं रूपमस्याः इति। • रूपमस्याः — her form. • दहराकाशरूपिणी — she whose form is the subtle inner ether. दहराकाशरूपिणी means one who is the subtle ether in the cave of the heart. in the heart of every being there is a subtle hidden space, and she dwells there as the inner ether. this daharākāśa is the subtle inner space identified with brahman. the inner sky: daharākāśa is the tiny luminous space in the heart that contains the vastness of reality. she is that pristine inner ether.","esoteric":["The Inner Sky: Daharākāśa is the tiny luminous space in the heart that contains the vastness of reality. She is that pristine inner ether."]},{"number":610,"name":"प्रतिपन्मुख्यराकान्ततिथिमण्डलपूजिता","samasa":["• प्रतिपत्तिथिः मुख्या यस्मिन्, राकातिथिः अन्ते यस्मिन् तिथिमण्डले तस्मिन् पूजिता।"],"wordByWord":["• प्रतिपत्तिथिः — the first lunar day.","• मुख्या — principal, beginning.","• यस्मिन् — in which.","• राकातिथिः — the full-moon day.","• अन्ते — at the end.","• तिथिमण्डले — in the circle of lunar days.","• तस्मिन् — in that.","• पूजिता — worshipped.","• प्रतिपन्मुख्यराकान्ततिथिमण्डलपूजिता — She who is worshipped in the circle of lunar days from Pratipat to Rākā."],"summary":["प्रतिपन्मुख्यराकान्ततिथिमण्डलपूजिता means one who is worshipped in the circle of lunar days beginning with Pratipat and ending with the full moon. Pratipat is the first lunar day and Rākā is the full-moon day. She is worshipped through all fifteen days in tantric rites. Each tithi has its presiding Nityā Devī. The sixteen include the fifteen Tithi Nityās and Lalitā Mahānityā in the bindu. Tithi-Nityā worship is an important part of Śrīvidyā worship."],"searchText":"610 प्रतिपन्मुख्यराकान्ततिथिमण्डलपूजिता • प्रतिपत्तिथिः मुख्या यस्मिन्, राकातिथिः अन्ते यस्मिन् तिथिमण्डले तस्मिन् पूजिता। • प्रतिपत्तिथिः — the first lunar day. • मुख्या — principal, beginning. • यस्मिन् — in which. • राकातिथिः — the full-moon day. • अन्ते — at the end. • तिथिमण्डले — in the circle of lunar days. • तस्मिन् — in that. • पूजिता — worshipped. • प्रतिपन्मुख्यराकान्ततिथिमण्डलपूजिता — she who is worshipped in the circle of lunar days from pratipat to rākā. प्रतिपन्मुख्यराकान्ततिथिमण्डलपूजिता means one who is worshipped in the circle of lunar days beginning with pratipat and ending with the full moon. pratipat is the first lunar day and rākā is the full-moon day. she is worshipped through all fifteen days in tantric rites. each tithi has its presiding nityā devī. the sixteen include the fifteen tithi nityās and lalitā mahānityā in the bindu. tithi-nityā worship is an important part of śrīvidyā worship. the lunar circle: she is worshipped through the lunar tithi-maṇḍala from pratipat to rākā. as the sixteenth light, she pervades and completes the cycle of the nityās.","esoteric":["The Lunar Circle: She is worshipped through the lunar tithi-maṇḍala from Pratipat to Rākā. As the sixteenth light, She pervades and completes the cycle of the Nityās."]},{"number":611,"name":"कलात्मिका","samasa":["कला आत्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कला — art; kalā; divine digit/power","आत्मा — self; essence","स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["कलात्मिका means one who is in the form of kalās. Kalā indicates several divisions of divine power: the kalās of fire, Sun, Moon, Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra, Īśvara and Sadāśiva, as well as the well-known sixty-four arts. All these kalās are forms of Śrīdevī. The states such as waking, dream, deep sleep and turīya are also related to different kalās. Their real form is Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"611 कलात्मिका कला आत्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। कला — art; kalā; divine digit/power आत्मा — self; essence स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature यस्याः — of whom; whose कलात्मिका means one who is in the form of kalās. kalā indicates several divisions of divine power: the kalās of fire, sun, moon, brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra, īśvara and sadāśiva, as well as the well-known sixty-four arts. all these kalās are forms of śrīdevī. the states such as waking, dream, deep sleep and turīya are also related to different kalās. their real form is śrīdevī. the manifested fractions: kalā represents the digits of the moon, the sixty-four cultural arts, or the functional fractions into which the absolute energy divides itself to construct the material universe. she is the soul of all these diverse expressions, animating the components while remaining internally undivided.","esoteric":["The Manifested Fractions: Kalā represents the digits of the moon, the sixty-four cultural arts, or the functional fractions into which the absolute energy divides itself to construct the material universe. She is the soul of all these diverse expressions, animating the components while remaining internally undivided."]},{"number":612,"name":"कलानाथा","samasa":["कलानां नाथा।"],"wordByWord":["कलानां — of the kalās"],"summary":["कलानाथा means the Moon is called the lord of kalās. She is the head of all kalās. Since the Śrīcakra itself is contemplated in the form of the lunar sphere, the name Kalānāthā is appropriate for Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"612 कलानाथा कलानां नाथा। कलानां — of the kalās कलानाथा means the moon is called the lord of kalās. she is the head of all kalās. since the śrīcakra itself is contemplated in the form of the lunar sphere, the name kalānāthā is appropriate for śrīdevī. the controller of time and expression: as kalānāthā, she governs the light digits that determine the movement of time and lunar calendars. concurrently, she rules as the supreme source behind all fine arts and creative intelligence, directing how aesthetic energy is formulated.","esoteric":["The Controller of Time and Expression: As Kalānāthā, She governs the light digits that determine the movement of time and lunar calendars. Concurrently, She rules as the supreme source behind all fine arts and creative intelligence, directing how aesthetic energy is formulated."]},{"number":613,"name":"काव्यालापविमोदिनी","samasa":["काव्यानाम् आलापेन मोदिनी।"],"wordByWord":["काव्यानाम् — of poems; poetic works","आलापेन — by speech; discourse"],"summary":["काव्यालापविमोदिनी means one who gets delighted with poetical speech, dialogue and description. Kāvyas are works of poetry. Their rasa, beautiful speech and figures of speech delight Her. A devotee who worships Śrīdevī methodically gains the capacity for poetic expression, as in the examples of Kālidāsa, Mūka and other great devotees."],"searchText":"613 काव्यालापविमोदिनी काव्यानाम् आलापेन मोदिनी। काव्यानाम् — of poems; poetic works आलापेन — by speech; discourse काव्यालापविमोदिनी means one who gets delighted with poetical speech, dialogue and description. kāvyas are works of poetry. their rasa, beautiful speech and figures of speech delight her. a devotee who worships śrīdevī methodically gains the capacity for poetic expression, as in the examples of kālidāsa, mūka and other great devotees. the muse of divine literature: true poetry (kāvya) is not ordinary wording; it is the harmonious expression of cosmic truth and beauty captured by inspired seers (kavis). she functions as the inner muse behind this literature and is deeply pleased when her children engage in refined, elevating artistic compositions that mirror divine order.","esoteric":["The Muse of Divine Literature: True poetry (Kāvya) is not ordinary wording; it is the harmonious expression of cosmic truth and beauty captured by inspired seers (kavis). She functions as the inner muse behind this literature and is deeply pleased when Her children engage in refined, elevating artistic compositions that mirror divine order."]},{"number":614,"name":"सचामररमावाणीसव्यदक्षिणसेविता","samasa":["चामराभ्यां सहिते सचामरे। तादृशीभ्यां रमावाणीभ्यां लक्ष्मीसरस्वतीभ्यां सव्ये दक्षिणे क्रमेण सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["चामराभ्यां — by two cāmaras/fans","सहिते — accompanied by","रमावाणीभ्यां — by Ramā/Lakṣmī and Vāṇī/Sarasvatī","सव्ये — on the left","दक्षिणे — on the right","क्रमेण — in order"],"summary":["सचामररमावाणीसव्यदक्षिणसेविता means one who is attended on either side by Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī holding cāmaras. Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī serve Śrīdevī on both sides. A devotee who becomes merged in devotion to Śrīdevī is also blessed by Lakṣmī and Sarasvatī. The reference is also supported by the Soundaryalaharī statement that Brahmā and Hari sport with Sarasvatī and Lakṣmī."],"searchText":"614 सचामररमावाणीसव्यदक्षिणसेविता चामराभ्यां सहिते सचामरे। तादृशीभ्यां रमावाणीभ्यां लक्ष्मीसरस्वतीभ्यां सव्ये दक्षिणे क्रमेण सेविता। चामराभ्यां — by two cāmaras/fans सहिते — accompanied by रमावाणीभ्यां — by ramā/lakṣmī and vāṇī/sarasvatī सव्ये — on the left दक्षिणे — on the right क्रमेण — in order सचामररमावाणीसव्यदक्षिणसेविता means one who is attended on either side by lakṣmī and sarasvatī holding cāmaras. lakṣmī and sarasvatī serve śrīdevī on both sides. a devotee who becomes merged in devotion to śrīdevī is also blessed by lakṣmī and sarasvatī. the reference is also supported by the soundaryalaharī statement that brahmā and hari sport with sarasvatī and lakṣmī. sovereignty over wealth and wisdom: humans spend lifetimes pursuing either material wealth (lakṣmī) or intellectual learning (sarasvatī). this name establishes that when a practitioner approaches the absolute center, both cosmic principles stand submissively as entry-level attendants holding fans at her throne, demonstrating her absolute status as the supreme source of all capability.","esoteric":["Sovereignty over Wealth and Wisdom: Humans spend lifetimes pursuing either material wealth (Lakṣmī) or intellectual learning (Sarasvatī). This name establishes that when a practitioner approaches the absolute center, both cosmic principles stand submissively as entry-level attendants holding fans at Her throne, demonstrating Her absolute status as the supreme source of all capability."]},{"number":615,"name":"आदिशक्तिः","samasa":["आदिः कारणभूता च सा शक्तिश्च।"],"wordByWord":["आदिः — beginning; primordial cause","कारणभूता — being the cause","सा — she"],"summary":["आदिशक्तिः means one who is the original power. She is the primordial Śakti and the root cause before all later manifestations. The later names describe many forms and functions, but this name points to the causal power from which they arise."],"searchText":"615 आदिशक्तिः आदिः कारणभूता च सा शक्तिश्च। आदिः — beginning; primordial cause कारणभूता — being the cause सा — she आदिशक्तिः means one who is the original power. she is the primordial śakti and the root cause before all later manifestations. the later names describe many forms and functions, but this name points to the causal power from which they arise. the uncaused kinetic cause: she is ādi-śakti because she exists prior to the first movement of cosmic manifestation. she is the baseline energy matrix that belongs to the absolute brahman, acting as the primary source from which all secondary forces (like gravity, light, and electricity) branch out.","esoteric":["The Uncaused Kinetic Cause: She is Ādi-śakti because She exists prior to the first movement of cosmic manifestation. She is the baseline energy matrix that belongs to the absolute Brahman, acting as the primary source from which all secondary forces (like gravity, light, and electricity) branch out."]},{"number":616,"name":"अमेया","samasa":["मातुमशक्या।","मेयं न विद्यते यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मेयं — measurable object","विद्यते — exists","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["अमेया means one who cannot be measured. She cannot be limited by thought, word, number, place, time or object. The name indicates that Her form is beyond the reach of ordinary means of measurement or description."],"searchText":"616 अमेया मातुमशक्या। मेयं न विद्यते यस्याः सा। मेयं — measurable object विद्यते — exists यस्याः — of whom; whose अमेया means one who cannot be measured. she cannot be limited by thought, word, number, place, time or object. the name indicates that her form is beyond the reach of ordinary means of measurement or description. beyond mathematical quantification: finite objects can be measured, weighted, and fully computed by human instruments. but because she is the infinite, shoreless background awareness within which space itself exists, she can never be turned into an object to be measured. she remains immeasurable, accessible only through direct absorption.","esoteric":["Beyond Mathematical Quantification: Finite objects can be measured, weighted, and fully computed by human instruments. But because She is the infinite, shoreless background awareness within which space itself exists, She can never be turned into an object to be measured. She remains immeasurable, accessible only through direct absorption."]},{"number":617,"name":"आत्मा","samasa":["जीवरूपा।","यच्चाप्नोति यदादत्तेयच्चात्ति विषयानिह। यच्चास्य सततो भावस्तस्मादात्मेति कीर्त्यते॥"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["आत्मा means one who is in the form of Ātman or jīva. This name indicates the jīvātman, while the following name indicates Paramātman. Ātman may mean body, mind, Brahman, nature, firmness and intelligence; as She is present in all these, the name is apt."],"searchText":"617 आत्मा जीवरूपा। यच्चाप्नोति यदादत्तेयच्चात्ति विषयानिह। यच्चास्य सततो भावस्तस्मादात्मेति कीर्त्यते॥ word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. आत्मा means one who is in the form of ātman or jīva. this name indicates the jīvātman, while the following name indicates paramātman. ātman may mean body, mind, brahman, nature, firmness and intelligence; as she is present in all these, the name is apt. the pervasive subject: she is ātmā because she fulfills the four criteria of the self: she pervades all space (आप्नोति), absorbs all elements into herself (आदत्ते), experiences and illuminates all objective fields (अत्ति), and exists constantly as the baseline background layer of reality. she is the true inner identity of every living being.","esoteric":["The Pervasive Subject: She is Ātmā because She fulfills the four criteria of the Self: She pervades all space (आप्नोति), absorbs all elements into Herself (आदत्ते), experiences and illuminates all objective fields (अत्ति), and exists constantly as the baseline background layer of reality. She is the true inner identity of every living being."]},{"number":618,"name":"परमा","samasa":["परब्रह्मरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["परमा means one who is supreme and great in all ways. She reveals and limits for us the immeasurable Brahman. For those without devotion She seems distant; in relation to the previous name as jīvātman, this name points to Paramātman."],"searchText":"618 परमा परब्रह्मरूपा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. परमा means one who is supreme and great in all ways. she reveals and limits for us the immeasurable brahman. for those without devotion she seems distant; in relation to the previous name as jīvātman, this name points to paramātman. the absolute ceiling: she is paramā because she marks the absolute ceiling of existence. there is no higher state, no finer consciousness, and no authority back behind her station, identifying her directly with the unconditioned parabrahman.","esoteric":["The Absolute Ceiling: She is Paramā because She marks the absolute ceiling of existence. There is no higher state, no finer consciousness, and no authority back behind Her station, identifying Her directly with the unconditioned Parabrahman."]},{"number":619,"name":"पावनाकृतिः","samasa":["पावनी आकृतिः यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पावनी — purifying; sanctifying","आकृतिः — form","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["पावनाकृतिः means one whose body and form are holy and sanctifying. The very thought of Śrīdevī washes away sins and makes one pure. Kṛti may also mean action; therefore the name may also indicate one whose actions are pure and sanctifying."],"searchText":"619 पावनाकृतिः पावनी आकृतिः यस्याः सा। पावनी — purifying; sanctifying आकृतिः — form यस्याः — of whom; whose पावनाकृतिः means one whose body and form are holy and sanctifying. the very thought of śrīdevī washes away sins and makes one pure. kṛti may also mean action; therefore the name may also indicate one whose actions are pure and sanctifying. the purifying presence: her structural form—whether visualized as the anthropomorphic mother or as the geometric framework of the śrī cakra—possesses a natural purifying frequency (pāvanī). simply anchoring the attention upon her structure cleanses the practitioner's subconscious, burning away mental impurities.","esoteric":["The Purifying Presence: Her structural form—whether visualized as the anthropomorphic mother or as the geometric framework of the Śrī Cakra—possesses a natural purifying frequency (pāvanī). Simply anchoring the attention upon Her structure cleanses the practitioner's subconscious, burning away mental impurities."]},{"number":620,"name":"अनेककोटिब्रह्माण्डजननी","samasa":["अनेका अनन्ताः कोटयो ये ब्रह्माण्डास्तेषां जननी जनयित्री।","अनेककोटयः ब्रह्माण्डाः येषां विराडादीनां ते। तेषां जन"],"wordByWord":["अनेका — many","अनन्ताः — endless","जननी — mother","ब्रह्माण्डाः — cosmic eggs; universes"],"summary":["अनेककोटिब्रह्माण्डजननी means one who gave birth to many crores of worlds. Virāṭ, Hiraṇyagarbha and Īśvara create crores of worlds, and She is the mother even of them. Brahmāṇḍa arises from the gross elements and their modifications; She is the source of all such cosmic spheres."],"searchText":"620 अनेककोटिब्रह्माण्डजननी अनेका अनन्ताः कोटयो ये ब्रह्माण्डास्तेषां जननी जनयित्री। अनेककोटयः ब्रह्माण्डाः येषां विराडादीनां ते। तेषां जन अनेका — many अनन्ताः — endless जननी — mother ब्रह्माण्डाः — cosmic eggs; universes अनेककोटिब्रह्माण्डजननी means one who gave birth to many crores of worlds. virāṭ, hiraṇyagarbha and īśvara create crores of worlds, and she is the mother even of them. brahmāṇḍa arises from the gross elements and their modifications; she is the source of all such cosmic spheres. the architect of the multiverse: she is not the mother of a single world or an isolated galaxy. her creative womb projects infinite systems of multiverses (aneka-koṭi-brahmāṇḍa) simultaneously. they float within her vast space like tiny foam bubbles on an ocean, showcasing her shoreless creative scale.","esoteric":["The Architect of the Multiverse: She is not the mother of a single world or an isolated galaxy. Her creative womb projects infinite systems of multiverses (aneka-koṭi-brahmāṇḍa) simultaneously. They float within Her vast space like tiny foam bubbles on an ocean, showcasing Her shoreless creative scale."]},{"number":621,"name":"दिव्यविग्रहा","samasa":["दिव्यो रमणीयो विग्रहो देहो यस्याः सा।","दिव अन्तरिक्षे भवो दिव्यो विग्रहो रणो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["दिव्यविग्रहा means one who has a divine and beautiful form. The name may also recall the Purāṇic description of Devī appearing in a divine body and fighting even in the sky. Her form is not ordinary or material but divya, fit for divine contemplation."],"searchText":"621 दिव्यविग्रहा दिव्यो रमणीयो विग्रहो देहो यस्याः सा। दिव अन्तरिक्षे भवो दिव्यो विग्रहो रणो यस्याः सा। यस्याः — of whom; whose दिव्यविग्रहा means one who has a divine and beautiful form. the name may also recall the purāṇic description of devī appearing in a divine body and fighting even in the sky. her form is not ordinary or material but divya, fit for divine contemplation. the body of light: her form (vigraha) is not composed of dense biological tissue; it is made of pure, self-luminous light energy (aprakṛta). the high battlefield: alternatively, her cosmic battle (vigraha) against ignorance is conducted in the subtle space of pure consciousness, clearing the internal heavens for the seeker.","esoteric":["The Body of Light: Her form (vigraha) is not composed of dense biological tissue; it is made of pure, self-luminous light energy (aprakṛta).","The High Battlefield: Alternatively, Her cosmic battle (vigraha) against ignorance is conducted in the subtle space of pure consciousness, clearing the internal heavens for the seeker."]},{"number":622,"name":"क्लींकारी","samasa":["क्लीं कामं बीजं करोतीति।","कामबीजस्वरूपेति।","क्लींकारस्य शिवकामस्य स्त्रीति।"],"wordByWord":["क्लीं — klīṃ bīja","कामं — Kāma; desire","बीजं — seed syllable"],"summary":["क्लींकारी means one who is the personification of the letter klīṃ, the Kāmarāja bīja. Klīṃ is the seed connected with Kāma or Manmatha and also with Kāmeśvara. The bīja indicates the union of Śiva and Śakti, and Śrīdevī is its living form."],"searchText":"622 क्लींकारी क्लीं कामं बीजं करोतीति। कामबीजस्वरूपेति। क्लींकारस्य शिवकामस्य स्त्रीति। क्लीं — klīṃ bīja कामं — kāma; desire बीजं — seed syllable क्लींकारी means one who is the personification of the letter klīṃ, the kāmarāja bīja. klīṃ is the seed connected with kāma or manmatha and also with kāmeśvara. the bīja indicates the union of śiva and śakti, and śrīdevī is its living form. the seed of absolute attraction: क्लीं is the celebrated kāmarāja-bīja — the syllable of divine attraction, love, and creative desire. she is klīṁkārī because she animates the primal vibration that draws elements together to form worlds and calls the individual soul back into non-dual union with śiva.","esoteric":["The Seed of Absolute Attraction: क्लीं is the celebrated Kāmarāja-bīja — the syllable of divine attraction, love, and creative desire. She is Klīṁkārī because She animates the primal vibration that draws elements together to form worlds and calls the individual soul back into non-dual union with Śiva."]},{"number":623,"name":"केवला","samasa":["निखिलधर्मराहित्येनैकाकित्वात्केवला।","पूर्वोक्तकामबीजे केवलत्वं ककारलकारात्मकव्यञ्जनराहित्यम्। तेन केवलतुर्यस्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["केवला means one who is absolute, alone and devoid of all attributes. Kevala means the state not mixed with any other attribute. It is the remaining truth of non-duality. In relation to the klīṃ bīja, the name is also connected with the inner secret of kāmakalā and the turīya state leading to kaivalya."],"searchText":"623 केवला निखिलधर्मराहित्येनैकाकित्वात्केवला। पूर्वोक्तकामबीजे केवलत्वं ककारलकारात्मकव्यञ्जनराहित्यम्। तेन केवलतुर्यस्वरूपा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. केवला means one who is absolute, alone and devoid of all attributes. kevala means the state not mixed with any other attribute. it is the remaining truth of non-duality. in relation to the klīṃ bīja, the name is also connected with the inner secret of kāmakalā and the turīya state leading to kaivalya. the attribute-less absolute: she is kevalā because she stands completely independent, devoid of all material properties and dualities (nirguṇa). the vowel light: in advanced mantra grammar, kevala describes the extraction of the pure vowel sound after dropping the outer consonant frames (क and ल). this identifies her as the unconditioned transcendental light behind all spoken syllables.","esoteric":["The Attribute-less Absolute: She is Kevalā because She stands completely independent, devoid of all material properties and dualities (Nirguṇa).","The Vowel Light: In advanced mantra grammar, kevala describes the extraction of the pure vowel sound after dropping the outer consonant frames (क and ल). This identifies Her as the unconditioned transcendental light behind all spoken syllables."]},{"number":624,"name":"गुह्या","samasa":["गुहां प्रविष्टा।"],"wordByWord":["गुहां — cave; secret place"],"summary":["गुह्या means one who is most secret in form and meaning. Guhyā also means one who dwells in the cave of the heart. She is to be known by inward search, as the secret reality of jīvātman, Paramātman and their unity."],"searchText":"624 गुह्या गुहां प्रविष्टा। गुहां — cave; secret place गुह्या means one who is most secret in form and meaning. guhyā also means one who dwells in the cave of the heart. she is to be known by inward search, as the secret reality of jīvātman, paramātman and their unity. the secret core: she is guhyā because she chooses to remain hidden away from casual, superficial minds. she resides deep inside the secret cavern (guhā) of the heart and within the highly guarded, internal instructions of the śrīvidyā tradition, accessible strictly through refined devotion.","esoteric":["The Secret Core: She is Guhyā because She chooses to remain hidden away from casual, superficial minds. She resides deep inside the secret cavern (guhā) of the heart and within the highly guarded, internal instructions of the Śrīvidyā tradition, accessible strictly through refined devotion."]},{"number":625,"name":"कैवल्यपददायिनी","samasa":["कैवल्यं मुक्तिस्तदेव पदं ददाति।","कैवल्यं च पदानि च स्थानानि सालोक्यादिमुक्तिचतुष्टयं च दातुं शीलमस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["कैवल्यं — kaivalya; non-dual liberation","पदं — state; abode"],"summary":["कैवल्यपददायिनी means one who bestows kaivalya, the solitary non-dual state of liberation. The states of liberation such as sālokya, sārūpya, sāmīpya, sāyujya and kaivalya are mentioned; She grants these states. Kaivalya is the final state of singleness without attributes, the direct understanding of the Self."],"searchText":"625 कैवल्यपददायिनी कैवल्यं मुक्तिस्तदेव पदं ददाति। कैवल्यं च पदानि च स्थानानि सालोक्यादिमुक्तिचतुष्टयं च दातुं शीलमस्याः इति। कैवल्यं — kaivalya; non-dual liberation पदं — state; abode कैवल्यपददायिनी means one who bestows kaivalya, the solitary non-dual state of liberation. the states of liberation such as sālokya, sārūpya, sāmīpya, sāyujya and kaivalya are mentioned; she grants these states. kaivalya is the final state of singleness without attributes, the direct understanding of the self. the giver of non-dual freedom: कैवल्य (kaivalya) is the ultimate state of liberation where the illusion of duality dissolves completely, leaving the soul in its pristine isolation as pure brahman.","esoteric":["The Giver of Non-Dual Freedom: कैवल्य (Kaivalya) is the ultimate state of liberation where the illusion of duality dissolves completely, leaving the soul in its pristine isolation as pure Brahman."]},{"number":626,"name":"त्रिपुरा","samasa":["तिसृभ्यो मूर्तिभ्यः पुरातनत्वात् त्रिपुरा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["त्रिपुरा means one who is older than the three gods Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra. She assumes the three forms for creation, protection and destruction and is therefore prior to them. Tripurā also indicates Her presence in the three states, three cities and threefold manifestations."],"searchText":"626 त्रिपुरा तिसृभ्यो मूर्तिभ्यः पुरातनत्वात् त्रिपुरा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. त्रिपुरा means one who is older than the three gods brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra. she assumes the three forms for creation, protection and destruction and is therefore prior to them. tripurā also indicates her presence in the three states, three cities and threefold manifestations. prior to the triads: she is tripurā because she exists before (पुरत) the emergence of the foundational triads (त्रि) that build the universe. she stands before the three gods (brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra), the three primary channels (iḍā, piṅgalā, suṣumṇā), the three guṇas, and the three states of consciousness, serving as their shared unmanifested source.","esoteric":["Prior to the Triads: She is Tripurā because She exists before (पुरत) the emergence of the foundational triads (त्रि) that build the universe. She stands before the three gods (Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra), the three primary channels (Iḍā, Piṅgalā, Suṣumṇā), the three guṇas, and the three states of consciousness, serving as their shared unmanifested source."]},{"number":627,"name":"त्रिजगद्वन्द्या","samasa":["त्रिभिर्जगद्भिर्वन्द्या।","त्रयो जगद्वन्द्या यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["त्रिजगद्वन्द्या means one who is worshipped by the three worlds. The beings of heaven, earth and the intermediate world bow to Her. The name indicates universal reverence toward Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"627 त्रिजगद्वन्द्या त्रिभिर्जगद्भिर्वन्द्या। त्रयो जगद्वन्द्या यस्याः सा। यस्याः — of whom; whose त्रिजगद्वन्द्या means one who is worshipped by the three worlds. the beings of heaven, earth and the intermediate world bow to her. the name indicates universal reverence toward śrīdevī. the object of universal adoration: the three worlds—the celestial realms (svarga), the terrestrial plane (bhūmi), and the subterranean zones (pātāla)—all bow before her authority. not a single plane of existence is independent of her law, making her the central destination for all expressions of devotion.","esoteric":["The Object of Universal Adoration: The three worlds—the celestial realms (svarga), the terrestrial plane (bhūmi), and the subterranean zones (pātāla)—all bow before Her authority. Not a single plane of existence is independent of Her law, making Her the central destination for all expressions of devotion."]},{"number":628,"name":"त्रिमूर्तिः","samasa":["त्रैवर्षिककन्यारूपत्वात्रिमूर्तित्वम्।","रक्तशुक्लमिश्रात्मकचरणमूर्तित्रयरूपा।","ब्रह्मादिमूर्तित्रयं वामादित्रयमिच्छादिमूर्तित्रयं चास्या एवेति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["त्रिमूर्तिः means one who has the three forms. These may be understood as Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra; or as the three Śaktis and other triads described in the tradition. The threefold universe and its functions are Her own manifestation."],"searchText":"628 त्रिमूर्तिः त्रैवर्षिककन्यारूपत्वात्रिमूर्तित्वम्। रक्तशुक्लमिश्रात्मकचरणमूर्तित्रयरूपा। ब्रह्मादिमूर्तित्रयं वामादित्रयमिच्छादिमूर्तित्रयं चास्या एवेति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. त्रिमूर्तिः means one who has the three forms. these may be understood as brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra; or as the three śaktis and other triads described in the tradition. the threefold universe and its functions are her own manifestation. the triple manifestation: she embodies the three core administrative faces of the absolute (brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra) and the three creative drives (icchā, jñāna, kriyā). the alchemical colors: she represents the three foundational rays of the feet: red, white, and mixed. ritualistically, it also maps her onto the pure energy of a three-year-old maiden (traivarṣika-kanyā) within tantric liturgy.","esoteric":["The Triple Manifestation: She embodies the three core administrative faces of the absolute (Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra) and the three creative drives (Icchā, Jñāna, Kriyā).","The Alchemical Colors: She represents the three foundational rays of the feet: red, white, and mixed. Ritualistically, it also maps Her onto the pure energy of a three-year-old maiden (Traivarṣika-kanyā) within Tantric liturgy."]},{"number":629,"name":"त्रिदशेश्वरी","samasa":["त्रिदशानां देवानां तिसृणां वा दशानामवस्थानां त्रियुक्तदशानां त्रयोदशानां विश्वेषां देवानां वा त्रिगुणितदशानां त्रिंशता लक्षणया त्रयस्त्रिंशद्गणानां चेश्वरी स्वामिनी।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["त्रिदशेश्वरी means one who is the head of the devas. Tridaśa refers to the gods, including the well-known groups such as Vasus, Ādityas, Rudras and Viśvedevas. She is the sovereign over all such divine hosts and their powers."],"searchText":"629 त्रिदशेश्वरी त्रिदशानां देवानां तिसृणां वा दशानामवस्थानां त्रियुक्तदशानां त्रयोदशानां विश्वेषां देवानां वा त्रिगुणितदशानां त्रिंशता लक्षणया त्रयस्त्रिंशद्गणानां चेश्वरी स्वामिनी। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. त्रिदशेश्वरी means one who is the head of the devas. tridaśa refers to the gods, including the well-known groups such as vasus, ādityas, rudras and viśvedevas. she is the sovereign over all such divine hosts and their powers. the sovereign over celestial hierarchies: त्रिदश (tridaśa) is a classic vedic code for the gods, referencing the thirty-three primary administrative classes of deities. she is their absolute empress. the ruler of states: alternatively, it represents the three states of consciousness (jāgrat, svapna, suṣupti) multiplied across the ten operational directions of space, all governed by her background light.","esoteric":["The Sovereign over Celestial Hierarchies: त्रिदश (Tridaśa) is a classic Vedic code for the gods, referencing the thirty-three primary administrative classes of deities. She is their absolute empress.","The Ruler of States: Alternatively, it represents the three states of consciousness (jāgrat, svapna, suṣupti) multiplied across the ten operational directions of space, all governed by Her background light."]},{"number":630,"name":"त्र्यक्षरी","samasa":["त्रयाणामक्षराणां वाक्कामशक्तिबीजात्मकानां समाहारः।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["त्र्यक्षरी means one who is of three letters. The three letters may be understood as the seed-forms connected with speech, desire and power. The name points to Her mantra-form and to the triadic structure of Śrīvidyā."],"searchText":"630 त्र्यक्षरी त्रयाणामक्षराणां वाक्कामशक्तिबीजात्मकानां समाहारः। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. त्र्यक्षरी means one who is of three letters. the three letters may be understood as the seed-forms connected with speech, desire and power. the name points to her mantra-form and to the triadic structure of śrīvidyā. the triadic sound formula: the name points directly to the three supreme seed-syllables that build the vāgbhava, kāmarāja, and śakti blocks of her text—specifically the sounds ऐं, क्लीं, सौः (aiṁ, klīṁ, sauḥ). she is the direct phonic embodiment of this triadic formula, which contains the complete energetic geometry of creation.","esoteric":["The Triadic Sound Formula: The name points directly to the three supreme seed-syllables that build the Vāgbhava, Kāmarāja, and Śakti blocks of Her text—specifically the sounds ऐं, क्लीं, सौः (Aiṁ, Klīṁ, Sauḥ). She is the direct phonic embodiment of this triadic formula, which contains the complete energetic geometry of creation."]},{"number":631,"name":"दिव्यगन्धाढ्या","samasa":["दिवि भवा दिव्या देवादयश्चेतनाचेतनात्मकपदार्थसमूहाः। तेषां गन्धैः सम्बन्धैराढ्या परिपूर्णा।","दिव्यगन्धो हरिचन्दनादिपरिमलः, तेनाढ्या।","दिव्यगन्धा आढ्याः सम्पन्ना यया प्रसादात्सा।"],"wordByWord":["दिवि — in heaven","भवा — existing","गन्धैः — by fragrances/relations"],"summary":["दिव्यगन्धाढ्या means one who is rich in divine fragrance. Divya-gandha may mean celestial sandal and other divine perfumes. It may also indicate that the divine beings and their relationships are pervaded by Her grace."],"searchText":"631 दिव्यगन्धाढ्या दिवि भवा दिव्या देवादयश्चेतनाचेतनात्मकपदार्थसमूहाः। तेषां गन्धैः सम्बन्धैराढ्या परिपूर्णा। दिव्यगन्धो हरिचन्दनादिपरिमलः, तेनाढ्या। दिव्यगन्धा आढ्याः सम्पन्ना यया प्रसादात्सा। दिवि — in heaven भवा — existing गन्धैः — by fragrances/relations दिव्यगन्धाढ्या means one who is rich in divine fragrance. divya-gandha may mean celestial sandal and other divine perfumes. it may also indicate that the divine beings and their relationships are pervaded by her grace. the fabric of relations: while it physically marks her perfume as divine sandalwood (hari-candana), गन्ध (gandha) means connection or relational alignment. she is divyagandhāḍhyā because she is perfectly filled with the invisible, interconnected fabric that ties every element, space coordinate, and soul together in cosmic harmony.","esoteric":["The Fabric of Relations: While it physically marks Her perfume as divine sandalwood (Hari-candana), गन्ध (gandha) means connection or relational alignment. She is Divyagandhāḍhyā because She is perfectly filled with the invisible, interconnected fabric that ties every element, space coordinate, and soul together in cosmic harmony."]},{"number":632,"name":"सिन्दूरतिलकाञ्चिता","samasa":["सिन्दूरस्य तिलकेन चित्रकेणाञ्चिता युक्ता।","सिन्दूरतिलकाभ्यामञ्चिता।"],"wordByWord":["सिन्दूरस्य — of vermilion","तिलकेन — by a forehead mark"],"summary":["सिन्दूरतिलकाञ्चिता means one adorned with a vermilion mark. The sindūra tilaka beautifies Her forehead and is a sign of auspiciousness. The name is connected with the traditional contemplation of Devī as adorned with auspicious marks."],"searchText":"632 सिन्दूरतिलकाञ्चिता सिन्दूरस्य तिलकेन चित्रकेणाञ्चिता युक्ता। सिन्दूरतिलकाभ्यामञ्चिता। सिन्दूरस्य — of vermilion तिलकेन — by a forehead mark सिन्दूरतिलकाञ्चिता means one adorned with a vermilion mark. the sindūra tilaka beautifies her forehead and is a sign of auspiciousness. the name is connected with the traditional contemplation of devī as adorned with auspicious marks. the radiance of the brow center: the bright red vermilion mark (sindūra-tilaka) sits directly over the ājñā chakra center. it visually represents the blazing, active presence of her creative intent and protective force anchored at the command bridge of the subtle body, radiating auspiciousness to the seeker.","esoteric":["The Radiance of the Brow Center: The bright red vermilion mark (sindūra-tilaka) sits directly over the Ājñā chakra center. It visually represents the blazing, active presence of Her creative intent and protective force anchored at the command bridge of the subtle body, radiating auspiciousness to the seeker."]},{"number":633,"name":"उमा","samasa":["उकारः शिववाचकस्तस्य मा लक्ष्मीः।","उं परशिवं माति परिच्छिनत्तीति।","उः उत्तमा च सा मा चित्तवृत्तिश्चेति।","अकारोकारमकारा मदीये प्रणवे स्थिताः।उकारं च मकारं च अकारं च क्रमेरितम्॥"],"wordByWord":["उकारः — the syllable u","सा — she"],"summary":["उमा means umā is interpreted in many ways. U may indicate Śiva and mā may indicate Lakṣmī or measuring power; thus the name contains Śiva-Śakti meanings. The name is also connected with the praṇava and with traditional interpretations of Umā in Śaiva and Śākta texts."],"searchText":"633 उमा उकारः शिववाचकस्तस्य मा लक्ष्मीः। उं परशिवं माति परिच्छिनत्तीति। उः उत्तमा च सा मा चित्तवृत्तिश्चेति। अकारोकारमकारा मदीये प्रणवे स्थिताः।उकारं च मकारं च अकारं च क्रमेरितम्॥ उकारः — the syllable u सा — she उमा means umā is interpreted in many ways. u may indicate śiva and mā may indicate lakṣmī or measuring power; thus the name contains śiva-śakti meanings. the name is also connected with the praṇava and with traditional interpretations of umā in śaiva and śākta texts. the mirror of shiva: उ (u) signifies lord śiva (pure consciousness), and मा (mā) means his light, wealth, or mirror. she is the dynamic reflection that allows consciousness to know itself. the synthesis of the praṇava: he notes her structural identity within the syllables of ओम् (aum), where the sounds are inverted and integrated to prove her non-differentiation from the ultimate word.","esoteric":["The Mirror of Shiva: उ (u) signifies Lord Śiva (pure consciousness), and मा (mā) means His light, wealth, or mirror. She is the dynamic reflection that allows consciousness to know itself.","The Synthesis of the Praṇava: He notes Her structural identity within the syllables of ओम् (Aum), where the sounds are inverted and integrated to prove Her non-differentiation from the ultimate word."]},{"number":634,"name":"शैलेन्द्रतनया","samasa":["शैलेन्द्रस्य पर्वतराजस्य हिमवतस्तनया पुत्री।"],"wordByWord":["शैलेन्द्रस्य — of the mountain lord"],"summary":["शैलेन्द्रतनया means daughter of the lord of mountains, Himavān. The name identifies Her as Pārvatī, born as the daughter of the mountain king. It also recalls Her manifest form for devotees."],"searchText":"634 शैलेन्द्रतनया शैलेन्द्रस्य पर्वतराजस्य हिमवतस्तनया पुत्री। शैलेन्द्रस्य — of the mountain lord शैलेन्द्रतनया means daughter of the lord of mountains, himavān. the name identifies her as pārvatī, born as the daughter of the mountain king. it also recalls her manifest form for devotees. the spine of earthly stability: she chose to manifest as pārvatī, daughter of the himālayas (śailendra). mountains represent the firm, unmoving, structural anchors of the earth element. by anchoring her physical manifestation to this range, she establishes the firm, grounded channel within the spine of the earth, aligning with the macrocosmic suṣumṇā.","esoteric":["The Spine of Earthly Stability: She chose to manifest as Pārvatī, daughter of the Himālayas (Śailendra). Mountains represent the firm, unmoving, structural anchors of the earth element. By anchoring Her physical manifestation to this range, She establishes the firm, grounded channel within the spine of the earth, aligning with the macrocosmic Suṣumṇā."]},{"number":635,"name":"गौरी","samasa":["गौरवर्णत्वाद्गौरी।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["गौरी means one who is fair or radiant. Gaurī means the bright or fair one. The name points to Her auspicious and shining form."],"searchText":"635 गौरी गौरवर्णत्वाद्गौरी। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. गौरी means one who is fair or radiant. gaurī means the bright or fair one. the name points to her auspicious and shining form. the pristine radiance: as gaurī, her skin radiates a brilliant, unblemished golden-white light. this frequency represents the complete purification of the material field (prakṛti) when it is brought into proximity with pure consciousness. she is the light that contains no dark corners of ignorance, radiating absolute clarity.","esoteric":["The Pristine Radiance: As Gaurī, Her skin radiates a brilliant, unblemished golden-white light. This frequency represents the complete purification of the material field (Prakṛti) when it is brought into proximity with pure consciousness. She is the light that contains no dark corners of ignorance, radiating absolute clarity."]},{"number":636,"name":"गन्धर्वसेविता","samasa":["गन्धर्वैः सेविता।"],"wordByWord":["गन्धर्वैः — by Gandharvas"],"summary":["गन्धर्वसेविता means one served by Gandharvas. The celestial musicians praise and worship Her. Their service shows that divine music and praise belong to Her worship."],"searchText":"636 गन्धर्वसेविता गन्धर्वैः सेविता। गन्धर्वैः — by gandharvas गन्धर्वसेविता means one served by gandharvas. the celestial musicians praise and worship her. their service shows that divine music and praise belong to her worship. the sovereign of harmonics: the gandharvas are the celestial masters of music, fine melody, and rhythm. their constant service at her throne indicates that every perfect musical note, scale, and harmonic frequency in the universe is merely a faint echo of her inner cosmic voice, adoring her as the source of sound.","esoteric":["The Sovereign of Harmonics: The Gandharvas are the celestial masters of music, fine melody, and rhythm. Their constant service at Her throne indicates that every perfect musical note, scale, and harmonic frequency in the universe is merely a faint echo of Her inner cosmic voice, adoring Her as the source of sound."]},{"number":637,"name":"विश्वगर्भा","samasa":["विश्वं प्रपञ्चजातं गर्भे यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वं — universe","गर्भे — in the womb","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["विश्वगर्भा means one who has the universe in Her womb. The entire manifest world is contained in Her before and during manifestation. She is therefore the cosmic mother and source of all worlds."],"searchText":"637 विश्वगर्भा विश्वं प्रपञ्चजातं गर्भे यस्याः सा। विश्वं — universe गर्भे — in the womb यस्याः — of whom; whose विश्वगर्भा means one who has the universe in her womb. the entire manifest world is contained in her before and during manifestation. she is therefore the cosmic mother and source of all worlds. the safe embryo of consciousness: the universe does not sit outside of her space like an independent house built by a carpenter. the entire projection remains permanently inside her causal womb (garbha), drawing its baseline existence and nourishment directly from her field, fully protected like a child within its mother.","esoteric":["The Safe Embryo of Consciousness: The universe does not sit outside of Her space like an independent house built by a carpenter. The entire projection remains permanently inside Her causal womb (garbha), drawing its baseline existence and nourishment directly from Her field, fully protected like a child within its mother."]},{"number":638,"name":"स्वर्णगर्भा","samasa":["स्वर्णं हिरण्यं गर्भे यस्याः सा।","स्वर्णस्य गर्भभवा।","अर्णानां वर्णानां मातृकाणां गर्भः शोभनो यया सा।","स्वर्णाः शोभनार्णा मन्त्रा गर्भे यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्वर्णं — gold","हिरण्यं — golden principle","गर्भे — in the womb","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["स्वर्णगर्भा means one whose womb is golden or who contains hiraṇya. The name may also be read in relation to varṇas, mātr̥kās and auspicious mantras held within Her. She is the womb of radiant creation and mantra-consciousness."],"searchText":"638 स्वर्णगर्भा स्वर्णं हिरण्यं गर्भे यस्याः सा। स्वर्णस्य गर्भभवा। अर्णानां वर्णानां मातृकाणां गर्भः शोभनो यया सा। स्वर्णाः शोभनार्णा मन्त्रा गर्भे यस्याः सा। स्वर्णं — gold हिरण्यं — golden principle गर्भे — in the womb यस्याः — of whom; whose स्वर्णगर्भा means one whose womb is golden or who contains hiraṇya. the name may also be read in relation to varṇas, mātr̥kās and auspicious mantras held within her. she is the womb of radiant creation and mantra-consciousness. the cosmic light source: she is identical with हिरण्यगर्भ (hiraṇyagarbha — the golden womb of cosmic light that initiates creation). the mantric repository: under the phonetic track, सु-वर्ण means beautiful, potent letters. she is svarṇagarbhā because she contains the complete matrix of all brilliant, hidden mantras inside her causal field, holding their formatting codes safe.","esoteric":["The Cosmic Light Source: She is identical with हिरण्यगर्भ (Hiraṇyagarbha — the golden womb of cosmic light that initiates creation).","The Mantric Repository: Under the phonetic track, सु-वर्ण means beautiful, potent letters. She is Svarṇagarbhā because She contains the complete matrix of all brilliant, hidden mantras inside Her causal field, holding their formatting codes safe."]},{"number":639,"name":"अवरदा","samasa":["अवरदेति चतुरक्षरं नाम। अवराननार्यानसुरान् द्यति खण्डयतीति।","अवन्तीत्यवाः कान्तिमन्तो रदा दन्ता यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["अवरदा means it may indicate one who destroys the ignoble or demonic. The name is explained in more than one way. It may indicate one who destroys the ignoble or demonic; it may also be connected with beautiful, shining teeth. The traditional explanations preserve both a protective and a beauty-related sense."],"searchText":"639 अवरदा अवरदेति चतुरक्षरं नाम। अवराननार्यानसुरान् द्यति खण्डयतीति। अवन्तीत्यवाः कान्तिमन्तो रदा दन्ता यस्याः सा। यस्याः — of whom; whose अवरदा means it may indicate one who destroys the ignoble or demonic. the name is explained in more than one way. it may indicate one who destroys the ignoble or demonic; it may also be connected with beautiful, shining teeth. the traditional explanations preserve both a protective and a beauty-related sense. the dissolver of low intent: अवर (avara) refers to the dark, chaotic, unrighteous demonic forces that attack spiritual balance. she is the power that cuts down (dyati) these deviations. alternatively, her teeth are beautifully radiant, acting as a metaphor for the sharp, defensive boundary walls that guard her countenance.","esoteric":["The Dissolver of Low Intent: अवर (avara) refers to the dark, chaotic, unrighteous demonic forces that attack spiritual balance. She is the power that cuts down (dyati) these deviations. Alternatively, Her teeth are beautifully radiant, acting as a metaphor for the sharp, defensive boundary walls that guard Her countenance."]},{"number":640,"name":"वागधीश्वरी","samasa":["वाचाम् अधीश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["वाचाम् — of speech/words"],"summary":["वागधीश्वरी means sovereign of speech. All words, expression and learning stand under Her rule. As the power behind speech, She is worshipped as the supreme source of vāṇī."],"searchText":"640 वागधीश्वरी वाचाम् अधीश्वरी। वाचाम् — of speech/words वागधीश्वरी means sovereign of speech. all words, expression and learning stand under her rule. as the power behind speech, she is worshipped as the supreme source of vāṇī. this states her supreme legislative control over communication: the commander of language: she is the absolute director governing the entire grid of human and divine expression (vāk). she rules over grammar, semantic translation, and philosophical formulation. every word spoken or written operates strictly under her structural coordination, making her the ultimate master of wisdom.","esoteric":["this states Her supreme legislative control over communication:","The Commander of Language: She is the absolute director governing the entire grid of human and divine expression (Vāk). She rules over grammar, semantic translation, and philosophical formulation. Every word spoken or written operates strictly under Her structural coordination, making Her the ultimate master of wisdom."]},{"number":641,"name":"ध्यानगम्या","samasa":["ध्यानेन विभावनेन गम्या ज्ञेया।"],"wordByWord":["ध्यानेन — by meditation","गम्या — attainable; knowable"],"summary":["ध्यानगम्या means one who is reached through meditation. She is known by dhyāna and inner contemplation, not by external perception alone. By meditating on Her, the devotee becomes absorbed in Her presence."],"searchText":"641 ध्यानगम्या ध्यानेन विभावनेन गम्या ज्ञेया। ध्यानेन — by meditation गम्या — attainable; knowable ध्यानगम्या means one who is reached through meditation. she is known by dhyāna and inner contemplation, not by external perception alone. by meditating on her, the devotee becomes absorbed in her presence. the internal approach: she cannot be uncovered by external physical travel, ostentatious public displays, or dry intellectual debate. she is dhyānagamyā—accessible exclusively when the practitioner turns the attention inward, quietens the cognitive ripples, and enters a state of deep, continuous mental absorption (dhyāna).","esoteric":["The Internal Approach: She cannot be uncovered by external physical travel, ostentatious public displays, or dry intellectual debate. She is Dhyānagamyā—accessible exclusively when the practitioner turns the attention inward, quietens the cognitive ripples, and enters a state of deep, continuous mental absorption (dhyāna)."]},{"number":642,"name":"अपरिच्छेद्या","samasa":["न परिच्छेद्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["अपरिच्छेद्या means one who cannot be delimited. She cannot be divided by space, time, object or thought. Her nature is unlimited and beyond all finite boundaries."],"searchText":"642 अपरिच्छेद्या न परिच्छेद्या। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. अपरिच्छेद्या means one who cannot be delimited. she cannot be divided by space, time, object or thought. her nature is unlimited and beyond all finite boundaries. beyond partition: material objects can be chopped into pieces, limited by boundary walls, or cut off by the passage of time. as the unconditioned absolute reality, she possesses no edges. she cannot be partitioned by spatial lines, split by historical eras, or fragmented by mental concepts, remaining eternally whole.","esoteric":["Beyond Partition: Material objects can be chopped into pieces, limited by boundary walls, or cut off by the passage of time. As the unconditioned absolute reality, She possesses no edges. She cannot be partitioned by spatial lines, split by historical eras, or fragmented by mental concepts, remaining eternally whole."]},{"number":643,"name":"ज्ञानदा","samasa":["ज्ञानं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["ज्ञानं — knowledge"],"summary":["ज्ञानदा means giver of knowledge. She grants knowledge of both worldly and spiritual truths. Ultimately She gives the liberating knowledge of the Self."],"searchText":"643 ज्ञानदा ज्ञानं ददातीति। ज्ञानं — knowledge ज्ञानदा means giver of knowledge. she grants knowledge of both worldly and spiritual truths. ultimately she gives the liberating knowledge of the self. the granting of awakening: the individual soul is trapped by the illusion of separation. she acts as jñānadā, directly bestowing ब्रह्मज्ञान (brahma-jñāna — non-dual self-knowledge). this gift instantly vaporizes the structural ignorance of the seeker, dissolving their bondage and granting immediate spiritual freedom.","esoteric":["The Granting of Awakening: The individual soul is trapped by the illusion of separation. She acts as Jñānadā, directly bestowing ब्रह्मज्ञान (Brahma-jñāna — non-dual self-knowledge). This gift instantly vaporizes the structural ignorance of the seeker, dissolving their bondage and granting immediate spiritual freedom."]},{"number":644,"name":"ज्ञानविग्रहा","samasa":["ज्ञानमेव विग्रहः शरीरं यस्याः सा।","ज्ञानस्य विग्रहो विस्तारो यस्याः सकाशात् सा।"],"wordByWord":["ज्ञानमेव — knowledge itself","विग्रहः — body; form","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["ज्ञानविग्रहा means one whose very body is knowledge. Knowledge is not merely Her attribute but Her form itself. The expansion of knowledge proceeds from Her."],"searchText":"644 ज्ञानविग्रहा ज्ञानमेव विग्रहः शरीरं यस्याः सा। ज्ञानस्य विग्रहो विस्तारो यस्याः सकाशात् सा। ज्ञानमेव — knowledge itself विग्रहः — body; form यस्याः — of whom; whose ज्ञानविग्रहा means one whose very body is knowledge. knowledge is not merely her attribute but her form itself. the expansion of knowledge proceeds from her. identity with wisdom: lest a student think that she is a person who simply holds information, this name states her body is made of nothing but pure knowledge itself (jñāna-svarūpa). alternatively, she is the primary fountainhead out of which the complete expansion (vigraha) of all sciences and arts streams into the cosmos.","esoteric":["Identity with Wisdom: Lest a student think that She is a person who simply holds information, this name states Her body is made of nothing but pure knowledge itself (Jñāna-svarūpa). Alternatively, She is the primary fountainhead out of which the complete expansion (vigraha) of all sciences and arts streams into the cosmos."]},{"number":645,"name":"सर्ववेदान्तसंवेद्या","samasa":["सर्वैर्वेदान्तैरुपनिषत्समूहैः समयग्वेद्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सर्ववेदान्तसंवेद्या means one known by all Vedānta. The Upaniṣads and Vedānta texts point to Her as the supreme reality. She is the truth to be realised through the culmination of scriptural enquiry."],"searchText":"645 सर्ववेदान्तसंवेद्या सर्वैर्वेदान्तैरुपनिषत्समूहैः समयग्वेद्या। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सर्ववेदान्तसंवेद्या means one known by all vedānta. the upaniṣads and vedānta texts point to her as the supreme reality. she is the truth to be realised through the culmination of scriptural enquiry. the core subject of non-duality: वेदान्त (vedānta) represents the peak upanishadic records. every riddle, statement, and paradox found inside the upanishads has only one ultimate target. their corporate intent is to point directly to her essential nature as the non-dual absolute consciousness baseline of existence.","esoteric":["The Core Subject of Non-Duality: वेदान्त (Vedānta) represents the peak Upanishadic records. every riddle, statement, and paradox found inside the Upanishads has only one ultimate target. Their corporate intent is to point directly to Her essential nature as the non-dual absolute consciousness baseline of existence."]},{"number":646,"name":"सत्यानन्दस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["सत्यमानन्दश्च स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["सत्यानन्दस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is truth and bliss. Satya and ānanda are Her own nature. The name points to Her as the blissful reality beyond false appearances."],"searchText":"646 सत्यानन्दस्वरूपिणी सत्यमानन्दश्च स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। स्वरूपं — own form; essential nature यस्याः — of whom; whose सत्यानन्दस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is truth and bliss. satya and ānanda are her own nature. the name points to her as the blissful reality beyond false appearances. the reality of bliss: she embodies the two primary operational attributes that define the absolute absolute reality—सत्य (satya — uncorrupted existence/truth) and आनन्द (ānanda — unconditioned bliss). she is the living expression of this reality, comforting the practitioner that the source of existence is full of ecstatic joy.","esoteric":["The Reality of Bliss: She embodies the two primary operational attributes that define the absolute absolute reality—सत्य (Satya — uncorrupted existence/truth) and आनन्द (Ānanda — unconditioned bliss). She is the living expression of this reality, comforting the practitioner that the source of existence is full of ecstatic joy."]},{"number":647,"name":"लोपामुद्रार्चिता","samasa":["लोपामुद्रया अगस्त्यपत्न्या कर्त्र्या अर्चिता उपासिता।"],"wordByWord":["लोपामुद्रया — by Lopāmudrā","अर्चिता — worshipped"],"summary":["लोपामुद्रार्चिता means worshipped by Lopāmudrā, the wife of Agastya. Lopāmudrā is one of the great Śrīvidyā upāsakās. The name links Her worship to the lineage of Agastya and Lopāmudrā."],"searchText":"647 लोपामुद्रार्चिता लोपामुद्रया अगस्त्यपत्न्या कर्त्र्या अर्चिता उपासिता। लोपामुद्रया — by lopāmudrā अर्चिता — worshipped लोपामुद्रार्चिता means worshipped by lopāmudrā, the wife of agastya. lopāmudrā is one of the great śrīvidyā upāsakās. the name links her worship to the lineage of agastya and lopāmudrā. the hādi lineage crown: lopāmudrā, the consort of sage agastya, is one of the premier master seers of the śrīvidyā tradition, credited with bringing down the highly revered हादि-मत (hādi-mata) formulation of the core mantra. her intense adoration confirms the absolute authority and scriptural validity of this branch of practice.","esoteric":["The Hādi Lineage Crown: Lopāmudrā, the consort of Sage Agastya, is one of the premier master seers of the Śrīvidyā tradition, credited with bringing down the highly revered हादि-मत (Hādi-mata) formulation of the core mantra. Her intense adoration confirms the absolute authority and scriptural validity of this branch of practice."]},{"number":648,"name":"लीलाकॢप्तब्रह्माण्डमण्डला","samasa":["लीलामात्रेणानायासेन कॢप्तानि ब्रह्माण्डमण्डलानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कॢप्तानि — created; fashioned","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["लीलाकॢप्तब्रह्माण्डमण्डला means one who playfully creates the spheres of countless Brahmāṇḍas. Creation is only līlā for Her, done without effort. The cosmic egg-clusters arise by Her mere sport."],"searchText":"648 लीलाकॢप्तब्रह्माण्डमण्डला लीलामात्रेणानायासेन कॢप्तानि ब्रह्माण्डमण्डलानि यस्याः सा। कॢप्तानि — created; fashioned यस्याः — of whom; whose लीलाकॢप्तब्रह्माण्डमण्डला means one who playfully creates the spheres of countless brahmāṇḍas. creation is only līlā for her, done without effort. the cosmic egg-clusters arise by her mere sport. effortless cosmic architecture: the creation, structuring, and alignment of infinite planetary grids and universal caskets require no heavy labor, planning committees, or structural fatigue from her end. it is a spontaneous, effortless overflow of her playful energy (līlā), projected as easily as a child breathing out soap bubbles.","esoteric":["Effortless Cosmic Architecture: The creation, structuring, and alignment of infinite planetary grids and universal caskets require no heavy labor, planning committees, or structural fatigue from Her end. It is a spontaneous, effortless overflow of Her playful energy (līlā), projected as easily as a child breathing out soap bubbles."]},{"number":649,"name":"अदृश्या","samasa":["दृश्यविलक्षणत्वाददृश्या।","चक्षुरादीन्द्रियायोग्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["अदृश्या means one who is invisible. She is different from all visible objects and is not grasped by the eyes or senses. Her reality is to be known inwardly, not by ordinary sight."],"searchText":"649 अदृश्या दृश्यविलक्षणत्वाददृश्या। चक्षुरादीन्द्रियायोग्या। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. अदृश्या means one who is invisible. she is different from all visible objects and is not grasped by the eyes or senses. her reality is to be known inwardly, not by ordinary sight. the invisible subject: human eyes and sensory channels are designed strictly to capture external, material objects (dṛśya). because she is the foundational subjective consciousness that sits behind the eyes, enabling them to see in the first place, she can never be seen as an external object. she is the ultimate seer, permanently invisible to outer sight.","esoteric":["The Invisible Subject: Human eyes and sensory channels are designed strictly to capture external, material objects (dṛśya). Because She is the foundational subjective consciousness that sits behind the eyes, enabling them to see in the first place, She can never be seen as an external object. She is the ultimate seer, permanently invisible to outer sight."]},{"number":650,"name":"दृश्यरहिता","samasa":["दृश्येण रहिता"],"wordByWord":["रहिता — devoid of"],"summary":["दृश्यरहिता means one who is free from the visible. She is not an object of perception and is not limited by what can be seen. The visible world depends on Her, but She transcends it."],"searchText":"650 दृश्यरहिता दृश्येण रहिता रहिता — devoid of दृश्यरहिता means one who is free from the visible. she is not an object of perception and is not limited by what can be seen. the visible world depends on her, but she transcends it. the resolution of duality: दृश्य (dṛśya) represents the entire field of changing, objective material appearances. she is dṛṣyarahitā because in her ultimate essential state (svarūpa), the illusion of a separate objective universe completely dissolves. when the practitioner achieves the highest absorption (nirvikalpa-samādhi), the movie of the world vanishes, leaving her to shine alone in her pristine, non-dual subjective purity.","esoteric":["The Resolution of Duality: दृश्य (dṛśya) represents the entire field of changing, objective material appearances. She is Dṛṣyarahitā because in Her ultimate essential state (Svarūpa), the illusion of a separate objective universe completely dissolves. When the practitioner achieves the highest absorption (Nirvikalpa-Samādhi), the movie of the world vanishes, leaving Her to shine alone in Her pristine, non-dual subjective purity."]},{"number":651,"name":"विज्ञात्री","samasa":["विशेषेण जानातीति विज्ञात्री।"],"wordByWord":["विशेषेण — especially"],"summary":["विज्ञात्री means one who is the knower. She is the special intelligence behind all knowledge. Though She is the power of knowing, She is distinct from every known object."],"searchText":"651 विज्ञात्री विशेषेण जानातीति विज्ञात्री। विशेषेण — especially विज्ञात्री means one who is the knower. she is the special intelligence behind all knowledge. though she is the power of knowing, she is distinct from every known object. the absolute knower: she is the ultimate subject (draṣṭā) behind all acts of perception. while ordinary intellects analyze separate objects, she is the non-dual baseline awareness that comprehends the entire cosmos comprehensively and distinctively, without error or modification.","esoteric":["The Absolute Knower: She is the ultimate subject (draṣṭā) behind all acts of perception. While ordinary intellects analyze separate objects, She is the non-dual baseline awareness that comprehends the entire cosmos comprehensively and distinctively, without error or modification."]},{"number":652,"name":"वेद्यवर्जिता","samasa":["वेद्येन वेद्यस्य वा वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["वेद्येन — by the knowable"],"summary":["वेद्यवर्जिता means one who is devoid of anything to be known apart from Herself. There is no separate object by which She can be fully known. As the ultimate knower, She is beyond the category of the knowable."],"searchText":"652 वेद्यवर्जिता वेद्येन वेद्यस्य वा वर्जिता। वेद्येन — by the knowable वेद्यवर्जिता means one who is devoid of anything to be known apart from herself. there is no separate object by which she can be fully known. as the ultimate knower, she is beyond the category of the knowable. beyond knower and known: though she functions as the ultimate knower (vijñātrī), she is simultaneously vedyavarjitā because there is no independent second object outside of her own nature to be known. in her essential state of absolute absorption (samādhi), the triad of knower, knowing, and known dissolves into pure, unified awareness.","esoteric":["Beyond Knower and Known: Though She functions as the ultimate Knower (Vijñātrī), She is simultaneously Vedyavarjitā because there is no independent second object outside of Her own nature to be known. In Her essential state of absolute absorption (Samādhi), the triad of knower, knowing, and known dissolves into pure, unified awareness."]},{"number":653,"name":"योगिनी","samasa":["योगः एकत्वभावना अस्याः अस्तीति।","योगः विषयसङ्गः भोगः, सः अस्याः अस्तीति भोक्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["योगः — yoga; union","एकत्वभावना — contemplation of oneness"],"summary":["योगिनी means one who is in the form of yoga. Yoga means the union or identity of the individual and the supreme. It may also be explained as bhoga in another interpretive line; She is present in both yoga and experience."],"searchText":"653 योगिनी योगः एकत्वभावना अस्याः अस्तीति। योगः विषयसङ्गः भोगः, सः अस्याः अस्तीति भोक्त्री। योगः — yoga; union एकत्वभावना — contemplation of oneness योगिनी means one who is in the form of yoga. yoga means the union or identity of the individual and the supreme. it may also be explained as bhoga in another interpretive line; she is present in both yoga and experience. the spirit of union: योग represents the intense internal cultivation of oneness (ekatva-bhāvanā) between the individual soul and the universal self. the cosmic consumer: alternatively, yoga can denote cosmic experience and sensory contact (bhoga). she is the ultimate consumer who experiences the universe through all forms while remaining untainted. in agamic geometry, it also names her as the supreme source behind all attendant yogini energy hosts.","esoteric":["The Spirit of Union: योग represents the intense internal cultivation of oneness (ekatva-bhāvanā) between the individual soul and the universal Self.","The Cosmic Consumer: Alternatively, Yoga can denote cosmic experience and sensory contact (bhoga). She is the ultimate consumer who experiences the universe through all forms while remaining untainted. In Agamic geometry, it also names Her as the supreme source behind all attendant yogini energy hosts."]},{"number":654,"name":"योगदा","samasa":["योगं ददातीति।","योगः विषयसङ्गः भोगः, तं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["योगं — yoga","योगः — yoga; union"],"summary":["योगदा means one who gives yoga. She grants union with the supreme reality. In another sense She also gives the experiences appropriate to the devotee."],"searchText":"654 योगदा योगं ददातीति। योगः विषयसङ्गः भोगः, तं ददातीति। योगं — yoga योगः — yoga; union योगदा means one who gives yoga. she grants union with the supreme reality. in another sense she also gives the experiences appropriate to the devotee. the dispenser of liberation and enjoyment: she is the dynamic force that grants the gift of spiritual union (yoga), linking the disciplined seeker back to the absolute. concurrently, for those on the path of integrated practice, she perfectly measures out the appropriate external alignment and cosmic experience (bhoga) needed for overall evolution.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of Liberation and Enjoyment: She is the dynamic force that grants the gift of spiritual union (Yoga), linking the disciplined seeker back to the absolute. Concurrently, for those on the path of integrated practice, She perfectly measures out the appropriate external alignment and cosmic experience (bhoga) needed for overall evolution."]},{"number":655,"name":"योग्या","samasa":["योगः विषयसङ्गः भोगः, योग्यत्वात् भोग्या।"],"wordByWord":["योगः — yoga; union"],"summary":["योग्या means one who is fit to be attained through yoga. She is the proper object of spiritual union and worship. In an alternate interpretation, the name also connects with bhogya, that which is fit for enjoyment or experience."],"searchText":"655 योग्या योगः विषयसङ्गः भोगः, योग्यत्वात् भोग्या। योगः — yoga; union योग्या means one who is fit to be attained through yoga. she is the proper object of spiritual union and worship. in an alternate interpretation, the name also connects with bhogya, that which is fit for enjoyment or experience. the proper object of realization: she is yogyā because she is the only reality truly fit (yogya) to be sought after, adored, and meditated upon by advanced intellects. every other material object provides transient distraction, while she represents the ultimate, correct destination of human consciousness.","esoteric":["The Proper Object of Realization: She is Yogyā because She is the only reality truly fit (yogya) to be sought after, adored, and meditated upon by advanced intellects. Every other material object provides transient distraction, while She represents the ultimate, correct destination of human consciousness."]},{"number":656,"name":"योगानन्दा","samasa":["योगस्य आनन्दः यस्याः सा।","निद्रायाः आनन्दप्रधानत्वात् योगनिद्रा।","योगानन्दः नृसिंहः तद्रूपा।","/अयोगा।","योगः सङ्गः न विद्यते यस्याः सा।","अयेन शुभावहविधिना उं परशिवं गच्छतीति।","/नन्दा।","अलकनन्दात्मकगङ्गारूपा।","नन्दजा नन्दा मूर्तिविशेषरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["योगस्य — of yoga","आनन्दः — bliss","यस्याः — of whom; whose","योगः — yoga; union","विद्यते — exists"],"summary":["योगानन्दा means one who is the bliss obtained through yoga. The union of Śiva and Śakti is yoga, and its bliss is yogānanda. The name is also interpreted through sleep, Yogānanda Nṛsiṃha, and alternate readings such as Ayogā and Nandā."],"searchText":"656 योगानन्दा योगस्य आनन्दः यस्याः सा। निद्रायाः आनन्दप्रधानत्वात् योगनिद्रा। योगानन्दः नृसिंहः तद्रूपा। /अयोगा। योगः सङ्गः न विद्यते यस्याः सा। अयेन शुभावहविधिना उं परशिवं गच्छतीति। /नन्दा। अलकनन्दात्मकगङ्गारूपा। नन्दजा नन्दा मूर्तिविशेषरूपा। योगस्य — of yoga आनन्दः — bliss यस्याः — of whom; whose योगः — yoga; union विद्यते — exists योगानन्दा means one who is the bliss obtained through yoga. the union of śiva and śakti is yoga, and its bliss is yogānanda. the name is also interpreted through sleep, yogānanda nṛsiṃha, and alternate readings such as ayogā and nandā. the bliss of yoga: as yogānandā, she is the ecstatic bliss experienced when the mind enters perfect stillness (samādhi), or identical to the cosmic rest state yoga-nidrā. the unconnected absolute: as ayogā, she possesses no binding contact (saṅga) with material mutations. alternatively, she leads practitioners to lord śiva through pure auspicious pathways (ayena). the source of delight: as nandā, she manifests as the cleansing current of the gaṅgā or the ancient protective structural deity born in the nanda lineage.","esoteric":["The Bliss of Yoga: As Yogānandā, She is the ecstatic bliss experienced when the mind enters perfect stillness (Samādhi), or identical to the cosmic rest state Yoga-nidrā.","The Unconnected Absolute: As Ayogā, She possesses no binding contact (saṅga) with material mutations. Alternatively, She leads practitioners to Lord Śiva through pure auspicious pathways (ayena).","The Source of Delight: As Nandā, She manifests as the cleansing current of the Gaṅgā or the ancient protective structural deity born in the Nanda lineage."]},{"number":657,"name":"युगन्धरा","samasa":["युगं धारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["युगं — era; yuga"],"summary":["युगन्धरा means one who supports the yuga or era. Yuga has several meanings, including an era, a pair, a yoke and a measure. The Kr̥ta and other yugas are supported only by the Śiva-Śakti form; therefore She is Yugandharā."],"searchText":"657 युगन्धरा युगं धारयतीति। युगं — era; yuga युगन्धरा means one who supports the yuga or era. yuga has several meanings, including an era, a pair, a yoke and a measure. the kr̥ta and other yugas are supported only by the śiva-śakti form; therefore she is yugandharā. the upholder of time cycles: the universe passes through the massive cycles of the four eras (yugas — satya, tretā, dvāpara, and kali). she is yugandharā because she functions as the absolute background axis that bears the weight of these epochal shifts, ensuring the continuity of cosmic balance across vast expanses of time.","esoteric":["The Upholder of Time Cycles: The universe passes through the massive cycles of the four eras (yugas — Satya, Tretā, Dvāpara, and Kali). She is Yugandharā because She functions as the absolute background axis that bears the weight of these epochal shifts, ensuring the continuity of cosmic balance across vast expanses of time."]},{"number":658,"name":"इच्छाशक्तिज्ञानशक्तिक्रियाशक्तिस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["इच्छाज्ञानक्रियारूपगुणत्रयं स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["इच्छाशक्तिज्ञानशक्तिक्रियाशक्तिस्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the three powers: desire, knowledge and action. Every task needs icchā-śakti, jñāna-śakti and kriyā-śakti, and all three are Śrīdevī. These three powers are also seen as the forms behind creation, protection and destruction."],"searchText":"658 इच्छाशक्तिज्ञानशक्तिक्रियाशक्तिस्वरूपिणी इच्छाज्ञानक्रियारूपगुणत्रयं स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. इच्छाशक्तिज्ञानशक्तिक्रियाशक्तिस्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the three powers: desire, knowledge and action. every task needs icchā-śakti, jñāna-śakti and kriyā-śakti, and all three are śrīdevī. these three powers are also seen as the forms behind creation, protection and destruction. the triadic force matrix: she is the absolute consolidation of the three baseline functional energies that project the universe. as इच्छाशक्ति (icchā-śakti), she provides the initial divine intent to create. as ज्ञानशक्ति (jñāna-śakti), she maintains the intellectual blueprint of design. as क्रियाशक्ति (kriyā-śakti), she executes the actual kinetic movement into dense material elements, proving her status as the full dynamic expression of reality.","esoteric":["The Triadic Force Matrix: She is the absolute consolidation of the three baseline functional energies that project the universe. As इच्छाशक्ति (Icchā-śakti), She provides the initial divine intent to create. As ज्ञानशक्ति (Jñāna-śakti), She maintains the intellectual blueprint of design. As क्रियाशक्ति (Kriyā-śakti), She executes the actual kinetic movement into dense material elements, proving Her status as the full dynamic expression of reality."]},{"number":659,"name":"सर्वाधारा","samasa":["अन्तर्यामित्वात् सर्वमाधारः यस्याः सा।","सर्वेषाम् आधारा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose","सर्वेषाम् — of all"],"summary":["सर्वाधारा means one who supports all. The three powers mentioned above are the support of everything happening in the world. She has all supports as Her form and is the underlying basis of the universe."],"searchText":"659 सर्वाधारा अन्तर्यामित्वात् सर्वमाधारः यस्याः सा। सर्वेषाम् आधारा। यस्याः — of whom; whose सर्वेषाम् — of all सर्वाधारा means one who supports all. the three powers mentioned above are the support of everything happening in the world. she has all supports as her form and is the underlying basis of the universe. the inner controller: she does not simply support things externally. as the omnipresent अन्तर्यामी (antaryāmī — inner controller), she permeates the inside and outside of every atom. the entire cosmos rests upon her fabric, drawing its space, existence, and stability directly from her baseline field.","esoteric":["The Inner Controller: She does not simply support things externally. As the omnipresent अन्तर्यामी (Antaryāmī — inner controller), She permeates the inside and outside of every atom. The entire cosmos rests upon Her fabric, drawing its space, existence, and stability directly from Her baseline field."]},{"number":660,"name":"सुप्रतिष्ठा","samasa":["जगतः शोभना प्रतिष्ठा अधिष्ठानम्।"],"wordByWord":["जगतः — of the world","प्रतिष्ठा — foundation; establishment"],"summary":["सुप्रतिष्ठा means one who is firmly and auspiciously established. She is established as the support of the universe and gives auspiciousness to all. Supratiṣṭhā is also a metrical name, and She is of that form as well."],"searchText":"660 सुप्रतिष्ठा जगतः शोभना प्रतिष्ठा अधिष्ठानम्। जगतः — of the world प्रतिष्ठा — foundation; establishment सुप्रतिष्ठा means one who is firmly and auspiciously established. she is established as the support of the universe and gives auspiciousness to all. supratiṣṭhā is also a metrical name, and she is of that form as well. the immutable substratum: material objects shift and collapse because they lack a permanent foundation. she is supratiṣṭhā because she is the perfectly established, unmoving, and absolute base (adhibhṭhāna) of the entire universe. she remains constant across all cosmic transitions, providing the secure anchor for existence.","esoteric":["The Immutable Substratum: Material objects shift and collapse because they lack a permanent foundation. She is Supratiṣṭhā because She is the perfectly established, unmoving, and absolute base (adhibhṭhāna) of the entire universe. She remains constant across all cosmic transitions, providing the secure anchor for existence."]},{"number":661,"name":"सदसद्रूपधारिणी","samasa":["सदसद्र्रूपे धारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सदसद्रूपधारिणी means one who assumes the form of being and non-being. Sat is the eternal Brahman; asat is the universe which appears and changes. From Her standpoint both are resolved in the one reality of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"661 सदसद्रूपधारिणी सदसद्र्रूपे धारयतीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सदसद्रूपधारिणी means one who assumes the form of being and non-being. sat is the eternal brahman; asat is the universe which appears and changes. from her standpoint both are resolved in the one reality of śrīdevī. the encompasser of reality and potential: सत् (sat) represents the visible, tangible, and currently manifested world of objects. असत् (asat) represents the hidden, unmanifested causal potentials. she is sadasadrūpadāriṇī because both conditions are waves of her own dynamic energy. she holds the visible universe and the dark unmanifested vacuum together in absolute synchronization.","esoteric":["The Encompasser of Reality and Potential: सत् (Sat) represents the visible, tangible, and currently manifested world of objects. असत् (Asat) represents the hidden, unmanifested causal potentials. She is Sadasadrūpadāriṇī because both conditions are waves of Her own dynamic energy. She holds the visible universe and the dark unmanifested vacuum together in absolute synchronization."]},{"number":662,"name":"अष्टमूर्तिः","samasa":["लक्ष्मीर्मेधा धरा पुष्टिर्गौरी तुष्टिः प्रभा धृतिः सरस्वती चेति अष्टौ मूर्तयो यस्याः सा।","जीवात्मा अन्तरात्मा परमात्मा निर्मलः शुद्धात्मा ज्ञानरूपात्मा महात्मा भूतात्मा चेति अष्टौ मूर्तयो यस्याः सा।","पञ्चमहाभूतानि सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ जीवात्मस्वर्गदीक्षितानामन्यतम एक इत्यष्टौ मूर्तयो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अष्टौ — eight","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["अष्टमूर्तिः means one who has eight forms. The eight forms are explained in many ways: eight mothers, eight Vāgdevatās, eight forms of Śiva, eight parts of nature and other traditional groups. Thus many octads are treated as Her own forms."],"searchText":"662 अष्टमूर्तिः लक्ष्मीर्मेधा धरा पुष्टिर्गौरी तुष्टिः प्रभा धृतिः सरस्वती चेति अष्टौ मूर्तयो यस्याः सा। जीवात्मा अन्तरात्मा परमात्मा निर्मलः शुद्धात्मा ज्ञानरूपात्मा महात्मा भूतात्मा चेति अष्टौ मूर्तयो यस्याः सा। पञ्चमहाभूतानि सूर्याचन्द्रमसौ जीवात्मस्वर्गदीक्षितानामन्यतम एक इत्यष्टौ मूर्तयो यस्याः सा। अष्टौ — eight यस्याः — of whom; whose अष्टमूर्तिः means one who has eight forms. the eight forms are explained in many ways: eight mothers, eight vāgdevatās, eight forms of śiva, eight parts of nature and other traditional groups. thus many octads are treated as her own forms. the eight divine attributes: she manifests as the eight corporate energies of well-being (lakṣmī, medhā, etc.). the eight strata of soul: she governs the eight layers of internal consciousness running from the individual soul (jīvātmā) up to the absolute paramātmā. the shiva-anatomy grid: she is identical with the aṣṭamūrti layout of lord śiva, where the body consists of the five base elements (earth, water, fire, air, space) along with the sun, the moon, and the conscious observer (jīva), proving her total immanence in nature.","esoteric":["The Eight Divine Attributes: She manifests as the eight corporate energies of well-being (Lakṣmī, Medhā, etc.).","The Eight Strata of Soul: She governs the eight layers of internal consciousness running from the individual soul (Jīvātmā) up to the absolute Paramātmā.","The Shiva-Anatomy Grid: She is identical with the Aṣṭamūrti layout of Lord Śiva, where the body consists of the five base elements (earth, water, fire, air, space) along with the Sun, the Moon, and the conscious observer (Jīva), proving Her total immanence in nature."]},{"number":663,"name":"अजाजैत्री","samasa":["अविद्यारूपायाः अजायाः जैत्री।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["अजाजैत्री means one who conquers ajā, meaning avidyā or ignorance. She is knowledge itself and enables devotees to conquer ignorance. The name therefore indicates the victory of wisdom over avidyā."],"searchText":"663 अजाजैत्री अविद्यारूपायाः अजायाः जैत्री। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. अजाजैत्री means one who conquers ajā, meaning avidyā or ignorance. she is knowledge itself and enables devotees to conquer ignorance. the name therefore indicates the victory of wisdom over avidyā. conquering the primordial veil: अजा (ajā) is a classical scriptural code for अविद्या (avidyā — primordial ignorance or cosmic illusion), which has no birth date and veils the true self. she is ajājaitrī because her supreme non-dual light forcefully conquers and dismantles this ancient illusion, dissolving the veil to reveal the pristine truth of brahman.","esoteric":["Conquering the Primordial Veil: अजा (Ajā) is a classical scriptural code for अविद्या (Avidyā — primordial ignorance or cosmic illusion), which has no birth date and veils the true Self. She is Ajājaitrī because Her supreme non-dual light forcefully conquers and dismantles this ancient illusion, dissolving the veil to reveal the pristine truth of Brahman."]},{"number":664,"name":"लोकयात्राविधायिनी","samasa":["लोकानां चतुर्दशसङ्ख्यानां यात्रां (प्रलयं संरक्षणं वा) विधातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["लोकानां — of worlds","यात्रां — course; movement"],"summary":["लोकयात्राविधायिनी means one who directs the continuous course of the worlds. The world is constantly arising, continuing and ending in countless individual forms. She has the power to regulate this cyclic travel of the universe."],"searchText":"664 लोकयात्राविधायिनी लोकानां चतुर्दशसङ्ख्यानां यात्रां (प्रलयं संरक्षणं वा) विधातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति। लोकानां — of worlds यात्रां — course; movement लोकयात्राविधायिनी means one who directs the continuous course of the worlds. the world is constantly arising, continuing and ending in countless individual forms. she has the power to regulate this cyclic travel of the universe. the conductor of the cosmic journey: लोकयात्रा refers to the continuous operational journey, evolutionary progression, and historical transitions of the fourteen structural realms of creation. she acts as the master director who organizes these cycles, ensuring that the laws of karma, natural physics, and spiritual preservation run smoothly across all planes.","esoteric":["The Conductor of the Cosmic Journey: लोकयात्रा refers to the continuous operational journey, evolutionary progression, and historical transitions of the fourteen structural realms of creation. She acts as the master director who organizes these cycles, ensuring that the laws of karma, natural physics, and spiritual preservation run smoothly across all planes."]},{"number":665,"name":"एकाकिनी","samasa":["द्वितीयराहित्यात् एका (५.३.५२ एकादाकिनिच्चासहाये)।"],"wordByWord":["द्वितीयराहित्यात् — because of absence of a second","एका — one; alone"],"summary":["एकाकिनी means one who is alone. She has no second and needs no support. The name Kevalā may be compared. The Upaniṣadic teaching 'ekam eva advitīyam' is recalled: She alone is the non-dual truth."],"searchText":"665 एकाकिनी द्वितीयराहित्यात् एका (५.३.५२ एकादाकिनिच्चासहाये)। द्वितीयराहित्यात् — because of absence of a second एका — one; alone एकाकिनी means one who is alone. she has no second and needs no support. the name kevalā may be compared. the upaniṣadic teaching 'ekam eva advitīyam' is recalled: she alone is the non-dual truth. the matchless absolute: she is ekākinī because she stands entirely alone in her ultimate essential nature, completely devoid of any second entity (dvitīya-rāhitā). before creation and after dissolution, she shines as the singular, non-dual baseline awareness. there are no neighbors, no rivals, and no companions competing with her absolute status.","esoteric":["The Matchless Absolute: She is Ekākinī because She stands entirely alone in Her ultimate essential nature, completely devoid of any second entity (dvitīya-rāhitā). Before creation and after dissolution, She shines as the singular, non-dual baseline awareness. There are no neighbors, no rivals, and no companions competing with Her absolute status."]},{"number":666,"name":"भूमरूपा","samasa":["ब्रह्मरूपा।","एकाकिनी अपि बहुरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["एकाकिनी — alone","अपि — also; even"],"summary":["भूमरूपा means one who is the aggregate of all existing things. The word Bhūmā means Brahman. She is in the form of Brahman. Bhūmā also means the many; though She was described as one in the previous name, here She is described as many. What is seen as one Brahman in the supreme state appears as many in the nature of this universe. Many forms of Śrīdevī are described in the Devī Purāṇa."],"searchText":"666 भूमरूपा ब्रह्मरूपा। एकाकिनी अपि बहुरूपा। एकाकिनी — alone अपि — also; even भूमरूपा means one who is the aggregate of all existing things. the word bhūmā means brahman. she is in the form of brahman. bhūmā also means the many; though she was described as one in the previous name, here she is described as many. what is seen as one brahman in the supreme state appears as many in the nature of this universe. many forms of śrīdevī are described in the devī purāṇa. the infinite vastness: यो वै भूमा तत्सुखं नाल्पे सुखमस्ति (\"the infinite vastness alone is bliss; there is no joy in the finite\"). she is that bhūmā — the shoreless, unconditioned, and all-encompassìng absolute reality. though she is completely alone (ekākinī), her infinite vastness encompasses every single form in existence.","esoteric":["The Infinite Vastness: यो वै भूमा तत्सुखं नाल्पे सुखमस्ति (\"The infinite vastness alone is bliss; there is no joy in the finite\"). She is that Bhūmā — the shoreless, unconditioned, and all-encompassìng absolute reality. though She is completely alone (Ekākinī), Her infinite vastness encompasses every single form in existence."]},{"number":667,"name":"निर्द्वैता","samasa":["निर्गतं द्वैतं यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["निर्द्वैता means one who is non-dual, without duality. Dvaita is the feeling that another exists in addition to the Self. She does not have such duality. When the soul is thought of as different from the Supreme Being, that is duality. When this is gone, only Brahman indicated by Ekākinī and Kevalā remains; such is Śrīdevī, or She endows that state."],"searchText":"667 निर्द्वैता निर्गतं द्वैतं यस्यां सा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. निर्द्वैता means one who is non-dual, without duality. dvaita is the feeling that another exists in addition to the self. she does not have such duality. when the soul is thought of as different from the supreme being, that is duality. when this is gone, only brahman indicated by ekākinī and kevalā remains; such is śrīdevī, or she endows that state. the non-dual screen: duality (dvaita) is the root cause of confusion, fear, and moral judgment. she is nirdvaitā because her essential nature contains no internal cleavages, no splits, and no subject-object distinctions. she is the unified screen upon which the appearance of duality is projected, remaining unblemished.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Screen: Duality (dvaita) is the root cause of confusion, fear, and moral judgment. She is Nirdvaitā because Her essential nature contains no internal cleavages, no splits, and no subject-object distinctions. She is the unified screen upon which the appearance of duality is projected, remaining unblemished."]},{"number":668,"name":"द्वैतवर्जिता","samasa":["द्वैतेन वर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["द्वैतेन — by duality"],"summary":["द्वैतवर्जिता means one who is free from the state of duality. This name stresses more clearly the message of the previous name. The state of duality is unreal. At no point of time is there anything other than Śrīdevī, who is the form of Brahman."],"searchText":"668 द्वैतवर्जिता द्वैतेन वर्जिता। द्वैतेन — by duality द्वैतवर्जिता means one who is free from the state of duality. this name stresses more clearly the message of the previous name. the state of duality is unreal. at no point of time is there anything other than śrīdevī, who is the form of brahman. exclusion of separation: by placing nirdvaitā and dvaitavarjitā side-by-side, the text eliminates any misconception that duality has a real, independent foothold in reality. she thoroughly rejects and stands free from the boundaries of separation, anchoring the practitioner firmly in non-dual absorption.","esoteric":["Exclusion of Separation: By placing Nirdvaitā and Dvaitavarjitā side-by-side, the text eliminates any misconception that duality has a real, independent foothold in reality. She thoroughly rejects and stands free from the boundaries of separation, anchoring the practitioner firmly in non-dual absorption."]},{"number":669,"name":"अन्नदा","samasa":["अन्नं ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["अन्नदा means one who gives food to the entire universe. As the Mother of the universe, She protects the universe by giving food. In this function She is Annapūrṇā, holding a vessel full of food and a ladle. Before taking food, if one prays to Her and thinks that Śrīdevī alone has given the food, the blemish of food will not affect one and strength, knowledge and zeal will be gained."],"searchText":"669 अन्नदा अन्नं ददातीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. अन्नदा means one who gives food to the entire universe. as the mother of the universe, she protects the universe by giving food. in this function she is annapūrṇā, holding a vessel full of food and a ladle. before taking food, if one prays to her and thinks that śrīdevī alone has given the food, the blemish of food will not affect one and strength, knowledge and zeal will be gained. the giver of nourishment: she is the cosmic mother who provides the physical food (anna) needed to maintain the biological frameworks of all living beings. अन्न represents that which is consumed and that which consumes. she is the material fuel that feeds the physical sheet (annamaya-kośa), keeping life viable so that spiritual growth can occur.","esoteric":["The Giver of Nourishment: She is the cosmic mother who provides the physical food (Anna) needed to maintain the biological frameworks of all living beings. अन्न represents that which is consumed and that which consumes. She is the material fuel that feeds the physical sheet (Annamaya-kośa), keeping life viable so that spiritual growth can occur."]},{"number":670,"name":"वसुदा","samasa":["वसु धनं रत्नं च ददातीति।"],"wordByWord":["वसु — wealth; treasure"],"summary":["वसुदा means one who gives wealth to all. Vasu has many meanings, such as wealth, gem and gold; She gives all these. The essence of this name is the feeling that all enjoyable wealth obtained in this world is due only to Her blessings. The Veda also speaks of annam and vasu in this connection."],"searchText":"670 वसुदा वसु धनं रत्नं च ददातीति। वसु — wealth; treasure वसुदा means one who gives wealth to all. vasu has many meanings, such as wealth, gem and gold; she gives all these. the essence of this name is the feeling that all enjoyable wealth obtained in this world is due only to her blessings. the veda also speaks of annam and vasu in this connection. the dispenser of riches: वसु (vasu) refers to gold, physical wealth, and precious gems. she dispenses these assets to maintain societal balance. the ray matrix: alternatively, vasu signifies the vital light rays projected by the sun and the specific group of foundational atmospheric deities (vasus). she gives this light energy to sustain planetary vitality.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of Riches: वसु (Vasu) refers to gold, physical wealth, and precious gems. She dispenses these assets to maintain societal balance.","The Ray Matrix: Alternatively, Vasu signifies the vital light rays projected by the sun and the specific group of foundational atmospheric deities (Vasus). She gives this light energy to sustain planetary vitality."]},{"number":671,"name":"वृद्धा","samasa":["सर्वज्येष्ठत्वात्।","वर्धयति जगत् इति।"],"wordByWord":["वर्धयति — nourishes; increases","जगत् — world"],"summary":["वृद्धा means one who is senior in age. Since She exists before everything else, She is the most ancient and the oldest. She may also be understood as the completely grown and matured world, or as one who nourishes the world."],"searchText":"671 वृद्धा सर्वज्येष्ठत्वात्। वर्धयति जगत् इति। वर्धयति — nourishes; increases जगत् — world वृद्धा means one who is senior in age. since she exists before everything else, she is the most ancient and the oldest. she may also be understood as the completely grown and matured world, or as one who nourishes the world. the primordial eldest: she is vṛddhā because she possesses absolute temporal priority over everything (सर्वज्येष्ठत्वात्). she exists before the oldest ancestors, the first elements, and the creator deities. concurrently, the root signifies her active role in causing the expansion and growth (vardhayati) of the universe from its seed state.","esoteric":["The Primordial Eldest: She is Vṛddhā because She possesses absolute temporal priority over everything (सर्वज्येष्ठत्वात्). She exists before the oldest ancestors, the first elements, and the creator deities. Concurrently, the root signifies Her active role in causing the expansion and growth (vardhayati) of the universe from its seed state."]},{"number":672,"name":"ब्रह्मात्मैक्यस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["ब्रह्मणा चैतन्येन सह आत्मनां जीवानामैक्यमेव स्वं निजं रूपमास्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["ब्रह्मणा — with Brahman","चैतन्येन — with consciousness"],"summary":["ब्रह्मात्मैक्यस्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the unity of Brahman and Ātman. Mahāvākyas such as Aham Brahmāsmi and mantras like Soham indicate that Brahman is to be realised in the breath of every soul. That is the real form of Śrīdevī. The Haṃsa mantra unites the soul with Śiva. The natural breath itself becomes ajapa mantra, and this meaning is also described in the Triśatī name Haṃsamantrārtha-rūpiṇī."],"searchText":"672 ब्रह्मात्मैक्यस्वरूपिणी ब्रह्मणा चैतन्येन सह आत्मनां जीवानामैक्यमेव स्वं निजं रूपमास्याः अस्तीति। ब्रह्मणा — with brahman चैतन्येन — with consciousness ब्रह्मात्मैक्यस्वरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the unity of brahman and ātman. mahāvākyas such as aham brahmāsmi and mantras like soham indicate that brahman is to be realised in the breath of every soul. that is the real form of śrīdevī. the haṃsa mantra unites the soul with śiva. the natural breath itself becomes ajapa mantra, and this meaning is also described in the triśatī name haṃsamantrārtha-rūpiṇī. the formula of liberation: this name states the ultimate core truth of advaita vedānta and high-tier śrīvidyā. she is not an external ruler to be feared; she is the very realization of the absolute identity (aikya) between the seeker's core identity (ātman) and the universal absolute (brahman). she is the experience of that non-dual bridge, vanishing the illusion of separation forever.","esoteric":["The Formula of Liberation: This name states the ultimate core truth of Advaita Vedānta and high-tier Śrīvidyā. She is not an external ruler to be feared; She is the very realization of the absolute identity (aikya) between the seeker's core identity (Ātman) and the universal absolute (Brahman). She is the experience of that non-dual bridge, vanishing the illusion of separation forever."]},{"number":673,"name":"बृहती","samasa":["महतो महीयत्वाद्बृहती।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["बृहती means one whose form is immensely great. Mahato Mahīyān — greater than the greatest. Bṛhat-sāman occurs in the Sāma Veda, and a metre of thirty-six letters is called Bṛhatī. She is in those forms also."],"searchText":"673 बृहती महतो महीयत्वाद्बृहती। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. बृहती means one whose form is immensely great. mahato mahīyān — greater than the greatest. bṛhat-sāman occurs in the sāma veda, and a metre of thirty-six letters is called bṛhatī. she is in those forms also. the boundless expansion: she is bṛhatī because her scale surpasses the highest imaginable metric of greatness (महतो महीयत्वात्). she cannot be contained by any boundary line, expanding infinitely beyond cosmic horizons, serving as the vast space within which multiverses float.","esoteric":["The Boundless Expansion: She is Bṛhatī because Her scale surpasses the highest imaginable metric of greatness (महतो महीयत्वात्). She cannot be contained by any boundary line, expanding infinitely beyond cosmic horizons, serving as the vast space within which multiverses float."]},{"number":674,"name":"ब्राह्मणी","samasa":["द्विजस्त्रीमात्ररूपा।","संविद्विशेषरूपा।","शिवस्य ब्राह्मणत्वजातिमत्त्वाद्ब्राह्मणी।"],"wordByWord":["शिवस्य — of Śiva"],"summary":["ब्राह्मणी means one who is in the form of a Brāhmin lady. The word Brāhmaṇī has several meanings, including a Brāhmin lady, a plant and wisdom. She is of all these forms. Since Śiva, Her consort, is spoken of as Brāhmaṇa and the deity of Brāhmaṇas, She is Brāhmaṇī."],"searchText":"674 ब्राह्मणी द्विजस्त्रीमात्ररूपा। संविद्विशेषरूपा। शिवस्य ब्राह्मणत्वजातिमत्त्वाद्ब्राह्मणी। शिवस्य — of śiva ब्राह्मणी means one who is in the form of a brāhmin lady. the word brāhmaṇī has several meanings, including a brāhmin lady, a plant and wisdom. she is of all these forms. since śiva, her consort, is spoken of as brāhmaṇa and the deity of brāhmaṇas, she is brāhmaṇī. the consort of the knower: lord śiva represents the ultimate, pristine repository of vedic wisdom—the archetypal brahman. she is his non-dual dynamic energy (brāhmaṇī). concurrently, she represents the refined, highly specialized state of pure internal awareness (saṁvit-viśeṣa-rūpā) that marks an illumined mind.","esoteric":["The Consort of the Knower: Lord Śiva represents the ultimate, pristine repository of Vedic wisdom—the archetypal Brahman. She is His non-dual dynamic energy (Brāhmaṇī). Concurrently, She represents the refined, highly specialized state of pure internal awareness (Saṁvit-viśeṣa-rūpā) that marks an illumined mind."]},{"number":675,"name":"ब्राह्मी","samasa":["अविद्यातिरिक्तजडजातिसद्भावे मानाभाव इत्यत आह ब्राह्मी। (ब्राह्मो जाताविति निपातनात्साधुः)।","वागात्मिका।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["ब्राह्मी means one who is in the form of Sarasvatī, the consort of Brahmā. She is in the form of speech and may be understood as Vāgīśvarī. She is also the senior-most among the eight mothers, shining with the swan, japa-mālā and kamaṇḍalu."],"searchText":"675 ब्राह्मी अविद्यातिरिक्तजडजातिसद्भावे मानाभाव इत्यत आह ब्राह्मी। (ब्राह्मो जाताविति निपातनात्साधुः)। वागात्मिका। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. ब्राह्मी means one who is in the form of sarasvatī, the consort of brahmā. she is in the form of speech and may be understood as vāgīśvarī. she is also the senior-most among the eight mothers, shining with the swan, japa-mālā and kamaṇḍalu. the non-dual substance: because there is no valid proof (mānābhāva) for the existence of any independent material matter separate from the absolute, the entire universe is fundamentally nothing but brahman. she is brāhmī — the expression of this non-dual reality. concurrently, she is the power of articulation (vāg-ātmikā) that animates creative sound.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Substance: Because there is no valid proof (mānābhāva) for the existence of any independent material matter separate from the absolute, the entire universe is fundamentally nothing but Brahman. She is Brāhmī — the expression of this non-dual reality. Concurrently, She is the power of articulation (Vāg-ātmikā) that animates creative sound."]},{"number":676,"name":"ब्रह्मानन्दा","samasa":["ब्रह्मैवानन्दो यस्याः सगुणायाः।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["ब्रह्मानन्दा means one who is in the form of supreme bliss. She has Brahman itself as Her bliss. The form of Śrīdevī is described as frozen or condensed bliss, just as Śrī Kṛṣṇa is described as one whose body is supreme bliss."],"searchText":"676 ब्रह्मानन्दा ब्रह्मैवानन्दो यस्याः सगुणायाः। यस्याः — of whom; whose ब्रह्मानन्दा means one who is in the form of supreme bliss. she has brahman itself as her bliss. the form of śrīdevī is described as frozen or condensed bliss, just as śrī kṛṣṇa is described as one whose body is supreme bliss. the bliss of the absolute: she is the living embodiment of that supreme, unconditioned happiness (ānanda) that defines brahman. when she assumes a qualified form (saguṇā) for the sake of the devotee, she radiates this unadulterated cosmic joy, lifting the practitioner out of earthly grief.","esoteric":["The Bliss of the Absolute: She is the living embodiment of that supreme, unconditioned happiness (Ānanda) that defines Brahman. When She assumes a qualified form (Saguṇā) for the sake of the devotee, She radiates this unadulterated cosmic joy, lifting the practitioner out of earthly grief."]},{"number":677,"name":"बलिप्रिया","samasa":["बलिनो विद्यानिराससमर्थाः कामादिशत्रुजेतारः प्रिया दयापात्रं यस्याः सा।","बलिनामको राजा प्रियो यस्य वामनस्य तदभिन्ना।","पूजोपहाराः प्रिया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विद्यानिराससमर्थाः — able to remove ignorance","प्रिया — dear","यस्याः — of whom; whose","पूजोपहाराः — worship offerings"],"summary":["बलिप्रिया means one who is delighted with the mighty. Dhīras or balis are those who overcome ignorance and the enemies such as desire. She is fond of them and blesses them. The name also recalls Viṣṇu's compassion for king Bali in the Vāmana incarnation, and also the bali offerings made during worship, which She accepts with joy."],"searchText":"677 बलिप्रिया बलिनो विद्यानिराससमर्थाः कामादिशत्रुजेतारः प्रिया दयापात्रं यस्याः सा। बलिनामको राजा प्रियो यस्य वामनस्य तदभिन्ना। पूजोपहाराः प्रिया यस्याः सा। विद्यानिराससमर्थाः — able to remove ignorance प्रिया — dear यस्याः — of whom; whose पूजोपहाराः — worship offerings बलिप्रिया means one who is delighted with the mighty. dhīras or balis are those who overcome ignorance and the enemies such as desire. she is fond of them and blesses them. the name also recalls viṣṇu's compassion for king bali in the vāmana incarnation, and also the bali offerings made during worship, which she accepts with joy. the love for spiritual warriors: बली refers to those strong, heroic practitioners who have conquered their internal enemies—lust, anger, and greed (kāmādi-śatru-jetāraḥ). they are her favorite children. ritual and mythological mappings: she accepts pure ritual offerings (upahāra) surrendered with devotion, and is non-different from the pervasive viṣṇu form that blessed king bali.","esoteric":["The Love for Spiritual Warriors: बली refers to those strong, heroic practitioners who have conquered their internal enemies—lust, anger, and greed (kāmādi-śatru-jetāraḥ). They are Her favorite children.","Ritual and Mythological Mappings: She accepts pure ritual offerings (upahāra) surrendered with devotion, and is non-different from the pervasive Viṣṇu form that blessed King Bali."]},{"number":678,"name":"भाषारूपा","samasa":["संस्कृतप्राकृतादिभाषा रूपं यस्याः सा।","भाषाभिर्निरूप्यत इति।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["भाषारूपा means one who is the form of languages. Since She is the head of speech, all languages are Her form. Her form is identified through languages; She can be recognised by speech."],"searchText":"678 भाषारूपा संस्कृतप्राकृतादिभाषा रूपं यस्याः सा। भाषाभिर्निरूप्यत इति। यस्याः — of whom; whose भाषारूपा means one who is the form of languages. since she is the head of speech, all languages are her form. her form is identified through languages; she can be recognised by speech. the matrix of articulation: she manifests directly as the structural architecture of language—including classical sanskrit, natural prākṛt, and every linguistic dialect spoken across the planetary grid. every word uttered is her voice. concurrently, she is the ultimate reality targeted and defined (nirūpyate) by all sacred philosophical descriptions.","esoteric":["The Matrix of Articulation: She manifests directly as the structural architecture of language—including classical Sanskrit, natural Prākṛt, and every linguistic dialect spoken across the planetary grid. Every word uttered is Her voice. Concurrently, She is the ultimate reality targeted and defined (nirūpyate) by all sacred philosophical descriptions."]},{"number":679,"name":"बृहत्सेना","samasa":["बृहती अपारा सेना चतुरङ्गबलं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["बृहती — great; vast","अपारा — boundless","सेना — army","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["बृहत्सेना means one who has a mighty army. Though She can perform creation, protection and destruction by Herself, She creates a vast army and completes Her tasks through it, giving share and pride to those who serve. Bṛhatsenā is also the name of a certain kingly line; She is in that form too."],"searchText":"679 बृहत्सेना बृहती अपारा सेना चतुरङ्गबलं यस्याः सा। बृहती — great; vast अपारा — boundless सेना — army यस्याः — of whom; whose बृहत्सेना means one who has a mighty army. though she can perform creation, protection and destruction by herself, she creates a vast army and completes her tasks through it, giving share and pride to those who serve. bṛhatsenā is also the name of a certain kingly line; she is in that form too. the boundless army of light: her \"army\" (senā) represents the infinite arrays of protective guardian energies, śaktis, and defensive rays that surround her throne. this boundless force stands perpetually mobilized to defend cosmic order and protect the practitioner from internal negative invasions.","esoteric":["The Boundless Army of Light: Her \"army\" (Senā) represents the infinite arrays of protective guardian energies, Śaktis, and defensive rays that surround Her throne. This boundless force stands perpetually mobilized to defend cosmic order and protect the practitioner from internal negative invasions."]},{"number":680,"name":"भावाभावविवर्जिता","samasa":["भावा द्रव्यगुणादयोऽभावाः प्रागभावादयस्तैरुभयैरपि विवर्जिता।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["भावाभावविवर्जिता means one who is beyond existence and non-existence. Bhāva means existence and abhāva means non-existence. Everything in the world passes between these states. Śrīdevī does not belong completely to either state; the Supreme Being is eternal."],"searchText":"680 भावाभावविवर्जिता भावा द्रव्यगुणादयोऽभावाः प्रागभावादयस्तैरुभयैरपि विवर्जिता। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. भावाभावविवर्जिता means one who is beyond existence and non-existence. bhāva means existence and abhāva means non-existence. everything in the world passes between these states. śrīdevī does not belong completely to either state; the supreme being is eternal. beyond conceptual dialectics: in logical systems (nyāya/vaiśeṣika), the universe is divided into positive categories of being (bhāva — substance, quality, action) and states of negation (abhāva — prior non-existence, destruction). as the absolute transcendent consciousness, she stands completely outside this binary dualism. she is the baseline screen that precedes logical divisions,","esoteric":["Beyond Conceptual Dialectics: In logical systems (Nyāya/Vaiśeṣika), the universe is divided into positive categories of being (bhāva — substance, quality, action) and states of negation (abhāva — prior non-existence, destruction). As the absolute transcendent consciousness, She stands completely outside this binary dualism. She is the baseline screen that precedes logical divisions,"]},{"number":681,"name":"सुखाराध्या","samasa":["सुखेन (उपवासादिरूपकायक्लेशं ध्येयस्वरूपनियमनिर्बन्धादिकं चान्तरेण) आराध्या ।"],"wordByWord":["सुखेन — comfortably","आराध्या — worshipped"],"summary":["सुखाराध्या means one who can be worshipped comfortably, without much effort. She can be worshipped without bodily pain such as fasting and without harsh restrictions on meditation. To worship Her, it is enough to imagine any form in the mind as Śrīdevī with devotion. Thus Her worship is very easy."],"searchText":"681 सुखाराध्या सुखेन (उपवासादिरूपकायक्लेशं ध्येयस्वरूपनियमनिर्बन्धादिकं चान्तरेण) आराध्या । सुखेन — comfortably आराध्या — worshipped सुखाराध्या means one who can be worshipped comfortably, without much effort. she can be worshipped without bodily pain such as fasting and without harsh restrictions on meditation. to worship her, it is enough to imagine any form in the mind as śrīdevī with devotion. thus her worship is very easy. worship free from physical friction: she does not require harsh physical mortification, extreme fasting (upavāsa), or torturous bodily postures (kāya-kleśa). she is sukhārādhyā because she can be worshipped with ease (sukhena), yielding her presence to sincere internal devotion and simple love rather than complex mechanical constraints.","esoteric":["Worship Free from Physical Friction: She does not require harsh physical mortification, extreme fasting (upavāsa), or torturous bodily postures (kāya-kleśa). She is Sukhārādhyā because She can be worshipped with ease (sukhena), yielding Her presence to sincere internal devotion and simple love rather than complex mechanical constraints."]},{"number":682,"name":"शुभकरी","samasa":["शुभं पुण्यमेव करोति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["शुभकरी means one who grants auspiciousness to Her devotees. After saying that She can be worshipped easily, this name removes the doubt that lack of fasting or strict observance may cause sin. She bestows auspiciousness on Her devotees."],"searchText":"682 शुभकरी शुभं पुण्यमेव करोति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. शुभकरी means one who grants auspiciousness to her devotees. after saying that she can be worshipped easily, this name removes the doubt that lack of fasting or strict observance may cause sin. she bestows auspiciousness on her devotees. the engine of auspiciousness: she is śubhakarī because her continuous influence automatically transforms the seeker's mental environment, producing auspicious thoughts, moral purity (puṇya), and benign outer circumstances that support spiritual growth.","esoteric":["The Engine of Auspiciousness: She is Śubhakarī because Her continuous influence automatically transforms the seeker's mental environment, producing auspicious thoughts, moral purity (puṇya), and benign outer circumstances that support spiritual growth."]},{"number":683,"name":"शोभनासुलभागतिः","samasa":["मोक्षादिपुरुषार्थरूपत्वाच्छोभना। गम्यत इति गतिः फलम्। सुखोपास्यत्वात्सुलभा च गतिः प्राप्तव्यं स्थानम्।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["शोभनासुलभागतिः means one whose path is beautiful and easy to attain. Gati means goal, path, destiny, knowledge or salvation. Śobhanā means auspicious and sulabhā means easily attainable. The name indicates that even the difficult-to-attain freedom from rebirth becomes attainable by Her grace."],"searchText":"683 शोभनासुलभागतिः मोक्षादिपुरुषार्थरूपत्वाच्छोभना। गम्यत इति गतिः फलम्। सुखोपास्यत्वात्सुलभा च गतिः प्राप्तव्यं स्थानम्। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. शोभनासुलभागतिः means one whose path is beautiful and easy to attain. gati means goal, path, destiny, knowledge or salvation. śobhanā means auspicious and sulabhā means easily attainable. the name indicates that even the difficult-to-attain freedom from rebirth becomes attainable by her grace. the magnificent goal: her station (gati) represents the highest human aim (puruṣārtha)—liberation itself, making it शोभना (śobhanā — glorious). yet, because her path is grounded in grace rather than friction, this ultimate state remains सुलभा (sulabhā — easily reachable) for those who take refuge in her.","esoteric":["The Magnificent Goal: Her station (gati) represents the highest human aim (puruṣārtha)—liberation itself, making it शोभना (śobhanā — glorious). Yet, because Her path is grounded in grace rather than friction, this ultimate state remains सुलभा (sulabhā — easily reachable) for those who take refuge in Her."]},{"number":684,"name":"राजराजेश्वरी","samasa":["राज्ञां देवराजादीनां ये राजानो ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्रास्तेषामपीश्वरी।","राजराजस्य कुबेरस्येश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["राजराजेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the king of kings. She is the head of the rulers of the eight directions and also of Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Śiva. Kubera is also called Rājarāja; She is the ruler even of him."],"searchText":"684 राजराजेश्वरी राज्ञां देवराजादीनां ये राजानो ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्रास्तेषामपीश्वरी। राजराजस्य कुबेरस्येश्वरी। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. राजराजेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the king of kings. she is the head of the rulers of the eight directions and also of brahmā, viṣṇu and śiva. kubera is also called rājarāja; she is the ruler even of him. sovereign over the trinity: secondary gods like indra rule the heavens, but their rulers are the primary trinity—brahmā, viṣṇu, and rudra. she is rājarājeśvarī because she sits as the supreme empress over this trinity itself. concurrently, she governs kubera (rājarāja), holding total command over all cosmic treasuries.","esoteric":["Sovereign over the Trinity: Secondary gods like Indra rule the heavens, but their rulers are the primary trinity—Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and Rudra. She is Rājarājeśvarī because She sits as the supreme empress over this trinity itself. Concurrently, She governs Kubera (Rājarāja), holding total command over all cosmic treasuries."]},{"number":685,"name":"राज्यदायिनी","samasa":["राज्यं स्वाराज्यवैकुण्ठकैलासाधिपत्यादिकं दातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["राज्यदायिनी means one who bestows dominion. Rājya indicates liberation, Vaikuṇṭha or Kailāsa; She grants these. The posts and roles of the directional lords and other rulers are also given by Her. Rājya is described in several forms such as vairājya, bhaujya and sāmrājya."],"searchText":"685 राज्यदायिनी राज्यं स्वाराज्यवैकुण्ठकैलासाधिपत्यादिकं दातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. राज्यदायिनी means one who bestows dominion. rājya indicates liberation, vaikuṇṭha or kailāsa; she grants these. the posts and roles of the directional lords and other rulers are also given by her. rājya is described in several forms such as vairājya, bhaujya and sāmrājya. the dispenser of heavenly realms: she does not merely grant temporal earthly kingdoms. she is rājyadāyinī because she dispenses spiritual sovereignty—including absolute self-rule (svārājya), access to the celestial realms of viṣṇu (vaikuṇṭha) and śiva (kailāsa), and ultimate dominion over one's internal senses.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of Heavenly Realms: She does not merely grant temporal earthly kingdoms. She is Rājyadāyinī because She dispenses spiritual sovereignty—including absolute self-rule (svārājya), access to the celestial realms of Viṣṇu (Vaikuṇṭha) and Śiva (Kailāsa), and ultimate dominion over one's internal senses."]},{"number":686,"name":"राज्यवल्लभा","samasa":["राज्यानि वल्लभानि प्रियाणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वल्लभानि — dear; beloved","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["राज्यवल्लभा means one to whom dominions are dear. The previous name indicates kingdoms and their rulers such as Brahmā, Indra and others. Śrīdevī has affection for all such kings. It is said in Āryā Dviśatī that such kings wait in Śrīpura for the sight of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"686 राज्यवल्लभा राज्यानि वल्लभानि प्रियाणि यस्याः सा। वल्लभानि — dear; beloved यस्याः — of whom; whose राज्यवल्लभा means one to whom dominions are dear. the previous name indicates kingdoms and their rulers such as brahmā, indra and others. śrīdevī has affection for all such kings. it is said in āryā dviśatī that such kings wait in śrīpura for the sight of śrīdevī. the guardian of sovereign order: she is rājyavallabhā because she delights in righteous governance, order, and the expanding sovereignty of her devotees. she protects organized, righteous realms (rājya) so that wisdom and dharma can flourish without chaotic disruption.","esoteric":["The Guardian of Sovereign Order: She is Rājyavallabhā because She delights in righteous governance, order, and the expanding sovereignty of Her devotees. She protects organized, righteous realms (rājya) so that wisdom and Dharma can flourish without chaotic disruption."]},{"number":687,"name":"राजत्कृपा","samasa":["राजन्ती शोभमाना कृपा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["राजन्ती — shining","कृपा — compassion","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["राजत्कृपा means one whose compassion shines gloriously. Since She is the form of a mother, She is full of compassion. Her grace shines and protects the devotees."],"searchText":"687 राजत्कृपा राजन्ती शोभमाना कृपा यस्याः सा। राजन्ती — shining कृपा — compassion यस्याः — of whom; whose राजत्कृपा means one whose compassion shines gloriously. since she is the form of a mother, she is full of compassion. her grace shines and protects the devotees. the radiant grace: her compassion (kṛpā) is not a hidden or passive sentiment; it is राजन्ती (rājantī — splendidly active and luminous). it shines out continuously to illuminate dark places in the seeker's mind, dispelling fear and granting immediate protection.","esoteric":["The Radiant Grace: Her compassion (kṛpā) is not a hidden or passive sentiment; it is राजन्ती (rājantī — splendidly active and luminous). It shines out continuously to illuminate dark places in the seeker's mind, dispelling fear and granting immediate protection."]},{"number":688,"name":"राजपीठनिवेशितनिजाश्रिता","samasa":["राज्ञां नृपाणामिन्द्रादीनां च पीठेषु सिंहासनेषु निवेशिता निजा आश्रिता यया सा  ।"],"wordByWord":["सिंहासनेषु — on thrones","आश्रिता — those who have taken refuge","सा — she"],"summary":["राजपीठनिवेशितनिजाश्रिता means one who raises those who resort to Her to royal status. She gives the posts of Indra and others to Her devotees; examples are known from stories such as Dhruva and Suratha. True devotees do not accept even such posts as final; She grants them the still higher state of Brahman."],"searchText":"688 राजपीठनिवेशितनिजाश्रिता राज्ञां नृपाणामिन्द्रादीनां च पीठेषु सिंहासनेषु निवेशिता निजा आश्रिता यया सा  । सिंहासनेषु — on thrones आश्रिता — those who have taken refuge सा — she राजपीठनिवेशितनिजाश्रिता means one who raises those who resort to her to royal status. she gives the posts of indra and others to her devotees; examples are known from stories such as dhruva and suratha. true devotees do not accept even such posts as final; she grants them the still higher state of brahman. the elevating power of grace: she takes those who seek refuge in her (nijāśritā) and installs them upon the thrones (rājapīṭha) of worldly governance, heavenly positions (like indra's seat), or spiritual mastery. her refuge transforms the spiritually destitute into sovereign masters over life.","esoteric":["The Elevating Power of Grace: She takes those who seek refuge in Her (nijāśritā) and installs them upon the thrones (rājapīṭha) of worldly governance, heavenly positions (like Indra's seat), or spiritual mastery. Her refuge transforms the spiritually destitute into sovereign masters over life."]},{"number":689,"name":"राज्यलक्ष्मीः","samasa":["राज्याभिमानिनी लक्ष्मी।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["राज्यलक्ष्मीः means one who is the goddess of sovereignty. Rājyalakṣmī indicates the entire wealth of all kings and devas such as Indra. She is that form, and the mantra of Rājyalakṣmī is described in Tantrarāja."],"searchText":"689 राज्यलक्ष्मीः राज्याभिमानिनी लक्ष्मी। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. राज्यलक्ष्मीः means one who is the goddess of sovereignty. rājyalakṣmī indicates the entire wealth of all kings and devas such as indra. she is that form, and the mantra of rājyalakṣmī is described in tantrarāja. the splendor of rulership: power without grace leads to destruction. she is rājyalakṣmīḥ because she is the living fortune, majesty, and dignity (lakṣmī) that animates a kingdom. when her presence leaves a reign, its wealth and stability crumble; when she resides within it, prosperity flourishes.","esoteric":["The Splendor of Rulership: Power without grace leads to destruction. She is Rājyalakṣmīḥ because She is the living fortune, majesty, and dignity (lakṣmī) that animates a kingdom. When Her presence leaves a reign, its wealth and stability crumble; when She resides within it, prosperity flourishes."]},{"number":690,"name":"कोशनाथा","samasa":["कोशस्य भाण्डागारस्य दिव्यस्य अन्नमयादेर्वा नाथा स्वामिनी।"],"wordByWord":["कोशस्य — of treasury or sheath","भाण्डागारस्य — of the treasury","नाथा — mistress; lord"],"summary":["कोशनाथा means one who presides over treasure. Kośa means a treasury; She is the head of all wealth. Kośa also refers to the five sheaths of the body — annamaya, prāṇamaya, manomaya, vijñānamaya and ānandamaya. As their head, She blesses devotees with life, thought, knowledge and happiness."],"searchText":"690 कोशनाथा कोशस्य भाण्डागारस्य दिव्यस्य अन्नमयादेर्वा नाथा स्वामिनी। कोशस्य — of treasury or sheath भाण्डागारस्य — of the treasury नाथा — mistress; lord कोशनाथा means one who presides over treasure. kośa means a treasury; she is the head of all wealth. kośa also refers to the five sheaths of the body — annamaya, prāṇamaya, manomaya, vijñānamaya and ānandamaya. as their head, she blesses devotees with life, thought, knowledge and happiness. ruler of material and subtle sheaths: materially, she is the master (nāthā) of all royal treasuries and stores (bhāṇḍāgāra). esoterically, kośa refers to the five sheaths of human existence (annamaya, prāṇamaya, manomaya, vijñānamaya, ānandamaya). she is kośanāthā because she commands these internal sheaths, opening their hidden wealth to the inward-bound practitioner.","esoteric":["Ruler of Material and Subtle Sheaths: Materially, She is the master (nāthā) of all royal treasuries and stores (bhāṇḍāgāra). Esoterically, Kośa refers to the five sheaths of human existence (Annamaya, Prāṇamaya, Manomaya, Vijñānamaya, Ānandamaya). She is Kośanāthā because She commands these internal sheaths, opening their hidden wealth to the inward-bound practitioner."]},{"number":691,"name":"चतुरङ्गबलेश्वरी","samasa":["चत्वारि हस्त्यश्वरथपादातरूपाण्यङ्गानि येषां तेषां बलानामीश्वरी।","अङ्गान्येव बलं येषां तेऽङ्गबला व्यूहाः।"],"wordByWord":["चत्वारि — four"],"summary":["चतुरङ्गबलेश्वरी means one who rules the fourfold army. The fourfold army consists of cavalry, elephants, chariots and infantry. For the soul, the four faculties are mind, intellect, volition and ego. The four aggregates are also explained through the deities connected with creation, protection and destruction; She is the head of all that is fourfold."],"searchText":"691 चतुरङ्गबलेश्वरी चत्वारि हस्त्यश्वरथपादातरूपाण्यङ्गानि येषां तेषां बलानामीश्वरी। अङ्गान्येव बलं येषां तेऽङ्गबला व्यूहाः। चत्वारि — four चतुरङ्गबलेश्वरी means one who rules the fourfold army. the fourfold army consists of cavalry, elephants, chariots and infantry. for the soul, the four faculties are mind, intellect, volition and ego. the four aggregates are also explained through the deities connected with creation, protection and destruction; she is the head of all that is fourfold. the mistress of the four divisions: traditionally, a complete imperial army consists of elephants, cavalry, chariots, and infantry. she is the absolute empress (īśvarī) directing this four-fold defensive grid. esoterically, she commands the four internal functional divisions of the cognitive apparatus (अन्तःकरण) — mind, intellect, memory, and ego — marshaling them to protect the practitioner's path.","esoteric":["The Mistress of the Four Divisions: Traditionally, a complete imperial army consists of elephants, cavalry, chariots, and infantry. She is the absolute empress (Īśvarī) directing this four-fold defensive grid. Esoterically, She commands the four internal functional divisions of the cognitive apparatus (अन्तःकरण) — mind, intellect, memory, and ego — marshaling them to protect the practitioner's path."]},{"number":692,"name":"साम्राज्यदायिनी","samasa":["साम्राज्यं [ताच्छील्येन] दत्ते इति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["साम्राज्यदायिनी means one who bestows imperial dominion on Her devotees. As indicated earlier in Rājyadāyinī, She directly blesses the devotees with sāmrājya, greater than other forms of rulership. She bestows the status of emperor or maṇḍaleśvara."],"searchText":"692 साम्राज्यदायिनी साम्राज्यं [ताच्छील्येन] दत्ते इति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. साम्राज्यदायिनी means one who bestows imperial dominion on her devotees. as indicated earlier in rājyadāyinī, she directly blesses the devotees with sāmrājya, greater than other forms of rulership. she bestows the status of emperor or maṇḍaleśvara. the giver of spiritual sovereignty: while she can grant external material kingdoms, her primary gift as sāmrājyadāyinī is स्वाराज्य (svārājya — the inner empire of self-mastery). she bestows that high state of realization where the practitioner rules over their own senses, mind, and destinies, completely liberated from external dependency.","esoteric":["The Giver of Spiritual Sovereignty: While She can grant external material kingdoms, Her primary gift as Sāmrājyadāyinī is स्वाराज्य (Svārājya — the inner empire of self-mastery). She bestows that high state of realization where the practitioner rules over their own senses, mind, and destinies, completely liberated from external dependency."]},{"number":693,"name":"सत्यसन्धा","samasa":["सत्ये अनुल्लङ्घ्ये सन्धे प्रतिज्ञामर्यादे यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सत्ये — in truth","सन्धे — in vow; promise","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["सत्यसन्धा means one whose promises and vows are unbroken. The promises of Śrīdevī and Her limits of protection cannot be broken by anyone. She has vowed to protect the entire universe and firmly keeps Her word."],"searchText":"693 सत्यसन्धा सत्ये अनुल्लङ्घ्ये सन्धे प्रतिज्ञामर्यादे यस्याः सा। सत्ये — in truth सन्धे — in vow; promise यस्याः — of whom; whose सत्यसन्धा means one whose promises and vows are unbroken. the promises of śrīdevī and her limits of protection cannot be broken by anyone. she has vowed to protect the entire universe and firmly keeps her word. the absolute guarantee: her vows and universal laws are अनुल्लङ्घ्य (anullaṅghya — inviolable/unbreakable). when she promises protection, grace, or eventual liberation to a devotee who surrenders to her path, that vow is absolute truth. cosmic laws may bend, but her covenant with her children remains unyielding.","esoteric":["The Absolute Guarantee: Her vows and universal laws are अनुल्लङ्घ्य (anullaṅghya — inviolable/unbreakable). When She promises protection, grace, or eventual liberation to a devotee who surrenders to Her path, that vow is absolute truth. Cosmic laws may bend, but Her covenant with Her children remains unyielding."]},{"number":694,"name":"सागरमेखला","samasa":["सागराः समुद्रा एव मेखला काञ्ची यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सागराः — oceans","मेखला — girdle","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["सागरमेखला means one whose girdle is the ocean. The oceans themselves form Her girdle. This points to Her cosmic body, in which the seas encircle the worlds as an ornament."],"searchText":"694 सागरमेखला सागराः समुद्रा एव मेखला काञ्ची यस्याः सा। सागराः — oceans मेखला — girdle यस्याः — of whom; whose सागरमेखला means one whose girdle is the ocean. the oceans themselves form her girdle. this points to her cosmic body, in which the seas encircle the worlds as an ornament. the sovereign of the earth body: the physical earth is her manifest body, wrapped around the center by the vast oceans acting as a royal waistband (mekhalā). this reinforces her absolute presence across the terrestrial grid, showing that the physical structures of geography are components of her form.","esoteric":["The Sovereign of the Earth Body: The physical earth is Her manifest body, wrapped around the center by the vast oceans acting as a royal waistband (mekhalā). This reinforces Her absolute presence across the terrestrial grid, showing that the physical structures of geography are components of Her form."]},{"number":695,"name":"दीक्षिता","samasa":["दीक्षा।","धियं ज्ञानं क्षिणोति प्रापयतीति।","शिष्येभ्यो मन्त्रदानेन पापं क्षपयतीति।","दीक्षा अस्य सञ्जाता इति दीक्षितः। तदभिन्ना।"],"wordByWord":["दीक्षा — initiation"],"summary":["दीक्षिता means one who helps others gain knowledge through initiation. Dīkṣā destroys the sins of disciples through the giving of mantra. This is the duty of the teacher. Since Śrīdevī is Gurumūrti, She is Dīkṣitā. There is no difference between the teacher, mantra and presiding deity."],"searchText":"695 दीक्षिता दीक्षा। धियं ज्ञानं क्षिणोति प्रापयतीति। शिष्येभ्यो मन्त्रदानेन पापं क्षपयतीति। दीक्षा अस्य सञ्जाता इति दीक्षितः। तदभिन्ना। दीक्षा — initiation दीक्षिता means one who helps others gain knowledge through initiation. dīkṣā destroys the sins of disciples through the giving of mantra. this is the duty of the teacher. since śrīdevī is gurumūrti, she is dīkṣitā. there is no difference between the teacher, mantra and presiding deity. the core of initiatory power: दी signifies the bestowal of spiritual knowledge (dhiyaṁ jñānaṁ dadāti), and क्षा signifies the absolute destruction of past binding sins (pāpaṁ kṣapayati). she is dīkṣitā because she is the internal source and the non-dual power running through the initiation process, performing the purification of the student's soul.","esoteric":["The Core of Initiatory Power: दी signifies the bestowal of spiritual knowledge (dhiyaṁ jñānaṁ dadāti), and क्षा signifies the absolute destruction of past binding sins (pāpaṁ kṣapayati). She is Dīkṣitā because She is the internal source and the non-dual power running through the initiation process, performing the purification of the student's soul."]},{"number":696,"name":"दैत्यशमनी","samasa":["दैत्यानां भण्डादीनां शमनी नाशिका।"],"wordByWord":["शमनी — pacifier; destroyer"],"summary":["दैत्यशमनी means one who destroys or pacifies demons. Daityas such as Bhaṇḍāsura are subdued by Her. The name indicates Her protective power that removes the forces opposed to divine order."],"searchText":"696 दैत्यशमनी दैत्यानां भण्डादीनां शमनी नाशिका। शमनी — pacifier; destroyer दैत्यशमनी means one who destroys or pacifies demons. daityas such as bhaṇḍāsura are subdued by her. the name indicates her protective power that removes the forces opposed to divine order. the pacification of egotism: demons (daityas) represent the wild, aggressive distortions of rajas and tamas inside the mind. she does not just fight them; she pacifies (śamanī) them, drawing the chaotic energy back into its baseline source, converting the practitioner's inner turbulence into tranquil silence.","esoteric":["The Pacification of Egotism: Demons (Daityas) represent the wild, aggressive distortions of rajas and tamas inside the mind. She does not just fight them; She pacifies (śamanī) them, drawing the chaotic energy back into its baseline source, converting the practitioner's inner turbulence into tranquil silence."]},{"number":697,"name":"सर्वलोकवशङ्करी","samasa":["सर्वान् लोकान् स्ववशे कुरुते।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वान् — all","लोकान् — worlds","स्ववशे — under one’s control"],"summary":["सर्वलोकवशङ्करी means one who brings all worlds under Her control. She makes all worlds act according to Her will. All lokas and beings are governed by Her sovereign power."],"searchText":"697 सर्वलोकवशङ्करी सर्वान् लोकान् स्ववशे कुरुते। सर्वान् — all लोकान् — worlds स्ववशे — under one’s control सर्वलोकवशङ्करी means one who brings all worlds under her control. she makes all worlds act according to her will. all lokas and beings are governed by her sovereign power. the supreme fascination: she does not enforce control through external tyrannical violence. she is sarvalokavaśaṅkarī because her essential nature is so boundlessly beautiful, blissful, and full of truth that every realm, deity, and living soul is naturally fascinated, drawn inward, and aligned under her command.","esoteric":["The Supreme Fascination: She does not enforce control through external tyrannical violence. She is Sarvalokavaśaṅkarī because Her essential nature is so boundlessly beautiful, blissful, and full of truth that every realm, deity, and living soul is naturally fascinated, drawn inward, and aligned under Her command."]},{"number":698,"name":"सर्वार्थदात्री","samasa":["सर्वेषां चतुर्णामर्थानां पुरुषार्थानां दात्री।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सर्वार्थदात्री means one who gives all aims of life. She grants the four puruṣārthas: dharma, artha, kāma and mokṣa. Thus every true human aim is obtained through Her grace."],"searchText":"698 सर्वार्थदात्री सर्वेषां चतुर्णामर्थानां पुरुषार्थानां दात्री। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सर्वार्थदात्री means one who gives all aims of life. she grants the four puruṣārthas: dharma, artha, kāma and mokṣa. thus every true human aim is obtained through her grace. the dispenser of the four aims: she handles the complete grid of the four human objectives: धर्म (righteousness), अर्थ (wealth), काम (desire), and मोक्ष (liberation). she ensures that her devotees do not suffer material lack while seeking spirit, nor get trapped in wealth without spirit, organizing a balanced distribution of all human aims.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of the Four Aims: She handles the complete grid of the four human objectives: धर्म (righteousness), अर्थ (wealth), काम (desire), and मोक्ष (liberation). She ensures that Her devotees do not suffer material lack while seeking spirit, nor get trapped in wealth without spirit, organizing a balanced distribution of all human aims."]},{"number":699,"name":"सावित्री","samasa":["सवितुर्जगत्प्रसूतेः परशिवस्येयं सावित्री।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सावित्री means She is Sāvitrī. Savitṛ is the creator or impeller of the world; She is the Śakti of that supreme source. The name also recalls the Gāyatrī-Sāvitrī contemplation connected with the Sun and the supreme being."],"searchText":"699 सावित्री सवितुर्जगत्प्रसूतेः परशिवस्येयं सावित्री। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सावित्री means she is sāvitrī. savitṛ is the creator or impeller of the world; she is the śakti of that supreme source. the name also recalls the gāyatrī-sāvitrī contemplation connected with the sun and the supreme being. the power of the divine creator: सवीतृ (savitā) refers to the supreme generator of the universe—paramaśiva. she is his non-dual dynamic power (sāvitrī). this confirms her absolute identity with the inner essence of the gāyatrī mantra, acting as the brilliant light that awakens the spiritual intellect.","esoteric":["The Power of the Divine Creator: सवीतृ (Savitā) refers to the supreme generator of the universe—Paramaśiva. She is His non-dual dynamic power (Sāvitrī). This confirms Her absolute identity with the inner essence of the Gāyatrī Mantra, acting as the brilliant light that awakens the spiritual intellect."]},{"number":700,"name":"सच्चिदानन्दरूपिणी","samasa":["सत्त्वं चित्त्वमानन्दश्च रूपं स्वरूपमस्या इति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सच्चिदानन्दरूपिणी means one whose form is existence, consciousness and bliss. Sat, cit and ānanda together constitute Brahman. That Brahman is Śrīdevī; this completes the group of kalās described here."],"searchText":"700 सच्चिदानन्दरूपिणी सत्त्वं चित्त्वमानन्दश्च रूपं स्वरूपमस्या इति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सच्चिदानन्दरूपिणी means one whose form is existence, consciousness and bliss. sat, cit and ānanda together constitute brahman. that brahman is śrīdevī; this completes the group of kalās described here. the supreme definition of brahman: this name frames her identity with the unconditioned absolute. she is not a passing manifestation; her entire essential body is made of nothing but pure, uncorrupted, eternal existence (sat), infinite, self-luminous awareness (cit), and boundless, unshakeable bliss (ānanda), serving as the ultimate refuge of reality.","esoteric":["The Supreme Definition of Brahman: This name frames Her identity with the unconditioned absolute. She is not a passing manifestation; Her entire essential body is made of nothing but pure, uncorrupted, eternal existence (Sat), infinite, self-luminous awareness (Cit), and boundless, unshakeable bliss (Ānanda), serving as the ultimate refuge of reality."]},{"number":701,"name":"देशकालापरिच्छिन्ना","samasa":["देशकालाभ्यामपरिच्छिन्ना।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["देशकालापरिच्छिन्ना means one who is not limited by space and time. Some things are limited by place or time; She is eternal and available at all times, so such distinctions do not apply to Her. The meanings of Nityā, Nirnāśā and Vyāpinī are brought together in this name."],"searchText":"701 देशकालापरिच्छिन्ना देशकालाभ्यामपरिच्छिन्ना। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. देशकालापरिच्छिन्ना means one who is not limited by space and time. some things are limited by place or time; she is eternal and available at all times, so such distinctions do not apply to her. the meanings of nityā, nirnāśā and vyāpinī are brought together in this name. spatial and temporal infinity: material entities exist at a specific location and endure for a finite duration. she is deśakālāparicchinnā because she stands completely outside these structural coordinates. she lacks spatial boundaries, meaning she is omnipresent; and she lacks temporal boundaries, meaning she is eternal. she acts as the baseline screen within which space and time themselves unfold.","esoteric":["Spatial and Temporal Infinity: Material entities exist at a specific location and endure for a finite duration. She is Deśakālāparicchinnā because She stands completely outside these structural coordinates. She lacks spatial boundaries, meaning She is omnipresent; and She lacks temporal boundaries, meaning She is eternal. She acts as the baseline screen within which space and time themselves unfold."]},{"number":702,"name":"सर्वगा","samasa":["सर्वं वस्तुमात्रं गच्छत्यभेदेन प्राप्नोतीति सर्वगा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सर्वगा means one who pervades all. She reaches all things by non-difference and is present everywhere. No place or object is outside Her presence."],"searchText":"702 सर्वगा सर्वं वस्तुमात्रं गच्छत्यभेदेन प्राप्नोतीति सर्वगा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सर्वगा means one who pervades all. she reaches all things by non-difference and is present everywhere. no place or object is outside her presence. the pervasive substance: she does not simply move from place to place. she is sarvagā because she reaches and permeates every single objective entity (vastu-mātra) through absolute structural identity (अभेदेन). there is no gap between her consciousness field and the material forms it animates; she is the essential substance inside every coordinate of the universe.","esoteric":["The Pervasive Substance: She does not simply move from place to place. She is Sarvagā because She reaches and permeates every single objective entity (vastu-mātra) through absolute structural identity (अभेदेन). There is no gap between Her consciousness field and the material forms it animates; She is the essential substance inside every coordinate of the universe."]},{"number":703,"name":"सर्वमोहिनी","samasa":["सर्वान्प्राकृतजनान् भेदभाने सत्यत्वं मन्यमानान् मोहयति अद्वैतविषयकज्ञानविधुरान् कुरुते इति।"],"wordByWord":["मोहयति — bewilders"],"summary":["सर्वमोहिनी means one who bewilders all. She bewilders ordinary people who take apparent duality as real and deprives them of the knowledge of unity. The apparent difference between Brahman and the universe is illusory; this power of bewilderment is described also in Saptashatī."],"searchText":"703 सर्वमोहिनी सर्वान्प्राकृतजनान् भेदभाने सत्यत्वं मन्यमानान् मोहयति अद्वैतविषयकज्ञानविधुरान् कुरुते इति। मोहयति — bewilders सर्वमोहिनी means one who bewilders all. she bewilders ordinary people who take apparent duality as real and deprives them of the knowledge of unity. the apparent difference between brahman and the universe is illusory; this power of bewilderment is described also in saptashatī. the magic of duality: as sarvamohinī, she binds those who view the relative world as an absolute reality (bheda-bhāna). she temporarily veils their non-dual realization (advaita-jñāna-vidhura), causing them to see differences instead of unity. this enchantment is the foundational mechanism that allows the cosmic play (līlā) to appear real to the individual observer.","esoteric":["The Magic of Duality: As Sarvamohinī, She binds those who view the relative world as an absolute reality (bheda-bhāna). She temporarily veils their non-dual realization (advaita-jñāna-vidhura), causing them to see differences instead of unity. This enchantment is the foundational mechanism that allows the cosmic play (Līlā) to appear real to the individual observer."]},{"number":704,"name":"सरस्वती","samasa":["सरो नीरं तद्वत् रसो वा अस्त्यस्या इति।","द्विवर्षा तु सरस्वतीति धौम्यवचनात्तादृशकन्यारूपति।","विषयानवच्छिन्नज्ञानरूपेति।","ज्ञानाभिमानिनी देवता ज्ञानसमुद्ररूपेत्यर्थः।"],"wordByWord":["सरो — lake; water"],"summary":["सरस्वती means She is the form of knowledge and speech, and the deity presiding over knowledge. Sarasvatī. She is like an ocean of knowledge and is also connected with the traditional form of Sarasvatī."],"searchText":"704 सरस्वती सरो नीरं तद्वत् रसो वा अस्त्यस्या इति। द्विवर्षा तु सरस्वतीति धौम्यवचनात्तादृशकन्यारूपति। विषयानवच्छिन्नज्ञानरूपेति। ज्ञानाभिमानिनी देवता ज्ञानसमुद्ररूपेत्यर्थः। सरो — lake; water सरस्वती means she is the form of knowledge and speech, and the deity presiding over knowledge. sarasvatī. she is like an ocean of knowledge and is also connected with the traditional form of sarasvatī. the shoreless ocean of wisdom: she is identical to the supreme goddess of wisdom, sarasvatī. she represents unconditioned awareness (viṣayānavacchinna-jñāna), flowing like a vast, fluid ocean of insight. ritual maidens: in the liturgical framework of kumārī-pūjā defined by sage dhaumya, she manifests as the pristine energy of a two-year-old girl, representing pure potential before worldly conditioning.","esoteric":["The Shoreless Ocean of Wisdom: She is identical to the supreme goddess of wisdom, Sarasvatī. She represents unconditioned awareness (viṣayānavacchinna-jñāna), flowing like a vast, fluid ocean of insight.","Ritual Maidens: In the liturgical framework of Kumārī-Pūjā defined by Sage Dhaumya, She manifests as the pristine energy of a two-year-old girl, representing pure potential before worldly conditioning."]},{"number":705,"name":"शास्त्रमयी","samasa":["सर्वं खल्विदं ब्रह्मेत्यादिशास्त्रप्रधाना।","शास्त्रात्मकस्वावयवशालिविग्रहत्वाच्छास्त्रविकारेत्यप्यर्थः।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["शास्त्रमयी means one who is composed of śāstra. The scriptures beginning with teachings such as sarvaṃ khalvidaṃ brahma are centred on Her. Her body is understood as made of scripture, or as the source and transformation of śāstra."],"searchText":"705 शास्त्रमयी सर्वं खल्विदं ब्रह्मेत्यादिशास्त्रप्रधाना। शास्त्रात्मकस्वावयवशालिविग्रहत्वाच्छास्त्रविकारेत्यप्यर्थः। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. शास्त्रमयी means one who is composed of śāstra. the scriptures beginning with teachings such as sarvaṃ khalvidaṃ brahma are centred on her. her body is understood as made of scripture, or as the source and transformation of śāstra. the body of the sacred word: she is śāstramayī because her subtle body is woven out of the foundational declarations of non-duality, such as “sarvaṁ khalvidaṁ brahma” (\"all this is indeed brahman\"). every sacred science, text, and structural formula is a limb of her manifest form, making her the literal substance of divine revelation.","esoteric":["The Body of the Sacred Word: She is Śāstramayī because Her subtle body is woven out of the foundational declarations of non-duality, such as “Sarvaṁ khalvidaṁ Brahma” (\"All this is indeed Brahman\"). every sacred science, text, and structural formula is a limb of Her manifest form, making Her the literal substance of divine revelation."]},{"number":706,"name":"गुहाम्बा","samasa":["गुहायां स्थिताम्बा।","गुहस्य स्कन्दस्याम्बा माता"],"wordByWord":["गुहस्य — of Guha/Subrahmaṇya","माता — mother"],"summary":["गुहाम्बा means one who dwells in the cave. The cave is the heart. The Upaniṣadic idea of shadow and light in the cave of the heart is discussed here. The name may also mean the mother of Guha or Subrahmaṇya, as narrated in Purāṇic accounts."],"searchText":"706 गुहाम्बा गुहायां स्थिताम्बा। गुहस्य स्कन्दस्याम्बा माता गुहस्य — of guha/subrahmaṇya माता — mother गुहाम्बा means one who dwells in the cave. the cave is the heart. the upaniṣadic idea of shadow and light in the cave of the heart is discussed here. the name may also mean the mother of guha or subrahmaṇya, as narrated in purāṇic accounts. the guardian of the secret cavern: mythologically, she is the mother of the warrior lord skanda (guha). esoterically, गुहा (guhā) refers to the hidden, secret cavern of the human heart. she is the primordial, protective mother energy (ambā) that sits inside this internal cave, guarding the individual spark of consciousness.","esoteric":["The Guardian of the Secret Cavern: Mythologically, She is the mother of the warrior lord Skanda (Guha). Esoterically, गुहा (guhā) refers to the hidden, secret cavern of the human heart. She is the primordial, protective mother energy (Ambā) that sits inside this internal cave, guarding the individual spark of consciousness."]},{"number":707,"name":"गुह्यरूपिणी","samasa":["गुहायां स्थितं गुह्यं परमरहस्यं व्यावहारिकदृष्ट्ययोग्यं ज्ञानमेव रूपमस्याः।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["गुह्यरूपिणी means one whose form is most secret. The permanent truth is secret, beyond the phenomenal universe and beyond the senses. She is the secret knowledge residing in the secret place, beloved by secret devotees."],"searchText":"707 गुह्यरूपिणी गुहायां स्थितं गुह्यं परमरहस्यं व्यावहारिकदृष्ट्ययोग्यं ज्ञानमेव रूपमस्याः। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. गुह्यरूपिणी means one whose form is most secret. the permanent truth is secret, beyond the phenomenal universe and beyond the senses. she is the secret knowledge residing in the secret place, beloved by secret devotees. the transcendent secret: ordinary physical vision is tuned exclusively to capture relative, external material objects. her true, essential form is guhya — a supreme secret that cannot be objectified by common, worldly intellects (vyāvahārika-dṛṣṭi-ayogya). she is the unmanifested, mystical core of reality, realized solely through internal absorption.","esoteric":["The Transcendent Secret: Ordinary physical vision is tuned exclusively to capture relative, external material objects. Her true, essential form is Guhya — a supreme secret that cannot be objectified by common, worldly intellects (vyāvahārika-dṛṣṭi-ayogya). She is the unmanifested, mystical core of reality, realized solely through internal absorption."]},{"number":708,"name":"सर्वोपाधिविनिर्मुक्ता","samasa":["सर्वैः उपाधिभिः विशिष्य निःशेषेण मुक्ता त्यक्ता धर्मसम्बन्धशून्या।","तार्किकप्रसिद्धोपाधिशून्या तादृशसद्धेतुगम्येति।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वैः — by all","उपाधिभिः — by limiting adjuncts","मुक्ता — free"],"summary":["सर्वोपाधिविनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from all limitations and adjuncts. Every attribute becomes a limiting adjunct of place, time or object. She is free from all such upādhis. The relation of qualities to the qualified thing is ultimately illusory; She, as Brahman, is unrelated to every limiting quality."],"searchText":"708 सर्वोपाधिविनिर्मुक्ता सर्वैः उपाधिभिः विशिष्य निःशेषेण मुक्ता त्यक्ता धर्मसम्बन्धशून्या। तार्किकप्रसिद्धोपाधिशून्या तादृशसद्धेतुगम्येति। सर्वैः — by all उपाधिभिः — by limiting adjuncts मुक्ता — free सर्वोपाधिविनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from all limitations and adjuncts. every attribute becomes a limiting adjunct of place, time or object. she is free from all such upādhis. the relation of qualities to the qualified thing is ultimately illusory; she, as brahman, is unrelated to every limiting quality. absolute freedom from adjuncts: an upādhi is a conditioning lens—like a piece of red glass that makes a clear crystal appear red. space, time, names, forms, and elements are all cosmic lenses. she is sarvopādhivinirmuktā because in her pristine essential nature as parabrahman, she stands completely free from all these attributes (धर्मसम्बन्धशून्या), remaining unconditioned and pure.","esoteric":["Absolute Freedom from Adjuncts: An Upādhi is a conditioning lens—like a piece of red glass that makes a clear crystal appear red. Space, time, names, forms, and elements are all cosmic lenses. She is Sarvopādhivinirmuktā because in Her pristine essential nature as Parabrahman, She stands completely free from all these attributes (धर्मसम्बन्धशून्या), remaining unconditioned and pure."]},{"number":709,"name":"सदाशिवपतिव्रता","samasa":["शिव एव पतिरिति व्रतं नियमः सदा सार्वकालिको यस्याः सा।","सदाशिवस्य पतिव्रतेति।"],"wordByWord":["सदा — always","यस्याः — of whom; whose"],"summary":["सदाशिवपतिव्रता means one who is the devoted spouse of Sadāśiva. She remains always with Śiva in all three times. This name establishes Her equality with, and inseparability from, Brahman while preserving the devotional image of Śiva and Śakti."],"searchText":"709 सदाशिवपतिव्रता शिव एव पतिरिति व्रतं नियमः सदा सार्वकालिको यस्याः सा। सदाशिवस्य पतिव्रतेति। सदा — always यस्याः — of whom; whose सदाशिवपतिव्रता means one who is the devoted spouse of sadāśiva. she remains always with śiva in all three times. this name establishes her equality with, and inseparability from, brahman while preserving the devotional image of śiva and śakti. the eternal fusion of consciousness and energy: this names the absolute, unbreakable dynamic law of non-duality. she (śakti) possesses an unceasing, timeless vow (sada-vrata) to never separate herself from sadāśiva (pure, static consciousness). energy cannot exist without consciousness, and consciousness cannot express itself without energy. they remain in an eternal, unbroken embrace.","esoteric":["The Eternal Fusion of Consciousness and Energy: This names the absolute, unbreakable dynamic law of non-duality. She (Śakti) possesses an unceasing, timeless vow (sada-vrata) to never separate Herself from Sadāśiva (pure, static consciousness). Energy cannot exist without consciousness, and consciousness cannot express itself without energy. They remain in an eternal, unbroken embrace."]},{"number":710,"name":"सम्प्रदायेश्वरी","samasa":["सम्यक् शिष्येभ्यः प्रदीयत इति सम्प्रदायः। तत्रेश्वरी समर्था समर्थनक्षमा।"],"wordByWord":["शिष्येभ्यः — to disciples"],"summary":["सम्प्रदायेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the tradition. Sampradāya is that which is properly handed down from teacher to disciple. She is the authority and power behind that lineage and its transmission."],"searchText":"710 सम्प्रदायेश्वरी सम्यक् शिष्येभ्यः प्रदीयत इति सम्प्रदायः। तत्रेश्वरी समर्था समर्थनक्षमा। शिष्येभ्यः — to disciples सम्प्रदायेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the tradition. sampradāya is that which is properly handed down from teacher to disciple. she is the authority and power behind that lineage and its transmission. the mistress of the lineage: सम्प्रदाय (sampradāya) is the uninterrupted chain through which sacred wisdom is correctly and directly transmitted from master to disciple (samyak pradīyate). she is the absolute ruler and animating spirit behind this entire pedagogical pipeline, ensuring that the initiatory power stays alive and uncorrupted across generations.","esoteric":["The Mistress of the Lineage: सम्प्रदाय (Sampradāya) is the uninterrupted chain through which sacred wisdom is correctly and directly transmitted from master to disciple (samyak pradīyate). She is the absolute ruler and animating spirit behind this entire pedagogical pipeline, ensuring that the initiatory power stays alive and uncorrupted across generations."]},{"number":711,"name":"साध्वी","samasa":["सद्गतिदायिनी।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["साध्वी means one who is virtuous and gives the good path. Sādhvī means the one of noble conduct. She leads devotees to the right and auspicious path."],"searchText":"711 साध्वी सद्गतिदायिनी। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. साध्वी means one who is virtuous and gives the good path. sādhvī means the one of noble conduct. she leads devotees to the right and auspicious path. the guide to the highest goal: she is sādhvī because her operations are entirely aligned with uncorrupted cosmic order (ṛta). for the practitioner, she acts as सद्गतिदायिनी (sadgati-dāyinī) — the force that safely guides the soul along the upward path, ensuring they reach the ultimate destination of liberation without falling into spiritual deviation.","esoteric":["The Guide to the Highest Goal: She is Sādhvī because Her operations are entirely aligned with uncorrupted cosmic order (Ṛta). For the practitioner, She acts as सद्गतिदायिनी (Sadgati-dāyinī) — the force that safely guides the soul along the upward path, ensuring they reach the ultimate destination of liberation without falling into spiritual deviation."]},{"number":712,"name":"ई","samasa":["तुर्यस्वरूपमेकाक्षरं कामकलासंज्ञकमिदं नाम।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["ई means the one-letter name Ī. This single syllable is connected with the turīya state and kāmakalā. It is a secret mantra-name and is to be understood through the proper tradition."],"searchText":"712 ई तुर्यस्वरूपमेकाक्षरं कामकलासंज्ञकमिदं नाम। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. ई means the one-letter name ī. this single syllable is connected with the turīya state and kāmakalā. it is a secret mantra-name and is to be understood through the proper tradition. the monosyllable of kāmakalā: the vowel ई (ī) is the phonetic seed-syllable that represents कामकला (kāmakalā) — the primal, creative flash of divine desire where shiva and shakti recognize their union. it is the fourth transcendent state (turya-svarūpa). she is the direct phonic reality of this single syllable, which contains the complete blueprint of creation within its resonance.","esoteric":["The Monosyllable of Kāmakalā: The vowel ई (Ī) is the phonetic seed-syllable that represents कामकला (Kāmakalā) — the primal, creative flash of divine desire where Shiva and Shakti recognize their union. It is the fourth transcendent state (Turya-svarūpa). She is the direct phonic reality of this single syllable, which contains the complete blueprint of creation within its resonance."]},{"number":713,"name":"गुरुमण्डलरूपिणी","samasa":["गुरवः परमशिवादिस्वस्वगुरुपर्यन्तास्तेषां मण्डलं परम्परा सैव रूपं निरूपणमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["गुरवः — gurus","परम्परा — tradition; succession"],"summary":["गुरुमण्डलरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the circle of Gurus. The secret kāmakalā form must be learnt through a proper teacher and not merely from books. The lineage from Paramaśiva down to one's own Guru is the Gurumaṇḍala; She is in that form."],"searchText":"713 गुरुमण्डलरूपिणी गुरवः परमशिवादिस्वस्वगुरुपर्यन्तास्तेषां मण्डलं परम्परा सैव रूपं निरूपणमस्याः अस्तीति। गुरवः — gurus परम्परा — tradition; succession गुरुमण्डलरूपिणी means one who is in the form of the circle of gurus. the secret kāmakalā form must be learnt through a proper teacher and not merely from books. the lineage from paramaśiva down to one's own guru is the gurumaṇḍala; she is in that form. the corporate chain of preceptors: the guru lineage in śrīvidyā is stratified into three distinct tiers: दिव्यौघ (divyaugha — celestial masters), सिद्धौघ (siddhaugha — perfected masters), and मानवौघ (mānavaugha — human masters), initiating from paramaśiva himself. she is gurumaṇḍalarūpiṇī because she is the continuous light running through this entire corporate chain, proving that every true guru is an execution of her presence.","esoteric":["The Corporate Chain of Preceptors: The Guru lineage in Śrīvidyā is stratified into three distinct tiers: दिव्यौघ (Divyaugha — celestial masters), सिद्धौघ (Siddhaugha — perfected masters), and मानवौघ (Mānavaugha — human masters), initiating from Paramaśiva Himself. She is Gurumaṇḍalarūpiṇī because She is the continuous light running through this entire corporate chain, proving that every true guru is an execution of Her presence."]},{"number":714,"name":"कुलोत्तीर्णा","samasa":["कुलमिन्द्रियसमूहमुत्तीर्णा अतिक्रान्ता।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["कुलोत्तीर्णा means one who has crossed beyond kula. Kula is here the group of senses. She is beyond recognition through the senses. She can be reached only through imagination, devotion and knowledge; related names such as Bhāvanāgamyā and Bhaktigamyā are recalled."],"searchText":"714 कुलोत्तीर्णा कुलमिन्द्रियसमूहमुत्तीर्णा अतिक्रान्ता। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. कुलोत्तीर्णा means one who has crossed beyond kula. kula is here the group of senses. she is beyond recognition through the senses. she can be reached only through imagination, devotion and knowledge; related names such as bhāvanāgamyā and bhaktigamyā are recalled. beyond the sensory matrix: in internal alignment, कुल (kula) denotes the network of the senses, the physical elements, and the structured system of the lower chakras. she is kulottīrṇā because while she animates these systems, she simultaneously stands completely past them (atikrāntā). she represents the shoreless, unmanifested sky of pure consciousness (akula) that remains untouched by material mechanics.","esoteric":["Beyond the Sensory Matrix: In internal alignment, कुल (Kula) denotes the network of the senses, the physical elements, and the structured system of the lower chakras. She is Kulottīrṇā because while She animates these systems, She simultaneously stands completely past them (atikrāntā). She represents the shoreless, unmanifested sky of pure consciousness (Akula) that remains untouched by material mechanics."]},{"number":715,"name":"भगाराध्या","samasa":["भगे सवितृमण्डले आराध्योपास्या।","भगेन एकाकारेण आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["भगे — in bhaga; solar disc/triangle","सवितृमण्डले — in the solar orb"],"summary":["भगाराध्या means one who is to be worshipped in the Sun's disc. Bhaga indicates the Sun's disc, and She is secretly worshipped there; this recalls Bhānumaṇḍala-madhyasthā. The triangular letter Ī and the union of Śiva and Śakti are also connected with this name, and the meaning must be learnt through a proper teacher."],"searchText":"715 भगाराध्या भगे सवितृमण्डले आराध्योपास्या। भगेन एकाकारेण आराध्या। भगे — in bhaga; solar disc/triangle सवितृमण्डले — in the solar orb भगाराध्या means one who is to be worshipped in the sun's disc. bhaga indicates the sun's disc, and she is secretly worshipped there; this recalls bhānumaṇḍala-madhyasthā. the triangular letter ī and the union of śiva and śakti are also connected with this name, and the meaning must be learnt through a proper teacher. the meditation in the sun: भग (bhaga) refers directly to the radiant, life-giving orb of the sun (savitṛ-maṇḍala). she is the inner consciousness worshipped at the absolute center of this solar light. the unified adoration: alternatively, it denotes that she is correctly approached and adored through a completely undivided, unified state of internal awareness (ekākāra), where the practitioner sheds all sense of fragmented tracking.","esoteric":["The Meditation in the Sun: भग (Bhaga) refers directly to the radiant, life-giving orb of the sun (Savitṛ-maṇḍala). She is the inner consciousness worshipped at the absolute center of this solar light.","The Unified Adoration: Alternatively, it denotes that She is correctly approached and adored through a completely undivided, unified state of internal awareness (ekākāra), where the practitioner sheds all sense of fragmented tracking."]},{"number":716,"name":"माया","samasa":["प्रसिद्धतरस्याप्यप्रकटीकरणानुकूला शक्तिर्माया।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["माया means one who is the form of māyā. Māyā is the power that hides what is clear and makes appear what is not available. Dreams and supernatural appearances are also connected with māyā. The Devī Purāṇa, Varāha Purāṇa, Bhagavad Gītā, Śāṇḍilya Sūtra, Saptashatī and Śākta tradition explain this power. In Śrīvidyā it is the Śakti of Brahman; by worshipping Her, māyā is crossed."],"searchText":"716 माया प्रसिद्धतरस्याप्यप्रकटीकरणानुकूला शक्तिर्माया। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. माया means one who is the form of māyā. māyā is the power that hides what is clear and makes appear what is not available. dreams and supernatural appearances are also connected with māyā. the devī purāṇa, varāha purāṇa, bhagavad gītā, śāṇḍilya sūtra, saptashatī and śākta tradition explain this power. in śrīvidyā it is the śakti of brahman; by worshipping her, māyā is crossed. the engine of selective concealment: māyā is not a simple hallucination. she commands this operational filter to sustain the cosmic projection.","esoteric":["The Engine of Selective Concealment: Māyā is not a simple hallucination. She commands this operational filter to sustain the cosmic projection."]},{"number":717,"name":"मधुमती","samasa":["मधु मद्यं पुष्परसः क्षौद्रं वा पूजनादिसमये अस्याः अस्तीति।","आदित्यो वै देवमध्विति श्रुतौ विहितमधुमत्याख्यविद्याविशेषरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["मधु — honey; wine","पुष्परसः — flower-juice; honey"],"summary":["मधुमती means one who is connected with madhu, meaning honey or wine. Madhu may mean honey, wine or sweetness, and such offerings are part of certain forms of worship. The name is also related to Vedic and Upaniṣadic statements about honey, to the yogic stage called Madhumatī, and to a river of that name."],"searchText":"717 मधुमती मधु मद्यं पुष्परसः क्षौद्रं वा पूजनादिसमये अस्याः अस्तीति। आदित्यो वै देवमध्विति श्रुतौ विहितमधुमत्याख्यविद्याविशेषरूपा। मधु — honey; wine पुष्परसः — flower-juice; honey मधुमती means one who is connected with madhu, meaning honey or wine. madhu may mean honey, wine or sweetness, and such offerings are part of certain forms of worship. the name is also related to vedic and upaniṣadic statements about honey, to the yogic stage called madhumatī, and to a river of that name. the solar honey: the chāndogya upaniṣad celebrates the sun as the divine honey of the cosmos (adityo vai devamadhu). she is the living essence of this मधुमती विद्या (madhumatī vidyā), the high scriptural science that tracks this solar nectar. the internal sweetness: in internal yoga, it represents her presence within the ultimate sweet fluid that floods the channels during deep concentration.","esoteric":["The Solar Honey: The Chāndogya Upaniṣad celebrates the sun as the divine honey of the cosmos (Adityo vai devamadhu). She is the living essence of this मधुमती विद्या (Madhumatī Vidyā), the high scriptural science that tracks this solar nectar.","The Internal Sweetness: In internal yoga, it represents Her presence within the ultimate sweet fluid that floods the channels during deep concentration."]},{"number":718,"name":"मही","samasa":["रहस्यरूपापि पृथ्वीवदतिप्रकटा।","मह्याख्यनदीविशेषरूपा।","महद्व्याप्य स्थिता।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["मही means one who is in the form of the earth. Though previous names spoke of secret forms, She is clearly visible like the earth. She supports the whole universe like the earth. Eternal nature is also Mahī; She is that form and also the river called Mahī."],"searchText":"718 मही रहस्यरूपापि पृथ्वीवदतिप्रकटा। मह्याख्यनदीविशेषरूपा। महद्व्याप्य स्थिता। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. मही means one who is in the form of the earth. though previous names spoke of secret forms, she is clearly visible like the earth. she supports the whole universe like the earth. eternal nature is also mahī; she is that form and also the river called mahī. the hyper-manifest reality: though she is highly secret (rahasya-rūpā), as mahī, she is simultaneously as blindingly obvious and tangible as the solid earth beneath our feet (pṛthivīvat ati-prakaṭā). she occupies and pervades the entire physical expansion (mahad-vyāpya), showing her absolute accessibility within the material elements.","esoteric":["The Hyper-Manifest Reality: Though She is highly secret (rahasya-rūpā), as Mahī, She is simultaneously as blindingly obvious and tangible as the solid earth beneath our feet (pṛthivīvat ati-prakaṭā). She occupies and pervades the entire physical expansion (mahad-vyāpya), showing Her absolute accessibility within the material elements."]},{"number":719,"name":"गणाम्बा","samasa":["गणस्य प्रमथादेः अम्बा।","गणस्य गजाननस्य अम्बा।"],"wordByWord":["गणस्य — of the host","प्रमथादेः — of Pramatha and others","गजाननस्य — of Gaṇeśa"],"summary":["गणाम्बा means one who is the mother of hosts. Gaṇa means a group; She is the mother of the Pramatha and other hosts of Paramaśiva. Since the head of Śiva's hosts is Gaṇeśa, She is also understood as his mother."],"searchText":"719 गणाम्बा गणस्य प्रमथादेः अम्बा। गणस्य गजाननस्य अम्बा। गणस्य — of the host प्रमथादेः — of pramatha and others गजाननस्य — of gaṇeśa गणाम्बा means one who is the mother of hosts. gaṇa means a group; she is the mother of the pramatha and other hosts of paramaśiva. since the head of śiva's hosts is gaṇeśa, she is also understood as his mother. the mother of assemblies: mythologically, she is the mother of the elephant-faced lord gaṇapati, who commands the dynamic forces. esoterically, गण (gaṇa) represents the groupings, categories, and mathematical sets of phonemes and elements that construct the universe. she sits as the original maternal source (ambā) that gives birth to and organizes these sets.","esoteric":["The Mother of Assemblies: Mythologically, She is the mother of the elephant-faced lord Gaṇapati, who commands the dynamic forces. Esoterically, गण (gaṇa) represents the groupings, categories, and mathematical sets of phonemes and elements that construct the universe. She sits as the original maternal source (Ambā) that gives birth to and organizes these sets."]},{"number":720,"name":"गुह्यकाराध्या","samasa":["गुह्यकैर्देवविशेषैः आराध्या।","अज्ञातरहस्यस्थले आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["गुह्यकाराध्या means one who is worshipped by Guhyakas. Kubera, the god of wealth, is the sage for one variety of Pañcadaśī; his hosts are called Guhyakas. She is worshipped by Kubera and those hosts. In the Kaula method, Guhyaka also indicates worship in a secret place, unknown to others."],"searchText":"720 गुह्यकाराध्या गुह्यकैर्देवविशेषैः आराध्या। अज्ञातरहस्यस्थले आराध्या। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. गुह्यकाराध्या means one who is worshipped by guhyakas. kubera, the god of wealth, is the sage for one variety of pañcadaśī; his hosts are called guhyakas. she is worshipped by kubera and those hosts. in the kaula method, guhyaka also indicates worship in a secret place, unknown to others. adoration by the hidden hosts: the guhyakas are a highly specialized class of protective, subterranean celestial beings who guard the hidden treasures of the cosmos under kubera. their adoration establishes her status as the ruler of unmanifested wealth. the secret sanctuary: alternatively, it confirms that she is correctly approached and adored within the most private, silent, and deeply interior chambers of spiritual realization.","esoteric":["Adoration by the Hidden Hosts: The Guhyakas are a highly specialized class of protective, subterranean celestial beings who guard the hidden treasures of the cosmos under Kubera. Their adoration establishes Her status as the ruler of unmanifested wealth.","The Secret Sanctuary: Alternatively, it confirms that She is correctly approached and adored within the most private, silent, and deeply interior chambers of spiritual realization."]},{"number":721,"name":"कोमलाङ्गी","samasa":["कोमलानि सुकुमाराण्यङ्गानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कोमलानि — delicate; soft","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["कोमलाङ्गी means one whose form is delicate and pleasing. The message given in the name Nalinī is stressed here. Her body is gentle and soft, as praised in devotional poetry such as Śyāmala Daṇḍaka."],"searchText":"721 कोमलाङ्गी कोमलानि सुकुमाराण्यङ्गानि यस्याः सा। कोमलानि — delicate; soft यस्याः — whose; of whom कोमलाङ्गी means one whose form is delicate and pleasing. the message given in the name nalinī is stressed here. her body is gentle and soft, as praised in devotional poetry such as śyāmala daṇḍaka. the softness of grace: her limbs and geometric lines are described as tender (sukumāra), reminding the practitioner that her interaction with the universe is free from crude, heavy violence. even her massive cosmic operations are driven by a highly refined, delicate grace, ensuring that the alignment of souls occurs with gentle precision.","esoteric":["The Softness of Grace: Her limbs and geometric lines are described as tender (sukumāra), reminding the practitioner that Her interaction with the universe is free from crude, heavy violence. Even Her massive cosmic operations are driven by a highly refined, delicate grace, ensuring that the alignment of souls occurs with gentle precision."]},{"number":722,"name":"गुरुप्रिया","samasa":["गुरुः प्रियो यस्याः सा।","गुरुपत्न्यभिन्ना। जगद्गुरोः शिवस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["गुरुः — guru; teacher","यस्याः — whose; of whom","शिवस्य — of Śiva"],"summary":["गुरुप्रिया means one who has affection for the Guru. She has great love for Parameśvara, the great teacher of the world. She is pleased with the teachers who initiate eligible disciples into Śrīvidyā and keep the worshipping tradition unbroken. She is also understood as the consort of the Guru of every worshipper. This implies that the Guru's wife is to be treated as Śrīdevī herself; in this worship every lady is to be regarded as Śrīdevī. Guru can also mean Bṛhaspati, the teacher of the devas; She has care for him also."],"searchText":"722 गुरुप्रिया गुरुः प्रियो यस्याः सा। गुरुपत्न्यभिन्ना। जगद्गुरोः शिवस्य पत्नी। गुरुः — guru; teacher यस्याः — whose; of whom शिवस्य — of śiva गुरुप्रिया means one who has affection for the guru. she has great love for parameśvara, the great teacher of the world. she is pleased with the teachers who initiate eligible disciples into śrīvidyā and keep the worshipping tradition unbroken. she is also understood as the consort of the guru of every worshipper. this implies that the guru's wife is to be treated as śrīdevī herself; in this worship every lady is to be regarded as śrīdevī. guru can also mean bṛhaspati, the teacher of the devas; she has care for him also. the beloved of the universal master: lord śiva is the eternal, primordial जगद्गुरु (jagadguru — teacher of the worlds). she is his beloved non-dual consort (gurupriyā). concurrently, this name establishes that she is deeply affectionate toward any true preceptor who correctly preserves and teaches the sacred lineage keys, holding them close to her grace.","esoteric":["The Beloved of the Universal Master: Lord Śiva is the eternal, primordial जगद्गुरु (Jagadguru — teacher of the worlds). She is His beloved non-dual consort (Gurupriyā). Concurrently, this name establishes that She is deeply affectionate toward any true preceptor who correctly preserves and teaches the sacred lineage keys, holding them close to Her grace."]},{"number":723,"name":"स्वतन्त्रा","samasa":["स्वस्य तन्त्रं प्राधान्यं यस्यां सा।","स्वान्यात्मीयानि तन्त्राणि यस्याः सा।","कारकपारतन्त्र्यमन्तरेणैव सर्वकर्तृत्वात्।","स्वतन्त्राख्यनित्यातन्त्ररूपा।","स्व आत्मीयः स्वाधीनः परशिवस्तत्तन्त्रा तदधीना।"],"wordByWord":["स्वस्य — of herself","तन्त्राणि — tantras","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["स्वतन्त्रा means one who acts on Her own, without depending on others. She does not require the help of others for any activity. She does not even need instruments; by Her mere will or declaration She acts. She owns Her consort Parameśvara, and He owns Her; they mutually belong to each other. She is in the form of the nityā tantra called Svatantra. This name may also be connected with the Svatantra mentioned in Soundaryalaharī. All tantras are ultimately Her own, because even worship of other deities is made possible only by the life-energy that is Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"723 स्वतन्त्रा स्वस्य तन्त्रं प्राधान्यं यस्यां सा। स्वान्यात्मीयानि तन्त्राणि यस्याः सा। कारकपारतन्त्र्यमन्तरेणैव सर्वकर्तृत्वात्। स्वतन्त्राख्यनित्यातन्त्ररूपा। स्व आत्मीयः स्वाधीनः परशिवस्तत्तन्त्रा तदधीना। स्वस्य — of herself तन्त्राणि — tantras यस्याः — whose; of whom स्वतन्त्रा means one who acts on her own, without depending on others. she does not require the help of others for any activity. she does not even need instruments; by her mere will or declaration she acts. she owns her consort parameśvara, and he owns her; they mutually belong to each other. she is in the form of the nityā tantra called svatantra. this name may also be connected with the svatantra mentioned in soundaryalaharī. all tantras are ultimately her own, because even worship of other deities is made possible only by the life-energy that is śrīdevī. absolute sovereignty: she is svatantrā because she operates with absolute freedom, entirely unconditioned by external factors or causal dependencies (कारकपारतन्त्र्यमन्तरेण सर्वकर्तृत्वात्). she rules her own systems. the mirror of shiva: alternatively, स्व refers to her own non-dual counterpart, paramaśiva, meaning her entire operational system is fully synchronized and dependent solely on him, tracking her onto the svatantrā nityā deity of the lunar calendar.","esoteric":["Absolute Sovereignty: She is Svatantrā because She operates with absolute freedom, entirely unconditioned by external factors or causal dependencies (कारकपारतन्त्र्यमन्तरेण सर्वकर्तृत्वात्). She rules Her own systems.","The Mirror of Shiva: Alternatively, स्व refers to Her own non-dual counterpart, Paramaśiva, meaning Her entire operational system is fully synchronized and dependent solely on Him, tracking Her onto the Svatantrā Nityā deity of the lunar calendar."]},{"number":724,"name":"सर्वतन्त्रेशी","samasa":["सर्वाणि चतुःषष्टिसंख्याकानि तन्त्राणीष्टे समर्थयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वाणि — all"],"summary":["सर्वतन्त्रेशी means one who is the head of all tantras. She establishes and supports the sixty-four tantras and makes them meaningful."],"searchText":"724 सर्वतन्त्रेशी सर्वाणि चतुःषष्टिसंख्याकानि तन्त्राणीष्टे समर्थयतीति। सर्वाणि — all सर्वतन्त्रेशी means one who is the head of all tantras. she establishes and supports the sixty-four tantras and makes them meaningful. this confirms her legislative mastery over all traditions: the overlord of the sixty-four lineages: the agamic universe features sixty-four primary textual systems and lineages (catuḥṣaṣṭi-tantra). she is sarvatantreśī because she sits at the absolute peak apex above all sixty-four books. they are merely partial, specialized charts of her energy, drawing their functional authority exclusively from her supreme command.","esoteric":["this confirms Her legislative mastery over all traditions:","The Overlord of the Sixty-Four Lineages: The Agamic universe features sixty-four primary textual systems and lineages (Catuḥṣaṣṭi-tantra). She is Sarvatantreśī because She sits at the absolute peak apex above all sixty-four books. They are merely partial, specialized charts of Her energy, drawing their functional authority exclusively from Her supreme command."]},{"number":725,"name":"दक्षिणामूर्तिरूपिणी","samasa":["शिवस्य दक्षिणाभिमुखी मूर्तिर्ब्रह्मनारायणादेरध्यापकत्वेन प्रसिद्धा। यस्या मन्त्रास्तन्त्रेषु प्रसिद्धाः स एव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["शिवस्य — of Śiva","दक्षिणाभिमुखी — south-facing"],"summary":["दक्षिणामूर्तिरूपिणी means one who is in the form of Dakṣiṇāmūrti. Dakṣiṇāmūrti teaches the principle of non-duality. Śiva and Śrīdevī appear in individual forms, in the integrated form such as Ardhanārīśvara, and in forms where one is merged in the other. Śrīdevī is also understood as merged in the form of Dakṣiṇāmūrti. The Dakṣiṇāmūrti idea continues in the following names."],"searchText":"725 दक्षिणामूर्तिरूपिणी शिवस्य दक्षिणाभिमुखी मूर्तिर्ब्रह्मनारायणादेरध्यापकत्वेन प्रसिद्धा। यस्या मन्त्रास्तन्त्रेषु प्रसिद्धाः स एव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। शिवस्य — of śiva दक्षिणाभिमुखी — south-facing दक्षिणामूर्तिरूपिणी means one who is in the form of dakṣiṇāmūrti. dakṣiṇāmūrti teaches the principle of non-duality. śiva and śrīdevī appear in individual forms, in the integrated form such as ardhanārīśvara, and in forms where one is merged in the other. śrīdevī is also understood as merged in the form of dakṣiṇāmūrti. the dakṣiṇāmūrti idea continues in the following names. the soul of the silent teacher: dakṣiṇāmūrti is lord śiva sitting in absolute silence under the banyan tree, instructing the ancient rishis through unuttered resonance. this name reveals that she is non-different from this supreme masculine teaching form. she is the internal illumination, the code, and the processing power that allows that silent instruction to break open inside the disciple's mind.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Silent Teacher: Dakṣiṇāmūrti is Lord Śiva sitting in absolute silence under the banyan tree, instructing the ancient rishis through unuttered resonance. This name reveals that She is non-different from this supreme masculine teaching form. She is the internal illumination, the code, and the processing power that allows that silent instruction to break open inside the disciple's mind."]},{"number":726,"name":"सनकादिसमाराध्या","samasa":["सनकसनन्दनादिभिः सम्यगाराध्योपास्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सनकादिसमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by Sanaka and other sages. The four sages Sanaka, Sanandana, Sanātana and Sanatkumāra contemplated Śrīdevī in the form of Dakṣiṇāmūrti and received instruction from Śiva. These sages are the mind-born sons of Brahmā, great yogins and highly knowledgeable disciples. They are included in the lineage of teachers and are known in connection with the Samaya method of Śrīvidyā worship."],"searchText":"726 सनकादिसमाराध्या सनकसनन्दनादिभिः सम्यगाराध्योपास्या। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सनकादिसमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by sanaka and other sages. the four sages sanaka, sanandana, sanātana and sanatkumāra contemplated śrīdevī in the form of dakṣiṇāmūrti and received instruction from śiva. these sages are the mind-born sons of brahmā, great yogins and highly knowledgeable disciples. they are included in the lineage of teachers and are known in connection with the samaya method of śrīvidyā worship. the meditation of the primeval ascetics: sages like sanaka represent the absolute pinnacle of lifelong celibacy, internal detachment, and unshakeable absorption in brahman. their intense adoration (samārādhyā) indicates that she is not a deity sought merely for temporary worldly gain, but the ultimate, non-dual absolute targeted by the most advanced ascetics in existence.","esoteric":["The Meditation of the Primeval Ascetics: Sages like Sanaka represent the absolute pinnacle of lifelong celibacy, internal detachment, and unshakeable absorption in Brahman. Their intense adoration (samārādhyā) indicates that She is not a deity sought merely for temporary worldly gain, but the ultimate, non-dual absolute targeted by the most advanced ascetics in existence."]},{"number":727,"name":"शिवज्ञानप्रदायिनी","samasa":["शिवविषयकं ज्ञानं प्रकर्षेण दत्ते।","शिवो ज्ञानप्रदायी यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रकर्षेण — excellently; fully","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["शिवज्ञानप्रदायिनी means one who bestows knowledge relating to Śiva. Śiva means auspiciousness; She gives the knowledge of Brahman. The pure and peaceful Śiva can be known only through Śrīdevī, His vibratory power. It may also be understood that Śiva gives knowledge about Śrīdevī. This continues the Dakṣiṇāmūrti meaning of the previous name."],"searchText":"727 शिवज्ञानप्रदायिनी शिवविषयकं ज्ञानं प्रकर्षेण दत्ते। शिवो ज्ञानप्रदायी यस्याः सा। प्रकर्षेण — excellently; fully यस्याः — whose; of whom शिवज्ञानप्रदायिनी means one who bestows knowledge relating to śiva. śiva means auspiciousness; she gives the knowledge of brahman. the pure and peaceful śiva can be known only through śrīdevī, his vibratory power. it may also be understood that śiva gives knowledge about śrīdevī. this continues the dakṣiṇāmūrti meaning of the previous name. the granting of absolute awakening: the individual soul can know many relative sciences, but it remains bound until it uncovers the true nature of śiva (pure consciousness). she acts as śivajñānapradāyinī, directly delivering this supreme, non-dual realization. she reveals śiva, vanishing the illusion of separation and initiating final liberation.","esoteric":["The Granting of Absolute Awakening: The individual soul can know many relative sciences, but it remains bound until it uncovers the true nature of Śiva (pure consciousness). She acts as Śivajñānapradāyinī, directly delivering this supreme, non-dual realization. She reveals Śiva, vanishing the illusion of separation and initiating final liberation."]},{"number":728,"name":"चित्कला","samasa":["चिदेव कला सच्चिदानन्दात्मनो ब्रह्मण एकदेश इव यस्यां सा।","अन्तःकरणोपाधिकं चैतन्यं निरुपाधिकायाश्चितः कला एकदेश इति।"],"wordByWord":["कला — part; digit; aspect"],"summary":["चित्कला means one who is with divine consciousness. Cit means knowledge or consciousness, and kalā means a part. Brahman cannot be fully objectified, but Sat, Cit and Ānanda are spoken of as its inseparable aspects. Here She is the Cit aspect. The consciousness present in the inner self of the soul is described as a part of Brahman; She is that Cit-kalā."],"searchText":"728 चित्कला चिदेव कला सच्चिदानन्दात्मनो ब्रह्मण एकदेश इव यस्यां सा। अन्तःकरणोपाधिकं चैतन्यं निरुपाधिकायाश्चितः कला एकदेश इति। कला — part; digit; aspect चित्कला means one who is with divine consciousness. cit means knowledge or consciousness, and kalā means a part. brahman cannot be fully objectified, but sat, cit and ānanda are spoken of as its inseparable aspects. here she is the cit aspect. the consciousness present in the inner self of the soul is described as a part of brahman; she is that cit-kalā. the dynamic ray of awareness: while the absolute brahman is completely unconditioned and still, citkalā is that specialized, highly kinetic ray of awareness that steps down to illuminate the internal cognitive apparatus (antaḥkaraṇa-upādhika-caitanya). she is the active intelligence that allows living beings to process thought, perceive life, and sense existence.","esoteric":["The Dynamic Ray of Awareness: While the absolute Brahman is completely unconditioned and still, Citkalā is that specialized, highly kinetic ray of awareness that steps down to illuminate the internal cognitive apparatus (antaḥkaraṇa-upādhika-caitanya). She is the active intelligence that allows living beings to process thought, perceive life, and sense existence."]},{"number":729,"name":"आनन्दकलिका","samasa":["आनन्द एव कलैकदेश इव यस्याः सा।","जीवगतानन्दैकदेशरूपा।","(स्वार्थे कः)।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["आनन्दकलिका means one who is the bud of divine bliss. As the consciousness of the soul is a part of Brahman-consciousness, the bliss of the soul is a part of Brahman-bliss. She is the form of supreme bliss, Sat-cit-ānanda. Kalikā means a bud. The bliss latent in the soul is like a bud that can, at the proper time, open into supreme bliss."],"searchText":"729 आनन्दकलिका आनन्द एव कलैकदेश इव यस्याः सा। जीवगतानन्दैकदेशरूपा। (स्वार्थे कः)। यस्याः — whose; of whom आनन्दकलिका means one who is the bud of divine bliss. as the consciousness of the soul is a part of brahman-consciousness, the bliss of the soul is a part of brahman-bliss. she is the form of supreme bliss, sat-cit-ānanda. kalikā means a bud. the bliss latent in the soul is like a bud that can, at the proper time, open into supreme bliss. the blossom of joy: the unconditioned bliss of brahman is massive and shoreless. inside individual living beings (jīvas), this joy is experienced as a tiny, subtle fraction—a delicate bud of happiness (ānanda-aika-deśa-rūpā) that breaks open during moments of deep love or peace. she is that exact internal blossom of joy, waiting to expand into full cosmic realization.","esoteric":["The Blossom of Joy: The unconditioned bliss of Brahman is massive and shoreless. Inside individual living beings (Jīvas), this joy is experienced as a tiny, subtle fraction—a delicate bud of happiness (ānanda-aika-deśa-rūpā) that breaks open during moments of deep love or peace. She is that exact internal blossom of joy, waiting to expand into full cosmic realization."]},{"number":730,"name":"प्रेमरूपा","samasa":["प्रेम स्नेहो भक्तिरेव स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रेम — love","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["प्रेमरूपा means one who is in the form of love. The love or devotion of the devotees towards Her is indicated as Śrīdevī herself. Love takes different names according to its object: devotion towards elders, love towards equals, affection towards children. She is present in all these forms."],"searchText":"730 प्रेमरूपा प्रेम स्नेहो भक्तिरेव स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। प्रेम — love यस्याः — whose; of whom प्रेमरूपा means one who is in the form of love. the love or devotion of the devotees towards her is indicated as śrīdevī herself. love takes different names according to its object: devotion towards elders, love towards equals, affection towards children. she is present in all these forms. pure devotion incarnate: she does not simply feel affection or receive love. her entire essential substance is nothing but pure, unadulterated divine love itself (prema-svarūpa). this love is the absolute emotional expression of non-duality—the intense attraction that pulls the fragment back into the whole, comforting the seeker that the heart of reality is pure love.","esoteric":["Pure Devotion Incarnate: She does not simply feel affection or receive love. Her entire essential substance is nothing but pure, unadulterated divine love itself (Prema-svarūpa). This love is the absolute emotional expression of non-duality—the intense attraction that pulls the fragment back into the whole, comforting the seeker that the heart of reality is pure love."]},{"number":731,"name":"प्रियङ्करी","samasa":["प्रियं करोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["प्रियं — dear; desired"],"summary":["प्रियङ्करी means one who grants what is dear to Her devotees. She gives what devotees seek, according to their inner disposition, whether enjoyment or liberation. As soul-consciousness, She causes interest in worldly objects through the senses, and also gives the knowledge that even this interest arises because of the Self."],"searchText":"731 प्रियङ्करी प्रियं करोतीति। प्रियं — dear; desired प्रियङ्करी means one who grants what is dear to her devotees. she gives what devotees seek, according to their inner disposition, whether enjoyment or liberation. as soul-consciousness, she causes interest in worldly objects through the senses, and also gives the knowledge that even this interest arises because of the self. the engine of universal delight: she is priyaṅkarī because her dynamic operations are naturally formatted to project what is ultimately beneficial, pleasing, and evolutionary for all living beings. she does not design systemic cruelty; her baseline nature works to convert the friction of existence into deep, soul-level comfort and alignment.","esoteric":["The Engine of Universal Delight: She is Priyaṅkarī because Her dynamic operations are naturally formatted to project what is ultimately beneficial, pleasing, and evolutionary for all living beings. She does not design systemic cruelty; Her baseline nature works to convert the friction of existence into deep, soul-level comfort and alignment."]},{"number":732,"name":"नामपारायणप्रीता","samasa":["नामपारायणाभ्यां प्रीता।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["नामपारायणप्रीता means one who is pleased with the recitation of Her names. Here nāma may indicate this Sahasranāma itself. The fruits of such recitation are explained in the result section. Different modes of pārāyaṇa are taught in the tradition and are regarded as secret and powerful means to approach Śrīdevī. Laghustuti and Devī Bhāgavatam are cited in connection with the formation and recitation of sacred names."],"searchText":"732 नामपारायणप्रीता नामपारायणाभ्यां प्रीता। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. नामपारायणप्रीता means one who is pleased with the recitation of her names. here nāma may indicate this sahasranāma itself. the fruits of such recitation are explained in the result section. different modes of pārāyaṇa are taught in the tradition and are regarded as secret and powerful means to approach śrīdevī. laghustuti and devī bhāgavatam are cited in connection with the formation and recitation of sacred names. the sonic alignment: a pārāyaṇa is not a casual, distracted chanting; it is the highly structured, continuous, and focused verbal layout of divine phonic names from start to finish. she is deeply pleased by this process because the systematic vibration of her names clears the colored filters of the practitioner's mind, perfectly tuning their internal environment to receive her light.","esoteric":["The Sonic Alignment: A Pārāyaṇa is not a casual, distracted chanting; it is the highly structured, continuous, and focused verbal layout of divine phonic names from start to finish. She is deeply pleased by this process because the systematic vibration of Her names clears the colored filters of the practitioner's mind, perfectly tuning their internal environment to receive Her light."]},{"number":733,"name":"नन्दिविद्या","samasa":["नन्दिनो नन्दिकेश्वरस्य विद्या तदुपासितविद्या।"],"wordByWord":["विद्या — knowledge; mantra"],"summary":["नन्दिविद्या means one who is in the form of the mantra taught by Nandikeśvara. Among the sages connected with Śrīvidyā, Nandi is also counted along with Manu, Candra, Kubera, Lopāmudrā, Agastya, Agni, Sūrya, Indra, Skanda, Śiva and others."],"searchText":"733 नन्दिविद्या नन्दिनो नन्दिकेश्वरस्य विद्या तदुपासितविद्या। विद्या — knowledge; mantra नन्दिविद्या means one who is in the form of the mantra taught by nandikeśvara. among the sages connected with śrīvidyā, nandi is also counted along with manu, candra, kubera, lopāmudrā, agastya, agni, sūrya, indra, skanda, śiva and others. the nandikeśvara lineage: within the structural history of śrīvidyā, lord nandi stands as one of the premier master seers who received the core mantra directly from shiva and formatted a highly revered operational tradition (nandividyā). she is the literal phonic substance and target of this lineage, ensuring the protection of its initiatory keys.","esoteric":["The Nandikeśvara Lineage: Within the structural history of Śrīvidyā, Lord Nandi stands as one of the premier master seers who received the core mantra directly from Shiva and formatted a highly revered operational tradition (Nandividyā). She is the literal phonic substance and target of this lineage, ensuring the protection of its initiatory keys."]},{"number":734,"name":"नटेश्वरी","samasa":["नटेश्वरस्येयमिति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["नटेश्वरी means one who is the consort of Naṭeśa. This means She is the consort of Naṭarāja, who dances in Chidambara. Chidambara may mean the sacred place or the ether of the heart. She dances together with Naṭeśa, as indicated in the Soundaryalaharī verse describing the dance of Śiva and Śakti."],"searchText":"734 नटेश्वरी नटेश्वरस्येयमिति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. नटेश्वरी means one who is the consort of naṭeśa. this means she is the consort of naṭarāja, who dances in chidambara. chidambara may mean the sacred place or the ether of the heart. she dances together with naṭeśa, as indicated in the soundaryalaharī verse describing the dance of śiva and śakti. the rhythm behind the dancer: lord śiva as naṭeśvara executes the cosmic dance of creation, preservation, and dissolution (tāṇḍava). she is naṭeśvarī — his non-dual dynamic energy. she provides the structural rhythm, the stage, and the kinetic power that allows the cosmic dance to unfold, remaining the silent witness to every movement.","esoteric":["The Rhythm behind the Dancer: Lord Śiva as Naṭeśvara executes the cosmic dance of creation, preservation, and dissolution (Tāṇḍava). She is Naṭeśvarī — His non-dual dynamic energy. She provides the structural rhythm, the stage, and the kinetic power that allows the cosmic dance to unfold, remaining the silent witness to every movement."]},{"number":735,"name":"मिथ्याजगदधिष्ठाना","samasa":["मिथ्यारूपस्य जगतोऽधिष्ठानं भानाधिकरणं रजतस्येव शुक्तिः। (गुणत्रयापचयविवक्षया स्त्रीलिङ्गम्।)","जगदधिष्ठानरूपं ब्रह्मैव अनः प्राणो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["मिथ्याजगदधिष्ठाना means one who is the substratum of the falsely appearing world. Just as a shell is mistaken for silver until true knowledge arises, the changing universe appears on the real substratum, Śrīdevī as the Supreme Being. Scriptural statements are cited to show that duality is ultimately illusory and that the Supreme alone is real. This name can also be interpreted as She whose breath is Brahman, the support of the universe. In the tantric view, the universe is not different from Brahman, just as a pot is not different from clay; perceived difference is only apparent."],"searchText":"735 मिथ्याजगदधिष्ठाना मिथ्यारूपस्य जगतोऽधिष्ठानं भानाधिकरणं रजतस्येव शुक्तिः। (गुणत्रयापचयविवक्षया स्त्रीलिङ्गम्।) जगदधिष्ठानरूपं ब्रह्मैव अनः प्राणो यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom मिथ्याजगदधिष्ठाना means one who is the substratum of the falsely appearing world. just as a shell is mistaken for silver until true knowledge arises, the changing universe appears on the real substratum, śrīdevī as the supreme being. scriptural statements are cited to show that duality is ultimately illusory and that the supreme alone is real. this name can also be interpreted as she whose breath is brahman, the support of the universe. in the tantric view, the universe is not different from brahman, just as a pot is not different from clay; perceived difference is only apparent. the reality behind the appearance: in classical philosophy, an illusion requires a real base to appear—just as a silver illusion (rajata) requires the actual mother-of-pearl shell (śukti) beneath it. the material universe is mithyā (transient, relative, and non-permanent). she is mithyājagadadhiṣṭhānā because she is the absolute, unchanging consciousness baseline that supports this entire changing projection, allowing it to be perceived.","esoteric":["The Reality behind the Appearance: In classical philosophy, an illusion requires a real base to appear—just as a silver illusion (rajata) requires the actual mother-of-pearl shell (śukti) beneath it. The material universe is mithyā (transient, relative, and non-permanent). She is Mithyājagadadhiṣṭhānā because She is the absolute, unchanging consciousness baseline that supports this entire changing projection, allowing it to be perceived."]},{"number":736,"name":"मुक्तिदा","samasa":["मुक्तिं मोक्षं ददातीति मुक्तिदा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["मुक्तिदा means one who gives liberation. The Purāṇas say that those desirous of freedom should seek refuge in Parvatī, Parameśvarī, the Self of all beings and of Śiva. Those who worship the supreme Śakti, whether by regular or irregular methods, do not remain bound in saṃsāra; they are indeed liberated."],"searchText":"736 मुक्तिदा मुक्तिं मोक्षं ददातीति मुक्तिदा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. मुक्तिदा means one who gives liberation. the purāṇas say that those desirous of freedom should seek refuge in parvatī, parameśvarī, the self of all beings and of śiva. those who worship the supreme śakti, whether by regular or irregular methods, do not remain bound in saṃsāra; they are indeed liberated. the dispenser of ultimate freedom: worldly achievements provide localized, temporary transitions. she acts as muktidā, directly bestowing the absolute gift of final spiritual liberation. she forcefully cuts the core ignorance that anchors the soul to the wheel of rebirth, returning the practitioner to their pristine state of baseline consciousness.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of Ultimate Freedom: Worldly achievements provide localized, temporary transitions. She acts as Muktidā, directly bestowing the absolute gift of final spiritual liberation. She forcefully cuts the core ignorance that anchors the soul to the wheel of rebirth, returning the practitioner to their pristine state of baseline consciousness."]},{"number":737,"name":"मुक्तिरूपिणी","samasa":["मुक्तिरेव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["मुक्तिरूपिणी means one who is the form of liberation itself. Liberation is not merely an external result but the manifestation of one's own bliss when ignorance is removed. The true nature of the Self is hidden by ignorance; when that ignorance goes, the self-bliss shines forth. She is that true bliss. Knowledge does not create liberation; it reveals the Self that was veiled."],"searchText":"737 मुक्तिरूपिणी मुक्तिरेव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. मुक्तिरूपिणी means one who is the form of liberation itself. liberation is not merely an external result but the manifestation of one's own bliss when ignorance is removed. the true nature of the self is hidden by ignorance; when that ignorance goes, the self-bliss shines forth. she is that true bliss. knowledge does not create liberation; it reveals the self that was veiled. identity with freedom: lest a student think that she is an external entity who simply hands over a reward called liberation, this name establishes that her very body is nothing but liberation itself (mukti-svarūpa). realizing her person is identical to entering the state of unconditioned, boundless freedom.","esoteric":["Identity with Freedom: Lest a student think that She is an external entity who simply hands over a reward called liberation, this name establishes that Her very body is nothing but liberation itself (Mukti-svarūpa). Realizing Her person is identical to entering the state of unconditioned, boundless freedom."]},{"number":738,"name":"लास्यप्रिया","samasa":["लास्यं नर्तनं प्रियं यस्याः सा।","तालैर्नृत्यगीतयोः समकालपरिच्छेदो वा लयः।","तस्य करी कर्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["प्रियं — dear; desired","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["लास्यप्रिया means one who is fond of dance. The dance performed by women is called lāsya, while male dance is called tāṇḍava. Śrīdevī Herself dances and is also pleased with the dance of others. As in royal courts and temples, dance and music are offered before the Empress Śrīdevī. She is pleased by dance performed with rhythm, song and devotion."],"searchText":"738 लास्यप्रिया लास्यं नर्तनं प्रियं यस्याः सा। तालैर्नृत्यगीतयोः समकालपरिच्छेदो वा लयः। तस्य करी कर्त्री। प्रियं — dear; desired यस्याः — whose; of whom लास्यप्रिया means one who is fond of dance. the dance performed by women is called lāsya, while male dance is called tāṇḍava. śrīdevī herself dances and is also pleased with the dance of others. as in royal courts and temples, dance and music are offered before the empress śrīdevī. she is pleased by dance performed with rhythm, song and devotion. the joy of harmonious expression: while the masculine tāṇḍava represents fierce, destructive kinetic velocity, लास्य (lāsya) represents the highly refined, graceful, and harmonizing dance frequency associated with creation and nourishment. she is deeply affectionate toward this gentle expression, reflecting her mode of uplifting the cosmos through pure grace.","esoteric":["The Joy of Harmonious Expression: While the masculine Tāṇḍava represents fierce, destructive kinetic velocity, लास्य (Lāsya) represents the highly refined, graceful, and harmonizing dance frequency associated with creation and nourishment. She is deeply affectionate toward this gentle expression, reflecting Her mode of uplifting the cosmos through pure grace."]},{"number":739,"name":"लयकरी","samasa":["लयश्चित्तावस्थाविशेषः।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["लयकरी means one who causes absorption. Laya is a special state of mind, greater than ordinary meditation. When the mind becomes wholly absorbed in seeing, hearing or contemplation, it forgets everything else. Such absorption in the Supreme Being is granted by Her. Laya also refers to the measured time of music and dance; She is that form also."],"searchText":"739 लयकरी लयश्चित्तावस्थाविशेषः। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. लयकरी means one who causes absorption. laya is a special state of mind, greater than ordinary meditation. when the mind becomes wholly absorbed in seeing, hearing or contemplation, it forgets everything else. such absorption in the supreme being is granted by her. laya also refers to the measured time of music and dance; she is that form also. cosmic dissolution: she safely draws the manifest universe back into its unmanifest source during the grand collapse. rhythmic absorption: she acts as the soul of time-keeping (laya) that binds music and dance into harmony. mental stillness: for the practitioner, she coordinates that unique, quiet state of consciousness (citta-avasthā-viśeṣa) where all cognitive ripples dissolve, leading to deep samādhi.","esoteric":["Cosmic Dissolution: She safely draws the manifest universe back into its unmanifest source during the grand collapse.","Rhythmic Absorption: She acts as the soul of time-keeping (laya) that binds music and dance into harmony.","Mental Stillness: For the practitioner, She coordinates that unique, quiet state of consciousness (citta-avasthā-viśeṣa) where all cognitive ripples dissolve, leading to deep Samādhi."]},{"number":740,"name":"लज्जा","samasa":["या देवी सर्वभूतेषु लज्जारूपेण संस्थितेति स्मरणाल्लज्जा।","हृल्लेखाबीजस्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["लज्जा means one who is in the form of modesty. Modesty or shyness is an important quality, especially of devoted women, and is described as a form of Śrīdevī. The Saptashatī praises the Goddess abiding in all beings as modesty. The word Hrīṃ is connected with modesty and is an important bīja of Śrīdevī. Thus lajjā also points cryptically to that bīja."],"searchText":"740 लज्जा या देवी सर्वभूतेषु लज्जारूपेण संस्थितेति स्मरणाल्लज्जा। हृल्लेखाबीजस्वरूपा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. लज्जा means one who is in the form of modesty. modesty or shyness is an important quality, especially of devoted women, and is described as a form of śrīdevī. the saptashatī praises the goddess abiding in all beings as modesty. the word hrīṃ is connected with modesty and is an important bīja of śrīdevī. thus lajjā also points cryptically to that bīja. the shield of internal discernment: as celebrated in the devī māhātmya, she resides in all living beings as the natural property of modesty (lajjā), acting as an internal moral compass that restrains base, animalistic tendencies. the core seed of the heart: in secret śrīvidyā grammar, lajjā is a highly guarded code name for the supreme हृल्लेखा बीज (hṛllekhā bīja — the sound ह्रीं / hrīṁ). she is the direct acoustic reality of this core sound, which serves as the cleansing engine of the heart center.","esoteric":["The Shield of Internal Discernment: As celebrated in the Devī Māhātmya, She resides in all living beings as the natural property of modesty (Lajjā), acting as an internal moral compass that restrains base, animalistic tendencies.","The Core Seed of the Heart: In secret Śrīvidyā grammar, Lajjā is a highly guarded code name for the supreme हृल्लेखा बीज (Hṛllekhā Bīja — the sound ह्रीं / Hrīṁ). She is the direct acoustic reality of this core sound, which serves as the cleansing engine of the heart center."]},{"number":741,"name":"रम्भादिवन्दिता","samasa":["रम्भोर्वश्यादिभिरप्सरोभिर्वन्दिता।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["रम्भादिवन्दिता means one who is adored by Rambhā and other celestial damsels. From this name onwards the beautiful form of Śrīdevī is described in a series of names."],"searchText":"741 रम्भादिवन्दिता रम्भोर्वश्यादिभिरप्सरोभिर्वन्दिता। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. रम्भादिवन्दिता means one who is adored by rambhā and other celestial damsels. from this name onwards the beautiful form of śrīdevī is described in a series of names. sovereignty over aesthetic radiance: celestial nymphs (apsaras) represent the peak expression of sensory attraction, grace, and vital beauty across the heavenly planes. their continuous adoration at her feet establishes her status as the original source of all allure and kinetic charm. she coordinates the parameters of beauty while remaining untouched by sensory delusion.","esoteric":["Sovereignty over Aesthetic Radiance: Celestial nymphs (apsaras) represent the peak expression of sensory attraction, grace, and vital beauty across the heavenly planes. Their continuous adoration at Her feet establishes Her status as the original source of all allure and kinetic charm. She coordinates the parameters of beauty while remaining untouched by sensory delusion."]},{"number":742,"name":"भवदावसुधावृष्टिः","samasa":["भवः संसार एव दावो वनवह्निस्तस्य शामकत्वात्सुधावृष्टिः पीयूषवर्षमिव।","भवः संसार एव दावोऽरण्यम्। तस्य पुङ्खानुपुङ्खतया उज्जीवनात्पीयूषवृष्टिरिव।","भवं परशिवं दत्ते वसु रत्नं धनं च धत्ते एतादृशी वृष्टिरिति त्रिपदं नाम वा।"],"wordByWord":["भवः — worldly existence","दत्ते — gives","नाम — name"],"summary":["भवदावसुधावृष्टिः means one who is the rain of nectar falling on the forest-fire of worldly existence. Bhava means worldly existence and dāva means forest fire. She is the nectar-rain that extinguishes that fire. The name may also be split to mean She who grants Śiva, wealth and auspicious abundance. For the great devotees of Śrīdevī, both enjoyment and liberation are available by Her grace."],"searchText":"742 भवदावसुधावृष्टिः भवः संसार एव दावो वनवह्निस्तस्य शामकत्वात्सुधावृष्टिः पीयूषवर्षमिव। भवः संसार एव दावोऽरण्यम्। तस्य पुङ्खानुपुङ्खतया उज्जीवनात्पीयूषवृष्टिरिव। भवं परशिवं दत्ते वसु रत्नं धनं च धत्ते एतादृशी वृष्टिरिति त्रिपदं नाम वा। भवः — worldly existence दत्ते — gives नाम — name भवदावसुधावृष्टिः means one who is the rain of nectar falling on the forest-fire of worldly existence. bhava means worldly existence and dāva means forest fire. she is the nectar-rain that extinguishes that fire. the name may also be split to mean she who grants śiva, wealth and auspicious abundance. for the great devotees of śrīdevī, both enjoyment and liberation are available by her grace. the extinguisher of rebirth: under the primary track, the cyclical friction of worldly existence (bhava) is a blazing forest fire (dāva) burning the bound soul. her downpour of non-dual nectar (sudhā-vṛṣṭi) cools this internal panic. the nourisher of spirit: alternatively, the world is a parched forest; her nectar acts as the refreshing irrigation that brings dead spiritual channels back to life. under the split-word key, she functions as a continuous downpour that systematically delivers the direct realization of lord śiva alongside all material assets.","esoteric":["The Extinguisher of Rebirth: Under the primary track, the cyclical friction of worldly existence (Bhava) is a blazing forest fire (dāva) burning the bound soul. Her downpour of non-dual nectar (sudhā-vṛṣṭi) cools this internal panic.","The Nourisher of Spirit: Alternatively, the world is a parched forest; Her nectar acts as the refreshing irrigation that brings dead spiritual channels back to life. Under the split-word key, She functions as a continuous downpour that systematically delivers the direct realization of Lord Śiva alongside all material assets."]},{"number":743,"name":"पापारण्यदवानला","samasa":["पापान्येवारण्यानि दुःखजनकत्वात्। तेषां दवानल इव नाशकत्वात्।","पापारण्यानां दवानलो यस्या नाम सा।","पापारण्यानां ये दवाः दावाग्नयो नाशनोपायभूता उपास्त्यादयस्तेषां अनान् प्राणान् लाति आदत्ते तान् जीवयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["नाम — name"],"summary":["पापारण्यदवानला means one who is the forest fire that burns down the forest of sins. She destroys sins just as a forest fire consumes a forest. Sins such as prārabdha, sañcita and āgāmi cannot be destroyed merely by worldly enjoyment; by Her grace and true knowledge they are ruined. Remembering the feet of the supreme Śakti is taught as the highest expiation for sins committed knowingly or unknowingly."],"searchText":"743 पापारण्यदवानला पापान्येवारण्यानि दुःखजनकत्वात्। तेषां दवानल इव नाशकत्वात्। पापारण्यानां दवानलो यस्या नाम सा। पापारण्यानां ये दवाः दावाग्नयो नाशनोपायभूता उपास्त्यादयस्तेषां अनान् प्राणान् लाति आदत्ते तान् जीवयतीति। नाम — name पापारण्यदवानला means one who is the forest fire that burns down the forest of sins. she destroys sins just as a forest fire consumes a forest. sins such as prārabdha, sañcita and āgāmi cannot be destroyed merely by worldly enjoyment; by her grace and true knowledge they are ruined. remembering the feet of the supreme śakti is taught as the highest expiation for sins committed knowingly or unknowingly. the incineration of accumulated karmas: sins (pāpa) resemble a dense, dark, overgrown jungle because they form an interconnected tangle that creates existential blockages and blocks out the light of the self. she acts as davānalā—a high-velocity fire that leaves no branch unburned, reducing the seeker's historical load of negative impressions (saṁskāras) to pure ash.","esoteric":["The Incineration of Accumulated Karmas: Sins (pāpa) resemble a dense, dark, overgrown jungle because they form an interconnected tangle that creates existential blockages and blocks out the light of the Self. She acts as Davānalā—a high-velocity fire that leaves no branch unburned, reducing the seeker's historical load of negative impressions (saṁskāras) to pure ash."]},{"number":744,"name":"दौर्भाग्यतूलवातूला","samasa":["दौर्भाग्यमेव तूलं कार्पासं तस्य वातूल इव वात्येव दूरं निरासिकेति।","दौर्भाग्यं तूलं येषां ते दौर्भाग्यतूलाः दौर्भाग्यस्य तूलस्येव निरासका धर्मविशेषाः। अत एव ते धर्मा एव वातूले गौण्यावृत्त्या तेन दौर्भाग्यतूलः वातूला यस्याः सकाशात् सा।","दौर्भाग्यनिरासकानि कर्माणि यस्याः सकाशादुद्भवन्ति यस्याः सम्बन्धीनि वा सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["दौर्भाग्यतूलवातूला means one who is the cyclone that drives away the cotton-bundles of misfortune. Misfortune from actions of previous births may appear huge, like bundles of cotton, but Her force scatters it like a strong wind. The actions that remove such misfortune arise from Her and are connected with Her grace."],"searchText":"744 दौर्भाग्यतूलवातूला दौर्भाग्यमेव तूलं कार्पासं तस्य वातूल इव वात्येव दूरं निरासिकेति। दौर्भाग्यं तूलं येषां ते दौर्भाग्यतूलाः दौर्भाग्यस्य तूलस्येव निरासका धर्मविशेषाः। अत एव ते धर्मा एव वातूले गौण्यावृत्त्या तेन दौर्भाग्यतूलः वातूला यस्याः सकाशात् सा। दौर्भाग्यनिरासकानि कर्माणि यस्याः सकाशादुद्भवन्ति यस्याः सम्बन्धीनि वा सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom दौर्भाग्यतूलवातूला means one who is the cyclone that drives away the cotton-bundles of misfortune. misfortune from actions of previous births may appear huge, like bundles of cotton, but her force scatters it like a strong wind. the actions that remove such misfortune arise from her and are connected with her grace. the cyclone of auspiciousness: misfortune (daurbhāgya) has no solid ontological reality; it is merely a weightless collection of negative conditions, like cotton flakes (tūla). she acts as a powerful whirlwind (vātūlā), blowing these scattered blocks entirely out of the practitioner's path, replacing structural obstacles with instant alignment.","esoteric":["The Cyclone of Auspiciousness: Misfortune (daurbhāgya) has no solid ontological reality; it is merely a weightless collection of negative conditions, like cotton flakes (tūla). She acts as a powerful whirlwind (vātūlā), blowing these scattered blocks entirely out of the practitioner's path, replacing structural obstacles with instant alignment."]},{"number":745,"name":"जराध्वान्तरविप्रभा","samasa":["जरैव ध्वान्तमन्धकारं तस्य नाशकत्वाद्रवेः प्रभेव।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["जराध्वान्तरविप्रभा means one who removes the darkness of old age by Her light. Childhood, youth and old age belong to the body, not to the eternal Self. When the knowledge that body and soul are different arises, the fear of old age and death is removed. She is like the sunlight that removes the darkness called old age."],"searchText":"745 जराध्वान्तरविप्रभा जरैव ध्वान्तमन्धकारं तस्य नाशकत्वाद्रवेः प्रभेव। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. जराध्वान्तरविप्रभा means one who removes the darkness of old age by her light. childhood, youth and old age belong to the body, not to the eternal self. when the knowledge that body and soul are different arises, the fear of old age and death is removed. she is like the sunlight that removes the darkness called old age. the ray of timeless vitality: jarā represents the dark creeping rust of time, decay, mental fog, and biological slowing down that veils the body's internal radiance. she is raviprabhā — the blinding, rejuvenating morning sun ray that cuts through this internal stagnation, restoring the pristine, timeless vitality of pure consciousness inside the subtle matrix.","esoteric":["The Ray of Timeless Vitality: Jarā represents the dark creeping rust of time, decay, mental fog, and biological slowing down that veils the body's internal radiance. She is Raviprabhā — the blinding, rejuvenating morning sun ray that cuts through this internal stagnation, restoring the pristine, timeless vitality of pure consciousness inside the subtle matrix."]},{"number":746,"name":"भाग्याब्धिचन्द्रिका","samasa":["भाग्यलक्षणस्याब्धेरुल्लासकत्वाच्चन्द्रिका कौमुदीव।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["भाग्याब्धिचन्द्रिका means one who is the moonlight that illumines the ocean of good fortune. Good fortune comes from virtue done in previous births. When others recognise a person's good fortune, the joy swells like the ocean under moonlight. By Her compassion, She makes the good fortune of Her devotees expand and become recognised."],"searchText":"746 भाग्याब्धिचन्द्रिका भाग्यलक्षणस्याब्धेरुल्लासकत्वाच्चन्द्रिका कौमुदीव। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. भाग्याब्धिचन्द्रिका means one who is the moonlight that illumines the ocean of good fortune. good fortune comes from virtue done in previous births. when others recognise a person's good fortune, the joy swells like the ocean under moonlight. by her compassion, she makes the good fortune of her devotees expand and become recognised. the tidal surge of grace: when the full moon shines, the ocean naturally experiences massive gravitational tidal surges. similarly, when her moon-like light (candrikā) rises inside the practitioner's consciousness, the dormant ocean of inner spiritual and material merit (bhāgya) expands dramatically, flooding the entire system with active prosperity.","esoteric":["The Tidal Surge of Grace: When the full moon shines, the ocean naturally experiences massive gravitational tidal surges. Similarly, when Her moon-like light (Candrikā) rises inside the practitioner's consciousness, the dormant ocean of inner spiritual and material merit (bhāgya) expands dramatically, flooding the entire system with active prosperity."]},{"number":747,"name":"भक्तचित्तकेकिघनाघना","samasa":["भक्तानां चित्तान्येव केकिनो मयूरास्तेषामुल्लासकत्वाद्घनाघना मेघस्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["भक्तचित्तकेकिघनाघना means one who is the cloud that excites the peacocks which are the minds of Her devotees. Just as peacocks dance when they see dark rainclouds, devotees' minds rejoice on seeing Śrīdevī. Her continuous life-work nourishes the devotees spiritually, like rainclouds sustaining life."],"searchText":"747 भक्तचित्तकेकिघनाघना भक्तानां चित्तान्येव केकिनो मयूरास्तेषामुल्लासकत्वाद्घनाघना मेघस्वरूपा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. भक्तचित्तकेकिघनाघना means one who is the cloud that excites the peacocks which are the minds of her devotees. just as peacocks dance when they see dark rainclouds, devotees' minds rejoice on seeing śrīdevī. her continuous life-work nourishes the devotees spiritually, like rainclouds sustaining life. the relief of the monsoon: peacocks suffer during the hot summer months and burst into ecstatic dance the exact moment they hear the first low thunder of a dark monsoon rain-cloud (ghanāghana). the devotee's mind, parched by the anxieties of worldly life, experiences this exact cooling relief upon her entry, bursting into natural, joyous spiritual alignment.","esoteric":["The Relief of the Monsoon: Peacocks suffer during the hot summer months and burst into ecstatic dance the exact moment they hear the first low thunder of a dark monsoon rain-cloud (ghanāghana). The devotee's mind, parched by the anxieties of worldly life, experiences this exact cooling relief upon Her entry, bursting into natural, joyous spiritual alignment."]},{"number":748,"name":"रोगपर्वतदम्भोलिः","samasa":["रोगा एव पर्वताः स्थूलत्वात्तेषां दम्भोलिर्वज्र इव।"],"wordByWord":["पर्वताः — mountains"],"summary":["रोगपर्वतदम्भोलिः means one who is the thunderbolt that strikes the mountain of diseases. Diseases are compared to mountains, and Śrīdevī to Indra's thunderbolt that can shatter them. This recalls the name Sarvavyādhi-praśamanī, the pacifier of all diseases."],"searchText":"748 रोगपर्वतदम्भोलिः रोगा एव पर्वताः स्थूलत्वात्तेषां दम्भोलिर्वज्र इव। पर्वताः — mountains रोगपर्वतदम्भोलिः means one who is the thunderbolt that strikes the mountain of diseases. diseases are compared to mountains, and śrīdevī to indra's thunderbolt that can shatter them. this recalls the name sarvavyādhi-praśamanī, the pacifier of all diseases. the shattering of disease vectors: chronic physical illnesses and deep-seated subconscious mental complexes behave like massive, unmoving stone mountains (parvata), blocking path progression. she is the piercing, high-voltage diamond thunderbolt (dambholi — indra's vajra) that strikes these structural densities, shattering the root vectors of disease instantly.","esoteric":["The Shattering of Disease Vectors: Chronic physical illnesses and deep-seated subconscious mental complexes behave like massive, unmoving stone mountains (parvata), blocking path progression. She is the piercing, high-voltage diamond thunderbolt (Dambholi — Indra's Vajra) that strikes these structural densities, shattering the root vectors of disease instantly."]},{"number":749,"name":"मृत्युदारुकुठारिका","samasa":["मृत्युरूपदारूणां कुठारा इव।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["मृत्युदारुकुठारिका means one who is the axe that cuts down the tree of death. Death and related pains grow like a tree rooted in birth and time; She cuts it down like an axe. A devotee who firmly thinks, \"I worship Śrīdevī and will gain liberation,\" is freed from the fear of death. Therefore death is aptly compared to a tree and Śrīdevī to the axe."],"searchText":"749 मृत्युदारुकुठारिका मृत्युरूपदारूणां कुठारा इव। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. मृत्युदारुकुठारिका means one who is the axe that cuts down the tree of death. death and related pains grow like a tree rooted in birth and time; she cuts it down like an axe. a devotee who firmly thinks, \"i worship śrīdevī and will gain liberation,\" is freed from the fear of death. therefore death is aptly compared to a tree and śrīdevī to the axe. the cutter of the rebirth trunk: physical death (mṛtyu) is the heavy, stubborn log framework that keeps the soul trapped in the engine of rebirth. as kuṭhārikā, she strikes directly at the base root of this wood, slicing the illusion of mortality cleanly away and anchoring the practitioner in non-dual permanence.","esoteric":["The Cutter of the Rebirth Trunk: Physical death (Mṛtyu) is the heavy, stubborn log framework that keeps the soul trapped in the engine of rebirth. As Kuṭhārikā, She strikes directly at the base root of this wood, slicing the illusion of mortality cleanly away and anchoring the practitioner in non-dual permanence."]},{"number":750,"name":"महेश्वरी","samasa":["महती च सेश्वरी च।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great"],"summary":["महेश्वरी means one who is the supreme sovereign. This name differs from the earlier Māheśvarī by the long and short form of the vowel, and therefore is not a mere repetition."],"searchText":"750 महेश्वरी महती च सेश्वरी च। महती — great महेश्वरी means one who is the supreme sovereign. this name differs from the earlier māheśvarī by the long and short form of the vowel, and therefore is not a mere repetition. sovereignty past the lesser gods: a local ruler governs a territory; the secondary deities govern specific cosmic departments. she is maheśvarī because her sovereign rule (īśvaritva) is completely unbounded (mahat). she stands as the absolute, non-dual empress who formats the laws of nature, directs the motion of universes, and acts as the supreme consort of maheśvara, sealing all cosmic authority directly to her person.","esoteric":["Sovereignty Past the Lesser Gods: A local ruler governs a territory; the secondary deities govern specific cosmic departments. She is Maheśvarī because Her sovereign rule (Īśvaritva) is completely unbounded (Mahat). She stands as the absolute, non-dual empress who formats the laws of nature, directs the motion of universes, and acts as the supreme consort of Maheśvara, sealing all cosmic authority directly to Her person."]},{"number":751,"name":"महाकाली","samasa":["महती च सा काली च।","महाकालस्य स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["महती — great","सा — she","काली — Kālī","महाकालस्य — of Mahākāla"],"summary":["महाकाली means one who is great and in the form of Kāli. Kāli may mean She who determines time; Mahākāli determines even the time of Yama, the deity of death. She is worshipped as Mahākāli, the consort of Mahākāla, and as the deity of the first story of Saptashatī. In Her fierce form She appears dark. Death itself is explained as an act of compassion that temporarily releases beings from the bondage of action and prepares the way for peace and future growth."],"searchText":"751 महाकाली महती च सा काली च। महाकालस्य स्त्री। महती — great सा — she काली — kālī महाकालस्य — of mahākāla महाकाली means one who is great and in the form of kāli. kāli may mean she who determines time; mahākāli determines even the time of yama, the deity of death. she is worshipped as mahākāli, the consort of mahākāla, and as the deity of the first story of saptashatī. in her fierce form she appears dark. death itself is explained as an act of compassion that temporarily releases beings from the bondage of action and prepares the way for peace and future growth. the devourer of time: mahākāla is the supreme aspect of consciousness that dissolves the entire universe at the end of an epoch. she is mahākālī because she is the dynamic kinetic capacity that acts as the container and consumer of even that ultimate time-principle. she marks the final absolute rest state where all temporal mutations return to stillness.","esoteric":["The Devourer of Time: Mahākāla is the supreme aspect of consciousness that dissolves the entire universe at the end of an epoch. She is Mahākālī because She is the dynamic kinetic capacity that acts as the container and consumer of even that ultimate time-principle. She marks the final absolute rest state where all temporal mutations return to stillness."]},{"number":752,"name":"महाग्रासा","samasa":["महानपरिमितो ग्रासः कवलो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["ग्रासः — mouthful; devouring","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["महाग्रासा means one who is the great devourer. The Upaniṣad speaks of Brahmins and Kṣatriyas as food and death as condiment for the Supreme. At dissolution She, as the supreme consuming power, swallows the universe and the thirty-six tattvas."],"searchText":"752 महाग्रासा महानपरिमितो ग्रासः कवलो यस्याः सा। ग्रासः — mouthful; devouring यस्याः — whose; of whom महाग्रासा means one who is the great devourer. the upaniṣad speaks of brahmins and kṣatriyas as food and death as condiment for the supreme. at dissolution she, as the supreme consuming power, swallows the universe and the thirty-six tattvas. the single morsel of creation: during the grand dissolution (mahāpralaya), the creation of names, forms, elements, and structural spatial coordinates is not dissolved slowly or with friction. she takes the entire multi-dimensional cosmos as a single, effortless mouthful (grāsa), absorbing it completely back into her non-dual unmanifested matrix.","esoteric":["The Single Morsel of Creation: During the grand dissolution (mahāpralaya), the creation of names, forms, elements, and structural spatial coordinates is not dissolved slowly or with friction. She takes the entire multi-dimensional cosmos as a single, effortless mouthful (grāsa), absorbing it completely back into Her non-dual unmanifested matrix."]},{"number":753,"name":"महाशना","samasa":["महच्चराचरकर्मकत्वादशनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["महाशना means one who is a great eater. Continuing the previous name, She consumes the entire animate and inanimate universe. This name differs from the earlier Mahāsanā and should not be confused with it."],"searchText":"753 महाशना महच्चराचरकर्मकत्वादशनं यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom महाशना means one who is a great eater. continuing the previous name, she consumes the entire animate and inanimate universe. this name differs from the earlier mahāsanā and should not be confused with it. this reinforces her ultimate consuming authority: the absolute appetite: complementing mahāgrāsā, she is mahāśanā because her ultimate consumption (aśana) encompasses the entire created universe. nothing is left over as waste matter outside her field; every single spark of objective appearance is digested, showing her status as the unified final terminal for all cosmic properties.","esoteric":["this reinforces Her ultimate consuming authority:","The Absolute Appetite: Complementing Mahāgrāsā, She is Mahāśanā because Her ultimate consumption (aśana) encompasses the entire created universe. Nothing is left over as waste matter outside Her field; every single spark of objective appearance is digested, showing Her status as the unified final terminal for all cosmic properties."]},{"number":754,"name":"अपर्णा","samasa":["अपगतमृणं यस्याः सा।","पर्णं पतनमिति नैरुक्तात्पतनरहितेति।","पर्णमप्यदनीयत्वेन न विद्यते यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["अपर्णा means one who is without debt, or one who ate not even a leaf. She gives more than devotees expect and is therefore not indebted to them. As Pārvatī, while performing penance to marry Śiva, She did not eat even a leaf; hence the name Aparṇā. The name may also mean one without falling or decline."],"searchText":"754 अपर्णा अपगतमृणं यस्याः सा। पर्णं पतनमिति नैरुक्तात्पतनरहितेति। पर्णमप्यदनीयत्वेन न विद्यते यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom अपर्णा means one who is without debt, or one who ate not even a leaf. she gives more than devotees expect and is therefore not indebted to them. as pārvatī, while performing penance to marry śiva, she did not eat even a leaf; hence the name aparṇā. the name may also mean one without falling or decline. the pinnacle of tapas: historically, during her intense tapas to fuse with shiva, she abandoned consuming even fallen leaves (parṇa). the fallless substratum: under the etymological track, parṇa denotes falling (patana); she is entirely free from falling into spatial or temporal degradation. the debtless absolute: she has no outstanding liabilities or cosmic debts (ṛṇa), existing completely secure in her independent status.","esoteric":["The Pinnacle of Tapas: Historically, during Her intense tapas to fuse with Shiva, She abandoned consuming even fallen leaves (parṇa).","The Fallless Substratum: Under the etymological track, parṇa denotes falling (patana); She is entirely free from falling into spatial or temporal degradation.","The Debtless Absolute: She has no outstanding liabilities or cosmic debts (ṛṇa), existing completely secure in Her independent status."]},{"number":755,"name":"चण्डिका","samasa":["अभक्तेषु कोपनत्वात् चण्डयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["अभक्तेषु — towards non-devotees"],"summary":["चण्डिका means one who is fierce or angry. She is angry with those who lack devotion. Anger is also described as a characteristic of Brahman in certain scriptural passages. In Saptashatī the combined form of Mahākāli, Mahālakṣmī and Mahāsarasvatī is called Caṇḍikā."],"searchText":"755 चण्डिका अभक्तेषु कोपनत्वात् चण्डयतीति। अभक्तेषु — towards non-devotees चण्डिका means one who is fierce or angry. she is angry with those who lack devotion. anger is also described as a characteristic of brahman in certain scriptural passages. in saptashatī the combined form of mahākāli, mahālakṣmī and mahāsarasvatī is called caṇḍikā. the fierce filter of justice: her anger is not a mundane psychological distortion. she is caṇḍikā because she expresses an intense, high-velocity defensive fury (caṇḍatva) directed specifically at unrighteous entities and stubborn internal blockages (abhaktas). this fierce light tears down the structures of ego, providing the necessary shocks to realign the soul.","esoteric":["The Fierce Filter of Justice: Her anger is not a mundane psychological distortion. She is Caṇḍikā because She expresses an intense, high-velocity defensive fury (caṇḍatva) directed specifically at unrighteous entities and stubborn internal blockages (abhaktas). This fierce light tears down the structures of ego, providing the necessary shocks to realign the soul."]},{"number":756,"name":"चण्डमुण्डासुरनिषूदिनी","samasa":["चण्डश्च मुण्डश्च, तौ च तावसुरौ च, तौ निषूदयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["चण्डमुण्डासुरनिषूदिनी means one who destroyed the demons Caṇḍa and Muṇḍa. In the form of Kālī, She destroyed the demons Caṇḍa and Muṇḍa of the group of Śumbha and Niśumbha; hence She was named Cāmuṇḍā. Other Purāṇic explanations also connect the name Cāmuṇḍā with the slaying of demons and the carrying of their heads. This name recalls one of the forms among the eight mothers."],"searchText":"756 चण्डमुण्डासुरनिषूदिनी चण्डश्च मुण्डश्च, तौ च तावसुरौ च, तौ निषूदयतीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. चण्डमुण्डासुरनिषूदिनी means one who destroyed the demons caṇḍa and muṇḍa. in the form of kālī, she destroyed the demons caṇḍa and muṇḍa of the group of śumbha and niśumbha; hence she was named cāmuṇḍā. other purāṇic explanations also connect the name cāmuṇḍā with the slaying of demons and the carrying of their heads. this name recalls one of the forms among the eight mothers. the extraction of passion and delusion: in the internal battlefield of the mind, चण्ड represents the violent force of aggressive passion (rajas), and मुण्ड represents the low, stubborn weight of intellectual blindness and delusion (tamas). as niṣūdinī, she extracts these twin root distortions from the subconscious channels, freeing the practitioner's path.","esoteric":["The Extraction of Passion and Delusion: In the internal battlefield of the mind, चण्ड represents the violent force of aggressive passion (Rajas), and मुण्ड represents the low, stubborn weight of intellectual blindness and delusion (Tamas). As Niṣūdinī, She extracts these twin root distortions from the subconscious channels, freeing the practitioner's path."]},{"number":757,"name":"क्षराक्षरात्मिका","samasa":["क्षराण्यनियतसंख्यान्यक्षराणि वर्णानि आत्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।","क्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते। तदुभयमात्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वर्णानि — letters","आत्मा — self; essence","यस्याः — whose; of whom","क्षरः — perishable","सर्वाणि — all"],"summary":["क्षराक्षरात्मिका means one whose form is both the perishable and the imperishable. It may mean She is the form of countless letters or syllables, since mantras are formed from letters. It may also mean She is the Self of both kṣara, the changing beings, and akṣara, the unchanging principle. Thus She is the one and many, the source of mantra and the basis of all beings."],"searchText":"757 क्षराक्षरात्मिका क्षराण्यनियतसंख्यान्यक्षराणि वर्णानि आत्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। क्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते। तदुभयमात्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। वर्णानि — letters आत्मा — self; essence यस्याः — whose; of whom क्षरः — perishable सर्वाणि — all क्षराक्षरात्मिका means one whose form is both the perishable and the imperishable. it may mean she is the form of countless letters or syllables, since mantras are formed from letters. it may also mean she is the self of both kṣara, the changing beings, and akṣara, the unchanging principle. thus she is the one and many, the source of mantra and the basis of all beings. the encompasser of perishable and imperishable: kṣara represents the changing, material world of moving elements; akṣara represents the still, changeless, and hidden spiritual witness (kūṭastha). she is kṣarākṣarātmikā because both conditions are expressions of her non-dual body, acting as the bridge that synthesizes form and formlessness.","esoteric":["The Encompasser of Perishable and Imperishable: Kṣara represents the changing, material world of moving elements; Akṣara represents the still, changeless, and hidden spiritual witness (Kūṭastha). She is Kṣarākṣarātmikā because both conditions are expressions of Her non-dual body, acting as the bridge that synthesizes form and formlessness."]},{"number":758,"name":"सर्वलोकेशी","samasa":["सर्वेषां लोकानामीशी ईश्वरी।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["सर्वलोकेशी means one who is the ruler of all worlds. All lokas are under Her authority; She is their sovereign mistress."],"searchText":"758 सर्वलोकेशी सर्वेषां लोकानामीशी ईश्वरी। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. सर्वलोकेशी means one who is the ruler of all worlds. all lokas are under her authority; she is their sovereign mistress. universal imperial sovereignty: her administrative authority is not bounded by a single solar system or isolated dimension. she rules over the complete multi-dimensional network of the fourteen operational worlds (sarva-loka), directing their laws of karma and evolutionary paths with neutral accuracy.","esoteric":["Universal Imperial Sovereignty: Her administrative authority is not bounded by a single solar system or isolated dimension. She rules over the complete multi-dimensional network of the fourteen operational worlds (sarva-loka), directing their laws of karma and evolutionary paths with neutral accuracy."]},{"number":759,"name":"विश्वधारिणी","samasa":["विश्वं धारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["विश्वधारिणी means one who supports the universe. The whole universe is borne, sustained and held by Her power."],"searchText":"759 विश्वधारिणी विश्वं धारयतीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. विश्वधारिणी means one who supports the universe. the whole universe is borne, sustained and held by her power. the structural pillar of existence: the universe does not hang in a vacuum by chance. she is viśvadhāriṇī because her dynamic energy field acts as the permanent, invisible structural support that holds planetary spheres, gravity metrics, and spatial dimensions perfectly in place, preventing cosmic collapse.","esoteric":["The Structural Pillar of Existence: The universe does not hang in a vacuum by chance. She is Viśvadhāriṇī because Her dynamic energy field acts as the permanent, invisible structural support that holds planetary spheres, gravity metrics, and spatial dimensions perfectly in place, preventing cosmic collapse."]},{"number":760,"name":"त्रिवर्गदात्री","samasa":["त्रयाणां धर्मार्थकामानां वर्गः समूहः। (त्रिवर्गो धर्मकामार्थैश्चतुर्वर्गः समोक्षकैरित्यमरः)। तस्य दात्री।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["त्रिवर्गदात्री means one who gives the threefold aims of life. Trivarga means dharma, artha and kāma. She grants these worldly aims. Since mokṣa has already been described separately, this name here points especially to the three aims connected with worldly life."],"searchText":"760 त्रिवर्गदात्री त्रयाणां धर्मार्थकामानां वर्गः समूहः। (त्रिवर्गो धर्मकामार्थैश्चतुर्वर्गः समोक्षकैरित्यमरः)। तस्य दात्री। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. त्रिवर्गदात्री means one who gives the threefold aims of life. trivarga means dharma, artha and kāma. she grants these worldly aims. since mokṣa has already been described separately, this name here points especially to the three aims connected with worldly life. the organization of earthly aspiration: before a soul is ready for final liberation (mokṣa), it requires balanced evolution across the three mundane planes: धर्म (moral alignment), अर्थ (material stability), and काम (refined desire). she systematically dispenses the resources for this triple framework (trivarga), ensuring her children do not experience unnatural lack during their earthly journey.","esoteric":["The Organization of Earthly Aspiration: Before a soul is ready for final liberation (Mokṣa), it requires balanced evolution across the three mundane planes: धर्म (moral alignment), अर्थ (material stability), and काम (refined desire). She systematically dispenses the resources for this triple framework (trivarga), ensuring Her children do not experience unnatural lack during their earthly journey."]},{"number":761,"name":"सुभगा","samasa":["शोभना श्रीकाममाहात्म्यवीर्ययत्नकीर्त्यादयो भगाः यस्यां सा।","शोभनो भगः सूर्यो यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["शोभना — auspicious; beautiful","भगाः — fortunes; powers"],"summary":["सुभगा means one who is supremely fortunate and bestows auspicious affluence. Bhaga includes prosperity, desire, greatness, power, effort and fame. All affluence in moving and unmoving beings is due to Her. Worship of auspicious women is an important part of Śrīvidyā practice because Śrīdevī Herself is present in such auspiciousness."],"searchText":"761 सुभगा शोभना श्रीकाममाहात्म्यवीर्ययत्नकीर्त्यादयो भगाः यस्यां सा। शोभनो भगः सूर्यो यया सा। शोभना — auspicious; beautiful भगाः — fortunes; powers सुभगा means one who is supremely fortunate and bestows auspicious affluence. bhaga includes prosperity, desire, greatness, power, effort and fame. all affluence in moving and unmoving beings is due to her. worship of auspicious women is an important part of śrīvidyā practice because śrīdevī herself is present in such auspiciousness. *, the six divine splendors: classical lexicon rules define bhaga as a corporate set of six attributes: absolute wealth, virtue, fame, beauty, wisdom, and effortless intent. she is subhagā because she contains these traits in their most refined condition. the solar engine: alternatively, she is the inner consciousness that gives the sun (bhaga) its brilliant capacity to illuminate worlds.","esoteric":["*,","The Six Divine Splendors: Classical lexicon rules define Bhaga as a corporate set of six attributes: absolute wealth, virtue, fame, beauty, wisdom, and effortless intent. She is Subhagā because She contains these traits in their most refined condition.","The Solar Engine: Alternatively, She is the inner consciousness that gives the sun (Bhaga) its brilliant capacity to illuminate worlds."]},{"number":762,"name":"त्र्यम्बका","samasa":["त्रीण्यम्बकानि नेत्राणि यस्याः सा।","त्रयाणां ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्राणामम्बिका माता।"],"wordByWord":["नेत्राणि — eyes","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["त्र्यम्बका means one who is three-eyed. Her three eyes are the Sun, Moon and Fire. The same meaning is conveyed in the names Trinayanā and Trilocanā. She may also be understood as the mother of the three gods, Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra."],"searchText":"762 त्र्यम्बका त्रीण्यम्बकानि नेत्राणि यस्याः सा। त्रयाणां ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्राणामम्बिका माता। नेत्राणि — eyes यस्याः — whose; of whom त्र्यम्बका means one who is three-eyed. her three eyes are the sun, moon and fire. the same meaning is conveyed in the names trinayanā and trilocanā. she may also be understood as the mother of the three gods, brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra. the vision past linear time: her three eyes correspond to the sun, the moon, and fire, scanning past, present, and future simultaneously. the parent of the trinity: under the second precise track, अम्बका means mother. she is tryambakā because she is the original maternal source (ambikā) that gives birth to and formats the entire administrative trinity of the cosmos—brahmā, viṣṇu, and rudra.","esoteric":["The Vision Past Linear Time: Her three eyes correspond to the Sun, the Moon, and Fire, scanning past, present, and future simultaneously.","The Parent of the Trinity: Under the second precise track, अम्बका means mother. She is Tryambakā because She is the original maternal source (Ambikā) that gives birth to and formats the entire administrative trinity of the cosmos—Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and Rudra."]},{"number":763,"name":"त्रिगुणात्मिका","samasa":["त्रिगुणात्मिका सत्त्वरजस्तमोरूपगुणत्रयसाम्यविग्रहा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["त्रिगुणात्मिका means one who is in the form of the three guṇas: sattva, rajas and tamas. Since the three deities are connected with these three qualities, She includes them all. Though She manifests as the three guṇas, She is also described elsewhere as beyond guṇas."],"searchText":"763 त्रिगुणात्मिका त्रिगुणात्मिका सत्त्वरजस्तमोरूपगुणत्रयसाम्यविग्रहा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. त्रिगुणात्मिका means one who is in the form of the three guṇas: sattva, rajas and tamas. since the three deities are connected with these three qualities, she includes them all. though she manifests as the three guṇas, she is also described elsewhere as beyond guṇas. the matrix of material form: before the universe is structured, energy exists as a perfectly balanced, unmanifested equilibrium of the three qualities (guṇas). she is triguṇātmikā because her manifest body forms the very fabric of this triadic matrix, directing how light (sattva), movement (rajas), and mass (tamas) combine to weave the material universe.","esoteric":["The Matrix of Material Form: Before the universe is structured, energy exists as a perfectly balanced, unmanifested equilibrium of the three qualities (guṇas). She is Triguṇātmikā because Her manifest body forms the very fabric of this triadic matrix, directing how light (Sattva), movement (Rajas), and mass (Tamas) combine to weave the material universe."]},{"number":764,"name":"स्वर्गापवर्गदा","samasa":["क्षयिष्णु सुखं वर्गः। नित्यं तु सुखमपवर्गः। तदुभयं दत्ते इति।"],"wordByWord":["दत्ते — gives"],"summary":["स्वर्गापवर्गदा means one who bestows heaven and liberation. Heaven is happiness earned by righteous deeds, but it is not permanent. When accumulated merit is exhausted, one returns to mortal life. Apavarga means permanent liberation. She grants both."],"searchText":"764 स्वर्गापवर्गदा क्षयिष्णु सुखं वर्गः। नित्यं तु सुखमपवर्गः। तदुभयं दत्ते इति। दत्ते — gives स्वर्गापवर्गदा means one who bestows heaven and liberation. heaven is happiness earned by righteous deeds, but it is not permanent. when accumulated merit is exhausted, one returns to mortal life. apavarga means permanent liberation. she grants both. fulfillment of all degrees of joy: svarga represents the temporary, structural rewards achieved through virtuous action in the higher planes. apavarga represents the permanent, non-dual bliss of final awakening. she acts as the singular portal for both paths, giving the appropriate worldly experience to the relative seeker and absolute liberation to the advanced ascetic.","esoteric":["Fulfillment of All Degrees of Joy: Svarga represents the temporary, structural rewards achieved through virtuous action in the higher planes. Apavarga represents the permanent, non-dual bliss of final awakening. She acts as the singular portal for both paths, giving the appropriate worldly experience to the relative seeker and absolute liberation to the advanced ascetic."]},{"number":765,"name":"शुद्धा","samasa":["आविद्यकमालिन्यशून्या।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["शुद्धा means one who is ever pure. She is free from the impurity called ignorance. In truth She is the form of knowledge."],"searchText":"765 शुद्धा आविद्यकमालिन्यशून्या। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. शुद्धा means one who is ever pure. she is free from the impurity called ignorance. in truth she is the form of knowledge. untouched by cosmic ignorance: material entities gather stains and undergo decay due to time and contact. she is śuddhā because her essential nature stands completely free from the ultimate stain—आविद्यकमालिन्य (āvidyaka-mālinya — the structural rust of cosmic ignorance or illusion). she remains eternally pristine, clear, and unblemished.","esoteric":["Untouched by Cosmic Ignorance: Material entities gather stains and undergo decay due to time and contact. She is Śuddhā because Her essential nature stands completely free from the ultimate stain—आविद्यकमालिन्य (āvidyaka-mālinya — the structural rust of cosmic ignorance or illusion). She remains eternally pristine, clear, and unblemished."]},{"number":766,"name":"जपापुष्पनिभाकृतिः","samasa":["जपापुष्पनिभा ओड्रपुष्पेण तुल्या आकृतिः स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["आकृतिः — form","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["जपापुष्पनिभाकृतिः means one whose form is like the hibiscus flower. The red colour of Śrīdevī is mentioned in many names and in the meditation verse. The name may also be interpreted through Ajapā, the natural mantra of breath, pointing to the union of Śiva and Śakti."],"searchText":"766 जपापुष्पनिभाकृतिः जपापुष्पनिभा ओड्रपुष्पेण तुल्या आकृतिः स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। आकृतिः — form यस्याः — whose; of whom जपापुष्पनिभाकृतिः means one whose form is like the hibiscus flower. the red colour of śrīdevī is mentioned in many names and in the meditation verse. the name may also be interpreted through ajapā, the natural mantra of breath, pointing to the union of śiva and śakti. the effulgence of kinetic grace: the hibiscus flower possesses a unique, intensely deep red radiance. this visual profile represents the concentrated energy of विमर्शशक्ति (vimarśa-śakti — active self-awareness) overflowing with creative compassion. meditating on this crimson geometry burns away internal dark lethargy, realigning the practitioner's channels with dynamic clarity.","esoteric":["The Effulgence of Kinetic Grace: The hibiscus flower possesses a unique, intensely deep red radiance. This visual profile represents the concentrated energy of विमर्शशक्ति (Vimarśa-śakti — active self-awareness) overflowing with creative compassion. Meditating on this crimson geometry burns away internal dark lethargy, realigning the practitioner's channels with dynamic clarity."]},{"number":767,"name":"ओजोवती","samasa":["ओजः अष्टमधातुः इन्द्रियसामर्थ्यं तेजः बलम् दीप्तिः च अस्यां सन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["ओजः — vital energy","बलम् — strength","दीप्तिः — radiance"],"summary":["ओजोवती means one who possesses ojas, the vitality of the body. Ojas is the vital essence that protects the body in times of difficulty. It also means light, strength, splendour and radiance; She possesses all these."],"searchText":"767 ओजोवती ओजः अष्टमधातुः इन्द्रियसामर्थ्यं तेजः बलम् दीप्तिः च अस्यां सन्तीति। ओजः — vital energy बलम् — strength दीप्तिः — radiance ओजोवती means one who possesses ojas, the vitality of the body. ojas is the vital essence that protects the body in times of difficulty. it also means light, strength, splendour and radiance; she possesses all these. the soul of the eighth tissue: in classical physiology, ojas is the ultimate, highly refined eighth tissue matrix (अष्टमधातु) that distills from the processing of all other bodily fluids. it acts as the root of immune resilience, sensory capacity, and mental brilliance. she is the internal structural intelligence that animates this vital reserve, keeping life vibrant.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Eighth Tissue: In classical physiology, Ojas is the ultimate, highly refined eighth tissue matrix (अष्टमधातु) that distills from the processing of all other bodily fluids. It acts as the root of immune resilience, sensory capacity, and mental brilliance. She is the internal structural intelligence that animates this vital reserve, keeping life vibrant."]},{"number":768,"name":"द्युतिधरा","samasa":["धरतीति धरा। द्युतेः कान्तेर्धरा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["द्युतिधरा means one who bears splendour. The brightness arising from the satisfaction of mind and body is called lustre, and She has that radiance. This recalls the earlier name Kāntimatī."],"searchText":"768 द्युतिधरा धरतीति धरा। द्युतेः कान्तेर्धरा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. द्युतिधरा means one who bears splendour. the brightness arising from the satisfaction of mind and body is called lustre, and she has that radiance. this recalls the earlier name kāntimatī. the pillar of luminous aura: she does not simply receive external light rays. she is dyutidharā because she acts as the active container and sustainer of the universal aura (kānti). every luminous frequency projected by the stars, fire, or awakened human intellects is a ray supported by her field.","esoteric":["The Pillar of Luminous Aura: She does not simply receive external light rays. She is Dyutidharā because She acts as the active container and sustainer of the universal aura (kānti). Every luminous frequency projected by the stars, fire, or awakened human intellects is a ray supported by Her field."]},{"number":769,"name":"यज्ञरूपा","samasa":["यज्ञो वै विष्णुरिति श्रुतेः तदभिन्ना देवी यज्ञरूपा।","यज्ञ एव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["यज्ञरूपा means one who is the embodiment of sacrifice. The five sacrifices prescribed for human beings are Deva-yajña, Pitṛ-yajña, Brahmā-yajña, Manuṣya-yajña and Bhūta-yajña; She is the form of all these. Offering knowledge and experience gained through the senses is also a jñāna-yajña, and She is that form. The Gītā and Veda also identify the highest forms of yajña with the divine."],"searchText":"769 यज्ञरूपा यज्ञो वै विष्णुरिति श्रुतेः तदभिन्ना देवी यज्ञरूपा। यज्ञ एव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. यज्ञरूपा means one who is the embodiment of sacrifice. the five sacrifices prescribed for human beings are deva-yajña, pitṛ-yajña, brahmā-yajña, manuṣya-yajña and bhūta-yajña; she is the form of all these. offering knowledge and experience gained through the senses is also a jñāna-yajña, and she is that form. the gītā and veda also identify the highest forms of yajña with the divine. identity with the sacrificial engine: the śruti explicitly declares “yajño vai viṣṇuḥ” (\"the sacrifice is indeed viṣṇu\"). she is yajñarūpā because she is non-different from this cosmic alignment mechanism. she is the intention, the action, the offering, and the alchemical transformation running through every holy rite, linking humanity to the absolute.","esoteric":["Identity with the Sacrificial Engine: The Śruti explicitly declares “Yajño vai Viṣṇuḥ” (\"The sacrifice is indeed Viṣṇu\"). She is Yajñarūpā because She is non-different from this cosmic alignment mechanism. She is the intention, the action, the offering, and the alchemical transformation running through every holy rite, linking humanity to the absolute."]},{"number":770,"name":"प्रियव्रता","samasa":["प्रियाणि व्रतान्यविशेषात्सर्वदेवताविषयकाणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["प्रियव्रता means one who is fond of vows. A vow is the determination to begin and complete an act, such as Ekādaśī, Ṣaṣṭhī or Varalakṣmī vrata. She is pleased with all vows, even those formally made to other deities, because the whole universe is Śiva-Śakti-maya."],"searchText":"770 प्रियव्रता प्रियाणि व्रतान्यविशेषात्सर्वदेवताविषयकाणि यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom प्रियव्रता means one who is fond of vows. a vow is the determination to begin and complete an act, such as ekādaśī, ṣaṣṭhī or varalakṣmī vrata. she is pleased with all vows, even those formally made to other deities, because the whole universe is śiva-śakti-maya. the affection for dedicated rules: she is priyavratā because she values the structural sincerity of the practitioner. it does not matter which entry-level deity a student targets; if they perform their vows (vrata) with continuous discipline and internal cleanliness, she accepts that focused energy, using it to clear their path toward non-dual awakening.","esoteric":["The Affection for Dedicated Rules: She is Priyavratā because She values the structural sincerity of the practitioner. It does not matter which entry-level deity a student targets; if they perform their vows (vrata) with continuous discipline and internal cleanliness, She accepts that focused energy, using it to clear their path toward non-dual awakening."]},{"number":771,"name":"दुराराध्या","samasa":["दुःखेन आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["दुःखेन — with difficulty"],"summary":["दुराराध्या means one who is difficult to worship. She is difficult for the incompetent, for those who cannot control the senses, and for the fickle-minded. Control of the senses and concentration of mind require great effort, and therefore Her worship is not easy for all."],"searchText":"771 दुराराध्या दुःखेन आराध्या। दुःखेन — with difficulty दुराराध्या means one who is difficult to worship. she is difficult for the incompetent, for those who cannot control the senses, and for the fickle-minded. control of the senses and concentration of mind require great effort, and therefore her worship is not easy for all. the filter against hypocrisy: she is not durārādhyā because she is harsh or unpredictable. rather, she cannot be accessed by superficial minds, deceptive intellects, or ostentatious public displays performed for vanity. her gate remains locked against egoic manipulation, requiring absolute internal transparency and intense, prolonged purification before swinging open.","esoteric":["The Filter against Hypocrisy: She is not Durārādhyā because She is harsh or unpredictable. Rather, She cannot be accessed by superficial minds, deceptive intellects, or ostentatious public displays performed for vanity. Her gate remains locked against egoic manipulation, requiring absolute internal transparency and intense, prolonged purification before swinging open."]},{"number":772,"name":"दुराधर्षा","samasa":["दुःखरूप आधर्षः स्वायत्तीकरणं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["दुराधर्षा means one who is hard to resist or subdue. She cannot be attracted by luxury or strength. She is attained only through devotion."],"searchText":"772 दुराधर्षा दुःखरूप आधर्षः स्वायत्तीकरणं यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom दुराधर्षा means one who is hard to resist or subdue. she cannot be attracted by luxury or strength. she is attained only through devotion. unconquerable by egoic assault: the individual ego often tries to conquer spiritual energy using aggressive manipulation, raw intellectual pride, or forced mechanical loops. she is durādharṣā because her field is completely unassailable. she bows to no external command, remaining independent (svātantrya) and accessible only through total surrender (prapatti).","esoteric":["Unconquerable by Egoic Assault: The individual ego often tries to conquer spiritual energy using aggressive manipulation, raw intellectual pride, or forced mechanical loops. She is Durādharṣā because Her field is completely unassailable. She bows to no external command, remaining independent (Svātantrya) and accessible only through total surrender (prapatti)."]},{"number":773,"name":"पाटलीकुसुमप्रिया","samasa":["पाटलीनामकं कुसुमं प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रियं — dear; desired","यस्याः — whose; of whom"],"summary":["पाटलीकुसुमप्रिया means one who is fond of the pāṭalī flower. This flower has a mixed red and white colour, suggesting the union of Śiva and Śakti. Other names also mention flowers dear to Śrīdevī, such as Kadamba, Campaka, Mandāra and the flower of consciousness."],"searchText":"773 पाटलीकुसुमप्रिया पाटलीनामकं कुसुमं प्रियं यस्याः सा। प्रियं — dear; desired यस्याः — whose; of whom पाटलीकुसुमप्रिया means one who is fond of the pāṭalī flower. this flower has a mixed red and white colour, suggesting the union of śiva and śakti. other names also mention flowers dear to śrīdevī, such as kadamba, campaka, mandāra and the flower of consciousness. the hue of balanced devotion: the pāṭalī flower exhibits a soft, pale-red or pink color metric. in tantric visualization, this specific shade represents a harmonious blending of intense devotion with quiet internal peace. offering this frequency back to her calms the practitioner's nervous system, realigning the heart channels.","esoteric":["The Hue of Balanced Devotion: The Pāṭalī flower exhibits a soft, pale-red or pink color metric. In Tantric visualization, this specific shade represents a harmonious blending of intense devotion with quiet internal peace. Offering this frequency back to Her calms the practitioner's nervous system, realigning the heart channels."]},{"number":774,"name":"महती","samasa":["परममहत्परिमाणत्वात्।","महान्कस्मान्मानेनान्याञ्जहतीति।","महनीयो भवतीति।","नारदमुनेर्वीणाविशेषो, तत्स्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["Word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above."],"summary":["महती means one who is very great. She is greater than the greatest, as indicated by the Upaniṣadic expression Mahato Mahīyān. Other things can be measured only through Her. The name also means one worthy of worship. Mahatī is also the name of Nārada's vīṇā; She is in that form also."],"searchText":"774 महती परममहत्परिमाणत्वात्। महान्कस्मान्मानेनान्याञ्जहतीति। महनीयो भवतीति। नारदमुनेर्वीणाविशेषो, तत्स्वरूपा। word meanings are read directly from the samāsa expression above. महती means one who is very great. she is greater than the greatest, as indicated by the upaniṣadic expression mahato mahīyān. other things can be measured only through her. the name also means one worthy of worship. mahatī is also the name of nārada's vīṇā; she is in that form also. the shoreless scale: she is mahatī because her metric of size represents absolute, infinite expansion, leaving nothing outside herself (मानेन अन्यान् जहतीति). the absolute object of worship: she commands automatic, timeless reverence from every tier of intelligence. the lute of resonance: mythologically, she is identical to the highly sacred lute (mahatī) played by sage nārada, acting as the soul of all spiritual harmonics.","esoteric":["The Shoreless Scale: She is Mahatī because Her metric of size represents absolute, infinite expansion, leaving nothing outside Herself (मानेन अन्यान् जहतीति).","The Absolute Object of Worship: She commands automatic, timeless reverence from every tier of intelligence.","The Lute of Resonance: Mythologically, She is identical to the highly sacred lute (Mahatī) played by Sage Nārada, acting as the soul of all spiritual harmonics."]},{"number":775,"name":"मेरुनिलया","samasa":["मेरुरेव निलयो यस्याः सा।","नवाक्षरो मन्त्रो मेरुपदवाच्यः स एव निलयः सर्वमन्त्रोद्भवस्थानं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose; of whom","निलयः — abode"],"summary":["मेरुनिलया means one who dwells in Meru. Meru is the golden mountain; Śrīdevī's Cintāmaṇi house is said to be on the central peak. After the destruction of Bhaṇḍāsura, the divine architects constructed the cities and abodes of Śrīdevī on the peaks and regions connected with Meru. In Śrīcakra worship, Meru-prastāra is one of the modes of contemplation, and She has that Meru as Her dwelling. Meru may also mean the nine-letter mantra from which all mantras arise, or the central point in a rosary or counting method; She dwells there also."],"searchText":"775 मेरुनिलया मेरुरेव निलयो यस्याः सा। नवाक्षरो मन्त्रो मेरुपदवाच्यः स एव निलयः सर्वमन्त्रोद्भवस्थानं यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose; of whom निलयः — abode मेरुनिलया means one who dwells in meru. meru is the golden mountain; śrīdevī's cintāmaṇi house is said to be on the central peak. after the destruction of bhaṇḍāsura, the divine architects constructed the cities and abodes of śrīdevī on the peaks and regions connected with meru. in śrīcakra worship, meru-prastāra is one of the modes of contemplation, and she has that meru as her dwelling. meru may also mean the nine-letter mantra from which all mantras arise, or the central point in a rosary or counting method; she dwells there also. the axis of the cosmos and mantras: geographically, she sits at the peak of mount meru, the golden center axis of planetary worlds. internally, meru corresponds to the vertical pillar of the suṣumṇā channel. critically, in high mantra grammar, meru refers to the supreme nine-syllabled code matrix that acts as the original source for all subsequent mantras. she sits at the absolute hub of this formula.","esoteric":["The Axis of the Cosmos and Mantras: Geographically, She sits at the peak of Mount Meru, the golden center axis of planetary worlds. Internally, Meru corresponds to the vertical pillar of the Suṣumṇā channel. Critically, in high mantra grammar, Meru refers to the supreme nine-syllabled code matrix that acts as the original source for all subsequent mantras. She sits at the absolute hub of this formula."]},{"number":776,"name":"मन्दारकुसुमप्रिया","samasa":["मन्दारो देवतरुः श्वेतार्को वा तस्य कुसुमं प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मन्दारो — Mandara tree or flower","देवतरुः — celestial tree","प्रियं — dear"],"summary":["मन्दारकुसुमप्रिया means one who is fond of Mandara flowers. Mandara is a celestial tree and is also identified with the white arka flower. Flowers used in worship represent pure and fragrant devotion offered to Śrīdevī. As She was earlier described as dwelling in Meru, the heavenly Mandara flower is fittingly mentioned as dear to Her."],"searchText":"776 मन्दारकुसुमप्रिया मन्दारो देवतरुः श्वेतार्को वा तस्य कुसुमं प्रियं यस्याः सा। मन्दारो — mandara tree or flower देवतरुः — celestial tree प्रियं — dear मन्दारकुसुमप्रिया means one who is fond of mandara flowers. mandara is a celestial tree and is also identified with the white arka flower. flowers used in worship represent pure and fragrant devotion offered to śrīdevī. as she was earlier described as dwelling in meru, the heavenly mandara flower is fittingly mentioned as dear to her. the ray of unfading light: the mandāra is a legendary tree of the heavenly worlds whose blossoms never fade. earthly liturgy maps it onto the highly potent śvetārka (white calotropis). this flower represents pure, uncorrupted, and resilient solar energy. offering this frequency back to her signifies the surrender of one's immortal potential, stabilizing the internal centers.","esoteric":["The Ray of Unfading Light: The Mandāra is a legendary tree of the heavenly worlds whose blossoms never fade. Earthly liturgy maps it onto the highly potent Śvetārka (white calotropis). This flower represents pure, uncorrupted, and resilient solar energy. Offering this frequency back to Her signifies the surrender of one's immortal potential, stabilizing the internal centers."]},{"number":777,"name":"वीराराध्या","samasa":["वीरैः आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["वीरैः — by heroes"],"summary":["वीराराध्या means one who is worshipped by heroes. Vira means a heroic worshipper, one who has steadiness, courage and fitness for the path of worship. Śrīdevī is adored by such qualified upasakas who are firm in practice and are not overcome by fear or weakness."],"searchText":"777 वीराराध्या वीरैः आराध्या। वीरैः — by heroes वीराराध्या means one who is worshipped by heroes. vira means a heroic worshipper, one who has steadiness, courage and fitness for the path of worship. śrīdevī is adored by such qualified upasakas who are firm in practice and are not overcome by fear or weakness. the path of heroic consecration: in agamic classification, practitioners are stratified into three temperaments: paśu (bound/animalistic), vīra (heroic/dynamic), and divya (divine/absorbed). she is vīrārādhyā because she is correctly approached through the वीर-भाव (vīra-bhāva) — the path of intense, courageous, and uncompromising internal discipline where the seeker treats their own egoic doubts as enemies to be crushed, fighting forward without fear.","esoteric":["The Path of Heroic Consecration: In Agamic classification, practitioners are stratified into three temperaments: Paśu (bound/animalistic), Vīra (heroic/dynamic), and Divya (divine/absorbed). She is Vīrārādhyā because She is correctly approached through the वीर-भाव (Vīra-bhāva) — the path of intense, courageous, and uncompromising internal discipline where the seeker treats their own egoic doubts as enemies to be crushed, fighting forward without fear."]},{"number":778,"name":"विराड्रूपा","samasa":["विराड् रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विराड् — cosmic form; Virat"],"summary":["विराड्रूपा means one whose form is the Virat. The Virat is the cosmic form, the gross universal body. All beings and worlds are included in that vast manifestation. Śrīdevī is not merely an individual deity-form; She is the universal form itself."],"searchText":"778 विराड्रूपा विराड् रूपं यस्याः सा। विराड् — cosmic form; virat विराड्रूपा means one whose form is the virat. the virat is the cosmic form, the gross universal body. all beings and worlds are included in that vast manifestation. śrīdevī is not merely an individual deity-form; she is the universal form itself. the visible garment of god: lest a practitioner think that she remains hidden only in secret unmanifested corners, this name establishes that the entire visible, physical universe—stars, mountains, oceans, and living shapes—is her macrocosmic body (virāṭ-sūtra). every atom seen is a cell of her physical form, proving her presence in the element layer.","esoteric":["The Visible Garment of God: Lest a practitioner think that She remains hidden only in secret unmanifested corners, this name establishes that the entire visible, physical universe—stars, mountains, oceans, and living shapes—is Her macrocosmic body (Virāṭ-sūtra). Every atom seen is a cell of Her physical form, proving Her presence in the element layer."]},{"number":779,"name":"विरजा","samasa":["विगतं रजः पापं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विगतं — gone; free from","रजः — rajas; dust; impurity; sin"],"summary":["विरजा means one who is free from rajas or impurity. Rajas may mean dust, passion, activity or sin. She is untouched by these impurities. She is pure consciousness, beyond the taint of karma and the agitations born of rajas."],"searchText":"779 विरजा विगतं रजः पापं यस्याः सा। विगतं — gone; free from रजः — rajas; dust; impurity; sin विरजा means one who is free from rajas or impurity. rajas may mean dust, passion, activity or sin. she is untouched by these impurities. she is pure consciousness, beyond the taint of karma and the agitations born of rajas. the spotless screen: रजस् (rajas) represents the dust of mental agitation, binding desires, and the stains of karmic impurity (pāpa). she is virajā because her essential nature is completely free from this friction. she remains an unblemished screen, allowing worlds to turn without gathering any dark residue.","esoteric":["The Spotless Screen: रजस् (Rajas) represents the dust of mental agitation, binding desires, and the stains of karmic impurity (pāpa). She is Virajā because Her essential nature is completely free from this friction. She remains an unblemished screen, allowing worlds to turn without gathering any dark residue."]},{"number":780,"name":"विश्वतोमुखी","samasa":["विश्वतः सर्वावच्छेदेन मुखं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वतः — on all sides","मुखं — face"],"summary":["विश्वतोमुखी means one whose face is everywhere. The name indicates that She faces all directions and is present in all forms. Nothing is outside Her awareness; all beings are seen, sustained and governed by Her."],"searchText":"780 विश्वतोमुखी विश्वतः सर्वावच्छेदेन मुखं यस्याः सा। विश्वतः — on all sides मुखं — face विश्वतोमुखी means one whose face is everywhere. the name indicates that she faces all directions and is present in all forms. nothing is outside her awareness; all beings are seen, sustained and governed by her. the omnidirectional portal: she does not possess a limited front or back orientation. as viśvatomukhī, she stands face-to-face with every single coordinate of the universe simultaneously (सर्वावच्छेदेन). wherever a devotee calls out, and whichever atom experiences a transition, she is already looking, listening, and interfacing at that exact spot, showcasing her omnipresence.","esoteric":["The Omnidirectional Portal: She does not possess a limited front or back orientation. As Viśvatomukhī, She stands face-to-face with every single coordinate of the universe simultaneously (सर्वावच्छेदेन). Wherever a devotee calls out, and whichever atom experiences a transition, She is already looking, listening, and interfacing at that exact spot, showcasing Her omnipresence."]},{"number":781,"name":"प्रत्यग्रूपा","samasa":["प्रत्यगवलोक्यमानं रूपं स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रत्यगवलोक्यमानं — component from the samasa above","रूपं — component from the samasa above","स्वरूपं — component from the samasa above","यस्याः — component from the samasa above","सा। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["प्रत्यग्रूपा means one whose form is the inner Self. Pratyag means inward or inner. Her real form is known by turning within. She is not merely an external object of worship but the innermost consciousness in the worshipper."],"searchText":"781 प्रत्यग्रूपा प्रत्यगवलोक्यमानं रूपं स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। प्रत्यगवलोक्यमानं — component from the samasa above रूपं — component from the samasa above स्वरूपं — component from the samasa above यस्याः — component from the samasa above सा। — component from the samasa above प्रत्यग्रूपा means one whose form is the inner self. pratyag means inward or inner. her real form is known by turning within. she is not merely an external object of worship but the innermost consciousness in the worshipper. the subjective core: most human tracking looks outward (parāñci) to process objects. she is pratyagrūpā because her form is discovered exclusively when the attention is turned 180 degrees backward, looking directly into the internal observer (pratyag-ātman). she is the ultimate inner subject, found by tracking the source of the \"i\" sensation.","esoteric":["The Subjective Core: Most human tracking looks outward (parāñci) to process objects. She is Pratyagrūpā because Her form is discovered exclusively when the attention is turned 180 degrees backward, looking directly into the internal observer (pratyag-ātman). She is the ultimate inner subject, found by tracking the source of the \"I\" sensation."]},{"number":782,"name":"पराकाशा","samasa":["पर उत्कृष्टश्चासावाकाशश्च।","पराकशब्दः कृच्छ्रविशेषवाचकः संस्तपोमात्रोपलक्षकः तस्य आशा दिक्।","परे उत्कृष्टे अके पापदुःखे अश्नाति नाशयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["पर — higher; supreme"],"summary":["पराकाशा means one who is the supreme ether. Akasha is space; Parakasha is the higher and subtler space beyond ordinary physical space. She is the supreme expanse of consciousness in which everything appears and into which everything resolves. The samasa also allows meanings connected with removal of sin and suffering through supreme tapas."],"searchText":"782 पराकाशा पर उत्कृष्टश्चासावाकाशश्च। पराकशब्दः कृच्छ्रविशेषवाचकः संस्तपोमात्रोपलक्षकः तस्य आशा दिक्। परे उत्कृष्टे अके पापदुःखे अश्नाति नाशयतीति। पर — higher; supreme पराकाशा means one who is the supreme ether. akasha is space; parakasha is the higher and subtler space beyond ordinary physical space. she is the supreme expanse of consciousness in which everything appears and into which everything resolves. the samasa also allows meanings connected with removal of sin and suffering through supreme tapas. the ultimate sky of spirit: she is the parākāśa — the pristine, unconditioned, and high-velocity space of pure consciousness (cidākāśa) that sits above and inside the material space element. the purifier of distress: alternatively, she functions as the absolute target of intense physical penance (parāka-tapas), and acts as the active force that devours (aśnati) the practitioner's stored sins and existential suffering (aka).","esoteric":["The Ultimate Sky of Spirit: She is the Parākāśa — the pristine, unconditioned, and high-velocity space of pure consciousness (Cidākāśa) that sits above and inside the material space element.","The Purifier of Distress: Alternatively, She functions as the absolute target of intense physical penance (parāka-tapas), and acts as the active force that devours (aśnati) the practitioner's stored sins and existential suffering (aka)."]},{"number":783,"name":"प्राणदा","samasa":["प्राणान् दत्ते इति।"],"wordByWord":["प्राणान् — life-breaths","दत्ते — gives"],"summary":["प्राणदा means one who gives life-breath. prāṇa is the vital force by which living beings function. Śrīdevī grants and sustains prana in all beings; life itself is Her gift."],"searchText":"783 प्राणदा प्राणान् दत्ते इति। प्राणान् — life-breaths दत्ते — gives प्राणदा means one who gives life-breath. prāṇa is the vital force by which living beings function. śrīdevī grants and sustains prana in all beings; life itself is her gift. the fountain of life: physical bodies are merely cold combinations of element matter until they are animated by the vital breaths (prāṇa). she is prāṇadā because she dispenses this underlying life-force currency, breathing her active energy into the biological shell to initiate heartbeat, breath, and sensory transmission.","esoteric":["The Fountain of Life: Physical bodies are merely cold combinations of element matter until they are animated by the vital breaths (prāṇa). She is Prāṇadā because She dispenses this underlying life-force currency, breathing Her active energy into the biological shell to initiate heartbeat, breath, and sensory transmission."]},{"number":784,"name":"प्राणरूपिणी","samasa":["प्राणः ब्रह्म रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्राणः — life-breath; vital force","ब्रह्म — Brahman"],"summary":["प्राणरूपिणी means one who is in the form of prana. prāṇa is also understood as Brahman in the scriptures. She is the life-principle itself, not merely the giver of life."],"searchText":"784 प्राणरूपिणी प्राणः ब्रह्म रूपं यस्याः सा। प्राणः — life-breath; vital force ब्रह्म — brahman प्राणरूपिणी means one who is in the form of prana. prāṇa is also understood as brahman in the scriptures. she is the life-principle itself, not merely the giver of life. identity with the life current: lest a student think she is a distant deity who simply hands over breath like a machine, this name establishes her body is the vital life current itself (prāṇa-svarūpa). every internal movement of energy running through the nāḍīs is the literal pulsing of her cosmic form inside the practitioner.","esoteric":["Identity with the Life Current: Lest a student think She is a distant deity who simply hands over breath like a machine, this name establishes Her body is the vital life current itself (Prāṇa-svarūpa). Every internal movement of energy running through the Nāḍīs is the literal pulsing of Her cosmic form inside the practitioner."]},{"number":785,"name":"मार्ताण्डभैरवाराध्या","samasa":["मार्ताण्डभैरवाभ्यामाराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["मार्ताण्डभैरवाभ्यामाराध्या। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["मार्ताण्डभैरवाराध्या means one who is worshipped by Martanda Bhairava. Martanda is connected with the Sun and Bhairava with the fierce form of Śiva. Even such powerful deities worship Her, showing Her supreme status in the tradition."],"searchText":"785 मार्ताण्डभैरवाराध्या मार्ताण्डभैरवाभ्यामाराध्या। मार्ताण्डभैरवाभ्यामाराध्या। — component from the samasa above मार्ताण्डभैरवाराध्या means one who is worshipped by martanda bhairava. martanda is connected with the sun and bhairava with the fierce form of śiva. even such powerful deities worship her, showing her supreme status in the tradition. adoration by the solar commander: mārtāṇḍa bhairava represents the high-velocity, blazing solar consciousness that commands the defense of the energetic grid. his adoration at her feet demonstrates that even the most brilliant, crushing solar forces in nature act as entry-level ministers submissive to her central throne.","esoteric":["Adoration by the Solar Commander: Mārtāṇḍa Bhairava represents the high-velocity, blazing solar consciousness that commands the defense of the energetic grid. His adoration at Her feet demonstrates that even the most brilliant, crushing solar forces in nature act as entry-level ministers submissive to Her central throne."]},{"number":786,"name":"मन्त्रिणीन्यस्तराज्यधूः","samasa":["मन्त्रिणः नयतीति मन्त्रिणी। तस्मिन् न्यस्ता राज्यस्य स्वसाम्राज्यरूपस्यैक्यरहस्यस्य धूः तज्जनकतावच्छेदको धर्मो यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["न्यस्ता — entrusted; placed","राज्यस्य — of kingdom"],"summary":["मन्त्रिणीन्यस्तराज्यधूः means one who placed the burden of the kingdom upon Mantriṇī. Mantriṇī, the minister-deity of Śrīdevī, is entrusted with the administration of Her empire. The name indicates the royal order of Śrīdevī's kingdom and the confidence with which She delegates the work of governance to Her ministerial power."],"searchText":"786 मन्त्रिणीन्यस्तराज्यधूः मन्त्रिणः नयतीति मन्त्रिणी। तस्मिन् न्यस्ता राज्यस्य स्वसाम्राज्यरूपस्यैक्यरहस्यस्य धूः तज्जनकतावच्छेदको धर्मो यया सा। न्यस्ता — entrusted; placed राज्यस्य — of kingdom मन्त्रिणीन्यस्तराज्यधूः means one who placed the burden of the kingdom upon mantriṇī. mantriṇī, the minister-deity of śrīdevī, is entrusted with the administration of her empire. the name indicates the royal order of śrīdevī's kingdom and the confidence with which she delegates the work of governance to her ministerial power. the delegation of governance: she sits at the absolute center of the śrī cakra as pure, unmoving, non-dual bliss. to run the heavy, complex mechanics of universe administration and scriptural instruction, she delegates the complete operational burden (dhura) to her trusted minister mantriṇī (goddess śyāmalā). this allows the practitioner to approach the minister first to gain clean access to the queen.","esoteric":["The Delegation of Governance: She sits at the absolute center of the Śrī Cakra as pure, unmoving, non-dual bliss. To run the heavy, complex mechanics of universe administration and scriptural instruction, She delegates the complete operational burden (dhura) to Her trusted minister Mantriṇī (Goddess Śyāmalā). This allows the practitioner to approach the minister first to gain clean access to the Queen."]},{"number":787,"name":"त्रिपुरेशी","samasa":["त्रिपुराणामीशी।","सर्वाशापरिपूरकचक्राधीश्वर्यास्त्रिपुरेशीति नाम। तदभेदादियमम्बापि।"],"wordByWord":["त्रिपुराणामीशी। — component from the samasa above","सर्वाशापरिपूरकचक्राधीश्वर्यास्त्रिपुरेशीति — component from the samasa above","नाम। — component from the samasa above","तदभेदादियमम्बापि। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["त्रिपुरेशी means one who is the ruler of Tripurā. Tripurā means the three cities, the three states, or the threefold universe. She is the sovereign of all triplicities and is identified with the Tripureshi of the Śrī cakra tradition."],"searchText":"787 त्रिपुरेशी त्रिपुराणामीशी। सर्वाशापरिपूरकचक्राधीश्वर्यास्त्रिपुरेशीति नाम। तदभेदादियमम्बापि। त्रिपुराणामीशी। — component from the samasa above सर्वाशापरिपूरकचक्राधीश्वर्यास्त्रिपुरेशीति — component from the samasa above नाम। — component from the samasa above तदभेदादियमम्बापि। — component from the samasa above त्रिपुरेशी means one who is the ruler of tripurā. tripurā means the three cities, the three states, or the threefold universe. she is the sovereign of all triplicities and is identified with the tripureshi of the śrī cakra tradition. the ruler of the outer ring: in the anatomy of the śrī yantra, tripureśī is the specific administrative deity placed in absolute charge of the fifth major enclosure—the सर्वाशापरिपूरक चक्र (sarvāśāparipūraka cakra — the circle that fulfills all desires). she is non-different from this structural goddess, commanding the fulfillment of spiritual aspirations.","esoteric":["The Ruler of the Outer Ring: In the anatomy of the Śrī Yantra, Tripureśī is the specific administrative deity placed in absolute charge of the fifth major enclosure—the सर्वाशापरिपूरक चक्र (Sarvāśāparipūraka Cakra — the circle that fulfills all desires). She is non-different from this structural goddess, commanding the fulfillment of spiritual aspirations."]},{"number":788,"name":"जयत्सेना","samasa":["जयन्ती सेना शक्तिसमूहो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["जयन्ती — victorious","सेना — army"],"summary":["जयत्सेना means one whose army is victorious. Her army consists of divine Śaktis who always overcome hostile forces. The victory of Her army symbolises the victory of divine knowledge and power over ignorance and obstruction."],"searchText":"788 जयत्सेना जयन्ती सेना शक्तिसमूहो यस्याः सा। जयन्ती — victorious सेना — army जयत्सेना means one whose army is victorious. her army consists of divine śaktis who always overcome hostile forces. the victory of her army symbolises the victory of divine knowledge and power over ignorance and obstruction. the victorious host of shaktis: her \"army\" (senā) is the corporate assembly of internal energy channels, guardian deities, and structural light rays that fight against ignorance. this host is jayantī — it cannot be checked, defeated, or turned back by chaotic forces, ensuring the eventual victory of the sincere seeker.","esoteric":["The Victorious Host of Shaktis: Her \"army\" (Senā) is the corporate assembly of internal energy channels, guardian deities, and structural light rays that fight against ignorance. This host is jayantī — it cannot be checked, defeated, or turned back by chaotic forces, ensuring the eventual victory of the sincere seeker."]},{"number":789,"name":"निस्त्रैगुण्या","samasa":["निर्गतं त्रैगुण्यं गुणत्रयवत्त्वं यस्याः  सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतं — gone; free from"],"summary":["निस्त्रैगुण्या means one who is beyond the three gunas. Sattva, rajas and tamas belong to Prakriti and to the manifested world. Though She manifests through them, in Her supreme nature She is free from their limitation."],"searchText":"789 निस्त्रैगुण्या निर्गतं त्रैगुण्यं गुणत्रयवत्त्वं यस्याः  सा। निर्गतं — gone; free from निस्त्रैगुण्या means one who is beyond the three gunas. sattva, rajas and tamas belong to prakriti and to the manifested world. though she manifests through them, in her supreme nature she is free from their limitation. beyond the element play: while she manifests the three qualities to construct forms (triguṇātmikā), her essential, unconditioned nature as parabrahman sits completely past this triad (nirguṇa). she instructs the practitioner to step out of the shifting currents of light, motion, and mass, anchoring themselves in her clean, quality-less space.","esoteric":["Beyond the Element Play: While She manifests the three qualities to construct forms (Triguṇātmikā), Her essential, unconditioned nature as Parabrahman sits completely past this triad (Nirguṇa). She instructs the practitioner to step out of the shifting currents of light, motion, and mass, anchoring themselves in Her clean, quality-less space."]},{"number":790,"name":"परापरा","samasa":["परशब्दोऽपरशब्दः परापरशब्दो वा यस्य वाचकस्तत्स्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["परशब्दोऽपरशब्दः — component from the samasa above","परापरशब्दो — component from the samasa above","वा — component from the samasa above","यस्य — component from the samasa above","वाचकस्तत्स्वरूपा। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["परापरा means one who is both para and apara. Para means the supreme, and apara means the lower or manifested form. She is both the transcendental Reality and the manifested universe; therefore She is Para-apara."],"searchText":"790 परापरा परशब्दोऽपरशब्दः परापरशब्दो वा यस्य वाचकस्तत्स्वरूपा। परशब्दोऽपरशब्दः — component from the samasa above परापरशब्दो — component from the samasa above वा — component from the samasa above यस्य — component from the samasa above वाचकस्तत्स्वरूपा। — component from the samasa above परापरा means one who is both para and apara. para means the supreme, and apara means the lower or manifested form. she is both the transcendental reality and the manifested universe; therefore she is para-apara. the non-dual integration: she is both परा (parā — the hidden, formless, unconditioned absolute) and अपरा (aparā — the visible, multiform, material universe of objects). she does not exclude the relative world to stay holy, nor does she lose her absolute status when projecting forms. she is the holistic reality that integrates both dimensions simultaneously, leaving zero room for structural duality.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Integration: She is both परा (Parā — the hidden, formless, unconditioned absolute) and अपरा (Aparā — the visible, multiform, material universe of objects). She does not exclude the relative world to stay holy, nor does She lose Her absolute status when projecting forms. She is the holistic reality that integrates both dimensions simultaneously, leaving zero room for structural duality."]},{"number":791,"name":"सत्यज्ञानानन्दरूपा","samasa":["सत्यं ज्ञानमानन्दश्च रूपं यस्याः सा।","सती सद्विद्या तद्विषये अज्ञा अनभिज्ञा ये तेषामनानन्दमानन्दभिन्नं दुःखमेव रूउपयति ददातीति।","सत्याविद्या देव्या अज्ञानं येषां ते सत्यज्ञानाः तेषामानन्दाख्यान् लोकान् रूपयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["सत्यं — truth","सती — true; devoted wife"],"summary":["सत्यज्ञानानन्दरूपा means one whose form is truth, knowledge and bliss. Satya, jnana and ananda are used to indicate the nature of Brahman. Śrīdevī is that Brahman-form, the reality that is true, conscious and blissful."],"searchText":"791 सत्यज्ञानानन्दरूपा सत्यं ज्ञानमानन्दश्च रूपं यस्याः सा। सती सद्विद्या तद्विषये अज्ञा अनभिज्ञा ये तेषामनानन्दमानन्दभिन्नं दुःखमेव रूउपयति ददातीति। सत्याविद्या देव्या अज्ञानं येषां ते सत्यज्ञानाः तेषामानन्दाख्यान् लोकान् रूपयतीति। सत्यं — truth सती — true; devoted wife सत्यज्ञानानन्दरूपा means one whose form is truth, knowledge and bliss. satya, jnana and ananda are used to indicate the nature of brahman. śrīdevī is that brahman-form, the reality that is true, conscious and blissful. the absolute identity of spirit: her essential substance consists of the core triad that defines the absolute reality—existence-truth (satya), luminous awareness (jñāna), and boundless bliss (ananda). to those who turn away from her light, reality appears as fragmented friction; to those who recognize her, she opens the gates of absolute joy.","esoteric":["The Absolute Identity of Spirit: Her essential substance consists of the core triad that defines the absolute reality—Existence-Truth (Satya), Luminous Awareness (Jñāna), and Boundless Bliss (Ananda). to those who turn away from Her light, reality appears as fragmented friction; to those who recognize Her, She opens the gates of absolute joy."]},{"number":792,"name":"सामरस्यपरायणा","samasa":["समो न्यूनानधिको रसो ययोस्तयोः शिवशक्त्योर्भावः सामरस्यमेव परमयनं स्थानं यस्याः सा।","सामरस्य लोकस्य परायणमाश्रय:।","रस्यन्ते गीयन्त इति रस्यानि सामानि च तानि रस्यानि च तानि परायणानि अभीष्टानि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["समो — component from the samasa above","न्यूनानधिको — component from the samasa above","रसो — component from the samasa above","ययोस्तयोः — component from the samasa above","शिवशक्त्योर्भावः — component from the samasa above","सामरस्यमेव — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["सामरस्यपरायणा means one who is devoted to perfect unity or sameness of essence. Samarasa means the non-difference or equal essence of Śiva and Śakti. She abides in the perfect harmony where Śiva and Śakti are not separate. The name also suggests that sacred chants and songs become desirable because they lead to this unity."],"searchText":"792 सामरस्यपरायणा समो न्यूनानधिको रसो ययोस्तयोः शिवशक्त्योर्भावः सामरस्यमेव परमयनं स्थानं यस्याः सा। सामरस्य लोकस्य परायणमाश्रय:। रस्यन्ते गीयन्त इति रस्यानि सामानि च तानि रस्यानि च तानि परायणानि अभीष्टानि यस्याः सा। समो — component from the samasa above न्यूनानधिको — component from the samasa above रसो — component from the samasa above ययोस्तयोः — component from the samasa above शिवशक्त्योर्भावः — component from the samasa above सामरस्यमेव — component from the samasa above सामरस्यपरायणा means one who is devoted to perfect unity or sameness of essence. samarasa means the non-difference or equal essence of śiva and śakti. she abides in the perfect harmony where śiva and śakti are not separate. the name also suggests that sacred chants and songs become desirable because they lead to this unity. the equilibrium of consciousness and energy: सामरस्य (sāmarasya) describes a state of chemical and spiritual equilibrium where two elements fuse so perfectly that they cannot be separated—like water mixed with milk. shiva (consciousness) and shakti (energy) exist in this exact condition of balanced, non-dual fusion. she is parāyaṇā because she is permanently anchored at this peak junction point, serving as the ultimate refuge where the seeker's individual duality is dissolved into the whole.","esoteric":["The Equilibrium of Consciousness and Energy: सामरस्य (Sāmarasya) describes a state of chemical and spiritual equilibrium where two elements fuse so perfectly that they cannot be separated—like water mixed with milk. Shiva (consciousness) and Shakti (energy) exist in this exact condition of balanced, non-dual fusion. She is Parāyaṇā because She is permanently anchored at this peak junction point, serving as the ultimate refuge where the seeker's individual duality is dissolved into the whole."]},{"number":793,"name":"कपर्दिनी","samasa":["गङ्गाया अपि पाविका यज्जटा, तद्वती।","कपर्दिनामकस्य शिवस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["गङ्गाया — component from the samasa above","अपि — component from the samasa above","पाविका — component from the samasa above","यज्जटा — component from the samasa above","तद्वती। — component from the samasa above","कपर्दिनामकस्य — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["कपर्दिनी means one who is Kapardini. Kapardin is Śiva, the matted-haired Lord; Kapardini is His consort. It also indicates Her association with the purifying matted locks from which even Ganga becomes sacred."],"searchText":"793 कपर्दिनी गङ्गाया अपि पाविका यज्जटा, तद्वती। कपर्दिनामकस्य शिवस्य पत्नी। गङ्गाया — component from the samasa above अपि — component from the samasa above पाविका — component from the samasa above यज्जटा — component from the samasa above तद्वती। — component from the samasa above कपर्दिनामकस्य — component from the samasa above कपर्दिनी means one who is kapardini. kapardin is śiva, the matted-haired lord; kapardini is his consort. it also indicates her association with the purifying matted locks from which even ganga becomes sacred. the containment of the cosmic current: कपर्द refers to the coiled, sacred matted hair worn by ascetics and lord śiva. as kapardinī, her hair strands represent the interwoven, high-velocity currents of cosmic energy and inspiration. just as shiva's hair caught and safely tamed the violent downward crash of the river gaṅgā, her structural matted channels contain and direct the vast currents of spiritual power, preventing them from destroying the practitioner's nervous system.","esoteric":["The Containment of the Cosmic Current: कपर्द refers to the coiled, sacred matted hair worn by ascetics and Lord Śiva. As Kapardinī, Her hair strands represent the interwoven, high-velocity currents of cosmic energy and inspiration. Just as Shiva's hair caught and safely tamed the violent downward crash of the river Gaṅgā, Her structural matted channels contain and direct the vast currents of spiritual power, preventing them from destroying the practitioner's nervous system."]},{"number":794,"name":"कलामाला","samasa":["कलानां चतुःषष्ट्यादिरूपाणां माला परम्परा।","कलां लावण्यं मां शोभां च लातीति।"],"wordByWord":["माला — garland; series"],"summary":["कलामाला means one who is the garland of kalas. Kalas are arts, digits, powers or phases. She is the continuous series and source of all kalas, including the sixty-four arts and all forms of beauty and skill."],"searchText":"794 कलामाला कलानां चतुःषष्ट्यादिरूपाणां माला परम्परा। कलां लावण्यं मां शोभां च लातीति। माला — garland; series कलामाला means one who is the garland of kalas. kalas are arts, digits, powers or phases. she is the continuous series and source of all kalas, including the sixty-four arts and all forms of beauty and skill. the unbroken chain of creative rays: she wears the entire network of the sixty-four cultural arts (catuḥ-ṣaṣṭhi-kalā), the digits of lunar time, and the operational phases of element evolution as a continuous, beautiful garland (mālā). every single expression of aesthetic brilliance, mathematical phase, or design ray is a link in her corporate chain.","esoteric":["The Unbroken Chain of Creative Rays: She wears the entire network of the sixty-four cultural arts (catuḥ-ṣaṣṭhi-kalā), the digits of lunar time, and the operational phases of element evolution as a continuous, beautiful garland (mālā). Every single expression of aesthetic brilliance, mathematical phase, or design ray is a link in Her corporate chain."]},{"number":795,"name":"कामधुक्","samasa":["कामान् दोग्धीति कामधुक्।","कामधेनुस्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["कामान् — desires"],"summary":["कामधुक् means one who fulfils desires like the wish-yielding cow. Kamadhuk means one who milks or yields desired objects. Like Kamadhenu, She grants the legitimate desires of devotees and supports their spiritual and worldly needs."],"searchText":"795 कामधुक् कामान् दोग्धीति कामधुक्। कामधेनुस्वरूपा। कामान् — desires कामधुक् means one who fulfils desires like the wish-yielding cow. kamadhuk means one who milks or yields desired objects. like kamadhenu, she grants the legitimate desires of devotees and supports their spiritual and worldly needs. the wish-fulfilling fountain: she functions as the ultimate cosmic kāmadhenu — the celestial cow that effortlessly yields the fulfillment of whatever a sincere heart requires. she does not delay or force painful bargaining; if the seeker's alignment is clean, she milks out the necessary resource immediately, providing overall support for the path.","esoteric":["The Wish-Fulfilling Fountain: She functions as the ultimate cosmic Kāmadhenu — the celestial cow that effortlessly yields the fulfillment of whatever a sincere heart requires. She does not delay or force painful bargaining; if the seeker's alignment is clean, She milks out the necessary resource immediately, providing overall support for the path."]},{"number":796,"name":"कामरूपिणी","samasa":["कामः परशिव एव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।","कामं यथेच्छं वा रूपाण्यस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["कामः — desire; Parashiva"],"summary":["कामरूपिणी means one whose form is desire or the supreme Kama. Kama here may indicate Parashiva, the supreme beloved, or the power that assumes forms according to will. All forms desired in worship are forms of Her."],"searchText":"796 कामरूपिणी कामः परशिव एव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। कामं यथेच्छं वा रूपाण्यस्याः अस्तीति। कामः — desire; parashiva कामरूपिणी means one whose form is desire or the supreme kama. kama here may indicate parashiva, the supreme beloved, or the power that assumes forms according to will. all forms desired in worship are forms of her. the body of divine desire: काम represents paramaśiva as pure, unconditioned cosmic attraction. she is her non-dual counterpart, giving visible expression to that baseline consciousness. absolute morphological freedom: alternatively, she is kāmarūpiṇī because she possesses the absolute freedom to project and assume any physical or geometric form whatsoever (yatheccha-rūpā) to guide and protect her devotees.","esoteric":["The Body of Divine Desire: काम represents Paramaśiva as pure, unconditioned cosmic attraction. She is Her non-dual counterpart, giving visible expression to that baseline consciousness.","Absolute Morphological Freedom: Alternatively, She is Kāmarūpiṇī because She possesses the absolute freedom to project and assume any physical or geometric form whatsoever (yatheccha-rūpā) to guide and protect Her devotees."]},{"number":797,"name":"कलानिधिः","samasa":["कलानां नानाविधतया निधिः।","आत्मैवास्य षोडशी कलेति बृहदारण्यकोक्तेरात्मनां जीवानां निधिः।","कलाः कर्माणि निधीयन्तेऽस्यामिति।"],"wordByWord":["कलानां — component from the samasa above","नानाविधतया — component from the samasa above","निधिः। — component from the samasa above","आत्मैवास्य — component from the samasa above","षोडशी — component from the samasa above","कलेति — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["कलानिधिः means one who is the treasure-house of kalas. She is the repository of many kinds of arts, powers and digits. The Upanishadic idea of the sixteenfold Self is also suggested; the souls and their powers are contained in Her."],"searchText":"797 कलानिधिः कलानां नानाविधतया निधिः। आत्मैवास्य षोडशी कलेति बृहदारण्यकोक्तेरात्मनां जीवानां निधिः। कलाः कर्माणि निधीयन्तेऽस्यामिति। कलानां — component from the samasa above नानाविधतया — component from the samasa above निधिः। — component from the samasa above आत्मैवास्य — component from the samasa above षोडशी — component from the samasa above कलेति — component from the samasa above कलानिधिः means one who is the treasure-house of kalas. she is the repository of many kinds of arts, powers and digits. the upanishadic idea of the sixteenfold self is also suggested; the souls and their powers are contained in her. the storehouse of the sixteen digits: the true self constitutes the ultimate sixteenth digit (षोडशी कला) of existence. she is kalānidhi because she functions as the absolute treasure house where all these individual sparks of living consciousness (jīvas) are stored, protected, and nourished during cosmic cycles, keeping their potential intact.","esoteric":["The Storehouse of the Sixteen Digits: the true Self constitutes the ultimate sixteenth digit (षोडशी कला) of existence. She is Kalānidhi because She functions as the absolute treasure house where all these individual sparks of living consciousness (Jīvas) are stored, protected, and nourished during cosmic cycles, keeping their potential intact."]},{"number":798,"name":"काव्यकला","samasa":["काव्यं च सा कला च।","काव्योत्पादककलारूपा।","काव्यस्य शुक्रस्य मृतसञ्जीवन्याख्यकलारूपा"],"wordByWord":["कला — art; digit; power"],"summary":["काव्यकला means one who is the art of poetry. She is the power that produces poetry, learning, refined expression and inspired speech. The life-giving power of poetic art and the revival of expression arise from Her grace."],"searchText":"798 काव्यकला काव्यं च सा कला च। काव्योत्पादककलारूपा। काव्यस्य शुक्रस्य मृतसञ्जीवन्याख्यकलारूपा कला — art; digit; power काव्यकला means one who is the art of poetry. she is the power that produces poetry, learning, refined expression and inspired speech. the life-giving power of poetic art and the revival of expression arise from her grace. the genius behind literature: she is the highly specialized, creative ray (kalā) that breaks open inside the intellect of a seer (kavi), allowing them to compose sublime, immortal literature that captures cosmic truth. the ray of resurrection: mythologically, kāvya is sage śukrācārya; she is the hidden, internal dynamic power behind his celebrated मृतसञ्जीवनी विद्या (mṛta-sañjīvanī vidyā — the science that restores life to the dead), demonstrating her capacity to revive stagnant systems.","esoteric":["The Genius behind Literature: She is the highly specialized, creative ray (kalā) that breaks open inside the intellect of a seer (kavi), allowing them to compose sublime, immortal literature that captures cosmic truth.","The Ray of Resurrection: Mythologically, Kāvya is Sage Śukrācārya; She is the hidden, internal dynamic power behind his celebrated मृतसञ्जीवनी विद्या (Mṛta-sañjīvanī Vidyā — the science that restores life to the dead), demonstrating Her capacity to revive stagnant systems."]},{"number":799,"name":"रसज्ञा","samasa":["रसान् शृङ्गारादिभेदेन दशविधान् जानातीति।","रसनेन्द्रियस्वरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["रसान् — aesthetic flavours; tastes"],"summary":["रसज्ञा means one who knows rasa. Rasa means aesthetic flavour such as shringara and other poetic sentiments, and also taste. She knows, enjoys and grants all rasa, both in art and in spiritual experience."],"searchText":"799 रसज्ञा रसान् शृङ्गारादिभेदेन दशविधान् जानातीति। रसनेन्द्रियस्वरूपा। रसान् — aesthetic flavours; tastes रसज्ञा means one who knows rasa. rasa means aesthetic flavour such as shringara and other poetic sentiments, and also taste. she knows, enjoys and grants all rasa, both in art and in spiritual experience. the master connoisseur of consciousness flavor: रस (rasa) represents the ten refined categories of aesthetic and spiritual emotion (love, peace, heroism, etc.). she is rasajñā because she perfectly understands, feels, and evaluates the exact flavor profile of the devotee's heart. concurrently, she manifests as the foundational sensory capacity of taste (rasanendriya), allowing life to experience sweetness.","esoteric":["The Master Connoisseur of Consciousness Flavor: रस (Rasa) represents the ten refined categories of aesthetic and spiritual emotion (love, peace, heroism, etc.). She is Rasajñā because She perfectly understands, feels, and evaluates the exact flavor profile of the devotee's heart. Concurrently, She manifests as the foundational sensory capacity of taste (rasanendriya), allowing life to experience sweetness."]},{"number":800,"name":"रसशेवधिः","samasa":["रसस्य ब्रह्मामृतस्य शेवधिर्निधिः।","कलानां रसनां च निधिः शेवधिर्यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निधिः — treasure; store"],"summary":["रसशेवधिः means one who is the treasure-house of rasa. The highest rasa is the nectar of Brahman. She is the storehouse of that nectar and of all forms of sweetness, taste and experience."],"searchText":"800 रसशेवधिः रसस्य ब्रह्मामृतस्य शेवधिर्निधिः। कलानां रसनां च निधिः शेवधिर्यस्याः सा। निधिः — treasure; store रसशेवधिः means one who is the treasure-house of rasa. the highest rasa is the nectar of brahman. she is the storehouse of that nectar and of all forms of sweetness, taste and experience. the reservoir of the non-dual nectar: the word शेवधि (śevadhi) denotes an inexhaustible, highly guarded divine treasure house. she is rasaśevadhi because she is the absolute reservoir that holds the infinite, sweet nectar of spiritual immortality (ब्रह्मामृत) generated within the sahasrāra crown center. finding her presence gives the practitioner immediate, permanent access to this source of unconditioned joy, concluding the 800-name milestone with absolute satisfaction.","esoteric":["The Reservoir of the Non-Dual Nectar: The word शेवधि (Śevadhi) denotes an inexhaustible, highly guarded divine treasure house. She is Rasaśevadhi because She is the absolute reservoir that holds the infinite, sweet nectar of spiritual immortality (ब्रह्मामृत) generated within the Sahasrāra crown center. Finding Her presence gives the practitioner immediate, permanent access to this source of unconditioned joy, concluding the 800-name milestone with absolute satisfaction."]},{"number":801,"name":"पुष्टा","samasa":["षट्त्रिंशत्तत्त्वविग्रहशीलत्वात्।","बहुभिर्गुणैर्ब्रह्मरसेन ब्राह्मणैर्वा पुष्टा।"],"wordByWord":["षट्त्रिंशत्तत्त्वविग्रहशीलत्वात्। — component from the samasa above","बहुभिर्गुणैर्ब्रह्मरसेन — component from the samasa above","ब्राह्मणैर्वा — component from the samasa above","पुष्टा। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["पुष्टा means one who is full and nourished. She is complete with the thirty-six tattvas and with countless qualities. She nourishes the universe and is Herself the fullness from which nourishment comes."],"searchText":"801 पुष्टा षट्त्रिंशत्तत्त्वविग्रहशीलत्वात्। बहुभिर्गुणैर्ब्रह्मरसेन ब्राह्मणैर्वा पुष्टा। षट्त्रिंशत्तत्त्वविग्रहशीलत्वात्। — component from the samasa above बहुभिर्गुणैर्ब्रह्मरसेन — component from the samasa above ब्राह्मणैर्वा — component from the samasa above पुष्टा। — component from the samasa above पुष्टा means one who is full and nourished. she is complete with the thirty-six tattvas and with countless qualities. she nourishes the universe and is herself the fullness from which nourishment comes. the fullness of the thirty-six tattvas: she is puṣṭā because her manifest body is perfectly filled and nourished by the complete deployment of the thirty-six foundational principles of reality (षट्त्रिंशत्तत्त्व). the essence of brahman: alternatively, she is continually nourished and amplified by absolute virtues, the nectar of brahman-bliss (brahma-rasa), and the spiritual realizations of realized seers, remaining absolute without decay.","esoteric":["The Fullness of the Thirty-Six Tattvas: She is Puṣṭā because Her manifest body is perfectly filled and nourished by the complete deployment of the thirty-six foundational principles of reality (षट्त्रिंशत्तत्त्व).","The Essence of Brahman: Alternatively, She is continually nourished and amplified by absolute virtues, the nectar of Brahman-bliss (brahma-rasa), and the spiritual realizations of realized seers, remaining absolute without decay."]},{"number":802,"name":"पुरातना","samasa":["सर्वेषामादिभूतत्वात्पुरातना।","पुरातना गुणा अस्यां सन्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["पुरातना — ancient"],"summary":["पुरातना means one who is ancient. She is prior to all beings and is the origin of everything. Since all qualities and worlds arise in Her, She is called Puratana, the ancient one."],"searchText":"802 पुरातना सर्वेषामादिभूतत्वात्पुरातना। पुरातना गुणा अस्यां सन्तीति। पुरातना — ancient पुरातना means one who is ancient. she is prior to all beings and is the origin of everything. since all qualities and worlds arise in her, she is called puratana, the ancient one. the primeval source: she is purātanā because she exists prior to the first movement of cosmic manifestation (सर्वेषाम आदिभूतत्वात्). before space formats itself and before time begins its count, she is already present as the timeless, uncreated background awareness.","esoteric":["The Primeval Source: She is Purātanā because She exists prior to the first movement of cosmic manifestation (सर्वेषाम आदिभूतत्वात्). Before space formats itself and before time begins its count, She is already present as the timeless, uncreated background awareness."]},{"number":803,"name":"पूज्या","samasa":["पूजयितुं योग्या।"],"wordByWord":["पूजयितुं — component from the samasa above","योग्या। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["पूज्या means one who is worthy of worship. She deserves worship by all beings because She is the source, support and goal of all. The name simply stresses Her universal worshipfulness."],"searchText":"803 पूज्या पूजयितुं योग्या। पूजयितुं — component from the samasa above योग्या। — component from the samasa above पूज्या means one who is worthy of worship. she deserves worship by all beings because she is the source, support and goal of all. the name simply stresses her universal worshipfulness. the apex of adoration: in the hierarchy of existence, finite objects are valued for utility, and lesser deities are approached for specific boons. she is pūjyā because she stands as the definitive ceiling of value—the only reality truly worthy of unconditioned adoration by realized intellects seeking final liberation.","esoteric":["The Apex of Adoration: In the hierarchy of existence, finite objects are valued for utility, and lesser deities are approached for specific boons. She is Pūjyā because She stands as the definitive ceiling of value—the only reality truly worthy of unconditioned adoration by realized intellects seeking final liberation."]},{"number":804,"name":"पुष्करा","samasa":["पुष्करं कमलम्, तत्स्वरूपा।","पुष्कं पोषणं रातीति।","पुष्कराख्यतीर्थरूपा।","रलयोरभेदात् पुष्कला व्याप्ता।"],"wordByWord":["कमलम् — lotus"],"summary":["पुष्करा means one who is lotus-like, nourishing, or connected with sacred waters. Pushkara may mean lotus, nourishment, or a sacred tirtha. She is the lotus-like, auspicious and nourishing principle praised through this name."],"searchText":"804 पुष्करा पुष्करं कमलम्, तत्स्वरूपा। पुष्कं पोषणं रातीति। पुष्कराख्यतीर्थरूपा। रलयोरभेदात् पुष्कला व्याप्ता। कमलम् — lotus पुष्करा means one who is lotus-like, nourishing, or connected with sacred waters. pushkara may mean lotus, nourishment, or a sacred tirtha. she is the lotus-like, auspicious and nourishing principle praised through this name. the sacred matrix: she is the pristine lotus (puṣkara) of pure space. by utilizing the phonetic equivalence of $r$ and $l$, she is puṣkalā—the absolute, all-pervasive presence that leaves no coordinate empty, continuously yielding vital nourishment to sustain the cosmic grid.","esoteric":["The Sacred Matrix: She is the pristine lotus (puṣkara) of pure space. By utilizing the phonetic equivalence of $r$ and $l$, She is Puṣkalā—the absolute, all-pervasive presence that leaves no coordinate empty, continuously yielding vital nourishment to sustain the cosmic grid."]},{"number":805,"name":"पुष्करेक्षणा","samasa":["पुष्कराणीव कमलानीवेक्षणानि नयनानि यस्याः सा।","पुष्करशब्दः पृथिवीपरः। मह्यादिविषये क्षण उत्सवो निर्व्यापारस्थितिर्वा यस्याः सा।","पुष्करशब्दो न्यग्रोधवृक्षपरः। न्यग्रोधपर्णशायित्वाद्विष्णुरत्र लक्षणया गृह्यते। तत्रेक्षणं कृपानिरीक्षणं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["पुष्कराणीव — component from the samasa above","कमलानीवेक्षणानि — component from the samasa above","नयनानि — component from the samasa above","यस्याः — component from the samasa above","सा। — component from the samasa above","पुष्करशब्दः — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["पुष्करेक्षणा means one whose eyes are like lotuses. Pushkara means lotus; Her eyes are compared to lotuses because of beauty, tenderness and grace. The name also permits meanings connected with earth, sacred trees and the compassionate glance of Viṣṇu, all absorbed in Her power."],"searchText":"805 पुष्करेक्षणा पुष्कराणीव कमलानीवेक्षणानि नयनानि यस्याः सा। पुष्करशब्दः पृथिवीपरः। मह्यादिविषये क्षण उत्सवो निर्व्यापारस्थितिर्वा यस्याः सा। पुष्करशब्दो न्यग्रोधवृक्षपरः। न्यग्रोधपर्णशायित्वाद्विष्णुरत्र लक्षणया गृह्यते। तत्रेक्षणं कृपानिरीक्षणं यस्याः सा। पुष्कराणीव — component from the samasa above कमलानीवेक्षणानि — component from the samasa above नयनानि — component from the samasa above यस्याः — component from the samasa above सा। — component from the samasa above पुष्करशब्दः — component from the samasa above पुष्करेक्षणा means one whose eyes are like lotuses. pushkara means lotus; her eyes are compared to lotuses because of beauty, tenderness and grace. the name also permits meanings connected with earth, sacred trees and the compassionate glance of viṣṇu, all absorbed in her power. the gaze of sustenance: her eyes operate like wide, liquid lotus petals. when her glance fixes upon the earth plane, it initiates an internal festival of stability (utsava). when her glance fixes upon the preserving energy of viṣṇu resting upon the banyan leaf, it feeds him the dynamic compassion needed to maintain planetary order.","esoteric":["The Gaze of Sustenance: Her eyes operate like wide, liquid lotus petals. When Her glance fixes upon the earth plane, it initiates an internal festival of stability (utsava). When Her glance fixes upon the preserving energy of Viṣṇu resting upon the banyan leaf, it feeds him the dynamic compassion needed to maintain planetary order."]},{"number":806,"name":"परंज्योतिः","samasa":["परमुत्कृष्टं ब्रह्मात्मकं ज्योतिः।"],"wordByWord":["परमुत्कृष्टं — component from the samasa above","ब्रह्मात्मकं — component from the samasa above","ज्योतिः। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["परंज्योतिः means one who is the supreme light. This light is not ordinary physical brightness but the highest Brahman-light. She is the light by which all lights shine and by which knowledge arises."],"searchText":"806 परंज्योतिः परमुत्कृष्टं ब्रह्मात्मकं ज्योतिः। परमुत्कृष्टं — component from the samasa above ब्रह्मात्मकं — component from the samasa above ज्योतिः। — component from the samasa above परंज्योतिः means one who is the supreme light. this light is not ordinary physical brightness but the highest brahman-light. she is the light by which all lights shine and by which knowledge arises. the light of pure awareness: she is not a physical fire or a bright stellar radiation. she is the paraṁjyotiḥ celebrated across the vedas—the unconditioned, self-luminous light of absolute consciousness (brahmātmakam) that illuminates the internal sky of the heart and enables human senses to perceive.","esoteric":["The Light of Pure Awareness: She is not a physical fire or a bright stellar radiation. She is the Paraṁjyotiḥ celebrated across the Vedas—the unconditioned, self-luminous light of absolute consciousness (brahmātmakam) that illuminates the internal sky of the heart and enables human senses to perceive."]},{"number":807,"name":"परंधाम","samasa":["परं धाम उत्कृष्टं तेजः।"],"wordByWord":["धाम — abode; radiance"],"summary":["परंधाम means one who is the supreme abode or supreme radiance. Dhama means abode, splendour or light. She is the highest resting-place and the supreme brilliance sought by worshippers."],"searchText":"807 परंधाम परं धाम उत्कृष्टं तेजः। धाम — abode; radiance परंधाम means one who is the supreme abode or supreme radiance. dhama means abode, splendour or light. she is the highest resting-place and the supreme brilliance sought by worshippers. the ultimate destination: dhāma signifies both a blinding, infinite energy field (tejas) and the final spiritual coordinate where the soul rests. she is paraṁdhāma because she marks the absolute ceiling of spiritual attainment—the shoreless, non-dual home from which no traveler returns to bondage.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Destination: Dhāma signifies both a blinding, infinite energy field (tejas) and the final spiritual coordinate where the soul rests. She is Paraṁdhāma because She marks the absolute ceiling of spiritual attainment—the shoreless, non-dual home from which no traveler returns to bondage."]},{"number":808,"name":"परमाणुः","samasa":["परमा च साण्वी च।","परम उत्कृष्टोऽणुर्मन्त्रः।"],"wordByWord":["परमा — component from the samasa above","च — component from the samasa above","साण्वी — component from the samasa above","च। — component from the samasa above","परम — component from the samasa above","उत्कृष्टोऽणुर्मन्त्रः। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["परमाणुः means one who is subtler than the subtlest atom. She is extremely subtle and also the supreme mantra-principle. Although She pervades the universe, She is also present as the minute and inward principle beyond ordinary perception."],"searchText":"808 परमाणुः परमा च साण्वी च। परम उत्कृष्टोऽणुर्मन्त्रः। परमा — component from the samasa above च — component from the samasa above साण्वी — component from the samasa above च। — component from the samasa above परम — component from the samasa above उत्कृष्टोऽणुर्मन्त्रः। — component from the samasa above परमाणुः means one who is subtler than the subtlest atom. she is extremely subtle and also the supreme mantra-principle. although she pervades the universe, she is also present as the minute and inward principle beyond ordinary perception. the infinitesimal core: she is paramāṇuḥ because she is subtler than the subtlest particle of matter, sitting at the hidden core of every atom as its animating spark. concurrently, she manifests as the most highly condensed, potent, and supreme seed-syllable mantra (para-manu), packed with cosmic power.","esoteric":["The Infinitesimal Core: She is Paramāṇuḥ because She is subtler than the subtlest particle of matter, sitting at the hidden core of every atom as its animating spark. Concurrently, She manifests as the most highly condensed, potent, and supreme seed-syllable mantra (para-manu), packed with cosmic power."]},{"number":809,"name":"परात्परा","samasa":["परादुत्कृष्टाद्ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्रादपि परा श्रेष्ठतरा।"],"wordByWord":["परादुत्कृष्टाद्ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्रादपि — component from the samasa above","परा — component from the samasa above","श्रेष्ठतरा। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["परात्परा means one who is higher than the highest. She is superior even to those considered supreme, such as Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Rudra. Therefore She is called Paratpara, beyond the beyond."],"searchText":"809 परात्परा परादुत्कृष्टाद्ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्रादपि परा श्रेष्ठतरा। परादुत्कृष्टाद्ब्रह्मविष्णुरुद्रादपि — component from the samasa above परा — component from the samasa above श्रेष्ठतरा। — component from the samasa above परात्परा means one who is higher than the highest. she is superior even to those considered supreme, such as brahmā, viṣṇu and rudra. therefore she is called paratpara, beyond the beyond. the ceiling over the trinity: cosmic administration features high-level universal creators—brahmā, viṣṇu, and rudra—who are textually designated as parā (the high ones). she is parātparā because she stands completely superior to and back behind this entire trinity, serving as the ultimate source from which they draw their temporary power.","esoteric":["The Ceiling over the Trinity: Cosmic administration features high-level universal creators—Brahmā, Viṣṇu, and Rudra—who are textually designated as Parā (the high ones). She is Parātparā because She stands completely superior to and back behind this entire trinity, serving as the ultimate source from which they draw their temporary power."]},{"number":810,"name":"पाशहस्ता","samasa":["पाशो हस्ते वामाधःकरे यस्याः सा।","पाशान् हस्तयते हस्तेन निरस्यतीति।"],"wordByWord":["हस्ते — in the hand"],"summary":["पाशहस्ता means one who holds the noose in Her hand. The noose is held in Her lower left hand and is one of Her important weapons. It also symbolises Her power to remove bondage or draw devotees towards Herself."],"searchText":"810 पाशहस्ता पाशो हस्ते वामाधःकरे यस्याः सा। पाशान् हस्तयते हस्तेन निरस्यतीति। हस्ते — in the hand पाशहस्ता means one who holds the noose in her hand. the noose is held in her lower left hand and is one of her important weapons. it also symbolises her power to remove bondage or draw devotees towards herself. the tool of restraint and release: in śrīvidyā liturgy, the noose (pāśa) represents इच्छाशक्ति (icchā-śakti — divine will) in its capacity to bind or loose. she holds this implement to capture runaway sensory desires. under the second operational key, she uses her hand to actively cast off and dissolve the internal attachments (pāśas) that trap her children.","esoteric":["The Tool of Restraint and Release: In Śrīvidyā liturgy, the noose (pāśa) represents इच्छाशक्ति (Icchā-śakti — divine will) in its capacity to bind or loose. She holds this implement to capture runaway sensory desires. Under the second operational key, She uses Her hand to actively cast off and dissolve the internal attachments (pāśas) that trap Her children."]},{"number":811,"name":"पाशहन्त्री","samasa":["पाशानां हन्त्री नाशिका।"],"wordByWord":["हन्त्री — destroyer"],"summary":["पाशहन्त्री means one who destroys bonds. pāśa means bondage or fetter. She cuts the bonds that bind the individual soul, including ignorance, desire and limitation."],"searchText":"811 पाशहन्त्री पाशानां हन्त्री नाशिका। हन्त्री — destroyer पाशहन्त्री means one who destroys bonds. pāśa means bondage or fetter. she cuts the bonds that bind the individual soul, including ignorance, desire and limitation. the cutter of the eight tethers: individual souls are trapped by the eight tethers (pāśas — shame, doubt, fear, pride, lineage, custom, status, and judgment). as pāśahantrī, her sharp kinetic energy cuts these specific chords, breaking the energetic cages of the subconscious and instantly liberating the soul.","esoteric":["The Cutter of the Eight Tethers: Individual souls are trapped by the eight tethers (pāśas — shame, doubt, fear, pride, lineage, custom, status, and judgment). As Pāśahantrī, Her sharp kinetic energy cuts these specific chords, breaking the energetic cages of the subconscious and instantly liberating the soul."]},{"number":812,"name":"परमन्त्रविभेदिनी","samasa":["परेषां स्वोपासकद्विषां मन्त्रान्, परैरभिचाराद्यर्थं प्रयुक्तो मनुः परमन्त्रः, तान् वा, विशेषाद्भिनत्तीति।","पर उत्कृष्टो मन्त्रः पञ्चदशीरूपस्तं विभेदयति।","परा उत्कृष्टा ये मन्तारो मननकर्तारस्तेषामवीन् पापानि भेदयति नाशयति।"],"wordByWord":["मन्त्रान् — mantras","पर — higher; supreme"],"summary":["परमन्त्रविभेदिनी means one who breaks hostile or external mantras. She destroys mantras used by enemies of Her worshippers, including harmful rites. She also reveals or unfolds the supreme mantra, the Panchadashi, and destroys the sins of worthy contemplators."],"searchText":"812 परमन्त्रविभेदिनी परेषां स्वोपासकद्विषां मन्त्रान्, परैरभिचाराद्यर्थं प्रयुक्तो मनुः परमन्त्रः, तान् वा, विशेषाद्भिनत्तीति। पर उत्कृष्टो मन्त्रः पञ्चदशीरूपस्तं विभेदयति। परा उत्कृष्टा ये मन्तारो मननकर्तारस्तेषामवीन् पापानि भेदयति नाशयति। मन्त्रान् — mantras पर — higher; supreme परमन्त्रविभेदिनी means one who breaks hostile or external mantras. she destroys mantras used by enemies of her worshippers, including harmful rites. she also reveals or unfolds the supreme mantra, the panchadashi, and destroys the sins of worthy contemplators. the shield against subtle aggression: she completely deactivates and dismantles hostile energetic actions (abhicāra) aimed at her practitioners. the pierce of the core formula: concurrently, she breaks open and reveals the hidden meanings inside the supreme fifteen-syllabled pañcadaśī formula, clearing away intellectual blocks.","esoteric":["The Shield against Subtle Aggression: She completely deactivates and dismantles hostile energetic actions (abhicāra) aimed at Her practitioners.","The Pierce of the Core Formula: Concurrently, She breaks open and reveals the hidden meanings inside the supreme fifteen-syllabled Pañcadaśī formula, clearing away intellectual blocks."]},{"number":813,"name":"मूर्ता","samasa":["रूपवद्वस्तु मूर्तम्, तद्रूपा।","पञ्चीकृतानि महाभूतानि मूर्तानि, तद्रूपा।"],"wordByWord":["मूर्तम् — formed"],"summary":["मूर्ता means one who has form. All formed objects and the gross elements are Her forms. She is therefore worshipped in visible and tangible forms also."],"searchText":"813 मूर्ता रूपवद्वस्तु मूर्तम्, तद्रूपा। पञ्चीकृतानि महाभूतानि मूर्तानि, तद्रूपा। मूर्तम् — formed मूर्ता means one who has form. all formed objects and the gross elements are her forms. she is therefore worshipped in visible and tangible forms also. the dense fabric of nature: she is mūrtā because she forms the physical fabric of the five gross elements after they have undergone the process of quintuplication (पञ्चीकरण). every physical object, planetary body, and tangible biological shell is her solidified form, showing her total presence in the material plane.","esoteric":["The Dense Fabric of Nature: She is Mūrtā because She forms the physical fabric of the five gross elements after they have undergone the process of quintuplication (पञ्चीकरण). Every physical object, planetary body, and tangible biological shell is Her solidified form, showing Her total presence in the material plane."]},{"number":814,"name":"अमूर्ता","samasa":["वाय्वाकाशादिकममूर्तम्, तद्रूपा।","अपञ्चीकृतानि तु भूतसूक्ष्माण्यमूर्तानि, तद्रूपा।।"],"wordByWord":["वाय्वाकाशादिकममूर्तम् — component from the samasa above","तद्रूपा। — component from the samasa above","अपञ्चीकृतानि — component from the samasa above","तु — component from the samasa above","भूतसूक्ष्माण्यमूर्तानि — component from the samasa above","तद्रूपा।। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["अमूर्ता means one who is formless. Air, space and the subtle elements are without gross form; She is in those also. Thus She is both formed and formless, gross and subtle."],"searchText":"814 अमूर्ता वाय्वाकाशादिकममूर्तम्, तद्रूपा। अपञ्चीकृतानि तु भूतसूक्ष्माण्यमूर्तानि, तद्रूपा।। वाय्वाकाशादिकममूर्तम् — component from the samasa above तद्रूपा। — component from the samasa above अपञ्चीकृतानि — component from the samasa above तु — component from the samasa above भूतसूक्ष्माण्यमूर्तानि — component from the samasa above तद्रूपा।। — component from the samasa above अमूर्ता means one who is formless. air, space and the subtle elements are without gross form; she is in those also. thus she is both formed and formless, gross and subtle. the subtle substratum: while she is the visible object (mūrtā), she is simultaneously amūrtā — the formless, invisible sky of air and ether (ākāśa) and the unquintupled, subtle elemental seeds (tanmātras). she confirms that the unmanifest vacuum and the dense world are waves of a single energy field.","esoteric":["The Subtle Substratum: While She is the visible object (Mūrtā), She is simultaneously Amūrtā — the formless, invisible sky of air and ether (ākāśa) and the unquintupled, subtle elemental seeds (tanmātras). She confirms that the unmanifest vacuum and the dense world are waves of a single energy field."]},{"number":815,"name":"अनित्यतृप्ता","samasa":["अनित्यैरेवोपचारैस्तृप्तेति पञ्चाक्षरं नाम भक्तिमात्रप्रियत्वात्।","अनिति श्वसतीति जीवोऽनितिपदार्थः। तै: अतृप्ता।","इति एवंप्रकारेण अतृप्ता न तृप्ता न भवतीति न। (ईदृशः प्रकारो नास्ति येन तृप्ता न स्यात्। अपि तु सर्वैरपि प्रकारैस्तृप्तैव)।"],"wordByWord":["तृप्ता — satisfied"],"summary":["अनित्यतृप्ता means one who is satisfied even by impermanent offerings. Since She is pleased by devotion alone, even simple and temporary offerings satisfy Her. Another interpretation says there is no manner in which She is not satisfied; She is always fulfilled by every sincere mode of worship."],"searchText":"815 अनित्यतृप्ता अनित्यैरेवोपचारैस्तृप्तेति पञ्चाक्षरं नाम भक्तिमात्रप्रियत्वात्। अनिति श्वसतीति जीवोऽनितिपदार्थः। तै: अतृप्ता। इति एवंप्रकारेण अतृप्ता न तृप्ता न भवतीति न। (ईदृशः प्रकारो नास्ति येन तृप्ता न स्यात्। अपि तु सर्वैरपि प्रकारैस्तृप्तैव)। तृप्ता — satisfied अनित्यतृप्ता means one who is satisfied even by impermanent offerings. since she is pleased by devotion alone, even simple and temporary offerings satisfy her. another interpretation says there is no manner in which she is not satisfied; she is always fulfilled by every sincere mode of worship. sincerity over opulence: she does not demand permanent, impossible physical monuments; she is perfectly satisfied by transient, fleeting daily offerings (anitya-upacāra) if driven by pure devotion. the double negation: under the logical track, it is impossible for her to experience lack; she remains fully satisfied across every parameter and condition in existence.","esoteric":["Sincerity over Opulence: She does not demand permanent, impossible physical monuments; She is perfectly satisfied by transient, fleeting daily offerings (anitya-upacāra) if driven by pure devotion.","The Double Negation: Under the logical track, it is impossible for Her to experience lack; She remains fully satisfied across every parameter and condition in existence."]},{"number":816,"name":"मुनिमानसहंसिका","samasa":["मुनीनां मानसं मन एव श्लेषात् मानसाख्यं सरस्तत्र हंसीव। स्वार्थे कः।","मुनीनां माने बहुमानविषये सहंसिकेव"],"wordByWord":["मुनीनां — component from the samasa above","मानसं — component from the samasa above","मन — component from the samasa above","एव — component from the samasa above","श्लेषात् — component from the samasa above","मानसाख्यं — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["मुनिमानसहंसिका means one who is the swan in the minds of sages. The minds of munis are like Manasa lake, and She moves there like a swan. She is honoured in the esteem of sages and dwells in their pure contemplation."],"searchText":"816 मुनिमानसहंसिका मुनीनां मानसं मन एव श्लेषात् मानसाख्यं सरस्तत्र हंसीव। स्वार्थे कः। मुनीनां माने बहुमानविषये सहंसिकेव मुनीनां — component from the samasa above मानसं — component from the samasa above मन — component from the samasa above एव — component from the samasa above श्लेषात् — component from the samasa above मानसाख्यं — component from the samasa above मुनिमानसहंसिका means one who is the swan in the minds of sages. the minds of munis are like manasa lake, and she moves there like a swan. she is honoured in the esteem of sages and dwells in their pure contemplation. the swan of the interior lake: a pristine swan (haṁsī) leaves muddy swamps to swim exclusively in the clear waters of lake mānasa. similarly, she bypasses minds clouded by worldly desires, choosing to glide exclusively within the clear, calm, and undisturbed intellectual waters (mānasa) of deep, contemplative meditators.","esoteric":["The Swan of the Interior Lake: A pristine swan (haṁsī) leaves muddy swamps to swim exclusively in the clear waters of Lake Mānasa. Similarly, She bypasses minds clouded by worldly desires, choosing to glide exclusively within the clear, calm, and undisturbed intellectual waters (mānasa) of deep, contemplative meditators."]},{"number":817,"name":"सत्यव्रता","samasa":["सत्यं ब्रह्मैव व्रतं भक्ष्यमुपचारात्तद्वत्प्रियं यस्याः सा।","सत्यमेव व्रतं यस्याः सा।","सत्यानि शीघ्रफलदानि व्रतानि यस्याः सा।","सत्यव्रतोनाम ब्राह्मणः सूकरभयात् ऐ ऐ इत्युच्चार्य तावतैव तपसा महाकविर्देवीभक्तो जातस्तदभेदात्सत्यव्रता।"],"wordByWord":["सत्यं — truth"],"summary":["सत्यव्रता means one whose vow is truth. Truth, Brahman itself, is Her vow and Her delight. The name also recalls vows that quickly bear fruit, and the tradition of Satyavrata, who became a great poet and devotee through the power of the Goddess."],"searchText":"817 सत्यव्रता सत्यं ब्रह्मैव व्रतं भक्ष्यमुपचारात्तद्वत्प्रियं यस्याः सा। सत्यमेव व्रतं यस्याः सा। सत्यानि शीघ्रफलदानि व्रतानि यस्याः सा। सत्यव्रतोनाम ब्राह्मणः सूकरभयात् ऐ ऐ इत्युच्चार्य तावतैव तपसा महाकविर्देवीभक्तो जातस्तदभेदात्सत्यव्रता। सत्यं — truth सत्यव्रता means one whose vow is truth. truth, brahman itself, is her vow and her delight. the name also recalls vows that quickly bear fruit, and the tradition of satyavrata, who became a great poet and devotee through the power of the goddess. the absolute vow: her essential code of operation is absolute truth (satya). the power of the seed-syllable: under the historical track, she references a mute brahmin (satyavrata) who accidentally vibrated the primary wisdom seed-syllable ऐं (aiṁ) out of fear, instantly unlocking her presence and transforming into a master poet, proving the immediate responsiveness of her sound keys.","esoteric":["The Absolute Vow: Her essential code of operation is absolute truth (Satya).","The Power of the Seed-Syllable: Under the historical track, She references a mute Brahmin (Satyavrata) who accidentally vibrated the primary wisdom seed-syllable ऐं (Aiṁ) out of fear, instantly unlocking Her presence and transforming into a master poet, proving the immediate responsiveness of Her sound keys."]},{"number":818,"name":"सत्यरूपा","samasa":["सत्यं कालत्रयाबाध्यं रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सत्यं — truth"],"summary":["सत्यरूपा means one whose form is truth. Truth is that which is not contradicted in the three periods of time. She is that unchanging reality."],"searchText":"818 सत्यरूपा सत्यं कालत्रयाबाध्यं रूपं यस्याः सा। सत्यं — truth सत्यरूपा means one whose form is truth. truth is that which is not contradicted in the three periods of time. she is that unchanging reality. untouched by the three tenses: satya is defined as that reality which can never be contradicted, altered, or negated across the past, present, or future (kālatrayābādhya). every material object shifts and fails; she is satyarūpā because her baseline consciousness remains constant across all universal transitions.","esoteric":["Untouched by the Three Tenses: Satya is defined as that reality which can never be contradicted, altered, or negated across the past, present, or future (kālatrayābādhya). Every material object shifts and fails; She is Satyarūpā because Her baseline consciousness remains constant across all universal transitions."]},{"number":819,"name":"सर्वान्तर्यामिणी","samasa":["सर्वेषामन्तर्यामिणी ।","सर्वा च सान्तर्यामिणी च।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वेषामन्तर्यामिणी — component from the samasa above","। — component from the samasa above","सर्वा — component from the samasa above","च — component from the samasa above","सान्तर्यामिणी — component from the samasa above","च। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["सर्वान्तर्यामिणी means one who is the indwelling ruler of all. She is present within all beings as the inner controller. She governs from within as consciousness, life and law."],"searchText":"819 सर्वान्तर्यामिणी सर्वेषामन्तर्यामिणी । सर्वा च सान्तर्यामिणी च। सर्वेषामन्तर्यामिणी — component from the samasa above । — component from the samasa above सर्वा — component from the samasa above च — component from the samasa above सान्तर्यामिणी — component from the samasa above च। — component from the samasa above सर्वान्तर्यामिणी means one who is the indwelling ruler of all. she is present within all beings as the inner controller. she governs from within as consciousness, life and law. the thread behind the puppets: she does not govern the cosmos from a distant exterior sky. as the antaryāmiṇī, she sits inside the internal cognitive core of every single living soul, atom, and element. she directs their internal movements, formats their karmic translations, and animates their baseline existence from within.","esoteric":["The Thread behind the Puppets: She does not govern the cosmos from a distant exterior sky. As the Antaryāmiṇī, She sits inside the internal cognitive core of every single living soul, atom, and element. She directs their internal movements, formats their karmic translations, and animates their baseline existence from within."]},{"number":820,"name":"सती","samasa":["पातिव्रत्यात्सद्रूपत्वाच्च सती।"],"wordByWord":["पातिव्रत्यात्सद्रूपत्वाच्च — component from the samasa above","सती। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["सती means one who is Sati. She is the true and faithful consort, and also the form of Being itself. The name recalls both Her supreme reality and the sacred ideal of pativrata devotion."],"searchText":"820 सती पातिव्रत्यात्सद्रूपत्वाच्च सती। पातिव्रत्यात्सद्रूपत्वाच्च — component from the samasa above सती। — component from the samasa above सती means one who is sati. she is the true and faithful consort, and also the form of being itself. the name recalls both her supreme reality and the sacred ideal of pativrata devotion. the substance of being: she is satī because she is the non-dual expression of pure existence (sad-rūpa). mythologically, she is the historical daughter of dakṣa who chose absolute fusion with lord śiva, proving that uncorrupted devotion and absolute reality are one substance.","esoteric":["The Substance of Being: She is Satī because She is the non-dual expression of pure existence (Sad-rūpa). Mythologically, She is the historical daughter of Dakṣa who chose absolute fusion with Lord Śiva, proving that uncorrupted devotion and absolute reality are one substance."]},{"number":821,"name":"ब्रह्माणी","samasa":["ब्रह्मरूपा अणी पुच्छम्। आनन्दमयकोशस्थपुच्छब्रह्मरूपेत्यर्थः।","ब्रह्माणमानयति जीवयतीति वा।","ब्रह्माणशब्दः पितामहपरस्तस्य स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["ब्रह्मरूपा — component from the samasa above","अणी — component from the samasa above","पुच्छम्। — component from the samasa above","आनन्दमयकोशस्थपुच्छब्रह्मरूपेत्यर्थः। — component from the samasa above","ब्रह्माणमानयति — component from the samasa above","जीवयतीति — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["ब्रह्माणी means one who is Brahmani. She is connected with Brahmā and also with the Brahman principle. She is the tail or support of the Anandamaya sheath and the life-giving power of Brahmā."],"searchText":"821 ब्रह्माणी ब्रह्मरूपा अणी पुच्छम्। आनन्दमयकोशस्थपुच्छब्रह्मरूपेत्यर्थः। ब्रह्माणमानयति जीवयतीति वा। ब्रह्माणशब्दः पितामहपरस्तस्य स्त्री। ब्रह्मरूपा — component from the samasa above अणी — component from the samasa above पुच्छम्। — component from the samasa above आनन्दमयकोशस्थपुच्छब्रह्मरूपेत्यर्थः। — component from the samasa above ब्रह्माणमानयति — component from the samasa above जीवयतीति — component from the samasa above ब्रह्माणी means one who is brahmani. she is connected with brahmā and also with the brahman principle. she is the tail or support of the anandamaya sheath and the life-giving power of brahmā. the foundation of bliss: the upaniṣad describes the structure of bliss, concluding with “brahma pucchaṁ pratiṣṭhā” (\"brahman is the tail or structural foundation\"). as brahmāṇī, she functions as that absolute anchor point (puccha/aṇī) that stabilizes the entire framework of cosmic bliss, giving life to the creator deity himself.","esoteric":["The Foundation of Bliss: The Upaniṣad describes the structure of bliss, concluding with “Brahma pucchaṁ pratiṣṭhā” (\"Brahman is the tail or structural foundation\"). As Brahmāṇī, She functions as that absolute anchor point (puccha/aṇī) that stabilizes the entire framework of cosmic bliss, giving life to the creator deity himself."]},{"number":822,"name":"ब्रह्म","samasa":["ब्रह्म यन्मुक्तप्राप्यं तत् स्वात्माभिन्नं ज्ञानम्।"],"wordByWord":["ब्रह्म — Brahman"],"summary":["ब्रह्म means one who is Brahman. Brahman is the knowledge attained by the liberated and is not different from the Self. She is that supreme Brahman itself."],"searchText":"822 ब्रह्म ब्रह्म यन्मुक्तप्राप्यं तत् स्वात्माभिन्नं ज्ञानम्। ब्रह्म — brahman ब्रह्म means one who is brahman. brahman is the knowledge attained by the liberated and is not different from the self. she is that supreme brahman itself. identity with the whole: lest a student think she is merely a secondary power belonging to a higher absolute, this name establishes she is the unconditioned, non-dual परब्रह्म (parabrahman). she is that non-dual knowledge (jñāna) that is accessed by liberated ascetics, completely identical with one's own core self (svātmābhinna).","esoteric":["Identity with the Whole: Lest a student think She is merely a secondary power belonging to a higher absolute, this name establishes She is the unconditioned, non-dual परब्रह्म (Parabrahman). She is that non-dual knowledge (jñāna) that is accessed by liberated ascetics, completely identical with one's own core Self (svātmābhinna)."]},{"number":823,"name":"जननी","samasa":["सर्वप्रपञ्चस्योत्पादकत्वाज्जननी।","(ब्रह्माणीपदनिर्वचनपरत्वेन ब्रह्मजननीत्येकं पदं स्वीकर्तुं युक्तम्। एतत्पक्षे ८१९ सर्वान्तर्यामिणीत्यत्र सर्वेति भिन्नं पदमास्थेयम्)।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वप्रपञ्चस्योत्पादकत्वाज्जननी। — component from the samasa above","ब्रह्माणीपदनिर्वचनपरत्वेन — component from the samasa above","ब्रह्मजननीत्येकं — component from the samasa above","पदं — component from the samasa above","स्वीकर्तुं — component from the samasa above","युक्तम्। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["जननी means one who is the mother. She produces the entire manifest universe. Whether understood separately or along with Brahmani, the name proclaims Her as the source of creation."],"searchText":"823 जननी सर्वप्रपञ्चस्योत्पादकत्वाज्जननी। (ब्रह्माणीपदनिर्वचनपरत्वेन ब्रह्मजननीत्येकं पदं स्वीकर्तुं युक्तम्। एतत्पक्षे ८१९ सर्वान्तर्यामिणीत्यत्र सर्वेति भिन्नं पदमास्थेयम्)। सर्वप्रपञ्चस्योत्पादकत्वाज्जननी। — component from the samasa above ब्रह्माणीपदनिर्वचनपरत्वेन — component from the samasa above ब्रह्मजननीत्येकं — component from the samasa above पदं — component from the samasa above स्वीकर्तुं — component from the samasa above युक्तम्। — component from the samasa above जननी means one who is the mother. she produces the entire manifest universe. whether understood separately or along with brahmani, the name proclaims her as the source of creation. the source of the multiverse: she is the universal jananī because she is the primary womb out of which the complete manifestation of names, elements, and worlds is projected. reading this combined with the previous name as ब्रह्मजननी (brahma-jananī) identifies her as the source that brings forth even the functional creator principles.","esoteric":["The Source of the Multiverse: She is the universal Jananī because She is the primary womb out of which the complete manifestation of names, elements, and worlds is projected. reading this combined with the previous name as ब्रह्मजननी (Brahma-jananī) identifies Her as the source that brings forth even the functional creator principles."]},{"number":824,"name":"बहुरूपा","samasa":["बहूनि रूपाणि यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["बहूनि — many","रूपाणि — forms"],"summary":["बहुरूपा means one who has many forms. She assumes innumerable forms according to the needs of creation, worship and experience. The many deities and the many beings are Her expressions."],"searchText":"824 बहुरूपा बहूनि रूपाणि यस्याः सा। बहूनि — many रूपाणि — forms बहुरूपा means one who has many forms. she assumes innumerable forms according to the needs of creation, worship and experience. the many deities and the many beings are her expressions. the singular multitude: though she is completely alone and non-dual (ekākinī), she is simultaneously bahurūpā because every single changing form, planet, cell, and creature in the universe is a mask assumed by her energy field. duality is merely her unity displaying its infinite potential.","esoteric":["The Singular Multitude: Though She is completely alone and non-dual (Ekākinī), She is simultaneously Bahurūpā because every single changing form, planet, cell, and creature in the universe is a mask assumed by Her energy field. Duality is merely Her unity displaying its infinite potential."]},{"number":825,"name":"बुधार्चिता","samasa":["बुधैर्ज्ञानिभिरर्चिता पूजिता।"],"wordByWord":["बुधैर्ज्ञानिभिरर्चिता — component from the samasa above","पूजिता। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["बुधार्चिता means one who is worshipped by the wise. Budhas are learned and awakened persons. Those who know truth worship Her as the supreme principle."],"searchText":"825 बुधार्चिता बुधैर्ज्ञानिभिरर्चिता पूजिता। बुधैर्ज्ञानिभिरर्चिता — component from the samasa above पूजिता। — component from the samasa above बुधार्चिता means one who is worshipped by the wise. budhas are learned and awakened persons. those who know truth worship her as the supreme principle. the worship of the discerning: budha refers to those who have crossed past superficial emotionalism and dry logic, anchoring themselves in direct spiritual discernment (jñānīs). their structured adoration confirms that her path satisfies the highest operational demands of the human intellect.","esoteric":["The Worship of the Discerning: Budha refers to those who have crossed past superficial emotionalism and dry logic, anchoring themselves in direct spiritual discernment (jñānīs). Their structured adoration confirms that Her path satisfies the highest operational demands of the human intellect."]},{"number":826,"name":"प्रसवित्री","samasa":["प्रकर्षेण वियदादिप्रपञ्चं प्रजा वा सूत इति प्रसवित्री।"],"wordByWord":["प्रकर्षेण — component from the samasa above","वियदादिप्रपञ्चं — component from the samasa above","प्रजा — component from the samasa above","वा — component from the samasa above","सूत — component from the samasa above","इति — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["प्रसवित्री means one who gives birth abundantly. She brings forth space and the rest of the universe, and also all creatures. She is the great power of manifestation and generation."],"searchText":"826 प्रसवित्री प्रकर्षेण वियदादिप्रपञ्चं प्रजा वा सूत इति प्रसवित्री। प्रकर्षेण — component from the samasa above वियदादिप्रपञ्चं — component from the samasa above प्रजा — component from the samasa above वा — component from the samasa above सूत — component from the samasa above इति — component from the samasa above प्रसवित्री means one who gives birth abundantly. she brings forth space and the rest of the universe, and also all creatures. she is the great power of manifestation and generation. the generative matrix: as prasavitrī, she executes the high-velocity generation of the elements, cascading outward from pure space (viyat) down to dense physical matter. she pushes the potential into kinetic manifestation with flawless excellence.","esoteric":["The Generative Matrix: As Prasavitrī, She executes the high-velocity generation of the elements, cascading outward from pure space (viyat) down to dense physical matter. She pushes the potential into kinetic manifestation with flawless excellence."]},{"number":827,"name":"प्रचण्डा","samasa":["प्रकृष्टाश्चण्डाः कोपना यस्या दूताः सा।","प्रकृष्टा प्रीतिविषयत्वेन चण्डा शङ्खपुष्पी यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रकृष्टाश्चण्डाः — component from the samasa above","कोपना — component from the samasa above","यस्या — component from the samasa above","दूताः — component from the samasa above","सा। — component from the samasa above","प्रकृष्टा — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["प्रचण्डा means one who is exceedingly fierce. Her messengers and powers are intense and capable of destroying hostile forces. The name also allows a meaning connected with strong affection for the shankhapushpi flower."],"searchText":"827 प्रचण्डा प्रकृष्टाश्चण्डाः कोपना यस्या दूताः सा। प्रकृष्टा प्रीतिविषयत्वेन चण्डा शङ्खपुष्पी यस्याः सा। प्रकृष्टाश्चण्डाः — component from the samasa above कोपना — component from the samasa above यस्या — component from the samasa above दूताः — component from the samasa above सा। — component from the samasa above प्रकृष्टा — component from the samasa above प्रचण्डा means one who is exceedingly fierce. her messengers and powers are intense and capable of destroying hostile forces. the name also allows a meaning connected with strong affection for the shankhapushpi flower. the force of pure protection: she is pracaṇḍā because her protective heralds and defensive energy lines operate with unyielding, terrifying velocity (caṇḍatva) to crush egoic deviations. botanically, her connection to the cooling śaṅkhapuṣpī flower demonstrates that this intense fire serves to restore long-term internal peace.","esoteric":["The Force of Pure Protection: She is Pracaṇḍā because Her protective heralds and defensive energy lines operate with unyielding, terrifying velocity (caṇḍatva) to crush egoic deviations. Botanically, Her connection to the cooling Śaṅkhapuṣpī flower demonstrates that this intense fire serves to restore long-term internal peace."]},{"number":828,"name":"आज्ञा","samasa":["भगवदिच्छारूपा।"],"wordByWord":["भगवदिच्छारूपा। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["आज्ञा means one who is command. She is the very form of divine will and order. The universe functions by Her command."],"searchText":"828 आज्ञा भगवदिच्छारूपा। भगवदिच्छारूपा। — component from the samasa above आज्ञा means one who is command. she is the very form of divine will and order. the universe functions by her command. the executive decree of consciousness: she is the living embodiment of the supreme command (ājñā) issued by the absolute consciousness. this command is भगवदिच्छा (bhagavad-icchā — divine will), the unalterable cosmic law that dictates planetary orbits, elements, and karmic metrics. nothing moves outside this structural decree.","esoteric":["The Executive Decree of Consciousness: She is the living embodiment of the supreme command (Ājñā) issued by the absolute consciousness. This command is भगवदिच्छा (Bhagavad-icchā — divine will), the unalterable cosmic law that dictates planetary orbits, elements, and karmic metrics. Nothing moves outside this structural decree."]},{"number":829,"name":"प्रतिष्ठा","samasa":["प्रतितिष्ठत्यस्यां विश्वमिति।"],"wordByWord":["प्रतितिष्ठत्यस्यां — component from the samasa above","विश्वमिति। — component from the samasa above"],"summary":["प्रतिष्ठा means one who is the foundation. The whole universe stands established in Her. She is the support in which all existence rests."],"searchText":"829 प्रतिष्ठा प्रतितिष्ठत्यस्यां विश्वमिति। प्रतितिष्ठत्यस्यां — component from the samasa above विश्वमिति। — component from the samasa above प्रतिष्ठा means one who is the foundation. the whole universe stands established in her. she is the support in which all existence rests. the substratum of the world movie: a moving picture requires an unmoving, white screen to be projected upon. she is pratiṣṭhā because she is that exact stable screen within which the entire manifest universe (viśvam) stands, operates, and resides, remaining untouched by the transformations of the movie.","esoteric":["The Substratum of the World Movie: A moving picture requires an unmoving, white screen to be projected upon. She is Pratiṣṭhā because She is that exact stable screen within which the entire manifest universe (viśvam) stands, operates, and resides, remaining untouched by the transformations of the movie."]},{"number":830,"name":"प्रकटाकृतिः","samasa":["प्रकटा सर्वैरनुभूयमाना आकृतिः रूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रकटा — manifest","आकृतिः — form"],"summary":["प्रकटाकृतिः means one whose form is manifest. Her form is clearly experienced by all through the universe and through worship. Though supreme and subtle, She also appears openly as the visible form of all existence."],"searchText":"830 प्रकटाकृतिः प्रकटा सर्वैरनुभूयमाना आकृतिः रूपं यस्याः सा। प्रकटा — manifest आकृतिः — form प्रकटाकृतिः means one whose form is manifest. her form is clearly experienced by all through the universe and through worship. though supreme and subtle, she also appears openly as the visible form of all existence. the obvious reality: sages often describe her as hidden (guhyā). every flash of sensory awareness, every breath, and every pulse of existence is her direct, manifest appearance, blindingly obvious to anyone who truly looks.","esoteric":["The Obvious Reality: Sages often describe Her as hidden (Guhyā). Every flash of sensory awareness, every breath, and every pulse of existence is Her direct, manifest appearance, blindingly obvious to anyone who truly looks."]},{"number":831,"name":"प्राणेश्वरी","samasa":["प्राणानामिन्द्रियाणामधिष्ठातृत्वादीश्वरी।","प्राणस्य पञ्चवृत्तिकस्याधिपतिर्वा।","प्रकृष्टोऽणः शब्दो वेदरूपस्तदीश्वरी तत्प्रतिपाद्यदेवता।"],"wordByWord":["प्राणानाम् — of the pranas or vital powers","इन्द्रियाणाम् — of the senses","अधिष्ठातृत्वात् — because of presiding over","ईश्वरी — ruler; governing goddess","प्राणस्य — of prana","पञ्चवृत्तिकस्य — having five functions","अधिपतिः — lord; ruler"],"summary":["प्राणेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the pranas. prāṇa also denotes the vital functions and the senses. Śrīdevī presides over them and directs their activity. She is also the deity indicated by the Vedic sound, which is the highest form of sacred speech."],"searchText":"831 प्राणेश्वरी प्राणानामिन्द्रियाणामधिष्ठातृत्वादीश्वरी। प्राणस्य पञ्चवृत्तिकस्याधिपतिर्वा। प्रकृष्टोऽणः शब्दो वेदरूपस्तदीश्वरी तत्प्रतिपाद्यदेवता। प्राणानाम् — of the pranas or vital powers इन्द्रियाणाम् — of the senses अधिष्ठातृत्वात् — because of presiding over ईश्वरी — ruler; governing goddess प्राणस्य — of prana पञ्चवृत्तिकस्य — having five functions अधिपतिः — lord; ruler प्राणेश्वरी means one who is the ruler of the pranas. prāṇa also denotes the vital functions and the senses. śrīdevī presides over them and directs their activity. she is also the deity indicated by the vedic sound, which is the highest form of sacred speech. the ruler of the five breaths: she is the supreme director governing the five-fold life current (prāṇa, apāna, vyāna, udāna, samāna). concurrently, she rules over the sensory apparatus networks (indriyas). under the phonic key, she is the inner consciousness targeted by the refined words of the veda (pra-aṇa).","esoteric":["The Ruler of the Five Breaths: She is the supreme director governing the five-fold life current (prāṇa, apāna, vyāna, udāna, samāna). Concurrently, She rules over the sensory apparatus networks (indriyas). Under the phonic key, She is the inner consciousness targeted by the refined words of the Veda (pra-aṇa)."]},{"number":832,"name":"प्राणदात्री","samasa":["प्राणानां दात्री।"],"wordByWord":["प्राणानाम् — of the pranas","दात्री — giver; bestower"],"summary":["प्राणदात्री means one who gives prana. All life-breath and vitality proceed from Her. The living being functions because She grants the vital force."],"searchText":"832 प्राणदात्री प्राणानां दात्री। प्राणानाम् — of the pranas दात्री — giver; bestower प्राणदात्री means one who gives prana. all life-breath and vitality proceed from her. the living being functions because she grants the vital force. the dispenser of vitality: she does not simply watch over the energy fields; she actively dispenses the actual currency of life-force (prāṇa) required to keep the physical tissues viable, ensuring that the biological framework remains integrated so the soul can complete its evolution.","esoteric":["The Dispenser of Vitality: She does not simply watch over the energy fields; She actively dispenses the actual currency of life-force (Prāṇa) required to keep the physical tissues viable, ensuring that the biological framework remains integrated so the soul can complete its evolution."]},{"number":833,"name":"पञ्चाशत्पीठरूपिणी","samasa":["कामरूपादिच्छायाछत्रान्तैकपञ्चाशत्पीठानि रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्चाशत् — fifty","पीठ — sacred seat or pitha","रूपिणी — whose form is","कामरूपादि — beginning with Kamarupa","छायाछत्रान्त — ending with Chayachatra","पीठानि — pithas; sacred seats"],"summary":["पञ्चाशत्पीठरूपिणी means one whose form is the fifty-one pithas. The sacred seats beginning with Kamarupa and ending with Chayachatra are Her own forms. Thus the entire field of Śakti worship is included in Her body."],"searchText":"833 पञ्चाशत्पीठरूपिणी कामरूपादिच्छायाछत्रान्तैकपञ्चाशत्पीठानि रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। पञ्चाशत् — fifty पीठ — sacred seat or pitha रूपिणी — whose form is कामरूपादि — beginning with kamarupa छायाछत्रान्त — ending with chayachatra पीठानि — pithas; sacred seats पञ्चाशत्पीठरूपिणी means one whose form is the fifty-one pithas. the sacred seats beginning with kamarupa and ending with chayachatra are her own forms. thus the entire field of śakti worship is included in her body. the geography of energy: the manifest landscape features fifty-one highly strategic energy vortexes (śākta-pīṭhas), running from kāmarūpa down to chāyāchhatra. internally, these seats correspond perfectly to the fifty-one phonic letters of the sanskrit alphabet (mātṛkā) distributed across the petals of the subtle body. she is the integrated grid that coordinates this entire layout.","esoteric":["The Geography of Energy: The manifest landscape features fifty-one highly strategic energy vortexes (Śākta-Pīṭhas), running from Kāmarūpa down to Chāyāchhatra. Internally, these seats correspond perfectly to the fifty-one phonic letters of the Sanskrit alphabet (Mātṛkā) distributed across the petals of the subtle body. She is the integrated grid that coordinates this entire layout."]},{"number":834,"name":"विश‍ृङ्खला","samasa":["विगता शृङ्खला यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वि — without; free from","शृङ्खला — chain; fetter","विगतशृङ्खला — one whose chain has gone","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["विश‍ृङ्खला means one who is free from chains. A chain indicates bondage, dependence or limitation. She is unbound, independent and beyond every fetter."],"searchText":"834 विश‍ृङ्खला विगता शृङ्खला यस्याः सा। वि — without; free from शृङ्खला — chain; fetter विगतशृङ्खला — one whose chain has gone यस्याः सा — she whose विश‍ृङ्खला means one who is free from chains. a chain indicates bondage, dependence or limitation. she is unbound, independent and beyond every fetter. the unconditioned infinite: human minds are bound by the iron chains of linear logic, social convention, and emotional filters. the physical world is bound by laws of limitation. she is viśṛṅkhalā because her essential nature stands completely past these boundary lines, operating with absolute, unrestricted freedom (svātantrya).","esoteric":["The Unconditioned Infinite: Human minds are bound by the iron chains of linear logic, social convention, and emotional filters. The physical world is bound by laws of limitation. She is Viśṛṅkhalā because Her essential nature stands completely past these boundary lines, operating with absolute, unrestricted freedom (Svātantrya)."]},{"number":835,"name":"विविक्तस्था","samasa":["विविक्ते पवित्रे विजने स्थले तिष्ठतीति।","विविक्ते आत्मानात्मविवेकशीलेषु तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["विविक्ते — in a pure, solitary or discriminating place","पवित्रे — in purity","विजने स्थले — in a secluded place","तिष्ठति — abides","आत्मानात्मविवेकशीलेषु — in those who discriminate Self and non-Self"],"summary":["विविक्तस्था means one who abides in solitude and purity. Vivikta also means discrimination between the Self and the non-Self. She is present in the pure place and in the minds of those established in discrimination."],"searchText":"835 विविक्तस्था विविक्ते पवित्रे विजने स्थले तिष्ठतीति। विविक्ते आत्मानात्मविवेकशीलेषु तिष्ठतीति। विविक्ते — in a pure, solitary or discriminating place पवित्रे — in purity विजने स्थले — in a secluded place तिष्ठति — abides आत्मानात्मविवेकशीलेषु — in those who discriminate self and non-self विविक्तस्था means one who abides in solitude and purity. vivikta also means discrimination between the self and the non-self. she is present in the pure place and in the minds of those established in discrimination. the coordinate of discernment: geometrically and physically, she loves silent, pure, and undisturbed spaces free from chaotic noise. internally, vivikta refers to the sharp, highly refined capacity to differentiate the eternal self from the transient non-self (आत्मानात्मविवेक). she stations herself directly inside intellects that possess this clarity.","esoteric":["The Coordinate of Discernment: Geometrically and physically, She loves silent, pure, and undisturbed spaces free from chaotic noise. Internally, Vivikta refers to the sharp, highly refined capacity to differentiate the eternal Self from the transient non-self (आत्मानात्मविवेक). She stations Herself directly inside intellects that possess this clarity."]},{"number":836,"name":"वीरमाता","samasa":["वीरा उपासकधुरन्धरा, रणे अभिमुखे हता वा। तेषां माता जननी।","वीरं मद्यस्य भाजने इति विश्वकोशात्पानपात्रं तन्मातीति"],"wordByWord":["वीराः — heroes; qualified worshippers","उपासकधुरन्धराः — eminent upasakas","माता — mother","जननी — mother; source","रणे अभिमुखे हताः — those who face battle and are slain"],"summary":["वीरमाता means mother of heroes. Vira means the heroic upasaka, one fit for the demanding path of worship. She is the mother and source of such courageous devotees."],"searchText":"836 वीरमाता वीरा उपासकधुरन्धरा, रणे अभिमुखे हता वा। तेषां माता जननी। वीरं मद्यस्य भाजने इति विश्वकोशात्पानपात्रं तन्मातीति वीराः — heroes; qualified worshippers उपासकधुरन्धराः — eminent upasakas माता — mother जननी — mother; source रणे अभिमुखे हताः — those who face battle and are slain वीरमाता means mother of heroes. vira means the heroic upasaka, one fit for the demanding path of worship. she is the mother and source of such courageous devotees. the mother of the fearless: vīras are those advanced, courageous practitioners (upāsaka-dhurandharāḥ) who treat spiritual practice as a martial campaign against their own internal limitations. she acts as their proud maternal source (mātā). under the agamic key, she is the intelligence that formats the sacred ritual vessel, containing the nectar of transformation.","esoteric":["The Mother of the Fearless: Vīras are those advanced, courageous practitioners (upāsaka-dhurandharāḥ) who treat spiritual practice as a martial campaign against their own internal limitations. She acts as their proud maternal source (Mātā). Under the Agamic key, She is the intelligence that formats the sacred ritual vessel, containing the nectar of transformation."]},{"number":837,"name":"वियत्प्रसूः","samasa":["वियत आकाशस्य प्रसूर्जनिका।"],"wordByWord":["वियत् — space; akasha","प्रसूः — mother; progenitress","जनिका — producer; mother"],"summary":["वियत्प्रसूः means mother of space. Viyat means akasha, the element of space. Space itself is born from Her; therefore She is the source of the subtle elements."],"searchText":"837 वियत्प्रसूः वियत आकाशस्य प्रसूर्जनिका। वियत् — space; akasha प्रसूः — mother; progenitress जनिका — producer; mother वियत्प्रसूः means mother of space. viyat means akasha, the element of space. space itself is born from her; therefore she is the source of the subtle elements. the sky before the sky: space (akāśa) is the first element projected during creation, providing the room within which the other elements can step down. she is viyatprasūḥ because she stands before this first boundary, acting as the parent consciousness that breathes out the space matrix itself.","esoteric":["The Sky before the Sky: Space (Akāśa) is the first element projected during creation, providing the room within which the other elements can step down. She is Viyatprasūḥ because She stands before this first boundary, acting as the parent consciousness that breathes out the space matrix itself."]},{"number":838,"name":"मुकुन्दा","samasa":["मुक्तिं ददातीति मुकुन्दा।","विष्णुरूपत्वाद्वा।"],"wordByWord":["मुक्तिम् — liberation","ददाति — gives","मुकुन्दा — giver of liberation","विष्णुरूपत्वात् — because of being in the form of Vishnu"],"summary":["मुकुन्दा means one who gives liberation. Mukunda is one who grants mukti. The name also recalls Her identity with Viṣṇu, who is traditionally called Mukunda."],"searchText":"838 मुकुन्दा मुक्तिं ददातीति मुकुन्दा। विष्णुरूपत्वाद्वा। मुक्तिम् — liberation ददाति — gives मुकुन्दा — giver of liberation विष्णुरूपत्वात् — because of being in the form of vishnu मुकुन्दा means one who gives liberation. mukunda is one who grants mukti. the name also recalls her identity with viṣṇu, who is traditionally called mukunda. the non-dual pervasive savior: mukunda is a celebrated title for lord viṣṇu as the savior who grants liberation. she is mukundā because she is completely identical with this preserving and liberating light field. she steps across nominal boundaries, confirming that the energy of viṣṇu is her own dynamic presence.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Pervasive Savior: Mukunda is a celebrated title for Lord Viṣṇu as the savior who grants liberation. She is Mukundā because She is completely identical with this preserving and liberating light field. She steps across nominal boundaries, confirming that the energy of Viṣṇu is Her own dynamic presence."]},{"number":839,"name":"मुक्तिनिलया","samasa":["मुक्तीनां पञ्चविधमोक्षाणां निलय आकरो यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["मुक्तीनाम् — of liberations","पञ्चविधमोक्षाणाम् — of the five kinds of moksha","निलयः — abode","आकरः — mine; source","यस्याम् सा — she in whom"],"summary":["मुक्तिनिलया means the abode of liberation. The five kinds of liberation rest in Her. She is both the giver and the resting-place of moksha."],"searchText":"839 मुक्तिनिलया मुक्तीनां पञ्चविधमोक्षाणां निलय आकरो यस्यां सा। मुक्तीनाम् — of liberations पञ्चविधमोक्षाणाम् — of the five kinds of moksha निलयः — abode आकरः — mine; source यस्याम् सा — she in whom मुक्तिनिलया means the abode of liberation. the five kinds of liberation rest in her. she is both the giver and the resting-place of moksha. the storehouse of the five freedoms: liberation is processed through five distinct functional stages: sālokya (sharing the realm), sāmīpya (proximity), sārūpya (similarity of form), sāyujya (complete absorption), and kaivalya (absolute non-dual oneness). she is muktinilayā because she acts as the definitive reservoir (ākaraḥ) containing all five states, serving as the final dock for the soul.","esoteric":["The Storehouse of the Five Freedoms: Liberation is processed through five distinct functional stages: Sālokya (sharing the realm), Sāmīpya (proximity), Sārūpya (similarity of form), Sāyujya (complete absorption), and Kaivalya (absolute non-dual oneness). She is Muktinilayā because She acts as the definitive reservoir (ākaraḥ) containing all five states, serving as the final dock for the soul."]},{"number":840,"name":"मूलविग्रहरूपिणी","samasa":["बालाबगलादिशक्तीनां मूलभूतो यो राजराजेश्वरीविग्रहः स एव रूपमस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मूल — root; original","विग्रहः — form; image","राजराजेश्वरीविग्रहः — the form of Rajarajeshwari","बालाबगलादिशक्तीनाम् — of Bala, Bagala and other Shaktis","रूपिणी — whose form is"],"summary":["मूलविग्रहरूपिणी means one whose form is the original image. The basic form of Rajarajeshwari is the source of Bālā, Bagala and the other Śaktis. All derivative deity-forms have their root in Her."],"searchText":"840 मूलविग्रहरूपिणी बालाबगलादिशक्तीनां मूलभूतो यो राजराजेश्वरीविग्रहः स एव रूपमस्याः सा। मूल — root; original विग्रहः — form; image राजराजेश्वरीविग्रहः — the form of rajarajeshwari बालाबगलादिशक्तीनाम् — of bala, bagala and other shaktis रूपिणी — whose form is मूलविग्रहरूपिणी means one whose form is the original image. the basic form of rajarajeshwari is the source of bālā, bagala and the other śaktis. all derivative deity-forms have their root in her. the source behind the ray-deities: the tradition projects thousands of specialized female deities—such as bālā, bagalāmukhī, vārāhī, and mātaṅgī—to run distinct cosmic lines. this name reveals that all these goddesses are partial rays branching out from a single central master structure. that original, primordial matrix body (mūla-vigraha) is ललिता महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी (lalitā mahā-tripurasundarī / rājarājeśvarī). she sits at the absolute core of this form, anchoring the entire system to her person.","esoteric":["The Source behind the Ray-Deities: The tradition projects thousands of specialized female deities—such as Bālā, Bagalāmukhī, Vārāhī, and Mātaṅgī—to run distinct cosmic lines. This name reveals that all these goddesses are partial rays branching out from a single central master structure. That original, primordial matrix body (Mūla-vigraha) is ललिता महात्रिपुरसुन्दरी (Lalitā Mahā-Tripurasundarī / Rājarājeśvarī). She sits at the absolute core of this form, anchoring the entire system to Her person."]},{"number":841,"name":"भावज्ञा","samasa":["षड्विकाराः षट्पदार्थाः, संसारः,  भवस्य शिवस्य इमे, भक्तिः, भाः कान्तिः तां वान्ति इति सूर्यादयः च भावाः। तान् जानातीति।"],"wordByWord":["भावान् — states, feelings or modes","जानाति — knows","भवस्य — of Bhava, Shiva or worldly existence","भक्तिः — devotion","भाः — light; brilliance","कान्तिः — lustre"],"summary":["भावज्ञा means one who knows all states and feelings. Bhava may mean change, worldly existence, Śiva, devotion, light, or the shining powers such as the Sun. She knows all these bhavas and the inner disposition of every devotee."],"searchText":"841 भावज्ञा षड्विकाराः षट्पदार्थाः, संसारः,  भवस्य शिवस्य इमे, भक्तिः, भाः कान्तिः तां वान्ति इति सूर्यादयः च भावाः। तान् जानातीति। भावान् — states, feelings or modes जानाति — knows भवस्य — of bhava, shiva or worldly existence भक्तिः — devotion भाः — light; brilliance कान्तिः — lustre भावज्ञा means one who knows all states and feelings. bhava may mean change, worldly existence, śiva, devotion, light, or the shining powers such as the sun. she knows all these bhavas and the inner disposition of every devotee. comprehending the inner context: she is bhāvajñā because she understands every possible definition of existence: the six transformations of matter (ṣaḍ-vikāra), the categories of logic, the currents of devotion (bhakti) in the heart, and the secret code rays belonging to lord śiva (bhava). she captures the true internal intent behind every manifestation.","esoteric":["Comprehending the Inner Context: She is Bhāvajñā because She understands every possible definition of existence: the six transformations of matter (ṣaḍ-vikāra), the categories of logic, the currents of devotion (bhakti) in the heart, and the secret code rays belonging to Lord Śiva (Bhava). She captures the true internal intent behind every manifestation."]},{"number":842,"name":"भवरोगघ्नी","samasa":["भवः संसार एव रोगस्तं हन्ति इति।"],"wordByWord":["भवः — worldly existence; samsara","संसारः — the cycle of worldly life","रोगः — disease","घ्नी — destroyer","तं हन्ति — destroys that"],"summary":["भवरोगघ्नी means one who destroys the disease of worldly existence. saṃsāra is compared to a disease because it causes repeated suffering. She cures that disease by giving knowledge and liberation."],"searchText":"842 भवरोगघ्नी भवः संसार एव रोगस्तं हन्ति इति। भवः — worldly existence; samsara संसारः — the cycle of worldly life रोगः — disease घ्नी — destroyer तं हन्ति — destroys that भवरोगघ्नी means one who destroys the disease of worldly existence. saṃsāra is compared to a disease because it causes repeated suffering. she cures that disease by giving knowledge and liberation. the medicine for rebirth: worldly existence (bhava) is not viewed merely as a political space; it is classified as a chronic, systemic psycho-spiritual disease (roga) that causes the soul to wander in friction. she acts as the ultimate physician, forcefully eradicating this root sickness and restoring the soul to its healthy state of pure consciousness.","esoteric":["The Medicine for Rebirth: Worldly existence (Bhava) is not viewed merely as a political space; it is classified as a chronic, systemic psycho-spiritual disease (roga) that causes the soul to wander in friction. She acts as the ultimate physician, forcefully eradicating this root sickness and restoring the soul to its healthy state of pure consciousness."]},{"number":843,"name":"भवचक्रप्रवर्तिनी","samasa":["भवचक्रं संसारमण्डलं प्रवर्ततीति।","भवचक्रवत्प्रवर्तयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["भवचक्रम् — wheel of becoming; wheel of samsara","संसारमण्डलम् — circle of worldly existence","प्रवर्तते — moves; turns","प्रवर्तयति — sets in motion"],"summary":["भवचक्रप्रवर्तिनी means one who sets the wheel of becoming in motion. Bhavachakra is the wheel of samsara. She turns this wheel as the power behind creation and worldly experience."],"searchText":"843 भवचक्रप्रवर्तिनी भवचक्रं संसारमण्डलं प्रवर्ततीति। भवचक्रवत्प्रवर्तयतीति। भवचक्रम् — wheel of becoming; wheel of samsara संसारमण्डलम् — circle of worldly existence प्रवर्तते — moves; turns प्रवर्तयति — sets in motion भवचक्रप्रवर्तिनी means one who sets the wheel of becoming in motion. bhavachakra is the wheel of samsara. she turns this wheel as the power behind creation and worldly experience. the director of the cosmic wheel: the universe passes through massive cyclical rotations—birth, growth, decay, and death—known as the भवचक्र (bhava-cakra — the wheel of shifting becoming). she stands at the absolute hub of this wheel, acting as the dynamic axis that keeps the entire wheel spinning to execute cosmic evolution.","esoteric":["The Director of the Cosmic Wheel: The universe passes through massive cyclical rotations—birth, growth, decay, and death—known as the भवचक्र (Bhava-cakra — the wheel of shifting becoming). She stands at the absolute hub of this wheel, acting as the dynamic axis that keeps the entire wheel spinning to execute cosmic evolution."]},{"number":844,"name":"छन्दःसारा","samasa":["छन्दःसु सारो निष्कर्षो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["छन्दःसु — in the Vedic metres or Vedas","सारः — essence","निष्कर्षः — extracted essence","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["छन्दःसारा means the essence of the Vedas as metre. Chandas refers to Vedic metres and to the Veda itself. She is the essential meaning and power hidden in the Vedic metres."],"searchText":"844 छन्दःसारा छन्दःसु सारो निष्कर्षो यस्याः सा। छन्दःसु — in the vedic metres or vedas सारः — essence निष्कर्षः — extracted essence यस्याः सा — she whose छन्दःसारा means the essence of the vedas as metre. chandas refers to vedic metres and to the veda itself. she is the essential meaning and power hidden in the vedic metres. the soul of the metric grid: छन्दस् (chandas) denotes the sacred rhythmic meters of the vedas (like gāyatrī or anuṣṭubh) that contain light frequencies. she is chandaḥsārā because she is the exact, concentrated distillation (sāra) of these meters, acting as the underlying acoustic pulse that makes scriptural revelation effective.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Metric Grid: छन्दस् (Chandas) denotes the sacred rhythmic meters of the Vedas (like Gāyatrī or Anuṣṭubh) that contain light frequencies. She is Chandaḥsārā because She is the exact, concentrated distillation (sāra) of these meters, acting as the underlying acoustic pulse that makes scriptural revelation effective."]},{"number":845,"name":"शास्त्रसारा","samasa":["शास्त्रं शास्त्रे वा सारो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शास्त्रम् — scripture","शास्त्रे — in scripture","सारः — essence","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["शास्त्रसारा means the essence of the scriptures. The shastras have value because they reveal Her and lead the devotee to Her. She is the core teaching contained in all sacred texts."],"searchText":"845 शास्त्रसारा शास्त्रं शास्त्रे वा सारो यस्याः सा। शास्त्रम् — scripture शास्त्रे — in scripture सारः — essence यस्याः सा — she whose शास्त्रसारा means the essence of the scriptures. the shastras have value because they reveal her and lead the devotee to her. she is the core teaching contained in all sacred texts. the ultimate scriptural conclusion: sacred texts contain extensive procedural instructions, debates, and local charts. she is śāstrasārā because if one strips away the conditional wrappers of all these sciences, the ultimate, non-dual essence left at the bottom is strictly her own nature, serving as the shared target of all true knowledge.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Scriptural Conclusion: Sacred texts contain extensive procedural instructions, debates, and local charts. She is Śāstrasārā because if one strips away the conditional wrappers of all these sciences, the ultimate, non-dual essence left at the bottom is strictly Her own nature, serving as the shared target of all true knowledge."]},{"number":846,"name":"मन्त्रसारा","samasa":["मन्त्राणि सारो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मन्त्राणि — mantras","सारः — essence","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["मन्त्रसारा means the essence of mantras. All mantras obtain their power from Her. She is the inner potency and meaning of every mantra."],"searchText":"846 मन्त्रसारा मन्त्राणि सारो यस्याः सा। मन्त्राणि — mantras सारः — essence यस्याः सा — she whose मन्त्रसारा means the essence of mantras. all mantras obtain their power from her. she is the inner potency and meaning of every mantra. the potency inside the syllables: thousands of mantras exist across the global grid. she is mantrasārā because she is the hidden, activating spark and the ultimate resonance (nāda) that gives these phonic structures their actual power, functioning as the crown energy inside the syllables.","esoteric":["The Potency inside the Syllables: Thousands of mantras exist across the global grid. She is Mantrasārā because She is the hidden, activating spark and the ultimate resonance (nāda) that gives these phonic structures their actual power, functioning as the crown energy inside the syllables."]},{"number":847,"name":"तलोदरी","samasa":["तलं करतलादि तद्वत्कृशं समं चोदरं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["तलम् — palm or flat surface","करतलादि — palm and similar flat things","कृशम् — slender","समम् — even; smooth","उदरम् — belly","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["तलोदरी means one whose belly is slender like the palm. Tala may mean the palm or a flat surface. The name is part of the description of Her graceful form."],"searchText":"847 तलोदरी तलं करतलादि तद्वत्कृशं समं चोदरं यस्याः सा। तलम् — palm or flat surface करतलादि — palm and similar flat things कृशम् — slender समम् — even; smooth उदरम् — belly यस्याः सा — she whose तलोदरी means one whose belly is slender like the palm. tala may mean the palm or a flat surface. the name is part of the description of her graceful form. the slenderness of causal space: her description as slim-waisted (talodarī) represents the absolute refinement and lack of gross material density at her core center. she is free from physical bloating, symbolizing the clean, highly compressed causal space where cosmic energy is gathered before its outward projection.","esoteric":["The Slenderness of Causal Space: Her description as slim-waisted (talodarī) represents the absolute refinement and lack of gross material density at Her core center. She is free from physical bloating, symbolizing the clean, highly compressed causal space where cosmic energy is gathered before its outward projection."]},{"number":848,"name":"उदारकीर्तिः","samasa":["उदारा महत्तरा कीर्तिर्यस्याः सा।","उत्कृष्टा आसमन्ताद्व्याप्ता च अरा शीघ्रसाध्या च कीर्तिर्यदुपासनया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["उदारा — noble; great","महत्तरा — very great","कीर्तिः — fame","व्याप्ता — spread; pervading","उपासना — worship"],"summary":["उदारकीर्तिः means one of noble fame. Her glory is vast, excellent and widely spread. Worship of Her quickly leads to honour, merit and spiritual fruit."],"searchText":"848 उदारकीर्तिः उदारा महत्तरा कीर्तिर्यस्याः सा। उत्कृष्टा आसमन्ताद्व्याप्ता च अरा शीघ्रसाध्या च कीर्तिर्यदुपासनया यस्याः सा। उदारा — noble; great महत्तरा — very great कीर्तिः — fame व्याप्ता — spread; pervading उपासना — worship उदारकीर्तिः means one of noble fame. her glory is vast, excellent and widely spread. worship of her quickly leads to honour, merit and spiritual fruit. the fame of boundless grace: her renown is udāra because it spreads without boundaries (vyāptā). her practice is अरा (arā — swiftly successful). by aligning with her system, the practitioner's inner merit and pure spiritual voice are amplified across the cosmic grid with extreme speed.","esoteric":["The Fame of Boundless Grace: Her renown is Udāra because it spreads without boundaries (vyāptā). Her practice is अरा (arā — swiftly successful). By aligning with Her system, the practitioner's inner merit and pure spiritual voice are amplified across the cosmic grid with extreme speed."]},{"number":849,"name":"उद्दामवैभवा","samasa":["दाम बन्धनरज्जुः परिच्छेत्री तदुत्क्रान्तमुद्दामेयत्तानवच्छिन्नं वैभवं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["दाम — cord; binding rope","बन्धनरज्जुः — rope of bondage","उद्दाम — beyond restraint; unbounded","वैभवम् — splendour; majesty","अनवच्छिन्नम् — unlimited"],"summary":["उद्दामवैभवा means one whose splendour is unbounded. Dama is a limiting cord; uddama means beyond limitation. Her majesty cannot be confined or measured."],"searchText":"849 उद्दामवैभवा दाम बन्धनरज्जुः परिच्छेत्री तदुत्क्रान्तमुद्दामेयत्तानवच्छिन्नं वैभवं यस्याः सा। दाम — cord; binding rope बन्धनरज्जुः — rope of bondage उद्दाम — beyond restraint; unbounded वैभवम् — splendour; majesty अनवच्छिन्नम् — unlimited उद्दामवैभवा means one whose splendour is unbounded. dama is a limiting cord; uddama means beyond limitation. her majesty cannot be confined or measured. sovereignty past the rope of metric: a dāma is a cord used to measure boundaries or bind animals. her cosmic majesty, structural capacity, and infinite glory (vaibhava) have completely broken past this rope (इयत्तानवच्छिन्नम्). her power cannot be computed, quantified, or restricted by any conceptual grid, standing completely absolute.","esoteric":["Sovereignty Past the Rope of Metric: A dāma is a cord used to measure boundaries or bind animals. Her cosmic majesty, structural capacity, and infinite glory (vaibhava) have completely broken past this rope (इयत्तानवच्छिन्नम्). Her power cannot be computed, quantified, or restricted by any conceptual grid, standing completely absolute."]},{"number":850,"name":"वर्णरूपिणी","samasa":["वर्णाश्चतुःषष्टिसंख्याका रूपमस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वर्णाः — letters or colours","चतुःषष्टिसंख्यकाः — sixty-four in number","रूपम् — form","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["वर्णरूपिणी means one whose form is the letters. The letters of the Sanskrit alphabet are Her forms. Speech, mantra and sacred sound all arise as Her manifestation."],"searchText":"850 वर्णरूपिणी वर्णाश्चतुःषष्टिसंख्याका रूपमस्याः सा। वर्णाः — letters or colours चतुःषष्टिसंख्यकाः — sixty-four in number रूपम् — form यस्याः सा — she whose वर्णरूपिणी means one whose form is the letters. the letters of the sanskrit alphabet are her forms. speech, mantra and sacred sound all arise as her manifestation. the phonic and chromatic synthesis: वर्ण (varṇa) operates on two simultaneous non-dual tracks: it signifies the absolute matrix of the sanskrit phonic alphabet (mātṛkā) that constructs all spoken mantras, and it signifies the primary color ray frequencies that format the visible universe. she is varṇarūpiṇī because her entire manifest body is composed of this integrated grid of light and sound, ensuring that every word spoken and every ray seen is a literal cell of her cosmic form.","esoteric":["The Phonic and Chromatic Synthesis: वर्ण (Varṇa) operates on two simultaneous non-dual tracks: it signifies the absolute matrix of the Sanskrit phonic alphabet (Mātṛkā) that constructs all spoken mantras, and it signifies the primary color ray frequencies that format the visible universe. She is Varṇarūpiṇī because Her entire manifest body is composed of this integrated grid of light and sound, ensuring that every word spoken and every ray seen is a literal cell of Her cosmic form."]},{"number":851,"name":"जन्ममृत्युजरातप्तजनविश्रान्तिदायिनी","samasa":["जन्ममृत्युजराभिः तप्तेभ्यो जनेभ्यो विश्रान्तिभिः विश्रान्तिं दत्ते इति।"],"wordByWord":["जन्म — birth","मृत्यु — death","जरा — old age","तप्तेभ्यः — to those afflicted","जनेभ्यः — to people","विश्रान्तिम् — rest; repose","दत्ते — gives"],"summary":["जन्ममृत्युजरातप्तजनविश्रान्तिदायिनी means one who gives rest to those scorched by birth, death and old age. Human life is afflicted by repeated birth, decay and death. She grants repose, relief and final peace to those tormented by this cycle."],"searchText":"851 जन्ममृत्युजरातप्तजनविश्रान्तिदायिनी जन्ममृत्युजराभिः तप्तेभ्यो जनेभ्यो विश्रान्तिभिः विश्रान्तिं दत्ते इति। जन्म — birth मृत्यु — death जरा — old age तप्तेभ्यः — to those afflicted जनेभ्यः — to people विश्रान्तिम् — rest; repose दत्ते — gives जन्ममृत्युजरातप्तजनविश्रान्तिदायिनी means one who gives rest to those scorched by birth, death and old age. human life is afflicted by repeated birth, decay and death. she grants repose, relief and final peace to those tormented by this cycle. the oasis of saṁsāra: worldly existence is characterized by a three-fold chronic friction—the trauma of birth, the anxiety of decay, and the terror of physical termination. living beings are continuously scorched (tapta) by this existential heat. she does not offer temporary worldly distractions; she acts as viśrāntidāyinī — the deep, cooling sanctuary of non-dual consciousness where the exhausted soul can dissolve its burdens and rest permanently.","esoteric":["The Oasis of Saṁsāra: Worldly existence is characterized by a three-fold chronic friction—the trauma of birth, the anxiety of decay, and the terror of physical termination. Living beings are continuously scorched (tapta) by this existential heat. She does not offer temporary worldly distractions; She acts as Viśrāntidāyinī — the deep, cooling sanctuary of non-dual consciousness where the exhausted soul can dissolve its burdens and rest permanently."]},{"number":852,"name":"सर्वोपनिषदुद्घुष्टा","samasa":["सर्वास्वैतरेयादिषूपनिषत्सु रहस्यभूतासु उत्कर्षेण धुष्टा प्रतिपाद्या।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वासु — in all","उपनिषत्सु — in the Upanishads","रहस्यभूतासु — being secret or esoteric","उत्कर्षेण — excellently; emphatically","प्रतिपाद्या — taught; expounded"],"summary":["सर्वोपनिषदुद्घुष्टा means one who is loudly proclaimed by all Upanishads. The secret teaching of the Upanishads points to Her supreme nature. She is the Reality established by the highest Vedantic revelation."],"searchText":"852 सर्वोपनिषदुद्घुष्टा सर्वास्वैतरेयादिषूपनिषत्सु रहस्यभूतासु उत्कर्षेण धुष्टा प्रतिपाद्या। सर्वासु — in all उपनिषत्सु — in the upanishads रहस्यभूतासु — being secret or esoteric उत्कर्षेण — excellently; emphatically प्रतिपाद्या — taught; expounded सर्वोपनिषदुद्घुष्टा means one who is loudly proclaimed by all upanishads. the secret teaching of the upanishads points to her supreme nature. she is the reality established by the highest vedantic revelation. the shared voice of the secrets: the upaniṣads (like the aitareya, taittirīya, or bṛhadāraṇyaka) are the highly guarded, secret texts concluding the vedas. she is not a localized, secondary goddess mentioned in passing. she is sarvopaniṣadudghuṣṭā because every single upaniṣadic dialogue, paradox, and mahāvākya is loudly proclaiming her essential nature as the non-dual absolute brahman.","esoteric":["The Shared Voice of the Secrets: The Upaniṣads (like the Aitareya, Taittirīya, or Bṛhadāraṇyaka) are the highly guarded, secret texts concluding the Vedas. She is not a localized, secondary goddess mentioned in passing. She is Sarvopaniṣadudghuṣṭā because every single Upaniṣadic dialogue, paradox, and mahāvākya is loudly proclaiming Her essential nature as the non-dual absolute Brahman."]},{"number":853,"name":"शान्त्यतीतकलात्मिका","samasa":["आकाशनिष्ठा कला शान्त्यतीतेत्युच्यते। शान्तिम् अतीता। सा च असौ कला च। तदात्मिका तदभिन्ना।"],"wordByWord":["शान्तिम् — peace or Shanti-kala","अतीता — beyond","कला — kala; digit; spiritual power","आत्मिका — whose nature is","तदभिन्ना — not different from that"],"summary":["शान्त्यतीतकलात्मिका means one whose form is the kala beyond Shanti. Shantyatita is the state beyond the Shanti-kala and is associated with the highest subtle principle. She is identical with that transcendent kala."],"searchText":"853 शान्त्यतीतकलात्मिका आकाशनिष्ठा कला शान्त्यतीतेत्युच्यते। शान्तिम् अतीता। सा च असौ कला च। तदात्मिका तदभिन्ना। शान्तिम् — peace or shanti-kala अतीता — beyond कला — kala; digit; spiritual power आत्मिका — whose nature is तदभिन्ना — not different from that शान्त्यतीतकलात्मिका means one whose form is the kala beyond shanti. shantyatita is the state beyond the shanti-kala and is associated with the highest subtle principle. she is identical with that transcendent kala. the strata past cosmic peace: in śāiva-śākta cosmology, the creative manifestation is mapped across five sequential energetic zones or digits: nivṛtti, pratiṣṭhā, vidyā, śānti, and शान्त्यतीता (śāntyatītā — that which completely passes beyond peace). the śānti layer governs the ether element and cosmic stillness. she is śāntyatītakalātmikā because she embodies the absolute, highest fifth stratum, anchored directly in the unconditioned transcendent space beyond structural stillness.","esoteric":["The Strata past Cosmic Peace: In Śāiva-Śākta cosmology, the creative manifestation is mapped across five sequential energetic zones or digits: Nivṛtti, Pratiṣṭhā, Vidyā, Śānti, and शान्त्यतीता (Śāntyatītā — that which completely passes beyond peace). The Śānti layer governs the ether element and cosmic stillness. She is Śāntyatītakalātmikā because She embodies the absolute, highest fifth stratum, anchored directly in the unconditioned transcendent space beyond structural stillness."]},{"number":854,"name":"गम्भीरा","samasa":["आनन्त्याद्गम्भीरा। महाह्रदस्वरूपेत्यर्थः"],"wordByWord":["आनन्त्यात् — because of infinitude","गम्भीरा — deep; profound","महाह्रदस्वरूपा — of the nature of a great lake"],"summary":["गम्भीरा means one who is profound. Her depth is compared to an immeasurable great lake. Because She is infinite, Her nature cannot be sounded by ordinary thought."],"searchText":"854 गम्भीरा आनन्त्याद्गम्भीरा। महाह्रदस्वरूपेत्यर्थः आनन्त्यात् — because of infinitude गम्भीरा — deep; profound महाह्रदस्वरूपा — of the nature of a great lake गम्भीरा means one who is profound. her depth is compared to an immeasurable great lake. because she is infinite, her nature cannot be sounded by ordinary thought. the great cosmic lake: she is gambhīrā because her consciousness field possesses absolute, shoreless infinity (ānantya). she resembles a massive, completely still, and bottomless deep lake (mahā-hrada). worldly thoughts and elements ripple only on the very surface; her depths remain unperturbed, solid, and silent, holding the universe in equilibrium.","esoteric":["The Great Cosmic Lake: She is Gambhīrā because Her consciousness field possesses absolute, shoreless infinity (ānantya). She resembles a massive, completely still, and bottomless deep lake (mahā-hrada). Worldly thoughts and elements ripple only on the very surface; Her depths remain unperturbed, solid, and silent, holding the universe in equilibrium."]},{"number":855,"name":"गगनान्तस्था","samasa":["गगनस्य दहराकाशस्य भूताकाशस्य पराकाशस्य वान्तर्मध्ये तिष्ठतीति।","गगनस्यान्ते नाशकालेऽपि तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["गगनस्य — of space","दहराकाशस्य — of the inner subtle space","भूताकाशस्य — of physical space","पराकाशस्य — of supreme space","अन्ते — at the end","तिष्ठति — abides"],"summary":["गगनान्तस्था means one who abides at the end of space. She exists within and beyond the spaces called daharakasha, bhutakasha and parakasha. Even at the dissolution of space She remains."],"searchText":"855 गगनान्तस्था गगनस्य दहराकाशस्य भूताकाशस्य पराकाशस्य वान्तर्मध्ये तिष्ठतीति। गगनस्यान्ते नाशकालेऽपि तिष्ठतीति। गगनस्य — of space दहराकाशस्य — of the inner subtle space भूताकाशस्य — of physical space पराकाशस्य — of supreme space अन्ते — at the end तिष्ठति — abides गगनान्तस्था means one who abides at the end of space. she exists within and beyond the spaces called daharakasha, bhutakasha and parakasha. even at the dissolution of space she remains. the space inside space: she positions herself inside (antara) every tier of space—the physical sky (bhūtākāśa), the internal heart sky (daharākāśa), and the supreme space of consciousness (parākāśa). the survivor of dissolution: alternatively, anta signifies termination. when the cosmic sky collapses and dissolves at the end of time, she continues to stand (sthā) past the destruction point, showing her absolute independence.","esoteric":["The Space inside Space: She positions Herself inside (antara) every tier of space—the physical sky (bhūtākāśa), the internal heart sky (daharākāśa), and the supreme space of consciousness (parākāśa).","The Survivor of Dissolution: Alternatively, anta signifies termination. When the cosmic sky collapses and dissolves at the end of time, She continues to stand (sthā) past the destruction point, showing Her absolute independence."]},{"number":856,"name":"गर्विता","samasa":["गर्वो विश्वनिर्माणविषयिणी पराहन्ता सास्याः सञ्जाता इति।"],"wordByWord":["गर्वः — pride; majesty; self-assertion","विश्वनिर्माणविषयिणी — relating to creation of the universe","पराहन्ता — supreme I-consciousness","सञ्जाता — arisen"],"summary":["गर्विता means one who possesses the supreme pride of creation. This is not ordinary egoistic pride but the cosmic ahamta by which the universe is manifested. She stands as the sovereign power behind creation."],"searchText":"856 गर्विता गर्वो विश्वनिर्माणविषयिणी पराहन्ता सास्याः सञ्जाता इति। गर्वः — pride; majesty; self-assertion विश्वनिर्माणविषयिणी — relating to creation of the universe पराहन्ता — supreme i-consciousness सञ्जाता — arisen गर्विता means one who possesses the supreme pride of creation. this is not ordinary egoistic pride but the cosmic ahamta by which the universe is manifested. she stands as the sovereign power behind creation. the absolute pride of creation: her \"pride\" (garva) is the magnificent cosmic consciousness of her own independent existence—the uncorrupted sense of पराहन्ता (parāhantā — the absolute cosmic \"i\"). it is the ecstatic awareness: \"i am the entire universe, and i alone project it.\" this majestic self-recognition initiates the creation process.","esoteric":["The Absolute Pride of Creation: Her \"pride\" (garva) is the magnificent cosmic consciousness of Her own independent existence—the uncorrupted sense of पराहन्ता (Parāhantā — the absolute cosmic \"I\"). It is the ecstatic awareness: \"I am the entire universe, and I alone project it.\" This majestic self-recognition initiates the creation process."]},{"number":857,"name":"गानलोलुपा","samasa":["गानं ततानद्धसुषिरघनचतुष्टयसमुच्चयात्मकम्, वादित्रादिकं वा, शरीरं गान्धर्वं वा, साम वा तयोर्लोलुपा सतृष्णा।"],"wordByWord":["गानम् — music or singing","वादित्रादिकम् — instruments and the like","गान्धर्वम् — Gandharva music","साम — Saman chant","लोलुपा — fond of; eager for"],"summary":["गानलोलुपा means one who is fond of music. Music includes vocal song, instruments, the Gandharva art and the Saman. She delights in sacred music and is pleased by musical worship."],"searchText":"857 गानलोलुपा गानं ततानद्धसुषिरघनचतुष्टयसमुच्चयात्मकम्, वादित्रादिकं वा, शरीरं गान्धर्वं वा, साम वा तयोर्लोलुपा सतृष्णा। गानम् — music or singing वादित्रादिकम् — instruments and the like गान्धर्वम् — gandharva music साम — saman chant लोलुपा — fond of; eager for गानलोलुपा means one who is fond of music. music includes vocal song, instruments, the gandharva art and the saman. she delights in sacred music and is pleased by musical worship. the affection for rhythmic order: गान (gāna) encompasses the four classical structural classes of musical instruments (stringed, percussion, wind, and solid bronze), the celestial gandharva arts, and the sacred melodies of the sāma veda. she is gānalolupā because these perfect acoustic structures are reflections of her own inner harmonic law, absorbing her attention into their beauty.","esoteric":["The Affection for Rhythmic Order: गान (Gāna) encompasses the four classical structural classes of musical instruments (stringed, percussion, wind, and solid bronze), the celestial Gandharva arts, and the sacred melodies of the Sāma Veda. She is Gānalolupā because these perfect acoustic structures are reflections of Her own inner harmonic law, absorbing Her attention into their beauty."]},{"number":858,"name":"कल्पनारहिता","samasa":["कल्पना वासनामय्यो दृश्यवीचयस्ताभी रहिता।","नरस्य इमे नाराः जीवाः। कल्पे अपि नाराणां हिताः।"],"wordByWord":["कल्पना — imagination; mental construction","वासनामय्यः — made of vasanas","दृश्यवीचयः — waves of perceived forms","रहिता — free from"],"summary":["कल्पनारहिता means one who is free from imagination or mental construction. Kalpana is the flow of vasana-born images and notions. Her supreme nature is beyond such mental projections."],"searchText":"858 कल्पनारहिता कल्पना वासनामय्यो दृश्यवीचयस्ताभी रहिता। नरस्य इमे नाराः जीवाः। कल्पे अपि नाराणां हिताः। कल्पना — imagination; mental construction वासनामय्यः — made of vasanas दृश्यवीचयः — waves of perceived forms रहिता — free from कल्पनारहिता means one who is free from imagination or mental construction. kalpana is the flow of vasana-born images and notions. her supreme nature is beyond such mental projections. the screen free from projections: कल्पना (kalpanā) refers to the subconscious ripples, latent impressions (vāsanās), and conceptual partitions that fragment pure consciousness into objects. she is kalpanārahitā because her essential nature is completely still and unconditioned. she is the baseline awareness screen that lacks any internal projections, remaining perfectly whole.","esoteric":["The Screen Free from Projections: कल्पना (Kalpanā) refers to the subconscious ripples, latent impressions (vāsanās), and conceptual partitions that fragment pure consciousness into objects. She is Kalpanārahitā because Her essential nature is completely still and unconditioned. She is the baseline awareness screen that lacks any internal projections, remaining perfectly whole."]},{"number":859,"name":"काष्ठा","samasa":["अष्टादशनिमेषात्मकः कालः काष्ठा। दारुहरिद्रापि काष्ठा। तदुभयरूपा।","वेदान्तवाक्यार्थतत्त्वनिष्कर्षोऽपि काष्ठा।","गगनात्मकस्य भीमनामकस्य परशिवस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["काष्ठा — measure of time; limit; culmination","कालः — time","दारुहरिद्रा — wood-turmeric","वेदान्तवाक्यार्थतत्त्वनिष्कर्षः — final essence of Vedantic sentences"],"summary":["काष्ठा means one who is the limit or culmination. Kashtha may mean a measure of time, wood or turmeric, and also the final conclusion of Vedantic truth. She is the ultimate limit to which scriptural enquiry leads."],"searchText":"859 काष्ठा अष्टादशनिमेषात्मकः कालः काष्ठा। दारुहरिद्रापि काष्ठा। तदुभयरूपा। वेदान्तवाक्यार्थतत्त्वनिष्कर्षोऽपि काष्ठा। गगनात्मकस्य भीमनामकस्य परशिवस्य पत्नी। काष्ठा — measure of time; limit; culmination कालः — time दारुहरिद्रा — wood-turmeric वेदान्तवाक्यार्थतत्त्वनिष्कर्षः — final essence of vedantic sentences काष्ठा means one who is the limit or culmination. kashtha may mean a measure of time, wood or turmeric, and also the final conclusion of vedantic truth. she is the ultimate limit to which scriptural enquiry leads. the pinnacle of realization: kāṣṭhā denotes the absolute ceiling, ultimate limit, or final summary of a pursuit. she is the final conclusion (niṣkarṣa) targeted by all vedāntic statements. the pulse of time and form: she manifests as the precise micro-unit of temporal measurement (18 blinks of an eye), formats the cleansing properties of nature's herbs, and acts as the consort to shiva's expansive cosmic sky form (bhīma).","esoteric":["The Pinnacle of Realization: Kāṣṭhā denotes the absolute ceiling, ultimate limit, or final summary of a pursuit. She is the final conclusion (niṣkarṣa) targeted by all Vedāntic statements.","The Pulse of Time and Form: She manifests as the precise micro-unit of temporal measurement (18 blinks of an eye), formats the cleansing properties of nature's herbs, and acts as the consort to Shiva's expansive cosmic sky form (Bhīma)."]},{"number":860,"name":"अकान्ता","samasa":["अकं पापे च दुःखे च तयोरन्तो नाशो यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["अकम् — sin and sorrow","पापे — in sin","दुःखे — in sorrow","अन्तः — end; destruction","नाशः — destruction","यया सा — she by whom"],"summary":["अकान्ता means one who ends sin and sorrow. The name may be read as She by whom the end of sin and suffering is brought about. She removes the pain and impurities of devotees."],"searchText":"860 अकान्ता अकं पापे च दुःखे च तयोरन्तो नाशो यया सा। अकम् — sin and sorrow पापे — in sin दुःखे — in sorrow अन्तः — end; destruction नाशः — destruction यया सा — she by whom अकान्ता means one who ends sin and sorrow. the name may be read as she by whom the end of sin and suffering is brought about. she removes the pain and impurities of devotees. the solvent of karmic pain: अक (aka) is a classical lexicon code for the dual friction of moral error (pāpa) and its resulting existential pain (duḥkha). she is akāntā because her entry into the practitioner's consciousness acts as a powerful solvent that systematically brings this entire duplicate channel of suffering to an absolute end (anta).","esoteric":["The Solvent of Karmic Pain: अक (aka) is a classical lexicon code for the dual friction of moral error (pāpa) and its resulting existential pain (duḥkha). She is Akāntā because Her entry into the practitioner's consciousness acts as a powerful solvent that systematically brings this entire duplicate channel of suffering to an absolute end (anta)."]},{"number":861,"name":"कान्तार्धविग्रहा","samasa":["कान्तः परशिव एवार्धविग्रहो यस्याः सा।","कान्तस्यार्धं कान्तार्धम्, कान्तार्धं विग्रहो यस्याः सा।","ककारस्यान्तः कान्तः खकारस्तेन द्यौर्लक्ष्यते। अर्धशब्दो भागमात्रपरः। तेन द्यौः शरीरैकदेशो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कान्तः — beloved; Parashiva","अर्ध — half","विग्रहः — body; form","कान्तार्धविग्रहा — she whose body is half of Her beloved"],"summary":["कान्तार्धविग्रहा means one whose body is half of Her beloved. Her beloved is Parashiva, and She shares His form. The name indicates the non-separation of Śiva and Śakti."],"searchText":"861 कान्तार्धविग्रहा कान्तः परशिव एवार्धविग्रहो यस्याः सा। कान्तस्यार्धं कान्तार्धम्, कान्तार्धं विग्रहो यस्याः सा। ककारस्यान्तः कान्तः खकारस्तेन द्यौर्लक्ष्यते। अर्धशब्दो भागमात्रपरः। तेन द्यौः शरीरैकदेशो यस्याः सा। कान्तः — beloved; parashiva अर्ध — half विग्रहः — body; form कान्तार्धविग्रहा — she whose body is half of her beloved कान्तार्धविग्रहा means one whose body is half of her beloved. her beloved is parashiva, and she shares his form. the name indicates the non-separation of śiva and śakti. the sovereign half: this name highlights the iconic अर्धनारीश्वर (ardhanārīśvara) manifestation where shiva and shakti occupy a single structural body. she forms the left half of the display. कान्त also means the letter kha, which is a code for the infinite sky (dyauḥ), proving that her body incorporates the spatial heavens.","esoteric":["The Sovereign Half: This name highlights the iconic अर्धनारीश्वर (Ardhanārīśvara) manifestation where Shiva and Shakti occupy a single structural body. She forms the left half of the display. कान्त also means the letter Kha, which is a code for the infinite sky (Dyauḥ), proving that Her body incorporates the spatial heavens."]},{"number":862,"name":"कार्यकारणनिर्मुक्ता","samasa":["कार्याणि महत्त्वादीनि कारणं मूलप्रकृतिः तैर्निर्मुक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["कार्याणि — effects","महत्त्वादीनि — mahat and the rest","कारणम् — cause","मूलप्रकृतिः — primal nature","निर्मुक्ता — free from"],"summary":["कार्यकारणनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from cause and effect. Effects such as mahat and causes such as mulaprakriti do not bind Her. She transcends the entire chain of causation."],"searchText":"862 कार्यकारणनिर्मुक्ता कार्याणि महत्त्वादीनि कारणं मूलप्रकृतिः तैर्निर्मुक्ता। कार्याणि — effects महत्त्वादीनि — mahat and the rest कारणम् — cause मूलप्रकृतिः — primal nature निर्मुक्ता — free from कार्यकारणनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from cause and effect. effects such as mahat and causes such as mulaprakriti do not bind her. she transcends the entire chain of causation. beyond causal dependency: in material transformation (sāṅkhya cosmology), the universe shifts from the unmanifested cause (mūlaprakṛti) down to the manifested effects (mahat, elements). she is kāryakāraṇanirmuktā because her essential unconditioned reality as parabrahman sits entirely outside this wheel of dependency. she remains unaffected by changes, causes, or historical outcomes.","esoteric":["Beyond Causal Dependency: In material transformation (Sāṅkhya cosmology), the universe shifts from the unmanifested cause (Mūlaprakṛti) down to the manifested effects (Mahat, elements). She is Kāryakāraṇanirmuktā because Her essential unconditioned reality as Parabrahman sits entirely outside this wheel of dependency. She remains unaffected by changes, causes, or historical outcomes."]},{"number":863,"name":"कामकेलितरङ्गिता","samasa":["कामस्य कामेश्वरस्य केलीनां क्रीडाविलासानां तरङ्गाः परम्पराः सञ्जाता अस्याः इति।"],"wordByWord":["कामस्य — of Kama or Kameshwara","केलीनाम् — of sports or plays","क्रीडाविलासानाम् — of playful enjoyments","तरङ्गाः — waves","परम्पराः — series; succession"],"summary":["कामकेलितरङ्गिता means one who is rippled by the play of Kāmeśvara. The sport of Kāmeśvara is expressed as waves of divine play. She is moved by that current of love and creative delight."],"searchText":"863 कामकेलितरङ्गिता कामस्य कामेश्वरस्य केलीनां क्रीडाविलासानां तरङ्गाः परम्पराः सञ्जाता अस्याः इति। कामस्य — of kama or kameshwara केलीनाम् — of sports or plays क्रीडाविलासानाम् — of playful enjoyments तरङ्गाः — waves परम्पराः — series; succession कामकेलितरङ्गिता means one who is rippled by the play of kāmeśvara. the sport of kāmeśvara is expressed as waves of divine play. she is moved by that current of love and creative delight. the waves of absolute delight: कामकेलि refers to the unceasing, ecstatic creative interactions between her dynamic energy and lord kāmeśvara (pure consciousness). this interaction is not a static event; it surges in continuous, interwoven waves (taraṅga) that manifest as the unfolding patterns of universes, filling reality with dynamic joy.","esoteric":["The Waves of Absolute Delight: कामकेलि refers to the unceasing, ecstatic creative interactions between Her dynamic energy and Lord Kāmeśvara (pure consciousness). This interaction is not a static event; it surges in continuous, interwoven waves (taraṅga) that manifest as the unfolding patterns of universes, filling reality with dynamic joy."]},{"number":864,"name":"कनत्कनकताटङ्का","samasa":["कनती दीप्यमाने कनकस्य सुवर्णमये ताटङ्के कर्णाभरणविशेषौ यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["कनत् — shining","कनक — gold","ताटङ्के — large earrings","कर्णाभरणविशेषौ — special ear ornaments","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["कनत्कनकताटङ्का means one who wears shining golden Tatankas. Her earrings are made of bright gold and shine beautifully. The name continues the description of Her auspicious ornamented form."],"searchText":"864 कनत्कनकताटङ्का कनती दीप्यमाने कनकस्य सुवर्णमये ताटङ्के कर्णाभरणविशेषौ यस्याः सा। कनत् — shining कनक — gold ताटङ्के — large earrings कर्णाभरणविशेषौ — special ear ornaments यस्याः सा — she whose कनत्कनकताटङ्का means one who wears shining golden tatankas. her earrings are made of bright gold and shine beautifully. the name continues the description of her auspicious ornamented form. the orbs of sun and moon: her circular ear-ornaments (tāṭaṅka) are not mundane jewelry; they are the literal visual manifestations of the सूर्य (sun) and चन्द्र (moon) orbs spinning at the sides of her countenance. their continuous, radiant golden vibration (kanat) metrics illuminate and maintain the boundaries of time across the macrocosmic grid.","esoteric":["The Orbs of Sun and Moon: Her circular ear-ornaments (tāṭaṅka) are not mundane jewelry; they are the literal visual manifestations of the सूर्य (Sun) and चन्द्र (Moon) orbs spinning at the sides of Her countenance. Their continuous, radiant golden vibration (kanat) metrics illuminate and maintain the boundaries of time across the macrocosmic grid."]},{"number":865,"name":"लीलाविग्रहधारिणी","samasa":["लीलयाऽनायासेन विग्रहानवतारविशेषान्धारयतीति।","पद्मराजस्य महिषी लीलादेवी तद्विग्रहधारिणीति।"],"wordByWord":["लीलया — playfully; effortlessly","अनायासेन — without effort","विग्रहान् — forms; embodiments","अवतारविशेषान् — special incarnations","धारयति — assumes; bears"],"summary":["लीलाविग्रहधारिणी means one who assumes forms as divine play. She takes incarnations and special forms effortlessly, without compulsion. Her manifestations are lilas, acts of spontaneous grace."],"searchText":"865 लीलाविग्रहधारिणी लीलयाऽनायासेन विग्रहानवतारविशेषान्धारयतीति। पद्मराजस्य महिषी लीलादेवी तद्विग्रहधारिणीति। लीलया — playfully; effortlessly अनायासेन — without effort विग्रहान् — forms; embodiments अवतारविशेषान् — special incarnations धारयति — assumes; bears लीलाविग्रहधारिणी means one who assumes forms as divine play. she takes incarnations and special forms effortlessly, without compulsion. her manifestations are lilas, acts of spontaneous grace. effortless morphological descent: when cosmic balance requires an anthropomorphic descent (avatāra), she does not experience structural constraint or karmic binding. it is a spontaneous, completely effortless expression of her playful energy (līlā). she assumes physical geometry as easily as a actor changes garments, maintaining her complete transcendent purity underneath.","esoteric":["Effortless Morphological Descent: When cosmic balance requires an anthropomorphic descent (Avatāra), She does not experience structural constraint or karmic binding. It is a spontaneous, completely effortless expression of Her playful energy (līlā). She assumes physical geometry as easily as a actor changes garments, maintaining Her complete transcendent purity underneath."]},{"number":866,"name":"अजा","samasa":["न जायते इति अजा।"],"wordByWord":["अजा — unborn","न जायते — is not born"],"summary":["अजा means one who is unborn. Aja means that She is never born. Though She manifests in many forms, in truth She is beyond birth."],"searchText":"866 अजा न जायते इति अजा। अजा — unborn न जायते — is not born अजा means one who is unborn. aja means that she is never born. though she manifests in many forms, in truth she is beyond birth. the uncreated source: everything in the material world has a start date, an origin point, and a cause that brought it forth. she is ajā because she stands completely outside this birth framework. lacking a beginning, she is the eternal, uncreated source that brings forth creation while remaining unborn herself.","esoteric":["The Uncreated Source: Everything in the material world has a start date, an origin point, and a cause that brought it forth. She is Ajā because She stands completely outside this birth framework. Lacking a beginning, She is the eternal, uncreated source that brings forth creation while remaining unborn Herself."]},{"number":867,"name":"क्षयविनिर्मुक्ता","samasa":["क्षयेण मरणेन विनिर्मुक्ता।","क्षये गृह एव विशिष्य निर्मुक्ता यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["क्षयेण — by decay or death","मरणेन — by death","विनिर्मुक्ता — completely free"],"summary":["क्षयविनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from decay and destruction. Kshaya means wasting, death or loss. She is untouched by decay and remains ever complete."],"searchText":"867 क्षयविनिर्मुक्ता क्षयेण मरणेन विनिर्मुक्ता। क्षये गृह एव विशिष्य निर्मुक्ता यया सा। क्षयेण — by decay or death मरणेन — by death विनिर्मुक्ता — completely free क्षयविनिर्मुक्ता means one who is free from decay and destruction. kshaya means wasting, death or loss. she is untouched by decay and remains ever complete. the exhaustion-free baseline: physical elements wear out, stars exhaust their fuel, and biological systems undergo systemic decay (kṣaya). she is kṣayavinirmuktā because her unconditioned consciousness field is completely immune to reduction. she remains whole, unexhausted, and structurally stable across all transitions.","esoteric":["The Exhaustion-Free Baseline: Physical elements wear out, stars exhaust their fuel, and biological systems undergo systemic decay (kṣaya). She is Kṣayavinirmuktā because Her unconditioned consciousness field is completely immune to reduction. She remains whole, unexhausted, and structurally stable across all transitions."]},{"number":868,"name":"मुग्धा/अमुग्धा","samasa":["सङ्गं मोमोक्षतीति मुग्धा।","अकारप्रश्लेषेण न सन्ति मूढा यस्या इति अमुग्धा।"],"wordByWord":["मुग्धा — one who releases; also innocent","सङ्गम् — attachment","मोमोक्षति — seeks to release","अमुग्धा — not deluded","मूढाः — deluded ones"],"summary":["मुग्धा/अमुग्धा means one who is Mugdha or Amugdha. Mugdha can indicate one who releases bondage, while Amugdha means not deluded. She is free from dullness and removes the delusion of devotees."],"searchText":"868 मुग्धा/अमुग्धा सङ्गं मोमोक्षतीति मुग्धा। अकारप्रश्लेषेण न सन्ति मूढा यस्या इति अमुग्धा। मुग्धा — one who releases; also innocent सङ्गम् — attachment मोमोक्षति — seeks to release अमुग्धा — not deluded मूढाः — deluded ones मुग्धा/अमुग्धा means one who is mugdha or amugdha. mugdha can indicate one who releases bondage, while amugdha means not deluded. she is free from dullness and removes the delusion of devotees. artless grace and direct clarity: as mugdhā, she displays a beautiful, pristine, and artless grace that captivates the cosmos. when read as amugdhā, it confirms that she never experiences internal confusion or intellectual delusion (mūḍha-rahitā), standing secure in her absolute clarity.","esoteric":["Artless Grace and Direct Clarity: As Mugdhā, She displays a beautiful, pristine, and artless grace that captivates the cosmos. When read as Amugdhā, it confirms that She never experiences internal confusion or intellectual delusion (mūḍha-rahitā), standing secure in Her absolute clarity."]},{"number":869,"name":"क्षिप्रप्रसादिनी","samasa":["क्षिप्रं स्वल्पदिनैरेव प्रसीदतीति।"],"wordByWord":["क्षिप्रम् — quickly","स्वल्पदिनैः — in a short time","प्रसीदति — becomes pleased","प्रसादिनी — gracious one"],"summary":["क्षिप्रप्रसादिनी means one who is quickly pleased. She grants grace in a short time to sincere worshippers. Her compassion is immediate when worship is offered with devotion."],"searchText":"869 क्षिप्रप्रसादिनी क्षिप्रं स्वल्पदिनैरेव प्रसीदतीति। क्षिप्रम् — quickly स्वल्पदिनैः — in a short time प्रसीदति — becomes pleased प्रसादिनी — gracious one क्षिप्रप्रसादिनी means one who is quickly pleased. she grants grace in a short time to sincere worshippers. her compassion is immediate when worship is offered with devotion. the high-velocity response: some spiritual paths require lifetimes of complex mechanical loops before a signal of grace is received. she is k kṣipraprasādinī because if the practitioner's surrender is authentic and their internal alignment is clean, her response is immediate. she does not delay, instantly opening her gate to elevate the seeker.","esoteric":["The High-Velocity Response: Some spiritual paths require lifetimes of complex mechanical loops before a signal of grace is received. She is K Kṣipraprasādinī because if the practitioner's surrender is authentic and their internal alignment is clean, Her response is immediate. She does not delay, instantly opening Her gate to elevate the seeker."]},{"number":870,"name":"अन्तर्मुखसमाराध्या","samasa":["अन्तःस्वात्मप्रणवं मुखं चित्तवृत्तिर्येषां ते। तैः सम्यगाराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["अन्तः — within","स्वात्मप्रणवम् — inner Self and pranava","मुखम् — face; direction","चित्तवृत्तिः — mental mode","सम्यक् आराध्या — properly worshipped"],"summary":["अन्तर्मुखसमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by those turned inward. The inward-facing worshipper has the mind directed to the inner Self and pranava. She is rightly worshipped through inward contemplation."],"searchText":"870 अन्तर्मुखसमाराध्या अन्तःस्वात्मप्रणवं मुखं चित्तवृत्तिर्येषां ते। तैः सम्यगाराध्या। अन्तः — within स्वात्मप्रणवम् — inner self and pranava मुखम् — face; direction चित्तवृत्तिः — mental mode सम्यक् आराध्या — properly worshipped अन्तर्मुखसमाराध्या means one who is worshipped by those turned inward. the inward-facing worshipper has the mind directed to the inner self and pranava. she is rightly worshipped through inward contemplation. the internal alignment: antarmukha describes that condition where the active mental modifications (citta-vṛtti) have ceased chasing external objects, turning 180 degrees backward to track the internal self. she is samārādhyā within this specific field. she cannot be captured by outward displays, opening her presence strictly to those who explore the inner silence.","esoteric":["The Internal Alignment: Antarmukha describes that condition where the active mental modifications (citta-vṛtti) have ceased chasing external objects, turning 180 degrees backward to track the internal Self. She is Samārādhyā within this specific field. She cannot be captured by outward displays, opening Her presence strictly to those who explore the inner silence."]},{"number":871,"name":"बहिर्मुखसुदुर्लभा","samasa":["बहिर्विषयैकप्रवणं मुखं येषां ते। तेषां सुष्ठु दुर्लभा।"],"wordByWord":["बहिः — outward","विषयैकप्रवणम् — inclined only to objects","मुखम् — face; orientation","सुदुर्लभा — very difficult to attain"],"summary":["बहिर्मुखसुदुर्लभा means one who is very difficult for the outward-facing. Those whose minds run only after external objects do not easily attain Her. She is found by inwardness, not by outward distraction."],"searchText":"871 बहिर्मुखसुदुर्लभा बहिर्विषयैकप्रवणं मुखं येषां ते। तेषां सुष्ठु दुर्लभा। बहिः — outward विषयैकप्रवणम् — inclined only to objects मुखम् — face; orientation सुदुर्लभा — very difficult to attain बहिर्मुखसुदुर्लभा means one who is very difficult for the outward-facing. those whose minds run only after external objects do not easily attain her. she is found by inwardness, not by outward distraction. the locked gate of externalism: when an observer's intellect remains completely driven by external objects, sensory desires, and material differences (bahir-mukha), they are moving away from the source. she is sudurlabhā to this state of mind. no amount of aggressive external calculation can uncover her, as long as the internal coordinates remain neglected.","esoteric":["The Locked Gate of Externalism: When an observer's intellect remains completely driven by external objects, sensory desires, and material differences (bahir-mukha), they are moving away from the source. She is Sudurlabhā to this state of mind. No amount of aggressive external calculation can uncover Her, as long as the internal coordinates remain neglected."]},{"number":872,"name":"त्रयी","samasa":["वेदत्रयरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["त्रयी — the three Vedas","वेदत्रय — the triad of Vedas","रूपा — whose form is"],"summary":["त्रयी means one who is the three Vedas. Trayi refers to the Vedic triad. She is the very form of Vedic revelation."],"searchText":"872 त्रयी वेदत्रयरूपा। त्रयी — the three vedas वेदत्रय — the triad of vedas रूपा — whose form is त्रयी means one who is the three vedas. trayi refers to the vedic triad. she is the very form of vedic revelation. the soul of the three vedas: she is the living phonic embodiment of the त्रयी (trayī — the corporate triad of the ṛg, yajur, and sāma vedas). she is not a post-vedic addition; she is the code, the metric grid, and the dynamic resonance running through these primary revelations, formatting the laws of nature.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Three Vedas: She is the living phonic embodiment of the त्रयी (Trayī — the corporate triad of the Ṛg, Yajur, and Sāma Vedas). She is not a post-Vedic addition; She is the code, the metric grid, and the dynamic resonance running through these primary revelations, formatting the laws of nature."]},{"number":873,"name":"त्रिवर्गनिलया","samasa":["त्रिवर्गो धर्मकामार्थैरिति कोशः। तस्य निलयः स्थानं यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["त्रिवर्गः — dharma, artha and kama","धर्म — righteousness","काम — desire","अर्थ — wealth or purpose","निलयः — abode"],"summary":["त्रिवर्गनिलया means the abode of the three aims. Trivarga means dharma, artha and kama. These aims of life rest in Her and are fulfilled through Her grace."],"searchText":"873 त्रिवर्गनिलया त्रिवर्गो धर्मकामार्थैरिति कोशः। तस्य निलयः स्थानं यस्यां सा। त्रिवर्गः — dharma, artha and kama धर्म — righteousness काम — desire अर्थ — wealth or purpose निलयः — abode त्रिवर्गनिलया means the abode of the three aims. trivarga means dharma, artha and kama. these aims of life rest in her and are fulfilled through her grace. the sanctuary of balanced aspiration: she does not simply stand as a distant destination for ascetics. she is trivarganilayā because she acts as the absolute home and organizing source within which धर्म (virtue), अर्थ (stability), and काम (desire) find their proper coordinates, keeping human life in equilibrium.","esoteric":["The Sanctuary of Balanced Aspiration: She does not simply stand as a distant destination for ascetics. She is Trivarganilayā because She acts as the absolute home and organizing source within which धर्म (virtue), अर्थ (stability), and काम (desire) find their proper coordinates, keeping human life in equilibrium."]},{"number":874,"name":"त्रिस्था","samasa":["त्रिषु भूतादिकालेष्वकारोकारमकारेषु वा स्था स्थितिर्यस्याः सा।","त्रिषु लोकादिष्वभेदेन तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["त्रिषु — in three","भूतादिकालेषु — in the three times","अकारोकारमकारेषु — in A, U and M","स्थितिः — abiding","लोकादिषु — in worlds and the like"],"summary":["त्रिस्था means one who abides in the three. She stands in the three times, the three letters a-u-m, or the three worlds. She pervades every threefold principle without separation."],"searchText":"874 त्रिस्था त्रिषु भूतादिकालेष्वकारोकारमकारेषु वा स्था स्थितिर्यस्याः सा। त्रिषु लोकादिष्वभेदेन तिष्ठतीति। त्रिषु — in three भूतादिकालेषु — in the three times अकारोकारमकारेषु — in a, u and m स्थितिः — abiding लोकादिषु — in worlds and the like त्रिस्था means one who abides in the three. she stands in the three times, the three letters a-u-m, or the three worlds. she pervades every threefold principle without separation. the pervader of the triple states: she stands anchored uniformly across the three tenses of time (past, present, future), lives inside the three phonemes of the praṇava (अ, उ, म), and permeates the three states of human consciousness (jāgrat, svapna, suṣupti) without structural cleavage.","esoteric":["The Pervader of the Triple States: She stands anchored uniformly across the three tenses of time (past, present, future), lives inside the three phonemes of the Praṇava (अ, उ, म), and permeates the three states of human consciousness (jāgrat, svapna, suṣupti) without structural cleavage."]},{"number":875,"name":"त्रिपुरमालिनी","samasa":["त्रीणि पुराणि दलावृत्तयोयस्याः सा। सा चासौ मालिनी च।"],"wordByWord":["त्रीणि — three","पुराणि — cities or enclosures","मालिनी — garlanded one; Malini","त्रिपुरमालिनी — Malini of the three cities"],"summary":["त्रिपुरमालिनी means tripuramalini. She is related to the three cities or the three enclosures and is also Malini. The name belongs to the Śrī vidyā tradition and points to Her as the garlanded power of Tripurā."],"searchText":"875 त्रिपुरमालिनी त्रीणि पुराणि दलावृत्तयोयस्याः सा। सा चासौ मालिनी च। त्रीणि — three पुराणि — cities or enclosures मालिनी — garlanded one; malini त्रिपुरमालिनी — malini of the three cities त्रिपुरमालिनी means tripuramalini. she is related to the three cities or the three enclosures and is also malini. the name belongs to the śrī vidyā tradition and points to her as the garlanded power of tripurā. the ruler of the triadic garland: in the layout of the śrī yantra, tripuramālinī is the specific presiding goddess placed in absolute charge of the sixth major enclosure—the अन्तरदशार चक्र (antardaśāra cakra — the inner circle of ten radiant triangles). she represents that exact protective frequency, wearing the triadic garland of cosmic letters.","esoteric":["The Ruler of the Triadic Garland: In the layout of the Śrī Yantra, Tripuramālinī is the specific presiding goddess placed in absolute charge of the sixth major enclosure—the अन्तरदशार चक्र (Antardaśāra Cakra — the inner circle of ten radiant triangles). She represents that exact protective frequency, wearing the triadic garland of cosmic letters."]},{"number":876,"name":"निरामया","samasa":["निर्गता आमया रोगा यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गता — gone; removed","आमयाः — diseases","रोगाः — illnesses","निरामया — free from disease"],"summary":["निरामया means one who is free from disease. Amaya means disease or affliction. She is free from every defect and removes the diseases of worldly life."],"searchText":"876 निरामया निर्गता आमया रोगा यया सा। निर्गता — gone; removed आमयाः — diseases रोगाः — illnesses निरामया — free from disease निरामया means one who is free from disease. amaya means disease or affliction. she is free from every defect and removes the diseases of worldly life. the distortion-free screen: आमय (amaya) encompasses all physical biological illnesses, mental anxieties, and the ultimate sickness of spiritual confusion. she is niramayā because her essential unconditioned reality contains no internal cleavages or wear. she acts as a perfectly healthy screen that remains unaffected by the distortions projected upon it.","esoteric":["The Distortion-Free Screen: आमय (Amaya) encompasses all physical biological illnesses, mental anxieties, and the ultimate sickness of spiritual confusion. She is Niramayā because Her essential unconditioned reality contains no internal cleavages or wear. She acts as a perfectly healthy screen that remains unaffected by the distortions projected upon it."]},{"number":877,"name":"निरालम्बा","samasa":["निर्गतम् आलम्बनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतम् — gone; absent","आलम्बनम् — support; prop","निरालम्बा — one without support"],"summary":["निरालम्बा means one who is without support. Alambana is a prop or support. She depends on nothing, while everything depends on Her."],"searchText":"877 निरालम्बा निर्गतम् आलम्बनं यस्याः सा। निर्गतम् — gone; absent आलम्बनम् — support; prop निरालम्बा — one without support निरालम्बा means one who is without support. alambana is a prop or support. she depends on nothing, while everything depends on her. the independent substratum: finite objects require an external base to support their weight. she is nirālambā because she stands completely independent. lacking any neighbor or foundation back behind her station, she is the primary, uncaused foundation that supports the entire weight of the universe.","esoteric":["The Independent Substratum: Finite objects require an external base to support their weight. She is Nirālambā because She stands completely independent. Lacking any neighbor or foundation back behind Her station, She is the primary, uncaused foundation that supports the entire weight of the universe."]},{"number":878,"name":"स्वात्मारामा","samasa":["स्वात्मन्येवारामः क्रीडनं यस्याः सा।","स्वमात्मीयं जगच्च आत्मा ब्रह्म च अनयोरारामः क्रीडनं विहरणं वृत्तित्वं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्वात्मनि — in Her own Self","आरामः — delight; play","क्रीडनम् — playing","जगत् — universe","ब्रह्म — Brahman"],"summary":["स्वात्मारामा means one who rejoices in Her own Self. She sports in the Self alone. The universe and Brahman are also Her field of play, but Her joy is self-complete."],"searchText":"878 स्वात्मारामा स्वात्मन्येवारामः क्रीडनं यस्याः सा। स्वमात्मीयं जगच्च आत्मा ब्रह्म च अनयोरारामः क्रीडनं विहरणं वृत्तित्वं यस्याः सा। स्वात्मनि — in her own self आरामः — delight; play क्रीडनम् — playing जगत् — universe ब्रह्म — brahman स्वात्मारामा means one who rejoices in her own self. she sports in the self alone. the universe and brahman are also her field of play, but her joy is self-complete. the joy of self-absorption: human happiness is dependent on acquiring external objects, making it brief and fragile. she is svātmārāmā because she experiences absolute fulfillment entirely through her own intrinsic self-bliss (svarūpānanda). she balances the relative world (svam) and the absolute brahman (ātmā) as waves of a single, non-dual play.","esoteric":["The Joy of Self-Absorption: Human happiness is dependent on acquiring external objects, making it brief and fragile. She is Svātmārāmā because She experiences absolute fulfillment entirely through Her own intrinsic self-bliss (Svarūpānanda). She balances the relative world (svam) and the absolute Brahman (ātmā) as waves of a single, non-dual play."]},{"number":879,"name":"सुधासृतिः","samasa":["सुधायाः सहस्रारकर्णिकाचन्द्रगतायाः स्रुतिः स्रवणं यया कुण्डलिन्या सा।","सुधायाः स्रुतिरेव।"],"wordByWord":["सुधायाः — of nectar","सहस्रार — thousand-petalled lotus","चन्द्रगतायाः — located in the moon","स्रुतिः — flow","स्रवणम् — oozing; flowing"],"summary":["सुधासृतिः means one from whom nectar flows. Sudha is the nectar from the moon in the sahasrara. As Kuṇḍalinī, She causes that nectar to flow and grants bliss to the yogin."],"searchText":"879 सुधासृतिः सुधायाः सहस्रारकर्णिकाचन्द्रगतायाः स्रुतिः स्रवणं यया कुण्डलिन्या सा। सुधायाः स्रुतिरेव। सुधायाः — of nectar सहस्रार — thousand-petalled lotus चन्द्रगतायाः — located in the moon स्रुतिः — flow स्रवणम् — oozing; flowing सुधासृतिः means one from whom nectar flows. sudha is the nectar from the moon in the sahasrara. as kuṇḍalinī, she causes that nectar to flow and grants bliss to the yogin. the stream of immortality: when the internal kuṇḍalinī climbs past the lower centers, it triggers the lunar orb located inside the sahasrāra crown center. this trigger causes a massive downpour of cooling, alchemical nectar (sudhā). she is both the downpour itself and the active channel (srutiḥ) that distributes this essence throughout the practitioner's subtle channels, rejuvenating the entire system.","esoteric":["The Stream of Immortality: When the internal Kuṇḍalinī climbs past the lower centers, it triggers the lunar orb located inside the Sahasrāra crown center. This trigger causes a massive downpour of cooling, alchemical nectar (sudhā). She is both the downpour itself and the active channel (srutiḥ) that distributes this essence throughout the practitioner's subtle channels, rejuvenating the entire system."]},{"number":880,"name":"संसारपङ्कनिर्मग्नसमुद्धरणपण्डिता","samasa":["संसारलक्षणे कर्दमे निःशेषेण मग्नानां जनानां सम्यगुद्धरणे पण्डिता कुशला।"],"wordByWord":["संसार — worldly existence","पङ्क — mire; mud","निर्मग्नानाम् — of those deeply sunk","समुद्धरणे — in lifting up","पण्डिता — skilled; expert"],"summary":["संसारपङ्कनिर्मग्नसमुद्धरणपण्डिता means one skilled in lifting those sunk in the mire of samsara. saṃsāra is like a muddy marsh in which beings are deeply trapped. She expertly rescues devotees from that bondage."],"searchText":"880 संसारपङ्कनिर्मग्नसमुद्धरणपण्डिता संसारलक्षणे कर्दमे निःशेषेण मग्नानां जनानां सम्यगुद्धरणे पण्डिता कुशला। संसार — worldly existence पङ्क — mire; mud निर्मग्नानाम् — of those deeply sunk समुद्धरणे — in lifting up पण्डिता — skilled; expert संसारपङ्कनिर्मग्नसमुद्धरणपण्डिता means one skilled in lifting those sunk in the mire of samsara. saṃsāra is like a muddy marsh in which beings are deeply trapped. she expertly rescues devotees from that bondage. the expert rescuer: worldly delusion behaves like thick, heavy quicksand or mud (paṅka)—the more an individual struggles using simple egoic calculations, the deeper they sink. she is paṇḍitā (expertly skilled) at this rescue operation. she knows the exact leverage points, subtle frequencies, and initiatory channels needed to hook the bound soul and pull it safely out of the mud, establishing her status as the ultimate savior.","esoteric":["The Expert Rescuer: Worldly delusion behaves like thick, heavy quicksand or mud (paṅka)—the more an individual struggles using simple egoic calculations, the deeper they sink. She is Paṇḍitā (expertly skilled) at this rescue operation. She knows the exact leverage points, subtle frequencies, and initiatory channels needed to hook the bound soul and pull it safely out of the mud, establishing Her status as the ultimate savior."]},{"number":881,"name":"यज्ञप्रिया","samasa":["यज्ञाः प्रिया यस्याः सा।","यज्ञो वै विष्णुरिति श्रुतेस्तत्प्रियेति।"],"wordByWord":["यज्ञाः — sacrifices","प्रियाः — dear","विष्णुः — Vishnu","यज्ञप्रिया — She to whom sacrifices are dear"],"summary":["यज्ञप्रिया means one who loves sacrifice. Yajnas are dear to Her, and yajna is also identified with Viṣṇu in the Veda. Sacred offering, rightly performed, is pleasing to Her."],"searchText":"881 यज्ञप्रिया यज्ञाः प्रिया यस्याः सा। यज्ञो वै विष्णुरिति श्रुतेस्तत्प्रियेति। यज्ञाः — sacrifices प्रियाः — dear विष्णुः — vishnu यज्ञप्रिया — she to whom sacrifices are dear यज्ञप्रिया means one who loves sacrifice. yajnas are dear to her, and yajna is also identified with viṣṇu in the veda. sacred offering, rightly performed, is pleasing to her. the affinity for dedicated rites: a sacrifice (yajña) is the structural mechanism through which humans surrender material assets to nourish cosmic forces. she is yajñapriyā because she values this dedicated loop of mutual alignment. concurrently, she matches the declaration “yajño vai viṣṇuḥ”, showing her affinity for the cosmic preservation force.","esoteric":["The Affinity for Dedicated Rites: A sacrifice (Yajña) is the structural mechanism through which humans surrender material assets to nourish cosmic forces. She is Yajñapriyā because She values this dedicated loop of mutual alignment. Concurrently, She matches the declaration “Yajño vai Viṣṇuḥ”, showing Her affinity for the cosmic preservation force."]},{"number":882,"name":"यज्ञकर्त्री","samasa":["यज्ञस्य कर्ता यजमानात्मको दीक्षितमूर्तिः परमशिवस्तस्य पत्नी।"],"wordByWord":["यज्ञस्य — of sacrifice","कर्ता — performer","यजमानात्मकः — in the form of the sacrificer","दीक्षितमूर्तिः — initiated form","परमशिवः — Parashiva","पत्नी — consort"],"summary":["यज्ञकर्त्री means one connected with the performer of sacrifice. The yajna-karta is the sacrificer, ultimately identified with Parashiva. She is His Śakti and the power by which sacrifice is performed."],"searchText":"882 यज्ञकर्त्री यज्ञस्य कर्ता यजमानात्मको दीक्षितमूर्तिः परमशिवस्तस्य पत्नी। यज्ञस्य — of sacrifice कर्ता — performer यजमानात्मकः — in the form of the sacrificer दीक्षितमूर्तिः — initiated form परमशिवः — parashiva पत्नी — consort यज्ञकर्त्री means one connected with the performer of sacrifice. the yajna-karta is the sacrificer, ultimately identified with parashiva. she is his śakti and the power by which sacrifice is performed. the power behind the executor: lord śiva manifests as the archetypal consecrated sacrificer (dīkṣita-mūrti) who runs the macrocosmic sacrifice to maintain order. she is his non-dual dynamic energy (yajñakartrī). without her presence, the executor lacks the kinetic capacity to initiate, manage, or complete a single rite, making her the true inner engine of action.","esoteric":["The Power behind the Executor: Lord Śiva manifests as the archetypal consecrated sacrificer (Dīkṣita-mūrti) who runs the macrocosmic sacrifice to maintain order. She is His non-dual dynamic energy (Yajñakartrī). Without Her presence, the executor lacks the kinetic capacity to initiate, manage, or complete a single rite, making Her the true inner engine of action."]},{"number":883,"name":"यजमानस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["यजमानश्च स्वश्च यजमानस्वौ दीक्षितात्मानौ तौ रूपे अस्या इति।"],"wordByWord":["यजमानः — sacrificer","स्वः — self; one's own","दीक्षितात्मानौ — initiated selves","रूपे — forms","अस्याः — of Her"],"summary":["यजमानस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is the yajamana. The sacrificer and the initiated self are Her own forms. In sacrifice, the deity, act and worshipper are resolved in Her."],"searchText":"883 यजमानस्वरूपिणी यजमानश्च स्वश्च यजमानस्वौ दीक्षितात्मानौ तौ रूपे अस्या इति। यजमानः — sacrificer स्वः — self; one's own दीक्षितात्मानौ — initiated selves रूपे — forms अस्याः — of her यजमानस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is the yajamana. the sacrificer and the initiated self are her own forms. in sacrifice, the deity, act and worshipper are resolved in her. identity with the conscious observer: lest a practitioner think that she remains only a distant deity waiting to receive an offering from a human performer, this name establishes she is the very person performing the rite (yajamāna). she is the conscious intention and the internal observer driving the sacrifice, proving that the giver, the gift, and the receiver are one substance.","esoteric":["Identity with the Conscious Observer: Lest a practitioner think that She remains only a distant deity waiting to receive an offering from a human performer, this name establishes She is the very person performing the rite (Yajamāna). She is the conscious intention and the internal observer driving the sacrifice, proving that the giver, the gift, and the receiver are one substance."]},{"number":884,"name":"धर्माधारा","samasa":["धर्माणामासमन्तात्सर्वदेशेषु धारा निरर्गलप्रवाहः।","धर्म आधारो यस्याः सा।","धर्म आधारो यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["धर्माणाम् — of dharmas","धारा — stream; flow","आधारः — support","यया — by whom","धर्माधारा — support of dharma"],"summary":["धर्माधारा means the support of dharma. dharma flows everywhere because of Her. She is both the foundation of righteousness and the power by which it is sustained."],"searchText":"884 धर्माधारा धर्माणामासमन्तात्सर्वदेशेषु धारा निरर्गलप्रवाहः। धर्म आधारो यस्याः सा। धर्म आधारो यया सा। धर्माणाम् — of dharmas धारा — stream; flow आधारः — support यया — by whom धर्माधारा — support of dharma धर्माधारा means the support of dharma. dharma flows everywhere because of her. she is both the foundation of righteousness and the power by which it is sustained. the unbroken current of law: she acts as the unceasing, unblocked stream (dhārā) that distributes moral law and systemic justice across all coordinates of space. concurrently, she functions as the absolute foundation (ādhāra) that keeps dharma stable, ensuring that the laws of karma and cosmic cause-and-effect remain unyielding.","esoteric":["The Unbroken Current of Law: She acts as the unceasing, unblocked stream (dhārā) that distributes moral law and systemic justice across all coordinates of space. Concurrently, She functions as the absolute foundation (ādhāra) that keeps Dharma stable, ensuring that the laws of karma and cosmic cause-and-effect remain unyielding."]},{"number":885,"name":"धनाध्यक्षा","samasa":["धनस्याध्यक्षा स्वामिनी।"],"wordByWord":["धनस्य — of wealth","अध्यक्षा — superintendent; overseer","स्वामिनी — mistress; owner"],"summary":["धनाध्यक्षा means the superintendent of wealth. She is the mistress and controller of all wealth. All forms of prosperity are under Her authority."],"searchText":"885 धनाध्यक्षा धनस्याध्यक्षा स्वामिनी। धनस्य — of wealth अध्यक्षा — superintendent; overseer स्वामिनी — mistress; owner धनाध्यक्षा means the superintendent of wealth. she is the mistress and controller of all wealth. all forms of prosperity are under her authority. the overlord of the cosmic treasury: humans spend lifetimes tracking and accumulating physical assets. she is the absolute adhyakṣā (sovereign supervisor) over the complete universal repository of wealth. kubera and lakṣmī manage local departments under her executive decree, confirming her status as the ultimate owner of all resources.","esoteric":["The Overlord of the Cosmic Treasury: Humans spend lifetimes tracking and accumulating physical assets. She is the absolute Adhyakṣā (sovereign supervisor) over the complete universal repository of wealth. Kubera and Lakṣmī manage local departments under Her executive decree, confirming Her status as the ultimate owner of all resources."]},{"number":886,"name":"धनधान्यविवर्धिनी","samasa":["धनानि धान्यानि च विशेष्य वर्धयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["धनानि — wealths","धान्यानि — grains; food supplies","विशेष्य — especially; distinctly","वर्धयति — increases; causes to grow"],"summary":["धनधान्यविवर्धिनी means one who increases wealth and grain. Dhana means wealth and dhanya means grain or food-supply. She causes prosperity, nourishment and material welfare to grow for Her devotees."],"searchText":"886 धनधान्यविवर्धिनी धनानि धान्यानि च विशेष्य वर्धयतीति। धनानि — wealths धान्यानि — grains; food supplies विशेष्य — especially; distinctly वर्धयति — increases; causes to grow धनधान्यविवर्धिनी means one who increases wealth and grain. dhana means wealth and dhanya means grain or food-supply. she causes prosperity, nourishment and material welfare to grow for her devotees. the multiplier of sustenance: she does not ignore the material needs of her children. as vivardhinī, she actively multiplies their financial reserves (dhana) and foundational food nutrition (dhānya), realigning their external environment to ensure they do not suffer material panic while pursuing spiritual goals.","esoteric":["The Multiplier of Sustenance: She does not ignore the material needs of Her children. As Vivardhinī, She actively multiplies their financial reserves (dhana) and foundational food nutrition (dhānya), realigning their external environment to ensure they do not suffer material panic while pursuing spiritual goals."]},{"number":887,"name":"विप्रप्रिया","samasa":["विप्राः प्रिया अभीष्टा यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विप्राः — learned Brahmins; sacred knowers","प्रियाः — dear; beloved","अभीष्टाः — cherished; desired","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["विप्रप्रिया means one who is dear to learned Brahmins. Vipra means a Brahmin, a learned person or one who knows sacred knowledge. She is beloved of such knowers and worshippers of the Veda."],"searchText":"887 विप्रप्रिया विप्राः प्रिया अभीष्टा यस्याः सा। विप्राः — learned brahmins; sacred knowers प्रियाः — dear; beloved अभीष्टाः — cherished; desired यस्याः सा — she whose विप्रप्रिया means one who is dear to learned brahmins. vipra means a brahmin, a learned person or one who knows sacred knowledge. she is beloved of such knowers and worshippers of the veda. the affinity for the seekers of truth: विप्र (vipra) signifies those whose life is dedicated to the intense study, recitation, and contemplation of scriptural truth and the absolute brahman. she holds this specific class close to her grace because their internal efforts mirror her own radiant wisdom field.","esoteric":["The Affinity for the Seekers of Truth: विप्र (Vipra) signifies those whose life is dedicated to the intense study, recitation, and contemplation of scriptural truth and the absolute Brahman. She holds this specific class close to Her grace because their internal efforts mirror Her own radiant wisdom field."]},{"number":888,"name":"विप्ररूपा","samasa":["विप्राः रूपं स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।","विप्रान् रूपयति पूर्वरूपवतः करोत्याप्याययतीति।"],"wordByWord":["विप्राः — learned Brahmins","रूपम् — form","स्वरूपम् — own form","यस्याः सा — she whose","रूपयति — forms; restores","आप्याययति — nourishes; strengthens"],"summary":["विप्ररूपा means one whose form is the Vipras. The learned ones are regarded as Her own form because sacred knowledge shines through them. She also nourishes and restores the Vipras to their proper spiritual form."],"searchText":"888 विप्ररूपा विप्राः रूपं स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। विप्रान् रूपयति पूर्वरूपवतः करोत्याप्याययतीति। विप्राः — learned brahmins रूपम् — form स्वरूपम् — own form यस्याः सा — she whose रूपयति — forms; restores आप्याययति — nourishes; strengthens विप्ररूपा means one whose form is the vipras. the learned ones are regarded as her own form because sacred knowledge shines through them. she also nourishes and restores the vipras to their proper spiritual form. identity with the wisdom seers: she is non-different from the very seers who contemplate her nature. she is the internal processing power and the light of the intellect (buddhi) that enables them to comprehend truth. alternatively, she acts as the force that continuously nourishes (āpyāyayati) and restores their energetic form.","esoteric":["Identity with the Wisdom Seers: She is non-different from the very seers who contemplate Her nature. She is the internal processing power and the light of the intellect (buddhi) that enables them to comprehend truth. Alternatively, She acts as the force that continuously nourishes (āpyāyayati) and restores their energetic form."]},{"number":889,"name":"विश्वभ्रमणकारिणी","samasa":["विश्वेषां ब्रह्माण्डानां भ्रमणं सृष्टिस्थितिनाशरूपं यातायातं कारयति।","विश्वस्य विष्णोः भ्रमणकारिणी।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वेषाम् — of the worlds","ब्रह्माण्डानाम् — of the cosmic eggs","भ्रमणम् — movement; revolution","सृष्टि — creation","स्थिति — maintenance","नाश — dissolution","कारयति — causes"],"summary":["विश्वभ्रमणकारिणी means one who causes the movement of the universe. The movement of countless worlds includes creation, maintenance and dissolution. She is the power that makes the universe revolve through these cosmic processes."],"searchText":"889 विश्वभ्रमणकारिणी विश्वेषां ब्रह्माण्डानां भ्रमणं सृष्टिस्थितिनाशरूपं यातायातं कारयति। विश्वस्य विष्णोः भ्रमणकारिणी। विश्वेषाम् — of the worlds ब्रह्माण्डानाम् — of the cosmic eggs भ्रमणम् — movement; revolution सृष्टि — creation स्थिति — maintenance नाश — dissolution कारयति — causes विश्वभ्रमणकारिणी means one who causes the movement of the universe. the movement of countless worlds includes creation, maintenance and dissolution. she is the power that makes the universe revolve through these cosmic processes. the engine of cosmic rotation: the multiverses (viśva) do not sit static; they spin in continuous cycles of generation, orbit, and reabsorption (bhramaṇa). she is the dynamic kinetic engine (kāriṇī) that drives this entire movement. concurrently, she coordinates the various shifts and incarnations assumed by the pervasive energy of viṣṇu.","esoteric":["The Engine of Cosmic Rotation: The multiverses (viśva) do not sit static; they spin in continuous cycles of generation, orbit, and reabsorption (bhramaṇa). She is the dynamic kinetic engine (kāriṇī) that drives this entire movement. Concurrently, She coordinates the various shifts and incarnations assumed by the pervasive energy of Viṣṇu."]},{"number":890,"name":"विश्वग्रासा","samasa":["विश्वं चराचरं ग्रसतीति।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वम् — the universe","चराचरम् — moving and unmoving","ग्रसति — swallows; absorbs"],"summary":["विश्वग्रासा means one who swallows the universe. At dissolution, the moving and unmoving universe is withdrawn into Her. She is the power of final absorption in whom all manifestation is consumed."],"searchText":"890 विश्वग्रासा विश्वं चराचरं ग्रसतीति। विश्वम् — the universe चराचरम् — moving and unmoving ग्रसति — swallows; absorbs विश्वग्रासा means one who swallows the universe. at dissolution, the moving and unmoving universe is withdrawn into her. she is the power of final absorption in whom all manifestation is consumed. the total reabsorption: complementing her consuming titles, she is viśvagrāsā because during the grand dissolution, she pulls the entire manifest world back into her causal womb. nothing is left as an independent object outside her field; she digests the elements, space, and time, leaving her non-dual light to shine alone in the silence.","esoteric":["The Total Reabsorption: Complementing Her consuming titles, She is Viśvagrāsā because during the grand dissolution, She pulls the entire manifest world back into Her causal womb. Nothing is left as an independent object outside Her field; She digests the elements, space, and time, leaving Her non-dual light to shine alone in the silence."]},{"number":891,"name":"विद्रुमाभा","samasa":["विद्रूमाः प्रवालास्तद्वदारक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["विद्रुमाः — corals","प्रवालाः — corals","तद्वत् — like that","आरक्ता — reddish"],"summary":["विद्रुमाभा means one whose lustre is like coral. Vidruma means coral, bright red in colour. Her complexion is described as red and shining like coral."],"searchText":"891 विद्रुमाभा विद्रूमाः प्रवालास्तद्वदारक्ता। विद्रुमाः — corals प्रवालाः — corals तद्वत् — like that आरक्ता — reddish विद्रुमाभा means one whose lustre is like coral. vidruma means coral, bright red in colour. her complexion is described as red and shining like coral. the unblemished crimson aura: unlike passing emotional states, her complexion here is described as the rich, steady, unblemished red hue of high-grade coral (vidruma). this specific frequency represents the absolute fusion of इच्छाशक्ति (divine will) and क्रियाशक्ति (divine action) flowing together to protect the practitioner's psychic field, dispelling mental lethargy.","esoteric":["The Unblemished Crimson Aura: Unlike passing emotional states, Her complexion here is described as the rich, steady, unblemished red hue of high-grade coral (vidruma). This specific frequency represents the absolute fusion of इच्छाशक्ति (Divine Will) and क्रियाशक्ति (Divine Action) flowing together to protect the practitioner's psychic field, dispelling mental lethargy."]},{"number":892,"name":"वैष्णवी","samasa":["विष्णोरियम्।"],"wordByWord":["विष्णोः — of Vishnu","इयम् — this; belonging to"],"summary":["वैष्णवी means one who belongs to Viṣṇu, or one who is Vaishnavi. She is the Śakti associated with Viṣṇu and is not different from the divine preserving power. This name points to Her identity with the Vaishnavi aspect."],"searchText":"892 वैष्णवी विष्णोरियम्। विष्णोः — of vishnu इयम् — this; belonging to वैष्णवी means one who belongs to viṣṇu, or one who is vaishnavi. she is the śakti associated with viṣṇu and is not different from the divine preserving power. this name points to her identity with the vaishnavi aspect. the pervasive protective power: she is the dynamic, all-pervading kinetic capacity (śakti) that belongs to lord viṣṇu. in the agamic defensive framework, she manifests as vaiṣṇavī — the corporate goddess who commands the maintenance of order, stands ready with the discus weapon, and destroys unrighteous distortions.","esoteric":["The Pervasive Protective Power: She is the dynamic, all-pervading kinetic capacity (Śakti) that belongs to Lord Viṣṇu. In the Agamic defensive framework, She manifests as Vaiṣṇavī — the corporate goddess who commands the maintenance of order, stands ready with the discus weapon, and destroys unrighteous distortions."]},{"number":893,"name":"विष्णुरूपिणी","samasa":["विष्णुरेव रूपमस्या अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["विष्णुः — Vishnu","एव — itself","रूपम् — form","अस्याः — of Her","अस्तीति — is"],"summary":["विष्णुरूपिणी means one whose form is Viṣṇu. Viṣṇu himself is Her form, for the powers of preservation and pervasion are included in Her. She is not separate from Viṣṇu's sustaining principle."],"searchText":"893 विष्णुरूपिणी विष्णुरेव रूपमस्या अस्तीति। विष्णुः — vishnu एव — itself रूपम् — form अस्याः — of her अस्तीति — is विष्णुरूपिणी means one whose form is viṣṇu. viṣṇu himself is her form, for the powers of preservation and pervasion are included in her. she is not separate from viṣṇu's sustaining principle. identity with the preserver: lest a student think that she is a localized goddess who simply belongs to a higher male deity, this name establishes her body is the very person of lord viṣṇu (viṣṇu-svarūpa). the pervasive strength that supports the planets and maintains cosmic dharma is the literal expression of her form.","esoteric":["Identity with the Preserver: Lest a student think that She is a localized goddess who simply belongs to a higher male deity, this name establishes Her body is the very person of Lord Viṣṇu (Viṣṇu-svarūpa). The pervasive strength that supports the planets and maintains cosmic Dharma is the literal expression of Her form."]},{"number":894,"name":"अयोनिः","samasa":["अविद्यमाना योनिः कारणं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अविद्यमाना — non-existing; absent","योनिः — womb; source; cause","कारणम् — cause","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["अयोनिः means one who has no womb or source. Yoni means womb, source or cause. She has no prior cause and is not born from anything else."],"searchText":"894 अयोनिः अविद्यमाना योनिः कारणं यस्याः सा। अविद्यमाना — non-existing; absent योनिः — womb; source; cause कारणम् — cause यस्याः सा — she whose अयोनिः means one who has no womb or source. yoni means womb, source or cause. she has no prior cause and is not born from anything else. the uncaused primary cause: material objects are born from a specific source womb (yoni). she is ayoniḥ because she stands completely outside this dependency loop. having no mother, no creator, and no prior cause back behind her station, she exists as the absolute, self-existent root of reality.","esoteric":["The Uncaused Primary Cause: Material objects are born from a specific source womb (yoni). She is Ayoniḥ because She stands completely outside this dependency loop. Having no mother, no creator, and no prior cause back behind Her station, She exists as the absolute, self-existent root of reality."]},{"number":895,"name":"योनिनिलया","samasa":["निलीयते जगद्यस्यामिति निलया। योनिश्चासौ निलया च।","योनिर्मायैव निलयः परिच्छेदिका यस्याः सा।","योनीनां जगत्कारणानां ब्रह्मादीनां नितरां लयो यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["निलीयते — dissolves; is absorbed","जगत् — the world","यस्याम् — in whom","योनिः — womb; source","निलया — abode","माया — Maya","लयः — dissolution"],"summary":["योनिनिलया means one who is the abode of the yoni. The universe dissolves in Her as in its source. māyā, the causes of the world and the deities such as Brahmā finally rest in Her."],"searchText":"895 योनिनिलया निलीयते जगद्यस्यामिति निलया। योनिश्चासौ निलया च। योनिर्मायैव निलयः परिच्छेदिका यस्याः सा। योनीनां जगत्कारणानां ब्रह्मादीनां नितरां लयो यस्यां सा। निलीयते — dissolves; is absorbed जगत् — the world यस्याम् — in whom योनिः — womb; source निलया — abode माया — maya लयः — dissolution योनिनिलया means one who is the abode of the yoni. the universe dissolves in her as in its source. māyā, the causes of the world and the deities such as brahmā finally rest in her. the matrix and the terminal: she is the primordial womb (yoni) within which the entire universe rests safely (nilaya). concurrently, she functions as the absolute terminal where all secondary causal matrices, elements, and creator deities (brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra) are drawn back and completely dissolved (layam) at the end of time.","esoteric":["The Matrix and the Terminal: She is the primordial womb (Yoni) within which the entire universe rests safely (nilaya). Concurrently, She functions as the absolute terminal where all secondary causal matrices, elements, and creator deities (Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra) are drawn back and completely dissolved (layam) at the end of time."]},{"number":896,"name":"कूटस्था","samasa":["कूटयति छलयत्यात्मानमानन्दादिकमावृत्य संसारे पातयतीति कूटमज्ञानं तदध्यक्षतया तत्र तिष्ठतीति।","कूटस्याज्ञानस्य स्था स्थितिर्यस्यां सा।","कूटो गिरिशृङ्गं तद्वन्निष्क्रियतया तिष्ठतीति।","कूटानां विश्वसमूहानां स्थितिर्यस्यां सा।","वाग्भवादिकूटत्रये तिष्ठतीति।","कूटं पुरद्वारं स्त्रीचक्रान्तर्गतत्रिकोणं तत्र तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["कूटम् — mass; peak; deception; mantra-section","अज्ञानम् — ignorance","अध्यक्षतया — as presiding witness","तिष्ठति — stands; abides","वाग्भवादिकूटत्रये — in the three mantra-kutas"],"summary":["कूटस्था means one who is established in the kuta. Kuta is explained as ignorance that covers the Self, as a mountain peak, as groups of worlds, as the three mantra-kutas and as the triangle of the inner worship. She stands as the witness and support of all these meanings, while remaining unmoving and supreme."],"searchText":"896 कूटस्था कूटयति छलयत्यात्मानमानन्दादिकमावृत्य संसारे पातयतीति कूटमज्ञानं तदध्यक्षतया तत्र तिष्ठतीति। कूटस्याज्ञानस्य स्था स्थितिर्यस्यां सा। कूटो गिरिशृङ्गं तद्वन्निष्क्रियतया तिष्ठतीति। कूटानां विश्वसमूहानां स्थितिर्यस्यां सा। वाग्भवादिकूटत्रये तिष्ठतीति। कूटं पुरद्वारं स्त्रीचक्रान्तर्गतत्रिकोणं तत्र तिष्ठतीति। कूटम् — mass; peak; deception; mantra-section अज्ञानम् — ignorance अध्यक्षतया — as presiding witness तिष्ठति — stands; abides वाग्भवादिकूटत्रये — in the three mantra-kutas कूटस्था means one who is established in the kuta. kuta is explained as ignorance that covers the self, as a mountain peak, as groups of worlds, as the three mantra-kutas and as the triangle of the inner worship. she stands as the witness and support of all these meanings, while remaining unmoving and supreme. the unmoving witness on the peak: like an anvil (kūṭa) that stays completely still while the blacksmith beats iron shapes upon it, or a high mountain peak that watches changes below, she is the unmoving, changeless witness consciousness (kūṭastha). the mantric and geometric hub: she resides perfectly inside the three acoustic blocks (kūṭas) of her mantra and sits as the illuminating lamp inside the central inverted triangle of the śrī cakra.","esoteric":["The Unmoving Witness on the Peak: Like an anvil (kūṭa) that stays completely still while the blacksmith beats iron shapes upon it, or a high mountain peak that watches changes below, She is the unmoving, changeless witness consciousness (Kūṭastha).","The Mantric and Geometric Hub: She resides perfectly inside the three acoustic blocks (kūṭas) of Her mantra and sits as the illuminating lamp inside the central inverted triangle of the Śrī Cakra."]},{"number":897,"name":"कुलरूपिणी","samasa":["कुलं कौलमार्गो बाह्यपूजा वंश आचारो वा तद्रूपिणी।"],"wordByWord":["कुलम् — Kula; lineage; Kaula path","कौलमार्गः — Kaula path","बाह्यपूजा — external worship","वंशः — lineage","आचारः — conduct","रूपिणी — whose form is"],"summary":["कुलरूपिणी means one whose form is Kula. Kula may mean the Kaula path, external worship, family lineage or sacred conduct. She assumes the form of the Kula tradition and is its inner reality."],"searchText":"897 कुलरूपिणी कुलं कौलमार्गो बाह्यपूजा वंश आचारो वा तद्रूपिणी। कुलम् — kula; lineage; kaula path कौलमार्गः — kaula path बाह्यपूजा — external worship वंशः — lineage आचारः — conduct रूपिणी — whose form is कुलरूपिणी means one whose form is kula. kula may mean the kaula path, external worship, family lineage or sacred conduct. she assumes the form of the kula tradition and is its inner reality. the soul of the kaula lineage: कुल (kula) denotes the manifest universe of elements, body lineage, and the integrated agamic system of worship known as the kaula path. she is kularūpiṇī because she is the internal formatting code running through this entire structure, confirming that the visible matrix is an expression of her body.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Kaula Lineage: कुल (Kula) denotes the manifest universe of elements, body lineage, and the integrated Agamic system of worship known as the Kaula path. She is Kularūpiṇī because She is the internal formatting code running through this entire structure, confirming that the visible matrix is an expression of Her body."]},{"number":898,"name":"वीरगोष्ठीप्रिया","samasa":["वीराणां गोष्ठी सभा संल्लापो वा प्रिया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["वीराणाम् — of heroes; heroic worshippers","गोष्ठी — assembly; gathering","सभा — council","संल्लापः — conversation","प्रिया — dear"],"summary":["वीरगोष्ठीप्रिया means one who loves the assembly of heroes. Vira means the heroic worshipper; goshthi means assembly, gathering or sacred conversation. She delights in the company and worship of qualified heroic upasakas."],"searchText":"898 वीरगोष्ठीप्रिया वीराणां गोष्ठी सभा संल्लापो वा प्रिया यस्याः सा। वीराणाम् — of heroes; heroic worshippers गोष्ठी — assembly; gathering सभा — council संल्लापः — conversation प्रिया — dear वीरगोष्ठीप्रिया means one who loves the assembly of heroes. vira means the heroic worshipper; goshthi means assembly, gathering or sacred conversation. she delights in the company and worship of qualified heroic upasakas. the affection for heroic fellowship: vīras are those advanced, disciplined practitioners who approach practice with courage, cutting away their internal limitations. she is deeply affectionate toward their corporate gatherings (goṣṭhī) and technical spiritual dialogues. when these practitioners sit together to analyze the lineage keys, she manifests inside their circle to elevate their understanding.","esoteric":["The Affection for Heroic Fellowship: Vīras are those advanced, disciplined practitioners who approach practice with courage, cutting away their internal limitations. She is deeply affectionate toward their corporate gatherings (goṣṭhī) and technical spiritual dialogues. When these practitioners sit together to analyze the lineage keys, She manifests inside their circle to elevate their understanding."]},{"number":899,"name":"वीरा","samasa":["स्वयमपि वीर्यवत्त्वाद्वीरा।"],"wordByWord":["वीर्यवत्त्वात् — because of possessing heroic power","वीरा — heroic one"],"summary":["वीरा means one who is herself heroic. Vira also means one endowed with strength and potency. She is the very embodiment of divine courage and power."],"searchText":"899 वीरा स्वयमपि वीर्यवत्त्वाद्वीरा। वीर्यवत्त्वात् — because of possessing heroic power वीरा — heroic one वीरा means one who is herself heroic. vira also means one endowed with strength and potency. she is the very embodiment of divine courage and power. the ultimate hero: she is vīrā because she possesses absolute, unchecked vital energy and sovereign power (vīryavattvāt). she bows to no external threat, contains zero internal fear, and operates as the supreme warrior who strikes down cosmic distortions, serving as the template of courage for the seeker.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Hero: She is Vīrā because She possesses absolute, unchecked vital energy and sovereign power (vīryavattvāt). She bows to no external threat, contains zero internal fear, and operates as the supreme warrior who strikes down cosmic distortions, serving as the template of courage for the seeker."]},{"number":900,"name":"नैष्कर्म्या","samasa":["निर्गतानि कर्माणि यस्मात्स निष्कर्मा तस्य भावो नैष्कर्म्यं"],"wordByWord":["निर्गतानि — gone; removed","कर्माणि — actions","निष्कर्मा — actionless","भावः — state"],"summary":["नैष्कर्म्या means one who is free from karma. Naishkarmya is the state in which actions have gone and do not bind. She is beyond action and the fruit of action, though all action proceeds through Her power."],"searchText":"900 नैष्कर्म्या निर्गतानि कर्माणि यस्मात्स निष्कर्मा तस्य भावो नैष्कर्म्यं निर्गतानि — gone; removed कर्माणि — actions निष्कर्मा — actionless भावः — state नैष्कर्म्या means one who is free from karma. naishkarmya is the state in which actions have gone and do not bind. she is beyond action and the fruit of action, though all action proceeds through her power. the actionless substratum: material entities are driven by the mechanical laws of action and reaction (karma), gathering binding residue. she is naiṣkarmyā because her essential unconditioned reality sits completely past this mechanical framework. though she runs the kinetic engine of universes, she remains anchored in absolute, non-dual stillness, free from the stains of action, and guiding the practitioner toward this same resting space of liberation.","esoteric":["The Actionless Substratum: Material entities are driven by the mechanical laws of action and reaction (Karma), gathering binding residue. She is Naiṣkarmyā because Her essential unconditioned reality sits completely past this mechanical framework. Though She runs the kinetic engine of universes, She remains anchored in absolute, non-dual stillness, free from the stains of action, and guiding the practitioner toward this same resting space of liberation."]},{"number":901,"name":"नादरूपिणी","samasa":["नादः प्रणवशिरस्थितस्तद्रूपा।","नादे रूपमस्या अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["नादः — subtle sound","प्रणवशिरस्थितः — situated at the head of Pranava","तद्रूपा — of that form"],"summary":["नादरूपिणी means one whose form is Nada. Nada is the subtle sound associated with Pranava. She is the subtle sound-principle from which mantra and speech arise."],"searchText":"901 नादरूपिणी नादः प्रणवशिरस्थितस्तद्रूपा। नादे रूपमस्या अस्तीति। नादः — subtle sound प्रणवशिरस्थितः — situated at the head of pranava तद्रूपा — of that form नादरूपिणी means one whose form is nada. nada is the subtle sound associated with pranava. she is the subtle sound-principle from which mantra and speech arise. the apex of the praṇava: nāda represents the highly refined, subtle sound vibration located at the crown apex of the syllable ओम् (praṇava-śiras). it marks the transition point where sound dissolves back into silent awareness. she is nādarūpiṇī because she is the kinetic energy that flows through this acoustic ladder, acting as the uncreated stream that translates divine intent into universal manifestation.","esoteric":["The Apex of the Praṇava: Nāda represents the highly refined, subtle sound vibration located at the crown apex of the syllable ओम् (Praṇava-śiras). It marks the transition point where sound dissolves back into silent awareness. She is Nādarūpiṇī because She is the kinetic energy that flows through this acoustic ladder, acting as the uncreated stream that translates divine intent into universal manifestation."]},{"number":902,"name":"विज्ञानकलना","samasa":["विज्ञानस्य ब्रह्मसाक्षात्कारस्य कलना स्वात्मसाक्षात्कारः।"],"wordByWord":["विज्ञानस्य — of direct knowledge","ब्रह्मसाक्षात्कारस्य — of realization of Brahman","कलना — realization; reckoning","स्वात्मसाक्षात्कारः — realization of one’s own Self"],"summary":["विज्ञानकलना means one who is the realization of knowledge. Vijnana here points to direct realization of Brahman. She is the inner realization by which the Self is known."],"searchText":"902 विज्ञानकलना विज्ञानस्य ब्रह्मसाक्षात्कारस्य कलना स्वात्मसाक्षात्कारः। विज्ञानस्य — of direct knowledge ब्रह्मसाक्षात्कारस्य — of realization of brahman कलना — realization; reckoning स्वात्मसाक्षात्कारः — realization of one’s own self विज्ञानकलना means one who is the realization of knowledge. vijnana here points to direct realization of brahman. she is the inner realization by which the self is known. the dawn of self-experience: vijñāna is not dry, theoretical academic knowledge (jñāna); it is the direct, unmediated flash of cosmic self-realization (ब्रह्मसाक्षात्कार). she is vijñānakalanā because she acts as the precise internal spark and kinetic process (kalanā) that converts a theoretical understanding of the self into an immediate, lived reality.","esoteric":["The Dawn of Self-Experience: Vijñāna is not dry, theoretical academic knowledge (jñāna); it is the direct, unmediated flash of cosmic self-realization (ब्रह्मसाक्षात्कार). She is Vijñānakalanā because She acts as the precise internal spark and kinetic process (kalanā) that converts a theoretical understanding of the Self into an immediate, lived reality."]},{"number":903,"name":"कल्या","samasa":["कलासु साधुः।","कलयितुमर्हा।","कादम्बर्यादिरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["कलासु — in the kalas","साधुः — good; fit","कलयितुम् — to reckon; to know","अर्हा — worthy","कादम्बर्यादिरूपा — of forms such as Kadambari"],"summary":["कल्या means one who is Kalya. The name is connected with kala, fitness for being known, and also with forms such as Kadambari. She is fit to be contemplated through the kalas and is auspiciously knowable."],"searchText":"903 कल्या कलासु साधुः। कलयितुमर्हा। कादम्बर्यादिरूपा। कलासु — in the kalas साधुः — good; fit कलयितुम् — to reckon; to know अर्हा — worthy कादम्बर्यादिरूपा — of forms such as kadambari कल्या means one who is kalya. the name is connected with kala, fitness for being known, and also with forms such as kadambari. she is fit to be contemplated through the kalas and is auspiciously knowable. the master of design: she is kalyā because she possesses perfect, flawless mastery over all the creative arts and phases of time (कलासु साधुः). the attainable horizon: concurrently, she represents the ultimate, pure state of consciousness that is worthy of being measured and realized by refined minds, acting as the radiant dawn of the soul.","esoteric":["The Master of Design: She is Kalyā because She possesses perfect, flawless mastery over all the creative arts and phases of time (कलासु साधुः).","The Attainable Horizon: Concurrently, She represents the ultimate, pure state of consciousness that is worthy of being measured and realized by refined minds, acting as the radiant dawn of the soul."]},{"number":904,"name":"विदग्धा","samasa":["विशेषेण दग्धा इति विग्रहः। अर्थस्तु सौभाग्यभास्करे चातुर्यशीला इति। (कोशे अपि निपुणपरः विदग्धशब्दः)।"],"wordByWord":["विशेषेण — especially","दग्धा — burnt; refined","चातुर्यशीला — skilful; clever","विदग्ध — clever; accomplished"],"summary":["विदग्धा means one who is Vidagdha. Vidagdha is explained in the sense of clever, skilful and refined. She is the one of perfect skill and divine intelligence."],"searchText":"904 विदग्धा विशेषेण दग्धा इति विग्रहः। अर्थस्तु सौभाग्यभास्करे चातुर्यशीला इति। (कोशे अपि निपुणपरः विदग्धशब्दः)। विशेषेण — especially दग्धा — burnt; refined चातुर्यशीला — skilful; clever विदग्ध — clever; accomplished विदग्धा means one who is vidagdha. vidagdha is explained in the sense of clever, skilful and refined. she is the one of perfect skill and divine intelligence. the perfection of clever grace: while the literal grammatical derivation means \"thoroughly burned,\" the philosophical meaning denotes a highly refined, brilliant capacity of mind (चातुर्यशीला). she is vidagdhā because her consciousness manages the trillions of structural calculations required to run the multiverse with flawless, sharp, and graceful precision, leaving no room for operational error.","esoteric":["The Perfection of Clever Grace: While the literal grammatical derivation means \"thoroughly burned,\" the philosophical meaning denotes a highly refined, brilliant capacity of mind (चातुर्यशीला). She is Vidagdhā because Her consciousness manages the trillions of structural calculations required to run the multiverse with flawless, sharp, and graceful precision, leaving no room for operational error."]},{"number":905,"name":"बैन्दवासना","samasa":["भ्रूवोरुपरिभागे वृत्तसन्निवेशो बैन्दवं तदासनं यस्याः सा।","बिन्दुसम्बन्धिचक्रं सर्वानन्दमयाख्यमेवासनं यस्याः सा।","बिन्दुनां समूहो बैन्दवं तदेवासनं तदभिधेयार्थानामाधारोऽभिधायको यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["भ्रूवोः — of the eyebrows","उपरिभागे — above","वृत्तसन्निवेशः — circular arrangement","बिन्दु — bindu","आसनम् — seat","सर्वानन्दमय — all-blissful","आधारः — support"],"summary":["बैन्दवासना means one whose seat is Baindava. Baindava may be the circular arrangement above the eyebrows, the bindu-related Sarvanandamaya chakra, or the aggregate of bindus as support of meanings. She is seated in the bindu and in the supreme centre of bliss."],"searchText":"905 बैन्दवासना भ्रूवोरुपरिभागे वृत्तसन्निवेशो बैन्दवं तदासनं यस्याः सा। बिन्दुसम्बन्धिचक्रं सर्वानन्दमयाख्यमेवासनं यस्याः सा। बिन्दुनां समूहो बैन्दवं तदेवासनं तदभिधेयार्थानामाधारोऽभिधायको यस्याः सा। भ्रूवोः — of the eyebrows उपरिभागे — above वृत्तसन्निवेशः — circular arrangement बिन्दु — bindu आसनम् — seat सर्वानन्दमय — all-blissful आधारः — support बैन्दवासना means one whose seat is baindava. baindava may be the circular arrangement above the eyebrows, the bindu-related sarvanandamaya chakra, or the aggregate of bindus as support of meanings. she is seated in the bindu and in the supreme centre of bliss. the ultimate hub of the śrī yantra: geometrically, baindava refers to the absolute central dot—the बिन्दु (bindu)—of the śrī yantra, which is the internal ninth enclosure known as the सर्वानन्दमय चक्र (sarvānandamaya cakra). she is baindavāsanā because she sits enthroned at this exact center point. it is the unmoving anchor where all acoustic sounds and geometric lines dissolve into absolute non-dual unity.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Hub of the Śrī Yantra: Geometrically, Baindava refers to the absolute central dot—the बिन्दु (Bindu)—of the Śrī Yantra, which is the internal ninth enclosure known as the सर्वानन्दमय चक्र (Sarvānandamaya Cakra). She is Baindavāsanā because She sits enthroned at this exact center point. It is the unmoving anchor where all acoustic sounds and geometric lines dissolve into absolute non-dual unity."]},{"number":906,"name":"तत्त्वाधिका","samasa":["तत्त्वानि प्रलयपर्यन्तस्थायिवस्तूनि षट्त्रिंशत्संख्यान्येव। तेभ्योऽधिका तन्नाशेऽप्यवस्थानात्।","तत्त्वप्रचुरा।"],"wordByWord":["तत्त्वानि — principles; tattvas","षट्त्रिंशत् — thirty-six","तेभ्यः — beyond them","अधिका — greater; beyond","नाशे अपि — even at dissolution","अवस्थानात् — because of remaining"],"summary":["तत्त्वाधिका means one who is beyond the tattvas. The thirty-six tattvas remain only until dissolution. She transcends them and remains even when they are dissolved."],"searchText":"906 तत्त्वाधिका तत्त्वानि प्रलयपर्यन्तस्थायिवस्तूनि षट्त्रिंशत्संख्यान्येव। तेभ्योऽधिका तन्नाशेऽप्यवस्थानात्। तत्त्वप्रचुरा। तत्त्वानि — principles; tattvas षट्त्रिंशत् — thirty-six तेभ्यः — beyond them अधिका — greater; beyond नाशे अपि — even at dissolution अवस्थानात् — because of remaining तत्त्वाधिका means one who is beyond the tattvas. the thirty-six tattvas remain only until dissolution. she transcends them and remains even when they are dissolved. the transcendent remainder: the manifest universe is structured out of thirty-six foundational blocks of reality (tattvas), running from the gross earth element up to the shiva-shakti layer. these elements are durable but eventually dissolve during the grand collapse (mahāpralaya). she is tattvādhikā because she sits completely above and past this entire taxonomy. when the thirty-six principles are wiped out, she remains unaffected as the baseline awareness background.","esoteric":["The Transcendent Remainder: The manifest universe is structured out of thirty-six foundational blocks of reality (tattvas), running from the gross earth element up to the Shiva-Shakti layer. These elements are durable but eventually dissolve during the grand collapse (mahāpralaya). She is Tattvādhikā because She sits completely above and past this entire taxonomy. When the thirty-six principles are wiped out, She remains unaffected as the baseline awareness background."]},{"number":907,"name":"तत्त्वमयी","samasa":["तत्त्वप्रचुरा।"],"wordByWord":["तत्त्व — principle; tattva","प्रचुरा — abundant; full of"],"summary":["तत्त्वमयी means one who is full of the tattvas. Though She is beyond the tattvas, She also pervades them. The whole range of principles is filled with Her presence."],"searchText":"907 तत्त्वमयी तत्त्वप्रचुरा। तत्त्व — principle; tattva प्रचुरा — abundant; full of तत्त्वमयी means one who is full of the tattvas. though she is beyond the tattvas, she also pervades them. the whole range of principles is filled with her presence. immanence within the blocks: while she transcends the elements (tattvādhikā), she is simultaneously tattvamayī because she is the actual substance that constitutes them. she does not separate herself from the world to stay holy; every single element block is saturated with her consciousness. she is the material and spiritual fabric of everything that exists.","esoteric":["Immanence within the Blocks: While She transcends the elements (Tattvādhikā), She is simultaneously Tattvamayī because She is the actual substance that constitutes them. She does not separate Herself from the world to stay holy; every single element block is saturated with Her consciousness. She is the material and spiritual fabric of everything that exists."]},{"number":908,"name":"तत्त्वमर्थस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["तत्पदत्वम्पदयोरर्थौ शिवजीवौ स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["तत्पद — the word Tat","त्वम्पद — the word Tvam","अर्थौ — meanings","शिवजीवौ — Shiva and the individual soul","स्वरूपम् — form"],"summary":["तत्त्वमर्थस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is the meaning of Tat and Tvam. Tat indicates Śiva and Tvam indicates the individual soul. She is the identity of the two meanings revealed in the great saying."],"searchText":"908 तत्त्वमर्थस्वरूपिणी तत्पदत्वम्पदयोरर्थौ शिवजीवौ स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति। तत्पद — the word tat त्वम्पद — the word tvam अर्थौ — meanings शिवजीवौ — shiva and the individual soul स्वरूपम् — form तत्त्वमर्थस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is the meaning of tat and tvam. tat indicates śiva and tvam indicates the individual soul. she is the identity of the two meanings revealed in the great saying. the living bridge of non-duality: in the grand vedic statement \"tat tvam asi\" (\"that thou art\"), तत् (tat) represents the transcendent absolute consciousness (shiva), and त्वम् (tvam) represents the individualized localized living soul (jīva). she is tattvamarthasvarūpiṇī because she is the single, non-dual essence that bridges and unifies these two apparently distinct poles, showing they are one substance.","esoteric":["The Living Bridge of Non-Duality: In the grand Vedic statement \"Tat Tvam Asi\" (\"That Thou Art\"), तत् (Tat) represents the transcendent absolute consciousness (Shiva), and त्वम् (Tvam) represents the individualized localized living soul (Jīva). She is Tattvamarthasvarūpiṇī because She is the single, non-dual essence that bridges and unifies these two apparently distinct poles, showing they are one substance."]},{"number":909,"name":"सामगानप्रिया","samasa":["सामगानं प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["सामगानम् — singing of the Sama Veda","प्रियम् — dear","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["सामगानप्रिया means one who loves the singing of the Sama Veda. Sama-gana is sacred Vedic song. She is pleased by the chanting of the Sama, and by sacred music directed to Her."],"searchText":"909 सामगानप्रिया सामगानं प्रियं यस्याः सा। सामगानम् — singing of the sama veda प्रियम् — dear यस्याः सा — she whose सामगानप्रिया means one who loves the singing of the sama veda. sama-gana is sacred vedic song. she is pleased by the chanting of the sama, and by sacred music directed to her. the joy of the perfect melody: lord krishna states in the gītā, \"among the vedas, i am the sāma veda.\" the sāma chants represent the ultimate musical and rhythmic arrangement of vedic light metrics. she is sāmagānapriyā because these precise, soothing melodic patterns match the internal harmony of her own creative field, quickly calming the seeker's mind.","esoteric":["The Joy of the Perfect Melody: Lord Krishna states in the Gītā, \"Among the Vedas, I am the Sāma Veda.\" The Sāma chants represent the ultimate musical and rhythmic arrangement of Vedic light metrics. She is Sāmagānapriyā because these precise, soothing melodic patterns match the internal harmony of Her own creative field, quickly calming the seeker's mind."]},{"number":910,"name":"सोम्या/सौम्या","samasa":["सोम्या।","सोमयागार्हा।","उमया सहितः सोमोऽवयवोऽस्या अस्तीति।","सोम इवाह्लादिका।","सौम्या।","सोम्या एव सौम्या (चातुर्वर्ण्यादित्वात्स्वार्थे ष्यञ्)।तद्वती।","(अर्शादित्वान्मत्वर्थीयोऽप्रत्ययः। स्वार्थे वा ष्यङ्।)"],"wordByWord":["सोम्या — connected with Soma; gentle","सोमयागार्हा — fit for Soma sacrifice","उमया सहितः — united with Uma","आह्लादिका — delight-giving","सौम्या — gentle; pleasing"],"summary":["सोम्या/सौम्या means one who is Somya or Saumya. Somya is connected with Soma sacrifice, with Uma united with Soma, and with the cooling delight of the moon. She is gentle, pleasing and fit for sacred worship."],"searchText":"910 सोम्या/सौम्या सोम्या। सोमयागार्हा। उमया सहितः सोमोऽवयवोऽस्या अस्तीति। सोम इवाह्लादिका। सौम्या। सोम्या एव सौम्या (चातुर्वर्ण्यादित्वात्स्वार्थे ष्यञ्)।तद्वती। (अर्शादित्वान्मत्वर्थीयोऽप्रत्ययः। स्वार्थे वा ष्यङ्।) सोम्या — connected with soma; gentle सोमयागार्हा — fit for soma sacrifice उमया सहितः — united with uma आह्लादिका — delight-giving सौम्या — gentle; pleasing सोम्या/सौम्या means one who is somya or saumya. somya is connected with soma sacrifice, with uma united with soma, and with the cooling delight of the moon. she is gentle, pleasing and fit for sacred worship. the cooling radiance of consciousness: she is saumyā because she reflects the gentle, cooling, and blissful illumination of the moon (soma), soothing the existential burning of the mind. under the internal ritual key, she is the target who accepts the alchemical soma offering, and manifests as the unified form of shiva coupled with umā (स-उमा).","esoteric":["The Cooling Radiance of Consciousness: She is Saumyā because She reflects the gentle, cooling, and blissful illumination of the moon (Soma), soothing the existential burning of the mind. Under the internal ritual key, She is the target who accepts the alchemical Soma offering, and manifests as the unified form of Shiva coupled with Umā (स-उमा)."]},{"number":911,"name":"सदाशिवकुटुम्बिनी","samasa":["सदाशिवस्य कुटुम्बिनी।"],"wordByWord":["सदाशिवस्य — of Sadashiva","कुटुम्बिनी — wife; lady of the household"],"summary":["सदाशिवकुटुम्बिनी means one who is the family lady of Sadashiva. Kutumbini means the wife or lady of the household. She is inseparably associated with Sadashiva."],"searchText":"911 सदाशिवकुटुम्बिनी सदाशिवस्य कुटुम्बिनी। सदाशिवस्य — of sadashiva कुटुम्बिनी — wife; lady of the household सदाशिवकुटुम्बिनी means one who is the family lady of sadashiva. kutumbini means the wife or lady of the household. she is inseparably associated with sadashiva. the manager of the cosmic household: sadāśiva represents the absolute, unmoving consciousness baseline. she is his kuṭumbinī — his direct domestic consort. this role implies that while he remains the silent witness, she takes full charge of managing the vast corporate \"household\" of the universe, translating his presence into dynamic form.","esoteric":["The Manager of the Cosmic Household: Sadāśiva represents the absolute, unmoving consciousness baseline. She is His Kuṭumbinī — His direct domestic consort. This role implies that while He remains the silent witness, She takes full charge of managing the vast corporate \"household\" of the universe, translating His presence into dynamic form."]},{"number":912,"name":"सव्यापसव्यमार्गस्था","samasa":["सव्यश्चापसव्यश्च मार्गश्च सव्यापसव्यमार्गाः। तेषु स्थिताधिकृता।","सव्यो देवयानः। अपसव्यः पितृयाणः। मार्गेषु स्था स्थितिर्यस्मात् इति विष्णुलोकपरः।ईदृशमार्गत्रयरूपेत्यर्थः।"],"wordByWord":["सव्यः — right-hand path","अपसव्यः — left-hand path","मार्गः — path","स्थित — abiding","देवयानः — path of the gods","पितृयाणः — path of the ancestors"],"summary":["सव्यापसव्यमार्गस्था means one who abides in the right-hand and left-hand paths. Savya and apasavya indicate different ritual paths and also paths such as devayana and pitriyana. She is present in all legitimate paths and transcends the distinction between them."],"searchText":"912 सव्यापसव्यमार्गस्था सव्यश्चापसव्यश्च मार्गश्च सव्यापसव्यमार्गाः। तेषु स्थिताधिकृता। सव्यो देवयानः। अपसव्यः पितृयाणः। मार्गेषु स्था स्थितिर्यस्मात् इति विष्णुलोकपरः।ईदृशमार्गत्रयरूपेत्यर्थः। सव्यः — right-hand path अपसव्यः — left-hand path मार्गः — path स्थित — abiding देवयानः — path of the gods पितृयाणः — path of the ancestors सव्यापसव्यमार्गस्था means one who abides in the right-hand and left-hand paths. savya and apasavya indicate different ritual paths and also paths such as devayana and pitriyana. she is present in all legitimate paths and transcends the distinction between them. the master of all vehicles: in practice taxonomy, savya is the orthodox right-hand path (dakṣiṇācāra), and apasvya is the radical left-hand path (vāmācāra). in eschatology, they mark the solar path of the gods (devayāna) and the lunar path of ancestors (pitṛyāna). she is savyāpasavyamārgasthā because she is the sovereign director of both grids, ensuring that whichever road a soul travels, they ultimately interface with her energy field.","esoteric":["The Master of All Vehicles: In practice taxonomy, Savya is the orthodox right-hand path (Dakṣiṇācāra), and Apasvya is the radical left-hand path (Vāmācāra). In eschatology, they mark the solar path of the gods (Devayāna) and the lunar path of ancestors (Pitṛyāna). She is Savyāpasavyamārgasthā because She is the sovereign director of both grids, ensuring that whichever road a soul travels, they ultimately interface with Her energy field."]},{"number":913,"name":"सर्वापद्विनिवारिणी","samasa":["सर्वा आपदो विशिष्य नितरां वारयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वाः — all","आपदः — calamities; dangers","वारयति — wards off","विनिवारिणी — remover"],"summary":["सर्वापद्विनिवारिणी means one who removes all calamities. Apad means danger, distress or misfortune. She completely wards off the troubles of Her devotees."],"searchText":"913 सर्वापद्विनिवारिणी सर्वा आपदो विशिष्य नितरां वारयतीति। सर्वाः — all आपदः — calamities; dangers वारयति — wards off विनिवारिणी — remover सर्वापद्विनिवारिणी means one who removes all calamities. apad means danger, distress or misfortune. she completely wards off the troubles of her devotees. the absolute shield: distresses (āpad) can strike from physical, planetary, or internal psychological vectors. she does not offer partial protection. as vinivāriṇī, she operates as a high-velocity shield that completely dismantles these incoming crises at their root energetic levels, securing the practitioner's workspace.","esoteric":["The Absolute Shield: Distresses (āpad) can strike from physical, planetary, or internal psychological vectors. She does not offer partial protection. As Vinivāriṇī, She operates as a high-velocity shield that completely dismantles these incoming crises at their root energetic levels, securing the practitioner's workspace."]},{"number":914,"name":"स्वस्था","samasa":["स्वस्मिन्तिष्ठतीति।","स्वरित्यव्ययं स्वर्गवाचि। तत्र तिष्ठत्यध्यक्षतयेति।","शोभना अस्था स्थित्यभावो गतिर्यया सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्वस्मिन् — in one’s own self","तिष्ठति — abides","स्वः — heaven","स्थ — abiding","स्थितिः — state"],"summary":["स्वस्था means one who abides in Her own Self. Svastha means established in oneself; it may also indicate abiding in heaven or a beautiful state. She is self-established and gives stability to worshippers."],"searchText":"914 स्वस्था स्वस्मिन्तिष्ठतीति। स्वरित्यव्ययं स्वर्गवाचि। तत्र तिष्ठत्यध्यक्षतयेति। शोभना अस्था स्थित्यभावो गतिर्यया सा। स्वस्मिन् — in one’s own self तिष्ठति — abides स्वः — heaven स्थ — abiding स्थितिः — state स्वस्था means one who abides in her own self. svastha means established in oneself; it may also indicate abiding in heaven or a beautiful state. she is self-established and gives stability to worshippers. the anchor of self-existence: most entities depend on external objects to feel stable. she is svasthā because she rests completely within her own pristine nature (स्वस्मिन् तिष्ठति). in language, this denotes perfect health and ease. she is completely free from external disturbance, demonstrating the state of independent rest.","esoteric":["The Anchor of Self-Existence: Most entities depend on external objects to feel stable. She is Svasthā because She rests completely within Her own pristine nature (स्वस्मिन् तिष्ठति). In language, this denotes perfect health and ease. She is completely free from external disturbance, demonstrating the state of independent rest."]},{"number":915,"name":"स्वभावमधुरा","samasa":["स्व आत्मीयो भावोऽवस्थानं यस्यां सा च सा मधुरापुरी च।","स्वभामात्प्रज्ञानं ये वमन्ति सृजन्ति साधयन्ति तेषु धूरुत्तमा","स्वेषां भावेन भक्त्या मधु सत्फलं रातीति।"],"wordByWord":["स्व — own","भावः — nature; state","मधुरा — sweet","भक्त्या — through devotion","सत्फलम् — good fruit"],"summary":["स्वभावमधुरा means one whose nature is sweet. Her own state, Her devotees' feeling, and the good fruit She grants are all described through sweetness. She is naturally gentle and gracious."],"searchText":"915 स्वभावमधुरा स्व आत्मीयो भावोऽवस्थानं यस्यां सा च सा मधुरापुरी च। स्वभामात्प्रज्ञानं ये वमन्ति सृजन्ति साधयन्ति तेषु धूरुत्तमा स्वेषां भावेन भक्त्या मधु सत्फलं रातीति। स्व — own भावः — nature; state मधुरा — sweet भक्त्या — through devotion सत्फलम् — good fruit स्वभावमधुरा means one whose nature is sweet. her own state, her devotees' feeling, and the good fruit she grants are all described through sweetness. she is naturally gentle and gracious. intrinsic absolute sweetness: she does not require external ornaments or artificial updates to appear attractive. her core essence is pure, unconditioned bliss (madhura). like honey is naturally sweet without effort, her presence is automatically soothing and charming to any mind that touches her field.","esoteric":["Intrinsic Absolute Sweetness: She does not require external ornaments or artificial updates to appear attractive. Her core essence is pure, unconditioned bliss (madhura). Like honey is naturally sweet without effort, Her presence is automatically soothing and charming to any mind that touches Her field."]},{"number":916,"name":"धीरा","samasa":["धीरा पण्डिता।","धैर्यवती।","धियमद्वैतबुद्धिं राति ददातीति।","धीप्रदा इरा दशमीतिथिर्यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["धीरा — wise; steady","पण्डिता — learned","धैर्यवती — courageous; firm","धियम् — understanding","ददाति — gives"],"summary":["धीरा means one who is wise and steady. Dhira means learned, firm and courageous; it may also mean one who grants non-dual understanding. She is the giver of wisdom and steadiness."],"searchText":"916 धीरा धीरा पण्डिता। धैर्यवती। धियमद्वैतबुद्धिं राति ददातीति। धीप्रदा इरा दशमीतिथिर्यस्यां सा। धीरा — wise; steady पण्डिता — learned धैर्यवती — courageous; firm धियम् — understanding ददाति — gives धीरा means one who is wise and steady. dhira means learned, firm and courageous; it may also mean one who grants non-dual understanding. she is the giver of wisdom and steadiness. the giver of non-dual intellect: she is dhīra because she possesses unyielding courage and absolute wisdom. critically, she acts as the engine that dispenses non-dual intellect (धियम् अद्वैतबुद्धिं राति), breaking down the mental habits of fragmentation and anchoring the seeker in unity.","esoteric":["The Giver of Non-Dual Intellect: She is Dhīra because She possesses unyielding courage and absolute wisdom. Critically, She acts as the engine that dispenses non-dual intellect (धियम् अद्वैतबुद्धिं राति), breaking down the mental habits of fragmentation and anchoring the seeker in unity."]},{"number":917,"name":"धीरसमर्चिता","samasa":["धीसंज्ञं ज्ञानाभिन्नं रसमानन्दमुद्दिश्यार्चिता।"],"wordByWord":["धी — knowledge; understanding","रस — essence; bliss","आनन्दम् — bliss","अर्चिता — worshipped"],"summary":["धीरसमर्चिता means one who is worshipped by the wise. Dhira also points to knowledge and bliss. She is adored by those who seek the rasa of knowledge and the joy of realization."],"searchText":"917 धीरसमर्चिता धीसंज्ञं ज्ञानाभिन्नं रसमानन्दमुद्दिश्यार्चिता। धी — knowledge; understanding रस — essence; bliss आनन्दम् — bliss अर्चिता — worshipped धीरसमर्चिता means one who is worshipped by the wise. dhira also points to knowledge and bliss. she is adored by those who seek the rasa of knowledge and the joy of realization. worship with intellect and bliss: dhīra refers to those steady, unwavering seekers who cannot be distracted by worldly illusions. their worship is not based on blind emotion; they adore her by targeting the absolute fusion of pure knowledge (dhī) and non-dual bliss (rasa), matching her own nature.","esoteric":["Worship with Intellect and Bliss: Dhīra refers to those steady, unwavering seekers who cannot be distracted by worldly illusions. Their worship is not based on blind emotion; they adore Her by targeting the absolute fusion of pure knowledge (dhī) and non-dual bliss (rasa), matching Her own nature."]},{"number":918,"name":"चैतन्यार्घ्यसमाराध्या","samasa":["चैतन्यमेवार्घ्यं पूजायोग्यं जलादि तेन सम्यगाराध्या।","चैतन्यस्यात्मनोऽर्घ्येण ज्ञानेन स्वानुभूत्या सम्यगाराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["चैतन्यम् — consciousness","अर्घ्यम् — ritual offering","पूजायोग्यम् — fit for worship","ज्ञानेन — by knowledge","स्वानुभूत्या — by direct self-experience"],"summary":["चैतन्यार्घ्यसमाराध्या means one who is worshipped with consciousness as the offering. Chaitanya itself becomes the arghya, the water of worship. She is truly worshipped by the knowledge and direct experience of the Self."],"searchText":"918 चैतन्यार्घ्यसमाराध्या चैतन्यमेवार्घ्यं पूजायोग्यं जलादि तेन सम्यगाराध्या। चैतन्यस्यात्मनोऽर्घ्येण ज्ञानेन स्वानुभूत्या सम्यगाराध्या। चैतन्यम् — consciousness अर्घ्यम् — ritual offering पूजायोग्यम् — fit for worship ज्ञानेन — by knowledge स्वानुभूत्या — by direct self-experience चैतन्यार्घ्यसमाराध्या means one who is worshipped with consciousness as the offering. chaitanya itself becomes the arghya, the water of worship. she is truly worshipped by the knowledge and direct experience of the self. the offering of direct awareness: in external ritualism, one offers clean water (arghya) to honor a guest. in the high non-dual layout, the practitioner realizes that physical elements are insufficient. she is correctly worshipped when the seeker offers their own pure, unconditioned consciousness (caitanya) and direct self-experience (svānubhūti) back into her field, dissolving the separation between worshipper and worshipped.","esoteric":["The Offering of Direct Awareness: In external ritualism, one offers clean water (arghya) to honor a guest. In the high non-dual layout, the practitioner realizes that physical elements are insufficient. She is correctly worshipped when the seeker offers their own pure, unconditioned consciousness (Caitanya) and direct self-experience (svānubhūti) back into Her field, dissolving the separation between worshipper and worshipped."]},{"number":919,"name":"चैतन्यकुसुमप्रिया","samasa":["चैतन्यरूपकुसुमं प्रिया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["चैतन्य — consciousness","कुसुमम् — flower","प्रिया — dear"],"summary":["चैतन्यकुसुमप्रिया means one who loves the flower of consciousness. The proper flower offered to Her is not merely external; it is the flower of pure awareness. Consciousness offered in worship is dear to Her."],"searchText":"919 चैतन्यकुसुमप्रिया चैतन्यरूपकुसुमं प्रिया यस्याः सा। चैतन्य — consciousness कुसुमम् — flower प्रिया — dear चैतन्यकुसुमप्रिया means one who loves the flower of consciousness. the proper flower offered to her is not merely external; it is the flower of pure awareness. consciousness offered in worship is dear to her. the flower that never wears out: material flowers fade, dry up, and carry physical limitations. she is caitanyakusumapriyā because her favorite blossom is the glowing flower of internal awareness (caitanya). offering her a mind that is clear, still, and alert is the ultimate flower offering, satisfying her completely.","esoteric":["The Flower that Never Wears Out: Material flowers fade, dry up, and carry physical limitations. She is Caitanyakusumapriyā because Her favorite blossom is the glowing flower of internal awareness (Caitanya). Offering Her a mind that is clear, still, and alert is the ultimate flower offering, satisfying Her completely."]},{"number":920,"name":"सदोदिता","samasa":["सदा नित्यं उदिता उदयवती।","सत्सु सज्जनेषु आसमन्तादतिशयेनोदिता।"],"wordByWord":["सदा — always","नित्यम् — eternally","उदिता — risen; manifest","सज्जनेषु — among good people"],"summary":["सदोदिता means one who is always risen. She is ever manifest and never subject to setting or disappearance. Among the good and noble also, Her glory is constantly rising."],"searchText":"920 सदोदिता सदा नित्यं उदिता उदयवती। सत्सु सज्जनेषु आसमन्तादतिशयेनोदिता। सदा — always नित्यम् — eternally उदिता — risen; manifest सज्जनेषु — among good people सदोदिता means one who is always risen. she is ever manifest and never subject to setting or disappearance. among the good and noble also, her glory is constantly rising. the sun that never sets: physical stars and mental moods have rising and setting times. she is sadoditā because her consciousness sun is permanently risen. lacking any dark interval or setting phase, she shines continuously. for the practitioner, she stands instantly visible the exact moment the clouds of ego are cleared away.","esoteric":["The Sun that Never Sets: Physical stars and mental moods have rising and setting times. She is Sadoditā because Her consciousness sun is permanently risen. Lacking any dark interval or setting phase, She shines continuously. For the practitioner, She stands instantly visible the exact moment the clouds of ego are cleared away."]},{"number":921,"name":"सदातुष्टा","samasa":["सद्भिः जनैः आसमन्तात्तुष्टा।"],"wordByWord":["सद्भिः — by good people","जनैः — by persons","तुष्टा — satisfied; pleased"],"summary":["सदातुष्टा means one who is always satisfied. She is pleased by good people and true devotion. Being complete in Herself, She is ever content."],"searchText":"921 सदातुष्टा सद्भिः जनैः आसमन्तात्तुष्टा। सद्भिः — by good people जनैः — by persons तुष्टा — satisfied; pleased सदातुष्टा means one who is always satisfied. she is pleased by good people and true devotion. being complete in herself, she is ever content. eternally full: duality requires external acquisition to feel satisfied. she is sadātuṣṭā because her essential nature is permanently anchored in absolute fulfillment (tṛpti). lacking any internal void or unfulfilled desire, she remains continuously pleased. alternatively, she finds delight in the pure heart movements of virtuous seekers.","esoteric":["Eternally Full: Duality requires external acquisition to feel satisfied. She is Sadātuṣṭā because Her essential nature is permanently anchored in absolute fulfillment (tṛpti). Lacking any internal void or unfulfilled desire, She remains continuously pleased. Alternatively, She finds delight in the pure heart movements of virtuous seekers."]},{"number":922,"name":"तरुणादित्यपाटला","samasa":["तरुणो मध्याह्नकालिक आदित्यः सूर्यस्तद्वत्पाटला श्वेतरक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["तरुणः — young","आदित्यः — Sun","पाटला — rosy-white; red-tinged"],"summary":["तरुणादित्यपाटला means one who is red like the young sun. Taruna Aditya is the rising or young sun, and patala denotes a whitish-red or rosy colour. Her complexion shines with that tender red radiance."],"searchText":"922 तरुणादित्यपाटला तरुणो मध्याह्नकालिक आदित्यः सूर्यस्तद्वत्पाटला श्वेतरक्ता। तरुणः — young आदित्यः — sun पाटला — rosy-white; red-tinged तरुणादित्यपाटला means one who is red like the young sun. taruna aditya is the rising or young sun, and patala denotes a whitish-red or rosy colour. her complexion shines with that tender red radiance. the blinding rosy effulgence: पाटल (pāṭala) denotes a highly specialized color profile—a brilliant mix of white and intense red, similar to the blinding light of a clear sun. this color frequency represents the absolute activation of ज्ञानशक्ति (divine knowledge) and क्रियाशक्ति (divine action) blending together to flood the practitioner's subtle channels, burning away internal dark inertia.","esoteric":["The Blinding Rosy Effulgence: पाटल (Pāṭala) denotes a highly specialized color profile—a brilliant mix of white and intense red, similar to the blinding light of a clear sun. This color frequency represents the absolute activation of ज्ञानशक्ति (Divine Knowledge) and क्रियाशक्ति (Divine Action) blending together to flood the practitioner's subtle channels, burning away internal dark inertia."]},{"number":923,"name":"दक्षिणादक्षिणाराध्या","samasa":["दक्षिणया दक्षिणैः कुशलैराराध्या।","दक्षिणैः पण्डितैरदक्षिणैर्मूर्खैश्च आराध्या।","दक्षिणामार्गोपासकेन वाममार्गोपासकेन च आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["दक्षिणया — with dakshina; through right path","दक्षिणैः — by skilled persons","अदक्षिणैः — by unskilled or left-hand worshippers","आराध्या — worshipped"],"summary":["दक्षिणादक्षिणाराध्या means one worshipped by the dakshina and adakshina paths. She is worshipped by the skilled and the unskilled, by the learned and ordinary people, and by both right-hand and left-hand worshippers. She accepts worship through many modes."],"searchText":"923 दक्षिणादक्षिणाराध्या दक्षिणया दक्षिणैः कुशलैराराध्या। दक्षिणैः पण्डितैरदक्षिणैर्मूर्खैश्च आराध्या। दक्षिणामार्गोपासकेन वाममार्गोपासकेन च आराध्या। दक्षिणया — with dakshina; through right path दक्षिणैः — by skilled persons अदक्षिणैः — by unskilled or left-hand worshippers आराध्या — worshipped दक्षिणादक्षिणाराध्या means one worshipped by the dakshina and adakshina paths. she is worshipped by the skilled and the unskilled, by the learned and ordinary people, and by both right-hand and left-hand worshippers. she accepts worship through many modes. the target of every seeker: she does not reject any class of seeker. she is accessed by the highly refined master (dakṣiṇa) and the simple, unlettered devotee (adakṣiṇa). critically, she is the ultimate target inside both the structured right-hand vedic path (dakṣiṇāmārga) and the intense, radical left-hand agamic path (vāmāmārga), accepting sincere devotion from all sides.","esoteric":["The Target of Every Seeker: She does not reject any class of seeker. She is accessed by the highly refined master (dakṣiṇa) and the simple, unlettered devotee (adakṣiṇa). Critically, She is the ultimate target inside both the structured right-hand Vedic path (Dakṣiṇāmārga) and the intense, radical left-hand Agamic path (Vāmāmārga), accepting sincere devotion from all sides."]},{"number":924,"name":"दरस्मेरमुखाम्बुजा","samasa":["दरमीषद्यथा तथा स्मेरं स्मितवन्मुखाम्बुजं यस्याः सा।","मुखमम्बुजं यस्मिस्तन्मुखाम्बुजं ग्रीवावृत्तं दरवत् शङ्खवत्स्मेरं शोभमानं मुखाम्बुजं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["दरम् — slightly","स्मेरम् — smiling","मुखाम्बुजम् — lotus-face","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["दरस्मेरमुखाम्बुजा means one whose lotus face has a gentle smile. Dara means slight; smera means smiling. Her face is like a lotus softly illumined by a delicate smile."],"searchText":"924 दरस्मेरमुखाम्बुजा दरमीषद्यथा तथा स्मेरं स्मितवन्मुखाम्बुजं यस्याः सा। मुखमम्बुजं यस्मिस्तन्मुखाम्बुजं ग्रीवावृत्तं दरवत् शङ्खवत्स्मेरं शोभमानं मुखाम्बुजं यस्याः सा। दरम् — slightly स्मेरम् — smiling मुखाम्बुजम् — lotus-face यस्याः सा — she whose दरस्मेरमुखाम्बुजा means one whose lotus face has a gentle smile. dara means slight; smera means smiling. her face is like a lotus softly illumined by a delicate smile. the smile of cosmic reassurance: her countenance does not display fierce tension or cold indifference. she wears a continuous, gentle smile (dara-smera). this smile signifies her absolute confidence over cosmic laws and her deep compassion for the struggles of living beings, sending an immediate signal of safety to the heart of the meditator.","esoteric":["The Smile of Cosmic Reassurance: Her countenance does not display fierce tension or cold indifference. She wears a continuous, gentle smile (dara-smera). This smile signifies Her absolute confidence over cosmic laws and Her deep compassion for the struggles of living beings, sending an immediate signal of safety to the heart of the meditator."]},{"number":925,"name":"कौलिनीकेवला","samasa":["कौलिन्यः केवला ज्ञानवत्यो यया सा।","कौलिनीभिः केवला।"],"wordByWord":["कौलिन्यः — Kaulini worshippers or knowers","केवला — alone; unique","ज्ञानवत्यः — endowed with knowledge"],"summary":["कौलिनीकेवला means one who is alone with the Kaulinis. The Kaulinis are knowers of the Kaula tradition. She is attained by the Kaulinis and stands as the unique essence of that knowledge."],"searchText":"925 कौलिनीकेवला कौलिन्यः केवला ज्ञानवत्यो यया सा। कौलिनीभिः केवला। कौलिन्यः — kaulini worshippers or knowers केवला — alone; unique ज्ञानवत्यः — endowed with knowledge कौलिनीकेवला means one who is alone with the kaulinis. the kaulinis are knowers of the kaula tradition. she is attained by the kaulinis and stands as the unique essence of that knowledge. *, the core of the kaula system: kaulinī refers to the inner energy running through the elements and the specialized kaula lineage. she is kevalā within this system because she is the absolute, unconditioned consciousness that sits at the very end of the path. she is pure awareness itself, free from external rituals.","esoteric":["*,","The Core of the Kaula System: Kaulinī refers to the inner energy running through the elements and the specialized Kaula lineage. She is Kevalā within this system because She is the absolute, unconditioned consciousness that sits at the very end of the path. She is pure awareness itself, free from external rituals."]},{"number":926,"name":"अनर्घ्यकैवल्यपददायिनी/अनर्घ्यकैवल्यफलदायिनी","samasa":["अनर्घ्यममूल्यमपरिच्छिन्नं यत्कैवल्याख्यं पदम्/फलम्।  तद्दातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति।","अनर्घ्येति दीर्घान्तपाठे आसमन्ताद्व्याप्तं यत्कैवल्यमिति वा पदम्/फलम्।","न विद्यते कैवल्यं यस्मात्तदकैवल्यमीदृशं यत्पदमिति वा पदम्/फलम्।"],"wordByWord":["अनर्घ्यम् — priceless","कैवल्य — liberation","पदम् — state","फलम् — fruit","दातुं शीलम् — having the nature of giving"],"summary":["अनर्घ्यकैवल्यपददायिनी/अनर्घ्यकैवल्यफलदायिनी means one who grants the priceless state or fruit of liberation. Anarghya means beyond price; kaivalya is liberation. She bestows the immeasurable fruit of absolute freedom."],"searchText":"926 अनर्घ्यकैवल्यपददायिनी/अनर्घ्यकैवल्यफलदायिनी अनर्घ्यममूल्यमपरिच्छिन्नं यत्कैवल्याख्यं पदम्/फलम्।  तद्दातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति। अनर्घ्येति दीर्घान्तपाठे आसमन्ताद्व्याप्तं यत्कैवल्यमिति वा पदम्/फलम्। न विद्यते कैवल्यं यस्मात्तदकैवल्यमीदृशं यत्पदमिति वा पदम्/फलम्। अनर्घ्यम् — priceless कैवल्य — liberation पदम् — state फलम् — fruit दातुं शीलम् — having the nature of giving अनर्घ्यकैवल्यपददायिनी/अनर्घ्यकैवल्यफलदायिनी means one who grants the priceless state or fruit of liberation. anarghya means beyond price; kaivalya is liberation. she bestows the immeasurable fruit of absolute freedom. the priceless gift: worldly gains have price tags and expire over time. she is padadāyinī of कैवल्य (kaivalya — absolute, unconditioned non-dual liberation). this state is anarghya (priceless) because it cannot be bought with material currency, marking the absolute end of all individual lack and limitation.","esoteric":["The Priceless Gift: Worldly gains have price tags and expire over time. She is Padadāyinī of कैवल्य (Kaivalya — absolute, unconditioned non-dual liberation). This state is Anarghya (priceless) because it cannot be bought with material currency, marking the absolute end of all individual lack and limitation."]},{"number":927,"name":"स्तोत्रप्रिया","samasa":["स्तोत्रं प्रियं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्तोत्रम् — hymn of praise","प्रियं — dear","यस्याः सा — she whose"],"summary":["स्तोत्रप्रिया means one who loves hymns of praise. stotra is praise offered through sacred words. She is pleased by sincere recitation and glorification."],"searchText":"927 स्तोत्रप्रिया स्तोत्रं प्रियं यस्याः सा। स्तोत्रम् — hymn of praise प्रियं — dear यस्याः सा — she whose स्तोत्रप्रिया means one who loves hymns of praise. stotra is praise offered through sacred words. she is pleased by sincere recitation and glorification. the resonance of realignment: she does not seek public praise to satisfy an ego. she is stotrapriyā because when a practitioner recites a hymn (stotra), the poetic metrics and focused language gather their scattered mental energies. this process realigns their subtle nervous system, making it easy for her grace to flood their consciousness.","esoteric":["The Resonance of Realignment: She does not seek public praise to satisfy an ego. She is Stotrapriyā because when a practitioner recites a hymn (stotra), the poetic metrics and focused language gather their scattered mental energies. This process realigns their subtle nervous system, making it easy for Her grace to flood their consciousness."]},{"number":928,"name":"स्तुतिमती","samasa":["स्तुतिरस्यां कर्मतासम्बन्धेनास्तीति स्तुतिमती।","स्तुत्या मतिश्च ईश्च यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["स्तुतिः — praise","अस्याम् — in Her","मतिः — thought; regard","ईः — sovereignty or goddesshood"],"summary":["स्तुतिमती means one who is endowed with praise. Stuti is praise; the name indicates that praise properly belongs to Her. She is the worthy object of hymns and adoration."],"searchText":"928 स्तुतिमती स्तुतिरस्यां कर्मतासम्बन्धेनास्तीति स्तुतिमती। स्तुत्या मतिश्च ईश्च यस्याः सा। स्तुतिः — praise अस्याम् — in her मतिः — thought; regard ईः — sovereignty or goddesshood स्तुतिमती means one who is endowed with praise. stuti is praise; the name indicates that praise properly belongs to her. she is the worthy object of hymns and adoration. identity with the praise: lest a seeker think that she is an external entity who simply listens to independent words of praise, this name establishes she is the very substance of the praise itself (stuti-svarūpā). every word of adoration, every pure intent, and the capacity to praise are expressions of her own energy field.","esoteric":["Identity with the Praise: Lest a seeker think that She is an external entity who simply listens to independent words of praise, this name establishes She is the very substance of the praise itself (Stuti-svarūpā). Every word of adoration, every pure intent, and the capacity to praise are expressions of Her own energy field."]},{"number":929,"name":"श्रुतिसंस्तुतवैभवा","samasa":["श्रुतिभिः सम्यक् स्तुतं परिचितं वा वैभवं विभुत्वं यस्याः सा।","श्रुतिशब्दश्चतुःसंख्यापरो वा। (युगाब्धयोऽर्धाः श्रुतयश्चतस्र इति छन्दःसुधाकरात्।) तेन चतुर्धा परिचितं वैभवं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["श्रुतिभिः — by the Shrutis or Vedas","सम्यक् — well; fully","स्तुतम् — praised","वैभवम् — glory; greatness","विभुत्वम् — sovereignty"],"summary":["श्रुतिसंस्तुतवैभवा means one whose glory is praised by the Shrutis. Shruti means Veda, and may also be connected with the number four. Her greatness is fully celebrated and known through the Vedic revelation."],"searchText":"929 श्रुतिसंस्तुतवैभवा श्रुतिभिः सम्यक् स्तुतं परिचितं वा वैभवं विभुत्वं यस्याः सा। श्रुतिशब्दश्चतुःसंख्यापरो वा। (युगाब्धयोऽर्धाः श्रुतयश्चतस्र इति छन्दःसुधाकरात्।) तेन चतुर्धा परिचितं वैभवं यस्याः सा। श्रुतिभिः — by the shrutis or vedas सम्यक् — well; fully स्तुतम् — praised वैभवम् — glory; greatness विभुत्वम् — sovereignty श्रुतिसंस्तुतवैभवा means one whose glory is praised by the shrutis. shruti means veda, and may also be connected with the number four. her greatness is fully celebrated and known through the vedic revelation. the confirmed majesty: she is not a localized or modern invention. her majestic cosmic power (vaibhava) is thoroughly analyzed and validated across the ancient texts of the vedas (śrutis). her glory is perfectly distributed across the four foundational levels of speech (parā, paśyantī, madhyamā, vaikharī).","esoteric":["The Confirmed Majesty: She is not a localized or modern invention. Her majestic cosmic power (vaibhava) is thoroughly analyzed and validated across the ancient texts of the Vedas (Śrutis). Her glory is perfectly distributed across the four foundational levels of speech (Parā, Paśyantī, Madhyamā, Vaikharī)."]},{"number":930,"name":"मनस्विनी","samasa":["मनोऽस्याः स्वतन्त्रतया तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["मनः — mind","अस्याः — of Her","स्वतन्त्रतया — independently","तिष्ठति — stands"],"summary":["मनस्विनी means one who is Manasvini. Her mind stands free and independent. She is self-willed, sovereign and endowed with supreme inner power."],"searchText":"930 मनस्विनी मनोऽस्याः स्वतन्त्रतया तिष्ठतीति। मनः — mind अस्याः — of her स्वतन्त्रतया — independently तिष्ठति — stands मनस्विनी means one who is manasvini. her mind stands free and independent. she is self-willed, sovereign and endowed with supreme inner power. the independent will: in human beings, the mind is often pushed around by external sensory inputs and karmic impressions. she is manasvinī because her cosmic mind operates with absolute, unrestricted freedom (स्वतन्त्रतया तिष्ठति). her intent (icchā-śakti) is independent, directing the laws of nature without being bound by them.","esoteric":["The Independent Will: In human beings, the mind is often pushed around by external sensory inputs and karmic impressions. She is Manasvinī because Her cosmic mind operates with absolute, unrestricted freedom (स्वतन्त्रतया तिष्ठति). Her intent (Icchā-śakti) is independent, directing the laws of nature without being bound by them."]},{"number":931,"name":"मानवती","samasa":["मानश्चित्तसमुन्नतिरादरणं वा प्रियापराधसूचिका चेष्टा वा प्रमाणं वा प्रमितिर्वास्यामस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["मानः — honour; measure; mental elevation","चित्तसमुन्नतिः — elevation of mind","आदरणम् — respect","प्रमाणम् — means of knowledge","प्रमितिः — valid cognition"],"summary":["मानवती means one who is Manavati. Mana may mean honour, mental elevation, loving gesture, measure or valid knowledge. She possesses these forms of dignity, measure and knowledge."],"searchText":"931 मानवती मानश्चित्तसमुन्नतिरादरणं वा प्रियापराधसूचिका चेष्टा वा प्रमाणं वा प्रमितिर्वास्यामस्तीति। मानः — honour; measure; mental elevation चित्तसमुन्नतिः — elevation of mind आदरणम् — respect प्रमाणम् — means of knowledge प्रमितिः — valid cognition मानवती means one who is manavati. mana may mean honour, mental elevation, loving gesture, measure or valid knowledge. she possesses these forms of dignity, measure and knowledge. the matrix of valid knowledge: māna represents dignity, but philosophically it denotes प्रमिति (pramiti — valid, uncorrupted knowledge). she is mānavatī because she is the container and baseline source that validates all true information, allowing human intellects to comprehend reality accurately.","esoteric":["The Matrix of Valid Knowledge: Māna represents dignity, but philosophically it denotes प्रमिति (pramiti — valid, uncorrupted knowledge). She is Mānavatī because She is the container and baseline source that validates all true information, allowing human intellects to comprehend reality accurately."]},{"number":932,"name":"महेशी","samasa":["महेशस्य स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["महेशस्य — of Mahesha","स्त्री — wife; consort"],"summary":["महेशी means the consort of Mahesha. Mahesha is the great Lord, Śiva. She is His Śakti and inseparable consort."],"searchText":"932 महेशी महेशस्य स्त्री। महेशस्य — of mahesha स्त्री — wife; consort महेशी means the consort of mahesha. mahesha is the great lord, śiva. she is his śakti and inseparable consort. the shared throne of absolute power: maheśa is the great lord who oversees cosmic dissolution and transformation. she is his non-different dynamic energy (maheśī). she shares his supreme throne, executing the laws of nature while remaining anchored in transcendent stillness.","esoteric":["The Shared Throne of Absolute Power: Maheśa is the great lord who oversees cosmic dissolution and transformation. She is His non-different dynamic energy (Maheśī). She shares His supreme throne, executing the laws of nature while remaining anchored in transcendent stillness."]},{"number":933,"name":"मङ्गलाकृतिः","samasa":["मङ्गलरूपा आकृतिर्यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["मङ्गल — auspiciousness","रूपा — form","आकृतिः — appearance"],"summary":["मङ्गलाकृतिः means one whose form is auspiciousness. Mangala means auspicious, blessed and beneficent. Her very form and appearance are auspicious."],"searchText":"933 मङ्गलाकृतिः मङ्गलरूपा आकृतिर्यस्याः सा। मङ्गल — auspiciousness रूपा — form आकृतिः — appearance मङ्गलाकृतिः means one whose form is auspiciousness. mangala means auspicious, blessed and beneficent. her very form and appearance are auspicious. the geometry of absolute benevolence: she is maṅgalākṛtiḥ because her very shape is composed of pure auspiciousness. her geometric forms (the śrī yantra) and her physical descriptions are not designed for simple display; they are precise energy grids meant to clear away negative currents and bring harmony to the seeker's space.","esoteric":["The Geometry of Absolute Benevolence: She is Maṅgalākṛtiḥ because Her very shape is composed of pure auspiciousness. Her geometric forms (the Śrī Yantra) and Her physical descriptions are not designed for simple display; they are precise energy grids meant to clear away negative currents and bring harmony to the seeker's space."]},{"number":934,"name":"विश्वमाता","samasa":["विश्वस्य जगतो विष्णोर्वा माता।"],"wordByWord":["विश्वस्य — of the universe","जगतः — of the world","विष्णोः वा — or of Vishnu","माता — mother"],"summary":["विश्वमाता means mother of the universe. Vishva means the world or Viṣṇu. She is the mother of the whole universe and of all that pervades it."],"searchText":"934 विश्वमाता विश्वस्य जगतो विष्णोर्वा माता। विश्वस्य — of the universe जगतः — of the world विष्णोः वा — or of vishnu माता — mother विश्वमाता means mother of the universe. vishva means the world or viṣṇu. she is the mother of the whole universe and of all that pervades it. the universal womb: she is the viśvamātā because every single creature, element, star, and dimensional space was generated inside her womb. she watches over this macrocosmic creation with unbiased, protective care, ensuring that every soul is provided with the path inputs needed for its eventual evolution.","esoteric":["The Universal Womb: She is the Viśvamātā because every single creature, element, star, and dimensional space was generated inside Her womb. She watches over this macrocosmic creation with unbiased, protective care, ensuring that every soul is provided with the path inputs needed for its eventual evolution."]},{"number":935,"name":"जगद्धात्री","samasa":["जगद्धत्ते भूरूपेणेति जगद्धात्री।"],"wordByWord":["जगत् — the universe","धत्ते — holds; supports","भूरूपेण — in the form of the earth","धात्री — supporter; bearer"],"summary":["जगद्धात्री means She bears the world in the form of the earth. Supporter of the universe. The universe is sustained by Her supporting power."],"searchText":"935 जगद्धात्री जगद्धत्ते भूरूपेणेति जगद्धात्री। जगत् — the universe धत्ते — holds; supports भूरूपेण — in the form of the earth धात्री — supporter; bearer जगद्धात्री means she bears the world in the form of the earth. supporter of the universe. the universe is sustained by her supporting power. the supporting earth substratum: the world does not float by chance or hang unsupported. she is jagaddhātrī because she manifests directly as the grounding force—exemplified by the stabilizing element of the earth (भूरूपेण) — that holds the weight of living beings, protecting them from structural collapse.","esoteric":["The Supporting Earth Substratum: The world does not float by chance or hang unsupported. She is Jagaddhātrī because She manifests directly as the grounding force—exemplified by the stabilizing element of the Earth (भूरूपेण) — that holds the weight of living beings, protecting them from structural collapse."]},{"number":936,"name":"विशालाक्षी","samasa":["विशाले विस्तीर्णे अक्षिणी यस्याः सा।","विशालपीठमेवाक्षिस्थानं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["विशाले — large; expansive","विस्तीर्णे — wide","अक्षिणी — eyes","विशालपीठम् — the Vishala sacred seat","अक्षिस्थानम् — eye-place"],"summary":["विशालाक्षी means one with large eyes. Her eyes are wide and expansive. The name may also indicate that the great sacred seat is the place of Her vision."],"searchText":"936 विशालाक्षी विशाले विस्तीर्णे अक्षिणी यस्याः सा। विशालपीठमेवाक्षिस्थानं यस्याः सा। विशाले — large; expansive विस्तीर्णे — wide अक्षिणी — eyes विशालपीठम् — the vishala sacred seat अक्षिस्थानम् — eye-place विशालाक्षी means one with large eyes. her eyes are wide and expansive. the name may also indicate that the great sacred seat is the place of her vision. the wide gaze of infinite awareness: her eyes are described as viṣāla (immense) because her vision is completely unbounded. she tracks the entire universe at a single glance. geographically, she is non-different from the primary deity विशालाक्षी (viśālākṣī) presiding over the sacred city of kashi (varanasi), marking a key energy point on the earth grid.","esoteric":["The Wide Gaze of Infinite Awareness: Her eyes are described as viṣāla (immense) because Her vision is completely unbounded. She tracks the entire universe at a single glance. Geographically, She is non-different from the primary deity विशालाक्षी (Viśālākṣī) presiding over the sacred city of Kashi (Varanasi), marking a key energy point on the earth grid."]},{"number":937,"name":"विरागिणी","samasa":["विरागो वैराग्यमस्या अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["विरागः — detachment","वैराग्यम् — dispassion","अस्याः — of Her","अस्तीति — is"],"summary":["विरागिणी means one who is detached. Viraga means dispassion or freedom from attachment. Though She governs all, She remains untouched and free from worldly craving."],"searchText":"937 विरागिणी विरागो वैराग्यमस्या अस्तीति। विरागः — detachment वैराग्यम् — dispassion अस्याः — of her अस्तीति — is विरागिणी means one who is detached. viraga means dispassion or freedom from attachment. though she governs all, she remains untouched and free from worldly craving. the detached ruler of pleasures: though she manifests as the source of all cosmic attraction and play (līlā), her essential unconditioned nature remains completely detached (vairāgya). she does not cling to projects or seek external gratification, standing as a pristine template of dispassion that guides the seeker away from emotional dependency.","esoteric":["The Detached Ruler of Pleasures: Though She manifests as the source of all cosmic attraction and play (Līlā), Her essential unconditioned nature remains completely detached (vairāgya). She does not cling to projects or seek external gratification, standing as a pristine template of dispassion that guides the seeker away from emotional dependency."]},{"number":938,"name":"प्रगल्भा","samasa":["सृष्ट्यादिकर्मसु प्रौढत्वात्प्रगल्भा।"],"wordByWord":["सृष्ट्यादिकर्मसु — in creation and other functions","प्रौढत्वात् — because of maturity or greatness","प्रगल्भा — bold; competent"],"summary":["प्रगल्भा means one who is mature and bold. Pragalbha means fully capable or expert. She is supremely competent in the acts of creation and the other cosmic functions."],"searchText":"938 प्रगल्भा सृष्ट्यादिकर्मसु प्रौढत्वात्प्रगल्भा। सृष्ट्यादिकर्मसु — in creation and other functions प्रौढत्वात् — because of maturity or greatness प्रगल्भा — bold; competent प्रगल्भा means one who is mature and bold. pragalbha means fully capable or expert. she is supremely competent in the acts of creation and the other cosmic functions. the master executive: pragalbhā describes an expert who operates with absolute confidence and maturity (prauḍhatva), completely free from hesitation. she is pragalbhā because she executes the massive, complex processes of universal creation, preservation, and dissolution effortlessly, demonstrating absolute operational mastery.","esoteric":["The Master Executive: Pragalbhā describes an expert who operates with absolute confidence and maturity (prauḍhatva), completely free from hesitation. She is Pragalbhā because She executes the massive, complex processes of universal creation, preservation, and dissolution effortlessly, demonstrating absolute operational mastery."]},{"number":939,"name":"परमोदारा/अपरमोदारा","samasa":["परमोदारा।","परमा च सोदारा च महती च। (उदारो दातृमहतोरित्यमरः।)","परं प्रकृष्टं मोदमानन्दमासमन्ताद्रातीति।","परमाण्युदानि जलानि यस्मिन्स परमोदः समुद्रः, स च प्रकृते भवसमुद्ररूपः, तस्यारा आयुधविशेषो यस्याः सा।","अपरमोदारा।","अपगता रमा येषां तेऽपरमा दरिद्रास्तेभ्य उदारा ऐश्वर्यप्रदेति।"],"wordByWord":["परमा — supreme","उदारा — generous; noble","महतī — great","मोदम् — joy","आनन्दम् — bliss","दरिद्राः — poor people","ऐश्वर्यप्रदा — giver of prosperity"],"summary":["परमोदारा/अपरमोदारा means one who is supremely generous, or who is generous to those deprived of wealth. Paramodara is explained as great, noble, and giver of supreme joy; it may also refer to the ocean of worldly existence and Her special weapon connected with it. Aparamodara is explained as the one who grants prosperity to the poor and destitute."],"searchText":"939 परमोदारा/अपरमोदारा परमोदारा। परमा च सोदारा च महती च। (उदारो दातृमहतोरित्यमरः।) परं प्रकृष्टं मोदमानन्दमासमन्ताद्रातीति। परमाण्युदानि जलानि यस्मिन्स परमोदः समुद्रः, स च प्रकृते भवसमुद्ररूपः, तस्यारा आयुधविशेषो यस्याः सा। अपरमोदारा। अपगता रमा येषां तेऽपरमा दरिद्रास्तेभ्य उदारा ऐश्वर्यप्रदेति। परमा — supreme उदारा — generous; noble महतī — great मोदम् — joy आनन्दम् — bliss दरिद्राः — poor people ऐश्वर्यप्रदा — giver of prosperity परमोदारा/अपरमोदारा means one who is supremely generous, or who is generous to those deprived of wealth. paramodara is explained as great, noble, and giver of supreme joy; it may also refer to the ocean of worldly existence and her special weapon connected with it. aparamodara is explained as the one who grants prosperity to the poor and destitute. the sovereign giver: she is paramodārā because her generosity (udāratva) knows no bounds. she dispenses the highest, most refined bliss (paramam modam) to advanced ascetics. when read as aparamodārā, it highlights her active compassion toward the materially or spiritually destitute (aparama), flooding their lives with sudden abundance to balance their path.","esoteric":["The Sovereign Giver: She is Paramodārā because Her generosity (udāratva) knows no bounds. She dispenses the highest, most refined bliss (paramam modam) to advanced ascetics. When read as Aparamodārā, it highlights Her active compassion toward the materially or spiritually destitute (aparama), flooding their lives with sudden abundance to balance their path."]},{"number":940,"name":"परामोदा","samasa":["पर उत्कृष्ट आमोदः परिमलः कीर्तिः यस्याः सा।","आ समन्तान्मोदः सन्तोषो यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["परः — excellent; supreme","आमोदः — fragrance; delight; fame","परिमलः — fragrance","कीर्तिः — fame","सन्तोषः — satisfaction; joy"],"summary":["परामोदा means one whose fragrance, fame or delight is supreme. Para-amoda means excellent fragrance or renown; it also means one whose joy is all-pervading. She spreads supreme delight and auspicious fame everywhere."],"searchText":"940 परामोदा पर उत्कृष्ट आमोदः परिमलः कीर्तिः यस्याः सा। आ समन्तान्मोदः सन्तोषो यस्याः सा। परः — excellent; supreme आमोदः — fragrance; delight; fame परिमलः — fragrance कीर्तिः — fame सन्तोषः — satisfaction; joy परामोदा means one whose fragrance, fame or delight is supreme. para-amoda means excellent fragrance or renown; it also means one whose joy is all-pervading. she spreads supreme delight and auspicious fame everywhere. the fragrance of pure consciousness: āmoda refers to a rich, captivating fragrance that spreads automatically. she is parāmodā because her spiritual presence acts as the ultimate fragrance, sweetening the internal channels of anyone who remembers her. concurrently, she rests in a state of continuous, shoreless satisfaction and delight (moda), free from internal friction.","esoteric":["The Fragrance of Pure Consciousness: Āmoda refers to a rich, captivating fragrance that spreads automatically. She is Parāmodā because Her spiritual presence acts as the ultimate fragrance, sweetening the internal channels of anyone who remembers Her. Concurrently, She rests in a state of continuous, shoreless satisfaction and delight (moda), free from internal friction."]},{"number":941,"name":"मनोमयी","samasa":["शुद्धस्य ब्रह्मणो मनःस्थानीयत्वात्।","मनःप्रधाना। (मनसैवानुद्रष्टव्य इति स्वज्ञाने जननीये मनस एव प्राधान्यात्)"],"wordByWord":["शुद्धस्य — of the pure","मनोमयी। — component of the name"],"summary":["मनोमयी means one who has the mind itself as Her form. Bhairava, Śiva, is Chidakasha, and His own active energy, Spanda Śakti, is known as Manomayi. \"By mind alone it is to be seen.\" Thus the mind is the chief instrument in creating self-knowledge."],"searchText":"941 मनोमयी शुद्धस्य ब्रह्मणो मनःस्थानीयत्वात्। मनःप्रधाना। (मनसैवानुद्रष्टव्य इति स्वज्ञाने जननीये मनस एव प्राधान्यात्) शुद्धस्य — of the pure मनोमयी। — component of the name मनोमयी means one who has the mind itself as her form. bhairava, śiva, is chidakasha, and his own active energy, spanda śakti, is known as manomayi. \"by mind alone it is to be seen.\" thus the mind is the chief instrument in creating self-knowledge. the gateway of the refined mind: the scripture states, \"manasaivānudraṣṭavyam\" (\"through the mind alone is the self to be realized\"). while the absolute absolute is past the senses, it is discovered when the mind becomes perfectly clear, still, and reflective. she is manomayī because she acts as the very substance of this highly purified, refined intellect, functioning as the direct gateway to non-dual awakening.","esoteric":["The Gateway of the Refined Mind: The scripture states, \"Manasaivānudraṣṭavyam\" (\"Through the mind alone is the Self to be realized\"). While the absolute absolute is past the senses, it is discovered when the mind becomes perfectly clear, still, and reflective. She is Manomayī because She acts as the very substance of this highly purified, refined intellect, functioning as the direct gateway to non-dual awakening."]},{"number":942,"name":"व्योमकेशी","samasa":["व्योमैव केशा यस्या विराड्रूपायाः सा।","व्योमकेशस्य शिवस्य स्त्री।"],"wordByWord":["शिवस्य — of Shiva","व्योमकेशी। — component of the name"],"summary":["व्योमकेशी means one whose hair is the form of ether, that is, the form of Virat. Or She is the consort of Vyomakesha, Śiva. Since the directions are said to be His wives, She may be considered as the form of the directions. Vyoma means ether. With the suffix ka it indicates small ether; She is present there also. Thus She is omnipresent."],"searchText":"942 व्योमकेशी व्योमैव केशा यस्या विराड्रूपायाः सा। व्योमकेशस्य शिवस्य स्त्री। शिवस्य — of shiva व्योमकेशी। — component of the name व्योमकेशी means one whose hair is the form of ether, that is, the form of virat. or she is the consort of vyomakesha, śiva. since the directions are said to be his wives, she may be considered as the form of the directions. vyoma means ether. with the suffix ka it indicates small ether; she is present there also. thus she is omnipresent. the canopy of space: in her macrocosmic manifest body (virāṭ-rūpa), the entire open blue sky and cosmic space elements are nothing but the single strands of her loose hair (keśa). this imagery shows her vast containment of the planets. as the consort of shiva who bears the matted hair of space, she coordinates the cosmic fields with perfect balance.","esoteric":["The Canopy of Space: In Her macrocosmic manifest body (Virāṭ-rūpa), the entire open blue sky and cosmic space elements are nothing but the single strands of Her loose hair (keśa). This imagery shows Her vast containment of the planets. As the consort of Shiva who bears the matted hair of space, She coordinates the cosmic fields with perfect balance."]},{"number":943,"name":"विमानस्था","samasa":["विमानो व्योमयानं तत्र तिष्ठतीति।","विशेषेण मान आदरणे स्था स्थितिर्यस्याः सा।","विशिष्टा मा कान्तिर्यस्य तद्विमं तादृशं अनः शकटं किरिचक्रादिरूपो रथस्तत्र तिष्ठतीति।","विगतं मानं परिमाणं यस्य तदपरिच्छिन्नं ब्रह्म तन्निष्ठा।","माने परिमाणे स्था स्थितिः परिमाणाविच्छिन्नता विगता यस्याः सा।","विशिष्य माति निष्कृष्य प्रमां जनयतीति विमानो वेदस्तत्र  प्रतिपाद्यतया तिष्ठतीति वा।","विशिष्टेषु वेदाविरुद्धेषु मानेषु प्रमाणेषु धर्मब्रह्मरूपेण तिष्ठतीति।","विशिष्य मानं पुराणन्यायमीमांसेत्यादिना तद्व्यक्तित्वेन रूपेण परिगणनं येषां तेषु चतुर्दशस्वेव विद्याधर्मस्थानेषु तिष्ठतीति।"],"wordByWord":["विमानस्था। — component of the name"],"summary":["विमानस्था means one who is no different from the devas in the celestial chariot or flights. She is omniscient and supports Her devotees with great interest. She is present in the chariots such as Geya cakra, Kiri cakra and cakra Raja, in the immeasurable Brahman, in the Vedas, in valid evidences not opposed to the Vedas, and in the fourteen vidyās."],"searchText":"943 विमानस्था विमानो व्योमयानं तत्र तिष्ठतीति। विशेषेण मान आदरणे स्था स्थितिर्यस्याः सा। विशिष्टा मा कान्तिर्यस्य तद्विमं तादृशं अनः शकटं किरिचक्रादिरूपो रथस्तत्र तिष्ठतीति। विगतं मानं परिमाणं यस्य तदपरिच्छिन्नं ब्रह्म तन्निष्ठा। माने परिमाणे स्था स्थितिः परिमाणाविच्छिन्नता विगता यस्याः सा। विशिष्य माति निष्कृष्य प्रमां जनयतीति विमानो वेदस्तत्र  प्रतिपाद्यतया तिष्ठतीति वा। विशिष्टेषु वेदाविरुद्धेषु मानेषु प्रमाणेषु धर्मब्रह्मरूपेण तिष्ठतीति। विशिष्य मानं पुराणन्यायमीमांसेत्यादिना तद्व्यक्तित्वेन रूपेण परिगणनं येषां तेषु चतुर्दशस्वेव विद्याधर्मस्थानेषु तिष्ठतीति। विमानस्था। — component of the name विमानस्था means one who is no different from the devas in the celestial chariot or flights. she is omniscient and supports her devotees with great interest. she is present in the chariots such as geya cakra, kiri cakra and cakra raja, in the immeasurable brahman, in the vedas, in valid evidences not opposed to the vedas, and in the fourteen vidyās. established in the unmeasurable: while human eyes map her onto a celestial vehicle (vimāna), the high non-dual interpretation reveals that she is vimānasthā because she stands permanently anchored within that absolute brahman which is completely free from measurement or limitation (विगतं मानं यस्य). concurrently, she resides at the core of the vedas (vimāna) as the ultimate truth they reveal.","esoteric":["Established in the Unmeasurable: While human eyes map Her onto a celestial vehicle (vimāna), the high non-dual interpretation reveals that She is Vimānasthā because She stands permanently anchored within that absolute Brahman which is completely free from measurement or limitation (विगतं मानं यस्य). Concurrently, She resides at the core of the Vedas (Vimāna) as the ultimate truth they reveal."]},{"number":944,"name":"वज्रिणी","samasa":["वज्रिण इन्द्रस्य स्त्री।","वज्रम् अस्याः अस्तीति।","वज्राख्यरत्नैर्भूषिता।","महद्भयं वज्रमुद्यतमिति श्रुतौ वज्रपदस्य ब्रह्मपरत्वात् परिच्छेदकत्वसम्बन्धेन तद्वती।"],"wordByWord":["इन्द्रस्य — of Indra","वज्रिणी। — component of the name"],"summary":["वज्रिणी means one who is the consort of Indra, the possessor of the Vajra. Or one who has the thunderbolt in hand. Or one adorned with diamond-like gems. The Katha Upaniṣad uses Vajra in the sense of Brahman, and She is related to Brahman as its limiting power."],"searchText":"944 वज्रिणी वज्रिण इन्द्रस्य स्त्री। वज्रम् अस्याः अस्तीति। वज्राख्यरत्नैर्भूषिता। महद्भयं वज्रमुद्यतमिति श्रुतौ वज्रपदस्य ब्रह्मपरत्वात् परिच्छेदकत्वसम्बन्धेन तद्वती। इन्द्रस्य — of indra वज्रिणी। — component of the name वज्रिणी means one who is the consort of indra, the possessor of the vajra. or one who has the thunderbolt in hand. or one adorned with diamond-like gems. the katha upaniṣad uses vajra in the sense of brahman, and she is related to brahman as its limiting power. the awesome power of brahman: \"mahad bhayaṁ vajram udyatam\" (\"the absolute is a great, raised thunderbolt\"). this image denotes the unyielding, unchangeable laws of nature that ensure cosmic order. she is vajriṇī because she is the living embodiment of this unyielding law, holding the ultimate diamond power to shatter egoic deviations.","esoteric":["The Awesome Power of Brahman: \"Mahad bhayaṁ vajram udyatam\" (\"The absolute is a great, raised thunderbolt\"). This image denotes the unyielding, unchangeable laws of nature that ensure cosmic order. She is Vajriṇī because She is the living embodiment of this unyielding law, holding the ultimate diamond power to shatter egoic deviations."]},{"number":945,"name":"वामकेश्वरी","samasa":["वामकेश्वरतन्त्ररूपा।","वामकस्य तन्त्रस्य प्रतिपाद्या।","वामकानामीश्वरी।","वामा वाममार्गरताः। त एव कुत्सिता इति वामकाः।","वमन्ति जगत्सृजन्तीति वा वामका दक्षाद्याः।"],"wordByWord":["वामकेश्वरी। — component of the name"],"summary":["वामकेश्वरी means one who is in the form of the Vamakeshvara tantra. This tantra describes the worship of Śrīdevī, and Śrī Bhaskararya's Sethu Bandha is connected with its Nityashodashikarnava portion. She is the head of Vamaka worshippers, and also of those creators such as Daksha who bring forth the world."],"searchText":"945 वामकेश्वरी वामकेश्वरतन्त्ररूपा। वामकस्य तन्त्रस्य प्रतिपाद्या। वामकानामीश्वरी। वामा वाममार्गरताः। त एव कुत्सिता इति वामकाः। वमन्ति जगत्सृजन्तीति वा वामका दक्षाद्याः। वामकेश्वरी। — component of the name वामकेश्वरी means one who is in the form of the vamakeshvara tantra. this tantra describes the worship of śrīdevī, and śrī bhaskararya's sethu bandha is connected with its nityashodashikarnava portion. she is the head of vamaka worshippers, and also of those creators such as daksha who bring forth the world. the soul of the core tantra: she is the living embodiment and primary target of the highly sacred वामकेश्वर तन्त्र (vāmakeśvara tantra), which contains the secret geometry and mantra formulas of śrīvidyā. under the operational key, she acts as the supreme queen (īśvarī) governing those radical practitioners who follow the left-hand path (vāmakas), using intense methods to realign their awareness.","esoteric":["The Soul of the Core Tantra: She is the living embodiment and primary target of the highly sacred वामकेश्वर तन्त्र (Vāmakeśvara Tantra), which contains the secret geometry and mantra formulas of Śrīvidyā. Under the operational key, She acts as the supreme queen (Īśvarī) governing those radical practitioners who follow the left-hand path (Vāmakas), using intense methods to realign their awareness."]},{"number":946,"name":"पञ्चयज्ञप्रिया","samasa":["पञ्चसंख्याका यज्ञाः पञ्चयज्ञाः। ते प्रिया यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यज्ञाः — sacrifices","प्रिया — dear","यस्याः — whose"],"summary":["पञ्चयज्ञप्रिया means one who loves the five kinds of sacrifices. Different scriptures list the five sacrifices differently: Vedic sacrifices, Smriti sacrifices, Pancharatra practices, Kulagama forms, nityā tantra forms, and the Agnihotra-related five offerings. She is fond of all these forms of yajna."],"searchText":"946 पञ्चयज्ञप्रिया पञ्चसंख्याका यज्ञाः पञ्चयज्ञाः। ते प्रिया यस्याः सा। यज्ञाः — sacrifices प्रिया — dear यस्याः — whose पञ्चयज्ञप्रिया means one who loves the five kinds of sacrifices. different scriptures list the five sacrifices differently: vedic sacrifices, smriti sacrifices, pancharatra practices, kulagama forms, nityā tantra forms, and the agnihotra-related five offerings. she is fond of all these forms of yajna. the harmony of daily sacrifice: the scripture mandates the pañca-mahā-yajñas (sacrifice to the absolute, to ancestors, to deities, to humans, and to animals) to clear existential debts and balance the earth space. she is pañcayajñapriyā because this daily practice keeps human activity in harmony with the cosmos, turning routine life into a field of pure devotion.","esoteric":["The Harmony of Daily Sacrifice: The scripture mandates the Pañca-Mahā-Yajñas (sacrifice to the absolute, to ancestors, to deities, to humans, and to animals) to clear existential debts and balance the earth space. She is Pañcayajñapriyā because this daily practice keeps human activity in harmony with the cosmos, turning routine life into a field of pure devotion."]},{"number":947,"name":"पञ्चप्रेतमञ्चाधिशायिनी","samasa":["ब्रह्मादयश्चत्वारः प्रेताः पादाः। सदाशिवाख्यः प्रेतः फलकमेतादृशं मञ्चं पर्यङ्कमधिशेते।"],"wordByWord":["प्रेताः — corpses","पञ्चप्रेतमञ्चाधिशायिनी। — component of the name"],"summary":["पञ्चप्रेतमञ्चाधिशायिनी means one who reclines on a couch made of five corpses. To show that She is greater than the five cosmic functions, the performers of those functions are treated as the legs and plank of Her couch. Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra and Eshvara are the four legs, and Sadashiva is the plank or sheet. Without their Śaktis they cannot act; therefore they are described as corpses. This bed is praised in Bhairavayamala, Lalitā Stavaratna, Soundaryalahari, Rudrayamala and other texts."],"searchText":"947 पञ्चप्रेतमञ्चाधिशायिनी ब्रह्मादयश्चत्वारः प्रेताः पादाः। सदाशिवाख्यः प्रेतः फलकमेतादृशं मञ्चं पर्यङ्कमधिशेते। प्रेताः — corpses पञ्चप्रेतमञ्चाधिशायिनी। — component of the name पञ्चप्रेतमञ्चाधिशायिनी means one who reclines on a couch made of five corpses. to show that she is greater than the five cosmic functions, the performers of those functions are treated as the legs and plank of her couch. brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra and eshvara are the four legs, and sadashiva is the plank or sheet. without their śaktis they cannot act; therefore they are described as corpses. this bed is praised in bhairavayamala, lalitā stavaratna, soundaryalahari, rudrayamala and other texts. the supreme throne past the five functions: the couch where she rests at the center of the royal chamber is constructed out of the five cosmic administrators: ब्रह्मा (creation), विष्णु (preservation), रुद्र (dissolution), and ईश्वर (concealment) serve as the four vertical legs, while सदाशिव (grace) forms the flat seating plank. without her dynamic energy field, these five deities are inert like corpses (preta). she sits above them, demonstrating her status as the supreme, non-dual source that gives life to cosmic functions.","esoteric":["The Supreme Throne past the Five Functions: The couch where She rests at the center of the royal chamber is constructed out of the five cosmic administrators: ब्रह्मा (Creation), विष्णु (Preservation), रुद्र (Dissolution), and ईश्वर (Concealment) serve as the four vertical legs, while सदाशिव (Grace) forms the flat seating plank. Without Her dynamic energy field, these five deities are inert like corpses (preta). She sits above them, demonstrating Her status as the supreme, non-dual source that gives life to cosmic functions."]},{"number":948,"name":"पञ्चमी","samasa":["ब्रह्मादिषु पञ्चसु पञ्चमस्य सदाशिवस्य स्त्री।","मकारेषु पञ्चमस्यानन्दरूपत्वात्तद्रूपा।","पञ्चानां मानां मकाराणां समाहारः।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्चमी। — component of the name"],"summary":["पञ्चमी means one who is the consort of Sadashiva. Brahmā, Viṣṇu, Rudra, Eshvara and Sadashiva are described together; She is the Śakti of the fifth, Sadashiva. The name also relates to the fifth principle among the five."],"searchText":"948 पञ्चमी ब्रह्मादिषु पञ्चसु पञ्चमस्य सदाशिवस्य स्त्री। मकारेषु पञ्चमस्यानन्दरूपत्वात्तद्रूपा। पञ्चानां मानां मकाराणां समाहारः। पञ्चमी। — component of the name पञ्चमी means one who is the consort of sadashiva. brahmā, viṣṇu, rudra, eshvara and sadashiva are described together; she is the śakti of the fifth, sadashiva. the name also relates to the fifth principle among the five. the power of the fifth order: within the administrative framework, she is pañcamī because she is the dynamic consort of the absolute fifth principle—sadāśiva (the lord of grace). in the specialized vocabulary of agamic practice, she represents the critical fifth element—आनन्द (ananda — supreme non-dual bliss) — which functions as the crown energy that completes the purification process.","esoteric":["The Power of the Fifth Order: Within the administrative framework, She is Pañcamī because She is the dynamic consort of the absolute fifth principle—Sadāśiva (the Lord of Grace). In the specialized vocabulary of Agamic practice, She represents the critical fifth element—आनन्द (Ananda — supreme non-dual bliss) — which functions as the crown energy that completes the purification process."]},{"number":949,"name":"पञ्चभूतेशी","samasa":["पञ्चसंख्यानां भूतानां पृथिव्यादीनामीशी।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्चभूतेशी। — component of the name"],"summary":["पञ्चभूतेशी means one who is the ruler of the five elements. The five elements are earth, water, fire, air and ether. She is their presiding power and inner controller."],"searchText":"949 पञ्चभूतेशी पञ्चसंख्यानां भूतानां पृथिव्यादीनामीशी। पञ्चभूतेशी। — component of the name पञ्चभूतेशी means one who is the ruler of the five elements. the five elements are earth, water, fire, air and ether. she is their presiding power and inner controller. the governor of the material grid: the entire physical universe is constructed out of the combinations of the five gross elements (pañca-mahābhūta). she is the absolute īśvarī (empress) who designs and governs their laws, formatting how gravity, fluid dynamics, heat exchange, atmospheric friction, and spatial containment operate across the macrocosmic grid.","esoteric":["The Governor of the Material Grid: The entire physical universe is constructed out of the combinations of the five gross elements (pañca-mahābhūta). She is the absolute Īśvarī (empress) who designs and governs their laws, formatting how gravity, fluid dynamics, heat exchange, atmospheric friction, and spatial containment operate across the macrocosmic grid."]},{"number":950,"name":"पञ्चसंख्योपचारिणी","samasa":["पञ्चसंख्या उपचारा अस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["पञ्चसंख्योपचारिणी। — component of the name"],"summary":["पञ्चसंख्योपचारिणी means one who is worshipped with five upacharas. The five forms of worship are connected with the elements and with the prescribed offerings. She is pleased by worship performed through these five modes."],"searchText":"950 पञ्चसंख्योपचारिणी पञ्चसंख्या उपचारा अस्याः अस्तीति। पञ्चसंख्योपचारिणी। — component of the name पञ्चसंख्योपचारिणी means one who is worshipped with five upacharas. the five forms of worship are connected with the elements and with the prescribed offerings. she is pleased by worship performed through these five modes. the cosmos offered back to the source: the five primary ritual offerings—गन्ध (sandalwood paste), पुष्प (flowers), धूप (incense), दीप (light), and नैवेद्य (food)—are not simple external objects. in the internal alignment matrix, they correspond perfectly to the five elements: earth, space, air, fire, and water. she is pañcasaṅkhyopacāriṇī because when a practitioner performs this five-fold worship (pañcopacāra), they are systematically offering the entire element fabric of the cosmos back into her non-dual light, completing the loop of realization.","esoteric":["The Cosmos Offered Back to the Source: The five primary ritual offerings—गन्ध (Sandalwood paste), पुष्प (Flowers), धूप (Incense), दीप (Light), and नैवेद्य (Food)—are not simple external objects. In the internal alignment matrix, they correspond perfectly to the five elements: Earth, Space, Air, Fire, and Water. She is Pañcasaṅkhyopacāriṇī because when a practitioner performs this five-fold worship (pañcopacāra), they are systematically offering the entire element fabric of the cosmos back into Her non-dual light, completing the loop of realization."]},{"number":951,"name":"शाश्वती","samasa":["शश्वत् पौनःपुन्यं तत्सम्बन्धिनी पुनःपुनरभ्यस्यमानेत्यर्थः।","नित्या।"],"wordByWord":["शाश्वती। — component of the name"],"summary":["शाश्वती means one who is eternal. Shashvati also indicates that which is repeatedly practised or remembered. She is ever-existing and worthy of repeated contemplation."],"searchText":"951 शाश्वती शश्वत् पौनःपुन्यं तत्सम्बन्धिनी पुनःपुनरभ्यस्यमानेत्यर्थः। नित्या। शाश्वती। — component of the name शाश्वती means one who is eternal. shashvati also indicates that which is repeatedly practised or remembered. she is ever-existing and worthy of repeated contemplation. the continuous awakening: she is śāśvatī because her existence is completely unaffected by linear time modifications. under the practice track, she is the continuous phonic presence discovered through repetitive, rhythmic recitation (pounahpunya), remaining as the permanent substrate behind transient thoughts.","esoteric":["The Continuous Awakening: She is Śāśvatī because Her existence is completely unaffected by linear time modifications. Under the practice track, She is the continuous phonic presence discovered through repetitive, rhythmic recitation (pounahpunya), remaining as the permanent substrate behind transient thoughts."]},{"number":952,"name":"शाश्वतैश्वर्या","samasa":["शाश्वतं नित्यमैश्वर्यं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शाश्वतं — eternal","यस्याः — whose","शाश्वतैश्वर्या। — component of the name"],"summary":["शाश्वतैश्वर्या means one whose sovereignty is eternal. Her lordship is not temporary or dependent. It may be compared with the earlier description of the Panchapreta couch, where all divine powers depend on Her."],"searchText":"952 शाश्वतैश्वर्या शाश्वतं नित्यमैश्वर्यं यस्याः सा। शाश्वतं — eternal यस्याः — whose शाश्वतैश्वर्या। — component of the name शाश्वतैश्वर्या means one whose sovereignty is eternal. her lordship is not temporary or dependent. it may be compared with the earlier description of the panchapreta couch, where all divine powers depend on her. unbounded sovereignty: earthly rulers and secondary deities hold conditional power (aiśvarya) that updates or expires based on cosmic cycles. she is śāśvataiśvaryā because her executive legislative capacity is uncreated and permanent, running the matrices of creation without external authorization.","esoteric":["Unbounded Sovereignty: Earthly rulers and secondary deities hold conditional power (aiśvarya) that updates or expires based on cosmic cycles. She is Śāśvataiśvaryā because Her executive legislative capacity is uncreated and permanent, running the matrices of creation without external authorization."]},{"number":953,"name":"शर्मदा","samasa":["शर्म सुखं दत्ते।"],"wordByWord":["शर्म — happiness","शर्मदा। — component of the name"],"summary":["शर्मदा means one who gives happiness. Sharma means happiness, comfort or blessedness. She bestows such happiness on Her devotees."],"searchText":"953 शर्मदा शर्म सुखं दत्ते। शर्म — happiness शर्मदा। — component of the name शर्मदा means one who gives happiness. sharma means happiness, comfort or blessedness. she bestows such happiness on her devotees. the rest of the soul: śarma does not signify localized, passing sensory excitement. it refers to the absolute, unconditioned peace and comfort of resting within the true self (svarūpānanda). she acts as the direct channel that dispenses this baseline rest, terminating individual lack.","esoteric":["The Rest of the Soul: Śarma does not signify localized, passing sensory excitement. It refers to the absolute, unconditioned peace and comfort of resting within the true Self (Svarūpānanda). She acts as the direct channel that dispenses this baseline rest, terminating individual lack."]},{"number":954,"name":"शम्भुमोहिनी","samasa":["शम्भुं मोहयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["शम्भुमोहिनी। — component of the name"],"summary":["शम्भुमोहिनी means one who enchants Shambhu. Even Śiva, the auspicious Lord, is attracted by Her beauty and power. This name praises Her power to delight and enchant Shambhu Himself."],"searchText":"954 शम्भुमोहिनी शम्भुं मोहयतीति। शम्भुमोहिनी। — component of the name शम्भुमोहिनी means one who enchants shambhu. even śiva, the auspicious lord, is attracted by her beauty and power. this name praises her power to delight and enchant shambhu himself. the enchantment of stillness: lord śiva as śambhu is the still, self-contained, and unmanifest absolute. he would remain permanently unmoving without an internal stir. she is śambhumohinī because her dynamic, enchanting energy field charms him into self-awareness, drawing him out to witness the unfolding of the multiverse.","esoteric":["The Enchantment of Stillness: Lord Śiva as Śambhu is the still, self-contained, and unmanifest absolute. He would remain permanently unmoving without an internal stir. She is Śambhumohinī because Her dynamic, enchanting energy field charms Him into self-awareness, drawing Him out to witness the unfolding of the multiverse."]},{"number":955,"name":"धरा","samasa":["धरा पृथ्वीस्वरूपा।","सर्वस्य जगतो धारणात्।"],"wordByWord":["धरा — earth; supporter","धरा। — component of the name"],"summary":["धरा means one who is Earth. Dhara also means one who bears or supports. She supports the whole universe as the earth supports all beings."],"searchText":"955 धरा धरा पृथ्वीस्वरूपा। सर्वस्य जगतो धारणात्। धरा — earth; supporter धरा। — component of the name धरा means one who is earth. dhara also means one who bears or supports. she supports the whole universe as the earth supports all beings. the absolute support: she is dharā because she is the structural capacity that bears and anchors the entire manifest universe (jagat). materially, she manifests as the foundational element of earth (pṛthivī), providing the stabilizing ground metric that supports living things.","esoteric":["The Absolute Support: She is Dharā because She is the structural capacity that bears and anchors the entire manifest universe (jagat). Materially, She manifests as the foundational element of Earth (Pṛthivī), providing the stabilizing ground metric that supports living things."]},{"number":956,"name":"धरसुता","samasa":["धरस्य हिमवत्पर्वतस्य सुता।"],"wordByWord":["धरसुता। — component of the name"],"summary":["धरसुता means one who is the daughter of the mountain. Dhara is the mountain, especially Himavan. She is praised as the daughter of the mountain king."],"searchText":"956 धरसुता धरस्य हिमवत्पर्वतस्य सुता। धरसुता। — component of the name धरसुता means one who is the daughter of the mountain. dhara is the mountain, especially himavan. she is praised as the daughter of the mountain king. the offspring of solidity: mythologically, she takes birth as pārvatī, the daughter of the stable mountain king. metaphysically, a mountain represents unmoving structural stability, internal concentration, and spiritual altitude. by emerging as dharasutā, she confirms that her energy forms the peak of absolute, unbending meditation.","esoteric":["The Offspring of Solidity: Mythologically, She takes birth as Pārvatī, the daughter of the stable mountain king. Metaphysically, a mountain represents unmoving structural stability, internal concentration, and spiritual altitude. By emerging as Dharasutā, She confirms that Her energy forms the peak of absolute, unbending meditation."]},{"number":957,"name":"धन्या","samasa":["कृतार्था।","धनाय हिता।","धनं लब्ध्री।","योगिनीविशेषरूपा।","धन्याख्यध्यानरूपा।"],"wordByWord":["धन्या। — component of the name"],"summary":["धन्या means one who is blessed and fulfilled. Dhanya also means one who is beneficial for wealth, one who obtains wealth, a particular yoginī, and a form of meditation. She is the auspicious and fulfilled one who grants blessedness."],"searchText":"957 धन्या कृतार्था। धनाय हिता। धनं लब्ध्री। योगिनीविशेषरूपा। धन्याख्यध्यानरूपा। धन्या। — component of the name धन्या means one who is blessed and fulfilled. dhanya also means one who is beneficial for wealth, one who obtains wealth, a particular yoginī, and a form of meditation. she is the auspicious and fulfilled one who grants blessedness. the state of perfect completion: she is dhanyā because she exists in a state of absolute, self-contained fulfillment (kṛtārthā), lacking zero internal assets. yogically, she manifests as a specialized meditative light state (dhanyā-dhyāna) that clears mental fog, aligning the intellect with pristine metrics.","esoteric":["The State of Perfect Completion: She is Dhanyā because She exists in a state of absolute, self-contained fulfillment (kṛtārthā), lacking zero internal assets. Yogically, She manifests as a specialized meditative light state (dhanyā-dhyāna) that clears mental fog, aligning the intellect with pristine metrics."]},{"number":958,"name":"धर्मिणी","samasa":["धर्मः शीलमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["धर्मः — dharma; righteousness","धर्मिणी। — component of the name"],"summary":["धर्मिणी means one who possesses dharma. dharma is Her nature and conduct. She embodies righteousness and sacred order."],"searchText":"958 धर्मिणी धर्मः शीलमस्याः अस्तीति। धर्मः — dharma; righteousness धर्मिणी। — component of the name धर्मिणी means one who possesses dharma. dharma is her nature and conduct. she embodies righteousness and sacred order. the embodiment of righteousness: righteousness (dharma) is not an external code of conduct she follows out of duty. she is dharmiṇī because moral order, universal justice, and structural integrity constitute her baseline nature and character (śīla). she is the law itself.","esoteric":["The Embodiment of Righteousness: Righteousness (Dharma) is not an external code of conduct She follows out of duty. She is Dharmiṇī because moral order, universal justice, and structural integrity constitute Her baseline nature and character (śīla). She is the law itself."]},{"number":959,"name":"धर्मवर्धिनी","samasa":["धर्मं वर्धयतीति।","धर्ममात्रं दृश्यजातं छेदयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["धर्मवर्धिनी। — component of the name"],"summary":["धर्मवर्धिनी means one who increases dharma. She causes righteousness to grow. She also cuts away what obstructs true dharma."],"searchText":"959 धर्मवर्धिनी धर्मं वर्धयतीति। धर्ममात्रं दृश्यजातं छेदयतीति। धर्मवर्धिनी। — component of the name धर्मवर्धिनी means one who increases dharma. she causes righteousness to grow. she also cuts away what obstructs true dharma. the cultivator of justice: as vivardhinī, she actively amplifies the parameters of spiritual virtue (dharma) inside the heart of the seeker. under the second technical track, she acts as the sharp intelligence that cuts down the false reality of phenomenal properties (dharma-mātram), revealing the non-dual background.","esoteric":["The Cultivator of Justice: As Vivardhinī, She actively amplifies the parameters of spiritual virtue (Dharma) inside the heart of the seeker. Under the second technical track, She acts as the sharp intelligence that cuts down the false reality of phenomenal properties (dharma-mātram), revealing the non-dual background."]},{"number":960,"name":"लोकातीता","samasa":["लोकानतीतातिक्रम्य स्थिता।","लोकाञ्जीवान्वाऽतीता।"],"wordByWord":["लोकातीता। — component of the name"],"summary":["लोकातीता means one who transcends the worlds. She stands beyond all lokas and beyond individual beings. No world can limit Her."],"searchText":"960 लोकातीता लोकानतीतातिक्रम्य स्थिता। लोकाञ्जीवान्वाऽतीता। लोकातीता। — component of the name लोकातीता means one who transcends the worlds. she stands beyond all lokas and beyond individual beings. no world can limit her. the transcendent sky: the fourteen functional worlds (lokas) format the spaces for karmic transaction. she is lokātītā because her essential nature as parabrahman sits entirely outside and above this dimensional network, remaining unconfined by local coordinates.","esoteric":["The Transcendent Sky: The fourteen functional worlds (lokas) format the spaces for karmic transaction. She is Lokātītā because Her essential nature as Parabrahman sits entirely outside and above this dimensional network, remaining unconfined by local coordinates."]},{"number":961,"name":"गुणातीता","samasa":["गुणानतीता।"],"wordByWord":["गुणातीता। — component of the name"],"summary":["गुणातीता means one who is beyond the gunas. The three gunas belong to Prakriti. She transcends them completely."],"searchText":"961 गुणातीता गुणानतीता। गुणातीता। — component of the name गुणातीता means one who is beyond the gunas. the three gunas belong to prakriti. she transcends them completely. beyond the material triad: shifting material properties create colors, forms, and changes inside the mind. she is guṇātītā because her ultimate reality is completely unconditioned (nirguṇa). she instructs the practitioner to look past the movements of light and mass, anchoring themselves in her unblemished, quality-less space.","esoteric":["Beyond the Material Triad: Shifting material properties create colors, forms, and changes inside the mind. She is Guṇātītā because Her ultimate reality is completely unconditioned (Nirguṇa). She instructs the practitioner to look past the movements of light and mass, anchoring themselves in Her unblemished, quality-less space."]},{"number":962,"name":"सर्वातीता","samasa":["सर्वमतीता।","सर्वान् शब्दानतीता।"],"wordByWord":["सर्वातीता। — component of the name"],"summary":["सर्वातीता means one who is beyond everything. She surpasses all objects and all words. No category or description can contain Her."],"searchText":"962 सर्वातीता सर्वमतीता। सर्वान् शब्दानतीता। सर्वातीता। — component of the name सर्वातीता means one who is beyond everything. she surpasses all objects and all words. no category or description can contain her. the shoreless remainder: lest any conceptual boundary be left unaddressed, this title confirms that she is sarvātītā — completely beyond everything that can be named, counted, or computed. critically, she passes beyond all spoken language and definitions (śabda-ātītā), existing as the silent, unconditioned truth that sits past description.","esoteric":["The Shoreless Remainder: Lest any conceptual boundary be left unaddressed, this title confirms that She is Sarvātītā — completely beyond everything that can be named, counted, or computed. Critically, She passes beyond all spoken language and definitions (śabda-ātītā), existing as the silent, unconditioned truth that sits past description."]},{"number":963,"name":"शमात्मिका","samasa":["शमः प्रपञ्चोपशम एवात्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["शमः — peace; quiescence","यस्याः — whose","शमात्मिका। — component of the name"],"summary":["शमात्मिका means one whose nature is peace. Shama means the quieting or subsidence of the universe. Her own form is the peaceful cessation of the entire phenomenal display."],"searchText":"963 शमात्मिका शमः प्रपञ्चोपशम एवात्मा स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। शमः — peace; quiescence यस्याः — whose शमात्मिका। — component of the name शमात्मिका means one whose nature is peace. shama means the quieting or subsidence of the universe. her own form is the peaceful cessation of the entire phenomenal display. the quietude of the screen: śama is not a simple emotional calculation of calmness. it refers to the absolute, grand quietude that occurs when the entire movie of manifest worlds dissolves back into unmanifest stillness (प्रपञ्चोपशम). she is śamātmikā because her body is this pristine, unperturbed silence, offering a home where all mental friction is terminated.","esoteric":["The Quietude of the Screen: Śama is not a simple emotional calculation of calmness. It refers to the absolute, grand quietude that occurs when the entire movie of manifest worlds dissolves back into unmanifest stillness (प्रपञ्चोपशम). She is Śamātmikā because Her body is this pristine, unperturbed silence, offering a home where all mental friction is terminated."]},{"number":964,"name":"बन्धूककुसुमप्रख्या","samasa":["बन्धूको महावृक्षस्तस्य कुसुमं पुष्पं तस्येव प्रख्या कान्तिर्यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["प्रख्या — resembling; lustre","बन्धूककुसुमप्रख्या। — component of the name"],"summary":["बन्धूककुसुमप्रख्या means one whose complexion is like the Bandhuka flower. The Bandhuka blossom is bright and red. Her radiance is compared with that flower."],"searchText":"964 बन्धूककुसुमप्रख्या बन्धूको महावृक्षस्तस्य कुसुमं पुष्पं तस्येव प्रख्या कान्तिर्यस्याः सा। प्रख्या — resembling; lustre बन्धूककुसुमप्रख्या। — component of the name बन्धूककुसुमप्रख्या means one whose complexion is like the bandhuka flower. the bandhuka blossom is bright and red. her radiance is compared with that flower. the flash of active awareness: the bandhūka blossom exhibits an exceptionally deep, unblemished crimson-red hue. in the physics of visualization, this frequency represents the absolute activation of विमर्शशक्ति (vimarśa-śakti — active self-recognition) overflowing with compassionate intent. meditating on this color pattern burns away internal lethargy, tuning the channels to clear light.","esoteric":["The Flash of Active Awareness: The Bandhūka blossom exhibits an exceptionally deep, unblemished crimson-red hue. In the physics of visualization, this frequency represents the absolute activation of विमर्शशक्ति (Vimarśa-śakti — active self-recognition) overflowing with compassionate intent. Meditating on this color pattern burns away internal lethargy, tuning the channels to clear light."]},{"number":965,"name":"बाला","samasa":["कुमारी।"],"wordByWord":["बाला। — component of the name"],"summary":["बाला means one who is a young girl. Bālā means maiden or child. The name also points to Her youthful and worshipful Bālā form."],"searchText":"965 बाला कुमारी। बाला। — component of the name बाला means one who is a young girl. bālā means maiden or child. the name also points to her youthful and worshipful bālā form. the ever-youthful core: she is bālā because her energy remains permanently fresh, vibrant, and untouched by biological aging or structural decay. in the initiatory lineage, she is non-different from बाला त्रिपुरसुन्दरी (bālā tripurasundarī) — the highly potent three-syllabled entry gateway deity whose mantra formats the foundational channels of the student.","esoteric":["The Ever-Youthful Core: She is Bālā because Her energy remains permanently fresh, vibrant, and untouched by biological aging or structural decay. In the initiatory lineage, She is non-different from बाला त्रिपुरसुन्दरी (Bālā Tripurasundarī) — the highly potent three-syllabled entry gateway deity whose mantra formats the foundational channels of the student."]},{"number":966,"name":"लीलाविनोदिनी","samasa":["लीला","प्रापञ्चिकी क्रीडैव विनोदो यस्याः सा।","पद्यराजस्य भार्या लीलाख्या योगवासिष्ठे प्रसिद्धा तां विशिष्य सत्कर्मसु नोदयतीति।"],"wordByWord":["लीला — play; sport","यस्याः — whose","लीलाविनोदिनी। — component of the name"],"summary":["लीलाविनोदिनी means one who delights in sport. The play of the universe itself is Her pastime."],"searchText":"966 लीलाविनोदिनी लीला प्रापञ्चिकी क्रीडैव विनोदो यस्याः सा। पद्यराजस्य भार्या लीलाख्या योगवासिष्ठे प्रसिद्धा तां विशिष्य सत्कर्मसु नोदयतीति। लीला — play; sport यस्याः — whose लीलाविनोदिनी। — component of the name लीलाविनोदिनी means one who delights in sport. the play of the universe itself is her pastime. the delight of the play: the generation, maintenance, and dissolution of trillions of stellar systems is not a source of stress or heavy labor for her consciousness. it is handled as a spontaneous, completely effortless game (līlā). she watches this planetary deployment with pure amusement (vinoda), remaining detached and joyful.","esoteric":["The Delight of the Play: The generation, maintenance, and dissolution of trillions of stellar systems is not a source of stress or heavy labor for Her consciousness. It is handled as a spontaneous, completely effortless game (līlā). She watches this planetary deployment with pure amusement (vinoda), remaining detached and joyful."]},{"number":967,"name":"सुमङ्गली","samasa":["शोभनं मङ्गलमस्या अस्तीति।","शोभनं मङ्गलं ब्रह्मैवेति।"],"wordByWord":["सुमङ्गली। — component of the name"],"summary":["सुमङ्गली means one who is very auspicious. sumaṅgalī also denotes a woman whose husband is alive. Since auspiciousness indicates Brahman, She is the form of auspicious Brahman and removes sorrow."],"searchText":"967 सुमङ्गली शोभनं मङ्गलमस्या अस्तीति। शोभनं मङ्गलं ब्रह्मैवेति। सुमङ्गली। — component of the name सुमङ्गली means one who is very auspicious. sumaṅgalī also denotes a woman whose husband is alive. since auspiciousness indicates brahman, she is the form of auspicious brahman and removes sorrow. the auspicious anchor: she is sumaṅgalī because her presence generates overall protection, prosperity, and balance across the workspace. critically, the ultimate, uncorrupted auspiciousness (maṅgalam) is the absolute brahman itself. she is the literal embodiment of this baseline goodness.","esoteric":["The Auspicious Anchor: She is Sumaṅgalī because Her presence generates overall protection, prosperity, and balance across the workspace. Critically, the ultimate, uncorrupted auspiciousness (maṅgalam) is the absolute Brahman itself. She is the literal embodiment of this baseline goodness."]},{"number":968,"name":"सुखकरी","samasa":["सुखं करोति तच्छीलम्।"],"wordByWord":["करोति — makes; causes","सुखकरी। — component of the name"],"summary":["सुखकरी means one who gives happiness. This repeats the same message seen in names such as Sharmadayini, Sukhaprada and Sharmada. She grants joy and blessedness."],"searchText":"968 सुखकरी सुखं करोति तच्छीलम्। करोति — makes; causes सुखकरी। — component of the name सुखकरी means one who gives happiness. this repeats the same message seen in names such as sharmadayini, sukhaprada and sharmada. she grants joy and blessedness. the manufacturer of ease: her baseline operations are naturally formatted to convert the friction of material existence into steady, soul-level happiness (sukha). she does not distribute temporary psychological thrill; she sets the conditions that allow the seeker's mind to rest in ease.","esoteric":["The Manufacturer of Ease: Her baseline operations are naturally formatted to convert the friction of material existence into steady, soul-level happiness (sukha). She does not distribute temporary psychological thrill; She sets the conditions that allow the seeker's mind to rest in ease."]},{"number":969,"name":"सुवेषाढ्या","samasa":["शोभनेन वेषेणाढ्या युक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["सुवेषाढ्या। — component of the name"],"summary":["सुवेषाढ्या means one decked with beautiful garments and ornaments. Since She is sumaṅgalī, She is adorned with auspicious raiment and ornaments. She is richly decorated with jewels and gold ornaments."],"searchText":"969 सुवेषाढ्या शोभनेन वेषेणाढ्या युक्ता। सुवेषाढ्या। — component of the name सुवेषाढ्या means one decked with beautiful garments and ornaments. since she is sumaṅgalī, she is adorned with auspicious raiment and ornaments. she is richly decorated with jewels and gold ornaments. the raiment of pure radiance: her \"vestures\" (veṣa) are not woven fabrics. they are the beautiful visual rays of इच्छा, ज्ञान, क्रिया (will, knowledge, action) that drape around her form. she is suveṣāḍhyā because she is richly wrapped in these flawless aesthetic geometries, which serve to clear away dark, chaotic currents from the field of view.","esoteric":["The Raiment of Pure Radiance: Her \"vestures\" (veṣa) are not woven fabrics. They are the beautiful visual rays of इच्छा, ज्ञान, क्रिया (Will, Knowledge, Action) that drape around Her form. She is Suveṣāḍhyā because She is richly wrapped in these flawless aesthetic geometries, which serve to clear away dark, chaotic currents from the field of view."]},{"number":970,"name":"सुवासिनी","samasa":["सुवासिनी।","सुवासिनीनामर्चनेन प्रीता।"],"wordByWord":["सुवासिनी। — component of the name"],"summary":["सुवासिनी means one who lives with Her husband. Living with one's husband is praised as a great blessing for ladies, and the word Suvasini indicates that auspicious state. Texts such as Srimad Ramayana are cited to praise this sacred condition."],"searchText":"970 सुवासिनी सुवासिनी। सुवासिनीनामर्चनेन प्रीता। सुवासिनी। — component of the name सुवासिनी means one who lives with her husband. living with one's husband is praised as a great blessing for ladies, and the word suvasini indicates that auspicious state. texts such as srimad ramayana are cited to praise this sacred condition. the living shield of auspiciousness: suvāsinī denotes a woman who embodies active marital protection and auspicious vitality. metaphysically, she is suvāsinī because her eternal partner, paramaśiva, is perpetually alive and present. concurrently, she is the intelligence that perfumes (vāsa) the entire multiverse with the fragrance of consciousness, abiding securely inside all elements.","esoteric":["The Living Shield of Auspiciousness: Suvāsinī denotes a woman who embodies active marital protection and auspicious vitality. Metaphysically, She is Suvāsinī because Her eternal partner, Paramaśiva, is perpetually alive and present. Concurrently, She is the intelligence that perfumes (vāsa) the entire multiverse with the fragrance of consciousness, abiding securely inside all elements."]},{"number":971,"name":"सुवासिन्यर्चनप्रीता","samasa":["सुवासिनीनाम् अर्चनेन प्रीता।"],"wordByWord":["सुवासिन्यर्चनप्रीता। — component of the name"],"summary":["सुवासिन्यर्चनप्रीता means one who is pleased by the worship done by Suvasinis. Or one who is pleased by doing archana to Suvasinis. Worshipping Suvasinis is treated as an important part of Śrīdevī worship, since all women are to be regarded as forms of Śrīdevī."],"searchText":"971 सुवासिन्यर्चनप्रीता सुवासिनीनाम् अर्चनेन प्रीता। सुवासिन्यर्चनप्रीता। — component of the name सुवासिन्यर्चनप्रीता means one who is pleased by the worship done by suvasinis. or one who is pleased by doing archana to suvasinis. worshipping suvasinis is treated as an important part of śrīdevī worship, since all women are to be regarded as forms of śrīdevī. the living altars: she does not limit her presence to metallic icons or drawings. she sits actively inside living human forms that project auspicious energy (suvāsinīs). when a practitioner honors, clothes, and feeds these living women with absolute reverence, she accepts that energy directly, clearing away obstacles from the path.","esoteric":["The Living Altars: She does not limit Her presence to metallic icons or drawings. She sits actively inside living human forms that project auspicious energy (suvāsinīs). When a practitioner honors, clothes, and feeds these living women with absolute reverence, She accepts that energy directly, clearing away obstacles from the path."]},{"number":972,"name":"अशोभना/आशोभना","samasa":["अविद्यमानं शोभनं सौन्दर्यं यस्याः (पञ्चमी) सा।","आसमन्तात् शोभनं सौन्दर्यं यस्याः (षष्ठी) सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose","अशोभना — component of the name","आशोभना। — component of the name"],"summary":["अशोभना/आशोभना means one who is always and everywhere beautiful. Her beauty is described in many places in the sahasranāma. A large part of Soundaryalahari is devoted to the description of Her beauty."],"searchText":"972 अशोभना/आशोभना अविद्यमानं शोभनं सौन्दर्यं यस्याः (पञ्चमी) सा। आसमन्तात् शोभनं सौन्दर्यं यस्याः (षष्ठी) सा। यस्याः — whose अशोभना — component of the name आशोभना। — component of the name अशोभना/आशोभना means one who is always and everywhere beautiful. her beauty is described in many places in the sahasranāma. a large part of soundaryalahari is devoted to the description of her beauty. beyond mundane aesthetics: as aśobhanā, she stands completely free from mundane, superficial, and relative standards of physical beauty, which are transient and deceptive. when parsed as āśobhanā, it establishes that she possesses absolute, permanent, and infinite beauty (paramam saundaryam) radiating from every single coordinate of her cosmic form, blinding the intellect with absolute grace.","esoteric":["Beyond Mundane Aesthetics: As Aśobhanā, She stands completely free from mundane, superficial, and relative standards of physical beauty, which are transient and deceptive. When parsed as Āśobhanā, it establishes that She possesses absolute, permanent, and infinite beauty (paramam saundaryam) radiating from every single coordinate of Her cosmic form, blinding the intellect with absolute grace."]},{"number":973,"name":"शुद्धमानसा","samasa":["शुद्धं मानसं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose","शुद्धमानसा। — component of the name"],"summary":["शुद्धमानसा means one whose mind is pure. Her internal nature is untouched by impurity. She is the embodiment of purity of mind."],"searchText":"973 शुद्धमानसा शुद्धं मानसं यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose शुद्धमानसा। — component of the name शुद्धमानसा means one whose mind is pure. her internal nature is untouched by impurity. she is the embodiment of purity of mind. the unblemished screen: human minds gather dust through desires and prejudices. her cosmic mind (mānasa) is śuddha — completely free from any latent impressions, ignorance, or emotional fluctuations. she remains a clear, crystal-like awareness screen that reflects the universe without being stained by it.","esoteric":["The Unblemished Screen: Human minds gather dust through desires and prejudices. Her cosmic mind (mānasa) is Śuddha — completely free from any latent impressions, ignorance, or emotional fluctuations. She remains a clear, crystal-like awareness screen that reflects the universe without being stained by it."]},{"number":974,"name":"बिन्दुतर्पणसन्तुष्टा","samasa":["बिन्दौ सर्वानन्दमये चक्रे ब्राह्मणादिवर्णचतुष्टयकर्तृकेण तर्पणेन सम्यक्तुष्टा।","क्षीराज्यमध्वासवबिन्दुकरणकेन वा तर्पणेन सम्यक्तुष्टा।"],"wordByWord":["बिन्दुतर्पणसन्तुष्टा। — component of the name"],"summary":["बिन्दुतर्पणसन्तुष्टा means one satisfied by tarpana at the bindu. The bindu is the Sarvanandamaya cakra, and offerings there please Her. Tarpana with milk, ghee, honey, wine or other prescribed offerings is also indicated."],"searchText":"974 बिन्दुतर्पणसन्तुष्टा बिन्दौ सर्वानन्दमये चक्रे ब्राह्मणादिवर्णचतुष्टयकर्तृकेण तर्पणेन सम्यक्तुष्टा। क्षीराज्यमध्वासवबिन्दुकरणकेन वा तर्पणेन सम्यक्तुष्टा। बिन्दुतर्पणसन्तुष्टा। — component of the name बिन्दुतर्पणसन्तुष्टा means one satisfied by tarpana at the bindu. the bindu is the sarvanandamaya cakra, and offerings there please her. tarpana with milk, ghee, honey, wine or other prescribed offerings is also indicated. the alchemy of the center point: externally, this denotes offering drops (bindu) of milk, honey, or consecrated liquids into the central hub of the yantra. internally, bindu refers to the absolute central point of the sahasrāra crown. when the practitioner drives the internal energy up to this center, it melts the absolute nectar of immortality. offering this nectar back into the point satisfies her, stabilizing the system.","esoteric":["The Alchemy of the Center Point: Externally, this denotes offering drops (bindu) of milk, honey, or consecrated liquids into the central hub of the Yantra. Internally, Bindu refers to the absolute central point of the Sahasrāra crown. When the practitioner drives the internal energy up to this center, it melts the absolute nectar of immortality. Offering this nectar back into the point satisfies Her, stabilizing the system."]},{"number":975,"name":"पूर्वजा","samasa":["पूर्वं जा जाता अभिव्यक्ता।"],"wordByWord":["जा — born; manifested","पूर्वजा। — component of the name"],"summary":["पूर्वजा means one who is born or manifested first. She is prior to all manifestation. She is the first and original principle."],"searchText":"975 पूर्वजा पूर्वं जा जाता अभिव्यक्ता। जा — born; manifested पूर्वजा। — component of the name पूर्वजा means one who is born or manifested first. she is prior to all manifestation. she is the first and original principle. the primordial manifestation: before elements consolidate and before the secondary creators take their stations, she is the very first wave of manifestation (pūrvajā) emerging out of the absolute unmanifest silence. she is the first ray of dawn, setting the template for everything that follows.","esoteric":["The Primordial Manifestation: Before elements consolidate and before the secondary creators take their stations, She is the very first wave of manifestation (Pūrvajā) emerging out of the absolute unmanifest silence. She is the first ray of dawn, setting the template for everything that follows."]},{"number":976,"name":"त्रिपुराम्बिका","samasa":["त्रयाणां पुराणामवस्थारूपाणामम्बिका जनिका।","त्रीणि पुराणि यस्य स जीवः। तेषामम्बिका।"],"wordByWord":["त्रिपुराम्बिका। — component of the name"],"summary":["त्रिपुराम्बिका means mother of the three cities. The three cities may be the three states of experience. She is the mother of the jiva who identifies with those three states."],"searchText":"976 त्रिपुराम्बिका त्रयाणां पुराणामवस्थारूपाणामम्बिका जनिका। त्रीणि पुराणि यस्य स जीवः। तेषामम्बिका। त्रिपुराम्बिका। — component of the name त्रिपुराम्बिका means mother of the three cities. the three cities may be the three states of experience. she is the mother of the jiva who identifies with those three states. the parent of the three states: the \"three cities\" (tripura) are the three everyday states of human awareness: जाग्रत (waking), स्वप्न (dreaming), and सुषुप्ति (deep sleep). she is ambikā (the mother) to this entire triad. she generates and supports these states, serving as the hidden fourth space (turīya) that anchors them.","esoteric":["The Parent of the Three States: The \"three cities\" (tripura) are the three everyday states of human awareness: जाग्रत (Waking), स्वप्न (Dreaming), and सुषुप्ति (Deep Sleep). She is Ambikā (the mother) to this entire triad. She generates and supports these states, serving as the hidden fourth space (Turīya) that anchors them."]},{"number":977,"name":"दशमुद्रासमाराध्या","samasa":["दश मुद्राभिः करणभूताभिः सम्यक् आराध्या।"],"wordByWord":["दश — ten","दशमुद्रासमाराध्या। — component of the name"],"summary":["दशमुद्रासमाराध्या means one properly worshipped through the ten mudras. The ten mudras are ritual instruments of worship. She is specially adored through them."],"searchText":"977 दशमुद्रासमाराध्या दश मुद्राभिः करणभूताभिः सम्यक् आराध्या। दश — ten दशमुद्रासमाराध्या। — component of the name दशमुद्रासमाराध्या means one properly worshipped through the ten mudras. the ten mudras are ritual instruments of worship. she is specially adored through them. the ten energy seals: mudrās are precise physical gestures and internal seals (running from sarvasaṅkṣobhiṇī up to sarvatrikhaṇḍā) that match the nine enclosures of the śrī yantra. they are not symbolic dances. they act as precise energetic keys that lock the practitioner's nervous system into alignment, opening the channels to receive her grace.","esoteric":["The Ten Energy Seals: Mudrās are precise physical gestures and internal seals (running from Sarvasaṅkṣobhiṇī up to Sarvatrikhaṇḍā) that match the nine enclosures of the Śrī Yantra. They are not symbolic dances. They act as precise energetic keys that lock the practitioner's nervous system into alignment, opening the channels to receive Her grace."]},{"number":978,"name":"त्रिपुराश्रीवशङ्करी","samasa":["त्रिपुराश्रीनामिकां देवीं वशं कुरुते इति।","त्रिपुराश्रीनामिका देवी वशङ्करी यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose","त्रिपुराश्रीवशङ्करी। — component of the name"],"summary":["त्रिपुराश्रीवशङ्करी means one who brings Tripurā Śrī under control. Or Tripurā Śrī herself is the power of bringing under control. The name connects Her with the authority of Tripurā Śrī."],"searchText":"978 त्रिपुराश्रीवशङ्करी त्रिपुराश्रीनामिकां देवीं वशं कुरुते इति। त्रिपुराश्रीनामिका देवी वशङ्करी यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose त्रिपुराश्रीवशङ्करी। — component of the name त्रिपुराश्रीवशङ्करी means one who brings tripurā śrī under control. or tripurā śrī herself is the power of bringing under control. the name connects her with the authority of tripurā śrī. command over the fifth circle: within the anatomy of the śrī yantra, tripurāśrī is the specific administrative deity placed in charge of the fifth enclosure. she is the ultimate source back behind this goddess, directing the distribution of wealth and spiritual merit.","esoteric":["Command over the Fifth Circle: Within the anatomy of the Śrī Yantra, Tripurāśrī is the specific administrative deity placed in charge of the fifth enclosure. She is the ultimate source back behind this goddess, directing the distribution of wealth and spiritual merit."]},{"number":979,"name":"ज्ञानमुद्रा","samasa":["ज्ञानमुद्ररूपा।","ज्ञानेन मुदं रातीति।","ज्ञानं चिदंशं मुदमानन्दांशं द्रावयत्यावृणोतीति।"],"wordByWord":["ज्ञानमुद्रा। — component of the name"],"summary":["ज्ञानमुद्रा means one who is the Jnana Mudra. The name also means one who gives delight through knowledge. Knowledge and bliss are united in this mudra."],"searchText":"979 ज्ञानमुद्रा ज्ञानमुद्ररूपा। ज्ञानेन मुदं रातीति। ज्ञानं चिदंशं मुदमानन्दांशं द्रावयत्यावृणोतीति। ज्ञानमुद्रा। — component of the name ज्ञानमुद्रा means one who is the jnana mudra. the name also means one who gives delight through knowledge. knowledge and bliss are united in this mudra. the seal of awareness: physically, she manifests as the iconic hand gesture where the index finger touches the thumb, forming a complete circuit that symbols individual soul merging with universal spirit. internally, she acts as the force that dispenses intense spiritual joy (mudam) the exact moment pure knowledge (jñāna) flashes open inside the mind.","esoteric":["The Seal of Awareness: Physically, She manifests as the iconic hand gesture where the index finger touches the thumb, forming a complete circuit that symbols individual soul merging with universal spirit. Internally, She acts as the force that dispenses intense spiritual joy (mudam) the exact moment pure knowledge (jñāna) flashes open inside the mind."]},{"number":980,"name":"ज्ञानगम्या","samasa":["ज्ञानेन गम्या प्राप्या।"],"wordByWord":["गम्या — attainable; reached","ज्ञानगम्या। — component of the name"],"summary":["ज्ञानगम्या means one who is reached by knowledge. She is attained through true knowledge. Realisation, not mere external action, is the path to Her."],"searchText":"980 ज्ञानगम्या ज्ञानेन गम्या प्राप्या। गम्या — attainable; reached ज्ञानगम्या। — component of the name ज्ञानगम्या means one who is reached by knowledge. she is attained through true knowledge. realisation, not mere external action, is the path to her. the gate of awakening: she cannot be captured by emotional manipulation, mechanical rituals, or dry intellectual logic. she is jñānagamyā because her ultimate reality opens its gate exclusively to pure, non-dual realization (jñāna). every preliminary practice must eventually transform into direct awareness to step inside her sanctuary.","esoteric":["The Gate of Awakening: She cannot be captured by emotional manipulation, mechanical rituals, or dry intellectual logic. She is Jñānagamyā because Her ultimate reality opens its gate exclusively to pure, non-dual realization (Jñāna). Every preliminary practice must eventually transform into direct awareness to step inside Her sanctuary."]},{"number":981,"name":"ज्ञानज्ञेयस्वरूपिणी","samasa":["ज्ञानज्ञेये दृग्दृश्ये स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["ज्ञानज्ञेयस्वरूपिणी। — component of the name"],"summary":["ज्ञानज्ञेयस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is knowledge and the object known. She is both the seer and the seen, knowledge and the knowable. The distinction between knower, knowing and known resolves in Her."],"searchText":"981 ज्ञानज्ञेयस्वरूपिणी ज्ञानज्ञेये दृग्दृश्ये स्वरूपमस्याः अस्तीति। ज्ञानज्ञेयस्वरूपिणी। — component of the name ज्ञानज्ञेयस्वरूपिणी means one whose form is knowledge and the object known. she is both the seer and the seen, knowledge and the knowable. the distinction between knower, knowing and known resolves in her. the fusion of subject and object: human tracking splits reality into a subject who looks (dṛg / jñāna) and an object that is looked at (dṛśya / jñeya). she is jñānajñeyasvarūpiṇī because she is the single, non-dual energy field that manifests as both sides of the equation. there is no independent world out there separate from the light that sees it; the knower and the known are one substance.","esoteric":["The Fusion of Subject and Object: Human tracking splits reality into a subject who looks (Dṛg / Jñāna) and an object that is looked at (Dṛśya / Jñeya). She is Jñānajñeyasvarūpiṇī because She is the single, non-dual energy field that manifests as both sides of the equation. There is no independent world out there separate from the light that sees it; the knower and the known are one substance."]},{"number":982,"name":"योनिमुद्रा","samasa":["योनौ मुदं राति।","योनिरेव मुद्रा आछादिका यस्य बिन्दोस्तद्रूपा।"],"wordByWord":["मुद्रा — mudra","योनिमुद्रा। — component of the name"],"summary":["योनिमुद्रा means one who is the Yoni Mudra. She grants delight in the yoni, the source. The yoni itself is the concealing and revealing mudra of the bindu."],"searchText":"982 योनिमुद्रा योनौ मुदं राति। योनिरेव मुद्रा आछादिका यस्य बिन्दोस्तद्रूपा। मुद्रा — mudra योनिमुद्रा। — component of the name योनिमुद्रा means one who is the yoni mudra. she grants delight in the yoni, the source. the yoni itself is the concealing and revealing mudra of the bindu. the seal of primordial source: yonimudrā is the highly sacred, non-dual hand gesture that represents the matrix of creation. internally, it refers to the primary inverted triangle enclosure that tightly wraps and protects the central point (bindu). she is this seal, representing the absolute containment and conservation of spiritual power before it translates into manifestation.","esoteric":["The Seal of Primordial Source: Yonimudrā is the highly sacred, non-dual hand gesture that represents the matrix of creation. Internally, it refers to the primary inverted triangle enclosure that tightly wraps and protects the central point (Bindu). She is this seal, representing the absolute containment and conservation of spiritual power before it translates into manifestation."]},{"number":983,"name":"त्रिखण्डेशी","samasa":["त्रिखण्डाख्याया दशम्या मुद्राया ईशी स्वामिनी।","त्रयाणां सोमसूर्यानलाख्यमन्त्रखण्डानामीशी।"],"wordByWord":["ईशी — mistress","त्रिखण्डेशी। — component of the name"],"summary":["त्रिखण्डेशी means She is also the ruler of the three mantra divisions known as Soma, Surya and Anala. Mistress of Trikhanda. She is the ruler of the tenth mudra called Trikhanda."],"searchText":"983 त्रिखण्डेशी त्रिखण्डाख्याया दशम्या मुद्राया ईशी स्वामिनी। त्रयाणां सोमसूर्यानलाख्यमन्त्रखण्डानामीशी। ईशी — mistress त्रिखण्डेशी। — component of the name त्रिखण्डेशी means she is also the ruler of the three mantra divisions known as soma, surya and anala. mistress of trikhanda. she is the ruler of the tenth mudra called trikhanda. the master of the three blocks: trikhaṇḍā is the definitive tenth mudrā that seals the entire śrī yantra ritual work. phonetically, it refers to the three distinct blocks (khaṇḍas) of the supreme mantra—the moon section (soma), the sun section (sūrya), and the fire section (anala). she is the absolute īśvarī (empress) who governs this entire triple structure, binding it into a single power loop.","esoteric":["The Master of the Three Blocks: Trikhaṇḍā is the definitive tenth mudrā that seals the entire Śrī Yantra ritual work. Phonetically, it refers to the three distinct blocks (khaṇḍas) of the supreme mantra—the Moon section (Soma), the Sun section (Sūrya), and the Fire section (Anala). She is the absolute Īśvarī (empress) who governs this entire triple structure, binding it into a single power loop."]},{"number":984,"name":"त्रिगुणा","samasa":["त्रयो गुणा यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["त्रिगुणा। — component of the name"],"summary":["त्रिगुणा means one who has the three gunas. Though She transcends the gunas, they also exist in Her as the power of manifestation. She is the support of sattva, rajas and tamas."],"searchText":"984 त्रिगुणा त्रयो गुणा यस्यां सा। त्रिगुणा। — component of the name त्रिगुणा means one who has the three gunas. though she transcends the gunas, they also exist in her as the power of manifestation. she is the support of sattva, rajas and tamas. the weaver of form: while she transcends qualities (guṇātītā), she is simultaneously triguṇā because she coordinates the three qualities (sattva, rajas, tamas) to build the physical world. she acts as the master weaver who spins light, movement, and mass to construct the material universe.","esoteric":["The Weaver of Form: While She transcends qualities (Guṇātītā), She is simultaneously Triguṇā because She coordinates the three qualities (Sattva, Rajas, Tamas) to build the physical world. She acts as the master weaver who spins light, movement, and mass to construct the material universe."]},{"number":985,"name":"अम्बा","samasa":["अम्बा माता कारणभूता।"],"wordByWord":["अम्बा — Mother","अम्बा। — component of the name"],"summary":["अम्बा means mother. Amba means the mother and the causal source. She is the mother of all."],"searchText":"985 अम्बा अम्बा माता कारणभूता। अम्बा — mother अम्बा। — component of the name अम्बा means mother. amba means the mother and the causal source. she is the mother of all. the primordial maternal source: the entire cosmic system of mantras, elements, and geometries dissolves into a single word—ambā. she is the direct, unconditional mother of every living soul. she is the ultimate cause (jagat-kāraṇa) that provides love, protection, and the necessary path inputs to guide her children home.","esoteric":["The Primordial Maternal Source: The entire cosmic system of mantras, elements, and geometries dissolves into a single word—Ambā. She is the direct, unconditional mother of every living soul. She is the ultimate cause (jagat-kāraṇa) that provides love, protection, and the necessary path inputs to guide Her children home."]},{"number":986,"name":"त्रिकोणगा","samasa":["त्रिकोण योनिचक्रं गच्छतीति।"],"wordByWord":["त्रिकोण — triangle","त्रिकोणगा। — component of the name"],"summary":["त्रिकोणगा means one who abides in the triangle. The triangle is the yoni-chakra. She is present in that sacred triangular centre."],"searchText":"986 त्रिकोणगा त्रिकोण योनिचक्रं गच्छतीति। त्रिकोण — triangle त्रिकोणगा। — component of the name त्रिकोणगा means one who abides in the triangle. the triangle is the yoni-chakra. she is present in that sacred triangular centre. seated in the core triangle: in the layout of the śrī yantra, the त्रिकोण (trikoṇa) is the primary central triangle that surrounds the absolute center point (bindu). she is trikoṇagā because her consciousness resides directly inside this geometric hub, representing the absolute source out of which the lines of the universe branch out.","esoteric":["Seated in the Core Triangle: In the layout of the Śrī Yantra, the त्रिकोण (Trikoṇa) is the primary central triangle that surrounds the absolute center point (Bindu). She is Trikoṇagā because Her consciousness resides directly inside this geometric hub, representing the absolute source out of which the lines of the universe branch out."]},{"number":987,"name":"अनघा","samasa":["अंविद्यमानानि अघानि यस्यां सा।"],"wordByWord":["अघानि — sins","अनघा। — component of the name"],"summary":["अनघा means one who is sinless. Agha means sin or evil. No sin or blemish exists in Her."],"searchText":"987 अनघा अंविद्यमानानि अघानि यस्यां सा। अघानि — sins अनघा। — component of the name अनघा means one who is sinless. agha means sin or evil. no sin or blemish exists in her. the blemish-free screen: material entities gather stains (agha) through ignorant actions and historical distortions. she is anaghā because her unconditioned consciousness field is completely free from these defects. she remains a pristine, unblemished template of absolute purity, clearing away the errors of anyone who enters her space.","esoteric":["The Blemish-Free Screen: Material entities gather stains (agha) through ignorant actions and historical distortions. She is Anaghā because Her unconditioned consciousness field is completely free from these defects. She remains a pristine, unblemished template of absolute purity, clearing away the errors of anyone who enters Her space."]},{"number":988,"name":"अद्भुतचारित्रा","samasa":["अद्भुतान्याश्चर्यकराणि चारित्राणि यस्याः सा।","अद्भुतेषु भूकम्पादिषूत्पातेषु निमित्तेषु चरन्ती।","अद्भुतचारीणि दुष्टफलानि तेभ्यस्त्रायते इति।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose","अद्भुतचारित्रा। — component of the name"],"summary":["अद्भुतचारित्रा means one whose conduct is wonderful. Her deeds are extraordinary and astonishing. The name may also indicate protection from evil results connected with portents and disturbances."],"searchText":"988 अद्भुतचारित्रा अद्भुतान्याश्चर्यकराणि चारित्राणि यस्याः सा। अद्भुतेषु भूकम्पादिषूत्पातेषु निमित्तेषु चरन्ती। अद्भुतचारीणि दुष्टफलानि तेभ्यस्त्रायते इति। यस्याः — whose अद्भुतचारित्रा। — component of the name अद्भुतचारित्रा means one whose conduct is wonderful. her deeds are extraordinary and astonishing. the name may also indicate protection from evil results connected with portents and disturbances. the conductor of miracles: her cosmic management features deeds (cāritra) that spark absolute wonder (adbhuta), bypassing linear logical calculation. under the protective tracks, she acts as the stabilizing intelligence that moves through chaotic natural disturbances (like earthquakes), protecting her devotees from destructive outcomes.","esoteric":["The Conductor of Miracles: Her cosmic management features deeds (cāritra) that spark absolute wonder (adbhuta), bypassing linear logical calculation. Under the protective tracks, She acts as the stabilizing intelligence that moves through chaotic natural disturbances (like earthquakes), protecting Her devotees from destructive outcomes."]},{"number":989,"name":"वाञ्छितार्थप्रदायिनी","samasa":["वाञ्छितार्थान्प्रदातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["वाञ्छितार्थप्रदायिनी। — component of the name"],"summary":["वाञ्छितार्थप्रदायिनी means one who grants desired objects. She has the nature of bestowing what is longed for. Devotees receive their wished-for ends through Her grace."],"searchText":"989 वाञ्छितार्थप्रदायिनी वाञ्छितार्थान्प्रदातुं शीलमस्याः अस्तीति। वाञ्छितार्थप्रदायिनी। — component of the name वाञ्छितार्थप्रदायिनी means one who grants desired objects. she has the nature of bestowing what is longed for. devotees receive their wished-for ends through her grace. the fulfiller of pure intent: she is not indifferent to the practical needs of the seeker. as pradāyinī, she tracks the authentic desires (vāñchita) of the heart, whether material or spiritual, and systematically dispenses the necessary resources to ensure the practitioner does not experience anxiety while pursuing the path.","esoteric":["The Fulfiller of Pure Intent: She is not indifferent to the practical needs of the seeker. As Pradāyinī, She tracks the authentic desires (vāñchita) of the heart, whether material or spiritual, and systematically dispenses the necessary resources to ensure the practitioner does not experience anxiety while pursuing the path."]},{"number":990,"name":"अभ्यासातिशयज्ञाता","samasa":["ब्रह्मात्मैक्यानुसन्धानाभ्यास्य आवृत्त्याः अतिशयेन ज्ञाता।"],"wordByWord":["अतिशयेन — excessively; through intensity","अभ्यासातिशयज्ञाता। — component of the name"],"summary":["अभ्यासातिशयज्ञाता means one known through excess of practice. She is realised through repeated practice of the enquiry into the unity of Brahman and the Self. Persistent spiritual practice reveals Her."],"searchText":"990 अभ्यासातिशयज्ञाता ब्रह्मात्मैक्यानुसन्धानाभ्यास्य आवृत्त्याः अतिशयेन ज्ञाता। अतिशयेन — excessively; through intensity अभ्यासातिशयज्ञाता। — component of the name अभ्यासातिशयज्ञाता means one known through excess of practice. she is realised through repeated practice of the enquiry into the unity of brahman and the self. persistent spiritual practice reveals her. the momentum of realization: she cannot be uncovered by a casual or distracted interest. she is jñātā (realized) exclusively through अभ्यास-अतिशय (abhyāsa-atiśaya) — the continuous, intense, and unbroken habit of non-dual meditation on the identity of the individual soul and the absolute absolute (ब्रह्मात्मैक्य). this continuous momentum clears away the oldest layers of mental habits, revealing the self.","esoteric":["The Momentum of Realization: She cannot be uncovered by a casual or distracted interest. She is Jñātā (realized) exclusively through अभ्यास-अतिशय (abhyāsa-atiśaya) — the continuous, intense, and unbroken habit of non-dual meditation on the identity of the individual soul and the absolute absolute (ब्रह्मात्मैक्य). This continuous momentum clears away the oldest layers of mental habits, revealing the Self."]},{"number":991,"name":"षडध्वातीतरूपिणी","samasa":["षडध्वानान् अतीतं रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["षडध्वातीतरूपिणी। — component of the name"],"summary":["षडध्वातीतरूपिणी means one whose form transcends the six paths. The six adhvas are categories of mantra, word and manifestation. Her form is beyond all of them."],"searchText":"991 षडध्वातीतरूपिणी षडध्वानान् अतीतं रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। षडध्वातीतरूपिणी। — component of the name षडध्वातीतरूपिणी means one whose form transcends the six paths. the six adhvas are categories of mantra, word and manifestation. her form is beyond all of them. transcending the six pathways: the entire universe is structured across six major operational pathways (ṣaḍ-adhvā), split into the sound track (śabda-adhvā: varṇa, pada, mantra) and the object track (artha-adhvā: kalā, tattva, bhuvana). she is ṣaḍadhvātītarūpiṇī because her essential unconditioned nature sits completely above and outside this entire structural framework, serving as the raw consciousness that supports the path grid.","esoteric":["Transcending the Six Pathways: The entire universe is structured across six major operational pathways (ṣaḍ-adhvā), split into the sound track (Śabda-adhvā: Varṇa, Pada, Mantra) and the object track (Artha-adhvā: Kalā, Tattva, Bhuvana). She is Ṣaḍadhvātītarūpiṇī because Her essential unconditioned nature sits completely above and outside this entire structural framework, serving as the raw consciousness that supports the path grid."]},{"number":992,"name":"अव्याजकरुणामूर्तिः","samasa":["अव्याजा अनौपधिकी या करुणा सैव मूर्तिः स्वरूपं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["अव्याजा — without pretext; causeless","करुणा — compassion","मूर्तिः — form","यस्याः — whose"],"summary":["अव्याजकरुणामूर्तिः means one whose form is causeless compassion. Her mercy is not dependent on any condition or motive. Compassion itself is Her form."],"searchText":"992 अव्याजकरुणामूर्तिः अव्याजा अनौपधिकी या करुणा सैव मूर्तिः स्वरूपं यस्याः सा। अव्याजा — without pretext; causeless करुणा — compassion मूर्तिः — form यस्याः — whose अव्याजकरुणामूर्तिः means one whose form is causeless compassion. her mercy is not dependent on any condition or motive. compassion itself is her form. causeless grace: human compassion is usually savyāja — dependent on external conditions, personal relationships, or expectations of return. she is avyājakaruṇāmūrtiḥ because her grace is completely unconditioned (anaupadhikī). she showers love simply because it is her baseline nature to do so, requiring no complex bargaining from the practitioner.","esoteric":["Causeless Grace: Human compassion is usually savyāja — dependent on external conditions, personal relationships, or expectations of return. She is Avyājakaruṇāmūrtiḥ because Her grace is completely unconditioned (anaupadhikī). She showers love simply because it is Her baseline nature to do so, requiring no complex bargaining from the practitioner."]},{"number":993,"name":"अज्ञानध्वान्तदीपिका","samasa":["अज्ञानमेव ध्वान्तमन्धकारस्तस्य दीपिकेव।"],"wordByWord":["अज्ञानध्वान्तदीपिका। — component of the name"],"summary":["अज्ञानध्वान्तदीपिका means one who is the lamp for the darkness of ignorance. Ignorance is like dense darkness. She removes it like a lamp giving light."],"searchText":"993 अज्ञानध्वान्तदीपिका अज्ञानमेव ध्वान्तमन्धकारस्तस्य दीपिकेव। अज्ञानध्वान्तदीपिका। — component of the name अज्ञानध्वान्तदीपिका means one who is the lamp for the darkness of ignorance. ignorance is like dense darkness. she removes it like a lamp giving light. the solvent of ignorance: ignorance (ajñāna) behaves like a dense, dark room, causing the soul to stumble over illusions. she acts as the blinding, clear lamp (dīpikā) placed inside this room. she does not battle the darkness; her presence illuminates the space, causing the darkness of ignorance to vanish instantly.","esoteric":["The Solvent of Ignorance: Ignorance (ajñāna) behaves like a dense, dark room, causing the soul to stumble over illusions. She acts as the blinding, clear lamp (Dīpikā) placed inside this room. She does not battle the darkness; Her presence illuminates the space, causing the darkness of ignorance to vanish instantly."]},{"number":994,"name":"आबालगोपविदिता","samasa":["बालान् ब्रह्मादिकान् गोपयतीति बालगोपः। बालश्चासौ गोपश्च बालगोपः। बालगोपश्च बालगोपश्च बालगोपौ तावभिव्याप्य आबालगोपं तादृशेन विदितं ज्ञानं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["आबालगोपविदिता। — component of the name"],"summary":["आबालगोपविदिता means one known from children up to cowherds, or one known by all. The name is explained through Bālā and Gopa and by extension all beings. Her presence and fame are universally known."],"searchText":"994 आबालगोपविदिता बालान् ब्रह्मादिकान् गोपयतीति बालगोपः। बालश्चासौ गोपश्च बालगोपः। बालगोपश्च बालगोपश्च बालगोपौ तावभिव्याप्य आबालगोपं तादृशेन विदितं ज्ञानं यस्याः सा। आबालगोपविदिता। — component of the name आबालगोपविदिता means one known from children up to cowherds, or one known by all. the name is explained through bālā and gopa and by extension all beings. her presence and fame are universally known. the open secret: lest a seeker think she is accessible only to a small group of elite scholars, this name confirms her presence is universally felt. she is known by the simplest, most humble cowherds (gopas) through pure love, and by the highest creator principles (bālas like brahmā) through deep contemplation. she is an open reality accessible to anyone who approaches with a clean heart.","esoteric":["The Open Secret: Lest a seeker think She is accessible only to a small group of elite scholars, this name confirms Her presence is universally felt. She is known by the simplest, most humble cowherds (gopas) through pure love, and by the highest creator principles (bālas like Brahmā) through deep contemplation. She is an open reality accessible to anyone who approaches with a clean heart."]},{"number":995,"name":"सर्वानुल्लङ्घ्यशासना","samasa":["सर्वैर्ब्रह्मविष्ण्वादिभिरप्युल्लङ्घितुमयोग्यमशक्यम् च शासनं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose","सर्वानुल्लङ्घ्यशासना। — component of the name"],"summary":["सर्वानुल्लङ्घ्यशासना means one whose command cannot be transgressed by anyone. Even Brahmā, Viṣṇu and others cannot cross Her command. Her rule is supreme and inviolable."],"searchText":"995 सर्वानुल्लङ्घ्यशासना सर्वैर्ब्रह्मविष्ण्वादिभिरप्युल्लङ्घितुमयोग्यमशक्यम् च शासनं यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose सर्वानुल्लङ्घ्यशासना। — component of the name सर्वानुल्लङ्घ्यशासना means one whose command cannot be transgressed by anyone. even brahmā, viṣṇu and others cannot cross her command. her rule is supreme and inviolable. the absolute rule: the laws of nature—such as gravity, the tracking of karma, planetary orbits, and the steps of dissolution—are not random choices. they are her executive decrees (śāsana). no entity, from a tiny cell up to the highest cosmic administrators like brahmā or viṣṇu, has the capacity to break this law, ensuring absolute order across the multiverse.","esoteric":["The Absolute Rule: The laws of nature—such as gravity, the tracking of karma, planetary orbits, and the steps of dissolution—are not random choices. They are Her executive decrees (Śāsana). No entity, from a tiny cell up to the highest cosmic administrators like Brahmā or Viṣṇu, has the capacity to break this law, ensuring absolute order across the multiverse."]},{"number":996,"name":"श्रीचक्रराजनिलया","samasa":["श्रीचक्रराजं बिन्दुत्रिकोणादिरूपं निलयो वासस्थानं यस्याः सा।"],"wordByWord":["यस्याः — whose","श्रीचक्रराजनिलया। — component of the name"],"summary":["श्रीचक्रराजनिलया means one whose abode is the royal Śrīcakra. The Śrīcakra, formed of bindu, triangle and other parts, is Her dwelling place. She resides in the supreme yantra of Śrīvidyā."],"searchText":"996 श्रीचक्रराजनिलया श्रीचक्रराजं बिन्दुत्रिकोणादिरूपं निलयो वासस्थानं यस्याः सा। यस्याः — whose श्रीचक्रराजनिलया। — component of the name श्रीचक्रराजनिलया means one whose abode is the royal śrīcakra. the śrīcakra, formed of bindu, triangle and other parts, is her dwelling place. she resides in the supreme yantra of śrīvidyā. the dynamic sanctuary: she does not inhabit a distant, imaginary heaven. her definitive architectural palace is the श्रीचक्रराज (śrī cakra rāja) — the supreme arrangement of nine intersecting triangles forming forty-three secondary shapes around the central point. this chart is the exact structural model of her energy field, serving as the gateway where the practitioner communicates with her presence.","esoteric":["The Dynamic Sanctuary: She does not inhabit a distant, imaginary heaven. Her definitive architectural palace is the श्रीचक्रराज (Śrī Cakra Rāja) — the supreme arrangement of nine intersecting triangles forming forty-three secondary shapes around the central point. This chart is the exact structural model of Her energy field, serving as the gateway where the practitioner communicates with Her presence."]},{"number":997,"name":"श्रीमत्त्रिपुरसुन्दरी","samasa":["त्रिपुरस्य परशिवस्य सुन्दरी भार्या। श्रीमती च सा त्रिपुरसुन्दरी चेति।"],"wordByWord":["सा — she","त्रिपुरसुन्दरी — Tripura Sundari","श्रीमत्त्रिपुरसुन्दरी। — component of the name"],"summary":["श्रीमत्त्रिपुरसुन्दरी means the auspicious Tripurā Sundarī. She is the beautiful consort of Tripurā, the Supreme Śiva. She is endowed with Śrī and is Tripurā Sundarī Herself."],"searchText":"997 श्रीमत्त्रिपुरसुन्दरी त्रिपुरस्य परशिवस्य सुन्दरी भार्या। श्रीमती च सा त्रिपुरसुन्दरी चेति। सा — she त्रिपुरसुन्दरी — tripura sundari श्रीमत्त्रिपुरसुन्दरी। — component of the name श्रीमत्त्रिपुरसुन्दरी means the auspicious tripurā sundarī. she is the beautiful consort of tripurā, the supreme śiva. she is endowed with śrī and is tripurā sundarī herself. the empress of divine beauty: tripurasundarī denotes the sovereign beauty that outshines everything across the three enclosures of time, space, and consciousness. she belongs to tripura (lord paramaśiva). she is śrīmatī because she possesses the absolute, uncorrupted majesty of divine splendor, acting as the radiant queen who directs the lineage.","esoteric":["The Empress of Divine Beauty: Tripurasundarī denotes the sovereign beauty that outshines everything across the three enclosures of time, space, and consciousness. She belongs to Tripura (Lord Paramaśiva). She is Śrīmatī because She possesses the absolute, uncorrupted majesty of divine splendor, acting as the radiant queen who directs the lineage."]},{"number":998,"name":"श्रीशिवा","samasa":["श्रीयुक्ता शिवा।"],"wordByWord":["श्रीशिवा। — component of the name"],"summary":["श्रीशिवा means the blessed Śrī Śiva. She is Śiva endowed with Śrī, the sacred consort and integral part of Śiva. Whatever meaning applies to Śiva applies to Her also, because She is not separate from Him."],"searchText":"998 श्रीशिवा श्रीयुक्ता शिवा। श्रीशिवा। — component of the name श्रीशिवा means the blessed śrī śiva. she is śiva endowed with śrī, the sacred consort and integral part of śiva. whatever meaning applies to śiva applies to her also, because she is not separate from him. the non-dual alliance: this name fuses the two grand goals of human pursuit: श्री (śrī — material prosperity, beauty, and systemic abundance) and शिवा (śivā — pure, unconditioned consciousness, stillness, and final liberation). she is śrīśivā because she contains both traits simultaneously, ensuring that her path provides earthly support alongside spiritual freedom.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Alliance: This name fuses the two grand goals of human pursuit: श्री (Śrī — material prosperity, beauty, and systemic abundance) and शिवा (Śivā — pure, unconditioned consciousness, stillness, and final liberation). She is Śrīśivā because She contains both traits simultaneously, ensuring that Her path provides earthly support alongside spiritual freedom."]},{"number":999,"name":"शिवशक्त्यैक्यरूपिणी","samasa":["शिवशक्त्योरैक्यं सामरस्यमेव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति।"],"wordByWord":["शिवशक्त्यैक्यरूपिणी। — component of the name"],"summary":["शिवशक्त्यैक्यरूपिणी means one who is the union of Śiva and Śakti. She embodies the inseparable unity of Śiva and Śakti. Like light and illumination, word and meaning, sun and heat, She is the integrated non-dual form of both."],"searchText":"999 शिवशक्त्यैक्यरूपिणी शिवशक्त्योरैक्यं सामरस्यमेव रूपमस्याः अस्तीति। शिवशक्त्यैक्यरूपिणी। — component of the name शिवशक्त्यैक्यरूपिणी means one who is the union of śiva and śakti. she embodies the inseparable unity of śiva and śakti. like light and illumination, word and meaning, sun and heat, she is the integrated non-dual form of both. the non-dual oneness: as the sahasranāma reaches its penultimate peak, this name removes any remaining dualistic filters. shiva (pure, still consciousness) and shakti (dynamic, creative energy) are not two separate entities sitting together. they exist in a state of absolute, perfect fusion (sāmarasya) — like heat inside fire. she is this exact non-dual unity. duality is merely her unity displaying its options, anchoring the seeker in absolute oneness.","esoteric":["The Non-Dual Oneness: As the Sahasranāma reaches its penultimate peak, this name removes any remaining dualistic filters. Shiva (pure, still consciousness) and Shakti (dynamic, creative energy) are not two separate entities sitting together. They exist in a state of absolute, perfect fusion (Sāmarasya) — like heat inside fire. She is this exact non-dual unity. Duality is merely Her unity displaying its options, anchoring the seeker in absolute oneness."]},{"number":1000,"name":"ललिताम्बिका","samasa":["ललतेऽसौ ललिता च साम्बिका च।"],"wordByWord":["ललिता — playful; beautiful","ललिताम्बिका। — component of the name"],"summary":["ललिताम्बिका means one who is the beautiful Mother called Lalitā. This is the concluding name of the thousand names. The hymn begins with Śrīmātā, Mother, and ends with Ambikā, Mother. Though She is Brahman, devotees can easily approach Her as Mother. Lalitā means She who plays, She who is beautiful, and She who, through divine sport, creates and sustains the universe. At the end of this name, Om is to be pronounced."],"searchText":"1000 ललिताम्बिका ललतेऽसौ ललिता च साम्बिका च। ललिता — playful; beautiful ललिताम्बिका। — component of the name ललिताम्बिका means one who is the beautiful mother called lalitā. this is the concluding name of the thousand names. the hymn begins with śrīmātā, mother, and ends with ambikā, mother. though she is brahman, devotees can easily approach her as mother. lalitā means she who plays, she who is beautiful, and she who, through divine sport, creates and sustains the universe. at the end of this name, om is to be pronounced. the ultimate playful mother: the word ललिता (lalitā) defines her core style: she acts with absolute charm, effortless ease, and playful elegance (lalita), managing universes without friction. she links this play directly to her role as अम्बिका (ambikā — the deeply compassionate mother). she runs the grand play of the cosmos to guide, protect, and love her children. this name seals the text, confirming that the ultimate absolute is a mother who welcomes the practitioner home with open arms.","esoteric":["The Ultimate Playful Mother: The word ललिता (Lalitā) defines Her core style: She acts with absolute charm, effortless ease, and playful elegance (Lalita), managing universes without friction. She links this play directly to Her role as अम्बिका (Ambikā — the deeply compassionate mother). She runs the grand play of the cosmos to guide, protect, and love Her children. This name seals the text, confirming that the ultimate absolute is a mother who welcomes the practitioner home with open arms."]}];
